  ('04205d78-cae3-5451-9136-a8a2595c879f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '04205d78-cae3-5451-9136-a8a2595c879f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Public Register', E'Britain said it will introduce the world’s first public register of the owners of foreign companies holding property in the country. The move comes in response to growing concern over tax evaders’ and money-launderers’ use of shell companies to hide their identities. Most overseas companies that own property in London are registered in tax havens, particularly the British Virgin Islands.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('042222c5-6f87-5d6e-ac70-02fc09e1450b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '042222c5-6f87-5d6e-ac70-02fc09e1450b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Shopping Malls', E'In many towns and cities large shopping malls are replacing small local shops. Some people say that this is a positive development. To what extent do you agree?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether large shopping malls are replacing small local shops in many towns and cities has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that large shopping malls contribute to product selection diversity, whereas opponents contend that larger shopping centers foster market prosperity. From my perspective, I am convinced that the replacement of small local shops by large shopping malls is a positive development.\nTo begin with, large shopping malls significantly upgrade consumers'' shopping efficiency and overall experience. For example, large malls bring together multiple brands and stores, and provide numerous products, ranging from sports equipment to musical instruments. In addition to this, malls offer food courts, affordable parking services and entertainment options, making shopping trips more comfortable and efficient. Other than that, large chain stores make sure their products are of reliable quality and their service is dependable and professional. It is thus shown that large malls taking the place of local small shops represents a positive shift.\nBesides, I also believe that large shopping malls can promote economic development and employment rate. On top of that, large shopping malls require numerous staff for security and cleaning, offering more stable career growth compared to small shops. Moreover, well-known chain stores in malls attract business investment and boost local economic diversity. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that with higher sales and transparent finances, shopping malls generate greater tax revenue for local governments. This clearly proves that the replacement of small local shops with large malls is a beneficial advancement.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that enrichment of purchase experience and tax increase are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that it is a beneficial development for big shopping centers to take the place of small local stores.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('042a64ad-4d7c-5877-ab77-fa59cc496c85'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '042a64ad-4d7c-5877-ab77-fa59cc496c85'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the smallest particle of an element that retains its identity in a chemical reaction?', '20461a82-504a-5939-a45c-f2277e4f7172'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Atom', NULL, NULL),
  ('042b1f5f-0435-561d-9735-2f99bda105ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '042b1f5f-0435-561d-9735-2f99bda105ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In winter, what activities do people usually do on snow mountains by standing on long, thin boards?', '1d2d97d0-d380-5558-867d-227abc05e034'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Skiing', NULL, NULL),
  ('043b805e-5cbf-5b14-b2b0-abb89d0d3be2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '043b805e-5cbf-5b14-b2b0-abb89d0d3be2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pre-service Teachers', E'Each individual content-area course has a separate syllabus that highlights the specific technologies and pedagogy relevant to the content area. The technologies were selected after numerous meetings between methods and technology course instructors. After identifying the most appropriate technology, methods and technology course instructors co-develop their syllabi with projects spanning the two courses. Therefore, students learn about a specific technology in the technology course, and they integrate it in their practice teaching experiences within their methods course.\nIn a research collaboration with a methods area faculty member, the technology course instructor found that although preservice teachers know how to operate technology, they could not integrate it effectively within daily lesson plans and they were not able to envision the type of projects their students could develop. These findings influenced the technology course instructor to develop exemplary models of technology projects and pedagogy for each technology course section (i.e. content areas).\nFor example, a project was modeled to illustrate how students construct understanding of clouds using concept mapping within the science cohort. This project was supplemented by the instructor modeling effective teaching practices using concept mapping in the science classroom. The goal was to move the preservice teachers from focusing not only on the development of a final technology project in the course but encouraging them to think about successful integration in their future classrooms. These examples were placed online so the preservice teachers had access to them at all times in the development of their own projects for the technology course.', NULL, NULL, E'Each individual content-area course has a separate syllabus that highlights the specific technologies and pedagogy, and methods and technology course instructors co-develop their syllabi with projects spanning the two courses, but they could not integrate it effectively within daily lesson plans, which influenced the technology course instructor to develop exemplary models of technology projects and pedagogy, so a project was modeled to illustrate how students construct understanding of clouds using concept mapping.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('043ceea0-c679-59d7-851d-6a11f8826040'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '043ceea0-c679-59d7-851d-6a11f8826040'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dress Codes', E'The necessity of dress codes in society is a subject of {{1}} debate, reflecting the balance between individual freedom and societal norms. Proponents argue that dress codes, whether in schools, workplaces, or social settings, serve important functions: they can promote a sense of unity, minimize distractions, ensure safety, and uphold a professional or respectful {{2}} . For instance, in educational environments, dress codes {{3}} to foster a conducive learning environment by reducing peer pressure related to fashion trends and mitigating socioeconomic disparities. In professional settings, they contribute to a company''s image and can influence clients'' {{4}} positively. However, critics contend that strict dress codes can suppress individual expression, reinforce gender stereotypes, and exacerbate body image issues by {{5}} standards that may not accommodate diversity in body types and cultural backgrounds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.ongoing, 2.atmosphere, 3.are believed, 4.perceptions, 5.imposing', NULL, NULL),
  ('043e362a-79e9-5730-a40f-0988d670d2f2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '043e362a-79e9-5730-a40f-0988d670d2f2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4932b5ba-47f8-59bc-9f0f-26c340be82bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A computer virus has destroyed all my files.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0446962e-cf9c-5657-a086-ccf0434d6e73'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0446962e-cf9c-5657-a086-ccf0434d6e73'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the currency used in Russia?', 'c8e61733-c923-5504-8783-67f6db53742b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ruble', NULL, NULL),
  ('044798d1-b882-5ea6-964b-6341270603c1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '044798d1-b882-5ea6-964b-6341270603c1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ozone Pollution', E'China’s war on particulate air pollution is causing more severe ozone pollution. According to the new research, there was so much particulate matter in the smog around Chinese cities that it helped to quell ozone production by acting as a sponge that collected chemical radicals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0454a506-7f1c-5172-8db4-b007e976e174'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0454a506-7f1c-5172-8db4-b007e976e174'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Genetics', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('04552210-f647-5fca-a4b4-71e204423396'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '04552210-f647-5fca-a4b4-71e204423396'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'United Nation Library', E'The Dag Hammarskjold Library at United Nations Headquarters in New York is a library designated to facilitate the work of the United Nations and {{1}} mainly on the needs of the UN Secretariat and diplomatic missions. Anyone with a valid United Nations Headquarters grounds {{2}} , including specialized agencies, accredited media and NGO staff, is able to visit the library. Due to {{3}} constraints in place at the United Nations Headquarters complex, the library is not open to the general {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.focuses, 2.pass, 3.security, 4.public', NULL, NULL),
  ('0456bc02-311d-548d-9939-73c0370cf760'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0456bc02-311d-548d-9939-73c0370cf760'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sustained Economic Growth', E'China, which has both enjoyed sustained economic growth, face worrying challenges, there are worrying indications that social progress is starting to lag behind economic performance. With the slowdown in the rate of reduction in child deaths, a special concern, the un notes that china spends five per cent of its gdp on health, but public spending now amounts to less than two percent of gdp. The erosion of public funding, it says, has resulted in a mismatch between need and provision. With per capita spending in urban areas, three point five times that in rural areas, between seventy and eighty percent of the rural population have no health insurance. Children living in the poorest parts of rural China, face far greater health risks. And the gap is...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '2a134d52-4fca-5902-af73-cd2c1d4cd60a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'widening', NULL, NULL),
  ('0456d37e-ec06-567e-9838-512b94f0d88c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0456d37e-ec06-567e-9838-512b94f0d88c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '33fe9be7-d414-54b3-817b-c8a9419c4d46'::uuid, NULL, E'You will have the flexibility to choose your own path as a marine engineer.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('045cb58d-5e4c-5d7b-8717-95cf96b7cdd1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '045cb58d-5e4c-5d7b-8717-95cf96b7cdd1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Melanin', E'When you notice someone''s eye color, you''re looking at a part of the eye called the iris, a ring around the pupil filled with melanin. Melanin is a pigment that gives color to our hair, eyes and skin. Depending on the amount of melanin in the iris, it can be shades of gray, green, hazel, amber, brown or even red, and everyone''s eye color is unique.\nEye color isn''t just for aesthetics. Like most of your biology, eye color has a purpose. Thousands of years ago, the first humans had something in common, they all had brown eyes. Just like melanin in skin cells protect against the sun''s damaging UV rays, melanin in our eyes keeps harmful rays from causing long-term damage like cataracts or rare types of eye cancer.\nAs humans migrated and settled in climates with less harsh sun exposure, they required less melanin and human genetics adapted. Though the most common eye color is still brown across the world, it explains why people with European ancestors tend to have lighter hair, skin and eye colors.\nInterestingly, all melanin is brown. The more melanin an eye has, the darker it will appear. In eyes with less melanin, like blue or green, less light is absorbed and it scatters around the eye in a phenomenon called the Tyndall effect. It''s similar to why the sky appears blue.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('046283a1-15ae-5885-85a6-47e945285dc1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '046283a1-15ae-5885-85a6-47e945285dc1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'India', E'India''s movie history began in 1896 when the Lumière brothers wanted to {{1}} the art of cinema in Mumbai. Today, the films are known for their {{2}} singing and dancing. Indian dance, music and theater traditions {{3}} back more than 2,000 years. The major classical dance traditions {{4}} on themes from mythology and literature and have rigid presentation rules.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.demonstrate, 2.elaborate, 3.span, 4.draw', NULL, NULL),
  ('046c5cf9-f920-53be-9fd8-071503aba5e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '046c5cf9-f920-53be-9fd8-071503aba5e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A Flawed Project', E'You''re a project manager who has just reviewed a team''s project draft due next week. You notice several critical sections are incomplete, and the overall quality is below expectations. You need to address these issues promptly while motivating the team to improve their work before the deadline. What would you say to your team?', '269e9ce7-0d9d-5e29-b622-069297539f0d'::uuid, NULL, E'Hi guys, I''ve gone through our project draft and noticed some areas need more attention. Some critical sections are still incomplete, and we need to elevate our overall quality. Let''s use this as a chance to pull together and show what we''re capable of. I propose we organize a quick meeting tomorrow to discuss our strategy and allocate tasks efficiently. This way, everyone knows what''s needed, and we can ensure a strong finish.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('046ec81b-ec6e-591e-acb0-fcc8fd4094a5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '046ec81b-ec6e-591e-acb0-fcc8fd4094a5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '895dfb20-f1d6-5c25-860b-25f81a7ad1dc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We should have a meeting to discuss and report.', NULL, NULL),
