  ('062e58d5-d881-5689-8c17-9c7fc4de10b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '062e58d5-d881-5689-8c17-9c7fc4de10b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sports Salaries', E'Professional athletes can earn very high salaries. Many people argue that this is unfair and that other professions deserve higher salaries. To what extent do you agree or disagree?', NULL, NULL, E'Professional athletes often earn very high salaries, which some consider unfair. However, others argue that their earnings are well-deserved due to their unique skills, entertainment value, and contributions to the economy. This essay will discuss why high salaries for athletes are justified.\nFirstly, professional athletes possess exceptional skills and talents that few can achieve. They dedicate years to rigorous training and sacrifice personal time to excel in their sports. Their achievements inspire millions and serve as a symbol of determination and excellence. Such rare abilities naturally command high rewards, reflecting their value in a competitive market.\nSecondly, athletes bring significant entertainment and economic benefits. Sporting events captivate millions of fans worldwide, creating joy and unity among people. Furthermore, these events generate revenue through ticket sales, merchandise, and media rights, which contribute to economic growth. Athletes are the core reason for this success, and their salaries reflect their pivotal role in the industry.\nIn conclusion, professional athletes earn high salaries because of their exceptional skills, the entertainment they provide, and the economic impact they create. While some may view these earnings as excessive, they are proportional to the value athletes bring to society. Their hard work, dedication, and contributions justify their financial rewards, making their salaries fair in today’s market.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('06306e5a-bb7c-5802-8f14-9c4701923d13'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06306e5a-bb7c-5802-8f14-9c4701923d13'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the room that is under the ground floor?', '592b5900-033b-5927-8bc2-3849e6bdf7f4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Basement', NULL, NULL),
  ('06350302-ac44-5f78-b982-952b8bfd5cf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06350302-ac44-5f78-b982-952b8bfd5cf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aesop''s Fables', E'Today we {{1}} Aesop''s fables with childhood, and the Victorians are largely {{2}} for that. There were at least seven separate {{3}} or retellings in the 19th century, all targeted at children. Rewritten as parables, they were seen as an effective way of communicating Victorian morality. Yet, in antiquity, Aesop wasn''t read by children: {{4}} the talking animals and the sometimes childlike atmosphere of the tales, the setting was perceived at the time as being political.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.associate, 2.responsible, 3.translations, 4.despite', NULL, NULL),
  ('06446b52-621b-5c9f-a915-382fca53286f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06446b52-621b-5c9f-a915-382fca53286f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the small electronic device that you use for making mathematical calculations?', '1334b542-d38f-5469-bde0-a4d0001e06eb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Calculator', NULL, NULL),
  ('0646dc1b-4ee7-5ef1-b406-a9e1862d4e67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0646dc1b-4ee7-5ef1-b406-a9e1862d4e67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the largest island in the world?', 'd7ce2442-876e-503d-9305-de1fdebb61fb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Greenland', NULL, NULL),
  ('06518563-0712-5395-ae6e-fc5027ab9ed7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06518563-0712-5395-ae6e-fc5027ab9ed7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wind', E'Whether {{1}} or fierce, wind always starts in the same way. Wind is formed by the circulation of air. The sun heats up some parts of the sea and the land. The air among the {{2}} spots warms up and rises. The cold air drops because it is {{3}} . Some wind circulates within a small area. Others blow in the {{4}} globe.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.gentle, 2.hot, 3.heavy, 4.entire', NULL, NULL),
  ('06523ad6-0672-5d2a-9bb1-1167451e9197'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06523ad6-0672-5d2a-9bb1-1167451e9197'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Search for Meaning', E'Much of what people do today disguises a desperate search for meaning, the result of the crisis of belief that has become a major problem of the western world. On the one hand, the elites and their high culture suffer a loss of confidence, and aimless consumerism is widespread; on the other, powerful new myths arise, as with sporting heroes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0659b8c8-4e5f-519a-b645-cc9e56fd6e19'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0659b8c8-4e5f-519a-b645-cc9e56fd6e19'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where can you find index in the book?', '05e825b3-d7cd-5d83-84a7-12b74c387ce6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'At the end of the book', NULL, NULL),
  ('065bb7d4-5430-5e32-b13c-7ef4ff5d34db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '065bb7d4-5430-5e32-b13c-7ef4ff5d34db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Play Patterns', E'Observations of children''s play patterns {{1}} a preference for toys with bright, contrasting colors and repetitive shapes. Experts believe these features {{2}} children''s attention more effectively and aid in cognitive development. This preference for repetition and contrast appears to be an innate characteristic, aiding children in their early learning and {{3}} of their environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.indicate, 2.capture, 3.exploration', NULL, NULL),
  ('065be722-f442-5e61-8eac-2d1493bfad68'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '065be722-f442-5e61-8eac-2d1493bfad68'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call meat that comes from a cow?', 'ae1bdbac-2f1b-55fa-997c-41ac4d6b7af5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Beef', NULL, NULL),
  ('065f2a52-a950-50bc-affd-9febcb122a10'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '065f2a52-a950-50bc-affd-9febcb122a10'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f64d97d5-6589-5060-bcdf-9e1126e8688a'::uuid, NULL, E'Tutorials are held for two hours every Thursday during the semester.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('066253c2-78d5-5e85-87c1-78c8aa5e5106'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066253c2-78d5-5e85-87c1-78c8aa5e5106'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pavlov Experiment', NULL, 'b5f929fe-4213-523c-b2f0-d886cfffc004'::uuid, NULL, E'During this time my goals are going to be to talk about the phenomenon that we may share impart with other animals, and our language and that is emotion. And also talk about some new technology, brain imaging, functional magnetic imaging. And we try to answer some very old questions about ''how does motivation and emotion work''. I''m going to put you with the scenario first and some of you may be familiar with. This was developed by Pavlov over a century years ago. And in this scenario the dog presented with the sound, the dog waits, and then feeds food powder and this happened repeatedly, things starts to happen in the middle of the experiment there.\nInteresting things start to happen here. Pavlov''s study was on the salivation of the dog, the salivation increases more time to paralyzes. But other things happened here, too. You have a dog move around here more, all kinds of things are going on here. What we trying to capture was the experiment going on to describe today is what is going on in the brain to generate that state which we called it competitive state. But you can also think about state in terms of how the dogs'' feeling layer, how you are feeling about eating lunch today.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0664407c-36e7-506f-bc93-c82ca4282e66'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0664407c-36e7-506f-bc93-c82ca4282e66'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Consciousness and Creativity', NULL, 'b71f9d68-04b0-53db-b6bc-cebe2b5469d2'::uuid, NULL, E'M: I want you to talk a bit about consciousness and conscious consumption because I feel that you’ve got a different perspective on it. (Yeah) Than the typical... if you go and read a business school case on conscious consumption, it’s about where was the environmental footprint of this. (Yeah, yeah, yeah.) But you’re talking about something bigger (Yes.) than environmental impact, which matters, but you’re talking about almost something at the core.\nW: Everything we do on earth is about creativity. And I think that we live here, and oftentimes people fall into these patterns and they end up being recyclers, if you will, of somebody else’s life or a model. And that’s not your mission. Your mission in life is to break the mode, and do things independently that are very unique to you, just like an artist. So my mission is to create a network the infrastructure, if you will, the highway, if you will to support all kinds of artists and if these artists can all actually make a living like a thriving business, rather than be kind of a shunned career, then creativity will now be something that we, as a society, actually endorse and take pride in.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0668331e-12ac-5b2c-8ebf-13ad55843511'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0668331e-12ac-5b2c-8ebf-13ad55843511'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '518d94f2-225d-5129-89ed-fb195305a0dc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students of accounting should grasp profit and loss statements well.', NULL, NULL),
  ('066aae39-bf4e-5e33-9021-5e9b097c7568'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066aae39-bf4e-5e33-9021-5e9b097c7568'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd7697160-43a3-5e1f-8da9-9880df4d237b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Manufacturing now employs more people than agriculture and fishing combined.', NULL, NULL),
  ('066d1d08-0e66-5140-a5fa-1ee1af865b83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066d1d08-0e66-5140-a5fa-1ee1af865b83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '079decfc-d609-592f-b9d5-309ad75eedcc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Most university teaching still takes place in lectures and seminars.', NULL, NULL),
  ('066e7e3d-e68c-59a0-87a9-86e3add1e170'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066e7e3d-e68c-59a0-87a9-86e3add1e170'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lying to Ourselves', E'Why is lying to ourselves a problem? We need to tell ourselves the truth when we can, for the simple reason that we often pay a very high price for the short-term calm of our lies. We miss key opportunities for growth and learning. We''re not very nice to be around. We develop harmful systems. And not least, the truth will out. When we don''t let it emerge, it has a tendency to reveal itself through involuntary often physical symptoms. We become insomniac or impotent. An eyelid starts twitching. We acquire a stutter, and scream in our sleep and lose energy. We fall into depression. We owe it to ourselves to dare to start to confront ...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'b3f5d5c8-a06a-542d-a49f-1fb56653ca1e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'our real nature', NULL, NULL),
  ('066e8a6a-0d4b-51c7-9dad-a2ab14f7f31e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066e8a6a-0d4b-51c7-9dad-a2ab14f7f31e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a system of government by a king or a queen, such as the system of the UK?', '14a36f76-eec5-5f3f-8e0c-980dfbb32ace'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Monarchy', NULL, NULL),
  ('066f0480-e687-5367-8143-b488716d1d18'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '066f0480-e687-5367-8143-b488716d1d18'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a8972b38-cec8-5e54-9a28-1067800fb159'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'If you need a parking ticket, see me after the lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06755e90-27eb-54b4-a87d-74ecf6a6e9c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06755e90-27eb-54b4-a87d-74ecf6a6e9c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Innovative Product', E'An innovative new product or service can give a firm a head start over its rivals, which can be difficult for a new entrant to overcome. If the new technology is also patented, then other firms cannot simply copy its design. It is legally protected.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('067c81c6-c7c8-5f55-8f7f-125c8a429d16'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '067c81c6-c7c8-5f55-8f7f-125c8a429d16'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'Bread and cereals have a long history. The first bread was made in the nile valley about ten thousand years ago. The people used stones to crush the grain into coarse flour, and then they made the flour into primitive forms of bread. Primitive bread was not like the bread we know today, because it was simply flour dough dried on heated stones. The invention of ovens came later. Levin breads and cakes, which are made to rise by the action of yeast, were also a discovery of the ancient egyptians. The egyptians were the first people to master the art of baking. News of this new wonder food spread to other places in the middle east. Soon, other people were collecting seed, cultivating land and inventing ways to turn grain into flour. Baking used to be a social activity. While some homes had their own ovens, many families had to bake their dough and communal bakeries to identify their loaves. Each household would make a distinctive mark on the bread, sometimes with a special stamp bearing the family.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'df446d32-0c60-5a3d-af44-f732090e7126'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'name', NULL, NULL),
  ('068155dd-1ea1-51a1-ab83-7e01976c43aa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '068155dd-1ea1-51a1-ab83-7e01976c43aa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Archaeology', NULL, '337c7e49-ffe5-53ed-b15e-b9958901ffa5'::uuid, NULL, E'Archaeology is a source of history, not just a bumble auxiliary discipline. Archaeological data are historical documents in their own right, not mere illustrations to written texts, Just as much as any other historian, an archaeologist studies and tries to reconstitute the process that has created the human world in which we live - and us ourselves in so far as we are each creatures of our age and social environment. Archaeological data are all changes in the material world resulting from human action or, more succinctly, the fossilized results of human behavior. The sum total of these constitutes what may be called the archaeological record. This record exhibits certain peculiarities and deficiencies the consequences of which produce a rather superficial contrast between archaeological history and the more familiar kind based upon written records.\nNot all human behavior fossilizes. The words I utter and you hear as vibrations6 in the air are certainly human changes in the material world and may be of great historical significance. Yet they leave no sort of trace in the archaeological records unless they are captured by a dictaphone or written down by a clerk. The movement of troops on the battlefield may "change the course of history," but this is equally ephemeral from the archaeologist''s standpoint. What is perhaps worse, most organic materials are perishable. Everything made of wood, hide, wool, linen, grass, hair, and similar materials will decay and vanish in dust in a few years or centuries, save under very exceptional conditions. In a relatively brief period the archaeological record is reduce to mere scraps of stone, bone, glass, metal, and earthenware. Still modern archaeology, by applying appropriate techniques and comparative methods, aided by a few lucky finds from peat-bogs, deserts, and frozen soils, is able to fill up a good deal of the gap.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('06997a15-0681-5642-a6b7-78a4e74e0606'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06997a15-0681-5642-a6b7-78a4e74e0606'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the subject of study at a culinary institute?', '0c69cd01-8c13-52cb-bff5-238b021aec19'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cooking', NULL, NULL),
  ('069ba1dd-b89e-5dff-8a84-7843bacdd36f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '069ba1dd-b89e-5dff-8a84-7843bacdd36f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modern Wealth', E'Modern wealth has been created mainly through the action of market forces, which now dominate the whole of the industrial world. It is based on the {{1}} premise that we all start at an equal point. Of course nobody starts at the same point. Market forces help a few to become very wealthy at the {{2}} of the many who become poorer. This is taking place all over the world. There is an increasing number of hungry and desperate people living in utter poverty. Yet there are millionaires of all nationalities throughout the developed world. Market forces are inevitably acting to divide our world because they separate one section of society from another. Strangely enough, to create a society based on the free play of market forces, there must be a very strict control over the economy to ensure business efficiency. This is the poison of commercialization. It {{3}} restrictions on the natural needs of society. When the politicians are not meeting the needs of society, the people revolt . When the people''s voice is not heard, there will inevitably be revolution. Part of that revolution is the growing crime rate and the violent street protests which are the result of the {{4}} of our society - too great wealth side by side with too great poverty.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.false, 2.expense, 3.imposes, 4.imbalance', NULL, NULL),
  ('069d2b8b-6a58-53eb-b2ff-2b48b8fd1d01'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '069d2b8b-6a58-53eb-b2ff-2b48b8fd1d01'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2a4098a4-b4a3-53c2-b318-b876a92babb7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Your accountant will tell you how to complete these forms.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06a5b737-d618-5d62-8cb2-7e5783e72099'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06a5b737-d618-5d62-8cb2-7e5783e72099'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'When you react to a stimulus, is your response quick or slow?', '8e4762b1-a7f6-5663-83f9-19cdb9c392a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Quick', NULL, NULL),
  ('06aada9e-2476-5c36-9134-d8e99a58a5e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06aada9e-2476-5c36-9134-d8e99a58a5e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who studies mystery?', 'fa00eae0-dc3b-5d46-a92b-e082cdb85842'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mystic / occult', NULL, NULL),
  ('06b5969b-2061-5a91-9169-42306bae3082'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06b5969b-2061-5a91-9169-42306bae3082'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Satellite Imagery', E'Commercial satellite imagery is currently in a sweet spot: powerful enough to see a car, but not enough to tell the make and model; collected frequently enough for a farmer to keep tabs on crops’ health, but not so often that people could track the comings and goings of a neighbor. Federal regulations limit images taken by commercial satellites to a resolution of the length of a shoe.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('06ba5041-40ba-5b20-86dd-fd401342e23c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06ba5041-40ba-5b20-86dd-fd401342e23c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'University Terms', E'An industry or workplace often has its own terms for certain items, places, or groups of people, and a university is no different. Here we have attempted to explain some of the terms you may come across on our websites that are specific to higher education.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('06be043c-3e09-5ab7-9d74-0276f02f63ec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06be043c-3e09-5ab7-9d74-0276f02f63ec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '23d45cbc-2231-5b7e-9573-ebe90eef65cc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The same issue researched the same explanation of the problem.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06c16e4f-dfab-59cf-834f-8acdb45701bc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06c16e4f-dfab-59cf-834f-8acdb45701bc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Chronic Pain', E'When pain lasts for three months or longer, it is classified as chronic, a condition that affects more than 30 per cent of the world’s population. Chronic pain was long believed to be a stubborn version of {{1}} pain – which passes in less than three months once the damage is healed – and it was treated in much the same way. Yet an increasing body of research has led doctors to believe that chronic pain should be treated as a disease in its own right, rather than an {{2}} symptom of tissue damage or physical trauma. This could have major {{3}} for the treatment of lasting pain, together with the way we prescribe addictive opioids. Recent research has revealed that in some people, chronic pain is a problem with the brain. An injury can lead to pain that {{4}} after the tissue has recovered because the brain has rewired itself and learned to send pain signals, despite there no longer being a reason. Known as central sensitization, it is as if the volume has been turned up on pain.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.acute, 2.enduring, 3.implications, 4.persists', NULL, NULL),
  ('06cf5dfc-9f4b-5422-8c09-f285df8bde2e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06cf5dfc-9f4b-5422-8c09-f285df8bde2e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9ab7b778-b285-53c0-b4b3-7dde03e8029b'::uuid, NULL, E'The company doesn''t typically hire people with no work experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('06cf6982-2705-5626-bae6-44d75d6bab39'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06cf6982-2705-5626-bae6-44d75d6bab39'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the moving stairs that take people from one level of a building to another?', '1e742011-79de-5a03-88de-3e7e8661babd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Escalators', NULL, NULL),
  ('06d1c0b6-fd74-586f-a9f9-9cd3a92ab4f0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06d1c0b6-fd74-586f-a9f9-9cd3a92ab4f0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4aa97213-f3f2-54f4-8641-a95483f63085'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students with work experience may be successful in job applications.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06dc7dc1-e23a-5275-82aa-be9620b51448'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06dc7dc1-e23a-5275-82aa-be9620b51448'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Permissive Parenting', E'Permissive parenting involves being a friend to a child rather than an {{1}} figure. Children are allowed to make their own rules and {{2}} their own activities. Parents are warm and {{3}} but provide little structure for their children. Children may fail to learn self-discipline and may feel somewhat {{4}} because they do not know the limits.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.authority, 2.determine, 3.communicative, 4.insecure', NULL, NULL),
  ('06dcb794-f68b-5601-b84d-b8192304f9b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06dcb794-f68b-5601-b84d-b8192304f9b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'dc2f84d2-b914-5e55-8467-ba5e17549913'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We are looking for new ways to engage learners.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06e47d72-e8a5-59f7-b5b7-5e35e23b8a2b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06e47d72-e8a5-59f7-b5b7-5e35e23b8a2b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1cefa7e4-bb49-53c0-b345-4487626f021a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The study found a strong correlation between its two primary variables.', NULL, NULL),
  ('06e51bdf-ba8f-5698-a2b7-3580e06f6f95'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06e51bdf-ba8f-5698-a2b7-3580e06f6f95'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '85beedad-caf4-5976-ba5f-bd117318593a'::uuid, NULL, E'I wanted to say you''re the most beautiful woman I''ve ever seen.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('06ea8fc1-1c33-5d11-9259-575442d04dd1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '06ea8fc1-1c33-5d11-9259-575442d04dd1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Reindeer Sleep', E'The researchers found that the reindeer brain, like the human brain, knows how {{1}} sleep it needs. They measured the brain activity of four adult female reindeer using electrodes attached to their scalps, and observed their behavior during different seasons and light conditions. They discovered that the reindeer {{2}} the same amount of time asleep regardless of the season, and that their sleep {{3}} were similar to those of humans. However, the reindeer also had a unique ability to sleep while chewing the cud. This state was similar to non-REM sleep, and helped the reindeer reduce their sleepiness after eating. The researchers speculated that this ability might be especially important during the summer, when the reindeer need to eat a lot of food and {{4}} fat for the winter. By sleeping while digesting, the reindeer could balance their need for sleep and nutrition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.much, 2.spent, 3.patterns, 4.accumulate', NULL, NULL),
