  ('07026dc6-d7d8-5fdc-8051-a187ed5b2253'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '07026dc6-d7d8-5fdc-8051-a187ed5b2253'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Transportation System', E'A sustainable transportation system is one in which people''s needs and desires for access to jobs, commerce, recreation, culture and home are accommodated using a minimum of resources. Applying {{1}} of sustainability to transportation will reduce pollution generated by gasoline-powered engines, noise, traffic congestion, land devaluation, urban sprawl, economic segregation, and injury to drivers, pedestrians and cyclists. In addition, the costs of commuting, shipping, housing and goods will be {{2}} . Ultimately in a sustainable San Francisco, almost all trips to and {{3}} the City will be on public transit, foot or bicycle-as will a good part of trips to the larger Bay Region. Walking through streets designed for pedestrians and bicycles will be more pleasant than walking through those designed for the automobile. Street-front retail and commercial establishments will {{4}} from the large volume of foot traffic drawn to an environment enhanced by trees, appropriately designed ''street furniture'' ( street lights, bicycle racks, benches, and the like) and other people. Rents and property costs will be lowered as land for off-street parking is no {{5}} required or needed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.principles, 2.reduced, 3.within, 4.prosper, 5.longer', NULL, NULL),
  ('0709045e-6c15-5c2f-83c7-10988ae3cbaf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0709045e-6c15-5c2f-83c7-10988ae3cbaf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '22d411c5-c346-5c39-83a0-2e0b056133f3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A visit to the designed museum is of great value.', NULL, NULL),
  ('070ce0de-27de-5ea6-95d7-f85653e9d093'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '070ce0de-27de-5ea6-95d7-f85653e9d093'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fb5284f1-772f-55cc-a7ac-0137727de9a2'::uuid, NULL, E'You''ll be able to see the latest fashion and beauty news on this website.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('07147954-594f-55a8-8e34-1899b5379c0b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '07147954-594f-55a8-8e34-1899b5379c0b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Father (B)', E'Every morning, no matter how late he had been up, my father rose at 5:30, went to his study, wrote for a couple of hours, made us all breakfast, read the paper with my mother, and then went back to work for the rest of the morning. Many years passed before I realized that he did this by choice, for a living, and that he was not unemployed or mentally ill.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0715f4dc-8469-5946-8c9d-7f0d9072bd36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0715f4dc-8469-5946-8c9d-7f0d9072bd36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6098e2e3-8858-5ed8-8bc6-1ba189b5cdaf'::uuid, NULL, E'It may be said that the teacher has done his very best to help him.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('07194296-aebe-56c7-b026-6ce763a7e099'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '07194296-aebe-56c7-b026-6ce763a7e099'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the work during the night?', '23278d95-4f45-5593-8d8b-e9855b9c691a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Nightshift / graveyard shift', NULL, NULL),
  ('0719ddf8-0fe7-566e-bf94-f7e76e353cf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0719ddf8-0fe7-566e-bf94-f7e76e353cf7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Four Winds Historical Farm', NULL, '87f79e5c-7d57-5377-862b-9eb1541598f3'::uuid, NULL, E'Welcome to the Four Winds Historical Farm, where traditions of the past are preserved for visitors like you. Today, our master thatchers will begin giving this barn behind me a sturdy thatched roof, able to withstand heavy winds and last up to a hundred years. How do they do it? Well, in a nutshell, thatching involves covering the beams or rafters, the wooden skeleton of a roof with reeds or straw. Our thatchers here have harvested their own natural materials for the job, the bundles of water reeds you see lying over there beside the barn. Thatching is certainly uncommon in the Untied States today. I guess that''s why so many of you have come to see this demonstration. But it wasn''t always that way. In the seventeenth century, the colonists here thatched their roofs with reeds and straw, just as they had done in England. After a while, though, they began to replace the thatch with wooden shingles because wood was so plentiful. And eventually, other roofing materials like stone, slate, and clay tiles came into use. It''s a real shame that most people today don''t realize how strong and long lasting a thatched roof is. In Ireland, where thatching is still practiced, the roofs can survive winds of up to one hundred ten miles per hour. That''s because straw and reeds are so flexible. They bend but don''t break in the wind like other materials can. Another advantage is that the roofs keep the house cool in the summer and warm in the winter. And then, of course, there''s the roofs'' longevity—the average is sixty years, but they can last up to a hundred. With all these reasons to start thatching roofs again, wouldn''t it be wonderful to see this disappearing craft return to popularity?', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0721a578-84d5-5e3c-904d-3971f7414aa3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0721a578-84d5-5e3c-904d-3971f7414aa3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do humans and animals need to inhale for survival?', 'edf96d93-98bb-59d5-99fc-4e850d262864'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Air / oxygen', NULL, NULL),
