  ('07eddaa1-83f1-5caf-af60-d918cdc0aff0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '07eddaa1-83f1-5caf-af60-d918cdc0aff0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c0f8af4a-1b86-5d41-813f-efe563fe8a7e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Academic libraries across the world are steadily incorporating social media.', NULL, NULL),
  ('07f030d0-6a27-5176-8635-68d03cf0dc65'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '07f030d0-6a27-5176-8635-68d03cf0dc65'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Energy Demand', E'As our global population continues to expand, the pressure on our planet''s resources intensifies. A central challenge we face is how to meet the skyrocketing energy demand required to support this growth. This isn''t just about keeping the lights on; it''s about powering every facet of our modern lives. With the population growth, the demand for resources has been growing as well. This creates a complex chain reaction across various sectors.\nThere is an expected increase in demand for various alternative resources, raw materials, timber for paper using, and of course, energy. This surge is understandable. More people need more homes, consumer goods, and packaging, all of which require vast amounts of materials and the energy to produce them. However, the strain is not limited to renewable resources. The increase in demand also happens in the non-renewable resource field, such as metal. These metals are essential for construction, technology, and infrastructure, but their supply is finite. Furthermore, our reliance on fossil fuels remains deeply entrenched. The demand for petrol, diesel and crude oil is also huge to cope with the demand for manufacturing plastics and for powering the global transportation network that moves these goods around the world.\nThis interconnected demand presents a critical dilemma. On one hand, we need these resources to maintain and improve living standards. On the other, their extraction and consumption have significant environmental consequences. This is why a sustainable path forward is crucial. People should ensure the natural world can still work well to ensure future well-being because the world population rises.', NULL, NULL, E'The pressure on our planet''s resources intensifies, and a central challenge is how to meet the skyrocketing energy demand required to support this growth, while there is an expected increase in demand for various alternative resources, which also happens in the non-renewable resource field, so this interconnected demand presents a critical dilemma, meaning that a sustainable path forward is crucial.', NULL, 5, 75),
