  ('08bfa6b7-d2e5-5bed-b3a8-c895a7f658a5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '08bfa6b7-d2e5-5bed-b3a8-c895a7f658a5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Healthy Diet', E'A healthy diet is more effective for keeping fit than exercise. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether a healthy diet is more effective for keeping fit than exercise has sparked considerable controversy and aroused wide public concern. Some people believe that the former outweighs the latter, while others hold that regular exercise is the most effective way to stay fit. In my opinion, both are equally effective when it comes to health, for the following reasons.\nFirst and foremost, nutrition is the foundation of all physiological functions, and a healthy diet provides a wide variety of foods with balanced nutrients. For example, a diet rich in lean proteins, whole grains, and fresh vegetables can supply the body with essential vitamins, minerals, and energy. Therefore, people who stick to a healthy diet can greatly reduce the risk of malnutrition and maintain a stable metabolic rate.\nIn addition, a balanced diet prevents overeating. As is widely acknowledged, excessive calories pose a serious threat to physical health, increasing the risk of obesity, diabetes, heart disease and other illnesses. By controlling portion sizes and avoiding processed foods, individuals can maintain a healthy weight and reduce the strain on their cardiovascular system.\nHowever, calorie consumption is just as important as calorie intake. We cannot achieve good health without regular physical activity, which burns excess fat that would otherwise accumulate in the body. Whether people do aerobic exercises like running and swimming to boost cardiovascular endurance, or anaerobic exercises like weightlifting to build muscle mass, their metabolism can be significantly improved, thus enhancing overall health and fitness.\nTo sum up, I believe that a healthy diet and exercise are equally important for fitness, for the reasons mentioned above. Only by combining both can we achieve optimal health and well-being.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('08bfec90-aec9-556c-b64c-c53d7911c69e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '08bfec90-aec9-556c-b64c-c53d7911c69e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b4cb0eb8-41bc-5990-931e-07ac773c9142'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'If you need more help, the school''s help center is there.', NULL, NULL),
  ('08c333cf-5cac-5b69-868b-ee0bcca8af80'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '08c333cf-5cac-5b69-868b-ee0bcca8af80'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Statistics', E'Statistics is a bit of a mix between mathematics and probability. The point of statistics is to describe processes you can observe out in the world — the height of oak trees or the likelihood a vaccine will work to fend off disease — without having to measure every oak tree in the world or vaccinate every person before deciding how effective a drug is.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
