  ('0986dd8d-8d31-5a92-a710-5ebdef95a580'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0986dd8d-8d31-5a92-a710-5ebdef95a580'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the subjects that are taught in a school or college?', 'f541f144-89e1-54d6-b062-e838f1b75e04'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Curriculum / curricula / curriculums', NULL, NULL),
  ('0988ce60-8b7d-5ea0-86f7-671497ab59c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0988ce60-8b7d-5ea0-86f7-671497ab59c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '80ba7df4-a521-5c47-b847-d3e55055a036'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The study group has reviewed several models for potential use.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0989b49c-e9fc-5c27-b004-a89474da24d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0989b49c-e9fc-5c27-b004-a89474da24d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '993cd91c-4d0e-5a71-86f0-41d93e27ced5'::uuid, NULL, E'The accessible Russell Falls track is the park''s most frequented pathway.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('098bf3f2-0034-51de-8f98-394051d17836'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '098bf3f2-0034-51de-8f98-394051d17836'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Art', E'Many argue that art cannot be defined. We could go about this in several ways. Art is often considered as the process or product of deliberately arranging elements in a way that appeals to the senses or emotions. It encompasses a diverse range of human activities, creations and ways of expression, including music, literature, film, sculpture and paintings. The meaning of art is explored in a branch of philosophy known as aesthetics. At least, that is what Wikipedia claims.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Art is a difficult and complex form to explain.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0990e3ea-8679-56d8-9de8-462865b11e57'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0990e3ea-8679-56d8-9de8-462865b11e57'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Calcium', E'Calcium plays an extremely important role in the production of plant tissues and enables plants to grow better. It is responsible for keeping the cell walls of plants together. It is also crucial in activating signals that coordinate certain cellular activities. Calcium also increases the resistance to external attacks and increases the feed value of forage crops to livestock.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0995b007-0bf3-5602-9aaa-09883bd3aa36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0995b007-0bf3-5602-9aaa-09883bd3aa36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Written Language', E'The world engages in improving literacy of reading and writing, but it is not that important now. What is written language anyway? It''s an ancient technology for storing and retrieving information. We store information by writing it, and we retrieve it by reading it. Six thousand to 10,000 years ago, many of our ancestors'' hunter-gatherer societies settled on the land and began what''s known as the agricultural revolution. That new land settlement led to private property and increased production and trade of goods, generating a huge new influx of information. Unable to keep all this information in their memories, our ancestors created systems of written records that evolved over millennia into today''s written language. But this ancient technology is already becoming obsolete. Text has run its historic course and is now rapidly getting replaced in every area of our lives by the ever-increasing array of emerging technologies driven by voice, video, and body movement rather than the written word. In my view, this is a positive step forward in the evolution of human technology, and it carries great potential for a total positive redesign of education.', NULL, NULL, E'Written language is an ancient technology for storing and retrieving information, while we store information by writing it, and we retrieve it by reading it, where text has run its historic course and is now rapidly getting replaced in every area of our lives, so this is a positive step forward in the evolution of human technology, and it carries great potential for a total positive redesign of education.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('0998e162-9fee-58c5-b69e-6cbf93bf293f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0998e162-9fee-58c5-b69e-6cbf93bf293f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2c48073e-b2a9-5715-956e-66c3029ad8ab'::uuid, NULL, E'He was at the clinic recovering from an operation on his arm.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('09ad9316-fc0b-5e97-bd3f-92db0d3d1123'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09ad9316-fc0b-5e97-bd3f-92db0d3d1123'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fe466e06-dec0-5db5-b7cc-d33209bc0cf0'::uuid, NULL, E'After I graduated from college, I spent two years travelling around the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('09b59d3e-9589-57b6-bf4a-69d01f9bdf23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09b59d3e-9589-57b6-bf4a-69d01f9bdf23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c91c9eec-ccba-56df-b72f-c2db76892cc4'::uuid, NULL, E'It is quite clear that the rising prosperity does not make people feel more content.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('09b948d3-eb91-51a2-a3fa-1d13896bb517'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09b948d3-eb91-51a2-a3fa-1d13896bb517'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mind-Gut Connection', E'The intricate relationship between the gut and the brain, often termed the "gut-brain axis," has emerged as a fascinating area in medical and psychological research. This connection suggests that the state of our digestive system can have a profound impact on our mental health, shedding light on the interplay between diet, digestion, and psychological well-being.\nCentral to this connection is the microbiome, the vast community of microorganisms living in our intestines. These microbes not only aid in digestion but also produce neurotransmitters and other chemicals that can affect mood and cognition. For instance, a significant portion of the body’s serotonin, a key neurotransmitter involved in mood regulation, is produced in the gut.\nRecent studies have shown that alterations in gut microbiota can be linked to various psychological conditions, including anxiety, depression, and stress. For example, certain probiotics, known as "psychobiotics," have been found to potentially alleviate symptoms of depression and anxiety by influencing the gut-brain axis.\nDiet plays a crucial role in shaping our gut microbiome. Foods rich in fiber, probiotics, and omega-3 fatty acids can promote a healthy gut, potentially leading to improved mental health. Conversely, a diet high in processed and high-sugar foods can negatively impact the microbiome, potentially exacerbating psychological issues.\nThe gut-brain axis also highlights the importance of a holistic approach to health. Stress management, exercise, and a balanced diet are not only beneficial for physical health but also for maintaining a healthy mind-gut relationship.\nIn conclusion, the mind-gut connection opens a new realm in understanding mental health, emphasizing the role of the gut microbiome in psychological well-being. This emerging field underscores the need for integrated approaches in treating mental health disorders, considering both psychological and physiological factors.', NULL, NULL, E'The gut-brain axis reveals a critical link between our gut microbiome and mental health, indicating that gut health, influenced by diet and lifestyle, plays a significant role in conditions like anxiety and depression, and underscores the importance of a holistic approach to psychological well-being.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('09bbb7c2-c36f-578b-b1e7-738909cc7275'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09bbb7c2-c36f-578b-b1e7-738909cc7275'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we describe the space with no air in it?', '3caac8a0-0fed-5abc-8759-6d18c7898ed0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Vacuum', NULL, NULL),
  ('09c788b1-0f6e-5b3f-837b-6c0a3215f2f2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09c788b1-0f6e-5b3f-837b-6c0a3215f2f2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ambulances', E'Ambulances come in a variety of vehicle types and configurations, according to Dr. Ben Weston, an assistant professor at Medical College of Wisconsin. There''s the familiar minivan style, but other ambulances have a pickup-truck chassis with an attached patient compartment. Inside, ambulances carry an assortment of lifesaving equipment. They carry portable oxygen supplies and masks, cervical collars, slings, backboards to protect patients with spinal injuries, and kits with towels, dressings, scissors, clamps and sterile gloves to use in delivering babies. Among other equipment, they''re also equipped with disinfectant, shoe covers, coveralls and other gear for controlling exposure to infections. One of the most important — and costly — pieces of equipment on an ambulance is the heart monitor. "It''s one of the essentials," Buchle says. The device is capable of doing an electrocardiogram (EKG), and also transmitting the readings via wireless modem to a doctor at the hospital while they are in route. Additionally, the device can check oxygen levels and blood pressure, and even act as a pacemaker for patients whose hearts need such assistance. Ambulances also carry supplies of medications, with state regulations determining what they''re allowed to have. Ambulances can carry an extensive assortment of drugs, from various cardiac medications and drugs to treat patients who''ve suffered allergic reactions or asthma attacks. There also are various pain medications, ranging from aspirin to fentanyl. Another useful piece of equipment on ambulances these days is a laptop computer, which crews can use to receive detailed information from the 911 dispatcher. That enables them to be better prepared when they arrive on the scene.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('09c9c529-3853-5eda-81ee-448074fd42b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09c9c529-3853-5eda-81ee-448074fd42b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'UBI', E'Universal basic income (UBI) has become more popular as a way to {{1}} economic inequality. UBI entails {{2}} every citizen a regular, unconditional payment to provide a financial safety net and {{3}} the economy. While some see it as a way to address poverty and job displacement, others worry about its cost and potential disincentives to work, {{4}} a contentious debate in economics and politics.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.tackle, 2.giving, 3.boost, 4.sparking', NULL, NULL),
  ('09cb30b2-faf7-5512-a6d3-64e4b7299305'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09cb30b2-faf7-5512-a6d3-64e4b7299305'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'cd2c6613-8b44-5dd4-a74e-e141f986fb25'::uuid, NULL, E'Interpreters are not readily available in this department.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('09d33753-c947-5c93-942a-f4d149c8a061'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09d33753-c947-5c93-942a-f4d149c8a061'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('09d33ef0-60ca-599f-b074-323604ad12a5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09d33ef0-60ca-599f-b074-323604ad12a5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '367e888e-5907-5724-8aa6-d8b915aa0044'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'‌Computers are a great source of knowledge for students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('09da1fea-e982-5a1f-a157-83f101f227f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09da1fea-e982-5a1f-a157-83f101f227f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Navajo Nation', E'The Navajo Nation, one of the largest indigenous tribes in the United States, possesses a wealth of traditional ecological knowledge that has proven instrumental in addressing contemporary environmental challenges. Recent research has highlighted the significance of this indigenous wisdom in promoting sustainable practices and preserving the environment.\nThe Navajo people have inhabited the southwestern United States for centuries and have developed a deep understanding of their natural surroundings. This knowledge encompasses sustainable land management, water conservation, and the utilization of native plants for medicinal and cultural purposes.\nIn recent years, the Navajo Nation has faced environmental challenges, including droughts and the impacts of climate change. The tribe''s traditional ecological knowledge has become an invaluable resource in responding to these challenges. For instance, the Navajo people''s historical practices of water harvesting and efficient crop cultivation have been adapted to mitigate the effects of prolonged droughts.\nFurthermore, the Navajo Nation''s emphasis on the use of native plants in traditional ceremonies and healing practices aligns with modern efforts to protect biodiversity and promote the use of indigenous flora in sustainable agriculture and medicine.\nIncorporating traditional ecological knowledge into contemporary environmental initiatives not only benefits the Navajo people but also contributes to broader conservation efforts. It showcases the importance of indigenous perspectives in tackling complex environmental issues and reinforces the idea that cultural heritage and sustainable environmental practices can go hand in hand.\nIn conclusion, the traditional ecological knowledge of the Navajo Nation serves as a model for the integration of indigenous wisdom into modern environmental conservation efforts. It demonstrates how honoring and preserving cultural heritage can lead to innovative and sustainable solutions for protecting the environment, benefitting not only the Navajo people but the world at large.', NULL, NULL, E'The Navajo Nation''s traditional ecological knowledge, honed over centuries in the southwestern United States, has become crucial in addressing modern environmental challenges like droughts and climate change; their practices in sustainable land management, water conservation, and use of native plants for medicinal and cultural purposes offer valuable insights into promoting biodiversity and sustainable agriculture.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('09dc5deb-0059-5866-bb00-a691b1dfb721'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09dc5deb-0059-5866-bb00-a691b1dfb721'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lithium', E'The lightest of any solid element, lithium has, until now, played a {{1}} role in industry. Silvery in color, and softer than lead, it has been used mainly as an alloy of aluminum, a base for automobile grease, and in the {{2}} of glass and ceramics. It is so {{3}} that it is never found in its pure form in nature. Lithium floats on water — or, {{4}} , it skitters wildly about, trailing a vapor cloud of hydrogen, {{5}} it dissolves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.modest, 2.production, 3.unstable, 4.rather, 5.until', NULL, NULL),
  ('09e34000-95b0-5f9e-bf10-39596a6b133d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09e34000-95b0-5f9e-bf10-39596a6b133d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c33e655b-2f2e-5088-bffd-48734c8317df'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Science is found everywhere in society today.', NULL, NULL),
  ('09f1d93b-3499-5a66-9eec-233425d3c485'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09f1d93b-3499-5a66-9eec-233425d3c485'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '33ecae1f-71c6-54a2-bfb4-9761232a630e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We are looking at introducing new methods that are both practical and engaging.', NULL, NULL),
  ('09f47f2c-5680-50ba-98c4-ec387f33b1ed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09f47f2c-5680-50ba-98c4-ec387f33b1ed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Architectural Museum', E'The Edo-Tokyo Tatemono En is an open-air architectural museum, but could be better thought of as a park. Thirty buildings from the 19th and early 20th centuries from {{1}} around Tokyo were restored and relocated to the space, where they can be explored by future generations to come. The buildings are a collection of houses and businesses, shops, and bathhouses, all of which would have been present on a typical middle-class street from Edo-period to Showa-era Tokyo. The west section is {{2}} , with traditional thatched roof bungalows of the 19th century. Meiji-era houses are also on view, constructed in a more Westernstyle after Japan opened its borders in 1868. The Musashino Sabo Cafe occupies the {{3}} floor of one such house, where visitors can enjoy a cup of tea. Grand residences like that of Korekiyo Takahashi, an early 20th century politician assassinated over his controversial policies, demonstrate how the upper class lived during that time period. The east section is primarily businesses from the 1920s and 30s, preserved with their wares on display. Visitors are free {{4}} through a kitchenware shop, a florist’s, an umbrella store, a bar, a soy sauce shop, a tailor’s, a cosmetics shop, and an inn complete with an operational noodle shop .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.all, 2.residential, 3.ground, 4.to wander', NULL, NULL),
  ('09fdfeeb-021f-54a1-862a-7ce27420c3d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '09fdfeeb-021f-54a1-862a-7ce27420c3d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Top Executives Short(高管寿命变短)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 2, 3, 5, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a002589-ad01-5cd8-b129-500aad1998d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a002589-ad01-5cd8-b129-500aad1998d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'8,000 Steps', E'An international study led by the University of Granada (UGR) has provided the first scientific proof for how many steps you need to take per day to significantly reduce the risk of premature death: 8,000. Given the average length of a human stride (76 centimeters for men and 67 centimeters for women), taking 8,000 steps is equivalent to walking approximately 6.4 kilometers a day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a0269ee-582f-5bfc-8739-0e37ebd24795'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a0269ee-582f-5bfc-8739-0e37ebd24795'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which literary genre describes all details of a famous person''s life?', '55c05790-70b0-56ca-a20c-dc435d0606c5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Biography / autobiography', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a0a4bd4-0fff-59c4-962c-5d3d10f5c526'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a0a4bd4-0fff-59c4-962c-5d3d10f5c526'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Studying Abroad', E'It is often argued that studying overseas is overrated. There are many scholars who study locally. To what extent do you agree with this?', NULL, NULL, E'Studying overseas has long been considered a hallmark of academic excellence and personal growth. However, in recent years, there has been a growing debate on whether studying overseas is overrated. While some may argue that studying locally is equally beneficial, I believe that studying overseas provides students with unique opportunities and experiences that cannot be replicated in a local setting.\nFirstly, studying overseas exposes students to different cultures and ways of thinking. Being immersed in a foreign environment allows students to gain a deeper understanding of different perspectives and worldviews. This can broaden their horizons and help them develop a more nuanced and empathetic approach to problem-solving. Moreover, studying overseas can enhance language skills and employability. In today''s globalized economy, being multilingual and having cross-cultural competencies are highly valued by employers.\nSecondly, studying overseas can lead to personal growth and development. Living in a foreign country can be challenging, but it also offers opportunities for self-discovery and personal transformation. Students who study overseas often become more independent, resilient, and adaptable. They learn to navigate unfamiliar environments and develop a sense of self-reliance that can serve them well in their personal and professional lives.\nIn conclusion, while some may argue that studying locally is equally beneficial, I believe that studying overseas provides students with unique opportunities and experiences that cannot be replicated in a local setting. Therefore, I encourage students to consider studying overseas as an enriching and transformative experience that can shape their lives in profound ways.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0a0ba169-0670-5f5d-8a3c-f7e6fb2a4255'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a0ba169-0670-5f5d-8a3c-f7e6fb2a4255'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Marketing', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 3, 1, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a0d6b24-9562-5267-a0cf-f7ef4f3ca439'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a0d6b24-9562-5267-a0cf-f7ef4f3ca439'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Disabled People and Technology', E'The use of technologies for the inclusion and empowerment of persons with disabilities is not new — from the creation of Braille and the first hearing aid to the invention of the wheelchair. For disabled persons, new assistive technology can make all the difference, while technology and innovation are breaking down the barriers to achieving full participation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a0e599d-b549-5506-9c3a-429f9176a23b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a0e599d-b549-5506-9c3a-429f9176a23b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Passionate Individuals', E'When someone is passionate about what they do, they are more likely to invest time and effort into mastering their craft and pushing the boundaries of their potential. Passionate individuals often inspire others with their dedication and unwavering commitment. Passion has the power to transform our lives and make a positive impact on the world around us.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
