  ('0a649980-1584-5f30-9961-ffa1e4b5e84a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a649980-1584-5f30-9961-ffa1e4b5e84a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for a piece of land surrounded by water?', 'a6aa5557-8eea-5a10-be5a-6f36c773784c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Island', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a67981c-eae2-5bbd-b385-d2073b312372'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a67981c-eae2-5bbd-b385-d2073b312372'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call an opening or a door in the deck of a ship or the bottom of an aircraft, through which goods to be carried are passed?', '70f5abc8-ba67-59ee-a33f-54e91ad26f06'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hatch / hatchway / trap door / trapdoor', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a692a64-5675-55a0-8d96-d1ccd4df82c7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a692a64-5675-55a0-8d96-d1ccd4df82c7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '90f8861c-faeb-58ff-bd9c-d22caa533e28'::uuid, NULL, E'The students have been asked to comment on their peers'' work.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a6a580e-bf03-5352-9c3e-db47c21b2024'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a6a580e-bf03-5352-9c3e-db47c21b2024'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c2c1cea7-c143-585c-8118-d5e9cdf1db86'::uuid, NULL, E'This session is not supported by documentation.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a6f9514-f1dc-5ee5-bffe-a3caf189c52f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a6f9514-f1dc-5ee5-bffe-a3caf189c52f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lewis', E'C. S. Lewis, or Jack Lewis, as he preferred to be called, was born in Belfast, Ireland (now Northern Ireland) on November 29,1898. He was the second son of Albert Lewis, a lawyer, and Flora Hamilton Lewis. His older brother, Warren Hamilton Lewis, who was known as Warnie, had been born three years {{1}} in 1895. Lewis'' s early childhood was relatively happy and carefree. In those days Northern Ireland was not yet {{2}} by bitter civil strife, and the Lewis'' were comfortably off. The family home, called Little Lea, was a large, gabled house with dark, narrow passages and an overgrown garden, which Warnie and Jack played in and {{3}} together. There was also a library that was crammed with books -- two of Jack'' s favorites were Treasure Island by Robert Louis Stevenson and The Secret Garden by Frances Hodgson Burnett. This somewhat idyllic boyhood came to an end for Lewis when his mother became ill and died of cancer in 1908. Barely a month after her death the two boys were sent away from home to go to boarding school in England. Lewis hated the school with its strict rules and hard {{4}} headmaster, and he missed Belfast terribly. Fortunately for him, the school closed in 1910, and he was able to return to Ireland. After a year, however, he was sent back to England to study this time, the {{5}} proved to be mostly positive. As a teenager, Lewis learned to love poetry, especially the works of Virgil and Homer. He also developed an interest in modern languages, mastering French, German, and Italian.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.earlier, 2.plagued, 3.explored, 4.unsympathetic, 5.experience', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a6fd6d1-168a-5236-b5ef-f5b1dc4c376c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a6fd6d1-168a-5236-b5ef-f5b1dc4c376c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which U.S. state is known as the ''Sunshine State''?', '43502206-ec86-5125-ad7e-418158779e53'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Florida', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a735e03-b293-57b4-89c6-8284d3215d22'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a735e03-b293-57b4-89c6-8284d3215d22'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '601c82ea-0b8e-5987-b6fa-8372cb39a8a1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Children need books in their own language with settings that reflect their lives.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a77594d-0923-5c73-9a46-342c827756ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a77594d-0923-5c73-9a46-342c827756ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dinosaurs', E'What killed off the dinosaurs? The end of the Cretaceous Period saw one of the most dramatic mass extinctions the Earth has ever seen. The fossil record shows that throughout their 160-million-year {{1}} , dinosaurs took on a huge variety of forms as the environment changed and new species evolved that were suited to these new conditions. Others that failed to adapt {{2}} extinct. But then 66 million years ago, over a relatively short time, dinosaurs disappeared {{3}} (except for birds). Many other animals also died out, including pterosaurs, large marine reptiles, and other sea creatures such as ammonites. {{4}} the number of dinosaur species was already declining, this suggests a sudden catastrophic event sealed their fate, causing unfavorable changes to the environment more quickly than dinosaurs and other creatures could adapt. The exact nature of this catastrophic event is still {{5}} to scientific debate. The catastrophe could have been an asteroid impact, volcanic eruptions or the effect of both, together with more {{6}} changes in the Earth''s climate over millions of years. Whatever the causes, the huge extinction that ended the age of the dinosaur left gaps in the ecosystem that were subsequently filled by mammals and birds, allowing them to evolve rapidly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.existence, 2.went, 3.completely, 4.Although, 5.open, 6.gradual', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a79484a-c4d1-5b4c-b6a8-23a609fd82b0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a79484a-c4d1-5b4c-b6a8-23a609fd82b0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Single Research', E'Rarely, however, does a single research study produce the certainty needed to assume that the same results will apply in all or most settings. Rather, research is usually an ongoing process, based on many accumulated understandings and explanations that, when taken together, lead to a generalization about educational issues and practice, and ultimately, to the development of theories.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a795020-271b-5ab9-a9e7-48b5d68c025c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a795020-271b-5ab9-a9e7-48b5d68c025c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Listening Skills', NULL, 'a91032d2-1ef3-572d-abad-14fca365de34'::uuid, NULL, E'The most important factor in communicating more effectively is actually the opposite of talking. It’s improving your listening skills. You must learn to start asking questions and listen attentively without interruptions. As a rule you pay attention to people you most value. When you pay close attention to another person when they are talking, you signal to that person that you very much value them and the content of their comments. This is very flattering to another person and it causes them to respond warmly to your attentiveness. The major reason that most people have poor listening skills is that they’re busy preparing a reply while the other person is still speaking. In fact, they’re not even listening closely to what the other person is saying. They are thinking of other things and formulating their comments to be ready as soon as the other person takes a breath. Effective communication requires that you face the other person directly, lean slightly forward and hang on to every word, listen as though there were nothing else in the world more fascinating to you than what the other person is saying.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a7c8bd0-34d9-54f8-a853-cda80bf7a5b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a7c8bd0-34d9-54f8-a853-cda80bf7a5b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1198035d-aa3c-541e-8068-78d06e6edb85'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'These college lectures are available only for certain students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a81aa97-bcd7-5d14-a0e1-e8f23afe2817'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a81aa97-bcd7-5d14-a0e1-e8f23afe2817'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indian Tribes', NULL, 'a649a3ef-281d-5a3f-9cad-532629356c12'::uuid, NULL, E'I understand your professor has been discussing several Eastern Woodland Indian tribes in your study of Native American cultures. As you have probably learned, the Eastern Woodland Indians get their name from the forest-covered areas of the Eastern United States where they lived. The earliest Woodland cultures date back 9,000 years, but the group we''ll focus on dates back only to about 700 A.D.. We now call these Native Americans the Mississippian culture, because they settled in the Mississippi River valley. This civilization is known for its flat-topped monuments called temple mounds. They were made of earth and used as temples and official residences. The temple mounds were located in the central square of the city, with the huts of the townspeople built in rows around the plaza. The Mississippian people were city dwellers. But some city residents earned their living as farmers, tending the fields of corn, beans, and squash that surrounded the city. The city''s artisans made arrowheads, leather goods, pottery, and jewelry. Traders came from far away to exchange raw materials for these items. In the slides I''m about to show, you will see models of a Mississippian city.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a856052-bfb9-5650-9703-5b793219e75e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a856052-bfb9-5650-9703-5b793219e75e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Side Effects', E'Where there are effects, there are often side effects. The car is a boon to mobility, but can lead to obesity, deaths and pollution. Burning fossil fuel may keep economies going but wreck the climate in the long run. In a similar way, there are side effects to information technology in education setting - from childcare to the classroom to the lecture hall and beyond.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0a88986e-b2d5-576b-8728-a1d42a164e24'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a88986e-b2d5-576b-8728-a1d42a164e24'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Longer Live', E'In general, people are living longer now. List some causes of this phenomenon.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0a9c3c0e-f350-5d57-b40a-e1eb43ddd789'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a9c3c0e-f350-5d57-b40a-e1eb43ddd789'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How many days are there in one year?', 'a812a67c-8723-5ae8-b900-dfecb38ef8c6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Three hundred and sixty-five', NULL, NULL),
  ('0a9cf5eb-605e-5ace-b35c-16b58adf6e1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0a9cf5eb-605e-5ace-b35c-16b58adf6e1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Customer Demand', E'It originally referred to the production of goods to meet customer {{1}} exactly in time, quality and quantity, {{2}} the ‘customer’ is the final purchaser of the product or another process {{3}} along the production line.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.demand, 2.whether, 3.further', NULL, NULL),
  ('0aa25eec-a126-543c-a52c-a0cce6a53857'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0aa25eec-a126-543c-a52c-a0cce6a53857'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '64caa4f7-c47f-52d6-a54b-47ac55640229'::uuid, NULL, E'I will have a meeting on Thursday.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0aab86b7-f608-5b37-8488-1c55c5a4ac77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0aab86b7-f608-5b37-8488-1c55c5a4ac77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '42e914d0-ae48-5eb4-a020-f2cd30c9067c'::uuid, NULL, E'Your aim is to recognize the impact of gender in all academic disciplines.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0aad2959-a657-5630-985b-1dfbd84573d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0aad2959-a657-5630-985b-1dfbd84573d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the tax that government collects on goods coming into a country?', '31c89a27-0fcf-5ee7-b7d6-da2e0366f169'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tariff / customs / duty', NULL, NULL),
  ('0aadc3e9-efcc-5ba3-bb3e-358a9ebd63cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0aadc3e9-efcc-5ba3-bb3e-358a9ebd63cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Health and Fitness', E'A renewed interest in well-being, especially among baby boomers, as well as rising personal incomes, led to more spending on health and fitness in 2005. This prompted an {{1}} in the number of fitness and recreation centres across the country. Golf courses also {{2}} renewed success, as the sport increased in popularity, possibly the result of retiring baby boomers heading to the links. In 2005, {{3}} spent an average $3,918 on recreation, up slightly from $3,678 in 2004. Items included in the 2005 figure are: an average $166 on sports and athletic equipment; $665 to buy and {{4}} recreational vehicles such as snowmobiles, bicycles and trailers; and $299 for the use of sports and recreation facilities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.expansion, 2.enjoyed, 3.households, 4.operate', NULL, NULL),
  ('0aaf3c16-e4da-5d22-82b5-37368bcff7e5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0aaf3c16-e4da-5d22-82b5-37368bcff7e5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Massive Asteroid', E'About 66 million years ago, a massive asteroid slammed into the Gulf of Mexico. Not long afterward, all non-bird dinosaurs died as did many other species on land and in the sea. Scientists don’t know the exact year this took place, but they now think they have figured out in what season it occurred: spring.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ab43f87-a114-592d-9211-fe5c65fca4bd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ab43f87-a114-592d-9211-fe5c65fca4bd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Laws', E'What is your opinion on the necessity of space laws and governance?', NULL, NULL, E'The necessity of space laws and governance in the realm of space exploration cannot be overstated. These frameworks are essential for fostering cooperation, regulating activities, and safeguarding celestial resources in the increasingly crowded domain of outer space.\nSpace laws serve as the cornerstone for promoting peaceful cooperation among nations engaged in space exploration endeavors. By establishing clear guidelines and protocols, these laws facilitate collaboration and prevent conflicts that may arise from competing interests in space activities. The framework provided by space laws encourages unity and shared objectives in exploring the vast expanse beyond Earth''s atmosphere.\nGovernance mechanisms play a pivotal role in regulating space activities to mitigate the risks of space debris and collisions. Through effective governance, authorities can implement measures to track and manage space debris, minimizing the threat it poses to operational satellites and spacecraft. Additionally, legal frameworks ensure the protection of celestial resources, such as minerals and water on celestial bodies, promoting sustainable and responsible exploration practices that prioritize conservation and preservation.\nIn conclusion, the necessity of space laws and governance is paramount in shaping the future of space exploration. By ensuring peaceful cooperation, regulating activities to prevent hazards, and protecting celestial resources, these frameworks lay the foundation for a sustainable and harmonious approach to exploring the vast unknowns of outer space. Embracing and enforcing robust space laws and governance structures is essential for advancing humanity''s exploration efforts while preserving the integrity of the cosmic environment for generations to come.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0ab766ef-3bd3-5db3-ac70-51ec3c5a3fa0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ab766ef-3bd3-5db3-ac70-51ec3c5a3fa0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Scientists'' Work', E'Scientists make observations, have assumptions, and do {{1}} . After these have been done, they get their {{2}} . Then there is a lot of {{3}} from scientists. The scientists around the world have a {{4}} of the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.experiments, 2.results, 3.data, 4.picture', NULL, NULL),
  ('0ab8bbf0-b20d-5d76-a371-7718e9e8dc09'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ab8bbf0-b20d-5d76-a371-7718e9e8dc09'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '59144833-e3ea-53c2-9574-b3ebeda0e5a8'::uuid, NULL, E'Next time, we''ll discuss the impact of media on shaping public policy.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
