  ('0b50ba66-5b5a-5a65-b75f-6f233c0f51cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b50ba66-5b5a-5a65-b75f-6f233c0f51cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7f980bbf-9832-5fa7-a25a-225f5347fb28'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'When you do research, it''s best to not have too much info.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b518c02-7ea8-5913-bd34-da1d266463cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b518c02-7ea8-5913-bd34-da1d266463cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Classical Music', E'Classical music competitions pit performers against each other. Obviously, the most important {{1}} for judges is sound. But that assumption needs a new...hearing. Because a player''s passion may be the best predictor of victory.\nIn a new study, nearly 200 novices had to choose the winners of 10 classical music competitions. Some heard a music clip of the top three {{2}} . Others saw a video with sound. Still others watched a silent video. And the participants were more likely to choose the winner if they watched the silent video, in all 10 of the competitions.\nThen {{3}} musicians gave it a try. These judges also only reliably selected the winners from the silent video. Musicians selected the winner more frequently even when all they saw was an outline of the motion of the performers.\nThe researchers say the {{4}} show that novices and experts make quick {{5}} about musical performances based on visual cues conveying involvement and passion. The study was published in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.\nSo next time you see a live concert, don''t close your eyes to focus on the music. You might be missing the most important part.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.criterion, 2.performances, 3.professional, 4.findings, 5.judgments', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b54c445-7b8f-50f6-b8ba-2b85b7e2b5b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b54c445-7b8f-50f6-b8ba-2b85b7e2b5b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which kind of vehicle can fly through the air?', '7cc60942-c0c7-5914-b623-1f862b432147'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Airplane / aeroplane / plane', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b551bc9-b622-520c-8bfd-1355ebb1435a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b551bc9-b622-520c-8bfd-1355ebb1435a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marshmallow', E'They call it the "marshmallow test." A four- to-six-year-old-child sits alone in a room at a table facing a marshmallow on a plate. The child is told: "If you don''t eat this {{1}} for 15 minutes you can have both it and a second one." Kids on average wait for five or six minutes before eating the marshmallow. The {{2}} a child can resist the temptation has been correlated with higher general competency later in life.\nNow a study shows that ability to resist temptation isn''t strictly {{3}} -- it''s aIso highly influenced by environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.treat, 2.longer, 3.innate', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b56c26c-9245-578a-9a06-148d8cbe3f44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b56c26c-9245-578a-9a06-148d8cbe3f44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Frost''s Poetry', E'There''s duplicity in Frost''s poetry, and there''s a certain doubleness in the figure that he {{1}} as a poet. I like to think of his obsession with {{2}} meanings, which he has, as a way of responding to a division in culture, between popular and elite readers, a division that he saw as {{3}} of a division in American culture between money and esteem, business and art.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.projects, 2.double, 3.expressive', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b59db22-277b-517c-9505-e71dd43e2828'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b59db22-277b-517c-9505-e71dd43e2828'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bb06d011-14d5-5b60-9600-bce16f8f83d9'::uuid, NULL, E'He was not the only one to call for legal reform in the sixteenth century.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0b5e0a9a-9460-51e1-a06c-5da2917ce8a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b5e0a9a-9460-51e1-a06c-5da2917ce8a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '28a45d85-e277-554e-80e0-685648e15399'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Today''s class will show you different ways to show data clearly.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b5e8143-ac5c-5118-9efa-70952cb766a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b5e8143-ac5c-5118-9efa-70952cb766a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c88c2ddd-7e56-5fae-a17e-83cf815fb347'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'An undergraduate is required to do many projects.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b64b8d1-0466-52e2-96d7-9e4731746ea6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b64b8d1-0466-52e2-96d7-9e4731746ea6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Seasons', E'Day and night provide the basic {{1}} of human existence. The seasons {{2}} the migration of animals upon which humans have depended for millennia for survival. With the invention of agriculture, the seasons became even more crucial, for {{3}} to recognize the proper time for planting could lead to starvation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.rhythm, 2.determine, 3.failure', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b678e5c-1cdc-59f4-87e3-35849e0e197f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b678e5c-1cdc-59f4-87e3-35849e0e197f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fb444643-4405-5f56-9e5a-e86da9acaf23'::uuid, NULL, E'The new hypothesis needs to be tested with a controlled experiment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0b686ce8-3b59-533a-967e-ea369a976ccb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b686ce8-3b59-533a-967e-ea369a976ccb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Allergies', E'What are allergies? Allergies are abnormal immune system reactions to things that are typically harmless to most people. When you''re allergic to something, your immune system {{1}} believes that this substance is harmful to your body. Substances that cause allergic reactions- such as certain foods, dust, plant pollen, or medicines- are known as allergens. In an attempt to {{2}} the body, the immune system produces IgE antibodies to that allergen. Those antibodies then cause certain cells in the body to {{3}} chemicals into the bloodstream, one of which is histamine (pronounced: HIS-tuh-meen). The histamine then {{4}} on the eyes, nose, throat, lungs, skin, or gastrointestinal tract and causes the symptoms of the allergic reaction. Future exposure to that same allergen will trigger this {{5}} response again. This means that every time you come into contact with that allergen, you''ll have some form of allergy symptoms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.mistakenly, 2.protect, 3.release, 4.acts, 5.antibody', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b689a75-1c63-536b-ad46-100bacaaecd9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b689a75-1c63-536b-ad46-100bacaaecd9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Era of Mayan', E'The Classic Era of Mayan came to an end around 900 AD. Why this happened is unclear; the cities were probably over-farming the land, so that a period of drought led to famine. Recent geological research supports this, as there appears to have been a 200-year drought around this time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0b701582-05f2-56bc-85a1-202f4ff56f68'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b701582-05f2-56bc-85a1-202f4ff56f68'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the measure of the average kinetic energy of the particles in a system?', '3e55793d-fa05-5ea3-ba87-d9c88b77a856'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Temperature', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b70b1b0-50a0-59c6-b386-832dc39e632f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b70b1b0-50a0-59c6-b386-832dc39e632f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Endangered Languages', E'Do you think that it is necessary to preserve endangered languages?', NULL, NULL, E'The preservation of endangered languages is a topic of significant debate in the realm of cultural conservation. While some may question the necessity of safeguarding these linguistic treasures, the retention of endangered languages holds profound implications for cultural diversity, knowledge preservation, and community unity.\nPreserving endangered languages plays a pivotal role in maintaining cultural diversity and heritage. These languages serve as unique repositories of traditions, beliefs, and stories that are integral to the identities of communities. By safeguarding endangered languages, we ensure that the rich tapestry of human culture remains vibrant and diverse, fostering a deeper appreciation for the richness of our collective heritage.\nEndangered languages encapsulate unique knowledge systems and perspectives on the world that are often not found in dominant languages. These linguistic treasures offer insights into local ecosystems, traditional practices, and indigenous wisdom that contribute to our understanding of the world. The preservation of endangered languages is essential for safeguarding this invaluable knowledge for future generations.\nIn conclusion, the preservation of endangered languages is not merely about linguistic conservation but about upholding cultural identities, preserving unique knowledge, and fostering community bonds. By recognizing the significance of endangered languages in maintaining cultural diversity, sharing diverse perspectives, and promoting intergenerational communication, we can appreciate the vital role these languages play in enriching the tapestry of human civilization. Therefore, it is imperative to prioritize the preservation of endangered languages to ensure the continuity of cultural heritage and the celebration of linguistic diversity.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0b723880-4796-55c5-81d9-20cdf9b95dab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b723880-4796-55c5-81d9-20cdf9b95dab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3635e075-d78d-5a72-be16-0dbc4f0be5be'::uuid, NULL, E'It is of the utmost importance that you follow the ethical guidelines carefully.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0b7262f8-165c-5331-9879-64820d3e456a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b7262f8-165c-5331-9879-64820d3e456a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Number and Form', E'Number and form are the essence of our world: from the patterns of the stars to the pulses of the market, from {{1}} beats of our hearts to catching a ball or tying our shoelaces. Drawing on science, literature, history and philosophy, and introducing {{2}} from Alcibiades to Gauss, this {{3}} book makes the mysteries of maths accessible and its rich {{4}} brilliantly clear.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.the, 2.geniuses, 3.inspiring, 4.patterns', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b7eace9-6ba9-5967-89fb-2e8003c1a5c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b7eace9-6ba9-5967-89fb-2e8003c1a5c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Guide Stick', E'Foldable white canes help the {{1}} impaired navigate their surroundings. But the guide stick''s tactile nature offers only so much information. The cane''s user must manually find and avoid obstructions. But new high-tech canes are on the horizon.\nLast year researchers in India tried to fill in some of the missing info with their experimental SmartCane. The device uses an attached ultrasonic transmitter and a sensor that vibrates the cane to warn its users when an obstacle is within three meters.\nStudents at the U.K.''s Birmingham City University are developing a cane that can even identify acquaintances as they {{4}} . Called the ''XploR'' mobility cane, it includes an {{5}} digital camera that analyzes the faces of people walking by and compares their images against a database stored on a memory card in the cane''s handle.\nIf there''s a facial recognition match, the cane alerts the user''s {{6}} via Bluetooth. The phone then identifies the approaching person to the user via its speaker or earbuds. The {{7}} are building a prototype they''ll test later this year.\nThe hurdles are significant: facial recognition is a tough problem, especially outdoors. But if the XploR works, it could actually give the visually impaired a leg up on everyone else — especially those of us who never remember people''s names.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.visually, 2.approach, 3.embedded, 4.smartphone, 5.students', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b8caf47-37c5-5e8a-9a55-1305b9d5b231'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b8caf47-37c5-5e8a-9a55-1305b9d5b231'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Identities', E'To comprehend how individuals {{1}} their digital identities, researchers sift through millions of social media posts. Selfies often serve as a medium for expressing and exploring identity online. A substantial {{2}} of these images focus on appearance, {{3}} other categories in frequency. Such online behavior reflects a broader phenomenon where individuals meticulously curate their digital presence, {{4}} the sentiment that in the virtual world, we are all performers on a global stage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.construct, 2.portion, 3.surpassing, 4.echoing', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b904620-c756-5d25-8440-8319db107885'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b904620-c756-5d25-8440-8319db107885'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Smartphone-based Treatments', E'Computer- and smartphone-based treatments appear to be effective in reducing symptoms of depression, and while it remains unclear whether they are as effective as face-to-face psychotherapy, they offer a promising alternative to address the growing mental health needs spawned by the COVID-19 pandemic.\n"The year 2020 marked 30 years since the first paper was published on a digital intervention for the treatment of depression. It also marked an unparalleled inflection point in the worldwide conversion of mental health services from face-to-face delivery to remote, digital solutions in response to the COVID-19 pandemic," said lead author Isaac Moshe, MA, a doctoral candidate at the University of Helsinki. "Given the accelerated adoption of digital interventions, it is both timely and important to ask to what extent digital interventions are effective in the treatment of depression, whether they may provide viable alternatives to face-to-face psychotherapy beyond the lab and what are the key factors that moderate outcomes."\nDigital interventions typically require patients to log in to a software program, website or app to read, watch, listen to and interact with content structured as a series of modules or lessons. Individuals often receive homework assignments relating to the modules and regularly complete digitally administered questionnaires relevant to their presenting problems. This allows clinicians to monitor patients'' progress and outcomes in cases where digital interventions include human support. Digital interventions are not the same as teletherapy, which has gotten much attention during the pandemic, according to Moshe. Teletherapy uses videoconferencing or telephone services to facilitate one-on-one psychotherapy.\n\nWhich of the following statements is true?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Teletherapy is not identical with digital interventions.\nVideoconferencing can be a viable method in teletherapy to promote one-on-one psychotherapy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b95711d-5143-53ff-95bd-054f80327362'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b95711d-5143-53ff-95bd-054f80327362'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Interludes', E'The interludes which break up the gameplay action, and which, because they can be made to a higher level of animation, often provide the most visually arresting sequences of a game. Combined with a taste for bizarrely complicated, recursive plots, and long sequences of wordy explicatory dialogue, this turns the games into a bit of a drag.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0b963cc1-4b7a-5294-a05a-7b1ae73d6c32'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b963cc1-4b7a-5294-a05a-7b1ae73d6c32'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the offspring of a male lion and a female tiger?', 'fa30529d-fbca-51f2-a860-08589648d48f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Liger', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b9b8075-982d-552f-8a72-71121af3b259'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b9b8075-982d-552f-8a72-71121af3b259'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pidgins', E'Pidgins are languages that are born after contact between at least two languages. As many pidgins developed during the period of empire and international trade, one of the language parents was frequently a European language such as French or English, and the other language parent was the language of the people with whom the Europeans were {{2}} or whom they were colonising. Usually one of the languages provided the majority of {{4}} items and the other provided the grammatical structure. When pidgins become learned as a mother tongue, they become {{1}} as creoles. I am not going to discuss pidgins and creoles and contact languages as such in this book in {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.trading, 2.vocabulary, 3.known, 4.any depth', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b9c25e7-c426-5d88-82bc-511ad4a7e236'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b9c25e7-c426-5d88-82bc-511ad4a7e236'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is typically deposited in a bank?', '91058956-42e0-5f66-9814-de50f5ae93ae'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Money / savings / checks', NULL, NULL),
  ('0b9eba09-3900-52c5-a688-606782d2eac5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0b9eba09-3900-52c5-a688-606782d2eac5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Feature Films', E'The universality of story feature films is narratives - they tell stories. Even films based on {{1}} events will fictionalize them in order to produce drama, to telescope time, to avoid being filled up with too many {{2}} characters, or simply to be more entertaining. Even in the current welter of special-effect movies, feature films are usually summarized by their plots - in their first ''treatment'' (or outline of the script idea), in the advance publicity, in the TV guide, in reviews, and in conversations. Films may differ from other {{3}} of narrative - literary fiction or television drama, for instance - in the medium used and the representational conventions. They do, however, {{4}} with literary fiction and television drama the basic structure and functions of narrative. Much work has been done by researchers in the field known as ''narratology'' on exactly what constitutes the structures and functions of the narrative. Their conclusions are of great use to students of the feature film.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.true, 2.minor, 3.kinds, 4.share', NULL, NULL),
  ('0bb29651-c8aa-5118-808d-2fa7e007765a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0bb29651-c8aa-5118-808d-2fa7e007765a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Malaria', E'An interesting account of a malaria {{1}} in Rome was in the late 19th century. The city was ravaged by malaria until a particularly harsh winter set in, bringing unusually low temperatures. The cold {{2}} significantly reduced the mosquito population, a key vector in the {{3}} of malaria, {{4}} aiding in the city''s recovery from the epidemic. This historical {{5}} illustrates the profound impact of environmental factors on the spread and control of infectious diseases.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.outbreak, 2.spell, 3.transmission, 4.thereby, 5.case', NULL, NULL),
  ('0bb496c9-a414-51b9-ae91-d6cc7f1b515b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0bb496c9-a414-51b9-ae91-d6cc7f1b515b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call an expert in a field?', '6ee1fd97-0a0e-5a57-97d2-e46e14bdf3dd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Specialist', NULL, NULL),
  ('0bb910aa-1732-5962-a022-105866b9d641'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0bb910aa-1732-5962-a022-105866b9d641'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Black Lives Matter', E'The Black Lives Matter movement has sparked a global conversation about systemic racism and police brutality. As people around the world demand justice and equality, it is clear that there is still much work to be done to create a more just and equitable society.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0bba3fc1-572b-5cf0-87d0-7cfa70a530be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0bba3fc1-572b-5cf0-87d0-7cfa70a530be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Strawberries', E'A recent study demonstrates that strawberries, consumed daily for 12 weeks, can improve memory and reduce depressive symptoms in middle-aged, overweight adults. This improvement is attributed to the anti-inflammatory effects of anthocyanins in strawberries, highlighting the fruit’s role in cognitive health.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
