  ('0c8af19e-03f9-5bd4-8872-1487c1ecf470'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0c8af19e-03f9-5bd4-8872-1487c1ecf470'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5aa526f1-861e-58a3-aa57-715dea67eff0'::uuid, NULL, E'Unfortunately, my schedule conflicts with several interesting economics classes this semester.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0c9492e0-b3bf-5964-bd06-8d3dcd135ea1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0c9492e0-b3bf-5964-bd06-8d3dcd135ea1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vegetable Nutrition', E'Recent trends in raw food diets overlook the fact that some vegetables are more nutritious when cooked. Cooking methods like steaming or roasting can enhance the availability of essential nutrients in vegetables such as asparagus, mushrooms, and spinach. This process releases important vitamins and antioxidants, which are sometimes trapped within the vegetables’ cell walls.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0c9ed8b5-3c5b-5085-bd19-dd326cf99606'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0c9ed8b5-3c5b-5085-bd19-dd326cf99606'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6fa989a9-57a8-51b6-84c8-247ff1176977'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Usually, older students adapt very well to the university environment.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0ca67883-25ed-5dc2-b685-64b8854c8073'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ca67883-25ed-5dc2-b685-64b8854c8073'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cash-flow Problem', E'While costs are rising, artist fees are not, and tickets to regular shows are harder to move than ever. Many fans aren’t ready to return to the crowded mosh; others are dealing with the cost of living crisis. And with the exception of blockbuster shows, people who do buy tickets are tending to buy them last-minute, creating a cash-flow problem for artists.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ca8b998-7ceb-54c3-9cea-baf601ee06b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ca8b998-7ceb-54c3-9cea-baf601ee06b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which U.S. state is the only one made up entirely of islands?', 'cd556317-1447-5c7d-b9c5-d96182272525'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hawaii', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cb0b67c-3531-528b-a97e-1111225f9a88'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cb0b67c-3531-528b-a97e-1111225f9a88'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'English Revolution (B)', E'The speaker reminisces about his views of the English Revolution when he was a student and how it seemed quite clear which side he was on - ''the aristocrats, not the puritans''. Later he realized there was more to it than that and there were several ways of interpreting the Revolution: as a struggle between the king and parliament, as a class war or as an unpredictable situation without clear sides.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cb28933-e2f0-5f81-9e28-a816d704d755'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cb28933-e2f0-5f81-9e28-a816d704d755'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Attention Economy', E'So we always had an attention economy, whether it was on radio or television there''s always been a race for our attention and it''s a zero sum game. If one TV station gets more of your attention the other TV station gets less. But now because we''re spending more and more time on screens and there’s so many things competing for our attention we really feel it. And on the attention economy with social media and with the Internet and our screens, everything needs your...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '35a82501-4853-5326-9b0f-754a64cb98b0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'attention', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cba1cb6-d1ac-5404-a97f-41e501519ae9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cba1cb6-d1ac-5404-a97f-41e501519ae9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a4f85f26-90e8-546b-ad4c-5d381e033e7c'::uuid, NULL, E'There are no restrictions on the amount of money you can withdraw.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cba519f-20ef-597c-a898-15cd1ac0f961'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cba519f-20ef-597c-a898-15cd1ac0f961'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Housing Insecurity and Cancer', E'A new study has shown that for cancer patients, housing insecurity in particular may make their cancer worse. “Social risks affect how we interact with the health care system and other social systems,” says Matthew Banegas, lead author on the study and a researcher at the Kaiser Permanente Center for Health Research in Portland, Oregon. “Slowly and surely, we have been able to show that these risks are important.”\nThis study builds on other work that has shown the negative effects of housing insecurity, from worsening people’s mental health to disrupting treatment for HIV/AIDS. Insecure living is, it seems, a health risk.\nThe study looked at the social risks experienced by more than 1,200 US cancer patients at the time of their diagnosis to see whether being exposed to risk factors — housing insecurity, food insecurity, financial hardship, transport difficulties — appeared to raise their risk of dying from their cancer. The researchers found there was a two-fold greater risk of death for patients experiencing unstable housing — which can refer to a range of housing-related challenges, including homelessness, difficulty paying rent, overcrowding, moving frequently, or spending the majority of income on housing — compared to people who were not.\nNotably, the study didn’t assess how insecure housing might influence cancer mortality. There are a lot of different ways that social risk can impact cancer care. The stress of insecure living, for instance, might raise the risk of cancer developing. Or disruption caused by housing insecurity might impact a person getting screening, or affect someone’s chances of receiving high-quality treatment. Housing acts as a hub for a person to access health care, and so instability can disrupt access to services.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('0cbcb8ca-794a-5a9a-98ba-4df4f3f3a060'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cbcb8ca-794a-5a9a-98ba-4df4f3f3a060'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Air Pollution', NULL, '5d3e61e5-5dd6-578f-aa70-ff0ba5f0605e'::uuid, NULL, E'In today''s lecture I''m going to talk about changes in air pollution since the middle of the last century and what has created these changes.\nSo, um — by the 1950s, air pollution was very visible with frequent thick black fogs known as ''smogs'' in many large cities around the world. The main source of this pollution was from factories and it caused severe health problems. For example, a particularly severe smog in London in 1952 caused over four thousand deaths. Obviously something had to be done and in 1956 a Clean Air Act was introduced in Britain. This addressed the pollution from factories and the smogs soon disappeared.\nHowever, as you know, these days air pollution is still a big issue. The main difference between now and the 1950s is that you can''t see it — it''s invisible. Also, the main source of pollution now is from cars and lorries, and although these don''t produce visible signs, this air pollution is still a significant risk to health. And one of the key factors in the rise of this type of pollution is that we have all become much more vehicle-dependent. There are far more cars and lorries, trains and planes than in the 1950s and this is now the main source of air pollution around the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cbd8e37-c2c1-5fd0-885a-342451bdfc52'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cbd8e37-c2c1-5fd0-885a-342451bdfc52'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sea Snakes', E'A snake at sea isn''t automatically a "sea snake". Lots of unrelated species frolic in our oceans from time to time. Reticulated pythons, for example, will swim between islands along the coasts of southeastern Asia, crossing distances that could wear out an Olympic gold medalist. That doesn''t, however, make them sea snakes. When naturalists talk about "sea snakes," they''re usually referring to two very specific groups of reptiles that are part of the cobra family: true sea snakes and sea kraits. We''ve already met one of the former species. Yellow-bellied sea snakes, those oddball knot-tiers, are classic hydrophiids. True sea snakes like these have sworn off dry land altogether. Fully marine, they give birth to live young at sea. Scientists recently learned that Australia''s Cleveland Bay is a biological nursery where pregnant spine-bellied sea snakes come to deliver their broods. Terrestrial births just aren''t an option. Hydrophiids never exit the water voluntarily because they lack the wide belly scales other snakes use to crawl over solid ground. Drop one on a beach and the poor creature will struggle to move under its own power. Sea kraits are a bit less streamlined, but they''re more competent on land. They mate, shed and digest some of their meals outside the water. Equipped with the requisite belly scales, the animals are free to hit the turf, and like sea turtles, they lay eggs in beachside nests.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('0cbff3bf-fc89-52d7-bddd-ca515b4b7c52'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cbff3bf-fc89-52d7-bddd-ca515b4b7c52'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5b454762-51f2-5950-b036-5f9ef83781d9'::uuid, NULL, E'The lecture on management in Japan will take place in week seven.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cc0c113-71d7-5d26-b79b-f62b580caa05'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cc0c113-71d7-5d26-b79b-f62b580caa05'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Big Mansions', E'Most people are overjoyed to have a couple thousand square feet to call their own, but the world''s ultra-wealthy are living in far more space than that. From ultramodern mansions to historically significant properties, there are a handful of truly huge houses scattered around the world, each with their own perks and amenities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cc51722-1677-56dc-843a-f584616d6ff4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cc51722-1677-56dc-843a-f584616d6ff4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f3ba7fd7-6bf3-5aac-a835-344d17cf35c7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Our class is going to be split into three groups.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cc92066-2f36-547b-ba88-b2a1e07e1d9b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cc92066-2f36-547b-ba88-b2a1e07e1d9b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yusuf Shah', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cc93ce4-d81d-5d2d-bad8-5fa26e28114a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cc93ce4-d81d-5d2d-bad8-5fa26e28114a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Infant Brain', E'Along with all that they have in common, infants also show unique individual traits. Some are more active than others, some are more sociable and some are more interested in the world around them. Infants earlier on show consistent differences in friendliness and anxiety level which form part of their early character.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ccebd5d-1268-5f8f-a4b2-6578dd283490'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ccebd5d-1268-5f8f-a4b2-6578dd283490'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the largest lake in the world?', '826f9e6d-9fc1-54f9-a194-fabceb8d1ed0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Caspian', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cced974-19c0-56dc-bb89-0ee56240b5b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cced974-19c0-56dc-bb89-0ee56240b5b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b47809a2-7f1f-550f-84aa-2be946765675'::uuid, NULL, E'He had been carrying on his business until he retired last year.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cd16367-b601-53fb-9a21-44a84d74ef54'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cd16367-b601-53fb-9a21-44a84d74ef54'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a scientist who specializes in the stars and planets?', 'fe22d920-a121-5de8-abc8-b01fd1d1c65d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Astronomer / astronomers', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cd67e3b-b22f-5e67-906b-7b2223f2e0f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cd67e3b-b22f-5e67-906b-7b2223f2e0f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modify Cultural Ideas', E'People modify cultural ideas in their minds, and sometimes they pass on the modified versions. Inevitably, there are unintentional modifications as well, partly because of straightforward error, and partly because inexplicit ideas are hard to {{2}} accurately: there is no way to download them directly from one brain to another like computer programs. {{4}} native speakers of a language will not give identical definitions of every word. So it can be only rarely, if {{1}} , that two people hold precisely the same cultural idea in their minds. That is why, when the founder of a philosophical movement or a religion dies, or {{5}} , schisms typically happen. The movements'' most devoted followers are often shocked to {{3}} that they disagree about what its doctrines—really are.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.convey, 2.Even, 3.ever, 4.even before, 5.discover', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cd944bd-7cef-51a5-8a43-d9548a051780'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cd944bd-7cef-51a5-8a43-d9548a051780'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cd567bcb-42e2-5763-8f4d-96d85639d87f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The skills of great stage actors cannot be taught.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cdace83-4ebd-5958-8078-7e0a1662e329'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cdace83-4ebd-5958-8078-7e0a1662e329'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we call the people who work in companies?', '8ca10fac-7098-52ae-bb73-7878aa185d10'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Employee', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cdefc8b-7483-5d1c-a313-74fb449b0df9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cdefc8b-7483-5d1c-a313-74fb449b0df9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nice Guys', E'Are you an agreeable person-you know, a nice guy? If so, a logical follow-up might be: how are your finances? And here''s why: "Agreeable people have lower savings, they have higher debt, and they''re also more likely to go bankrupt or default on their loans."\nSandra Matz is a computational social scientist at the Columbia Business School in New York City. And using a combination of questionnaires and bank data, she and her colleague Joe Gladstone found that people who score as more agreeable on personality tests have a better chance of ending up in dire financial straits - especially if they are low-income to begin with.\nThe researchers also combined personality data on millions of people in the U.S. and the U.K. with regional data on how many people were unable to pay their debts. And they found, again, that the nicer a county or local area''s people on average, the worse their finances.\nMatz thinks one factor could be that agreeable people just don''t care much about money. Maybe they pick up the tab more often, or loan money when they can''t afford to. They''re generous to a fault.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?', '42c3e2cb-31e8-5084-a099-31712e82e615'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Agreeable people are more generous and therefore more likely to take on debt.\nNice people like to help others, even to their own detriment.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0ce0dffc-e1ce-5d37-b5c8-6f0967bfb85c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ce0dffc-e1ce-5d37-b5c8-6f0967bfb85c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Economic Situation', E'In his landmark account, first published over twenty years ago, the author argues that the ignorance and lethargy of the poor are direct results of the whole situation of economic, social and political domination. By being kept in a situation in which critical awareness and response are practically impossible the disadvantaged are kept ‘submerged’.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ce83f8e-46c7-5588-b202-2d84b70a10ee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ce83f8e-46c7-5588-b202-2d84b70a10ee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Trauma', E'The death of a loved one through an accident or act of violence can be particularly traumatic because it is so sudden and unexpected. In the initial {{1}} of such a loss, you may experience intense emotions like anger, guilt, and deep sadness. Physically, you may feel exhausted, experience changes in appetite, or have {{2}} sleeping. All of these reactions are normal and expected. To cope with a traumatic loss, it is important to allow yourself to grieve in your own way and in your own time. The pain from a traumatic loss may never completely {{3}} , but it will soften over time. Be gentle with yourself and allow the grief process to unfold. {{4}} the happy memories you had with the loved one you lost. Honor them in the way you choose to live your own life going forward. Though life feels bleak now, you will heal and find happiness and meaning again.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.aftermath, 2.trouble, 3.fade, 4.Cherish', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cf26415-4598-5bf7-96a2-c7ad87dc870d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cf26415-4598-5bf7-96a2-c7ad87dc870d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6b67e6f5-3eb9-558d-9970-2d003648d856'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sociology has become a popular discipline among college students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cf2abf9-89d4-5caf-b7da-9d4956630859'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cf2abf9-89d4-5caf-b7da-9d4956630859'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Small Town', E'To live in a small town or a big city has become a hot topic. Which place would you prefer to live in?', NULL, NULL, E'The debate between living in a small town versus a big city has been ongoing for years, with both options having their own unique advantages and disadvantages. However, in my opinion, living in a small town is a better choice for several reasons.\nFirstly, small towns offer a close-knit community with a strong sense of belonging. In small towns, people tend to know each other and are more likely to form meaningful relationships with their neighbors. This sense of community can be particularly beneficial for families with children, as children can grow up in a safe and supportive environment.\nSecondly, the cost of living in small towns is often lower than in big cities. Housing prices, groceries, and other daily essentials tend to be more affordable in small towns. This can be particularly advantageous for individuals who are just starting out in their careers or for retirees who are living on a fixed income.\nIn conclusion, while big cities may offer more job opportunities and cultural diversity, I believe that small towns offer a better quality of life overall. With their close-knit communities, lower cost of living, and slower pace of life, small towns can provide individuals and families with a safe and supportive environment to grow and thrive. Therefore, if given the choice, I would choose to live in a small town over a big city.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0cf37842-916c-5556-bdfa-0f9e2a4895ff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cf37842-916c-5556-bdfa-0f9e2a4895ff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b678c051-6032-55c5-a867-275a80f76504'::uuid, NULL, E'Every student must participate in the exercise program as a requirement.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0cfb6dec-51a6-5d6a-96a5-592b8bba096c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cfb6dec-51a6-5d6a-96a5-592b8bba096c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'American Executive', E'The American executive, unlike the British, has no {{1}} with the legislature, and this lack of {{2}} between executive and legislature is one of the {{3}} features of American federal government. The Constitution guarded against executive control by {{4}} federal officials, whether civil or military, from membership in Congress.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.connection, 2.coordination, 3.distinctive, 4.disqualifying', NULL, NULL),
  ('0cfc305c-5f53-526b-bcc1-69545acd0a3e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0cfc305c-5f53-526b-bcc1-69545acd0a3e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-L', E'In small doses, stress can have quite a positive effect. It can make you feel more alive, even exhilarated. I suppose everyone has a set level at which stress becomes unbearable, at which point they cease to function properly. I suppose, too, that it''s possible for someone to train themselves to be able to take higher levels of stress by repeatedly putting\nthemselves in a stressful situation\n- to build up a tolerance for stress. Indeed, some jobs absolutely require this. But stress is a fact of life for all of us and, as the figures show, its effect is largely negative.\nEach year, about six million people in Britain consult their doctors because they feel stress or anxiety, and it is estimated that at least another six million suffer from stress-related illness but do not seek medical advice. Long working hours, fear of losing their jobs,\nthe difficult journey to and (rom work in crowded trains and buses, all contribute to increased levels\nof stress. Then there are domestic problems, such as a large mortgage on the house, children who want to drop out of school and join rock bands, not enough time to spare to be with the family.\n\nAccording to the text, which of the following statements is true about stress?', '85c29584-2077-5f26-b911-0ce077a1f09c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Working long hours can also contribute to stress.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d01270c-9c1d-5fd9-8d5a-c81825864523'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d01270c-9c1d-5fd9-8d5a-c81825864523'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which color do we make by blending black and white?', '74583f24-a086-53fa-807b-c6197519a415'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Grey', NULL, NULL),
