  ('0d2632f0-b8fe-528b-ad4e-52a5e7da3f32'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d2632f0-b8fe-528b-ad4e-52a5e7da3f32'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '31a302b3-bee2-597d-ac26-44bc6cc58266'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Anatomy is the study of internal and external body structures.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d2bc389-1719-5179-9c47-61fcd1fd349d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d2bc389-1719-5179-9c47-61fcd1fd349d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5be120f5-b0ae-5be2-b5b9-a373f60e0868'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Physical health can be improved by regular training.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d2eda08-0ff6-5301-b714-923d495bb636'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d2eda08-0ff6-5301-b714-923d495bb636'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mozart Effect', E'Researchers have debunked the much-publicised idea, known as the Mozart effect, that listening to classical music improves children''s ability to reason about spatial relations and other nonverbal tasks. Learning to play a musical instrument or to sing, {{1}} , may indeed give youngsters an intellectual edge over their peers, a new {{2}} suggests. Six-year-olds who took weekly piano or singing lessons throughout the school year {{3}} an average IQ increase of 7.0 points, says psychologist E. Glenn Schellenberg of the University of Toronto at Mississauga. Other 6-year-olds who {{4}} took weekly drama lessons or received no extracurricular lessons displayed an average IQ rise of 4. 3 points, Schellenberg reports in the August Psychological Science.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.however, 2.study, 3.exhibited, 4.either', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d36806f-8271-573f-b0c8-e4c2739d575d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d36806f-8271-573f-b0c8-e4c2739d575d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Civil Rights', NULL, 'eb0cc559-889e-5c9f-a2ae-651e614b02f9'::uuid, NULL, E'The way I started really, I was doing this type of work in United States where there are a number of lawyers doing it and it had not been done in the UK with the rest of Europe before. I think the reason I started in the United States was that there was a civil rights movement. And in the civil rights movement, lawyers became deeply involved right away because if you''re black civil rights your''re arrested. And some four cider?founders, so the environmental movement coming along just behind the civil rights movement in time and said ah, we need lawyers and environment movement as well. As a result, one of the main contributors to the environment now is how has been its lawyers. Here there were no need for civil rights movement, so environmental groups became expert campaigners, but law really wasn''t part of the deal and never has happened, they never use law strategically, they would say they have. I came here and one of our interviewed people and environmental groups in UK, in Brussels and so on and was very surprised of the positive views of law and that''s where client came from, so bringing their kind of intellectual DNA and work I''ve done in the United States into these very difficult cultures.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d39383d-0d64-5881-bf4c-d7dc9d21fbcb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d39383d-0d64-5881-bf4c-d7dc9d21fbcb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Air', E'The atmosphere is a mixture of different gases and air assaults. We usually call it air. The atmosphere is very important to our lives, and we cannot live without it. Almost every living creature on earth breathes it. It surrounds earth and protects us from deadly rays and radiation from space.\n\nWhat is the talk mainly about?', '58887009-eaba-5af0-b380-1919c77ea464'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The functions of air', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d3b30ba-20a3-53d0-bc19-257609b0c069'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d3b30ba-20a3-53d0-bc19-257609b0c069'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Underground Networks', E'Plants possess an intricate system of roots that extends far beyond what meets the eye. These underground networks serve a crucial purpose in absorbing water and nutrients from the soil. This remarkable feature enables plants to thrive in demanding environments like deserts. Mesquite trees, for example, have tap roots that can delve over 50 yards deep in search of water.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d3df860-afce-522a-a00b-47a7b0b5668d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d3df860-afce-522a-a00b-47a7b0b5668d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which sense of human relates to the following words, soft and roughness?', '4222ae26-c9b3-5bf9-a3e8-52d229c2d36b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tactile sensation / sense of touch / haptic', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d421010-4ae9-5e06-a6a4-2331c4249bf4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d421010-4ae9-5e06-a6a4-2331c4249bf4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Thymus', E'The thymus, a vital organ nestled within the chest, plays a pivotal role in immune function. Despite its small size, this gland orchestrates the maturation of T-cells, the guardians of our immune system. Like a conductor leading an orchestra, the thymus guides these cells through a complex process of education and selection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d436d9d-ea35-5f46-9397-8a939b64c940'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d436d9d-ea35-5f46-9397-8a939b64c940'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the organ below your eyes?', '9b83615e-6230-5c7b-ad29-dd9bdfc4dd5f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Nose', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d444563-8fe8-5572-b231-5d162c7d279b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d444563-8fe8-5572-b231-5d162c7d279b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '54047a1a-c205-518a-9025-34c72deb5d74'::uuid, NULL, E'Until you complete the form, you cannot attend.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d4c43a1-5a5e-594e-8811-a7084957cf8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d4c43a1-5a5e-594e-8811-a7084957cf8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sociology Career', E'Anthropology majors pursue a wide variety of careers, as do sociology students. Either of these degrees can lead to a career as a teacher, public sector employee, or academic. Students who major in sociology often go on to work at non-profit or governmental organizations and the degree can be a stepping stone to a career in politics or public administration.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d5353b7-a665-5c72-9e88-b0a0704a1402'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d5353b7-a665-5c72-9e88-b0a0704a1402'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4f230657-306f-5308-b0e8-c2e8e1548572'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We are more able to accommodate postgraduate students than previously possible.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d5774b6-1703-59be-9077-389aa9a3daa5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d5774b6-1703-59be-9077-389aa9a3daa5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Personal Values', E'When we {{1}} and consider an individual’s personality and values, we can more clearly predict how that person will {{2}} . Though a word of caution should be added to remind us that behavior is {{3}} by many factors and that every situation is unique, personality and values still {{4}} helpful predictors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.recognize, 2.behave, 3.influenced, 4.remain', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d58f279-058b-52a3-a607-64205846f482'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d58f279-058b-52a3-a607-64205846f482'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'18th Century Britain', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 4, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('0d5b11f4-f904-5695-9d44-29c1ca951427'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d5b11f4-f904-5695-9d44-29c1ca951427'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e41863cc-ad76-5289-8f72-6363cb33c23e'::uuid, NULL, E'I will now demonstrate how the reaction can be arrested by adding a dilute acid.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d600df5-c445-5ebb-b84b-8222b604acfc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d600df5-c445-5ebb-b84b-8222b604acfc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '593041dc-4096-56ae-92d8-d220e35364ec'::uuid, NULL, E'Having a shower before going to bed can help you sleep.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0d64c489-32b6-53c8-bf42-b6ceda12c6d6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d64c489-32b6-53c8-bf42-b6ceda12c6d6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Seattle Commuters', E'Seattle is among the fastest-growing cities in America, thanks largely to Amazon’s addition of 35,000 employees since 2010. For all the economic benefits that come with growth, it has also created a variety of civic headaches, traffic chief among them.\nBut thanks in part to efforts by the region’s largest employers, the share of commuters driving solo into downtown Seattle is on a dramatic decline. Just 25 percent of workers traveling into the city’s center drove themselves, according to the results of the latest annual commuter survey by the Seattle Department of Transportation (SDOT) and its nonprofit partner, Commute Seattle. This is the lowest share since the city started keeping track in 2010.\nThe number of cars is also trending downwards, according to responses collected from 1,784 downtown workers. While Seattle has gained about 60,000 jobs since 2010, there are approximately 4,500 fewer single-occupancy vehicles. Overwhelmingly, new workers are choosing transit. The share of commuters headed downtown by bus or train shot up from 42 to 48 percent from 2010 to 2017, with about 127,000 such trips during the average morning rush hour. Bus trips (as anyone who’s waited at a packed King County Metro stop on a weekday morning can attest) make up the vast majority of them.\nWalking, biking, and carpooling also picked up by thousands of trips per day, according to the survey. Note, though, that ride-hailing services such as Uber and Lyft weren’t explicitly identified as options in the survey, which comes from a state document that hasn’t changed much since 1991. Respondents might have registered those trips as “drive alone,” “other,” or as “rideshare” (meaning carpool), but there is currently no way of telling.', NULL, NULL, E'Seattle is among the fastest-growing cities in America, but the share of commuters driving solo into downtown Seattle is on a dramatic decline, and new workers are choosing transit, where the share of commuters headed downtown by bus or train shot up from 42 to 48 percent from 2010 to 2017; walking, biking, and carpooling also picked up by thousands of trips per day.', NULL, 5, 75),
