  ('0d9e06bc-d034-5283-8b5b-023dbb2ce9df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0d9e06bc-d034-5283-8b5b-023dbb2ce9df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Atomic Nuclei', E'Atomic nuclei come in a dizzying number of varieties. Scientists have discovered 118 chemical elements, {{1}} by the number of protons in their nuclei. Each of those elements has a variety of isotopes, different versions of the element formed by switching up the number of neutrons inside the nucleus. Scientists have predicted the {{2}} of about 8,000 isotopes of known elements, but only about 3,300 have made an appearance in detectors. Researchers expect FRIB will make a {{3}} dent in the missing isotopes. It may identify 80 percent of possible isotopes for all the elements up through uranium, including many never seen before. The most familiar nuclei are those of the roughly 250 isotopes that are stable: they don''t {{4}} to other types of atoms. The ranks of stable isotopes include the nitrogen-14 and oxygen-16 in the air we breathe and the carbon-12 found in all known living things. The number following the element''s name {{5}} the total number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distinguished, 2.existence, 3.sizable, 4.decay, 5.indicates', NULL, NULL),
  ('0da017a2-b857-550b-a362-68f11831afac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0da017a2-b857-550b-a362-68f11831afac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dictionary Publishers', E'For the first time, dictionary publishers are {{1}} real, spoken English into their data. It gives lexicographers (people who write dictionaries) {{2}} to a more vibrant, up-to-date {{3}} language which has never really been studied before.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.incorporating, 2.access, 3.vernacular', NULL, NULL),
