  ('0dad8373-b9a1-57a1-9ed9-2cf5bf6644d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dad8373-b9a1-57a1-9ed9-2cf5bf6644d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fa9a4cb3-e436-5bd3-b146-f89c84a5f897'::uuid, NULL, E'For this project, collaboration in trios will be a necessary requirement.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0dafbd29-7437-504c-8034-8a65b4e37dec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dafbd29-7437-504c-8034-8a65b4e37dec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Protein Songs', E'Likewise, several of the proteins in the study were chosen for their similarities to the key attributes of the Fantasy-Impromptu style. Most of the 18 proteins tested regulate functions including human emotion, cognition, sensation, or performance which the authors say connect to the emotional and expressive of the genre.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0db235ec-3ce1-50f3-a6c8-5ad74daf2d43'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0db235ec-3ce1-50f3-a6c8-5ad74daf2d43'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Different Attainments', E'In many areas of expertise ranging from music, dance, art and literature to sports, chess, mathematics, science and foreign-language acquisition, there is abundant evidence that young people differ from one another in their attainments and in the apparent ease with which they achieve them. {{1}} within a family there may be marked differences. For example, a child who struggles at a musical instrument without {{2}} success may be overtaken by a younger sibling.\nIt is widely believed that the likelihood {{3}} exceptionally competent in certain fields depends on the presence or absence of inborn attributes variously labelled ''talents'' or ''gifts'' or less often ''natural aptitudes''. According to an informal British survey, more than three-quarters of music educators who decide {{4}} young people are to receive instruction believe that children cannot do well, unless they have special innate gifts (Davis 1994). The judgement that someone is talented is believed {{5}} explain (as distinct from merely describing) that person''s success. It is also widely believed that the innate talent that makes it possible for an individual to excel can be detected in early childhood.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Even, 2.much, 3.of becoming, 4.which, 5.to help', NULL, NULL),
  ('0db737d3-f614-5560-8adb-49a0406458c9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0db737d3-f614-5560-8adb-49a0406458c9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What can we use for typing?', '100fadfe-8525-5649-8a13-b3e359ef23dc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Keyboard', NULL, NULL),
  ('0dbcc535-0b5e-5a7f-a2f7-ccb4c92591d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dbcc535-0b5e-5a7f-a2f7-ccb4c92591d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Culture of Family', E'Sociology of the family is a subfield of sociology in which researchers examine the family as one of several key social institutions and units of socialization. The sociology of the family is a common {{1}} of introductory and pre-university academic curricula because the topic makes for a familiar and {{2}} example of patterned social relations and dynamics. To consider the sociology of a family, sociologists utilize family culture as the biggest research tool at their {{3}} . They do this by examining the existing structures and practices of each family to make sense of the pieces of the larger unit. The sociology of a family is founded on many cultural factors that shape its structures and processes, and sociologists must look at these to understand many {{4}} of the field.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.component, 2.illustrative, 3.disposal, 4.complexities', NULL, NULL),
  ('0dc6c4c5-f1f3-581e-8edd-f084837e12f6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dc6c4c5-f1f3-581e-8edd-f084837e12f6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'K-9 Cops', E'Walking through {{1}} , you''ve probably crossed paths with a few K-9 cops. But those dogs aren''t just {{2}} their noses. They may be led astray by where their handlers think drugs and explosives are hiding, too—even when there aren''t any. That''s {{3}} to a study in the journal Animal {{4}} .\nThe researchers {{5}} 18 dogs certified by law enforcement agencies. As a test site, they used four rooms in a drug-and-explosive-free church. The researchers left the first room untouched. In the second, they taped up a sheet of red paper. In the third, they hid a few Slim Jims as a decoy. And in the fourth, they taped red paper to a stash of Slim Jims.\nThe dog handlers were told they might encounter the scent of pot or {{6}} up to three times per room, sometimes marked with red paper. It was a flat-out lie—there were no target scents. But the dog teams still called 225 false alerts—most often at the site of the red paper, whether there were Slim Jims there or not.\nThe study doesn''t mean K-9 cops are totally {{7}} in the real world. But it does imply that the dogs aren''t immune to the power of suggestion—and neither are their handlers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.airports, 2.following, 3.according, 4.Cognition, 5.recruited, 6.gunpowder, 7.unreliable', NULL, NULL),
  ('0dc753f2-4981-527a-8858-fab978f534b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dc753f2-4981-527a-8858-fab978f534b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3edcc3bb-aa90-5f94-94b6-3b52d10c6ec8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'It is important to develop good study skills.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0dd853c9-6246-51a5-ad32-463646cba0eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dd853c9-6246-51a5-ad32-463646cba0eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Conservationists', E'Conservationists have long debated whether the koala should go on the Australian national threatened species list. {{1}} the koala is clearly in trouble in some parts of the country – in Queensland, for example, high numbers {{2}} by disease – in other parts such as Victoria and South Australia the problem is not that koala populations {{3}} , but that they have grown to the point where they are almost too numerous. For a species to be classed as vulnerable, its population {{4}} by more than 30 percent over the last three generations or 10 years. The problem is that when such a stipulation is applied to koalas, the Victorian boom offsets the Queensland bust, and the species stays off the list. This has repercussions because northern koalas are different to southern ones. They are smaller, for example, and they contain a genetic {{5}} not represented in the South. {{6}} , a split listing has been devised koalas from New South Wales, the ACT and Queensland are now officially ''Vulnerable''; those from Victoria and South Australia are not considered threatened.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.While, 2.are afflicted, 3.are falling, 4.must have decreased, 5.variation, 6.For this reason', NULL, NULL),
  ('0dda2cf1-1425-5f60-a7b9-aecd534ffd34'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dda2cf1-1425-5f60-a7b9-aecd534ffd34'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Detections', E'If a single medical objective could be applied to the entire range of cancers, it would be detecting the disease as soon as possible. “At the highest level, finding any cancer early gives you the opportunity for curative treatments,” says the CEO of a research funding organization.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ddacd5d-be82-56bb-926a-ef48b649cc69'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ddacd5d-be82-56bb-926a-ef48b649cc69'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'Scientists distinguish two basic ways in which we receive information from the outside world through the sense of touch: active and passive, or to put it more simply, touching and being touched. Being touched, or passive tactile awareness, includes sensing external pressure and temperature acting on parts of the body, and this gives us clues as to the nature of our environment. Active touching is when we explore our surrounding with our hands, feet, mouth, and so on. Because it''s difficult to guess what some objects are really like with the eyes alone - for example, their weight, hardness or softness, roughness or smoothness, etc. - touching them gives us a much fuller understanding of the objects around us. Yet, how touch works is very complex and [BEEP)\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '2c745bd5-d9d1-566c-a9fa-c1143b2833c8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'still poorly understood', NULL, NULL),
  ('0de21460-e80a-5a16-9217-af6f1282d11b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0de21460-e80a-5a16-9217-af6f1282d11b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Conflict', E'Most of us are {{1}} of open conflict and avoid it if we can. And there is a {{2}} to expressing and working through conflict. If the working involves harsh words and name-calling, people feel deeply hurt and relationships can be {{3}} . Some group members may be afraid that if they really {{4}} their anger, they may go out of control and become violent, or they may do this. These fears can be very {{5}} and based on experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.scared, 2.risk, 3.damaged, 4.express, 5.real', NULL, NULL),
  ('0deeda67-af93-5d60-a545-64065e301fe3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0deeda67-af93-5d60-a545-64065e301fe3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'License Change', E'New B.C. residents will only be required to provide their driver licence history — proof of insurance is no longer required. However, their premiums will be adjusted for the first three years {{1}} driving in B.C. {{2}} the increased risks associated with driving in a new area. Each year you remain crash-free, your discount increases.\nICBC will {{3}} you with up to 15 years of driving experience (up from eight years) upon receipt of a driver''s abstract {{4}} the original date that you received your license. When obtaining your B.C. license, you can provide your original driver''s abstract in person at a driver licensing office.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.of, 2.due to, 3.credit, 4.showing', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df0320d-5ee6-51f9-a3c3-a48cf5eb90e1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df0320d-5ee6-51f9-a3c3-a48cf5eb90e1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modern Team(现代化团队)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 3, 1, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df37a0c-3422-54fe-846f-2c56068f73b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df37a0c-3422-54fe-846f-2c56068f73b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the document that tells your qualification and work experience?', 'ad3298b5-a856-51fc-a3c3-5fb99d445bc4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'CV / curriculum vitae / resume', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df38733-3d01-5417-9950-91ac96ab2883'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df38733-3d01-5417-9950-91ac96ab2883'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the largest layer of the Earth, lying beneath the crust and above the core?', 'fbb2f841-995b-5bd5-a7a2-849fb37dda02'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mantle', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df39c4e-d4c9-5ef0-854a-5a4d9dc5b3fe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df39c4e-d4c9-5ef0-854a-5a4d9dc5b3fe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ff55fb1a-a0a9-52ef-a204-a3561c029234'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You will be able to develop computational and logic skills here.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df4588f-238b-5b4f-82c1-966ff371fbc3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df4588f-238b-5b4f-82c1-966ff371fbc3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'3D Printing', E'Madeline Gannon is a researcher, teacher at the Carnegie Mellon University School of Architecture and Ph.D. candidate in Computational Design — but that’s not all. She is on a mission to open up the infinite design possibilities of 3D printing to the world. “Currently you have to have a lot of technical background in order to participate in creating things for 3D printers,” Gannon says. “There is still a huge knowledge barrier for how we create digital models.” As the technology has advanced, prices have plummeted, and now anyone can buy a 3D printer for a few hundred dollars, Gannon notes. However, not just anyone can create original designs for 3D-printed artifacts. To put true creative power into the hands of any ordinary 3D printer owner, Gannon has developed an innovative new system called ''Tactum''. Tactum is a new type of software that lets users create their own unique designs for 3D printers by simply touching a projected image. Using their innate hand gestures, someone using Tactum can poke, rub and otherwise manipulate the projected image that will become their 3D printed object, and see it instantly change shape in response. In keeping with the goal of democratizing the process, Gannon designed her first series of Tactum artifacts on a surface that everyone can access freely and manipulate instinctively, that being the human body.\n“My goal was to bring the digital out to the physical world and out onto your body,” says Gannon.\nAlong with a companion project called Reverb — which translates these user-created designs into printable meshes — that impulse has resulted in a spectacular diversity of bracelet and necklace designs, ranging from smooth landscapes, intricate textures and chaotic free forms to delicate geometries derived from the 19th century art of chronography.', NULL, NULL, E'Madeline Gannon is on a mission to open up the infinite design possibilities of 3D printing to the world, who has developed an innovative new system called ''Tactum'', which lets users create their own unique designs for 3D printers, and Gannon designed her first series of Tactum artifacts on a surface that everyone can access freely and manipulate instinctively, which has resulted in a spectacular diversity of bracelet and necklace designs.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('0df7cda5-14c0-56bc-9836-edbfffe85988'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df7cda5-14c0-56bc-9836-edbfffe85988'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7fafd1a8-c616-5b40-a955-a8990e100e94'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They are most likely to achieve more of these objectives.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0df8c1d7-ce98-5f3b-aca4-b8d133a1a792'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0df8c1d7-ce98-5f3b-aca4-b8d133a1a792'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tradition and Commerce', E'Tradition and commerce often clash in many cultures. In Trinidad, it is the Carnival that is the cause of current friction. The complaint, as you would expect, is that traditional skills and creativity are being lost in the rush to make profits. And the profits are large: the two-day festival, which attracts up to 40,000 tourists each year, is estimated to generate somewhere between $27 million and $100 million.\nA particular problem for the traditionalists is that the extravagant colorful costumes people wear in the bands or processions are now largely being imported, especially from China. These costumes are cheaper and more revealing (another cause of complaint) than those made locally. Critics say these imports are a threat to traditional creations and, worse, mean sending work elsewhere. Others see turning the Carnival into a profitable and exportable industry as a progressive move, benefiting the country as a whole.\nA large number of people are in two minds. On the one hand, the changes are a reflection of what people - mainly tourists - want, and bring in money. On the other, there is a desire to preserve traditions. The transformation of the bands and processions into businesses has disrupted the social order, which used to be made up of friends getting together to relax, eat and drink, and make costumes. Both sides agree, though, that the country needs to make better use of the skills of the people in the Carnival business and that the country''s resources must appeal to a wider market.', NULL, NULL, E'In Trinidad, the Carnival that is the cause of current friction, in which one side complain that traditional skills and creativity are being lost in the rush to make profits, with extravagant colorful costumes people wear in the bands or processions being imported as a threat to traditional creations, and the other side see turning the Carnival into a profitable and exportable industry as a progressive move, benefiting the country as a whole.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('0dfc08b4-f485-584e-96bf-850ab26b2a3d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0dfc08b4-f485-584e-96bf-850ab26b2a3d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5aeeff51-0613-5321-8d7b-09cc427a3339'::uuid, NULL, E'Companies aim to earn money, not to change society.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
