  ('0e405268-a669-5782-afbb-ef0238354924'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0e405268-a669-5782-afbb-ef0238354924'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the word for a building or room where art exhibitions are held?', '0f238a5c-12ab-537d-9465-fc4954ebddc8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Art gallery / art museum', NULL, NULL),
  ('0e4b13e2-4f80-5e75-8098-dbd19c403fd4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0e4b13e2-4f80-5e75-8098-dbd19c403fd4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Old or Modern Buildings', E'Many countries spend large amounts of money on the restoration of historic buildings rather than on modern housing. To what extent do you agree or disagree with this analysis? What are advantages and disadvantages of this? Support your writing with your experience or examples.', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether many countries spend large amounts of money on the restoration of historic buildings rather than on modern housing has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that allocating much money to renovate historical structures is vital for safeguarding historic legacy, whereas opponents contend that investing significant funds in the repair and preservation of ancient buildings is exacerbating the residence dilemma. From my perspective, I partly agree with the analysis that considerable money should be spent on the refurbishment of historic buildings rather than on current housing, because this has both advantages and disadvantages.\nTo begin with, restoring old buildings is meaningful because it preserves important history and strengthens cultural identity. For example, heritage structures enable descendants to visualize past lifestyles, such as the architecture of ancient residences. Traditional styles have special art designs, like roof shapes and window patterns. Schools can organize educational visits for students to explore history and raise protection awareness. It is thus shown that repairing historic structures with much money is advantageous.\nBesides, I also believe that restoring old buildings is harmful because it fails to solve housing shortages, ignores basic living needs, and affects ordinary people''s life quality. People without shelter need a place to live, allocating funds to old buildings can''t solve their accommodation needs. Moreover, the insufficient housing supply makes low-income families live in crowded spaces, harming health and raising stress. Many average individuals face challenges renting apartments, stuck in shabby areas. This proves that funding the restoration of historic buildings instead of modern housing has drawbacks.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt cultural landmarks and dwelling demand are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that there are both benefits and disadvantages for investing funds on renovation of historic buildings rather than contemporary housing.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0e4c1059-6106-5d76-a320-79b463168ece'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0e4c1059-6106-5d76-a320-79b463168ece'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '20804fb8-7a4c-5d22-bd6d-aa73ecb30a70'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Part of the recipe includes adding boiling water to the mix.', NULL, NULL),
