  ('0f9e4614-7a05-51ba-8c26-a2a5273d4e11'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0f9e4614-7a05-51ba-8c26-a2a5273d4e11'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cd660334-f8d0-5535-9fbf-8bb44bfba2e5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We are centrally located within the heart of the hill park.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fb3fdc3-209a-5e80-9962-455b17fb92c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fb3fdc3-209a-5e80-9962-455b17fb92c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sport Time', E'Some young children spend a great amount of their time practicing sports. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('0fb4f83f-afa1-5cdb-93ee-1d363c2a00e0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fb4f83f-afa1-5cdb-93ee-1d363c2a00e0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wind', E'The world’s atmosphere is forever on the move. Wind is air in motion. Sometimes air moves slowly, giving a gentle breeze. At other times it moves rapidly, creating gales and hurricanes. {{5}} or fierce, wind always starts in the same way. As the sun moves through the sky, it heats up some parts of the sea and land more than others. The air above these {{4}} spots is warmed, becomes lighter than the surrounding air, and begins to rise. Elsewhere, cool air sinks, because it is {{3}} . Winds blow because air squeezed out by sinking, cold air is sucked in under rising, warm air. Winds will blow wherever there is a {{1}} in air temperature and pressure, always flowing from high to low pressure. Some winds blow in one place, and have a local name - North America’s chinook and France''s mistral. Others are part of a huge circulation pattern that sends winds over the {{2}} globe.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Gentle, 2.hot, 3.heavier, 4.difference, 5.entire', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fbb0012-2011-5e6d-a8a4-b62e530424b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fbb0012-2011-5e6d-a8a4-b62e530424b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5f670444-2728-5432-beab-82d348622d00'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Distance learning is providing multiple career opportunities for students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fc5c39a-2548-52e1-9a62-475873c8b036'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fc5c39a-2548-52e1-9a62-475873c8b036'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Student center', NULL, 'ef7f5747-6e08-5517-aa6e-38afc86ba613'::uuid, NULL, E'At last month''s meeting you asked me to draw up a report about the possibility of keeping the student center open twenty-four hours a day. I decided that the best way to assess the need for expanded hours was to talk to the people who were still in the student center at closing time. First, over the course of the two weeks, I interviewed more than fifty students as they left the student center at its regular closing time of twelve midnight. About eighty percent of them said they would prefer that the center stay open later. Of the three main uses of the center—eating in the snack bar, recreation in the game room or watching TV, and studying by far the most popular late night activity is—and this may surprise you—studying. Almost all of the people I talked to said that their main reason for being in the center after ten p.m. was to study in groups or to find a quiet place to study because their dorm was too noisy. Of course, many of these people used the snack bar or TV room for breaks. My recommendation is that we ask the administration to keep the center open after midnight for studying. The recreation room and snack bar can still close at the usual time. This should meet the objection that it costs too much to staff the center from midnight to eight a.m., which I''m sure will be the first response.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0fc7d92c-f362-53d6-b1d0-fbb27b8b3679'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fc7d92c-f362-53d6-b1d0-fbb27b8b3679'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the words that make up a language?', 'ea287965-71f0-5903-ab2d-eb994c55093b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Vocabulary / vocabularies', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fcd054d-2a77-5460-8f0d-ac525c0ff8f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fcd054d-2a77-5460-8f0d-ac525c0ff8f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Air Balloons', E'In the past before the discovery of aeroplanes, people used to travel using hot air balloons. Although it was not a very safe option in the beginning, it was an {{1}} means of transport. There were no roads or quickest means of travel for people so they took a risk of {{2}} in the air using this heated air vessel. Helium and hydrogen were used later on as an improvement to the earlier design. The structure was very aerodynamic and it works on the principle of displacement of air. Many kinds of {{3}} were used in the beginning, such as paper, plastic and even animal skin. The discovery of hot air balloon was {{4}} as people were traditionally used to flying sky lantern. Nowadays, the technology is so advanced and it is still used in the {{5}} areas where there are no roads built yet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.efficient, 2.traversing, 3.materials, 4.accidental, 5.remote', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fce8ebc-9fc1-5a12-b1b6-4698af274514'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fce8ebc-9fc1-5a12-b1b6-4698af274514'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Grapes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 3, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fcf3aac-b8c2-5c89-ac50-4fc0b2e92aa9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fcf3aac-b8c2-5c89-ac50-4fc0b2e92aa9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Banana Tree', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 3, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fd2abd1-b177-53f0-a98a-ac1bc4370a4e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fd2abd1-b177-53f0-a98a-ac1bc4370a4e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the process after becoming well again after an illness?', 'f2f80866-0ef0-5b85-aae0-4301135c97d8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Recovery', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fd5fee9-f614-5ed9-b96d-7a21a246cc2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fd5fee9-f614-5ed9-b96d-7a21a246cc2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '25f39c00-e221-5517-808f-2cd48272ac72'::uuid, NULL, E'Our city is home to people from more than two hundred nationalities.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0fd9bbf0-c8b4-5d48-8de5-0e044d6d7da9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fd9bbf0-c8b4-5d48-8de5-0e044d6d7da9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Deep Sleep', E'What if you could make your sleep more efficient? As a sleep scientist, this is the question that has captivated me for the past 10 years. Because while the light bulb and technology have brought about a world of 24-hour work and productivity, it has come at the cost of our naturally occurring circadian rhythm and our body''s need for sleep. The circadian rhythm dictates our energy level throughout the day, and only recently we''ve been conducting a global experiment on this rhythm, which is putting our sleep health and ultimately our life quality in jeopardy. Because of this, we aren''t getting the sleep we need, with the average American sleeping a whole hour less than they did in the 1940s. For some reason, we decided to wear it as a badge of honor that we can get by on not enough sleep. This all adds up to a real health crisis. Most of us know that poor sleep is linked to diseases like Alzheimer''s, cardiovascular disease, stroke and diabetes. And if you go untreated with a sleep disorder like sleep apnea, you''re more likely to get many of these illnesses. But did you know about sleep''s impact on your mental states? Poor sleep makes us make risky, rash decisions and is a drain on our capacity for empathy. When sleep deprivation literally makes us more sensitive to our own pain, it''s not so surprising that we have a hard time relating to others and just generally being a good and healthy person when we''re sleep-deprived.\n\nWhich of the following are mentioned as mental health issues caused by poor sleep?', 'cee36d71-27f3-5125-9534-030b35e144b6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'risky decision-making\nlack of empathy', NULL, NULL),
  ('0fdb6548-949d-57e1-bd70-3c679fc46ede'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fdb6548-949d-57e1-bd70-3c679fc46ede'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Literature', NULL, '4abcb436-b96a-5923-b1de-0c049e13951c'::uuid, NULL, E'Let''s unfold the realm of ''Literature'' and its profound impact on society. Literature is not just an escape; it''s a mirror that reflects our realities, a lens that sharpens our worldview. Literature fosters empathy. When we dive into the narratives of characters from diverse backgrounds, we live a multitude of lives. This vicarious experience enriches our understanding of others, bridging gaps across cultures and experiences. Furthermore, literature is a catalyst for social change. It has the power to challenge norms, to question policies, and to push boundaries. The works of authors like Harriet Beecher Stowe and George Orwell have spurred movements and reformed societies. As we engage with literature, let us recognize its role in shaping the contours of society. In the pages of books, we find the seeds of the future, sown with words that can move nations.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0fe097e4-2e6c-5299-b175-05967858e361'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fe097e4-2e6c-5299-b175-05967858e361'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c8224f94-63b8-5be4-a0eb-837e429fe767'::uuid, NULL, E'Most countries tend to impose some sort of tax on alcohol and tobacco.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0fe8a735-e405-5a46-9d94-d910183e9460'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0fe8a735-e405-5a46-9d94-d910183e9460'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drinking Water on Mars', NULL, 'e8b58f4f-2907-5286-a011-a5d318ff10a9'::uuid, NULL, E'There is a lot of water on Mars and there once was a lot of surface flowing water. You don''t see it because most of it is mixed with the soil which we call regolith on Mars. So the Martian soil can be anywhere from as little as one percent in some very dry desert-like areas to as much as 60 percent water. So one strategy for getting water when you’re on Mars is to break up the regolith which would take something like a jackhammer because it''s very cold, it''s very frozen. If you can imagine making a frozen brick or a chunk of ice that''s mostly soil and maybe half water and half soil that''s what you would be dealing with. So you need to break this up, put it in an oven. As it heats up it turns to steam. You run it through a distillation tube and you have pure drinking water that comes out the other end. There is a much easier way to get water on Mars. In this country we have developed industrial dehumidifiers. And they''re very simple machines that simply blow the air in a room or a building across a mineral called zeolite. Zeolite is very common on Earth, it''s very common on Mars. And zeolite is kind of like a sponge. It absorbs water like crazy. Takes the humidity right out of the air. Then you squeeze it and out, comes the water.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ff13211-375e-56d5-b6cb-b68ed2c13c9a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ff13211-375e-56d5-b6cb-b68ed2c13c9a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Conservancy', E'To qualify as a conservancy, a committee must define the conservancy'' s boundary, elect a {{1}} conservancy committee, negotiate a legal constitution, prove the committee''s ability to {{2}} funds, and produce an acceptable plan for {{3}} distribution of wildlife-related benefits. Once approved, registered conservancies acquire the {{4}} to a sustainable wildlife {{5}} , set by the ministry.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.representative, 2.manage, 3.equitable, 4.rights, 5.quota', NULL, NULL),
  ('0ffcb724-5fdb-5c48-89a7-2480a587ed41'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ffcb724-5fdb-5c48-89a7-2480a587ed41'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Global Market', NULL, '3e3d5900-3871-5ef0-872e-e9afb78d22ef'::uuid, NULL, E'Right now, I would like to talk about the global market, a dance floor where nations, large and small, move to the rhythm of supply and demand. In this dance, the markets are not just a place of transaction but a stage where the economic health of a country is displayed. Healthy markets signify a thriving economy, where goods, services, and currencies flow seamlessly across borders. Moreover, the concept of ''market equilibrium'' is key. It''s the sweet spot where the quantity of goods supplied meets the quantity demanded, leading to stable prices and satisfied consumers and producers. As we delve into the complex world of economics, let''s remember that it''s not just about numbers and charts. It''s about the human stories behind them - the jobs created, the families supported, and the communities built. Understanding the markets equips us with the tools to contribute to an economy that serves everyone.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0ffff29e-83e3-5583-b1cd-362d69dbf272'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '0ffff29e-83e3-5583-b1cd-362d69dbf272'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Virus Mutation', E'All viruses mutate constantly, and scientists can identify the different {{1}} .\nCoronavirus has mutated into a number of notable strains since the first case was detected in December 2019, with the latest found in Australia believed to originate in Russia. " {{2}} this is not considered a variant of concern, little is known about the strain," a letter sent to passengers said.\nScientists believe it could be up to 70 per cent more {{3}} than others and slightly more deadly. However, more studies will be needed to verify this claim. Last month, Germany''s Health Minister said the virus {{4}} first detected in Britain last year now accounts for more than a fifth of all positive tests in the country. The B.1.351 strain was first identified in South Africa, where it has become the dominant type infecting local residents.\nCases and deaths in South Africa have started to fall recently after a second {{5}} of the virus. However, the nation is still battling one of Africa''s most severe {{6}} , with more than 46,000 people dead. The P.1 strain was first detected in Brazil, and is suspected of {{7}} a COVID-19 resurgence in the nation. Brazilian authorities said 260,000 people have already died.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.strains, 2.Whilst, 3.transmissible, 4.variant, 5.surge, 6.outbreaks, 7.fuelling', NULL, NULL),
  ('100078d2-a5f5-5103-8f41-8ddb9878190c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '100078d2-a5f5-5103-8f41-8ddb9878190c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Infectious Diseases', E'The threat from infectious pathogens is greater today than ever. The outbreak or even resurgence of infectious diseases has shown how these types of diseases could in fact undermine a state’s control of what happens within its territory. Yet, it is unclear whether growing recognition of the severity of the threat of infectious diseases has led to adequate policy responses and definitive action by states.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
