  ('10fc815e-20cd-5e23-9b5f-ccb16d26a1a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '10fc815e-20cd-5e23-9b5f-ccb16d26a1a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a0c5f14c-8ab4-520c-bc7e-bea41c87f64f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You have to turn in your schoolwork at the end of weekend.', NULL, NULL),
  ('11004dff-37c5-5fca-832b-07387679934a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11004dff-37c5-5fca-832b-07387679934a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are your options in gender when you completing an application form?', '0d5af064-2cef-5da2-b686-90f619c2a6e2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Male and female', NULL, NULL),
  ('11032d0e-91eb-55bb-bca6-ed8eb25314ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11032d0e-91eb-55bb-bca6-ed8eb25314ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call an expert who studies birds?', '62c58bde-c988-529f-b58e-d6e90bb9b72d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ornithologist', NULL, NULL),
  ('110cf590-6fba-555d-a713-f37d1e58cec9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '110cf590-6fba-555d-a713-f37d1e58cec9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hurricane', E'A hurricane is a massive storm system. In fact, It''s the most powerful type of storm on earth. Hurricanes form over warm tropical waters and frequently move toward land. Ah. Before I forget to mention this, hurricanes are also called typhoons or cyclones. It depends on where exactly they form. Not all hurricanes are alike. Some are well, more powerful than others. Meteorologists have a rating system for them. They used the term category to rank. Every hurricane that forms the scale ranks hurricanes according to their wind speed and ability to cause damage. A category one hurricane is the weakest. A category five hurricane is the most powerful. A hurricane typically begins as a tropical storm. It has wind speeds between fifty to one hundred kilometers per hour. When the wind blows faster than one hundred kilometers per hour, the tropical storm has become a hurricane, a category one hurricanes winds are between one hundred to one hundred and thirty kilometers per hour. A category two hurricane has winds up to one hundred sixty kilometers per hour. Winds between one hundred sixty and one hundred eighty five kilometers per hour indicate a category three hurricane. A category four hurricane has winds speeds up to two hundred twenty kilometers per hour. Anything above that is a class five her. Again, thankfully, those are quite rare. They are simply devastating when they form and make landfall. Oh, by the way, before you ask typhoons and cyclones use different measuring systems. So what I just described only applies to hurricanes.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '00abe76b-e6ce-530b-939c-d9b1c44056bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The hurricanes, which are also refers to the typhoons or cyclones, are ranked according to their wind speed and ability to cause damage.', NULL, NULL),
  ('110d3aba-140b-5673-8ab8-cc39064a8540'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '110d3aba-140b-5673-8ab8-cc39064a8540'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a7d4733b-f601-5831-a354-66215ff8ee43'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'I didn''t understand the author''s point of view on immigration.', NULL, NULL),
  ('111c3c3c-514a-5026-a9cf-b07c1a633b0f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '111c3c3c-514a-5026-a9cf-b07c1a633b0f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the galaxy we live in?', '38429e6c-2244-5928-9de3-661aacbcffa9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Milky Way', NULL, NULL),
  ('112203c4-1905-59da-a377-4c01b0427bac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '112203c4-1905-59da-a377-4c01b0427bac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Air Moving', E'Wind is air moving around. Some winds can move as fast {{1}} a racing car, over 100 miles per {{2}} . Wind can travel around the world. Wind {{3}} make you feel cold because you lose heat from your body {{4}} when it is windy. Weather forecasters need {{5}} know the speed and direction of the wind. The strength of wind is measured using the Beaufort scale from wind force 0 when there is no wind, to wind force 12 which can damage houses and buildings and is called hurricane force.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.as, 2.hour, 3.can, 4.faster, 5.to', NULL, NULL),
  ('112474ef-097f-5934-affa-d724600b3327'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '112474ef-097f-5934-affa-d724600b3327'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'When you want to learn how to cook meals, what book should you turn to?', 'a617eb48-42e3-5918-bed7-08078448ad22'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cookery / recipe book / cookbook', NULL, NULL),
  ('11250351-47f0-552c-a0e0-092e260b29e4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11250351-47f0-552c-a0e0-092e260b29e4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Equivalence Principle', NULL, '7db206fe-eb61-59a8-b3e6-aff574d27448'::uuid, NULL, E'One of the most important principles of Einstein’s general relativity is the equivalence principle. It says that: all objects, regardless of their mass and composition, would accelerate in the same manner in the same gravitational field when no external forces act upon them. Confused? Let me put it in simple words. Suppose you simultaneously drop a feather and a stone towards the ground from the same height in a perfectly resistance-less environment. Which one, according to you, will touch the ground first? One may think that as a stone is more massive than a fragile feather, it should experience more gravitational force, and hit the ground first. But that’s not the case because as per the principle of equivalence, both objects should fall simultaneously on the ground. In other words, one can say that the inertial and gravitational mass of a body is proportional to each other, which makes the acceleration independent of the physical nature of the body. Now, what is the difference between inertial mass and gravitational mass? The mass that appears in Newton’s Second Law of Motion is termed inertial mass. It simply describes how difficult it is to accelerate an object. On the other hand, the mass that appears in Newton’s Universal Law of Gravitation is the gravitational mass. It depicts the strength with which gravity acts on a body. So although a stone has more gravitational mass than a feather, the force of gravity acting on it is greater. At the same time, its inertial mass is also greater, which makes it difficult to accelerate. So the two effects cancel out, and it falls with the same acceleration as that of the feather which is precisely the value of acceleration due to gravity in free fall. No matter how small, if there’s any violation in the proportionality between inertial and gravitational mass, Einstein’s entire system breaks down.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1126f7a6-36ab-54c8-98c4-3f45f821ebb7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1126f7a6-36ab-54c8-98c4-3f45f821ebb7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fireworks', E'A dramatic fireworks display can be the highlight of a summer. It also can provide a feast for the senses. Bright colors delight the eye. Thunderous booms and whistles surprise the ear. If you’re close to the show, you can feel the pressure waves that ripple from each exploding shell. And folks downwind of the action can smell the burnt gunpowder that fueled each rocket — and perhaps even taste it in the air.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('11279916-d11b-5dbc-a817-b35d85d97640'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11279916-d11b-5dbc-a817-b35d85d97640'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-L', E'I''d like to start this lecture on the use of technology in education by talking about a subject that''s probably close to all your hearts, which is the way that student work is graded, and specifically I want to talk to you about some of the ways written assignments or essays are marked.\nWell, as you all know, traditionally writing done by a student is checked, marked and graded by a teacher, a tutor or in some situations an examiner, in other words, a real person. Software to mark essays has been in development for some time and grading software on computers is already used by some universities to mark exams but it is still viewed with suspicion by some. How can a computer mark an essay they ask? Well. a recent study compared the human ability to give grades to student essays to the ability of a computer to do the same job. In the study, over 16,000 essays were used. These essays had already been previously marked by at least one trained human grader.\nThe study showed that the essay marks given by the computer software were almost the same as those from human graders - which I think you''ll agree is a controversial result and ifs likely to make us as teachers re-evaluate how we grade written work.\n\nThe purposes of this talk are to', '89792fd0-fe66-5b0c-9f8d-f9fc747f6abb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'present different methods for grading writing.\ndescribe the findings of a research project.', NULL, NULL),
  ('112b8ccc-28c6-572d-ba2f-007af820393b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '112b8ccc-28c6-572d-ba2f-007af820393b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roommates', E'When living with roommates, it is important to {{1}} responsibility for household tasks. Although sometimes challenging, the experience is often {{2}} because it teaches cooperation and independence. Roommates should also {{3}} bills fairly and determine the most important {{4}} that make living together successful, such as respect and communication.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.share, 2.worthwhile, 3.divide, 4.factors', NULL, NULL),
  ('11371d2d-4650-5caf-9a51-232ed6aaff33'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11371d2d-4650-5caf-9a51-232ed6aaff33'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cultivated Language', E'In every cultivated language there are two great classes of words which, taken together, comprise the whole vocabulary. First, there are those words with which we become acquainted in daily conversation, which we learn from the members of our own family and from our familiar associates, and which we should know and use even if we could not read or write.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('113b4e65-22c8-59e7-84d9-21be73bf2418'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '113b4e65-22c8-59e7-84d9-21be73bf2418'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '56a817b2-1952-5e76-99b0-0e78d55bcd59'::uuid, NULL, E'Income inequality is a major challenge facing many societies today.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1141fc36-74eb-5659-bc7c-6b65226b92b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1141fc36-74eb-5659-bc7c-6b65226b92b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'The theory of personality types suggests there are pairs of what are known as type preferences. Type preferences are not the same as character traits that can be worked on and changed, rather, their preferred ways of being in the world different, um, different ways of experiencing daily life. One well known pair of type preferences is extraversion introversion, some people are extrovert sand, some are introvert extroverted people are by nature continuously aware of events outside of themselves, extravert stern outward to the world around them to pick up uh, ideas, values and interests. Extravert therefore usually have a variety of interests and sort of take an active approach to life. Introversion is just the opposite. Introvert look inward for resources, introvert, spur, soo fewer interests. But on a much deeper level, they sort of take a reflective approach to life. What I mean is they involve themselves in inner events, ideas and impressions. Introverted people usually prefer to learn in private.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '118b46be-681a-5a67-bd87-c6237dd595f4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'individual ways', NULL, NULL),
  ('1144ecff-1778-56d1-9fcb-a156739eee98'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1144ecff-1778-56d1-9fcb-a156739eee98'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a6016edd-2d75-56e3-95e4-3e79a6648534'::uuid, NULL, E'No one is suggesting that any health risks attach to this product.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('11455e71-2635-50a0-8716-e4a7d68340f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11455e71-2635-50a0-8716-e4a7d68340f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rampant Corruption', E'The inevitable consequences {{1}} rampant corruption, an absence of globally competitive Latin American companies, {{2}} waste of resources, rampant environmental {{4}} and soaring inequality. Above all, the monopoly over power of an ideologically bankrupt party is {{3}} with the pluralism of opinion, security of property and vibrant competition on which a dynamic economy depends. As a result, Latin American development remains parasitic on know-how and institutions developed elsewhere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.include, 2.chronic, 3.degradation, 4.inconsistent', NULL, NULL),
  ('1145eda2-4e36-5f09-a874-830d5efc9a32'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1145eda2-4e36-5f09-a874-830d5efc9a32'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cats', E'Cats are popular pets around the world. They are known for their playful nature, soft fur, and independent personalities. Many people enjoy having cats as companions, as they can provide comfort and entertainment. However, it is important to take care of cats properly by providing them with food, water, and regular veterinary check-ups.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('114bb67c-4fc1-5cb1-821c-8b187cabee2b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '114bb67c-4fc1-5cb1-821c-8b187cabee2b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3cabd6de-1dca-527b-9053-7ff4d846e086'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students intending to attend the conference must register first.', NULL, NULL),
  ('114ef738-d075-5218-b64c-f928d11d7878'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '114ef738-d075-5218-b64c-f928d11d7878'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ADHD', E'Individuals diagnosed with Attention-Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) and prescribed pharmacological interventions may exhibit thermoregulatory dysfunctions, colloquially {{1}} to as heat sensitivity. This physiological anomaly may impair their ability to perceive elevated body temperatures or dehydration, {{2}} escalating the risk of hyperthermia and other heat-induced pathologies. It is noteworthy that this side effect is not exclusive to ADHD medications but is also {{3}} among other psychotropic drugs that modulate neurotransmitter activity in the brain. To mitigate the risk of heat-related complications, individuals on these medications are advised to {{4}} to standard heat-avoidance measures such as seeking shade, maintaining adequate hydration, and applying sunscreen. Furthermore, they are encouraged to {{5}} with their healthcare provider or pharmacist regarding any concerns about their medication’s interaction with heat. Abrupt discontinuation of medication without professional guidance is strongly discouraged.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.referred, 2.thereby, 3.prevalent, 4.adhere, 5.consult', NULL, NULL),
