  ('11baca85-2661-5ccd-b77c-33b4e71e5680'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11baca85-2661-5ccd-b77c-33b4e71e5680'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High Marks(拿高分)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 4, 3, 5', NULL, NULL),
  ('11bfec01-5066-57ae-bce9-584cbb94db61'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11bfec01-5066-57ae-bce9-584cbb94db61'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Seven Natural Wonders', E'The natural world is an incredible place. There are soaring mountains and rolling sand dunes, spectacular beaches and shimmering lakes, steaming geysers and bubbling volcanoes—and so much more. Although it’s all truly dazzling, there are a few destinations and sights around the world that stand out from the rest. And the most significant of all are the seven natural wonders of the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('11c1ff03-8903-555d-be07-3a0f07b46da4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11c1ff03-8903-555d-be07-3a0f07b46da4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a very young form of an insect that looks like a worm?', '4a0be10b-3992-5ce2-9f33-d995c5f06b00'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Larva / larvae', NULL, NULL),
  ('11c59f64-2844-5799-8a74-52be2d1f9638'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11c59f64-2844-5799-8a74-52be2d1f9638'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modern Life', E'People have different ways of escaping the stress and difficulties of modern life. Some read; some exercise; others work in their gardens. What is your way?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('11c5a7ad-6f26-520b-a2ab-45807fa4c6e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11c5a7ad-6f26-520b-a2ab-45807fa4c6e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4001f497-69aa-55d8-b5a6-51007f729044'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You will be able to work with different kinds of people.', NULL, NULL),
  ('11c7cd16-215b-5e16-a416-ed43b5c977d1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11c7cd16-215b-5e16-a416-ed43b5c977d1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Welfare Programs', E'Most societies throughout history employed some strategies to help people in poverty meet basic needs. Before the 20th century, religious groups and private charities often led such initiatives. Today, these are called welfare programs, and they usually take the form of government-provided subsidies for housing and healthcare.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('11ca84d5-21a8-511f-9383-f720d3ceb03b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11ca84d5-21a8-511f-9383-f720d3ceb03b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are the facilities on shore that monitor ships or communicate with them by radio signals?', '6b4ce9f2-ed75-5d23-86b0-657c95d0441b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Coast radio station', NULL, NULL),
  ('11cb782d-587f-5319-8fc0-4fb6d702dec2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11cb782d-587f-5319-8fc0-4fb6d702dec2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Technological Innovations', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 2, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('11cd178e-0b66-5967-91db-1dac11843569'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11cd178e-0b66-5967-91db-1dac11843569'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'de62edbd-3c12-5150-8559-3c25744bd1dc'::uuid, NULL, E'The students return in October for the start of the new academic year.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('11cd8c31-2416-5d22-9100-8dfc890f8678'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11cd8c31-2416-5d22-9100-8dfc890f8678'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Geothermal Energy', E'What is the solution for nations with increasing energy demands, hindered by frequent power cuts and an inability to compete in the international oil market? For East Africa at least, experts think geothermal energy is the answer. More promising still, the Kenyan government and international investors seem to be listening. This is just in time according to many, as claims of an acute energy crisis are afoot due to high oil prices, population spikes and droughts. Currently over 60% of Kenya''s power comes from hydroelectric sources but these are proving increasingly unreliable as the issue of seasonal variation is intensified by erratic rain patterns. Alternative energy sources are needed, and the leading energy supplier in Kenya, Kenya Electricity Generating Company, hopes to expand its geothermal energy supply from 13% to 25 % of its total usage by 2020. The potential of geothermal energy in the region was first realised internationally by the United Nations Development Program, when geologists observed thermal anomalies below the East African Rift system. Locals have been utilising this resource for centuries; using steam vents to create the perfect humidity for greenhouses, or simply to enjoy a swim in the many natural hot lakes. Along the 6000 km of the rift from the Red Sea to Mozambique, geochemical, geophysical and heat flow measurements were made to identify areas suitable for geothermal wells. One area lies next to the extinct Olkaria volcano, within the Hell''s Gate National Park, and sits over some of the thinnest continental crust on Earth. This is a result of the thinning of the crust by tectonic stretching, causing hotter material below the Earth''s surface to rise, resulting in higher temperatures. This thin crust was ideal for the drilling of geothermal wells, reaching depths of around 3000 m, where temperatures get up to 342°C, far higher than the usual temperature of 90°C at this depth. Water in the surrounding rocks is converted to steam by the heat. The steam can be used to drive turbines and produce electricity.', NULL, NULL, E'The solution for east Africa to compete in the international oil market is geothermal energy, but Kenya''s hydroelectric sources are increasingly unreliable, so measurements were made to identify areas suitable for geothermal wells, which is a result of the thinning of the crust by tectonic stretching, and water in the surrounding rocks is converted to steam by the heat, when the steam can be used to drive turbines and produce electricity.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('11d193c2-431d-5670-abcc-c6fd9207597a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '11d193c2-431d-5670-abcc-c6fd9207597a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Watershed', E'A watershed stores rainwater once it filters through the soil. Once the watershed''s soils are saturated, water will either percolate deeper, or runoff the surface. This can result in freshwater aquifers and springs. Also, water moves through the soil to seeps and springs, and is ultimately released into streams, rivers, and the ocean.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
