  ('12e5edb2-bf30-5f96-a944-1ba6e5f73095'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '12e5edb2-bf30-5f96-a944-1ba6e5f73095'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2dd2d0ac-1914-5604-9d53-f371a44205bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some academic departments have unique, specialized collections of books.', NULL, NULL),
  ('12ea2531-7e96-5d14-8391-67f9b0163969'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '12ea2531-7e96-5d14-8391-67f9b0163969'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How many years are there in a bicentennial?', 'a318100e-a733-518d-8451-2181b5ce47e1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Two hundred', NULL, NULL),
  ('12eca50c-e89c-5d3e-8f20-3d6f0d155a83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '12eca50c-e89c-5d3e-8f20-3d6f0d155a83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Benefits of Blueberries', NULL, '54d93553-3fcc-5d92-92d8-185c22e682a1'::uuid, NULL, E'The consumption of berries can enhance beneficial signaling in the brain. Plant foods are our primary source of antioxidant and anti-inflammatory compounds, but some plant foods may be better than others. As I’ve explained before, one cup of blueberries a day can improve cognition among older adults, as shown in this randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial. And the same thing in kids after just a single meal of blueberries; though, two cups may work better than one. That single hit of berries may also improve mood. A double-blind, placebo-controlled, crossover study in which kids are asked a series of questions: Are you very slightly or not at all, a little, moderately, quite a bit, or extremely interested, excited, strong, etc. Before and after drinking the placebo, no significant change, but two hours after consuming about two cups of blueberries, their positive mood scores significantly improved. They felt more enthusiastic, alert, inspired, attentive—that kind of thing. That was in young adults, ages 18 through 21; same thing in 7 to 10-year-old children. Some dangerous new mood enhancing drug or Ritalin? No, blueberries—and just after a single meal. Now blueberries can’t do everything. Although a cup of berries certainly appears to improve brain function... no improvement in walking or balance was observed.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('12fc1088-cf7a-5de1-af07-e9dfd9ca6c42'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '12fc1088-cf7a-5de1-af07-e9dfd9ca6c42'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'After-class Activities', E'There are numerous after-class activities for students. Is it good or not?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('13052069-db58-5e66-ad3e-b09a881f30a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '13052069-db58-5e66-ad3e-b09a881f30a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Apartment Fire', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 2, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('13069553-e391-58c8-95dc-4c1b41ad083c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '13069553-e391-58c8-95dc-4c1b41ad083c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Manga', E'If Japan''s rise to economic superpower dominated U.S. academic discussions in the 1980s, the last 15 years or so have been {{1}} by an intense fascination, both in academic and popular discourse, with the country''s perceived increase in global cultural influence. As Pokémon and Hello Kitty invaded U.S. TV screens and supermarket aisles at a time when, paradoxically, Japanese economic influence was on the decline, U.S. scholars started to point to the emergence of a new kind of Japanese superpower. The discussion shifted from Japan''s Gross National Product to its "Gross National Cool". The characters in Japanese animated cartoon series and in the related genre of manga (Japanese-style comic books or graphic novels), along with their video game cousins, came to symbolize a new order in millennial capitalism {{2}} by a decline in U.S. cultural hegemony and the fragmentation of global powers. Thus, Japanese animation provides a logical starting point to an analysis aimed at decentralizing the role of the United States as the world’s most significant global cultural producer. This chapter will demonstrate, however, that while intending to point to Japan''s growing influence and to a {{3}} relative decline in U.S. power, the academic and popular discourse about Japanese animation''s "global" popularity has paradoxically resulted in the re-centralizing of the United States as both a global cultural producer and a consumer of globalized cultural forms. Turning a translocal lens to the genre''s transnational spread, this chapter illustrates the multiple ways in which this discourse is problematic. Throughout the chapter, the names of a few scholars will frequently reappear. These scholars are most assertively critiqued here not because their work is particularly problematic but, {{4}} , because they have produced the most comprehensive and sophisticated studies of Japanese animation and/or comics. Their works have become seminal texts in the academic study of Japanese popular culture in general and have greatly contributed to our understanding of its influence in the U.S. context. The chapter''s deconstruction of these scholars'' characterization of global processes is offered in an effort to illustrate the productive potential of a more translocal approach. It does not invalidate their {{5}} positive contributions to the field of Japanese studies.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.marked, 2.characterized, 3.concomitant, 4.on the contrary, 5.otherwise', NULL, NULL),
  ('130bf3dc-b641-5cd2-a485-cca200f8735a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '130bf3dc-b641-5cd2-a485-cca200f8735a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6ad882d2-17a0-58f3-b6bc-2e4628299db4'::uuid, NULL, E'International students may receive help finding housing around the university.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('130d989c-13ae-5fab-8538-5af682363add'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '130d989c-13ae-5fab-8538-5af682363add'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2b1ea5f2-c19d-5592-bd60-a5615786bd2f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The advanced mathematics lab will be open again next semester.', NULL, NULL),
  ('130dd0d4-d87c-5e2a-b8ab-cdea2194c349'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '130dd0d4-d87c-5e2a-b8ab-cdea2194c349'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rural Population', E'Thus, a country might possess a sizeable rural population, but have an economic system in which the interests of the voters were predominantly related to their incomes, not to their occupations or location; and in such a country the political system would be unlikely to include an important agrarian party.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1314c532-028e-5dba-8466-0edf5037a9db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1314c532-028e-5dba-8466-0edf5037a9db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9aeb7ce5-5f77-5060-a365-ef0982f20467'::uuid, NULL, E'Most individuals experience feelings of loneliness at some point in life.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1316d4b9-76d8-5228-a3d0-6903aff04ca0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1316d4b9-76d8-5228-a3d0-6903aff04ca0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coffee', E'Coffee is enjoyed by millions of people every day and the ''coffee experience'' has become a staple of our modern life and culture. While the current body of research related to the effects of coffee consumption on human health has been contradictory, a study in the June issue of Comprehensive Reviews in Food Science and Food Safety, which is published by the Institute of Food Technologists (IFT), found that the potential benefits of moderate coffee drinking outweigh the risks in adult consumers for the majority of major health outcomes considered. Researchers at Ulster University systematically reviewed 1,277 studies from 1970 to-date on coffee''s effect on human health and found the general scientific consensus is that regular, moderate coffee drinking (defined as 3-4 cups per day) essentially has a neutral effect on health, or can be mildly beneficial. The authors noted causality of risks and benefits cannot be established for either with the research currently available as they are largely based on observational data. Further research is needed to quantify the risk-benefit balance for coffee consumption, as well as identify which of coffee''s many active ingredients, or indeed the combination of such, that could be inducing these health benefits.', NULL, NULL, E'The current body of research related to the effects of coffee consumption on human health found that the potential benefits of moderate coffee drinking outweigh the risks in adult consumers for the majority of major health outcomes considered, but further research is needed to quantify the risk-benefit balance for coffee consumption, as well as identify which of coffee''s many active ingredients, or indeed the combination of such, that could induce these health benefits.', NULL, 5, 75),
