  ('1549ec47-9bb4-5e14-8fe3-87884a0a8d71'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1549ec47-9bb4-5e14-8fe3-87884a0a8d71'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f980893f-9656-5156-9bdb-db8943b69826'::uuid, NULL, E'Today''s lecture is postponed because the lecturer is ill.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('154d2f98-02f4-57d4-af4e-c23a52b96d8a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '154d2f98-02f4-57d4-af4e-c23a52b96d8a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'By the time the American colonists took up arms against Great Britain in order to secure their independence, the institution of Black slavery was deeply entrenched. But the contradiction inherent in this situation was, for many, a source of constant embarrassment. "It always appeared a most iniquitous scheme to me,"Abigail Adams wrote her husband in 1774, "to fight ourselves for what we are daily robbing and plundering from those who have as good a right to freedom as we have."Many Americans besides Abigail Adams were struck by the inconsistency of their stand during the War of Independence, and they were not averse to making moves to emancipate the slaves. Quakers and other religious groups organized antislavery societies, while numerous individuals manumitted their slaves. In fact, within several years of the end of the War of Independence, most of the Eastern states had made provisions for the gradual emancipation of slaves.\n\nWhich of the following best states the central idea of the passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The War of Independence exposed to many Americans the contradiction of slavery in a country seeking its freedom and resulted in efforts to resolve that contradiction.', NULL, NULL),
  ('155056be-010f-5d82-98cd-5dc177474d9b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '155056be-010f-5d82-98cd-5dc177474d9b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Springtime', NULL, 'e880fdba-5b69-5241-8632-fe01a507e460'::uuid, NULL, E'The Earth’s temperature is rising. And as it does, springtime phenomena—like the first bloom of flowers—are getting earlier and earlier. But rising temperatures aren''t the only factor. Urban light pollution is also quickening the coming of spring. "So temperature and light are really contributing to a double whammy of making everything earlier." Richard ffrench-Constant, an entomologist at the University of Exeter. He and his colleagues compiled 13 years of data from citizen scientists in the U.K., who tracked the first bud burst of four common trees. Turns out, light pollution—from streetlights in cities, and along roads—pushed bud burst a full week earlier. Way beyond what rising temperatures could achieve. This disruptive timing can ripple through the ecosystem. "The caterpillars that feed on trees are trying to match the hatching of their eggs to the timing of bud burst. Because the caterpillars want to feed on the juiciest and least chemically protected leaves. And it''s not just the caterpillars, of course, that are important. But the knock-on effect is on nesting birds, which are also trying to hatch their chicks at the same time that there''s the maximum number of caterpillars." So earlier buds could ultimately affect the survival of birds, and beyond. The findings are in the Proceedings of the Royal Society B. The world''s becoming increasingly urbanized, and light pollution is growing—which ffrench-Constant says could trick trees into budding earlier and earlier. But smarter lighting—like LEDs that dial down certain wavelengths—could help. "Perhaps the exciting thing is, if we understand more about how light affects this bud burst, we might be able to devise smarter sort of street lighting that has less red components, and therefore less early bud burst." Thus keeping springtime an actual springtime phenomenon.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1554e470-45b5-5b70-a9a7-c43a48ed8e08'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1554e470-45b5-5b70-a9a7-c43a48ed8e08'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'American People', E'The American People: Creating a Nation and a Society examines U.S. history as revealed through the {{1}} of all Americans, both ordinary and extraordinary. With a thought-provoking and rich presentation, the authors explore the complex lives of Americans of all national {{2}} and cultural backgrounds, at all levels of society, and in all {{3}} of the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.experiences, 2.origins, 3.regions', NULL, NULL),
  ('1558e322-688f-57d1-a471-c66b7fb72887'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1558e322-688f-57d1-a471-c66b7fb72887'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3291443c-b1ee-5f47-944f-d959dc5e27b5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Many individuals continue to encounter challenges while working in labs.', NULL, NULL),
  ('155b8c9b-2442-5efb-911d-03333b254a22'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '155b8c9b-2442-5efb-911d-03333b254a22'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dam', E'Dams are huge man-made structures that act as barriers on a river. Today, the main reason people build dams is to produce electricity. They are also built to {{1}} and control the flow of water in a river. {{2}} history, dams have been used to prevent flooding and to irrigate (water) farmland. Dams supply about a sixth of the world''s electricity and they significantly reduce the risk of floods and droughts. They also make water easier to access, especially in desertlike areas, where water is in low supply. There are, {{3}} , some negative effects of damming rivers. Many people''s homes are {{4}} to make space for the dam, and flooding can occur in the reservoir, which is the area behind the dam where water collects . This can cause valuable farmland to become submerged under the lakes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.restrict, 2.Throughout, 3.however, 4.knocked down', NULL, NULL),
  ('155fdeff-cd31-531f-9946-3162bbfc2726'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '155fdeff-cd31-531f-9946-3162bbfc2726'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What natural resource is used in paper industry?', '0cb0402b-78d5-5980-9f49-d66c64db2e20'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Wood', NULL, NULL),
