  ('15c2a8ad-5a47-5350-888f-4359464bfc21'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15c2a8ad-5a47-5350-888f-4359464bfc21'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How many years are there in a half of a decade?', '7b8ef257-7265-59f7-b5ac-d26e336137bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Five', NULL, NULL),
  ('15c87a46-d4fe-5747-a98c-7d0afe20f669'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15c87a46-d4fe-5747-a98c-7d0afe20f669'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Media', E'Digital media and the internet have made the sharing of texts, music and images easier than ever, and the {{1}} of copyright restriction harder. This situation has encouraged the growth of IP law, and {{2}} increased industrial concentration on extending and ''policing'' IP protection, while also leading to the growth of an ''open access'', or ''creative commons'' movement which {{3}} such control of knowledge and {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.enforcement, 2.prompted, 3.challenges, 4.creativity', NULL, NULL),
  ('15cce13e-3468-5008-bc94-0358e50ae7fb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15cce13e-3468-5008-bc94-0358e50ae7fb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5c5dcd37-8c11-5327-953a-7d738af78b4a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There is a brief survey of public support in these colleges.', NULL, NULL),
  ('15d3d14b-e142-5575-96ec-3d94e5bb0459'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15d3d14b-e142-5575-96ec-3d94e5bb0459'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2ac8fa57-bc75-5a4d-bf4b-edc13ad8394a'::uuid, NULL, E'There are three candidates eligible for election in this ward.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('15dbad02-01a6-5815-abd7-26c7994ef5ec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15dbad02-01a6-5815-abd7-26c7994ef5ec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '861eed2f-4c7d-5262-b3e7-1e305ae5f114'::uuid, NULL, E'They have enough work to keep them going.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('15e420bd-7c22-5806-870f-064c0461b323'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15e420bd-7c22-5806-870f-064c0461b323'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In addition to the A, E, what are the other three vowels?', '77f00f87-1e34-5d01-893d-a7b59ba5e3e3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'U / I / O', NULL, NULL),
  ('15e49d2e-89df-5fec-bdb9-3b158a88fced'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15e49d2e-89df-5fec-bdb9-3b158a88fced'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Writing Style', E'Learning to write well in college means learning (or re-learning) how to write clearly and plainly. Now that doesn''t mean that plainness is the only good style, or that you should become a {{1}} to spare, unadorned writing. Formality and ornateness have their place, and in {{2}} hands complexity can take us on a dizzying, breathtaking journey. But most students, most of the time should {{3}} to be sensibly simple to develop a baseline style of short words, active verbs and relatively simple sentence {{4}} clear actions or identities. It''s faster, it makes arguments easier to follow, it increases the chances a busy reader will bother to pay attention, and it lets you {{5}} more attention on your moments of rhetorical flourish which I do not advise abandoning altogether.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.slave, 2.competent, 3.endeavor, 4.carrying, 5.center', NULL, NULL),
  ('15ebdd8a-20b0-57fb-b59d-ea85da1feb67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '15ebdd8a-20b0-57fb-b59d-ea85da1feb67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a piece of paper that you receive from the supermarket cashier after paying?', 'afca6bc8-edfc-50d7-94c3-5176caefec39'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Receipt', NULL, NULL),
  ('1604f735-e1f3-57a4-8971-b20976f4894d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1604f735-e1f3-57a4-8971-b20976f4894d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b2a10157-adcd-58c7-a57d-b89fe0327dd8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We''re trying to come up with new solutions for society''s big issues.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1606c175-d0f1-57a2-81fc-425bc751b3bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1606c175-d0f1-57a2-81fc-425bc751b3bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Givers', NULL, '4c8c73e8-7dc2-56f7-906d-34727fab3a61'::uuid, NULL, E'But actually, it turns out there’s a twist here, because givers are often sacrificing themselves, but they make their organizations better. We have a huge body of evidence — many, many studies looking at the frequency of giving behavior that exists in a team or an organization — and the more often people are helping and sharing their knowledge and providing mentoring, the better organizations do on every metric we can measure: higher profits, customer satisfaction, employee retention — even lower operating expenses. So givers spend a lot of time trying to help other people and improve the team, and then, unfortunately, they suffer along the way. I want to talk about what it takes to build cultures where givers actually get to succeed. So I wondered, then, if givers are the worst performers, who are the best performers? And let me start with the good news: it’s not the takers. Takers tend to rise quickly but also fall quickly in most jobs. And they fall at the hands of matchers. If you’re a matcher, you believe in “An eye for an eye” — a just world. And so when you meet a taker, you feel like it’s your mission in life to just punish the hell out of that person. And that way, justice gets served. Well, most people are matchers. And that means if you’re a taker, it tends to catch up with you eventually; what goes around will come around. And so the logical conclusion is: it must be the matchers who are the best performers. But they’re not. In every job, in every organization I’ve ever studied, the best results belong to the givers again.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('16071b43-2ab3-5f27-9cad-37770f767d7f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16071b43-2ab3-5f27-9cad-37770f767d7f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b5951e02-5cb4-52ee-8c24-db5a8ddc5ef0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tomorrow''s lecture has been canceled due to the power cut.', NULL, NULL),
  ('16076a92-66db-54fa-b2b8-15a22250781a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16076a92-66db-54fa-b2b8-15a22250781a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Planets', E'For decades, astronomers have endeavored to forecast with confidence the fate of planetary systems, including our own, throughout the cosmos. And these experts’ predictions have one central principle: to confidently guess what will eventually befall a planet, you have to know the size of its star.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('16100cb2-0918-56ac-9a86-9e9f127adf44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16100cb2-0918-56ac-9a86-9e9f127adf44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1ff03a15-1f15-5bcb-afed-0ce97b9c1dab'::uuid, NULL, E'The final exam will test material from all chapters covered in class this term.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1617eea1-8c23-5f4f-ad5c-90a8dd9d5321'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1617eea1-8c23-5f4f-ad5c-90a8dd9d5321'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f9ea109c-7529-5f68-9d5e-cd4f74295e11'::uuid, NULL, E'Car permits are available to students and staff.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1619ac5b-fa46-5dbe-976c-96a1117590eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1619ac5b-fa46-5dbe-976c-96a1117590eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '52a2cca8-4b49-5e79-a5b4-91fd7235f398'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The overall job satisfaction by university faculty members has declined.', NULL, NULL),
  ('161ea027-3559-5563-b5a2-51c680e553c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '161ea027-3559-5563-b5a2-51c680e553c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rock Art', E'For anthropologists and archaeologists, rock art is a kind of window into our ancestors'' evolution, migration and lifestyle. These insights that we get from rock art are highly valued by archaeologists because they complement the often scant information provided by excavated objects.\nIt turns out that there are common themes in rock art between sites in Europe and caves where they have discovered rock art in China. In fact, some recurring motifs in rock art have been observed all over the world. It is truly remarkable that the hunter-gatherers of the Yunnan province in China left very similar creations to the Magdalenians, who lived nearly 9,000 km away in Western Europe and thousands of years prior. Both feature outline images of human predators and prey, from bears and lions to stags, horses and bulls.\nNow, both regions were inhabited by hunter-gatherers, on similar terrain. But there''s more to it than that. One thing that we think it might reflect, this similarity of rock art in these distant places, is that human beings are essentially the same in their thinking. So, whether it''s the ancient people of Europe, or in Asia, they did things and drew things in very similar ways.\n\nWhat was significant about the rock art found in the Yunnan province and in Western Europe?', 'ad46c213-f4b8-53db-a94d-8ac5c56b0009'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Rock art in both places depicted animals of interest to humans.\nIt shows that people in widely separated places thought the same way.', NULL, NULL),
  ('161eea07-c95f-5281-b3ac-8c8363dc5eed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '161eea07-c95f-5281-b3ac-8c8363dc5eed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '90cc1b90-a2d0-53d5-b1cd-18ccee305542'::uuid, NULL, E'They were living well, in comparison with people elsewhere in the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('16295d81-399e-51e6-be29-3cff8cb4246d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16295d81-399e-51e6-be29-3cff8cb4246d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Paraphrasing', E'Paraphrasing is often defined as putting a passage from an author into your own words.\nHowever, what are your own words?\nHow different must your paraphrase be from the original?\nThe answer is it should be {{1}} different. The whole point of paraphrasing is to show you have read and understood another person''s ideas, and can summarize them in your own writing style rather than borrowing their phrases. If you just change a few words, or add some bits {{2}} your own to an otherwise reproduced passage, you will probably {{3}} for plagiarism.\nYou should aim to condense and simplify a writer''s ideas and describe them using different sentence structures and expressions. {{4}} also important to credit the original writer by referencing.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.considerably, 2.of, 3.be penalized, 4.It is', NULL, NULL),
  ('1629917f-0303-5bd8-b87f-7efe10a8388f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1629917f-0303-5bd8-b87f-7efe10a8388f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '34f1edab-9fe0-5db4-a9bb-64977f5a76e0'::uuid, NULL, E'Making a profit and protecting the environment needn''t be separate aims.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1633332d-2b99-5d50-9bdd-b85e47c3f7e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1633332d-2b99-5d50-9bdd-b85e47c3f7e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gas Stoves', E'In fact, a meta-analysis concluded that children living in homes with gas stoves were 42% more likely to have asthma symptoms and were 24% more likely to {{1}} lifelong asthma than those living in homes with electric stoves and ovens. During 2019 alone, almost two million cases worldwide of new childhood asthma were {{2}} to be due to nitrogen dioxide pollution — and nitrogen dioxide is a well-known pollutant {{3}} by gas stoves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.develop, 2.estimated, 3.released', NULL, NULL),
  ('1634a88f-e734-541e-9d09-53832f6572f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1634a88f-e734-541e-9d09-53832f6572f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mobile Commerce', E'IT may well change the way you live, yet again. Welcome to the world mobile commerce, where your hand-held device, be it a mobile phone, a personal digital assistant (PDA) or any other wireless application will soon be used for commercial transactions. Skeptical? Consider these facts In Japan, mobile phones are used for location based services where the mobile service providers tie up with a host of other players.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('16366b1b-e709-5fcb-b719-98c7c13d45fb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16366b1b-e709-5fcb-b719-98c7c13d45fb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call a place where you can take trains?', '548e78bc-0d70-5529-8e8f-3e5a8cf13ae1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Train station / railway station', NULL, NULL),
  ('163b2a75-cc27-537b-ac65-01aa5188e8c1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '163b2a75-cc27-537b-ac65-01aa5188e8c1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nanoplastics', E'A new study published in Cell Reports reveals that oral {{1}} to nanoplastics, or plastic particulates smaller than 500 nanometers, can affect brain function in mice by inducing inflammation in the gut. The researchers found that nanoplastics were more readily taken up by macrophages in the intestines than larger microplastics, and triggered the production of a pro-inflammatory cytokine. This cytokine then affected the brain through the gut-brain axis, resulting in cognitive and memory impairments. The authors hope that their findings will raise {{2}} of the potential health risks of nanoplastic pollution, which is a growing environmental concern. They estimate that humans consume about 5 grams of plastic per week, {{3}} to a credit card. The study adds to the growing body of evidence that microplastics and nanoplastics can have {{4}} effects on various biological systems, including the reproductive, immune, endocrine, and nervous systems. Previous studies have shown that aquatic species and laboratory animals in contact with plastic particulates exhibit neurotoxicity and endocrine {{5}} .The authors also note that microplastics have been detected in human tissues, highlighting the need for more research on the impact of plastic pollution on human health.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exposure, 2.awareness, 3.equivalent, 4.adverse, 5.disruption', NULL, NULL),
  ('163daf86-86ff-5d93-97fb-f23fb21b1831'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '163daf86-86ff-5d93-97fb-f23fb21b1831'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lie Detectors', E'A lie detector test includes a polygraph machine that records breathing rate, blood pressure and perspiration. More {{1}} machines include magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the brain. Physiological responses to {{2}} and relevant questions are compared to {{3}} lies. The subject may be asked to intentionally lie to help the examiner {{4}} baseline values. The test typically requires one to three hours to complete.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.sophisticated, 2.irrelevant, 3.identify, 4.establish', NULL, NULL),
  ('16422802-dea4-5ff3-93ed-dcba556a86fd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '16422802-dea4-5ff3-93ed-dcba556a86fd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Irony', E'Many people have problems with irony, both in their everyday lives and as it is used or deployed in literature. We learn early on at school about "dramatic irony", that is, we are told, when the audience of a play is aware of some situation or circumstance, or has information that one or more characters in the play do not. If you like, you are sharing a secret with the writer — you are in the know. Perhaps, as you go about your daily business, irony is not so clear-cut.\nHere''s an example: your neighbour draws your attention to how lovely the dandelions and daisies growing in your lawn are. Now, to someone not familiar with the care and attention many English people give to their gardens, this might need a bit of explanation. Lawns are grass, and are cut and rolled regularly so that a professional golfer could practice his putting on it. Daisies and dandelions are weeds. For a moment — but just for a moment — you wonder how serious your neighbour is being. Does he really think the weeds are lovely or is he telling you — in a rather superior way — that you''re a lousy gardener?\nIrony, however, usually needs an audience; and not only does it need some people to get the point, it also very much needs there to be people who don''t. There is, it has to be said, a rather undemocratic air of superiority about it.\nIrony is slippery, sometimes difficult to get a firm hold on, and can easily backfire, like a joke that falls flat. Those who don''t like irony — usually those who don''t get the point — argue that, in a world that is already difficult enough to deal with, why should we want to complicate things further? Why throw everything you say into doubt? Besides, there''s an unpleasant air of intellectual snobbery about it, and that sort of thing doesn''t go down well any more.', NULL, NULL, E'Many people have problems with irony, which is slippery, sometimes difficult to get a firm hold on, and can easily backfire, because those who don''t like irony argue that in a world that is already difficult enough to deal with, we shouldn''t want to complicate things further.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('1645ce07-42a5-5709-8a09-825c66a69795'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1645ce07-42a5-5709-8a09-825c66a69795'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alternative Energy', E'Nowadays, more and more countries are developing alternative energy, such as electrical energy. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
