  ('17db4b7f-ebb8-553d-a235-56becf46c624'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17db4b7f-ebb8-553d-a235-56becf46c624'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Legal Responsibility', E'Should parents be held legally responsible for the actions of their children? Support your opinion from your study, observations or experiences.', NULL, NULL, E'The question of parental legal responsibility for their children''s actions has become a subject of significant deliberation. This essay asserts that parents should be held legally accountable for their children''s behavior as their guidance profoundly influences their children''s actions and societal contributions.\nOne fundamental reason supporting the positive stance is the moral responsibility parents hold in nurturing and guiding their children. Parents are the primary influencers in a child''s life, responsible for instilling values, ethics, and acceptable behavior. Holding parents legally accountable for their children''s actions serves as a reminder of their duty to cultivate responsible individuals who contribute positively to society. This alignment between parental guidance and legal responsibility ensures that parents remain actively engaged in shaping their children''s moral compass.\nAnother compelling reason for advocating parental legal responsibility is the role it plays in maintaining societal harmony and preventing juvenile delinquency. By enforcing accountability, parents are incentivized to monitor their children''s activities more closely, helping to deter delinquent behaviors. This proactive approach can contribute to safer communities and foster a culture of personal responsibility. Holding parents legally liable also reinforces the importance of maintaining an open line of communication between parents and children, enabling the early identification and resolution of potential issues.\nIn conclusion, the notion of parents being held legally responsible for their children''s actions is grounded in the pivotal roles parents play in their children''s upbringing. To address this issue effectively, governments and communities should collaborate in creating support systems that empower parents to fulfill their role effectively, thus contributing to the overall well-being of society.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('17e18349-ef18-570a-be11-2821dc94887a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17e18349-ef18-570a-be11-2821dc94887a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Major Review(主要报告)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 4, 5, 1, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('17e64cd1-91dd-5f8c-8d6e-558945f8976c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17e64cd1-91dd-5f8c-8d6e-558945f8976c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pathogens', E'People, animals, plants, and fungi all get diseases. Pathogens caused them. Pathogens are things such as a bacteria and viruses. They enter living things and caused them to get sick and sometimes to die. But living things have defenses against pathogens. These defenses are found in their immune systems. There are two types of immune systems, innate and adaptive. First, let''s examine the innate immune system. An innate immune system in a living thing is always active. IT''s an organisms first line of defense against diseases. Let''s think about humans shall be the skin is our first defense. How well it prevents many things from entering the body. Also, the mucous in the nose prevents airborne foreign bodies, many of which are harmful from entering the body. What else? There were defenses in the body as well. For instance, both the stomach and intestines produce acids. Some of them are able to remove pathogens from the food we eat. There is another important defense inside the body. These are white blood cells. When pathogens enter the body, white blood cells move to fight them. IT''s like, uh, like their soldiers fighting an invading army, the white blood cells going where the pathogens are. They attack the pathogens and try to remove them from the body. As you can guess, they''re extremely useful. how about some innate systems and other animals and plants? Let me give you some specific examples of them. Type one.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '087e6d21-1d2e-5554-9255-dbcad1fda161'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The way that the immune system works is remarkably complex. Skin, the first line of defense, can keep foreign objects out of the body, while white blood cells, acting like soldiers fighting invaders, can fight pathogens in the body.', NULL, NULL),
  ('17fa3fdc-ae5c-5832-a3b7-d3b4da05ca2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17fa3fdc-ae5c-5832-a3b7-d3b4da05ca2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Our Ears', E'Our ears are highly sensitive to loud noise. Even very short exposures to high-level sounds – that’s anything above 132 decibels – can cause permanent hearing loss for some people. That’s true even if it’s just a brief blast; a single gunshot or fireworks explosion can cause immediate damage to the ear.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('17fd9bed-4053-53d9-9db4-11b5f2acba60'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17fd9bed-4053-53d9-9db4-11b5f2acba60'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2082baab-bbd6-5bed-8024-78fcf10e681d'::uuid, NULL, E'Parents should model and instill values in their children diligently.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('17fdc917-a852-5b4f-8ec0-c8d2b143f516'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '17fdc917-a852-5b4f-8ec0-c8d2b143f516'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Primary Carers', E'Slightly less than one in five carers (19%) were primary carers (475,000 people). That is, they were the main carer of a person who was limited in carrying out the core everyday activities of mobility, communication or self-care. Both primary carers and the larger group of other carers (close to 2 million) contribute to the wellbeing of older people and people with disabilities. However, because they care for people who otherwise would have difficulty carrying out basic everyday activities, there is particular interest in primary carers: in the contribution they make, their wellbeing, labor force experiences, motivations and the support they receive in caring.\nPrimary carers were more likely than other carers to be assisting someone who lived in the same household (81% compared with 76%). As with caring as a whole, the likelihood of being a primary carer increased with age to peak at age 55-64 years, where one in twenty people were primary carers. However, rather than then declining, the likelihood of being a primary carer remained at around this level among the older age groups. Consequently, primary carers had a somewhat older age profile than other carers. The median age of primary carers was 52 years, compared with 47 years for other carers.\nPrimary carers were more likely than other carers to be female (71% compared with 50%) and less likely to be in the labor force (39% compared with 60%). Women not in the labor force were by far the largest single group among primary carers (44%). In contrast, men employed full-time were the largest single group among other carers (25%).', NULL, NULL, E'While primary carers, the main carer of a person who would otherwise have difficulty carrying out basic everyday activities, have a somehow older age profile, they are more likely to be females who are less likely in the labor force, and men employed full-time were the largest single group among other carers.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('180853f4-acef-5c3f-9e81-2a360603fe1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '180853f4-acef-5c3f-9e81-2a360603fe1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0a564e9e-491e-55ab-a16c-9c154e47f194'::uuid, NULL, E'Don''t hesitate to email me if you have any questions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1809b113-c611-52a3-b532-a68707775108'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1809b113-c611-52a3-b532-a68707775108'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Man-killers', E'Considering their lingering reputation as man-killers, it''s hardly surprising that hackles are raised any time someone brings up the idea of {{1}} wolves to the Scottish Highlands. Debate on this topic has been raging for years; {{2}} would like to see the Highland environment returned to its natural state. Opponents {{3}} the animals'' {{4}} for killing livestock.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reintroducing, 2.proponents, 3.cite, 4.propensity', NULL, NULL),
  ('180ac29b-8ae6-5aa4-a16d-bd104705bb4c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '180ac29b-8ae6-5aa4-a16d-bd104705bb4c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a9e27357-72ed-5db6-8bcf-e10402541771'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Research shows that teachers contribute most to the students'' achievements.', NULL, NULL),
  ('180c54a0-a470-5808-91a7-efd7ff764429'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '180c54a0-a470-5808-91a7-efd7ff764429'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '599e864e-7d3c-5e3d-9972-80e5c1daa413'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A good assistant always makes sure to get all the information needed.', NULL, NULL),
  ('180c6dcd-cb06-50ed-9699-e526d27d8bdf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '180c6dcd-cb06-50ed-9699-e526d27d8bdf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Personal Libraries', E'Scholars build their own personal libraries to support not only particular projects but also general reading in their field. They buy or make photocopies of materials when possible, so they can consult them frequently, mark pages and write annotation on them. When moving into a new field, they add to their collections, usually concentrating on primary texts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('18188e1d-a09b-5012-a7dd-d8796ad8b39c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '18188e1d-a09b-5012-a7dd-d8796ad8b39c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the area designated for aircraft to take off and land?', 'fa2a2806-6f2c-5f5f-a37b-309a3d2cf9ca'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Runway', NULL, NULL),
