  ('1829887e-a3a6-55c9-bb66-63847af6343c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1829887e-a3a6-55c9-bb66-63847af6343c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '46bd75cb-b549-543f-b61b-ebcb054b77a7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Many graduate students can find a job in the communications field.', NULL, NULL),
  ('183302c4-f419-55f7-8570-1e57a6a95a1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '183302c4-f419-55f7-8570-1e57a6a95a1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'New Internet Addiction', E'Young people spend an average of six hours a day online, primarily using their smartphones, according to new research. Older people (those 24 years and older) spend 4.6 hours online. This research highlights the significant impact of digital technology on our daily lives and underscores the need for continued exploration of how we can balance our online and offline activities for optimal well-being.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('183873f1-c938-5eaa-91ea-49daf58badd9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '183873f1-c938-5eaa-91ea-49daf58badd9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ozone', E'Clones of an Eastern cottonwood ( Populus deltoides) in the Bronx and other city spots grew to double the biomass of clones {{1}} outside small towns upstate or on Long Island, says Jillian Gregg, now of the Environmental Protection Agency''s western-ecology division in Corvallis, Ore. The growth gap comes from {{2}} damage, she and her New York colleagues report. Ozone chemists have known that {{3}} may spike skyscraper high in city air, but during a full 24 hours, rural trees actually get a higher cumulative ozone exposure from {{4}} pollution that blows in and lingers. A series of new experiments now shows that this hang-around ozone is the {{5}} factor in tree growth, the researchers say in the July 10 Nature. "This study has profound importance in showing us most vividly that rural areas {{6}} the price for urban pollution," says Stephen P. Long of the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. "This work should be a wake-up call," he adds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.planted, 2.ozone, 3.concentrations, 4.urban, 5.overwhelming, 6.pay', NULL, NULL),
  ('1840e7dc-f068-5445-82f8-28dea37ccdb4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1840e7dc-f068-5445-82f8-28dea37ccdb4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0dec09b9-b6bf-5a42-8bf9-c0eef5052a32'::uuid, NULL, E'Occasionally, large corporations make suboptimal decisions influenced by group conformity.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('18449b73-e5c2-56b1-ab81-d6ff387037ef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '18449b73-e5c2-56b1-ab81-d6ff387037ef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a horse-like animal with a single horn on the head?', '8c37bcf2-0ff4-5b4f-a30c-b8ac0c1f1716'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Unicorn', NULL, NULL),
  ('1848300f-ce0b-5ce2-8ede-b1a0ab4c53b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1848300f-ce0b-5ce2-8ede-b1a0ab4c53b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Spanish Language', E'If after years of Spanish classes, some people still find it impossible to understand some native speakers, they should not worry. This does not {{1}} mean the lessons were wasted. Millions of Spanish speakers use neither standard Latin American Spanish nor Castilian, which {{2}} in US schools. The confusion is partly political - the Spanish-speaking world is very diverse. Spanish is the language of 19 separate countries and Puerto Rico. This means that there is no one standard dialect. The most common Spanish dialect taught in the US is standard Latin American. It is sometimes called "Highland" Spanish since it is generally spoken in the {{3}} areas of Latin America. While each country retains its own {{4}} and has some unique vocabulary, residents of countries such as Mexico, Colombia, Peru, and Bolivia generally speak Latin American Spanish, especially in urban centers. This dialect is noted for its {{5}} of each letter and its strong "r" sounds. This Spanish was spoken in Spain in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries and was brought to the Americas by the early colonists. However, the Spanish of Madrid and of northern Spain, called Castilian, developed {{6}} that never reached the New World. These include the pronunciation of "ci" and "ce" as "th." In Madrid, "gracias" (thank you) becomes "gratheas" (as opposed to "gras-see-as" in Latin America). Another difference is the use of the word "vosotros" (you all, or you guys) as the informal form of "ustedes" in Spain. Castilian sounds to Latin Americans much like British English sounds to US residents.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.necessarily, 2.predominate, 3.mountainous, 4.accents, 5.pronunciation, 6.characteristics', NULL, NULL),
  ('1852b64c-69b6-57a0-88e0-e8d83bdd09f2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1852b64c-69b6-57a0-88e0-e8d83bdd09f2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heart Disease Diagnosis', E'Before a heart disease diagnosis is made, your healthcare provider will gather a full medical history and perform a physical exam. If your doctor suspects heart disease, blood tests will be ordered to check your cholesterol and triglyceride levels, as well as look for proteins that could signal heart failure or plaque in your arteries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('18586e58-045b-5b64-9cf9-23d90efcbfee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '18586e58-045b-5b64-9cf9-23d90efcbfee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Catastrophic Thoughts', E'If your mind is {{1}} with catastrophic thoughts about what’s going to happen, your body responds in kind: the sympathetic nervous system {{2}} in, bracing you for a threat – your breathing becomes fast and shallow, and adrenaline races to your muscles, which can cause you to tremble and feel {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.racing, 2.kicks, 3.faint', NULL, NULL),
  ('185b32b6-9647-569b-8854-6d3453890f2a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '185b32b6-9647-569b-8854-6d3453890f2a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Leading Business Schools', E'In an attempt to lure new students, leading business schools - including Harvard, Stanford, the University of Chicago and Wharton - have moved away from the unofficial admissions and prerequisite of four years'' work experience and instead have set their sights on recent college graduates and so-called early career professionals with only a couple years of work under their belt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('185d7c4a-0f47-5d0d-ac72-2f5d915ed55c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '185d7c4a-0f47-5d0d-ac72-2f5d915ed55c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Technological Leap', E'Every technological leap comes with its compromises. In our {{1}} for advanced AI and robotics, we''ve encountered challenges in maintaining simplicity and user-friendliness. This phenomenon perhaps stems from the fact that most users are {{2}} to traditional interfaces, suggesting a need for {{3}} between innovation and usability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.quest, 2.accustomed, 3.balance', NULL, NULL),
  ('18619837-c0b0-5447-8c44-cac57e9831de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '18619837-c0b0-5447-8c44-cac57e9831de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Happiness', NULL, '7e194b36-858d-5417-b6d1-1537cdb42238'::uuid, NULL, E'As Joanne pointed out, only one country, tiny little Bhutan, wedged between China and India, has adopted the Gross National Happiness as the central index of the government policy, and actually has a good deal of success in education and in health and in economic growth and in environmental preservation. They have a rather sophisticated way of measuring the effects of different policies on people''s happiness. They are the only country to go that far. But you are now beginning to get other countries interested enough to do kind of white paper policy analyses of happiness research—what effects would it have if we used it more for public policy? You are beginning to get countries like Australia, France, Great Britain, that are considering publishing regular statistics on happiness. So it is beginning to become a subject of greater interest for policymakers and legislators in different advanced countries.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1864da50-f4b2-5f53-8240-8bbf4d4f650d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1864da50-f4b2-5f53-8240-8bbf4d4f650d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Shyness', E'A lack of confidence is often {{1}} to something we call shyness. But beneath shyness, there may lie something more surprising, {{2}} and poignant. We suffer from a suspicion of ourselves that gives us a sense that other people will always have {{3}} reasons to dislike us, to think ill of us, to {{4}} our motives and to mock us.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.put down, 2.pernicious, 3.sufficient, 4.question', NULL, NULL),
  ('186abc44-a80f-57af-8387-1222802e4cdc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '186abc44-a80f-57af-8387-1222802e4cdc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '08d4ab0e-ae8d-56ff-a1c5-05a1d2b94f9d'::uuid, NULL, E'He resigned from the company in order to take a more challenging job.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
