  ('19642d61-bae7-5e1d-af8a-34ace0a0b1cf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19642d61-bae7-5e1d-af8a-34ace0a0b1cf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the row of bones down your back?', 'fabb9e27-bedc-532b-a0e3-06868f81639b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Spine / backbone', NULL, NULL),
  ('1968d556-1fd3-53ea-b704-be946cd1161c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1968d556-1fd3-53ea-b704-be946cd1161c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for molten rock beneath the Earth''s surface?', '9165f961-1dc4-50ac-9d6b-f0cc37049f63'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Magma', NULL, NULL),
  ('196d7f37-3fd9-56c8-a135-ca9563591c55'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '196d7f37-3fd9-56c8-a135-ca9563591c55'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Freud', NULL, '25d46d84-c7c8-5c5e-be50-715ad2f6d322'::uuid, NULL, E'For better or worse, we live in a world profoundly affected by Sigmund Freud. If I had to ask you to name a famous psychologist, the answer of most of you would be Freud. He was the most famous psychologist ever and he had a profound influence on the 20th and 21st century. Some biographical information: he was born in the 1850s. He spent most of his life in Vienna, Austria, and, but he died in London and he escaped to London soon after retreating there at the beginning of World War Two as the Nazis began to occupy where he lived. He was one of the most famous scholars ever but he was not known for any single discovery. Instead, he was known for the development of an encompassing theory of mind, one that he developed over the span of many decades. He was in his time extremely well known, a celebrity recognized on the street, and throughout his life. He was a man of extraordinary energy and productivity, in part because he was a very serious cocaine addict, but also just in general. He was just a high-energy sort of person.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('19703ea0-6b5e-59f4-822e-268d36ed13e4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19703ea0-6b5e-59f4-822e-268d36ed13e4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Melk', NULL, '595b8cea-18cd-5a9c-9b97-a2898d0b5975'::uuid, NULL, E'The Melk is not typical of all monasteries for many reasons. Firstly, it is very grand which most especially later foundations aren''t. Secondly, it was founded in the countryside, whereas in 17th and 18th centuries, a good proportion of foundations were made in Towns. Thirdly, it still owns substantial amount of land, because fourthly it lies in the Austrian Republic, the only European country where grand old monasteries have been in continuous existence, since they were founded nine hundred a thousand even in one case twelve hundred years ago.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1972f300-8a17-5f35-b49c-d6e4d676bffd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1972f300-8a17-5f35-b49c-d6e4d676bffd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '23b4f904-7c2b-5c03-b53a-02caa746f467'::uuid, NULL, E'I’ve always been interested in biology and physics.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1975b03b-8bdf-5387-a86b-792948ca64ff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1975b03b-8bdf-5387-a86b-792948ca64ff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dark-silvery Rock', E'People in parts of western Africa and southwestern Asia were the first to realize that the dark-silvery rocks poking out of the earth could be worked into tools and weapons, sometime around 1500 B.C., evidence shows. The metal was probably discovered there {{1}} accident when some ore was dropped into a fire and cooled into wrought iron, historians think. The eureka moment didn''t reach Europe for {{2}} 500 years, traveling slowly north and west through Greece, Italy, central Europe and finally to the British Isles {{3}} the spread of the famous Celtic tribes. The Celts diffused iron technology over much of the continent through warfare, where their victory was assured due to the strength of iron weapons.\nPerhaps not the most peaceful of cultural exchanges, but where the technology did travel, it caught on fast.\nIron {{4}} life a lot easier in those days, when just living to the age of 45 was a feat. By that time, much of Europe had settled into small village life, {{5}} the soil with bronze and stone tools. Iron farming tools, such as sickles and plough tips, made the process more efficient and allowed farmers {{6}} tougher soils, try new crops and have more time for other activities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.by, 2.another, 3.with, 4.made, 5.toiling, 6.to exploit', NULL, NULL),
  ('197696f2-2dda-5e82-b099-688c821bdd44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '197696f2-2dda-5e82-b099-688c821bdd44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '64543058-c326-5646-a6fe-3ea87b6f2be0'::uuid, NULL, E'There is widespread concern that new houses will be built on protected land.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('197a17dc-94d9-5c03-a3d5-cdea1cadd071'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '197a17dc-94d9-5c03-a3d5-cdea1cadd071'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Work', E'The space work for an astronaut can be inside or outside. Inside they can monitor machines and the work is {{1}} out alongside the craft. They also need to make sure of the space {{2}} . {{3}} the craft, they can see how the seeds react in the space. Some seed company send seeds to them to {{4}} how seeds change their biological character. When outside the craft, they can set {{5}} experiments or clean up the space rubbish.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.carried, 2.travel, 3.Outside, 4.investigate, 5.up', NULL, NULL),
  ('197a7287-fe1e-5ad6-a7ee-ee59673c4f5b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '197a7287-fe1e-5ad6-a7ee-ee59673c4f5b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd3f9b01d-172e-500f-a0a5-25995b3efb03'::uuid, NULL, E'The whole class were told to stay behind after school.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1982a90c-34d0-504e-bf5a-190f830c413a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1982a90c-34d0-504e-bf5a-190f830c413a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Jobs', E'Since the coronavirus pandemic hit the U.S, over 40 millions of Americans have filed unemployment claims, but some benefited from the crisis already in mid-march. The largest online retailer Amazon announced its plans to hire an additional a hundred thousand people. A lot of other places are looking for delivery drivers and grocery stores are in constant need of employees. We have gone to a mobile world. We all are shopping online, will buy online, and I think that''s probably going to continue. I don''t think people are going to be anxious to get out to the stores anytime soon. They''ve learned the convenience for that. So I think e-commerce is really going to continue to grow and that means more jobs are in industry.\n\nThe woman believes that e-commerce is going to continue to grow because ___', '010df607-6b62-533b-93df-dfc7b61f4d96'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'consumers have learned how convenient it is to shop online.', NULL, NULL),
  ('198ad993-fb7a-51e4-8df9-3793d00c5a80'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '198ad993-fb7a-51e4-8df9-3793d00c5a80'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'Our knowledge of the oceans a hundred years ago was confined to the two dimensional shape of the sea surface. And the hazards of navigation presented by the irregularities in depth of the shallow water close to the land. The open sea was deep and mysterious, and anyone who gave more than a passing thought to the bottom confines of the oceans probably assumed that the sea bed was flat. Sir james clark ross had obtained a sounding of over two thousand four hundred fathoms in eighteen thirty nine. But it was not until eighteen sixty nine when h m s porcupine was put at the disposal of the royal society for several cruises, that a series of deep soundings was obtained in the atlantic. And the first samples were collected by dredging the bottom shortly after this, the famous h m s challenger expedition established the study of the sea floor as a subject worthy of the most qualified physicists. And geologists at burst of activity associated with the laying of submarine cables soon confirmed the challenges. Observation that many parts of the ocean were two to three miles deep, and the existence of underwater features of considerable.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'f77c25b4-076c-58e0-96b0-a3a2e0f83a76'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'magnitude', NULL, NULL),
  ('198d03c3-3301-53d2-96e3-56a678f7ba0c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '198d03c3-3301-53d2-96e3-56a678f7ba0c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6554dab4-00fd-5a04-be47-d7ac393808dc'::uuid, NULL, E'We have worked together to promote a healthy research culture.', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO _pte_local_seed_questions (question_public_id, created_at, updated_at, deleted, pte_task_type, task_type_key, task_type_section, visibility, tenant_id, status, revision_group_public_id, revision_number, supersedes_public_id, is_current, version, rejection_reason, title, prompt_text, audio_prompt_ref, image_prompt_ref, reference_answer_text, correct_answer_text, min_word_count, max_word_count) VALUES
  ('198d54af-5937-5f20-8f75-5c7de75f8984'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '198d54af-5937-5f20-8f75-5c7de75f8984'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Plants Research', E'Plants serve as the conduit of energy into the biosphere, provide food and materials used by humans, and shape our environment. According to Ehrhardt and Frommer, the three major challenges facing humanity in our time are food, energy, and environmental degradation. All three are plant related.\nAll of our food is produced by plants, either directly or indirectly via animals that eat them. Plants are a source of energy production. And they are intimately involved in climate change and a major factor in a variety of environmental concerns, including agricultural expansion and its impact on habitat destruction and waterway pollution.\nWhat''s more, none of these issues are independent of each other. Climate change places additional stresses on the food supply and on various habitats. So, plant research is instrumental in addressing all of these problems and moving into the future. For plant research to move significantly forward, Ehrhardt and Frommer say technological development is critical, both to test existing hypotheses and to gain new information and generate fresh hypotheses. If we are to make headway in understanding how these essential organisms function and build the foundation for a sustainable future, then we need to apply the most advanced technologies available to the study of plant life, they say.', NULL, NULL, E'Plants serve as the conduit of energy into the biosphere, provide food and materials used by humans, and shape our environment, and the three major challenges facing humanity are plant related, since all of our food is produced by plants, which are a source of energy production, where plant research is instrumental in addressing all of these problems and moving into the future, so technological development is critical.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('19a27a6e-a1fe-5829-b2ad-0042d7283c37'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19a27a6e-a1fe-5829-b2ad-0042d7283c37'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the chemical that is used for destroying plants, especially weeds?', '36130fc3-0533-54d7-bfe7-58e266d8b113'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Herbicide', NULL, NULL),
  ('19aa9182-42e4-56b2-b1c8-6ced559bd01c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19aa9182-42e4-56b2-b1c8-6ced559bd01c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tattoos', NULL, '8c5f30c8-83dc-52c3-a49d-6a8d012ca79b'::uuid, NULL, E'Tattoos have often been presented in popular media as either marks of the dangerous and deviant or trendy youth fads. But while tattoo styles come and go, and their meaning has differed greatly across cultures, the practice is as old as civilization itself. Decorative skin markings have been discovered in human remains all over the world, with the oldest found on a Peruvian mummy dating back to 6,000 BCE. But have you ever wondered how tattooing really works? You may know that we shed our skin, losing about 30-40,000 skin cells per hour. That’s about 1,000,000 per day. So, how come the tattoo doesn’t gradually flake off along with them? The simple answer is that tattooing involves getting pigment deeper into the skin than the outermost layer that gets shed. Throughout history, different cultures have used various methods to accomplish this. But the first modern tattooing machine was modeled after Thomas Edison’s engraving machine and ran on electricity. Tattooing machines used today insert tiny needles, loaded with dye, into the skin at a frequency of 50 to 3,000 times per minute. The needles punch through the epidermis, allowing ink to seep deep into the dermis, which is composed of collagen fibers, nerves, glands, blood vessels and more. Every time a needle penetrates, it causes a wound that alerts the body to begin the inflammatory process, calling immune system cells to the wound site to begin repairing the skin. And it is this very process that makes tattoos permanent.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('19ada1d3-b363-5430-88e9-e388a2d50b4e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19ada1d3-b363-5430-88e9-e388a2d50b4e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drone-delivering', E'Delivering packages with drones will reduce CO2 emissions in certain circumstances as compared to truck deliveries, a brand new study from University of Washington transportation engineers finds.\nIn a paper to be revealed in an upcoming issue of Transportation Analysis Part D, researchers found that drones tend to have CO2 emissions advantages over trucks once the drones don''t have to fly terribly far to their destinations or once a delivery route has few recipients.\nTrucks, which may provide environmental edges by carrying everything from garments to appliances to furniture in a very single trip, become a more climate-friendly option once a delivery route has several stops or is farther off from a central warehouse.\nFor small, light-weight packages — a bottle of drugs or a kid''s bathing costume — drones perform particularly well. However, the carbon benefits erode because the weight of a package increases since these unmanned aerial vehicles have to be compelled to use extra energy to remain aloft with a significant load.', NULL, NULL, E'Delivering packages with drones will reduce CO2 emissions in certain circumstances, as drones tend to have CO2 emissions advantages over trucks once the drones don''t have to fly terribly far to their destinations or once a delivery route has few recipients, whereas trucks become a more climate-friendly option once a delivery route has several stops or is farther off from a central warehouse, while for small, light-weight packages, drones perform particularly well.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('19b4bb5a-007a-5e20-bc67-e3829fa70ac1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '19b4bb5a-007a-5e20-bc67-e3829fa70ac1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Contribution to Book', E'Many individuals have unwittingly contributed to this book through sharing ideas with us as colleagues, students, practitioners, tourists, and residents of destination areas. They are too numerous to thank individually. And indeed, it is not possible to isolate exactly their specific contributions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
