  ('1c4a7df9-960b-5737-a489-2d096c8a0746'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c4a7df9-960b-5737-a489-2d096c8a0746'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'6G Networks', E'High-speed Internet access has become crucial in a world where school, business, personal life and emergency communications increasingly take place through a handheld device. But surprisingly large swaths of the U.S. still lack a speedy-enough broadband or cellular connection. One potential solution could be a sixth-generation cellular network, which experts say will add a space-based system to ground-based coverage options.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1c4f1daf-ee8b-5342-ba33-9dbb28152b1e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c4f1daf-ee8b-5342-ba33-9dbb28152b1e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'John Robertson', E'When he was awarded an Honorary Degree by the University of Newcastle, even John Robertson himself must surely have looked back in wonder at his astonishing rise to success. The year was 1910, and those assembled were to hear not only of his generosity to the University, which enabled it to contribute to the pioneering research into tropical diseases being carried out at that time, but also of his humanitarian work in southern Africa, where he was ahead of his time in improving the working conditions of local mine workers. To those who knew John in his youth, it will have come as no surprise to hear of his success. He was now enjoying the rewards of the fierce determination, desire to succeed and extraordinary ability to acquire knowledge, which they had noticed in the young man.\n\nWhat does the reader of this text learn about John Robertson?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'His abilities were evident at a young age.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c5f2ea1-e00c-59cd-820e-0ef73435037c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c5f2ea1-e00c-59cd-820e-0ef73435037c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Body Language', E'Body language—how you dress as well as your mannerisms—is another powerful communication element. The core idea is that we make judgments based on body language, and those judgments can {{1}} meaningful life outcomes. In one example {{2}} , social scientist Alex Todorov found that one-second judgments of political candidates’ faces predict 70 percent of U.S. Senate and gubernatorial race outcomes. What is perhaps more important, however, is that our body language {{3}} how we judge, think, and feel about ourselves. The key {{4}} from this is that our bodies change our minds. That is, we can change not only how we are perceived but how we perceive ourselves by {{5}} our body language. As a speaker, you must be conscious of, and cultivate, the presence you bring to your speech.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.predict, 2.cited, 3.reflects, 4.takeaway, 5.managing', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c69b3df-093c-5bd1-b803-b0706ab150f4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c69b3df-093c-5bd1-b803-b0706ab150f4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'FIB', E'The scientific {{1}} needs to be involved in promoting science education, {{2}} evolution. So says the January issue of the FASEB Journal. FASEB is the Federation of American Societies for Experimental Biology. Sixteen other organizations also signed on to the recommendation, including the {{3}} Academy of Sciences and the American Institute of Physics. The article notes that the introduction of nonscience, such as {{4}} and intelligent design, undermines fundamentals of science education—such as using the scientific method, understanding how to reach scientific consensus and telling scientific explanations for natural phenomena apart from nonscientific ones.\nThe article {{5}} a survey of a thousand likely US voters. Those able to answer simple questions about plate tectonics, proper antibiotic use and prehistory were far more likely to support evolution education. Said journal editor Gerald, "The bottom line is that the world is round, humans evolved from an extinct species, and Elvis is dead. This survey is a wake-up call for anyone who supports teaching information based on {{6}} rather than speculation or hope; people want to hear the truth, and they want to hear it from scientists."', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.community, 2.including, 3.National, 4.creationism, 5.included, 6.evidence', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c6cb659-7932-5c1e-ae38-2822e6d0d616'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c6cb659-7932-5c1e-ae38-2822e6d0d616'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skin and Hair', E'Skin and hair will change with age. The skin becomes drier, thinner, and less {{1}} during the aging process. Scars and imperfections become more {{2}} as fewer cells grow underneath the surface of the skin. Exposure to the sun, or photoaging, {{3}} these changes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.elastic, 2.noticeable, 3.accelerates', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c6cbcaa-ea21-508d-9c26-f2e88f5e1620'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c6cbcaa-ea21-508d-9c26-f2e88f5e1620'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Physical Activity', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 3, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c719e69-99dd-5a9d-80cb-5a7547a60c13'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c719e69-99dd-5a9d-80cb-5a7547a60c13'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biological Systems', E'Since biological systems with signs of {{1}} engineering are unlikely to have arisen from accidents or coincidences, their {{2}} must come from natural selection, and hence should have {{3}} useful for survival and reproduction in the environments in which humans evolved.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.complex, 2.organization, 3.functions', NULL, NULL),
  ('1c7bed64-3589-579e-8c4c-d3c80217392d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c7bed64-3589-579e-8c4c-d3c80217392d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Public Transportation', E'What are the advantages and problems of cheaper public transportation? Give your opinion from your own experience.', NULL, NULL, E'Public transportation is an essential part of modern society, and its affordability is a crucial factor in determining its accessibility. Cheaper public transportation has been a topic of discussion for a long time, and it has its advantages and problems. In this essay, I will discuss the advantages and problems of cheaper public transportation based on my own experience.\nOne of the most significant advantages of cheaper public transportation is that it can make transportation more accessible to low-income individuals and families. Cheaper fares mean that people who cannot afford private transportation can still travel to work, school, or other places they need to go. This can help reduce social inequality and promote equal opportunities for all.\nHowever, there are also some problems associated with cheaper public transportation. One of the most significant issues is that it can lead to overcrowding and discomfort for passengers. Cheaper fares may encourage more people to use public transportation, which can lead to increased demand and overcrowding. This can result in uncomfortable conditions for passengers, such as standing-room-only situations or long wait times.\nIn conclusion, cheaper public transportation has its advantages and problems. While it can make transportation more accessible to low-income individuals and families and reduce traffic congestion and air pollution, it can also lead to overcrowding and discomfort for passengers and may not be financially sustainable in the long run. In my opinion, the benefits of cheaper public transportation outweigh the problems, but it is important to find a balance between affordability and service quality to ensure that public transportation remains accessible, comfortable, and sustainable for all.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('1c980f49-5b91-58ab-95be-22eb129e49fd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1c980f49-5b91-58ab-95be-22eb129e49fd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '85403bd5-bc77-5bf9-9b1c-443f691e9bcf'::uuid, NULL, E'We encourage participants to develop their own understanding of the market.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1ca21332-2cd0-504c-91ee-406855a90329'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1ca21332-2cd0-504c-91ee-406855a90329'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coastal Hypothesis', E'The coastal hypothesis {{1}} an economy based on marine mammal hunting, saltwater fishing, shellfish gathering, and the use of watercraft. {{2}} of the barrier of ice to the east, the Pacific Ocean to the west, and populated areas to the north, there may have been a greater {{3}} for people to move in a southerly direction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.suggests, 2.Because, 3.impetus', NULL, NULL),
  ('1ca2c404-311c-59c0-955a-7f63940d0b77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1ca2c404-311c-59c0-955a-7f63940d0b77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skin Types', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('1cb32eb6-c2b2-538a-88b8-8e4375259386'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1cb32eb6-c2b2-538a-88b8-8e4375259386'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hair', E'All mammals have hair—commonly called fur when it''s on your cat or a koala. And the thickness of individual hairs varies from species to species. For example, elephant hairs are more than four times thicker than a strand from an adult human.\n"Normally, when the animal is larger, the hair tends to be thicker."\nUniversity of California, San Diego, materials scientist Wen Yang. She''s interested in how biological structures like hair hold up under stress. That interest comes from a desire to design better synthetic materials.\nYang''s team tested the tensile strength of hair from eight different mammal species, including humans. They subjected those hairs to increasing levels of tension until the fibers broke. The researchers assumed that thick hair—from giraffes, elephants and boars, for example, would be more robust. But they were wrong.\n\nWhich of the following statements about hair are correct?', '1850f632-f982-56fd-b3a3-7975614ccec5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Generally speaking, the size of an animal is directly proportional to the thickness of its hair.\nDifferent species have different hair thickness.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1cb3e826-c2f7-54e0-84eb-af8c58591afa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1cb3e826-c2f7-54e0-84eb-af8c58591afa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pursuit of Wellness', E'The pursuit of wellness has gained increasing attention in recent years due to its potential benefits for preventing chronic diseases, promoting longevity, and improving quality of life. However, achieving optimal wellness requires a holistic approach that considers the unique needs and circumstances of each individual. Wellness interventions and programs should be tailored to the specific needs of individuals and communities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1cb40785-d144-5ebf-b3a7-c8d6d0e3063f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1cb40785-d144-5ebf-b3a7-c8d6d0e3063f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5a2b20cf-12e5-5193-a821-e2c2a28cce99'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Typical mistakes are difficult to find.', NULL, NULL),
