  ('1d0193dd-ffd1-5350-b5e0-6ae0511f3282'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d0193dd-ffd1-5350-b5e0-6ae0511f3282'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '30444757-595f-5f61-b36f-fc7d5bc4d56f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She was sitting outside a cafe in the sunshine.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d0475fe-3d4e-5009-acae-f673c75cbc08'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d0475fe-3d4e-5009-acae-f673c75cbc08'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8d7f44a1-c2e5-5168-a415-b178edf81ba9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Relying on natural ability will not get you far in science.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d067187-9154-5215-a97a-2dde87b58b2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d067187-9154-5215-a97a-2dde87b58b2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3417e1c4-60f2-51cd-a316-afaba875f8a4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The school system is feeling the impact of the budget crisis.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d094984-f376-5cbd-a1e4-db5a6e0077f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d094984-f376-5cbd-a1e4-db5a6e0077f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Revolution', E'I want to look now at the three main approaches historians have taken towards the English Revolution or Civil War. There is a fourth point of view, taken up by most schoolchildren when they first meet the subject, but it can hardly be called historical. On the one hand, schoolchildren tend to have a romantic image of the Cavaliers, who were supporters of the monarchy, as aristocratic, charming, flashily dressed, and up for a bit of fun. On the other hand, they tend to regard the Roundheads or Puritans, who were followers of Oliver Cromwell, as miserable, working-class, dressed in black, and insisting on a life without luxuries. It isn''t difficult then to takes sides.\nThe first approach, which prevailed up until the middle of the 20th century, was that the Revolution was part of the age-old battle between parliament and the monarchy, with parliament representing the traditional rights of Englishmen against the attempt by the Royal Family to increase its power and dictate law. In reaction to this, the second approach saw it as a working-class revolution and an important stage in the development of capitalism. In other words, they saw it as a class war, and a forerunner of the French Revolution and those that came after. Historians who supported the third approach saw that things weren''t as clear cut as the others thought. Instead of seeing the Revolution as the result of long-term trends in the country''s history, and therefore almost unavoidable, they focused on the details of the period immediately leading up to its outbreak and allowed for its unpredictability. The two sides,also, weren''t so clear cut, with some aristocrats supporting parliament and some members of the working class fighting on the side of the monarchy.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'a6104c3c-51dc-5342-b0bc-f77fd096b2bf'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There are three main interpretations of the English Revolution. The longest lasting interpretation was that the Revolution was the almost inevitable outcome of an age-old power struggle between parliament and crown. The second sees il as a class struggle, and a lead-up to the French and other revolutions. Finally, the third interpretation sees the other two as too fixed, not allowing for unpredictability, and that the outcome could have gone either way.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d0a962e-f8f6-5e18-9c42-afa90805de5f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d0a962e-f8f6-5e18-9c42-afa90805de5f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e869241e-cdf2-515d-8dc2-964b738203a1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Scientists are working hard to understand climate change better.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d0c999c-4b00-533d-bd0f-23317d0d6be4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d0c999c-4b00-533d-bd0f-23317d0d6be4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'daead4d2-7471-5b09-8f83-fc0d78e29396'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The remnants trickled down to the lowest part of the valley.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d0ea973-a823-5750-8c45-abc656350de0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d0ea973-a823-5750-8c45-abc656350de0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'febf6580-9cfb-5172-9204-19d4e0fd7fda'::uuid, NULL, E'The study showed that people''s moods can be affected by news and weather reports.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d11b6b7-e379-5d11-b675-5cbd8b2d1baa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d11b6b7-e379-5d11-b675-5cbd8b2d1baa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Organic Vegetable', E'Although compared to {{1}} grown vegetables, organic food items are less likely to have pesticide residues, organic produce can also lead to health risks. Leafy greens are particularly {{2}} to fecal contamination due to their {{3}} to the ground and the likelihood of humans consuming them without cooking.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.conventionally, 2.susceptible, 3.proximity', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d12fee2-5be3-5ee3-afae-63f28a14a256'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d12fee2-5be3-5ee3-afae-63f28a14a256'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Morning Work', E'Some people prefer to get up early in the morning and start the day’s work. Others prefer to get up later in the day and work until late at night. Which do you prefer? Explain it with your own experience.', NULL, NULL, E'As someone who prefers to get up early in the morning and start the day’s work, I firmly believe that this approach offers numerous advantages that make it the ideal choice for me.\nFirstly, rising early allows me to kickstart my day with a sense of purpose and productivity. When I wake up early, I am greeted by a quiet and serene environment, free from distractions. This peaceful atmosphere enables me to focus my mind and channel my energy towards the tasks at hand. Consequently, I find that I am more alert, motivated, and capable of tackling challenges head-on. By capitalizing on the early morning hours, I can accomplish important tasks without interruptions, setting a positive tone for the rest of the day.\nFurthermore, getting up early provides me with ample time for self-care and personal development. By carving out extra time in the morning, I can engage in activities that nurture my physical, mental, and emotional well-being. Whether it is engaging in regular exercise, practicing mindfulness through meditation or journaling, or indulging in a leisurely breakfast, these rituals enhance my overall quality of life. This self-investment not only boosts my energy levels but also equips me with the resilience and focus necessary to navigate the challenges that lie ahead.\nIn conclusion, while individuals may have different preferences regarding their waking hours and work patterns, I firmly stand by the belief that getting up early is the optimal approach for me. Embracing the early morning hours empowers me to seize the day with purpose, maximize my productivity, and cultivate a healthy work-life balance. Ultimately, the choice of whether to rise early or work late rests upon individual preferences and circumstances. However, for me, the rewards of embracing the early morning hours are immeasurable, making it an integral part of my daily routine.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('1d15dba0-690c-54d7-9d33-9cb587131bf0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d15dba0-690c-54d7-9d33-9cb587131bf0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In the word ''postgraduate'', what does the ''post'' mean?', '173374d2-fed8-5ae6-85e3-ea92503b80fc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'After', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d19d8a7-ba72-53ab-bc0f-9e6a47e115c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d19d8a7-ba72-53ab-bc0f-9e6a47e115c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Evolution', E'A creature may have fine physical defenses such as hard armor or sharp spines. It may have powerful chemical defenses such as an {{1}} smell or a foul taste but none of these defenses is much used in the {{2}} for survival unless the animal also has the right behavior to go with it. Evolution shapes a living creature’s size and color, and it also {{3}} an animal’s actions and behavioral patterns. The most {{4}} behaviors are instinctive or in-built. In other words, the creatures can perform the actions without having to learn what to do it by {{5}} and error.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.appalling, 2.struggle, 3.shapes, 4.automatic, 5.trial', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d1dcb04-9e0c-576a-9ef9-62bec05f27b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d1dcb04-9e0c-576a-9ef9-62bec05f27b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '084033b6-09ee-53bd-acdb-2bc91f4118fe'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Most critics agreed with the new theory, but a few disagreed.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d1f0753-2690-58a4-9f6f-9d6618986cf1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d1f0753-2690-58a4-9f6f-9d6618986cf1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Childhood', E'Childhood is a pivotal phase in a person''s life, and it is essential to provide children with a nurturing and supportive environment that {{1}} their overall growth and development. It is during this period that children form the foundations of their character, values, and aspirations. Parents, caregivers, and educators play a crucial role in shaping a child''s early experiences. They must {{2}} the importance of positive role modeling and providing children with opportunities to explore their interests and passions. Moreover, fostering creativity and curiosity is vital in a child''s life. Encouraging them to {{3}} their innate talents and express themselves through art, music, and other forms of self-expression can ignite a lifelong passion for creativity. In addition to emotional and intellectual development, physical health is a cornerstone of a child''s well-being. Proper nutrition, regular exercise, and access to healthcare are vital in ensuring that children {{4}} their full potential.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.fosters, 2.recognize, 3.nurture, 4.achieve', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d23f8cf-54d4-5709-8d27-d457220e44ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d23f8cf-54d4-5709-8d27-d457220e44ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Implicit&Explicit Memory', NULL, 'daf6c4bb-2f92-58f8-abc0-4dd0d4d17b2a'::uuid, NULL, E'I want you to try and remember two things. First, I want you to try and remember learning how to ride a bike. Maybe you have a scar you received when you flipped over the handlebars. The next thing I want you to remember is how to ride a bike. The reason I asked you to recall both of these memories is that they belong to two different designated realms of memory. Memory is a fluid and dynamic system that is exceedingly complicated. To this end, psychologists have attempted to divide memory up to make it easier to study. There are two main categories. Explicit memory is a memory that can be intentionally and consciously recalled. This is your memory of riding a bike and falling over the handlebars, and skinning your knee. The other is implicit memory which is an exponential functional form of memory that cannot be consciously recalled. This is your memory of how to ride a bike or how to balance. These are often not tied to a visual memory, but a more like muscle memory. The examples of implicit memory include using language naturally, driving and reading, and answering multiple questions in the test, etc., will be natural. Let''s look at explicit and implicit memory in a little more detail, and see how age influences these. It is an experimental or functional form of memory. Explicit memory consists of a great deal of highly personal memories related to time, space and people. It is totally different from implicit memory. Now, if we look at the examples of explicit memory, it includes remembering people''s birthdays and answering multiple questions on the test.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d2ad42c-46f0-5636-847c-0b38e169d262'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d2ad42c-46f0-5636-847c-0b38e169d262'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Teamwork', NULL, 'c64440f0-f229-53be-bd27-35a03a03d8d3'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, let''s turn our focus to the bedrock of collaborative success — teamwork. In the realm of education, it''s teamwork that often propels us from the theoretical to the practical, from individual knowledge to collective wisdom. Engaging in teamwork enhances our learning experiences. It encourages the exchange of ideas, allowing us to gain multiple perspectives on a single topic. Research from educational psychology suggests that students who study in groups tend to develop stronger communication skills and understand material more deeply than those who work alone. Teamwork also mirrors the realities of the professional world. Rarely do we see isolated efforts in workplaces; instead, it''s the synergy of a team that drives innovation and success. By mastering the art of collaboration now, we are setting ourselves up for future triumphs in whatever careers we choose to pursue. As we continue on our academic journey, let''s embrace every opportunity to join forces with our peers. Together, we are stronger, wiser, and more capable than we could ever be alone.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d339654-7f39-5950-86d4-3f389168e7fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d339654-7f39-5950-86d4-3f389168e7fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a798cbfe-a99a-550b-a513-34a1ca13d9a7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The north campus car park will be closed on Sunday.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d347a2c-9e0a-5570-87f1-cd5390a0adba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d347a2c-9e0a-5570-87f1-cd5390a0adba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Introvert and Extrovert (B)', E'Although introvert and extrovert personality types differ from one another on various grounds, the major difference between the two is their source of rejuvenation. While for extroverts, this may mean interaction or excursions with friends and family, the same may mean reading a book or listening to music for introverts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d41b454-bba8-5cd1-990d-514ae3a6233b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d41b454-bba8-5cd1-990d-514ae3a6233b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Colonial Era', E'At the end of the colonial era, as many new nations gained independence, relative levels of economic development became an important criterion by which to distinguish between countries. The former colonial powers and {{1}} parts of the world generally became known as advanced industrial, or developed countries, {{2}} former colonies and poorer nations became known as less developed, or more positively, developing countries. Critics of the {{3}} distribution of wealth across the globe highlighted the role which wealth creation in some places had played in impoverishing poorer nations and, rather, described them as actively underdeveloped. The question as to {{4}} economic change is developing or underdeveloping countries remains a vital issue, as the debate over sweatshops highlights.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.wealthier, 2.while, 3.uneven, 4.whether', NULL, NULL),
