  ('1d5f7364-0442-5b4a-9b66-f4a98a17c63c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d5f7364-0442-5b4a-9b66-f4a98a17c63c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cybersecurity', E'With increased reliance on digital technologies, cybersecurity is a critical concern. Protecting sensitive data, preventing cyberattacks, and safeguarding privacy are paramount. Governments, businesses, and individuals must stay vigilant, implementing robust security measures and promoting cyber hygiene practices to mitigate risks in an interconnected world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d62e15e-6247-5db5-a676-480f6ded1d2b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d62e15e-6247-5db5-a676-480f6ded1d2b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Breakfast Option', E'For many people, breakfast is the day''s least-exciting meal. Our breakfast choice frequently {{1}} utilitarian needs; foods at breakfast are {{2}} simple, quick and easy to prepare and eat, and valued for the calorie boost that {{3}} the body and brain after a night''s rest. When people find a breakfast option they like, they {{4}} stick with it, day after day, scientists have found.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reflects, 2.typically, 3.revives, 4.generally', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d63c310-d54b-50e6-b934-d163f37fbb5b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d63c310-d54b-50e6-b934-d163f37fbb5b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5c257891-de40-5246-a6ee-f53019bb4cc6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Journalism has undergone many changes in recent years.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d64c6d6-2dc1-5443-87d0-f12b86803673'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d64c6d6-2dc1-5443-87d0-f12b86803673'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Forests', E'Forests {{1}} 31% of the land area on our planet. They help people thrive and survive by, for example, {{2}} water and air and providing people with jobs; some 13.2 million people across the world have a job in the forest {{3}} . Forests are also {{4}} to more than three-quarters of the world’s life on land.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.cover, 2.purifying, 3.sector, 4.home', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d66c0cc-a314-5395-8249-723ae8bb8de2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d66c0cc-a314-5395-8249-723ae8bb8de2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biomimicry', NULL, 'ea1c6ebd-2f3e-5ef1-ab34-5d669a0af600'::uuid, NULL, E'We often think of technology and invention and research as being somehow more sophisticated a proposition than nature - but actually, when we think about it, there are lots of really useful concepts that technology can take from the natural world. People are beginning to remember that other organisms on earth are doing things in a very similar way to what we need to do. And they''re looking closely at what we can learn from nature.\nTake the bright screens on our mobile phones - now, this brightness, this effect that they''ve managed to achieve there, came partly as a result of research into the iridescence of the wings of butterflies and the antireflective coatings that moths have on their eyes. And it doesn''t end there. They''re looking at what makes a spider''s web so strong, how glow worms produce light with almost zero energy. The list goes on. And this area of research is called biomimicry - that''s ''bio'', as in biology or life and ''mimicry'', copying or imitating. It''s a very interesting field of study.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d6a0f1d-f1e3-550b-9cb8-ef3b3a7e5563'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d6a0f1d-f1e3-550b-9cb8-ef3b3a7e5563'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tattoos', E'Tattoos are a popular form of self-expression and artistry, allowing individuals to adorn their bodies with meaningful symbols and designs. Whether you''re considering getting your first tattoo or adding to your existing collection, it''s important to choose a design with a significance that resonates with you.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d6a502b-040c-5f6f-a0ab-222eaddfb7a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d6a502b-040c-5f6f-a0ab-222eaddfb7a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Defining Work', E'Work, in sociology, is defined as the carrying out of tasks, which involves the {{1}} of mental and physical effort, and its objective is the production of goods and services that {{2}} to human needs. An occupation, or job, is work that is done in exchange for a regular wage or salary. In all cultures, work is the basis of the economy or economic system. The economic system for any given culture is made up of the institutions that provide for the production and {{3}} of goods and services. These institutions may vary from culture to culture, particularly in traditional societies versus modern societies. In traditional cultures, food gathering and food production is the type of work {{4}} by the majority of the population. In larger traditional societies, carpentry, stonemasonry, and shipbuilding are also prominent. In modern societies where industrial development exists, people work in a much wider variety of occupations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.expenditure, 2.cater, 3.distribution, 4.occupied', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d6a6523-5417-50fb-882a-bc14a2d09241'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d6a6523-5417-50fb-882a-bc14a2d09241'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7b47786d-6363-52c9-bff1-2a2b814c20da'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Insufficient sleep can raise the risk of various health issues.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d6ac3a0-0278-5d26-b48c-7343b21cdff3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d6ac3a0-0278-5d26-b48c-7343b21cdff3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'af2cbeb7-cb8f-5c71-b498-9184e866f923'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The most important details in this argument are missing.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d8aa0ef-3463-54d9-b784-b414c5b60c21'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d8aa0ef-3463-54d9-b784-b414c5b60c21'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alcoholic Beverage', NULL, '567251bf-9bab-5c7c-9ebb-7afad2a983f6'::uuid, NULL, E'Nobody knows exactly when humans began to create fermented beverages. The earliest known evidence comes from 7,000 BCE in China, where residue in clay pots has revealed that people were making an alcoholic beverage from fermented rice, millet, grapes, and honey. Within a few thousand years, cultures all over the world were fermenting their own drinks. Ancient Mesopotamians and Egyptians made beer throughout the year from stored cereal grains. This beer was available to all social classes, and workers even received it in their daily rations. They also made wine, but because the climate wasn’t ideal for growing grapes, it was a rare and expensive delicacy. By contrast, in Greece and Rome, where grapes grew more easily, wine was as readily available as beer was in Egypt and Mesopotamia. Because yeasts will ferment basically any plant sugars, ancient peoples made alcohol from whatever crops and plants grew where they lived. In South America, people made chicha from grains, sometimes adding hallucinogenic herbs. In what’s now Mexico, pulque, made from cactus sap, was the drink of choice, while East Africans made banana and palm beer. And in the area that’s now Japan, people made sake from rice.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1d8c07f5-c28e-5275-b675-0572ba5ea68c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d8c07f5-c28e-5275-b675-0572ba5ea68c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3c8c4405-3ac2-5c56-9a50-792e52f8fff0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The rising inflation rate indicates a decrease in demand for consumer products.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d8ea809-2c29-518e-a1af-b8ee8facabca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d8ea809-2c29-518e-a1af-b8ee8facabca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '935537f3-f4cb-54ec-9eee-a0aafa7ef6f1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Watching television can be very educational for children.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d95406a-3bb7-5dbd-9a10-ee86794f7bb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d95406a-3bb7-5dbd-9a10-ee86794f7bb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neutrinos', E'In June 1998, an international team of Japanese and US physicists unveiled strong evidence that elusive subatomic particles known as neutrinos have mass. These findings run {{1}} to the standard model of particle physics—the basic theory about the structure of matter—which holds that these electrically neutral, weakly interacting particles have no mass. The discovery means that existing theoretical models of matter must now be {{2}} to include neutrinos with mass. Neutrinos occur in three states: electron, muon, and tau, with the names signifying what is produced when a neutrino collides with another particle. {{3}} do not see the neutrinos themselves, but can detect the creation of electrons and muons from faint flashes of light following a particle collision.\nThe physicists used the giant Super-Kamiokande—the world''s biggest neutrino detector buried deep underground in Mozumi, Japan. In the experiment, {{4}} in a 50,000-ton tank of purified water, neutrinos created when cosmic rays bombard Earth''s upper atmosphere were counted relative to the number expected to penetrate the cavern. The experimenters found that the number of electron-neutrinos detected was relatively constant with theorized totals, while the number of muon-neutrinos was significantly lower. This indicated that they were disappearing into another state, or "flavor," such as an undetected tau-neutrino, or possibly another type.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.counter, 2.revised, 3.Observers, 4.submerged', NULL, NULL),
  ('1d96f83f-f3df-533a-8a99-ef58009460dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1d96f83f-f3df-533a-8a99-ef58009460dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2d12a01d-997f-58b6-a663-0b8798cb8af6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They demanded a refund on unsatisfactory goods.', NULL, NULL),
  ('1da41394-75e2-5741-a02e-cea413b8c0b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1da41394-75e2-5741-a02e-cea413b8c0b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Teenagers', E'Teenagers should receive lessons on principles of personal finance, such as investing and debt. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s world, personal finance has become an essential life skill that can help individuals make informed financial decisions and achieve financial stability. However, many teenagers are not taught the principles of personal finance in school or at home. This essay argues that providing personal finance education to teenagers can have a positive impact on their financial well-being and future success.\nTeaching teenagers about personal finance can help them develop financial literacy and responsibility. By learning about investing, debt management, and budgeting, teenagers can gain a better understanding of how to manage their money effectively. This knowledge can help them make better financial decisions in the future, such as avoiding high-interest debt and saving for long-term goals. Additionally, personal finance education can help reduce financial stress and anxiety, as teenagers who understand the principles of personal finance are less likely to make poor financial decisions that can lead to debt and financial hardship.\nLearning about investing and debt management can also help teenagers manage their finances when they become adults. By understanding the basics of investing, teenagers can learn how to grow their money over time and build wealth for the future. Additionally, learning about debt management can help teenagers avoid common pitfalls such as high-interest credit card debt and payday loans. By developing these skills early on, teenagers will be better equipped to manage their finances in adulthood and achieve long-term financial success.\nIn conclusion, providing personal finance education to teenagers is essential for their financial well-being and future success.', NULL, 200, 300),
