  ('1dbbd4b8-5c95-539e-9184-32103e9af257'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1dbbd4b8-5c95-539e-9184-32103e9af257'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parent-Child Bonds', E'In today''s fast-paced world, nurturing strong parent-child bonds and maintaining healthy family relationships can be challenging but is more crucial than ever. Quality time spent together plays a vital role in fostering meaningful connections within the family. First and foremost, communication is the cornerstone of a strong parent-child relationship. Engaging in open and honest conversations allows parents to understand their children''s thoughts, feelings, and concerns. Active listening is equally essential, as it conveys empathy and validation of the child''s experiences. Quality time also involves shared activities that promote bonding and create lasting memories. Whether it''s cooking together, playing games, going for a nature walk, or even just watching a movie, these shared experiences help build trust and strengthen the parent-child connection. Moreover, setting aside time for one-on-one interactions is essential. Spending individual time with each child allows for personalized attention and helps children feel valued and understood. It''s an opportunity for parents to show genuine interest in their child''s interests and passions. Consistency is key in nurturing family relationships. Establishing routines, such as family meals or bedtime rituals, provides a sense of stability and predictability. These routines create a safe and secure environment for children, allowing them to thrive emotionally and socially. In addition, setting boundaries and rules within the family unit is important. Clear expectations and consequences help children understand limits and develop a sense of responsibility. It''s essential to strike a balance between discipline and nurturing to create a supportive and loving atmosphere. Ultimately, the quality of time spent together, rather than quantity, is what matters most. Focusing on meaningful interactions, active listening, shared experiences, and individual attention fosters strong parent-child bonds and promotes a harmonious family life.', NULL, NULL, E'In our fast-paced society, nurturing strong parent-child relationships is vital, emphasizing open communication, active listening, shared activities, individual attention, consistent routines, and a balance of discipline and nurturing, all contributing to meaningful connections and a harmonious family life.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('1dc1ad5a-b10f-5b24-99e4-e4cc746d2122'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '1dc1ad5a-b10f-5b24-99e4-e4cc746d2122'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who decides how a criminal should be punished in a court?', '9f82710f-9423-5304-a62b-5ad7705ce6ea'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Judge', NULL, NULL),
