  ('20610c4c-5872-59fb-8c82-25ded5d20583'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '20610c4c-5872-59fb-8c82-25ded5d20583'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Students'' Declarations', E'For example, students might try to enrol for the free year despite having previously studied and therefore being ineligible. The report said the government held no records of study from before 2003 in order to verify eligibility, meaning it would have to rely on students'' declarations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('20679d19-d83a-503b-9ec4-9d0929d94010'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '20679d19-d83a-503b-9ec4-9d0929d94010'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5ca3167a-a9c3-5c98-9ece-abdad94c6252'::uuid, NULL, E'Psychologists use science to understand thoughts and figure out why we act certain ways.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2068b9b1-399c-5bc3-a609-871e21ca7b5c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2068b9b1-399c-5bc3-a609-871e21ca7b5c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the structure that plants use to capture light energy for photosynthesis?', '7f9a7c83-d618-50dd-b169-d0ea772deb5e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Chloroplast', NULL, NULL),
  ('206c0326-2ccf-562a-9439-7f5ea5d38099'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '206c0326-2ccf-562a-9439-7f5ea5d38099'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '35e6400e-083d-57c3-897d-4dcdba4edd86'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Specialist knowledge isn''t necessary to comprehend the contents of this book.', NULL, NULL),
  ('20702425-9fad-546e-90de-019578328fbe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '20702425-9fad-546e-90de-019578328fbe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pollution', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('2071f2ff-67f3-5772-81e1-98a59ad159d4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2071f2ff-67f3-5772-81e1-98a59ad159d4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Medical Technology', E'In recent years, the field of medical technology has witnessed remarkable advancements that are revolutionizing the healthcare industry. These innovations are not only improving patient outcomes but also enhancing the efficiency of healthcare delivery. In this article, we will explore some of the key developments in medical technology and their impact on healthcare.\nOne of the most exciting breakthroughs in medical technology is the development of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning algorithms. These AI systems can analyze vast amounts of medical data, from patient records to medical images, and identify patterns and trends that may not be apparent to human clinicians. This capability is leading to more accurate diagnoses and personalized treatment plans, ultimately improving patient care.\nTelemedicine is another area where technology is making a significant impact. With the widespread availability of high-speed internet and smartphones, patients can now consult with healthcare providers remotely. This has proven especially crucial during the COVID-19 pandemic, as it allows for safe and convenient healthcare access without physical contact.\nAdvancements in surgical technology have also been transformative. Minimally invasive surgical techniques, such as robotic surgery, have reduced recovery times and post-operative pain for patients. Surgeons can now perform complex procedures with greater precision, leading to better surgical outcomes.\nFurthermore, the development of wearable health devices and mobile health apps has empowered individuals to take control of their health. From fitness trackers that monitor activity levels to apps that help manage chronic conditions, these technologies are enabling people to make more informed decisions about their well-being.\nIn conclusion, the ongoing advancements in medical technology are reshaping the landscape of healthcare. AI and machine learning are improving diagnosis and treatment, telemedicine is increasing access to care, and innovative surgical techniques are enhancing surgical outcomes. Additionally, wearable devices and mobile apps are promoting proactive health management. These innovations are not only transforming healthcare but also promising a healthier and more connected future for all.', NULL, NULL, E'The continuous evolution of medical technology, encompassing artificial intelligence, telemedicine, innovative surgical procedures, and wearable health devices, is fundamentally reshaping the healthcare landscape by enhancing diagnostic accuracy, treatment efficacy, and patient engagement, promising a healthier and more accessible future for healthcare.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('2072a1b4-aaa9-549c-b157-0bddb82fca1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2072a1b4-aaa9-549c-b157-0bddb82fca1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Amount of Sleep', E'The amount of sleep you need depends on many {{1}} , especially your age. Newborns sleep between 16 and 18 hours a day and preschool children should sleep between 10 and 12 hours. Older children and teens need at least nine hours to be well rested. For most adults, seven to eight hours a night appears to the best amount of sleep. However, for some people" enough sleep" may be as few as five hours or as many as 10 hours of sleep.\nAs you get older, your sleeping {{2}} change. Older adults tend to sleep more lightly and awaken more frequently in the night than younger adults. This can have many causes including medical conditions and medications used to treat them. But there''s no evidence that older adults need less sleep than younger adults.\nGetting enough sleep is {{3}} to your health because it boosts your {{4}} system, which makes your body better able to fight disease. Sleep is necessary for your nervous system to work properly. Too little sleep makes you drowsy and unable to concentrate. It also impairs memory and physical performance.\nSo how many hours of sleep are enough for You? Experts say that if you feel drowsy during the day - even during boring activities - you are not getting enough sleep. Also, quality of sleep is just as important as quantity. People whose sleep is frequently interrupted or cut short are not getting quality sleep.\nIf you experience frequent daytime sleepiness, even after increasing the amount of quality sleep you get, talk to your doctor. He or she may be able to {{5}} the cause of sleep problems and offer advice on how to get a better night''s sleep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.factors, 2.patterns, 3.important, 4.immune, 5.identify', NULL, NULL),
  ('207f477d-3cf6-5d9d-8de1-2a5f53f8db5b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '207f477d-3cf6-5d9d-8de1-2a5f53f8db5b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Peer Checking', E'Peer checking is a very useful and productive way of developing your reviewing skills. When you read your friend''s work, you are assuming the role of the reader (and the teacher). If your friend''s work is well written, then it will be fluent and easy to read, and you will have no problems understanding the overall content.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2083de3f-d794-5cde-abfd-b9f583efdf6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2083de3f-d794-5cde-abfd-b9f583efdf6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Large Factories', E'Some large factories are built near the communities. What are the benefits and problems of this phenomenon?', NULL, NULL, E'The construction of large factories near communities has long been a controversial issue. While some argue that it can bring significant benefits to the community, others believe that it can also cause problems. In this essay, I will examine both the benefits and problems of large factories being built near communities.\nFirstly, the construction of large factories can bring significant economic benefits to the community. Large factories can provide job opportunities for local residents, which can boost the local economy and improve the standard of living. Additionally, large factories can attract other businesses and investments to the area, creating a more diverse and vibrant community.\nHowever, there are also several problems associated with the construction of large factories near communities. Firstly, large factories can generate pollution and environmental hazards that can harm the health and well-being of community members. Secondly, large factories can contribute to traffic congestion and noise pollution, which can disrupt the peace and quiet of the community. Finally, the influx of workers and economic changes in the community can lead to negative social impacts, such as increased crime rates and social inequality.\nIn conclusion, while the construction of large factories near communities can bring significant economic benefits, it also has several problems that must be addressed. It is important for policymakers to carefully consider the potential impacts of large factories on the environment, public health, and social well-being of the community before approving their construction. With proper planning and regulation, it is possible for large factories to coexist with communities in a way that benefits both parties.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('20841dc9-e12f-5fb0-a908-339c54bc54ac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '20841dc9-e12f-5fb0-a908-339c54bc54ac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Over-training', E'Athletes often complain about the physical and mental effects of over-training. Over-training occurs when the amount or intensity of exercise exceeds the body’s ability to recover from the stress placed upon it. Although athletes need to push their physical limits in order to improve, repeated strenuous exercise without sufficient recovery can eventually reduce rather than enhance their performance.\nOver-training can occur in three main ways: failing to allow enough rest between training sessions, repeatedly training the same part of the body, and increasing the intensity or volume of exercise too quickly. A lack of rest prevents damaged muscles and tissues from repairing themselves properly. Similarly, working the same body part too frequently places repeated stress on muscles, joints and tendons, increasing the risk of overuse injuries. Athletes who suddenly increase their workload may also demand more from their bodies than they are physically prepared to tolerate.', NULL, NULL, E'Over-training occurs when the amount or intensity of exercise exceeds the body’s ability to recover, and repeated strenuous exercise without sufficient recovery can eventually reduce rather than enhance their performance; over-training can occur in three main ways: failing to allow enough rest between training sessions, repeatedly training the same part of the body, and increasing the intensity or volume of exercise too quickly.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('20843538-2d34-580c-9d26-e82665b930ca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '20843538-2d34-580c-9d26-e82665b930ca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0628649b-eced-5572-894a-fe1ec26c874f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The terms illness and disease are confusing despite clear differences.', NULL, NULL),
