  ('230d5779-582a-57fb-bf31-fd0570d0f51d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '230d5779-582a-57fb-bf31-fd0570d0f51d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8f99ed56-85a3-56d7-9900-53c802231baa'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'It may not be possible to solve the problem easily.', NULL, NULL),
  ('231157c4-0312-5e33-ab93-b8b61389c4ac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '231157c4-0312-5e33-ab93-b8b61389c4ac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '12492edd-12b0-5d91-a93a-128c684b3566'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This cart is made for transporting single items at one time.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2318fb63-3077-561b-acc4-f7820f5b2383'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2318fb63-3077-561b-acc4-f7820f5b2383'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electric Current', E'Almost 200 years after French physicist Jean Peltier discovered that electric current flowing through the junction of two different metals could be used to produce a heating or cooling effect, researchers say it is time to step up efforts to find new materials for the thermoelectric cooling market.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('231b4a0d-16e3-5d04-bbe6-7f2cb76c2141'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '231b4a0d-16e3-5d04-bbe6-7f2cb76c2141'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cause of Unemployment', E'One cause of unemployment may be downswings in the trade cycle, i.e. periods of recession. Another explanation of wide-scale unemployment refers to {{1}} unemployment. Structural unemployment arises from longer-term changes in the economy, affecting {{2}} industries, regions and occupations. Structural unemployment often explains regional unemployment. Some regions of the UK such as Central Scotland, and the North-West have higher rates of unemployment because the {{3}} heavy industries which were {{4}} there have gone into decline as they are {{5}} by cheaper imports from abroad. The new high-tech industries based on new technologies tend to be based in the South-East and along particular growth corridors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.structural, 2.specific, 3.traditional, 4.located, 5.replaced', NULL, NULL),
  ('2328412f-ef9b-5d07-a0f6-b5d64cfdf0f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2328412f-ef9b-5d07-a0f6-b5d64cfdf0f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Smartphone Apps', NULL, 'dc88fab3-fdc6-5f1b-97ae-85ce58c9c644'::uuid, NULL, E'Computer scientist Shwetak Patel and his team are developing new sensing systems. The initial focus was really around energy and water monitoring. They built a new generation of smart sensors that monitor electronic interference on a home’s power line or water pressure changes in the plumbing. Most of this technology has already found industrial applications, and Patel and his team turned their attention to adapting the technology for personal health monitoring. ‘So how do we take this noise and make it into a signal interest was hard to us, hard to us in the core of what we did for many years and we’re taking that work and applying it to other domains.’ They’re looking to take advantage of all the functionality built in our smartphones. With the users’ permission, this app can use the microphone built into most smartphones to listen to background noises, such as coughing searching for patterns that suggest a trip to the doctor might be an order. ‘We''ve constructed these models that try and understand how sound works, how it, what its patterns are and we give it a whole bunch of examples of different kinds of audio, things like people talking, things like people laughing, sneezing and of course coughing.’ This app uses a phone’s camera to check hemoglobin levels in blood by analyzing the color of capillary fluid through the skin. ‘Generally, what happens is if you’re anemic, your bloods maybe a little less red and we take advantage of that by putting your finger over a camera of a phone, the camera of the phone can actually see the coloration of the blood.’ and this test uses the camera to tell parents worried about jaundice in newborn infants. ‘Now, jaundice is something that doctors who have seen tons of babies. He just can figure out on a very basic level of it. Is this baby, do they need to get treatment or are they in a good condition, while the first-time parent has no idea necessarily what jaundice might look like.’ The researchers say the built-in sensors found in smart phones are already commonplace, but their applications and their implications for our health and well-being may be more far-reaching than we ever imagined.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('232cdb39-abb1-581f-8751-175d33462343'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '232cdb39-abb1-581f-8751-175d33462343'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mathematics and Statistics', E'Mathematics and statistics play a {{1}} in almost all daily activities. They are at the {{2}} of advances in science and technology, as well as providing {{3}} problem-solving and decision-making tools in many {{4}} of life. They underpin the rigorous analysis and modelling required for new policies, designs and systems. Mathematical and statistical knowledge is much sought after by employers for a wide {{5}} of jobs, not least in teaching the subject, and a qualification in any one of the areas we offer can bring real benefits in your professional life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.part, 2.heart, 3.indispensable, 4.areas, 5.variety', NULL, NULL),
  ('232d62e6-0b77-5805-93e8-b232f9faaaa7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '232d62e6-0b77-5805-93e8-b232f9faaaa7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rowling', E'J.K. Rowling''s journey from a struggling single mother to a bestselling author is an inspiring tale of perseverance and creativity. Her initial manuscript of "Harry Potter" {{1}} multiple rejections before finding a home with a publisher {{2}} to take a chance on the magical world she created. Rowling''s storytelling {{3}} readers, leading to a series that has {{4}} millions of copies worldwide and evolved into a cultural phenomenon redefining the relationship between literature, fandom, and branding.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.faced, 2.willing, 3.captivated, 4.sold', NULL, NULL),
  ('2334b669-8fdd-501a-823e-c47037977005'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2334b669-8fdd-501a-823e-c47037977005'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The English Revolution', E'There are three main interpretations of the English Revolution. The longest lasting interpretation was that the Revolution was the almost inevitable outcome of an age-old power struggle between parliament and crown. The second sees it as a class struggle, and a lead-up to the French and other revolutions. Finally, the third interpretation sees the other two as too fixed, not allowing for unpredictability, and that the outcome could have gone either way.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('23355b11-cd24-5b24-9ce2-f82fa2d9e473'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '23355b11-cd24-5b24-9ce2-f82fa2d9e473'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The UN', E'Since its inception, the UN system has been working to ensure adequate food for all through sustainable agriculture. The majority of the world''s poorest people live in rural areas of developing countries. They depend on agriculture and related activities for their livelihoods. This makes them particularly vulnerable to man-made and natural influences that reduce agricultural production.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('233629f4-9c65-59a4-8dca-59ee5396ece2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '233629f4-9c65-59a4-8dca-59ee5396ece2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Calm and Pressure', E'Research suggests that some are more susceptible than others, especially those who are self-conscious, anxious, and afraid of being judged negatively by others. So, how can we avoid choking when it really counts? First, it helps to practice under stressful conditions. In a study on expert dart players, researchers found that those who hadn’t practiced under stress performed worse when anxious compared to those who had become accustomed to pressure. Secondly, many performers extol the virtues of a pre-performance routine, whether it’s taking a few deep breaths, repeating a cue word, or doing a rhythmic sequence of movements, studies on golfing, bowling, and water polo, find that short rituals can lead to more consistent and accurate performance under...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '6fda10d0-36bd-5344-ac44-76b1bc3ae651'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'pressure', NULL, NULL),
  ('2337da64-1134-52fb-96c9-4a8e47e3da0a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2337da64-1134-52fb-96c9-4a8e47e3da0a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Artificial Lighting', E'What is your opinion on the impact of artificial lighting on wildlife?', NULL, NULL, E'The impact of artificial lighting on wildlife is undeniable, with adverse effects that disrupt natural behavior patterns, disturb nocturnal animals, and lead to displacement from habitats. The pervasive presence of artificial lighting in natural environments has significant repercussions on wildlife populations, altering their behaviors and habitats in detrimental ways.\nArtificial lighting disrupts wildlife''s natural behavior patterns by interfering with crucial activities such as hunting and mating. The artificial illumination can confuse animals, affecting their ability to forage for food, find mates, and navigate their surroundings effectively. This disruption can lead to imbalances in ecosystems and threaten the survival of various species.\nThe bright lights at night caused by artificial lighting can disturb nocturnal animals'' navigation and feeding habits. Nocturnal species rely on darkness for hunting and feeding, and the presence of artificial light can disorient them, making it challenging to locate prey or find suitable food sources. This disturbance can have cascading effects on nocturnal wildlife populations and disrupt the delicate balance of nighttime ecosystems.\nIn conclusion, the impact of artificial lighting on wildlife is a pressing concern that must be addressed to protect biodiversity and ecosystem health. The disruption of natural behavior patterns, disturbance of nocturnal animals, and displacement from habitats highlight the detrimental effects of excessive artificial lighting on wildlife populations. It is essential to consider the ecological consequences of artificial lighting and implement measures to mitigate its negative impact on wildlife and preserve the delicate balance of natural ecosystems.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('233a531f-5cca-5a13-8f7f-c06dd6ed5c3d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '233a531f-5cca-5a13-8f7f-c06dd6ed5c3d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '615ba940-8993-51c4-83dd-6c8ce26eb30a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mathematics instructors are presently encountering certain challenges in their teaching roles.', NULL, NULL),
  ('233c64ba-4dbe-5ab8-bd8c-75f8df8f605d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '233c64ba-4dbe-5ab8-bd8c-75f8df8f605d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'One-dimensional Characters', E'Characters that lack internal conflict or multiple facets to their personality are often {{1}} as flat or one-dimensional characters. This is often seen as a bad thing in a story, especially for first-time writers, when all of the characters are one-dimensional. However, if there are one or two characters that are simplistic in nature for a reason, it may not be perceived as a negative {{2}} .As long as an author uses one-dimensional characters correctly, and with deliberate intention, there is nothing wrong with it. Often, a narrative is most successful with a {{3}} of flat and rounded characters. With that said, it''s important to have strong character development overall to create rounded characters that have some depth to them. This helps characters {{4}} being a real human being. Being able to relate to characters in this way, as a reader, makes them far more interesting and realistic.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dubbed, 2.trait, 3.combination, 4.imitate', NULL, NULL),
  ('233f6301-32af-5807-aaf0-0fd1763173d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '233f6301-32af-5807-aaf0-0fd1763173d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Play Writing', E'What is the role of writing theater plays and discussing historical writings in the study of high school students?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('233fa654-4868-58c6-8594-86238b799a77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '233fa654-4868-58c6-8594-86238b799a77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Robot', NULL, '3328b987-dda5-53cd-9c8e-f363de9eeef9'::uuid, NULL, E'This is a kind of object that you''re probably all familiar with when you had the term robot, but I''m gonna show you the very, very first robots. These were the very first robots. They were characters in a play in the 1920s called Rossum''s Universal Robots and they, the play was written by Czech writer called Karel Capek. And basically, these robots, you know, people tend to think of robots as kind of cute cuddly toys or, you know, Hollywood depictions kind of devoid of politics. But the first robots were actually created and imagined in a time of absolute political turmoil. You just had the First World War, you know, it finished had a devastating impact across Europe and so people will kind and people are kind of reflecting on what does it mean to be human, what makes us human, those kinds of question. And this kind of context is what inspired Capek to kind of write this play. And interestingly, these robots being human, they are actually in the play assembled on a production line, a bit like the Ford manufacturing production line. So even though they are human, they are assembled and these robots are designed to labor, and that is their primary purpose in society.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('23509e3a-7c88-504c-b479-491b2f0327e0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '23509e3a-7c88-504c-b479-491b2f0327e0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nature', E'Nature is a source of wonder and inspiration, offering a rich diversity of life forms and ecosystems that are essential to our survival and well-being. From the depths of the ocean to the highest peaks of the mountains, nature provides a wealth of opportunities for exploration and discovery. It is through our interactions with nature that we can learn valuable lessons about resilience, adaptability, and interconnectedness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
