  ('2505fca1-ba7d-5a96-953d-03a26792dcb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2505fca1-ba7d-5a96-953d-03a26792dcb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fusion', E'US scientists announced a breakthrough on fusion energy on Tuesday (Dec 13), potentially a step toward one day harnessing the process that fires the sun to generate carbon-free electricity as the world {{1}} with climate change. So, will fusion help fight climate change? Potentially. Besides vastly {{2}} up the energy from fusion reactions, scientists need to produce them multiple times per second on a constant basis. Scaling that process up to a power plant and building plants big enough to cover a significant chunk of the world''s growing electricity demand would take {{3}} efforts requiring materials, land and clear regulations for industry. Politicians supporting the existing fuels and infrastructure may be {{4}} to rapid change. As the quest for fusion energy develops over a decade or potentially much longer, countries should continue aggressive moves into wind and solar power, energy storage, including batteries, next generation fission power and other alternatives to reduce {{5}} on fossil fuels, scientists and environmentalists say.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.struggles, 2.ramping, 3.momentous, 4.resistant, 5.dependence', NULL, NULL),
  ('2506c917-8351-503a-99e2-00926c6867db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2506c917-8351-503a-99e2-00926c6867db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Particle Accelerator', E'Particle accelerators produce and accelerate beams of charged particles, such as electrons, protons and ions, of atomic and sub-atomic size. They are used not only in fundamental research for an improved understanding of matter, but also in plethora of socioeconomic applications related to environmental monitoring, food quality, energy and aerospace technologies.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2509fdde-a227-51b5-a906-805b1a9c3873'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2509fdde-a227-51b5-a906-805b1a9c3873'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Micromanaging', E'Leaders need to avoid micromanaging and stay {{1}} to what is happening in order to spot a change in context. By and large, line workers in a simple situation are more than capable of independently handling any issues that may {{2}} . Indeed, those with years of experience also have deep {{3}} into how the work should be done. Leaders should create a communication channel — an anonymous one, if necessary — that allows dissenters to provide early warnings about complacency. It''s important to remember that best practice is, by definition, past practice. Using best practices is common, and often {{4}} , in simple contexts. Difficulties arise, however, if staff members are {{5}} from bucking the process even when it''s not working anymore. Since hindsight no longer leads to foresight after a shift in context, a corresponding change in management style may be called for.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.connected, 2.arise, 3.insight, 4.appropriate, 5.discouraged', NULL, NULL),
  ('250c92be-d392-54a4-9269-4b79f0594937'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '250c92be-d392-54a4-9269-4b79f0594937'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the coldest planet in our solar system?', 'b2f296bd-62b0-557d-8075-5c4e57bf6b3a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Neptune', NULL, NULL),
