  ('25542db8-67c1-5426-a63f-f3cd934cd8c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25542db8-67c1-5426-a63f-f3cd934cd8c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cancer Immunotherapy', E'Cancer immunotherapy has emerged as a groundbreaking area in the {{1}} against cancer, leveraging the body''s immune system to target and {{2}} cancer cells. One prominent approach involves checkpoint inhibitors, which block specific proteins that inhibit immune responses, allowing the immune system to recognize and attack cancer cells more effectively. Another promising avenue is adoptive cell therapy, {{3}} T cells are extracted from the patient, genetically modified to express receptors targeting cancer cells, and then reintroduced into the patient. CAR-T cell therapy, a notable example of adoptive cell therapy, has shown remarkable success in treating certain types of leukemia and lymphoma. Ongoing research is focused on refining these immunotherapeutic strategies, addressing challenges like treatment resistance and expanding their applicability to a {{4}} range of cancers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.fight, 2.eliminate, 3.where, 4.broader', NULL, NULL),
