  ('25ee52ec-d44b-5def-ad54-3d91848c3d19'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25ee52ec-d44b-5def-ad54-3d91848c3d19'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Computers', E'Even though our computers are now better than 15 years ago, they still malfunction between 11 and 20 per cent of the time, a new study concludes. The researchers behind the study therefore find that there are major gains to be achieved for society by rethinking the systems and involving users more in their development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('25efe0ea-f861-5302-8137-2d695632987e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25efe0ea-f861-5302-8137-2d695632987e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ebac427b-e480-5b31-8509-3b020045c03e'::uuid, NULL, E'The average human lifespan in the developed countries has increased over the last decades.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('25f8289c-7fec-5b4b-9b86-21b3937b4ccd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25f8289c-7fec-5b4b-9b86-21b3937b4ccd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Context Clues', E'Context clues {{1}} of all the words and phrases that are near a word. Often, you can define words based on the other words around them. If you’re reading a lot of material, you don’t have time to look up {{2}} words. Reading words in context helps {{3}} a high level of focus, whereas breaking your {{4}} to lookup words is distracting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.consist, 2.individual, 3.ensure, 4.concentration', NULL, NULL),
  ('25fa7ffb-f686-5806-bed8-5fbfb2d5df93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25fa7ffb-f686-5806-bed8-5fbfb2d5df93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the son of a king or queen?', '6d4de8fa-ef7d-5780-b92c-ee7c815048bb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Prince', NULL, NULL),
  ('25fb1390-01e9-5037-a96d-31bd2ca07c9e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25fb1390-01e9-5037-a96d-31bd2ca07c9e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Children', E'Children need to discover their own strengths and weaknesses in order to find fulfillment as adults in both work and play. Watching television does not lead to these discoveries; it only limits children''s involvement in those real-life activities that might offer their abilities a genuine testing ground. And young children''s need for fantasy is gratified far better by their own make-believe activities than by the adult-made fantasies they are offered on television.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('25fdab4a-8496-5391-b97b-6abffa325db4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '25fdab4a-8496-5391-b97b-6abffa325db4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Stock Market', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('2602592f-17c1-55bb-807e-4abcdb567aa9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2602592f-17c1-55bb-807e-4abcdb567aa9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If you want to have a cup of coffee without milk or cream, what kind of coffee should you order?', 'ef94a55c-75cb-53b4-a978-fc7a6811d9b7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Black coffee', NULL, NULL),
  ('260530f1-c1b9-5fad-b37e-3977ef5b337d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '260530f1-c1b9-5fad-b37e-3977ef5b337d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6512f928-9079-580f-b2e2-88bc9d07f41e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Please confirm that you have received the textbook.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2611dd3c-dc8c-524c-bc59-eef03c8e9925'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2611dd3c-dc8c-524c-bc59-eef03c8e9925'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dogs'' Vision', E'The belief that dogs are colorblind, especially that they can only see in black and white, is a common misconception that has been {{1}} for many years. This misunderstanding likely {{2}} early scientific studies and the way the information was subsequently communicated to the public. Early studies on canine vision suggested that dogs could not perceive colors in the same way humans do. This was because dogs, unlike humans, have fewer cone cells in their eyes. Cone cells are responsible for {{3}} color. Humans typically have three types of cone cells, allowing them to see a {{4}} spectrum of colors (trichromatic vision). Initial research suggested that dogs might lack this complexity in their visual system, leading to the conclusion that they could only perceive the world in {{5}} of gray. Modern research, however, has shown that dogs do see colors, but their color vision is limited compared to humans.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.perpetuated, 2.stems from, 3.detecting, 4.wide, 5.shades', NULL, NULL),
  ('261441c7-eca7-5c5c-94e5-bb603c112a88'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '261441c7-eca7-5c5c-94e5-bb603c112a88'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e95efc05-e4be-5636-9490-24cf0ef86ed0'::uuid, NULL, E'The topic for discussion is usually related to the topic for a speech.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2614b6ae-7e6d-533a-8b05-6d82e45257b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2614b6ae-7e6d-533a-8b05-6d82e45257b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'bdb5e5c9-ce80-5cbc-910d-7b01f117b5d9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Teaching assistance plays a vital role in the learning process.', NULL, NULL),
  ('261a503e-d1ce-509f-a205-ab59ee4bf8e9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '261a503e-d1ce-509f-a205-ab59ee4bf8e9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ultrafast World', E'Glimpses of the ultrafast world of electrons are changing scientists’ vision of the inner workings of atoms and molecules. The 2023 Nobel Prize in physics goes to three physicists who illuminated this realm with ultrashort pulses of light, the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences announced October 3.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('261af0a8-0e82-5f45-bf03-d151fd25ad9d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '261af0a8-0e82-5f45-bf03-d151fd25ad9d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2732a60c-6e2c-5036-a9c8-bf0e9aa7e7df'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She finally settled down in her new house.', NULL, NULL),
  ('261d8c56-f5af-5598-889c-fd3d2048e443'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '261d8c56-f5af-5598-889c-fd3d2048e443'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Money and Happiness', E'This will just take a minute. We all know money can''t buy happiness. But according to a recent study, there may be a loophole. A team of researchers finds that shelling out for services that save time can bring greater feelings of life satisfaction than, say, simply buying more stuff. The results appear in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2623c52c-fd6c-5deb-901c-fa285cda92a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2623c52c-fd6c-5deb-901c-fa285cda92a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indian Languages', E'Despite extensive Hindi language education, travelers often find themselves at a linguistic crossroads in India, a country where the linguistic landscape is as diverse as its culture. This diversity is not indicative of a flawed education {{1}} but reflects the rich tapestry of languages that India is home to. {{2}} over 1,600 languages spoken across the subcontinent, the concept of a "standard" Indian language is a misnomer. Each region boasts its own linguistic heritage, with languages ranging from the Dravidian family in the south to the Indo-Aryan dialects in the north. Urban areas, especially, are {{3}} pots of languages, with residents often fluent in multiple tongues, including English, which serves as a lingua franca. The historical roots of this diversity trace back to ancient migrations and invasions, with each {{4}} of newcomers leaving a linguistic imprint. This has resulted in a country where language is deeply {{5}} to regional identity, and the idea of a single unifying language remains elusive.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.system, 2.With, 3.melting, 4.wave, 5.tied', NULL, NULL),
  ('26278975-fba6-5396-bed2-61634961064a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '26278975-fba6-5396-bed2-61634961064a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for a person who specializes in treating diseases of the eye?', '3a800455-f761-5a6d-988d-0df57bcc287b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ophthalmologist', NULL, NULL),
  ('263081b0-79ef-541a-833b-640a11929654'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '263081b0-79ef-541a-833b-640a11929654'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'aeeb24f2-32fb-501b-8149-e47ea1d09acf'::uuid, NULL, E'The food industry is facing numerous challenges related to health.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('26358b62-fd25-5791-9c1e-7e5c8597efda'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '26358b62-fd25-5791-9c1e-7e5c8597efda'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neuroscience', E'Neuroscience is the interdisciplinary field that seeks to understand the brain and nervous system, drawing on knowledge from biology, psychology, physics, and other disciplines. It encompasses a wide range of research areas, from molecular and cellular neuroscience to cognitive and behavioral neuroscience, each with its unique set of tools and techniques.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2641c392-30ea-5e2d-946b-be30a639e10c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2641c392-30ea-5e2d-946b-be30a639e10c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fuel Combustion', E'Humans need to use energy in order to exist. So it is unsurprising that the way people have been producing energy is largely responsible for current environmental problems. Pollution comes in many forms, but those that are most concerning, because of their impact on health, result from the combustion of fuels in power stations and cars.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('264521d6-23a3-585b-9441-5ca7cdc8bd3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '264521d6-23a3-585b-9441-5ca7cdc8bd3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tsunamis', E'Usually, we use pressure {{1}} on the sea floor to tell us when a tsunami is moving over the sensors. But these pressure changes only tell us there is a tsunami after it has passed the sensors. A team {{2}} used a set of sensors in the Pacific Ocean to measure magnetic field and sea level change {{3}} . They found that the tsunamis were indeed {{4}} by changes in the magnetic field in the water.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.gauges, 2.instead, 3.simultaneously, 4.preceded', NULL, NULL),
  ('2649767a-bdb7-5608-b553-e4cbf53bb98c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2649767a-bdb7-5608-b553-e4cbf53bb98c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3c89f0bd-9438-5c57-bed6-27626b19c7ea'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pick courses that are good for the job you want later.', NULL, NULL),
  ('264c55b5-6c4c-5a82-8e8a-815184e62663'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '264c55b5-6c4c-5a82-8e8a-815184e62663'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '17387835-c655-53ae-8db2-57366a660d2c'::uuid, NULL, E'The man is probably the best-known painter in the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2651a979-9d69-5815-a981-baef4f0ac6bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2651a979-9d69-5815-a981-baef4f0ac6bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Manhattan', E'One of the most famous misunderstandings in history is the sale of Manhattan. In 1626, Peter Minuit, a representative of the Dutch West India Company, is traditionally said to have "bought" Manhattan from the native Lenape people for trinkets and beads worth about 60 guilders, which has often been mistakenly {{1}} at a mere $24 in modern currency. This narrative has been widely propagated as a symbol of the naiveté of Indigenous peoples and the cunning of European colonizers. However, recent scholarship suggests this {{2}} oversimplifies a complex interaction. The Lenape likely had a fundamentally different concept of land use and stewardship, not {{3}} the exchange as a transfer of perpetual ownership as understood by Europeans but rather as a right to share the land or a {{4}} agreement for use. Additionally, the value equivalence of the goods exchanged has been vastly understated when considering their worth at the time to the Lenape.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.valued, 2.account, 3.viewing, 4.mutual', NULL, NULL),
  ('26572dcc-85c3-570d-bfee-9afe71f52f15'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '26572dcc-85c3-570d-bfee-9afe71f52f15'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Extreme Imagination', E'Our imaginations shape the world we {{1}} and make us who we are. These extremes of imagination are intriguing. A better {{2}} of what is going on in the brains of people who experience them could help {{3}} out the role of mental imagery in emotion and mental health – and may be promising territory in the search for {{4}} for various psychological disorders.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.perceive, 2.grasp, 3.tease, 4.treatments', NULL, NULL),
  ('2657e0a8-15f7-593d-8860-25e296f69bbf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2657e0a8-15f7-593d-8860-25e296f69bbf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '741116df-8fbb-55b8-b762-82faa8b914d9'::uuid, NULL, E'The university marked Earth Day by planting trees to celebrate.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2659c1b0-b565-5cf3-bc32-831331dea647'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2659c1b0-b565-5cf3-bc32-831331dea647'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What piece of furniture is specifically designed for sleeping all through the night?', '6e16f281-c687-52d5-bbf7-b152c6c4b0c3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bed', NULL, NULL),
  ('26611d93-03d5-572d-80e8-7d47916ca3f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '26611d93-03d5-572d-80e8-7d47916ca3f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Job Hunting', E'When it comes to job-hunting, first impressions are critical. Remember, you are marketing a product - yourself - to a potential employer. The first thing the employer sees when greeting you is your {{2}} ;thus, you must make every effort to have the proper dress for the type of job you are seeking. Will dressing properly get you the job? Of course not, but it will give you a competitive edge and a {{3}} first impression. Should you be judged by what you wear? Perhaps not, but the reality is, of course, that you are judged. Throughout the entire job-seeking process employers use short-cuts — heuristics or rules of thumb — to save time. With cover letters, it’s the opening paragraph and a quick scan of your qualifications. With resumes, it is a quick scan of your accomplishments. With the job interview, it’s how you’re dressed that sets the {{4}} of the interview.\nHow should you dress? Dressing conservatively is always the safest route, but you should also try and do a little investigating of your {{6}} employer so that what you wear to the interview makes you look as though you {{7}} in with the organization. If you overdress (which is rare but can happen) or under dress (the more likely scenario), the potential employer may feel that you don''t care enough about the job.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.attire, 2.positive, 3.tone, 4.prospective, 5.fit', NULL, NULL),
  ('2663793d-a0e5-5e30-a1ad-7af7742ee0d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2663793d-a0e5-5e30-a1ad-7af7742ee0d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '10d5c3a5-8356-58b4-b767-6ae58edc2edb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Several major companies and organizations are supporting this project.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2665f395-728d-5e38-821e-c97c5fe6e10f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2665f395-728d-5e38-821e-c97c5fe6e10f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite of groom?', '4e98795b-da79-5567-b62f-6db79245ab34'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bride', NULL, NULL),
  ('2668c3e1-fd72-504e-8f2c-0d0b370baacc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2668c3e1-fd72-504e-8f2c-0d0b370baacc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call people going to space?', 'ae166ef4-5197-56e5-a3f2-f6ab4b5e6381'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Astronauts', NULL, NULL),
  ('2673b158-3f47-5c4a-8020-ae0bfbcb52bf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2673b158-3f47-5c4a-8020-ae0bfbcb52bf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Good Learning Environment', NULL, 'e49c7c85-674a-54f3-919f-063ee700ae4e'::uuid, NULL, E'I think a good learning environment has to have, I think, the tenet, that brave failure is preferable to timid success. By which I mean, I think our minds are great and powerful things. And I think that to have courage inform our thinking, and to be able to go out, perhaps pass where we may be comfortable. To go in to the unknown between human beings, and see where that takes us. To not stay safe in our own position, but to make it safe for other people to be able to share. I think that that’s where we get to new ideas. I think that’s where we get to brave ideas. I think that’s where we get to solutions we might not otherwise have found. So fostering an environment that where people can be brave, and where ideas don’t always have to be pristine. I think it’s, it’s very important.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('26761830-5132-559b-8415-2b622f37cc56'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '26761830-5132-559b-8415-2b622f37cc56'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Plant and Protein', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 3, 2, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('2679a78f-e2cd-5364-8660-31bd0076c37e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2679a78f-e2cd-5364-8660-31bd0076c37e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'New Ideas', E'First, new ideas are the wheels of progress. Without them, stagnation {{1}} . Whether you''re a designer dreaming of another world, an {{2}} working on a new kind of structure, an {{3}} charged with developing a fresh business concept, an advertiser seeking a breakthrough way to sell your product, a fifth-grade teacher trying to plan memorable school {{4}} , or a volunteer looking for a new way to sell the same old raffle tickets, your ability to {{5}} good ideas is critical to your success.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reigns, 2.engineer, 3.executive, 4.assemblies, 5.generate', NULL, NULL),
