  ('2959c444-0265-5d36-a1cb-f5f37aa3236e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2959c444-0265-5d36-a1cb-f5f37aa3236e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Children and Peace', E'As war spreads to many corners of the globe, children sadly have been drawn into the center of conflicts. In Afghanistan, Bosnia, and Colombia, however, groups of children have been taking part in peace education {{1}} . The children, after learning to resolve conflicts, took on the {{2}} of peacemakers. The Children''s Movement for Peace in Colombia was even nominated for the Nobel Peace Prize in 1998. Groups of children {{3}} as peacemakers studied human rights and poverty issues.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.projects, 2.role, 3.acting', NULL, NULL),
