  ('29803f1d-0a4d-50a3-93f1-65b6afe7e3bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29803f1d-0a4d-50a3-93f1-65b6afe7e3bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Body and Water', E'Your body is nearly two-thirds water. And so it is really important that you {{1}} enough fluid to stay {{2}} and healthy. If you don''t get enough fluid you may feel {{3}} , get {{4}} , and not perform at your best.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.consume, 2.hydrated, 3.tired, 4.headaches', NULL, NULL),
  ('29823b71-5fc6-5a84-a8cd-acd3798d2160'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29823b71-5fc6-5a84-a8cd-acd3798d2160'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hippopotamus', E'Hippopotamus is Greek for “river horse,” and the animal has been known since ancient {{1}} . Hippopotamuses are often seen basking on the banks or sleeping in the waters of rivers, lakes, and swamps next to grasslands. Hippos are {{2}} adapted to aquatic life. The ears, eyes, and nostrils are located high on the head so that the rest of the body may remain submerged. The ears and nostrils can be folded shut to keep out water. The body is so {{3}} that they can walk underwater, where they can hold their breath for five minutes. Although often seen basking in the sun, hippos lose water rapidly through the skin and become dehydrated without periodic {{4}} . They must also retreat to the water to keep cool, for they do not sweat.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.times, 2.well, 3.dense, 4.dips', NULL, NULL),
  ('29844018-bdde-5e33-92c2-0a34d14b9274'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29844018-bdde-5e33-92c2-0a34d14b9274'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Common Good', E'As normally used today, the phrase “common good” refers to those facilities or institutions that all or most members of a community agree are necessary to {{1}} certain interests they have in common. A few of the things making up the common good in a modern democracy might include {{2}} rights and freedoms, police and public safety, and safe and {{3}} food supply.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.satisfy, 2.basic, 3.ample', NULL, NULL),
  ('29849e2b-d1e6-5592-8d16-eb5edc9ca7a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29849e2b-d1e6-5592-8d16-eb5edc9ca7a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lawyer', E'Consider defending a client you believe is guilty, or representing opposing {{1}} in a heated legal battle. Welcome to the daily reality of ethical {{2}} faced by lawyers, where professional obligations and personal beliefs clash, and loyalties become a tightrope walk. Navigating these situations requires navigating professional {{3}} of conduct, intricate maps outlining rules on conflicts of interest, confidentiality, and candor. But the terrain isn''t always clear-cut. What if a client confesses to a crime? Can a lawyer maintain confidentiality {{4}} upholding the law? These ethical landmines demand careful judgement, sometimes requiring withdrawal from cases or disclosing conflicts to clients for informed consent. Ultimately, being a lawyer goes beyond legal expertise; it demands balancing the letter of the law with a moral compass. It''s about advocating for fair trials, challenging unjust laws, and sometimes even choosing to walk {{5}} from ethically compromised cases. It''s a constant balancing act, requiring both legal prowess and unwavering ethical grounding.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.sides, 2.conflicts, 3.codes, 4.while, 5.away', NULL, NULL),
  ('29953767-d541-56cf-83ad-f705b2a95f87'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29953767-d541-56cf-83ad-f705b2a95f87'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9218b3bd-4713-5e3d-81b5-cf45a3b5a962'::uuid, NULL, E'Elephants spend part of their sleep standing and part lying down.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
