  ('29a154c8-fde9-5bad-95f0-1265d940743e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29a154c8-fde9-5bad-95f0-1265d940743e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'aa0d2c0c-9132-52e1-9b14-4b4d4aaf0c41'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'My technique is to understand the sentence while writing the first letter of each word.', NULL, NULL),
  ('29a16809-e16a-53c4-92ff-e69e60bcf682'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29a16809-e16a-53c4-92ff-e69e60bcf682'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dwayne Johnson', E'Dwayne Johnson has thanked fans for their support after he opened up about his battle with depression. The 45 year old discussed his mother''s suicide attempt and a period he described as the "worst time" of his life in an interview with The Express. "Got tonnes of responses to this. Thank you," he wrote on Twitter on Monday. "We all go through the sludge and depression never discriminates.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29ab52d1-1f86-5a0f-9b46-817456734ff2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29ab52d1-1f86-5a0f-9b46-817456734ff2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Collaborative Endeavor', E'Science is a collaborative endeavor that transcends disciplines, borders, and beliefs. Scientists work together to share their knowledge and contribute to solving big-picture puzzles. {{1}} it is developing new tools, creating new models, or launching new initiatives, scientific collaboration drives innovation and progress. One example of the collaborative {{2}} of science is the global response to the COVID-19 pandemic. When the world was facing a health crisis, researchers from different fields and countries joined forces to track the virus, develop vaccines, and improve diagnostics. Their years of experience working together {{3}} off, as they were able to quickly share their findings and help the world collectively get {{4}} the pandemic. This shows how science can benefit from cooperation and altruism, not only for the greater good of humanity, but also for the advancement of knowledge.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Whether, 2.spirit, 3.paid, 4.through', NULL, NULL),
  ('29ac1008-c347-5df0-a3c1-46f57ea3a5f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29ac1008-c347-5df0-a3c1-46f57ea3a5f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f497f519-5cce-5e30-8741-06d3bfd26655'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You will each be given the chance to state your case.', NULL, NULL),
  ('29ac91fd-e059-590b-bf39-92208dda33b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29ac91fd-e059-590b-bf39-92208dda33b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd30f4035-e344-5884-94e8-8be4bae510ce'::uuid, NULL, E'He lives quietly in the country in a village near the sea.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29ad1b05-a3c4-5af9-ac96-e086155694c2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29ad1b05-a3c4-5af9-ac96-e086155694c2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mind Set', NULL, '2c4c2f72-bc03-531f-b97d-918aaa609728'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, I want to look at some research that has been done into what motivates people and, um, particularly on what is called the ''mind set'' - or more simply the mental attitude that highly motivated people have. And, of course, the attitude of those who aren''t so motivated, or who lose their motivation. Now, it''s obvious that motivation is crucial to performance, but that doesn''t tell us where it comes from. Why is it that some people work hard and do well while others can work just as hard and don''t, why some are committed to what they are doing and others aren''t? Finding answers to this question would be extremely useful to educators, as well as in other areas of life. Businesses, for example, have long believed that financial incentives - bonuses, perks, pay rises - are the great motivators, and to an extent they can make a difference, but what we are calling the mind set is more important.\nWhat has made it difficult to find out what the causes of motivation are, is that motivation and the capacity for hard work can be mistaken for talent - thinking it''s a gift. Either you''ve got it or you haven''t People who believe this have a fixed mind set and are not only going to perform less well than they could, but it''s also an attitude that will affect their whole Outlook on life. Some say that if talent is something people are born with and you''re unlucky enough not to have any, then there''s not much point in putting in all that extra effort for no real reward. However, research has shown that if you put in the hours, practice brings the same level of achievement as talent. It''s a question of changing this fixed attitude and adopting a growth attitude, which includes seeing mistakes and failures as opportunities to improve.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29b4c0b1-ebf2-5289-8bb2-b918d6c10d70'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29b4c0b1-ebf2-5289-8bb2-b918d6c10d70'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Who is the person who shares the same room with you?', '8a5c07ba-7da9-57c6-8902-1b91dea6a9a8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Roommate', NULL, NULL),
  ('29c2dc77-42d3-5268-babb-75548e814f7d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29c2dc77-42d3-5268-babb-75548e814f7d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '384a5204-8ef6-5c5b-aca0-b12f5c3747dc'::uuid, NULL, E'Pioneers of new ideas often face similar struggles and hardships.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29c4374f-c0ec-5498-8c3d-be1923065cc9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29c4374f-c0ec-5498-8c3d-be1923065cc9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'eaea934d-d871-5bbe-a679-9fb205336658'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Getting involved in art makes us really value the world around us.', NULL, NULL),
  ('29c8f76d-4025-50b8-ab38-45e905da972a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29c8f76d-4025-50b8-ab38-45e905da972a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dinner with Colleague', E'You plan to have dinner with your colleague and maybe later go to watch a movie, but right now you feel sick, and you have a headache and may have a cold. You see your colleague is having a coffee in the lunch room. What should you say?', '0cabc2d3-41bd-526d-ac06-c536b6b812c4'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey colleague, I want to talk to you about something.\nWe seem to have a little issue with our dinner and movie plan.\nIt''s like I originally planned to have dinner and watch a movie with you, but I’m feeling unwell now. I have a bad headache and think I might be catching a cold, so I’m afraid I can’t make it today.\nAnd I''d like to know what you think.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29ca302e-33da-5f10-985a-904cef849ec5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29ca302e-33da-5f10-985a-904cef849ec5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cannabis Science', E'In the final episode of a three-part podcast series, Christie Taylor explores some of the challenges and opportunities that cannabis presents for society, both now and in the future. One of the topics that Taylor examines is the possibility of growing cannabis compounds in labs, {{1}} the need for cultivating the plant itself. This could offer a more efficient and consistent way of producing cannabinoids, the active ingredients in cannabis, for medical and recreational {{2}} . Taylor talks to researchers who are working on developing methods to synthesize cannabinoids using yeast, bacteria, or algae. Another topic that Taylor discusses is the environmental impact of cannabis production, which is often {{3}} or underestimated. Growing cannabis, whether legally or illegally, consumes a lot of water, energy, land, and fertilizers, and generates greenhouse gas {{4}} and waste. Taylor interviews experts who are studying the ecological footprint of cannabis and looking for ways to make it more sustainable and less harmful to the planet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.without, 2.purposes, 3.overlooked, 4.emissions', NULL, NULL),
  ('29e04d45-4ab9-51f5-930a-52fc8f153080'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29e04d45-4ab9-51f5-930a-52fc8f153080'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Reproductive Strategies', E'The strategies plants employ in their quest for successful reproduction through pollination are as diverse as the species themselves. Some plants, like the cunning orchids, mimic the appearance and scent of female insects to {{1}} males and ensure the transfer of their pollen. Others, such as the night-blooming cereus, open only at night, relying on nocturnal creatures like bats or moths for pollination. This nocturnal strategy is particularly effective in desert environments where daytime temperatures can be {{2}} for both plants and their pollinators. In the realm of plants, then, pollination is not a uniform or straightforward process. Just as animal parents {{3}} their nurturing strategies to the specific needs and challenges of their environment, plants have evolved a broad {{4}} of pollination methods to enhance their chances of reproductive success. This diversity in reproductive strategies among plants is not only a testament to the complexity of nature but also crucial for the survival of myriad species, each adapted to its unique ecological niche. Without these specialized pollination strategies, many plants would struggle to reproduce, leading to {{5}} biodiversity and the potential collapse of ecosystems reliant on these plants.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.attract, 2.prohibitive, 3.adapt, 4.spectrum, 5.diminished', NULL, NULL),
  ('29e589c7-10f3-54cf-996f-1707f7d7b251'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29e589c7-10f3-54cf-996f-1707f7d7b251'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Love', E'It seems that when it comes to love, men and women are designed to misconstrue, misread and misunderstand one another and themselves. You discover that in fact they make good sense. Being a deluded romantic is often the best way to make a good — biologically successful — choice about a potential partner on the basis.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29e61f9e-97e1-5a99-bc62-d3f8e64f0597'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29e61f9e-97e1-5a99-bc62-d3f8e64f0597'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f1d3ccc8-70b1-5ff2-9bd3-2cb46d6f9f13'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She''s the chief executive of the country''s largest charity.', NULL, NULL),
  ('29e66f03-e941-51cb-8891-1f36a179f2db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29e66f03-e941-51cb-8891-1f36a179f2db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Temporary Job', E'Some people prefer to have temporary jobs which means they only work a few months and have more time to do what they want. Will you choose this kind of lifestyle? Why?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('29e7adcf-0219-56db-a8a8-1129718b7d96'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29e7adcf-0219-56db-a8a8-1129718b7d96'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '13bc8b15-f6ce-5f97-b13d-fb34e204502f'::uuid, NULL, E'Several universities in our city have rigid rules about student conduct.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29edb2e3-2e8f-5291-9a73-b4246506d07b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29edb2e3-2e8f-5291-9a73-b4246506d07b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Perspectives on Death', E'Infants and toddlers cannot understand death. They function in the present and are aware of loss and {{1}} , as well as disruptions in their routines. They are also {{2}} to the emotions and behaviors of significant adults in their lives, so a death of a loved one may cause a young child to become anxious and {{3}} , cry, or change their sleeping and eating habits.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.separation, 2.attuned, 3.irritable', NULL, NULL),
  ('29f1e7c8-46cb-5a17-9e4d-d53306947b3d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29f1e7c8-46cb-5a17-9e4d-d53306947b3d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Amazon Basin', E'Colorful poison frogs in the Amazon owe their great {{1}} to ancestors that leapt into the region from the Andes Mountains several times during the last 10 million years, a new study from The University of Texas at Austin suggests. This is the first study to show that the Andes have been a {{2}} {{3}} of diversity for the Amazon basin, one of the largest {{4}} of biological diversity on Earth. The finding runs {{5}} to the {{6}} that Amazonian diversity is the {{7}} of evolution only within the tropical forest itself. "Basically, the Amazon basin is ''melting pot'' for South American frogs," says graduate student Juan Santos, lead author of the study. "Poison frogs there have come from multiple places of {{8}} , notably the Andes Mountains, over many millions of years. We have shown that you cannot understand Amazonian biodiversity by looking only in the basin. Adjacent regions have played a major role."', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.diversity, 2.major, 3.source, 4.reservoirs, 5.counter, 6.idea, 7.result, 8.origin', NULL, NULL),
  ('29f41dfb-c137-58bc-8125-cc5b938c071f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29f41dfb-c137-58bc-8125-cc5b938c071f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the person who plays sports to make a living?', 'e0d99fff-6fa0-5cc4-b676-4719292923d4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Athlete / sportsman / sportswoman', NULL, NULL),
  ('29f6216c-07c6-5fd2-889a-d005ae128430'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29f6216c-07c6-5fd2-889a-d005ae128430'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Koala', E'Among those deeply committed to environmental protection, a persistent debate revolves around whether the koala should be officially {{1}} as a threatened species in Australia. The situation resembles a seesaw – in certain regions like Queensland, a {{2}} number of koalas grapple with diseases, while in the southern territories of Victoria and South Australia, their population has seemingly exploded. The {{3}} for labeling a species as ''vulnerable'' dictate a population decrease of more than 30 percent in the last three generations or ten years. However, applying this rule to koalas introduces a nuanced complexity, as the surge in Victoria seems to offset the decline {{4}} in Queensland. The challenge is further compounded by the recognition that northern koalas and their southern counterparts represent distinct branches of the koala family tree. In response to this intricacy, authorities have chosen a bifurcated approach – koalas in New South Wales, the ACT, and Queensland are officially recognized as ''Vulnerable,'' whereas those in Victoria and South Australia are not {{5}} at risk.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.designated, 2.substantial, 3.criteria, 4.observed, 5.deemed', NULL, NULL),
  ('29f851a7-456d-5b2b-b4b3-7c1a63b60d60'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29f851a7-456d-5b2b-b4b3-7c1a63b60d60'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Frank Gehry', NULL, '637ea6b9-6783-5034-b23f-7cd9b7f5c385'::uuid, NULL, E'So, continuing our series of lectures on Modernism, we now turn to architecture and, in particular, to the work of Frank O. Gehry. Now, I''m not going to go into his career in detail; it is enough to say that early on he was, like other modernist architects, tied to the rectangle, the straight line, and so on. Often their buildings would have this basic shape and they would just. urn, add bits of decoration like splashes of color or pointless balconies. Soon enough, Gehry wanted to break away from straight lines and gridlike designs. He wanted the freedom.\nto experiment with other shapes curves and unusually-angled roofs. What helped him with this was the computer, which allowed him to visualize and experiment with complex shapes, and to work on the whole design as one piece, without the added decoration being thrown in as an afterthought. Architecture as art, if you like ... or, or sculpture even. He himself said that he had struggled with crossing the line between architecture and sculpture. Now, I want to talk about one building in particular ... um ... the Guggenheim Museum in Bilbao, which I think you''ll agree is a masterpiece.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('29fc6179-c0a2-57b1-ae5e-c4498dd3b9f6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29fc6179-c0a2-57b1-ae5e-c4498dd3b9f6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the capital of France?', 'a8d17637-a61e-5c95-a965-5a72f094ce59'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Paris', NULL, NULL),
  ('29fdea7e-cbb1-5e33-9ab5-8c11c9f6fc4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '29fdea7e-cbb1-5e33-9ab5-8c11c9f6fc4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd738a242-a0c4-54f8-80d4-91979972d24b'::uuid, NULL, E'He''s worked in that same office year after year since he was eighteen.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2a022b6a-fbba-5645-9dcd-eefc205c4d59'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a022b6a-fbba-5645-9dcd-eefc205c4d59'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which season is the coldest?', '5dcf952c-31f4-5413-b389-a66caf89e76b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Winter', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a02eb68-2b61-5392-ac9f-94b3904daec3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a02eb68-2b61-5392-ac9f-94b3904daec3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mercury', E'Mercury is not found in many common products that we buy because it can be very dangerous. The most common products that {{1}} mercury are batteries, powerful outdoor lights, disinfectants and thermometers, which are used to measure our body''s temperature. It can also be found in barometers, which are used to measure air pressure and {{2}} changes in weather, and thermostats, which {{3}} the temperature of buildings. Mercury can also be found in printer and photocopy toners.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.contain, 2.show, 3.regulate', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a030141-7539-5955-9019-5ffc42a8caab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a030141-7539-5955-9019-5ffc42a8caab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is a microscope used to watch?', 'afa8d715-dc11-5fa0-9793-7833bfd90998'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Microbe', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a03dfe2-b9f7-5a33-a539-acb7234711db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a03dfe2-b9f7-5a33-a539-acb7234711db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '94480979-dea2-55d7-8c33-21a9b15c04b3'::uuid, NULL, E'She was able to pick out her father on the other side of the room.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2a0777e1-4275-5d61-a034-8564add9ede0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a0777e1-4275-5d61-a034-8564add9ede0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Regular Consumption', E'Regular consumption of a balanced diet has been proven to significantly benefit an individual’s health. A diet {{1}} in fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and lean proteins is crucial in mitigating the risk of {{2}} diseases such as heart disease, diabetes, and certain cancers. Nutritionists recommend a variety of foods to ensure a range of essential nutrients for {{3}} good health.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.rich, 2.chronic, 3.maintaining', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a0d5e4f-0caf-5b72-8c46-b33cd904f7ee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a0d5e4f-0caf-5b72-8c46-b33cd904f7ee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Moral Obligation', E'Do you believe that humans have a moral obligation to combat climate change?', NULL, NULL, E'The moral imperative for humans to combat climate change is undeniable, rooted in the fundamental responsibility we hold as stewards of the planet. Addressing climate change is not just a matter of environmental concern but a moral obligation that transcends generations and species, shaping the future of our planet and all its inhabitants.\nOne of the primary reasons why humans have a moral obligation to combat climate change is the critical need to protect future generations. By taking decisive action to address climate change now, we can ensure a sustainable and habitable planet for our children and grandchildren. Failing to act would jeopardize the well-being and prosperity of future generations, burdening them with the consequences of environmental degradation and climate-related challenges.\nIn addition to safeguarding future generations, combating climate change is essential for preserving biodiversity and upholding our global responsibility to protect all living beings. Climate change poses a significant threat to diverse ecosystems and species worldwide, leading to habitat destruction, species extinction, and ecological imbalances. By mitigating climate change through sustainable practices and conservation efforts, we can protect the rich tapestry of life on Earth and fulfill our duty to safeguard the planet for the benefit of all living beings.\nIn conclusion, the moral obligation to combat climate change is grounded in our commitment to protecting future generations, preserving biodiversity, and recognizing our global responsibility to safeguard the planet. Embracing this moral imperative requires collective action, sustainable practices, and a deep-seated sense of duty towards the Earth and its inhabitants.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2a0eff6c-87f1-5be9-8c60-6911e3870dda'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a0eff6c-87f1-5be9-8c60-6911e3870dda'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Environmental Policy', E'Thus the environmental policy does not contribute to the profitability in any real sense at all. In practice it is companies that are well organized and efficient, or that are already comfortably profitable, that have time to {{1}} and police environmental policies. However, if profitable companies are the ones most likely to establish ''environmental best {{2}} '' this is confusing cause with effect. It is not that environmental best practice causes profitability, but that being profitable allows for {{3}} for the environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.establish, 2.practice, 3.concern', NULL, NULL),
