  ('2a40c5bd-a5b0-5205-9550-31e46081cd2c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a40c5bd-a5b0-5205-9550-31e46081cd2c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Screen Time', E'A little screen time almost always works to calm kids down. But {{1}} with digital devices may lead to more problems with emotional reactivity down the road. There are two problems with distracting with media: it takes away an opportunity to teach the child about how to {{2}} to difficult emotions, and it can reinforce that big displays of their difficult emotions are effective ways to get what they want. Instead of punishing their expressions of frustration, anger or sadness with a time-out, it can be a good idea to {{3}} a comfy place for kids to collect their feelings -- maybe something with beanbags or blankets or a tent. But sometimes talking about emotions are too abstract for preschool-age kids, and in those cases Radesky recommended using color zonesto talk about emotions. Calm and content can be green; worried or {{4}} can be yellow; and upset or angry can be red, using graphics or images of faces to help kids match what they’re feeling with what color zone they are in.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.soothing, 2.respond, 3.set up, 4.agitated', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a46f3cd-6906-56ad-8143-3ab4504f3d91'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a46f3cd-6906-56ad-8143-3ab4504f3d91'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite to ‘still’?', '09c03833-ea71-53f3-9b07-7e2f11b95a83'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Moving / Active / Dynamic', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a49aaf6-03a0-54f4-a26d-a85beef8fad2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a49aaf6-03a0-54f4-a26d-a85beef8fad2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'City Population', E'Over half of population lives in cities. Is it a positive or negative development?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2a4af170-3743-5d93-9904-18fc1f4b19dd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a4af170-3743-5d93-9904-18fc1f4b19dd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Health Insurance', E'Before the Affordable Care Act came along, 80% of Americans had quality health insurance, like my wife and I, through their employer or through government programs like Medicare or Medicaid. For some, this insurance was far from ideal, as it featured high costs and a limited choice of providers. But overall, this was substantive coverage which enrollees were by and large satisfied. On the other hand, the other 20% of Americans were either uninsured or faced the prospect of buying insurance in the unstable and discriminatory non-group insurance market. This is a market where it was totally legal for insurers to discriminate against the sick for any reason. Insurers could deny the sick coverage; they could charge them much more than the healthy for insurance or they could exclude their pre-existing illnesses from coverage. As a result, if you were healthy, you could get health insurance. This defeats the whole notion of health insurance. Health insurance is supposed to protect you against financial risk, not protect your insurance company against the sick. And as a result, people in this market were just one bad gene or one bad traffic accident away from bankruptcy.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '81835eec-1a5a-5436-8f7d-a830566297ed'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Health insurance in America is not fair for everyone. Its aim should be protecting people against financial risk, instead of protecting their insurance company against the sick. If things go on the wrong track, people in this market would be very close to bankruptcy.', NULL, NULL),
