  ('2a703799-2136-5e23-bb25-6ff417b9cc8b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a703799-2136-5e23-bb25-6ff417b9cc8b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e4a67b58-d072-5813-8731-232a7e56e0e1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The new professor will teach their first chemistry class tomorrow.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a730430-956c-51e4-96f2-50aab4254762'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a730430-956c-51e4-96f2-50aab4254762'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Night Light', NULL, 'd5bd4412-8f4f-5de4-ade5-fb21886e4039'::uuid, NULL, E'In 2012, after reviewing the evidence, the American Medical Association released a major statement, night light can disrupt your sleep cycle. However, for whatever reason, not many people have been since informed about it. So here is the basics of what you need to know. When you’re exposed to a significant amount of light, specifically of the blue wavelengths, your body suppresses melatonin production to make you feel more awake. Normally this evolutionary design works pretty well. With the coming of night and day, our melatonin levels waxes and wanes giving us a circadian rhythm. However since the invention of artificial lights, we’re being exposed to more and more light at night time and these effects can be pretty big. Here’s what happens when you place participants in a room with similar brightness to your average household. This is where their melatonin levels would normally be if they were sleeping in a dark room, and here is their malotonin levels in that lit room. You can see the huge suppression of melatonin and it doesn’t take too much to see these effects either.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2a733c25-8e64-52ec-ac8a-32f9b490e99e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a733c25-8e64-52ec-ac8a-32f9b490e99e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language and Thought', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a7e14ef-2c12-5854-acfd-c44e0a55aca0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a7e14ef-2c12-5854-acfd-c44e0a55aca0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Finding a Job', E'Some people believe that finding a job is essential after graduation, while others believe that continuing education proves to be more essential. Discuss both sides and give your own opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2a828be3-9206-5ad4-9e2e-2257e55e0eec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a828be3-9206-5ad4-9e2e-2257e55e0eec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '383d7ca5-fef1-5949-9b90-354a0415e298'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'I am convinced that mathematical thinking is crucial for statistics study.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a8c059c-2732-5ac2-95ea-92ae35c8dd05'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a8c059c-2732-5ac2-95ea-92ae35c8dd05'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is commonly applied to hair for nourishment and growth?', '1a654ac0-f327-5162-a49e-02b4e5dd2a8e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Conditioner / Hair oil', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a96267e-0059-5fa9-8ed6-748076c18ed5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a96267e-0059-5fa9-8ed6-748076c18ed5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cats are Perfect', E'Cats have nailed this one thing so well that they all do it and just come up with slightly different sizes. That’s why they’re perfect, evolutionarily. They don’t need variation. They might get bigger or smaller, but they don’t change anything else because they’re doing it just right otherwise. They’re not jacks-of-all-trades; they’re masters of one.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2a992cd4-e87b-58cd-bfc2-1dbe1ca71381'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a992cd4-e87b-58cd-bfc2-1dbe1ca71381'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Resultant Force', E'The overall result of two or {{1}} forces acting on an object is called the resultant force. The resultant of two forces is a single force, which has the same effect as the two forces combined. If two forces pull an object in {{2}} directions, the size of the resultant can be found by subtracting one force from the {{3}} . If the forces are {{4}} , they balance each other, which means a resultant force of zero.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.more, 2.opposite, 3.other, 4.equal', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a99d0b5-91da-5b13-84c9-1ba779ac1010'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a99d0b5-91da-5b13-84c9-1ba779ac1010'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the total genetic content in a cell or organism?', '1bffad90-114b-5560-9383-d3954fb5b16e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Genome', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a9a1a92-daa5-5e9d-82c7-2b3ca6dd1afc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a9a1a92-daa5-5e9d-82c7-2b3ca6dd1afc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2c54255c-3dae-5489-a940-4345b4a19c92'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We got your application for money, and it''s all official now.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a9aec05-c609-5197-bfbb-e6a7c967aad5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a9aec05-c609-5197-bfbb-e6a7c967aad5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e7df03ca-c92f-582b-87d3-0514137ef8f4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The research shows that spending time outdoors has a range of benefits.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2a9b193b-3f6d-5b87-9e67-28d5ec21e13d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2a9b193b-3f6d-5b87-9e67-28d5ec21e13d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roman-era Graves', E'Hamas authorities in Gaza on Sunday announced the {{1}} of over 60 tombs in an ancient burial site dating back to the Roman era. Work crews have been {{2}} the site since it was discovered last January during preparations for an Egyptian-funded housing project. Hiyam al-Bitar, a researcher from the Hamas-run Ministry of Antiquities and Tourism, said a total of 63 graves have been identified and that a set of bones and artifacts from one tomb was dated back to the second century. She said the ministry is working with a team of French experts to learn more about the site. On Sunday, workers {{3}} through the soil and removed piles of dirt in wheelbarrows. Although the ancient cemetery is now blocked off from the public, construction on the housing project has continued and the site is surrounded by apartment buildings. Local media reported looting when the site was first discovered, with people using donkey-drawn carts to {{4}} items like a covered casket and inscribed bricks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.discovery, 2.excavating, 3.sifted, 4.haul away', NULL, NULL),
  ('2aa4a9ac-4ad6-5db5-a819-32da919c71fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aa4a9ac-4ad6-5db5-a819-32da919c71fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'decee6b9-b251-5d29-b40f-0ab691565e8c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Student representatives will be visiting the classes with voting forms.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2aa76f35-648d-5bfc-8728-5ddade2b5032'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aa76f35-648d-5bfc-8728-5ddade2b5032'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Team''s Emotions', E'If you''re putting together a team for a project, you might be inclined to pick people with cheerful, optimistic dispositions and flexible thinking. But a new management study indicates your team might also benefit from people who are exactly the opposite, according to experts at Rice University, the University of Western Australia, Bond University and the University of Queensland.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2aad4af9-9eba-5361-92f7-11fe0f444c8c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aad4af9-9eba-5361-92f7-11fe0f444c8c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '95faa95f-e73e-5d28-91e8-1c0b25e63186'::uuid, NULL, E'Children are not allowed in the chemical labs.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2aca9609-bdbc-54eb-9b1b-e68684162ec6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aca9609-bdbc-54eb-9b1b-e68684162ec6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Adaptation to Climate', NULL, '953a2c92-6395-5585-bc17-2ab8cad5f246'::uuid, NULL, E'We appear to take it as a rule, or as a law of nature, that each species is adapted to the climate of its own home. For example, species from the Arctic, or even a temperate region, could not survive in a tropical climate, nor could a tropical species last long if it found itself at the South Pole. But it is true to say there''s too much emphasis placed on the degree of adaptation of species to the climates where they live.\nWe assume that this adaptation - if all species are descended from a single form - must have taken place over millions of years, yet a large number of plants and animals brought from different countries remain perfectly healthy in their new home. Also, there are several examples of an imal species that have extended their range, within historical times, from warmer to cooler latitudes and the other way round. Rats and mice provide good examples: they have been transported by man to many parts of the world and now have a far wider range than any other rodent, and they can be found living in the cold climate of the Faroe Islands to the north through the tropical zones to the Falklands in the south. It is possible to see adaptation to any climate as a quality that is part of an inborn flexibility of the physical and mental constitution of most animals. Therefore, the ability to survive in the most different climates by both man and his domestic animals, and the fact that elephants once existed in an ice age while living species live in tropical areas, should not be seen as deviations from the rule, but as examples of this flexibility being brought into action under particular circumstances.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2acaa6be-e357-5635-9b5b-69352d175c8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2acaa6be-e357-5635-9b5b-69352d175c8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Materials', E'With the increase of digital media available online, the role of the library has become obsolete. Universities should only procure new digital media rather than constantly update textbooks. Discuss both the advantages and disadvantages of this position and give your own point of view.', NULL, NULL, E'In recent years, the explosion of new digital media has led many to question the role of traditional libraries. Some argue that universities should only procure digital materials rather than constantly updating textbooks. While there are certainly benefits to this position, there are also some drawbacks that must be considered.\nOn the one hand, the advantages of digital materials are clear. With the ability to access information from anywhere with an internet connection, students are no longer bound by the physical limitations of a traditional library. Digital materials are also often more up-to-date than traditional textbooks, which can become outdated quickly. Additionally, digital materials are often more cost-effective than traditional textbooks, which can be prohibitively expensive for some students.\nOn the other hand, there are some disadvantages to relying solely on digital materials. For one, not all students have equal access to technology and the internet. This could put some students at a disadvantage if they are unable to access necessary materials. Additionally, digital materials can be less engaging than physical books, which can lead to decreased retention and comprehension of the material.\nIn conclusion, while there are certainly benefits to universities procuring digital materials rather than constantly updating textbooks, there are also some potential drawbacks that must be considered. Ultimately, it is up to each individual university to weigh the pros and cons and determine what is best for their students.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2accf1a3-d6d3-5bf8-af81-b292683c326e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2accf1a3-d6d3-5bf8-af81-b292683c326e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Music available on the radio', NULL, 'de261a2b-31b4-57b8-9f47-e5173938a7cb'::uuid, NULL, E'These days we take for granted the wide variety of music available on the radio. But, this wasn''t always the case. In the early days of radio, stations were capable of broadcasting only a narrow range of sounds, which was all right for the human voice but music didn''t sound very good. There was also a great deal of crackling and other static noises that further interfered with the quality of the sound. A man named Edwin Armstrong, who was a music lover, set out to change this. He invented FM radio, a technology that allowed stations to send a broad range of frequencies that greatly improved the quality of the music. Now, you''d think that this would have made him a millionaire; it didn''t. Radio stations at that time had invested enormous amounts of money in the old technology. So the last thing they wanted was to invest millions more in the new technology. Nor did they want to have to compete with other radio stations that had a superior sound and could put them out of business. So they pressured the Federal Communications Commission, the department of the United States government that regulates radio stations, to put restrictive regulations on FM radio. The result was that its use was limited to a very small area around New England. Of course as we all know, Edwin Armstrong''s FM technology eventually prevailed and was adopted by thousands of stations around the world. But this took years of court battles and he never saw how it came to affect the lives of almost everyone.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2ad33ee3-4d5e-5c45-a5b6-8661ff6b7c8b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ad33ee3-4d5e-5c45-a5b6-8661ff6b7c8b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Paleoanthropologist', E'Forty years ago yesterday, November 24, 1974, paleoanthropologist Donald Johanson found in Ethiopia what''s arguably the most famous and important fossil of a human {{3}} : Lucy. Last month, at the ScienceWriters2014 meeting in Columbus, Ohio, Johanson talked about the moment he laid eyes on Lucy.\n"On that eventful day in 1974 I was out, with a graduate student, Tom Gray, and we were walking back to our Land Rover to go back to camp to enjoy a swim in the river with the crocodiles and enjoy a nice little lunch. And I am always looking at the ground. I find more quarters by parking meters than anybody I know, I think. And you know how it is you find what you''re looking for, right?\n"Because a year before the {{1}} a geologist had left his footprints four-to-five feet away from the {{4}} , because he was looking for rocks. I was looking for bones. And I found a little piece of elbow, that little {{2}} that allows us to flex and extend our arm. And I knew from my studies of osteology, of comparative anatomy and so on, that this had to be from a human ancestor.\n"And as I looked up the slope, I saw other {{5}} eroding out. And we recovered over a two-week-long excavation operation roughly, not counting hand and foot bones, 40 percent of a skeleton. And this was important because first of all it broke the three-million-year time barrier. All the fossils older than three million years at that point in the history of paleoanthropology would fit in the palm of your hand...we didn''t know it was a new species really until a few years later when we finally {{6}} in 1978 the name Australopithecus afarensis."\nFor more, check out the blog item on our Web site by Scientific American''s Kate Wong who, with Johanson, co-authored the book Lucy''s Legacy. Kate''s blog is titled The Fossil That Revolutionized the Search for Human Origins: A Q&A with Lucy Discoverer Donald Johanson.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.ancestor, 2.discovery, 3.skeleton, 4.hinge, 5.fragments, 6.published', NULL, NULL),
  ('2ad6046c-08cc-5bf5-bdf8-9a0c29ca1426'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ad6046c-08cc-5bf5-bdf8-9a0c29ca1426'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9fe0c18c-a86d-5869-8363-5722e314177f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'He is always nervous about the final exam.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2ad7767c-8f9a-5202-bc17-45c8158f5a61'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ad7767c-8f9a-5202-bc17-45c8158f5a61'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If knees are located in your legs, where are elbows located?', '0633c7ed-ff42-5a02-90d0-41aad966821f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Arms', NULL, NULL),
  ('2addfa92-d9e1-516a-9b02-28578a80d613'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2addfa92-d9e1-516a-9b02-28578a80d613'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f1143cda-bd6c-51de-ab80-c1045edc9a84'::uuid, NULL, E'All of our tutors have more than two years of teaching experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2ae5a666-534b-51ab-b92b-48a325181e8a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ae5a666-534b-51ab-b92b-48a325181e8a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ikebana', E'More than simply putting flowers in a {{1}} , ikebana is a disciplined art form in which nature and humanity are brought together. Contrary to the idea of a particolored or multicolored {{2}} of blossoms, ikebana often emphasizes other areas of the {{3}} , such as its stems and leaves, and puts emphasis on shape, line, and form. Though ikebana is an {{4}} of creativity, certain rules govern its form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.container, 2.arrangement, 3.plant, 4.expression', NULL, NULL),
  ('2aeb2c74-8ff0-56aa-a7ff-905ac23601c8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aeb2c74-8ff0-56aa-a7ff-905ac23601c8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a94f07ef-c560-57dc-b674-8860e13442fc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The history lecture has been moved to the lecture theater.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2aef358b-cde4-5be7-bdca-16ac9f512d20'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2aef358b-cde4-5be7-bdca-16ac9f512d20'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gift', E'A gift (such as a camera, a soccer ball, or an animal) can contribute to a child’s development. What gift would you give to help a child develop? Why do you choose it?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2af1fe85-c68c-5840-a756-86f1a2885f08'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2af1fe85-c68c-5840-a756-86f1a2885f08'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Organic Molecules', E'New research identifies a process that might have been key in producing the first organic molecules on Earth about 4 billion years ago, before the origin of life. The process, which is similar to what might have occurred in some ancient underwater hydrothermal vents, may also have relevance to the search for life elsewhere in the universe.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2af4addc-c3ea-5783-98f9-357657537c2f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2af4addc-c3ea-5783-98f9-357657537c2f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f46c1ae3-716c-52ee-bd10-33468962e8d0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Changing weather is starting to affect animals and where they live.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2afb4354-3c79-5437-bdfd-b656fb60a38b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2afb4354-3c79-5437-bdfd-b656fb60a38b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Whose job is it to treat people that are ill or have an injury at a hospital?', 'd095531c-8ae1-5a8f-854e-b0799ca25e3b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Doctor', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b00f20d-1a47-5353-9abf-ef3d86f30211'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b00f20d-1a47-5353-9abf-ef3d86f30211'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roman Writers', E'Roman writers and orators began to expand their imaginative and intellectual horizons and refine the Latin language through the study of Greek literature. Early Roman literature had two kinds the recording and examination of public life and behavior through life stories of famous men, and the particularly Roman art of satirical comedy and drama.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2b08c2fc-a57c-5dd9-9c56-ecbd7f1cf3f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b08c2fc-a57c-5dd9-9c56-ecbd7f1cf3f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Halloween Candy', E'Limiting your child’s candy this Halloween might be more of a trick than a treat. Once you’re a grown-up raising kids, that bag full of candy might be the scariest part of Halloween -- {{1}} it’s concern about a potential sugar rush, worries of parenting perfectionism or diet culture anxiety. But micromanaging your child’s candy supply can {{2}} , leading to an overvaluing of sweets, binge behavior or unhealthy restriction in your child. Some stress over limiting children’s Halloween candy may {{3}} the adults’ relationship with food. If you look at the candy in your child’s bag and worry that you will {{4}} on it or get anxiety about weight, it may be a good idea to talk to a mental health professional or dietitian about reworking your own relationship with food. It is especially important because what we say about food in front of children can make a big impact on the relationship they have with it and their bodies.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.whether, 2.backfire, 3.reflect, 4.binge', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b132dbf-fa41-5300-b0e2-85f017ff6be7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b132dbf-fa41-5300-b0e2-85f017ff6be7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Disposable Cups', E'What happens to disposable cups after we toss them in the trash? How do they affect the environment and our health? The answer depends on the type of cup: paper, plastic or polystyrene foam (also known as Styrofoam). Each of these materials has its own pros and {{1}} . Paper cups can end up in landfills where they decompose anaerobically, generating methane, a potent greenhouse gas. Plastic cups are made from petroleum, a non-renewable resource that {{2}} a lot of energy and water to produce. Plastic cups are also not biodegradable and can break down into microplastics, which can {{3}} the food chain and harm wildlife and human health. Polystyrene foam cups are lightweight and cheap, but they are also very harmful to the environment and health. They are made from styrene, a carcinogenic chemical that can leach into hot drinks. They are also not recyclable and can persist in the environment for centuries, {{4}} the land and water. Therefore, disposable cups have a significant impact on the environment and health, and it is important to be aware of the consequences of using them. A better {{5}} is to use reusable cups, which can reduce waste, save resources, and protect the planet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.cons, 2.requires, 3.enter, 4.polluting, 5.alternative', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b222748-4d0e-5775-8d7f-420bb89defae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b222748-4d0e-5775-8d7f-420bb89defae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bd6e81e0-32e1-5036-a226-991d69651d18'::uuid, NULL, E'He shared his own way to quickly adjust to college life.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2b22b222-411a-5ba8-af54-cbd20075c6d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b22b222-411a-5ba8-af54-cbd20075c6d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Business Emission', E'An American retail giant is set to ask its suppliers to measure and report their greenhouse gas emissions. There is a need to {{1}} business emission. The {{2}} of emission can be used to test which company causes climate change, and {{3}} the government campaigners and environmental {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.disclose, 2.data, 3.conflate, 4.invigilators', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b279541-197e-59a5-80a3-a1741f9bf13c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b279541-197e-59a5-80a3-a1741f9bf13c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Predators(捕食者)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b304da9-f8a1-5149-ad16-ec56966dface'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b304da9-f8a1-5149-ad16-ec56966dface'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6131a8f2-ce44-5053-88d6-87ee296fdccf'::uuid, NULL, E'Please leave any questions related to the topic until the end.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2b3064b7-4efc-5ba2-9334-90e39efe1efb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b3064b7-4efc-5ba2-9334-90e39efe1efb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the behavior of not buying products from an exact company as a way of protesting?', '51a1f1fd-4cfb-5f3d-ba4b-5a044c6cc262'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Boycott', NULL, NULL),
  ('2b35d5e3-81b1-5556-b927-616500052206'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b35d5e3-81b1-5556-b927-616500052206'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Extra Classes', E'It is important for children to take extra classes or play after school? Discuss both and give your opinions.', NULL, NULL, E'While structured extra classes can offer academic benefits, prioritising free play after school is fundamentally more important for a child''s holistic development. Play is not merely a leisure activity; it is the essential work of childhood, fostering creativity, resilience, and social skills that formal education often overlooks.\nFirstly, unstructured play is critical for cognitive and emotional growth. It allows children to experiment, solve problems independently, and learn from natural consequences in a low-pressure environment. For instance, building a fort with friends teaches negotiation, physics, and teamwork far more effectively than a passive lesson. This self-directed exploration builds intrinsic motivation and creative thinking, which are key to long-term success.\nSecondly, play is irreplaceable for physical health and social development. In an age of increasing screen time, active play combats sedentary habits and promotes motor skills. Socially, play is where children learn to navigate conflicts, share, and understand unspoken rules—skills crucial for building healthy relationships. The mental break from academic pressure also reduces stress, leading to a happier, more balanced child who is actually more receptive to learning when in the classroom.\nIn conclusion, while extra classes may target specific academic gaps, they risk creating burnout and neglecting the broader life skills cultivated through play. A childhood rich in play lays a stronger foundation for well-rounded adulthood. Therefore, safeguarding time for unstructured play after school is not a luxury, but a necessity for raising adaptable, healthy, and socially intelligent individuals.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('2b3fdb6f-c394-5bcf-8ae4-2f29f5919eca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2b3fdb6f-c394-5bcf-8ae4-2f29f5919eca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Advanced Robotics', E'Advanced Robotics is the international journal of the Robotics Society of Japan and has a history of more than thirty three years. It is an interdisciplinary journal which integrates publication of all aspects of research on robotics science and technology. Advanced Robotics publishes original research papers and survey papers from all over the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
