  ('2ddd92b1-5365-5e30-8b8a-c67da2666219'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ddd92b1-5365-5e30-8b8a-c67da2666219'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Soil', E'The tricky thing about soil is that no two {{1}} of it in the world are alike. One area might have a higher clay or sand content. Another might have more carbon from plants. One spot might be darker than another, and {{2}} more of the sun’s energy. In some places, like an Amazonian rainforest, trees might {{3}} almost all sunlight from hitting the earth.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.patches, 2.absorb, 3.block', NULL, NULL),
