  ('2e32c65f-730f-5e7a-80d7-29862595007e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e32c65f-730f-5e7a-80d7-29862595007e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Political Cooperation', E'For thousands of years, treaties have shaped international relations and led to complex {{1}} . International cooperative bodies such as the United Nations and the World Trade Organization exist today because of the increasing need for political cooperation at the global level. It is impossible for a country to remain {{2}} from events around the world. People’s ideas and expectations are shaped by what they see happening around them. Because of the rapid flow of information to most areas of the world, people are very {{3}} of events taking place around the globe virtually as they happen. However, some nations, such as North Korea, choose to try to isolate themselves from the rest of the world. Others try to control the flow of information within their borders. But technology makes it very difficult to control access to information. Depending on how it is used, technology can both reduce and increase political tensions and military {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.alliances, 2.isolated, 3.aware, 4.conflicts', NULL, NULL),
  ('2e393467-e402-5e08-bf50-a245bb162520'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e393467-e402-5e08-bf50-a245bb162520'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Risk Taking', E'An individual''s propensity to take risks is influenced by their own experience and that of others. The key {{1}} in risk taking is the balancing of perceptions of the risk and the possible rewards, and this balance may be a {{2}} of an individual''s particular type of {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.feature, 2.reflection, 3.personality', NULL, NULL),
  ('2e423b2c-bd50-519e-b0cb-5ee74e823b47'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e423b2c-bd50-519e-b0cb-5ee74e823b47'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Jane and Peter have three children. They are 4, 13 and 15 years old. They only have one son, who is their youngest child. How old is their middle child?', '30c2a441-32c3-57f2-8258-1e5960fe61d4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'13 years old', NULL, NULL),
  ('2e45d247-5ff3-5019-b48c-b051fea3ca62'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e45d247-5ff3-5019-b48c-b051fea3ca62'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9d210076-597b-5c7b-b606-069a39af7193'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'All of your assignments should be submitted by next Tuesday.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2e45e17c-43c3-576a-bf67-b15970caaf65'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e45e17c-43c3-576a-bf67-b15970caaf65'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Communication Systems', E'In most organizations there are both formal and informal information systems. Formal communication systems are the methods used to {{1}} information necessary for conducting the business of the organization. Formal communications {{2}} to rules and regulations prescribed by the profession or law (for example, formal reporting procedures for tracking injuries in the workplace). This is information that flows within the chain of command or within task responsibilities. The message may be procedures to provide regular progress reports to managers. It may be scheduled meetings to {{3}} information on the status of a project. Human resources may arrange seminars to convey new policies and procedures. The formal communication system makes sure necessary information flows through the organization and that {{4}} of this information is controlled. Not everyone in an organization has access to progress reports or attends project meetings. Formal communication systems ensure that information is available to those who need it and not to others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.convey, 2.conform, 3.exchange, 4.dissemination', NULL, NULL),
  ('2e5de4e2-c15a-5d76-8872-e90c11df50a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e5de4e2-c15a-5d76-8872-e90c11df50a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Time Paradox', NULL, 'f9623633-42f8-5138-830f-2ae05573507d'::uuid, NULL, E'So maybe you’re on vacation, you’re in Athens for the first time. During the day you’re experiencing a bunch of new events and new sights and sounds, and as it’s going by—that is prospectively it seems to be flying by. In retrospect however, maybe the next day or you’re back from vacation looking back upon that, it seems to be a long day. So retrospectively it seems that it was an extended period of time. And this is something that was pointed out as far back as William James in his Principles of Neuroscience over a hundred years ago. And the point is that retrospectively we’re not so much telling time but we’re rebuilding or estimating how much time has elapsed based on the number of experiences we have in memory. So retrospectively you’re more estimating how much time has elapsed, if there was a period full of new memories then you’re left with the impression that it was a long period of time retrospectively. But prospectively as it was taking place you were paying attention to some sort of internal clock in our brain, which you were looking at or querying, that was telling you that not much time has elapsed, because you weren’t paying much attention to time. So on the other hand when you’re very bored or in an anxious state people experience time as dragging or going slow (again, prospectively).', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2e60b87e-9d2c-5348-8810-3d2cb932c658'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2e60b87e-9d2c-5348-8810-3d2cb932c658'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'E-commerce', E'E-commerce giants like Amazon continue to grow and reshape traditional retail. While e-commerce offers convenience, competitive pricing, and a vast {{1}} of products, it can also lead to the {{2}} of market power in the hands of a few major players. This can stifle competition and limit consumer choice in the long {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.array, 2.concentration, 3.run', NULL, NULL),
