  ('2ea5dc6e-76b6-54dc-b333-fde137846803'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ea5dc6e-76b6-54dc-b333-fde137846803'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fc556db7-39cd-538e-a5f9-f0f9aba551e4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Several high schools are unable to offer an advanced diploma program.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2ea606e1-4f72-58ea-bed9-6a69c307a042'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ea606e1-4f72-58ea-bed9-6a69c307a042'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marshmallow Test', E'Mischel is the creator of the marshmallow test, one of the most famous experiments in the history of psychology, which is often cited as evidence of the importance of self-control. In the original test, which was administered at the Bing Nursery School, at Stanford, in the nineteen-sixties, Mischel''s team would present a child with a treat (marshmallows were just one option) and tell her that she could either eat the one treat {{1}} or wait alone in the room for several minutes until the researcher returned, at which point she could have two treats. The promised treats were always visible and the child knew that all she had to do to stop the agonizing {{2}} was ring a bell to call the experimenter back--although in that {{3}} , she wouldn''t get the second treat. The longer a child delayed gratification, Mischel found--that is, the longer she was able to wait--the better she would fare later in life at numerous measures of what we now call executive function. She would {{4}} better academically, earn more money, and be healthier and happier. She would also be more likely to avoid a number of negative outcomes, including jail time, obesity, and drug use.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.immediately, 2.wait, 3.case, 4.perform', NULL, NULL),
  ('2eb73cc5-1ca0-5361-ac78-918081526b47'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2eb73cc5-1ca0-5361-ac78-918081526b47'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '28235dd0-2815-505c-af3f-6412324e777b'::uuid, NULL, E'All the assignments are based on class discussion.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('2ebb9b60-17ea-5cba-b393-274a8e538ee0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ebb9b60-17ea-5cba-b393-274a8e538ee0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the largest main stem of a tree from which the branches grow?', '2fb078bc-0d64-518f-9e82-0b74f57d8761'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Trunk', NULL, NULL),
  ('2ebdd00d-c2fd-59a1-ae27-1efdd4c3c280'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ebdd00d-c2fd-59a1-ae27-1efdd4c3c280'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Media', E'Well, employers are currently experiencing a love hate relationship with social media. Some are using it to their advantage, their reaching more customers, increasing sales, and improving their brand image through social networking sites. They''re also using them for recruitment. On the other hand, many employers continue to see the bad side of social media and believe that it poses a threat to their business. Negative comments online can damage a brand, and employers also worry that employees might spend too much time online during working hours, stopping them from working effectively. And completing other tasks. At this problem provides employers with an opportunity. Employees who spend a lot of time on social networking sites do it because they''re bored. They don''t feel challenged and want to fill their time. This suggests that employers should take a more active role in providing development opportunities for their staff and setting new goals this way. They can benefit from the advantages of social media without experiencing the difficulties.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '10930bc5-9193-576f-a51c-4dca4ce9f267'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Social media can help employers to develop their businesses and find new staff. However, it is a problem when an employee criticises the company online or spends too much time using social media. To stop employees spending time on social media, employers must develop and challenge their staff.', NULL, NULL),
  ('2ebe7fad-d281-5efa-a903-2d31b0ba8ca2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '2ebe7fad-d281-5efa-a903-2d31b0ba8ca2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aphrodite', E'Aphrodite is the ancient Greek goddess of sexual love and beauty, {{1}} with Venus by the Romans. In early Greek art, representations of Aphrodite are fully dressed and without features that {{2}} her from other goddesses. Greek sculptors of the 5th century BCE were the first to {{3}} her with unique features.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.identified, 2.differentiate, 3.endow', NULL, NULL),
