  ('31146d85-ec5a-5f17-aa5c-c6de087689c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '31146d85-ec5a-5f17-aa5c-c6de087689c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Trisauropodiscus', E'Numerous fossil sites in southern Africa preserve distinctive three-toed footprints that have been named Trisauropodiscus. For many years, researchers have debated what animals might have left these tracks, as well as precisely how many different species (technically called ichnospecies) of Trisauropodiscus there are.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3119992b-c765-5e6f-b35a-51c9ccfeb8a8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3119992b-c765-5e6f-b35a-51c9ccfeb8a8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6036a1b8-de7a-57ea-a9eb-419972a2e598'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Physics is a key subject for understanding the world and the universe.', NULL, NULL),
  ('311ca571-4d42-5657-938d-7410d0248265'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '311ca571-4d42-5657-938d-7410d0248265'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Humans', E'Early humans were hunter-gatherers, roaming from place to place, but their movements were controlled by the need for water. When humans {{1}} to grow food and established permanent settlements, water was needed for crops and animals as well as for people, {{2}} settlements have always grown up near reliable sources of water. Most major towns lie on the banks of rivers, or, where there are no streams or rivers, settlements exist where underground water can be reached by digging wells. The management of water resources has a {{3}} . The oldest known dam in the world was constructed in Egypt about 5000 years ago, and was used for storing drinking and irrigation water. Farmers in Arabia at this time used the craters of extinct volcanoes as storage tanks for irrigation water and dug deep wells for their drinking water. Excavated ruins in India of similar antiquity retain the remains of water supply and drainage systems, {{4}} included baths and swimming pools.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.started, 2.so, 3.long history, 4.which', NULL, NULL),
  ('3122822f-fbe5-5e14-aeb4-6ad27c9103f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3122822f-fbe5-5e14-aeb4-6ad27c9103f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we describe a person who would like to help others?', '0972fb40-42a1-5225-ad13-4e37d0c75370'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Warm hearted / kind hearted / helper', NULL, NULL),
  ('3123cf14-1b6d-5491-8d1c-df0098441352'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3123cf14-1b6d-5491-8d1c-df0098441352'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '936f4e75-5f82-5b8e-b045-b45c93078cea'::uuid, NULL, E'Please prepare a PowerPoint presentation for tomorrow''s meeting.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('31281152-b8bf-5b60-bb95-0e2ef41c1c5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '31281152-b8bf-5b60-bb95-0e2ef41c1c5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Scientific Subject', E'Which subject will you choose for study of science? Explain it with examples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('312abf52-2143-5745-8e0d-fd3f22e885be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '312abf52-2143-5745-8e0d-fd3f22e885be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which mountain is the highest one in the world?', '15f460f5-6b15-5dc6-8952-c51f5b4e4a02'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Qomolangma / Mount Everest', NULL, NULL),
  ('312c183e-6cc4-5b3c-83c6-8317b7a1ffe6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '312c183e-6cc4-5b3c-83c6-8317b7a1ffe6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Linguistic Change', NULL, '8fb07dee-1269-5ef9-a22b-f99bc8946eed'::uuid, NULL, E'The Internet is changing everything. The world of language in the future is totally different from the world of language in the past and the reason is quite simple. There is more written language on the Internet now than all the libraries in the world combined. We''ve never seen anything like it before and we haven''t seen anything yet. When you''re talking about the future of a language. We are asking about its long-term prospects, where do they essentially lie? And my answer is they lie in the young people, they lie especially in the hands of teenagers. The teenagers are the parents of next generation of children. If teenagers are going to succeed in maintaining the intergenerational transmission of a language, then they have got to be infused about the minority language, the endangered language that their parents and others speak, so how would you get teenagers infused is the question. Well there is no question today, the only thing that infuses teenagers, apart from sex, is internet and all the electronic world. And so that is the area where one has got to focus. A minority language has got to get itself up electronically in all the varieties that are available to it. Now in the case of something like welsh, there is already quite a strong welsh presence on the World Wide Web and increasingly there are welsh chat rooms, welsh blogs, welsh face book interactions and so on. Well this is a very very positive sign, and it needs to be reinforced as much as possible. The future of the welsh language, I think all languages actually lies in the electronic domain.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3130a891-dd94-53be-90a3-01a0707a7b69'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3130a891-dd94-53be-90a3-01a0707a7b69'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '468db793-67ea-5c8e-a1f3-0695d124396e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This theory has been used to measure and report financial information.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3133e8b8-edee-5341-83ef-4b6b254ef5f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3133e8b8-edee-5341-83ef-4b6b254ef5f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Communication Skills', E'In terms of your own communication skills, it is important to give just as much of your attention to a message you are receiving as to one you are giving. Listening, {{1}} , as well as being a method for gathering information, {{2}} your interest in what the other person is concerned with. This in itself can have a positive effect on your relationship with them and, if you are their manager, their motivation. Asking questions {{3}} clarification of the detail of the message can also convey that you have understood the message and that you want to respond to it {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.for example, 2.can convey, 3.for, 4.appropriately', NULL, NULL),
  ('31371832-f726-5400-b08b-07e010ee7ea8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '31371832-f726-5400-b08b-07e010ee7ea8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f713e704-b5f1-5d68-a8c5-e5dd128493bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Science and technology is good for the global economy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('313a3f4b-8d48-50d8-91e5-e083e417b009'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '313a3f4b-8d48-50d8-91e5-e083e417b009'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the common name for sodium chloride?', 'b8edefea-656d-510a-9e10-d71a6e590910'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Salt', NULL, NULL),
  ('313babfd-738c-5169-b12b-2312152b232d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '313babfd-738c-5169-b12b-2312152b232d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yellow Stone', E'Most Americans know about Yellowstone National Park, the first national park in the US, which was established in 1872. Probably less well-known is the fact that Native American tribes were removed from the land to make the park possible.\nYellowstone is not an anomaly. Many Native American tribes once lived on sprawling ancestral lands that the U.S. government either forcibly took from them or purchased through treaties whose provisions were subsequently nullified. Some of this land later became part of the nation''s 400-plus national parks and sites, with the US government providing the historical interpretations. These interpretations, however, either downplayed or ignored the Indigenous point of view.\nCreating tribal national parks allows Indigenous people to be in charge of the narrative. Simply put, tribal national parks are national parks created on tribal lands. The first of these tribal national parks was Frog Bay Tribal National Park in Wisconsin, opened by the Red Cliff Band of Lake Superior Chippewa in 2012. The park is on the state''s Bayfield peninsula, across from the famous Apostle Islands National Lakeshore.\nSeveral more tribal national parks are in the works, as Indigenous people seek to preserve and protect their land, while creating recreational opportunities for their members and others, but there''s another important reason for these parks'' creation: They allow the tribes to tell their own stories.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('313bba73-a865-5741-92ec-ba3c97a54754'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '313bba73-a865-5741-92ec-ba3c97a54754'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cd5f77c3-0dac-56a9-8d56-db183f783c53'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Remember, the prestigious student stewardship has strict eligibility criteria.', NULL, NULL),
  ('313d131c-eee0-58a5-8113-40f96591115b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '313d131c-eee0-58a5-8113-40f96591115b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9569f3af-f652-5b40-ac89-556c3ef113b3'::uuid, NULL, E'I anticipate being tardy for the upcoming class that I have.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('313db141-a5b9-509c-9660-19237f796c33'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '313db141-a5b9-509c-9660-19237f796c33'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '83ddc71b-e61a-53fa-8a62-5440215bd89f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Review all your sources before drawing any definitive conclusions.', NULL, NULL),
  ('31427cae-57c7-5834-92b1-8c06808ab078'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '31427cae-57c7-5834-92b1-8c06808ab078'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a83f3acb-b6ed-519b-a380-9756bdd5eec1'::uuid, NULL, E'It took us over an hour to reach the crest of the hill in the countryside.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3142edeb-7b7a-54ae-beca-f87df2a0af67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3142edeb-7b7a-54ae-beca-f87df2a0af67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gunpowder and Fireworks', E'Gunpowder and fireworks might have been invented independently in Europe, but they probably reached Europe via the Mongols, who spread west from China as far as central Europe by the mid-13th century. In 1267, the English monk Roger Bacon {{1}} what were very likely firecrackers, which he compared with the flash of lightning and growl of thunder.\nIn 1377 fireworks accompanied a religious mystery play by the bishop''s palace in Vicenza, and were soon used to add sparks to figures of doves, representing the Holy Spirit, or angels, made to ascend and descend from the heavens on ropes.\nBy the 15th century, rockets were being used in Europe for military and peaceful purposes. Italian and Spanish cities in particular {{2}} fireworks for outdoor celebrations. The Italian metallurgist Vannoccio Biringuccio described festivities in Florence and Siena for feast days. These included ''girandoles'' or whirling decorated wheels packed with fireworks which {{3}} a rope hung across a street or square.\nFireworks were also used in the German lands. An elaborate colour-painted book {{4}} the Schembart carnival of Nuremberg, which saw men dressed in brightly-coloured costumes parading through the town. Often these included some kind of pyrotechnics. One image shows a man wearing a hat in the form of a castle with fireworks and smoke shooting up from the towers, and interestingly, what looks like a smoking artichoke.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.recorded seeing, 2.began to use, 3.were suspended from, 4.commemorates', NULL, NULL),
  ('3143a9b5-c31e-568d-b7ce-11679a2530a8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3143a9b5-c31e-568d-b7ce-11679a2530a8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biology and Mathematics', NULL, '25079533-e0ce-58de-8682-943a699145e7'::uuid, NULL, E'Now, you might think it strange that in a lecture on biology, I will be talking a lot about mathematics... urn ... If I may digress a bit ... When I was a student, mathematics, the language of dear abstraction, had nothing to do with life sciences like biology, the sphere of messy organic forms, cutting up frogs in the lab, and so on... um ... In fact, I started doing biology precisely to avoid matlls and physics.\nSo, I''ve had a lot of catching up to do. We are all aware of how the sciences have come to inter-relate more and more, and not only will mathematics impinge more and more on biology but also, I am told, in the 21" century, the driving force behind mathematics will be biology. This is partly because mathematicians are always on the look out for more areas to conquer. But a far greater reason is that the subject has been boiled down to physics and chemistry - obvious attractions for mathematicians.A number of mathematical fields can be applied to biology.\nFor example, knot theory is used in the analysis of the tangled strands of DNA, and abstract geometry in four or more dimensions is used to tell us about viruses. Again, neuroscience appears to be mathsfriendly and equations can also explain why hallucinogenic drugs cause the users to see spirals. So, if mathematicians are taking such a keen interest in biology, the least we can do as biologists is return the compliment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3148ef8b-74f0-5355-b84e-a8e7346454c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3148ef8b-74f0-5355-b84e-a8e7346454c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Honeybees Vaccination', E'It may still come as a surprise that human beings are not alone in having invented vaccination. Work just published in the Journal of Experimental Biology by Gyan Harwood of the University of Illinois, Urbana-Champaign, confirms that honeybees may invent vaccination earlier.\nBeing gregarious, honeybees are at constant risk of diseases sweeping through their hives. Most animals which live in crowded conditions have particularly robust immune systems, so it long puzzled entomologists that honeybees do not. Indeed, they actually possess fewer immune-related genes than most solitary bees.\nPart of the answer, discovered in 2015, is that queen bees vaccinate their eggs by transferring into them, before they are laid, fragments of proteins from disease-causing pathogens. These act as antigens which trigger the development of a protective immune response in the developing young. But that observation raises the question of how the queen receives her antigen supply in the first place, for she subsists purely on royal jelly, a substance secreted by worker bees which are at the stage of their lives (which precedes the period that they spend flying around foraging for nectar and pollen) when they act as nurses to larvae. Dr. Harwood therefore wondered if the nurses were mixing the royal jelly they were producing and fragments from pathogens they had consumed while eating the victuals brought to the hive by the foragers.\nLater, the findings suggest that nurse bees are indeed, via their royal jelly, passing antigens on to the queen for inoculation into her eggs. They also mean, because larvae, too, receive royal jelly for the first few days after they hatch, that the nurses are inoculating their larval charges as well. Each infant bee is therefore being vaccinated twice.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
