  ('33378f8b-1bd3-579f-ba79-375e43ec5391'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '33378f8b-1bd3-579f-ba79-375e43ec5391'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3f22f1bd-1cf2-5c6b-839b-451062747523'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The plight of wildlife has been ignored by local developers.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3337caef-b69f-5dd5-9cf2-30731eb178b0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3337caef-b69f-5dd5-9cf2-30731eb178b0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '441504f4-78b8-56a3-a8e8-ffdfd277199f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The cost of transport is a major expense for the industry.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3342c118-1972-584f-a41b-a241d51a2e41'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3342c118-1972-584f-a41b-a241d51a2e41'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Light Pollution', NULL, 'd06eab12-73be-5923-a2df-3a286136e430'::uuid, NULL, E'Look at any photo of earth’s night sight, and you see the planet lit up like a Christmas decoration. As the glowing lights of bustling cities expand, the serenity of natural darkness wanes. But the repercussions are not just the loss of the starry night sky. Light pollution also affects animals who depend on a nighttime environment to survive. Many bird species use the stars to navigate at night. Baby sea turtles use moonlight reflected off the ocean to guide them back to the water. City lights can confuse them, and fear them off course. Humans are not immune, either. Excessive exposure to artificial light at night can increase the risk of sleep disorders and it’s also been linked to obesity, depression, diabetes and even cancer.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('334b25e1-ce97-52dd-8e5a-93b2c6b9f521'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '334b25e1-ce97-52dd-8e5a-93b2c6b9f521'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A Messy Gym', E'You notice that the communal gym equipment at your apartment complex has been left in disarray with weights scattered all over the floor and machines left unattended. You decide to send a friendly reminder to your neighbors. What would you say to your neighbors?', 'a62ea212-a976-5aaa-9a37-8be60a9ce13d'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey neighbors, just a quick heads up about the gym. I noticed that things are a bit messy lately – weights all over, machines left hanging. Let''s all pitch in to keep it tidy. I think that it''s more enjoyable and convenient for everyone when it''s clean and organized. So, if you see something out of place, please do your part and put it back where it belongs. Thanks for keeping our gym a great place to work out!', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('334bfdd8-54af-53f7-97e8-2fd8eb97a6f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '334bfdd8-54af-53f7-97e8-2fd8eb97a6f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Therapeutic Goods', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('3351f974-47a4-595e-bccf-7f7b87c30b8e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3351f974-47a4-595e-bccf-7f7b87c30b8e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mark Deduction', E'Some universities deduct marks from students'' work if it is given late. What is your opinion? What other actions do you recommend?', NULL, NULL, E'In the world of academia, the issue of late submissions is a topic of ongoing debate. While some universities impose penalties, such as deducting marks, to encourage students to take their studies seriously and develop good habits, others argue that this practice can be unfair and create additional stress for students. In this essay, we will examine both sides of the argument and explore alternative actions that may be more effective in promoting academic success and reducing stress levels.\nOn the one hand, some argue that this practice is necessary to ensure that students learn to manage their time effectively and take their studies seriously. By imposing penalties for late submissions, universities can encourage students to prioritize their coursework and develop good habits that will serve them well in their future careers. Additionally, it can prevent students from taking advantage of lenient deadlines and submitting subpar work.\nOn the other hand, opponents of this practice argue that it can be unfair to students who may have legitimate reasons for submitting their work late, such as illness or family emergencies. Deducting marks can also create additional stress and anxiety for students who are already under pressure to perform well. Some argue that alternative actions, such as offering extensions or allowing students to submit work without penalty up to a certain date, may be more effective in promoting academic success and reducing stress levels.\nIn conclusion, while the practice of deducting marks from late submissions may have some benefits, it is important for universities to consider the potential drawbacks and explore alternative actions that may be more equitable and effective in promoting academic success.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3357c9f7-3942-56bd-b3e8-2830f473c22e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3357c9f7-3942-56bd-b3e8-2830f473c22e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Scientific Consensus', E'Although scientific consensus on human responsibility -- reaffirmed by the sixth report of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) -- has been in place for decades, a third of the population still doubts or disputes it. This phenomenon can be explained by the disinformation spread by certain companies and lobbies over the last 50 years.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
