  ('367ba988-0f1a-53ad-a9d9-1d7ee7c2a1cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '367ba988-0f1a-53ad-a9d9-1d7ee7c2a1cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6c4f1fe4-239e-5921-b143-c0b73d07ea81'::uuid, NULL, E'In the plant, skilled workers who perform key jobs form into groups.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('367cbf55-c09e-5159-b99d-edb19959ccc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '367cbf55-c09e-5159-b99d-edb19959ccc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heatwave', E'Australia is facing extreme weather conditions as a severe heatwave and heavy rainfall {{1}} different parts of the country. While some regions are experiencing temperatures above 40C, others are dealing with floods and cyclones. The Pilbara region in Western Australia is the worst affected by the heatwave, with temperatures reaching up to 48.3C on Sunday. The {{2}} of 50.7C, set in January 2022, could be broken as the heatwave continues into the next week. Meanwhile, a low pressure system has brought torrential rain to parts of the Northern Territory, causing floods and {{3}} supplies. Some areas have received more than six times their usual January rainfall. The system is expected to move outwards and bring relief to the affected areas. In addition, a tropical cyclone named Kirrily {{4}} to strike the coast of Queensland later this week, bringing strong winds and heavy rain.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.hit, 2.record, 3.disrupting, 4.is forecast', NULL, NULL),
  ('367ebabe-1b80-567d-8e03-0e44722e8130'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '367ebabe-1b80-567d-8e03-0e44722e8130'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roman and Water', E'Clean water was very important to the Romans. Cities, towns and forts were built near springs. However, as Roman cities and towns grew, they needed to bring in water from {{1}} . As the population grew, {{2}} did the need for clean water. Trying to shift {{3}} of water underground in pipes was not possible as lead pipes would be too weak and bronze pipes would be too expensive. The Romans could not make cast iron pipes as the {{4}} for doing this were not known to them. If water could not be brought via pipes, the Romans decided to bring it overland in what were conduits. When the water got to the city, it was fed off into smaller bronze or ceramic pipes. To get the water to flow at an even (and slow) pace, conduits were built on a slight slope. Valleys were crossed by using aqueducts. One of the most famous of these is the Pont du Gard aqueduct at Nimes in southern France. Where possible, the Romans did take water through tunnels but the hills needed to be relatively small for this to be successful.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.further afield, 2.so, 3.large volumes, 4.techniques', NULL, NULL),
  ('367f4016-9782-56a7-808c-a0d4ae0bcb93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '367f4016-9782-56a7-808c-a0d4ae0bcb93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urban Green Spaces', NULL, '894936ec-e8fa-58d4-a8ee-43b8d795f1cb'::uuid, NULL, E'The often overlooked impact of urban green spaces on community well-being it yet significant. In our fast-paced urban lives, these natural havens play a vital role in enhancing our quality of life. Urban green spaces, like parks and gardens, provide essential breathing spaces amidst the concrete landscape. They are not just areas of aesthetic beauty but also crucial for mental and physical health. Studies have shown that regular exposure to green spaces reduces stress, improves mood, and encourages physical activity, all of which are vital for a healthy lifestyle. Additionally, these green areas foster community interaction and engagement. They act as social hubs where people of all ages can come together, promoting a sense of belonging and community spirit. This is particularly important in urban settings where isolation and anonymity can be prevalent. In conclusion, urban green spaces are more than just patches of nature in our cities; they are essential components for enhancing community well-being. As we move forward, prioritizing and preserving these spaces is crucial for the health and happiness of urban populations.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('36874cbc-d3f0-5d64-a466-2b701b0aca0b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '36874cbc-d3f0-5d64-a466-2b701b0aca0b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Depression Symptons', E'Symptoms of depression decrease with improvements in sense of smell, particularly among patients with dysosmia. New research published in the journal Scientific Reports highlights the intricate relationship between depression and sense of smell. The study found that participants’ symptoms of depression dropped as their odor identification improved, particularly among those with an impaired sense of smell.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('368d1168-9df3-5d60-9fe4-f17073099018'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '368d1168-9df3-5d60-9fe4-f17073099018'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2dce6110-b802-5bfe-a073-dc7d521bca54'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Our goal is to effectively improve students'' pronunciation skills through instruction.', NULL, NULL),
  ('368d3d0a-4fd0-5bef-953d-fd8b8d0468e0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '368d3d0a-4fd0-5bef-953d-fd8b8d0468e0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '89248d63-07d6-56af-a6f5-0b852ea2cef1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'All dissertations must be accompanied by a submission form.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3694bc67-a4b2-5e1a-b3a3-8a6b366f7db1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3694bc67-a4b2-5e1a-b3a3-8a6b366f7db1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'British Banknotes', E'The first images of banknotes featuring Britain’s King Charles III were unveiled on Tuesday by the Bank of England. Charles’ {{1}} will appear on English notes of £5, £10, £20 and £50. Meanwhile, the rest of the design will {{2}} the same as the current notes that feature the late Queen Elizabeth II on the front. The reverse side of the notes will remain unchanged -- the current designs feature portraits of Winston Churchill, Jane Austen, JMW Turner and Alan Turing on the reverse of the £5, £10, £20 and £50 notes, {{3}} . And to minimize the environmental and financial impact of this change, new notes will only be printed to replace worn banknotes and to meet any overall increase in demand for banknotes. The new banknotes are expected to {{4}} circulation by mid-2024 and will co-circulate with notes featuring the Queen’s portrait, which will remain legal tender in the UK, according to the bank.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.portrait, 2.remain, 3.respectively, 4.enter', NULL, NULL),
  ('369cebb5-e4d5-55e1-bcc2-d60b53c94f50'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '369cebb5-e4d5-55e1-bcc2-d60b53c94f50'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What vehicle runs on railways?', 'fed02581-c520-5369-bff2-0bcac20d8ce3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Train', NULL, NULL),
  ('369ec815-69da-53c1-b7de-e90c05af66a5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '369ec815-69da-53c1-b7de-e90c05af66a5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'NASA Astronaut Requirement', E'If you ever dreamed of being an astronaut as a kid, then you know that its no easy feat. The US space agency has revealed on its website all of the requirements that need to be met by someone before they have a shot at going to space. The requirements to be a NASA astronaut have changed over the years to better align with the agency’s mission and values.\nFirst, a potential candidate must be a US citizen. They also have to have a master’s degree in a STEM field from an accredited institution — acceptable degrees include engineering, biological science, physical science, computer science, or mathematics.\nOn top of that, a potential candidate has to have at least two years of related professional experience after completing their degree, or ‘at least 1,000 hours pilot-in-command time on jet aircraft,’ the agency noted. NASA also emphasized the types of characteristics it’s looking for in its astronauts, including a skilled leader, a good communicator, and a good collaborator.\nIt’s not enough to simply be educated to be an astronaut, though, a candidate also has to be able to withstand the physical pressure of being in space. On that note, a person must be extremely healthy and able to pass the NASA long-duration flight astronaut physical, which tests agility, body coordination, eye coordination, and vision. Furthermore, NASA astronaut positions require a candidate to be of particular height and weight. To be a commander or pilot astronaut, you need to be 158cm to 190cm tall, and to be a mission specialist you need to be between 149cm to 193cm. In general, astronauts should weigh between 50 and 95 kilograms (110 and 209 pounds) and measure between 149.5cm and 190.5cm.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('369f6880-ed05-5b7a-8ce3-170b28239ca5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '369f6880-ed05-5b7a-8ce3-170b28239ca5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Economic Growth', E'Currently, spending on consumer services (think hotels, passenger transportation and hair salons, for example) is growing rapidly and keeping the economy above {{1}} . But this strong growth can’t {{2}} forever. As the fear of the pandemic subsides and households return to pre-pandemic spending patterns, the pace of recovery in consumer services will slow, and by 2023, job growth in this sector will no longer be unusually high. In its fight to {{3}} inflation and slow the economy, the Federal Reserve will continue to rapidly raise interest rates, which makes stock prices tend to decline, reducing households’ net worth and spending. This has created an economy where significant job growth and low inflation cannot coexist. It is either one or the other, because significant expansion of employment in a super-tight labor market will {{4}} wages, and therefore prices. In such an environment, we should expect slow economic and job growth for the rest of the decade.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.water, 2.persist, 3.tame, 4.accelerate', NULL, NULL),
  ('36a28bca-d6b8-5ffc-9339-afcfc6278d23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '36a28bca-d6b8-5ffc-9339-afcfc6278d23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f204bc32-e04f-5b93-aaa0-11e4b1ea7239'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We can all meet at my office after the lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('36a6507b-a84f-5e22-8db5-6bee2b5216ef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '36a6507b-a84f-5e22-8db5-6bee2b5216ef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who prepares, controls, and issues the financial statements of a company?', 'ca825a0d-06b4-561f-96fe-4277f48d23ec'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Accountant', NULL, NULL),
  ('36a9453e-1d9b-53a9-a95c-cee0891a44df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '36a9453e-1d9b-53a9-a95c-cee0891a44df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the money that you make in business after paying the costs involved?', '83e78a01-478c-5310-a489-e9260371be59'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Profit', NULL, NULL),
