  ('390bf5ac-29db-5810-a0e1-c4e801e53a6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '390bf5ac-29db-5810-a0e1-c4e801e53a6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call an animal that lives in or on another animal and gets food or protection from it?', 'fa436b23-f41c-5359-a5b3-c042fbaa0b09'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Parasite', NULL, NULL),
  ('390f16a6-b417-5634-9681-e2750597eebf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '390f16a6-b417-5634-9681-e2750597eebf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '42eac1a2-7d71-583b-b676-39f633406122'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some adult students have enrolled in an online degree program.', NULL, NULL),
  ('39105fb8-71a0-59b1-a1a6-8268ff43efa6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39105fb8-71a0-59b1-a1a6-8268ff43efa6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '95ed9ea4-7d74-5393-a3cb-e4ad2f173439'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She collected a vast body of information on the subject.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3911c507-186c-5e46-b6cc-67c898ba5eb6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3911c507-186c-5e46-b6cc-67c898ba5eb6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c4dd6bd0-9eab-56e6-9d4f-6ca09a605a03'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She left the lights turned on.', NULL, NULL),
  ('39152162-b02d-5a65-8a25-d4651dd11620'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39152162-b02d-5a65-8a25-d4651dd11620'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coffee Production', E'Climate change is intensifying and is putting the future of the entire coffee sector at risk. Roughly half of the land used to grow coffee will decrease and will no longer be suitable for coffee production. With effects from climate change rising at an alarming pace, higher temperatures are significantly impacting coffee cultivation at lower elevations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('39177290-4185-5809-b0b1-1f3471d0832d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39177290-4185-5809-b0b1-1f3471d0832d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Preface', E'Science is a dominant theme in our culture. Since it touches almost every facet of our life, educated people need at least some {{1}} with its structure and operation. They should also have an understanding of the subculture in which scientists live and the kinds of people they are. An understanding of general {{2}} of science as well as specific scientific concepts is easier to attain if one knows something about the things that excite and frustrate the scientist.\nThis book is written for the intelligent student or lay person whose acquaintance with science is superficial; for the person who has been presented with science as a musty storehouse of dried facts; for the person who sees the chief objective of science as the production of gadgets. The book can be used to {{3}} a course in any science, to accompany any course that attempts to give an understanding of the modern world, or independently of any course — simply to provide a better understanding of science. We hope this book will lead readers to a broader perspective on scientific attitudes and a more {{4}} view of what science is, who scientists are, and what they do.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.acquaintance, 2.characteristics, 3.supplement, 4.realistic', NULL, NULL),
  ('39294092-18a1-5ff8-b196-3922517c821b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39294092-18a1-5ff8-b196-3922517c821b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Landscape', E'Yet this landscape, which appeared so alien and confronting to the white settlers and explorers, had been home for thousands of years to Indigenous Australians for whom the plains, ranges and deserts were a sustaining, spiritual and integral part of their existence.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('392de0bd-389c-5266-aba9-f958c758b26f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '392de0bd-389c-5266-aba9-f958c758b26f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Worker Organization', E'In this newly emerging economic order, workers sometimes organized to protect their rights and traditional ways of life. Craft workers such as carpenters, printers, and tailors formed unions, and in 1834 individual unions came together in the National Trades'' Union. The labor movement gathered some momentum in the decade before the Panic of 1837, but in the depression that followed, labor''s strength collapsed. During hard times, few workers were willing to strike or engage in collective action. And skilled craft workers, who spearheaded the union movement, did not feel a particularly strong bond with semiskilled factory workers and unskilled laborers. More than a decade of agitation did finally bring a workday shortened to 10 hours to most industries by the 1850''s, and the courts also recognized workers'' right to strike, but these gains had little immediate impact.\n\nWhich of the following statements about the labor movement of the 1800''s is supported by the paragraph?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'It went down during times of economic crisis.\nIt was slow to improve conditions for workers.', NULL, NULL),
  ('39307b78-1b13-5221-85b7-3623af0528f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39307b78-1b13-5221-85b7-3623af0528f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What day is the first day of a week which starts with T?', 'dcaab7a5-b461-5261-87ff-8b0fa49cb5ff'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tuesday', NULL, NULL),
  ('39323fa6-8c62-5d04-9958-4682aa4a255d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '39323fa6-8c62-5d04-9958-4682aa4a255d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd1cf7372-1eb8-5207-8b16-97dd91dda5fe'::uuid, NULL, E'Ample affordable off-campus housing options are readily available to students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3937e34e-3dc6-5306-b204-37d16f0bb87f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3937e34e-3dc6-5306-b204-37d16f0bb87f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Town of Liberal', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 5, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('393f8140-a299-5f09-adc7-b0fac59e627c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '393f8140-a299-5f09-adc7-b0fac59e627c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Antarctica', E'Antarctica is a land mass located around the South Pole and it has more ice than any other place on Earth. In fact, 99.5 percent of its land mass is covered in ice. During Arctic winter, the ice sheet covering the continent gets even bigger. Antarctica is our fifth largest continent, at 5.4 million square miles, coming in between South America and Europe. Its shape is roughly circular, with one arm reaching out toward South America. This is why many trips to Antarctica are via Argentina.\nEven during its warmest period (November to February), Antarctica''s temperatures mostly stay below freezing. During the winter, they can drop as low as minus 90 degrees Fahrenheit. The continent receives little precipitation and its snow is dry and powdery. Its constant strong and blustery winds can reach speeds of 200 miles per hour.\nNaturally inhospitable to humans and most animals, Antarctica wasn''t even formally explored until the 19th century. Today, though, many scientists and researchers call Antarctica their temporary home, living in special facilities while they study the ecosystem and native life.\nWhat kind of life is there on Antarctica? The harsh climate and landscape isn''t kind to most land animal life. The sea, though, is a different story. The southern oceans are full of nutrients and protein. The abundant food sources sustain many species, including whales, sea birds, seals and more. The most famous ambassador of Antarctica is the penguin, a bird that lives in colonies on the Antarctica shores and feeds from the sea.\nSince Antarctica has no human inhabitants, many nations have laid claim to it, including Argentina, Australia, Chile, France, Great Britain, New Zealand and Norway. However, the terms of the Antarctic Treaty of 1959 state that the continent is reserved purely for scientific research. This also keeps Antarctica a war-free and nuclear-free zone. Currently, 47 countries have signatures on the treaty.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('393fdf83-63b1-5305-aa14-93aec2c9d0fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '393fdf83-63b1-5305-aa14-93aec2c9d0fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ee0ed2f8-475d-56ec-98b1-ad1a3a09b6f2'::uuid, NULL, E'Psychological and sociological studies emphasize the importance of the family.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
