  ('3a00bdbf-05bf-5b8c-979e-16765dd035a9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3a00bdbf-05bf-5b8c-979e-16765dd035a9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Light-driven Machinery', E'Chemists have developed a new approach to convert photo-switchable molecules from their stable state into metastable one with low-energy red light. Their work enables fast, highly selective, and efficient switching, providing new tools for energy storage, activation of drugs with light, and sensing applications.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3a020365-622a-5747-9789-af2a661c702f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3a020365-622a-5747-9789-af2a661c702f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Art and Culture', E'Art and culture can improve life quality. Should the government or private investment be responsible for the funding of art and culture? Give your opinion.', NULL, NULL, E'Art and culture are essential components of a thriving society, and funding for these areas is crucial for their continued growth and development. While some argue that charity or private investment should be responsible for funding art and culture, I believe that the government should take the lead in this area.\nFirstly, government funding is necessary to ensure that everyone has access to art and culture. Art and culture should not be reserved for the wealthy or privileged. By providing funding for art and cultural programs, the government can make these programs available to everyone. This can have a positive impact on social cohesion and community development, as people from diverse backgrounds come together to appreciate and participate in art and cultural activities.\nSecondly, government funding can help to support emerging artists and cultural organizations. Without government funding, it can be challenging for new artists and organizations to secure the resources they need to grow and develop. By providing funding for emerging artists and organizations, the government can help to promote creativity and innovation in the arts, which can lead to new ideas and new forms of artistic expression.\nIn conclusion, I believe that the government should be responsible for funding art and culture. By doing so, the government can ensure that everyone has access to these essential components of a thriving society. Additionally, government funding can help to support emerging artists and cultural organizations, which can lead to new forms of artistic expression and greater creativity in our society.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3a03b8d1-88a2-5438-9cf8-83036b2124d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3a03b8d1-88a2-5438-9cf8-83036b2124d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd9a20b8b-230d-5add-bc04-ca93f57678c4'::uuid, NULL, E'The Romans left in four hundred and ten at the beginning of the fifth century.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3a079e83-150f-53e6-9757-47d68d32470c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3a079e83-150f-53e6-9757-47d68d32470c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language Teaching Approaches', E'Over the years, language teachers have alternated between favoring teaching approaches that focus primarily on language use and those that focus on language forms or analysis. The alternation has been due to a fundamental disagreement concerning whether one learns to communicate in a second language by communicating in that language (such as in an immersion experience) or whether one learns to communicate in a second language by learning the lexicogrammar – the words and grammatical structures – of the target language. In other words, the argument has been about two different means of achieving the same end.\nAs with any enduring controversy, the matter is not easily resolved. For one thing, there is evidence to support both points of view. It is not uncommon to find learners who, for whatever reason, find themselves in a new country or a new region of their own country, who need to learn a new language, and who do so without the benefit of formal instruction. If they are postpubescent, they may well retain an accent of some kind, but they can pick up enough language to satisfy their communicative needs. In fact, some are natural acquirers who become highly proficient in this manner. In contrast, there are learners whose entire exposure to the new language comes in the form of classroom instruction in lexicogrammar. Yet they too achieve a measure of communicative proficiency, and certain of these learners become highly proficient as well. What we can infer from this is that humans are amazingly versatile learners and that some people have a natural aptitude for acquiring languages and will succeed no matter what the circumstances.', NULL, NULL, E'Over the years, language teachers have alternated between favoring teaching approaches that focus primarily on language use and those that focus on language forms or analysis, but the matter is not easily resolved, as there is evidence to support both points of view, whereas humans are amazingly versatile learners and that some people have a natural aptitude for acquiring languages and will succeed no matter what the circumstances.', NULL, 5, 75),
