  ('3ad1aa7f-506e-5031-b43f-c160143598cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ad1aa7f-506e-5031-b43f-c160143598cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e625d292-4fec-5f3f-9a53-2a399fdb09fc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The conclusions of our earlier study must be viewed cautiously.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3ad45598-4ea9-57dd-9dd6-523819c3bfc5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ad45598-4ea9-57dd-9dd6-523819c3bfc5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'English Colonies', E'English colonies {{1}} along the eastern seaboard for a variety of reasons. People, primarily men, originally migrated to Virginia to find gold and silver to make a quick profit. {{2}} it became evident that there were no precious metals in the area, men came to Virginia to start cultivating cash crops like tobacco.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.emerged, 2.After', NULL, NULL),
  ('3adfd8d6-24ee-5e3d-bebb-6f537e19ad27'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3adfd8d6-24ee-5e3d-bebb-6f537e19ad27'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ee7d2bf0-26b3-5a30-8384-ae566275ef88'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The firm has close ties with an American corporation.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3ae477f5-b6af-59d7-b183-939ee47c1f46'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ae477f5-b6af-59d7-b183-939ee47c1f46'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Perseverance Rover', E'Perseverance, like past rovers on Mars, has a weather station to {{1}} it of any unfavorable conditions for operation. The rover consistently sends weather {{2}} back to ground for scientists to analyze! The cameras on Perseverance also have covers that are only removed when the camera is in {{3}} , limiting its exposure. The cameras, {{4}} , still get dusty!', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.alert, 2.information, 3.use, 4.however', NULL, NULL),
  ('3af972ad-9254-5fa6-b1ec-d6f8efc97e5a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3af972ad-9254-5fa6-b1ec-d6f8efc97e5a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Salary on Achievements', E'Pay-for-performance is a trend for teachers. Some people agree that it is an incentive for teachers to link students'' achievements to teachers'' salaries, while others disagree. What is your opinion about paying teachers according to students'' achievement? Give your reasons.', NULL, NULL, E'Pay-for-performance is a trend for teachers that has been gaining attention in recent years. Supporters of this approach argue that it provides a powerful incentive for teachers to improve students'' academic outcomes, leading to a more motivated and effective teaching workforce. In this essay, I will outline the positive aspects of pay-for-performance policies for teachers.\nFirstly, pay-for-performance can motivate teachers to work harder and achieve better results. When teachers are rewarded based on their students'' academic achievements, they have a clear incentive to focus on improving those outcomes. This can lead to a more motivated and engaged teaching workforce, which can have a positive impact on students'' academic success.\nSecondly, pay-for-performance can be seen as a fair way to reward teachers who are performing well. In traditional salary structures, all teachers are paid the same regardless of their performance. This can be unfair for teachers who are performing well and achieving positive results. Pay-for-performance policies provide a way to reward those teachers who are achieving the best results, creating a more merit-based system that recognizes and rewards excellence.\nIn conclusion, pay-for-performance policies for teachers can provide a powerful incentive for teachers to focus on improving students'' academic outcomes. By motivating teachers to work harder and rewarding those who are achieving the best results, pay-for-performance policies can create a more effective and engaged teaching workforce.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3afb305c-b3f2-5d2f-b851-4a458b7b5a1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3afb305c-b3f2-5d2f-b851-4a458b7b5a1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'An Artist''s Life', E'The {{1}} decades of an artist'' s life do not generally make the biographer'' s heart beat faster, but Claude Monet is one of a handful of painters who bucks the pattern of an {{2}} old age. While it'' s true that by the time he was 73 he had {{3}} all the usual dragging baggage – outhouses full of fancy cars, a taste for expensive wine and a sprawl of dependents – it was also now that he produced career-defining work.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.closing, 2.irrelevant, 3.accumulated', NULL, NULL),
  ('3afd7f47-a15d-5873-8085-f72a349a57c4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3afd7f47-a15d-5873-8085-f72a349a57c4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Less Water', E'California grape growers in coastal areas can use less water during times of drought and cut irrigation levels without affecting crop yields or quality, according to a new study out of the University of California, Davis. Researchers focused on crop evapotranspiration, which was the amount of water lost to the atmosphere from the vineyard system based on canopy size. The weekly tests used irrigation to replace 25%, 50% and 100% of what had been lost by the crop to evapotranspiration. And they found that vineyards can use 50% of the irrigation water normally used by grape crops without compromising flavor, color and sugar content.\n\nHow much irrigation water is the most beneficial in maintaining the grape’s flavor profile and yield according to the research?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'50%', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b046835-a334-574a-a997-45241e5acb26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b046835-a334-574a-a997-45241e5acb26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1c75c6b8-c290-51cf-924d-3be40e41e528'::uuid, NULL, E'Every carmaker in Europe has been on the block, because of their dependence on diesel.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b06e16f-2775-52ba-abf3-5f5774b8885d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b06e16f-2775-52ba-abf3-5f5774b8885d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the largest asteroid in the asteroid belt?', 'a82b2b41-fbb0-52ef-9d9f-034889dc4c7d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ceres', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b07c6fb-8357-516c-ac68-f89861342d77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b07c6fb-8357-516c-ac68-f89861342d77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Benefits of Introversion', E'While thinking of extroverts, we imagine a character who is assertive, approachable, cheerful and charming. We are taught to admire these traits early on. Kids are often encouraged to interact, play and communicate with other children. It seems at times as though children are made to embrace a more outgoing lifestyle, with some people becoming pseudo-extroverts – introverts who mimic extrovert behaviour. While externally they may seem to enjoy the company of others, or being in the limelight, they can still become over-extended in intense social situations.\nSo, while the positive aspects of being an extrovert are plain to see, what are the benefits of introversion? While extroverts thrive on social interaction, introverts are more comfortable with levels of isolation. According to Dr Berit Brogaard, a professor of philosophy, extreme solitude, such as times like the recent lockdown, does not affect introverts as much as extroverts. Lack of social contact, something extroverts thrive on, can lead to depression, loneliness, and even premature death.\nBut it’s not just in an extreme situation that the pros of being an introvert shine through. These people seem to have more time for contemplation and introspection and thus can become more balanced. They also tend to be good listeners and think before they speak, meaning they could become great friends. Finally, introverts are often fantastic observers, as sitting out of the focus can give you more time to watch the behaviour of others. So, whatever your personality, either introvert or extrovert, there are clear advantages to being either, and if you meet an introvert, you might just end up with an amazing friend.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('3b0980b4-3545-5ff6-b26b-c36acbeaf40d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b0980b4-3545-5ff6-b26b-c36acbeaf40d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Analysis of prehistoric air trapped in tiny bubbles beneath the polar ice sheets and of the composition of ice surrounding those bubbles suggests a correlation between carbon dioxide levels in the Earth''s atmosphere and global temperature over the last 160,000 years. Estimates of global temperature at the time air in the bubbles was trapped rely on measuring the relative abundances of hydrogen and its heavier isotope, deuterium, in the ice surrounding the bubbles. When global temperatures are relatively low, water containing deuterium tends to condense and precipitate before reaching the poles; thus, ice deposited at the poles when the global temperature was cooler contained relatively less deuterium than ice deposited at warmer global temperatures. Estimates of global temperature based on this information, combined with analysis of the carbon dioxide content of air trapped in ice deep beneath the polar surface, suggest that during periods of postglacial warming carbon dioxide in the Earth''s atmosphere increased by approximately 40 percent.\n\nIn the passage, the author is primarily concerned with doing which of the following?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Describing a method of analysis that provides information regarding the relation between the carbon dioxide content of the Earth''s atmosphere and global temperature', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b0b573d-8d7a-54da-9ea2-fdd081e0f491'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b0b573d-8d7a-54da-9ea2-fdd081e0f491'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Next Task', E'Having tracked down research that is {{1}} to your area of interest, the next task is to actually {{2}} of that research. This section is intended to show you how to be critical of the research you {{3}} and how to check that the {{4}} is credible and represented appropriately. Unfortunately this means discussing the ways in which research findings may be misrepresented.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.relevant, 2.make sense, 3.are reviewing, 4.evidence', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b0eb415-68e6-55f8-979b-cd38df0658e9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b0eb415-68e6-55f8-979b-cd38df0658e9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Homework Assistance', E'Different types of maternal homework assistance have a different impact on the child''s way of completing school assignments in grades 2 to 4 of elementary school, according to a new study. Although all homework assistance presumably aims at helping the child, not all types of homework assistance lead to equally positive outcomes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b14ab85-53fa-58f3-8568-fe6d90e2fe03'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b14ab85-53fa-58f3-8568-fe6d90e2fe03'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Disaster', E'The definition of a disaster varies by organization. Various entities have different "pain thresholds" that define when an incident becomes a disaster. A bank, for example, will have different criteria than a poison-control hotline. With this fact in mind, any organization should begin the process of implementing "first alert" and response teams after it has completed a business impact analysis.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b1819cc-fd51-5877-a509-fe548097a216'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b1819cc-fd51-5877-a509-fe548097a216'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Group Project', E'You''re responsible for a crucial part of a group project due in a week. You''ve been waiting on important data from another group member, which they''ve just informed you will be delayed. This setback affects your ability to complete your section on time. What would you say to your group members?', 'd85b00fc-6864-5193-8b8a-1e9dc4c01583'::uuid, NULL, E'I know we''re tight on time with the presentation, but I heard you can''t finish your slides until Thursday. That''s cutting it really close for us to review and practice together. Could you maybe prioritize getting the critical parts done first, so we have something to work with earlier? Or, if there''s a part of your workload we can redistribute to help speed things up. We need a solid plan to ensure we''re all prepped and ready for a great presentation.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b1b091e-4d75-5800-84b9-0a77e6d68c8f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b1b091e-4d75-5800-84b9-0a77e6d68c8f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hurricane Evacuation', E'If you''ve been preparing to escape from a hurricane since a hurricane watch was issued, you should be ready to leave as soon as you get evacuation orders. The longer you wait, the bigger your chances of getting stuck in a massive traffic jam. Try to consolidate everything as much as possible when you''re packing. There is no need to pack up everything you own: just take the necessities.\nIf you have time, disconnect some major appliances (so there''s less risk of electrical shock when power is restored) and turn off the gas, electricity and water before you leave. Make sure you have all important papers and documents with you as well as all medications you take or might need.\nYou''re going to hit more congestion the farther you drive, so try to pick the closest possible evacuation destination. The best-case scenario would probably be a friend or relative who lives in your area but doesn''t have to evacuate. Oftentimes all you need to do is evacuate far enough so you can escape storm surge.\nIf you don''t have to evacuate, or if for some reason you can''t, you might decide to hunker down and ride out the hurricane at home. First and foremost, remember that most people who get hurt during a hurricane are injured by flying glass and debris, so don''t go outside, even if it seems like the storm is over. You might actually be in the eye of the storm, and you could be stranded outside when the winds kick up again.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('3b1b80f7-feff-5c2a-b406-322a8c95b558'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b1b80f7-feff-5c2a-b406-322a8c95b558'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '052f141a-7ad3-5f75-8dd6-3e0e1ed0ec69'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The tuition fees are charged each year and are payable at enrollment.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b1caa69-26f1-576b-a424-4cacdb7faf63'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b1caa69-26f1-576b-a424-4cacdb7faf63'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '119e9226-f053-5307-b72d-362a2adf0f86'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The art course has been cancelled due to the new policy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b1e232d-bf23-5631-9345-e1064277b00f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b1e232d-bf23-5631-9345-e1064277b00f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where do marine animals live?', '4739057d-dd39-50d6-8b0b-29c700a8c8f1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sea / ocean', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b2584a0-6523-5cdd-9132-c76e7fff33d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2584a0-6523-5cdd-9132-c76e7fff33d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lost Antiquities', E'Over a period of five years, James H. Clark, the internet pioneer whose Netscape browser once commanded that market, spent roughly $35 million to purchase dozens of Cambodian and Southeast Asian antiquities. After investigators convinced him these collections were all stolen and that he had been duped by a shady antiquities dealer, Mr. Clark said, “My doing might inspire other people to do the same, but I’m not sure — it’s hard for people to give up something they paid for, but for me, why would you want to own something that was stolen?”\n\nWe can infer from this passage that __', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Mr. Clark will give these antiquities to the police.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b27d931-978d-5f1c-a497-27190bdc37bd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b27d931-978d-5f1c-a497-27190bdc37bd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wage Cap', E'Many people say there should be a maximum wage for high-paying jobs as some people are paid too much. Do you support that?Can you give your point of view or your own experience?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether there should be a maximum wage for high-paying jobs has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that a wage ceiling for high-paying jobs is necessary for social harmony, whereas opponents contend that a top wage promotes competitive equity. From my perspective, I am convinced that there ought to be a maximum wage for high-paying jobs.\nTo begin with, setting a maximum wage can improve social stability by reducing the wealth gap, balancing resource distribution, and easing class conflicts. For example, limiting extremely high incomes can reduce the polarization between the rich and poor, avoiding dissatisfaction among lower-class groups. In addition to this, a maximum wage allocates part of high earnings to employees'' welfare, helping distribute pay more fairly. Other than that, when economic disparities are reduced, social unrest such as protests and clashes will decrease significantly. It is thus shown that there should be a peak wage limit applied to high-income jobs.\nBesides, I also believe that setting a maximum wage can encourage fair competition by promoting equal opportunities. On top of that, a maximum wage makes sure that earnings match abilities, preventing excessive pay from exceeding an individual''s actual contributions. Moreover, when pay gaps are properly regulated, career advancement relies more on staff''s skill accumulation rather than their privileged backgrounds. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that capping executives'' excessive salaries avoids resentment among average employees, keeping the trust needed for teamwork. This clearly proves that an upper wage limit is necessary for high-earning positions.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that public stability and opportunity parity are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that well-paid jobs should be subject to a maximum wage.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3b2bac0a-b9c6-5c68-a8c9-1a1233dc3a1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2bac0a-b9c6-5c68-a8c9-1a1233dc3a1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yellowstone Species', E'In addition to its unique geography and geology, Yellowstone is also home to many different species of plants and animals. For example, there are more than one thousand species of trees and plants native to the Yellowstone area. It is also home to many different species of fauna, many of which are considered megafaunas such as grizzly bears and bison.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b2c29e4-340e-57d3-9166-bfab6316c187'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2c29e4-340e-57d3-9166-bfab6316c187'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7be0bbf6-36a6-5fe8-a4da-d01a4a3bf778'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We are required to focus on our specific area of research.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b2ce946-334d-5610-be36-818ca393820c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2ce946-334d-5610-be36-818ca393820c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hernia', E'A hernia is a weakness or opening in the abdominal wall, which often results in soft tissue such as fat protruding through the abdominal muscles and occupying space under the skin. The mechanism of the hernia is similar to what happens with a bulge in a damaged tire, where the inner tube, normally contained by the hard rubber of the tire, extends through a thin or weakened place.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b2d5dc5-c5de-55e5-9cab-f86f35cf82db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2d5dc5-c5de-55e5-9cab-f86f35cf82db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '77f06a7d-4eae-5f44-b774-8ac5a051dc1b'::uuid, NULL, E'A public library can strengthen our communities by connecting people.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b2e1dbe-440e-59b9-9cb2-6be9c068da36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b2e1dbe-440e-59b9-9cb2-6be9c068da36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c52abe78-5f47-5513-9b8e-be623bd937d3'::uuid, NULL, E'As more students enroll, universities should also employ additional staff.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b3a46f6-3b07-592e-998a-09c436cde0a2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b3a46f6-3b07-592e-998a-09c436cde0a2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-L', E'A: Today we have Paul Witner, Head of Theatre Studies here to tell us a bit about the Theatre Studies program. Paul. what makes this course different?\nB: Well I think it''s the environment we can offer students. We''re a relatively small conservatoire and we offer superb courses in a number of subjects, with an opportunity for performance. We''ve built a reputation for producing both traditional and alternative performances. I guess the course would appeal to potential students for the level of support that''s available. and I mean from the tutors as well as from the fellow students and alumni. There''s a real sense of community.\nA: So, what are you looking for in prospective students!\nB: I guess we''re looking for people who are able to cope with the high demands that the course will put on them. In that way, I think the program reflects the workplace we''re preparing them for. so it''s incredibly intense and we cover a huge range of projects, and they will be introduced to areas of performance design which they might never have considered before. We need students with imagination and dedication, who are able to keep up when the going gets tough. It can be demanding but we have to remember that the college enjoys an excellent reputation for student retention, student satisfaction and student employment after graduation.\n\nWhat comments are made about students in the Theatre Studies program?', '2f1ac5a9-1661-53be-a233-26b6f252da49'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Past students offer them help.\nA high percentage complete the degree and get jobs in their field.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b400ddf-6369-557f-a772-ae3773a73a67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b400ddf-6369-557f-a772-ae3773a73a67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Home Fencing', E'The benefits of home fencing are not only as a barrier between the area of the house and the surrounding environment. In simple words, a fence is a formation or structure that is above the ground and is generally vertical, with the intention of limiting an area or areas, protecting everything inside the fence, from threatening danger from outside the fence.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b408d15-36e3-5f71-a27a-84e1b435a4d6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b408d15-36e3-5f71-a27a-84e1b435a4d6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Citizenship Education', E'Civics and citizenship education builds student''s knowledge and understanding of the ways in which citizens can actively {{1}} in Australia'' s diverse and inclusive society. Students learn about the civic institutions and the {{2}} through which decisions are made for the common good of the {{3}} and they also develop the {{4}} and understandings that relate to the organization of a harmonious democratic society.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.participate, 2.processes, 3.community, 4.skills', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b44da4a-eee3-5bf0-b977-c91d0b136102'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b44da4a-eee3-5bf0-b977-c91d0b136102'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Charlie Watts', E'Charlie Watts, the London-born Rolling Stones drummer who {{1}} the band''s sound for nearly 60 years, died at the age of 80. Watts is {{2}} as one of the greatest and most {{3}} rock drummers of all time. He was a member of the Rolling Stones since January 1963, when he joined Mick Jagger, Keith Richards, and Brian Jones in their {{4}} group. Watts helped them become one of the bands who took rock''n''roll to the spawning point in the 1960s with classics like Satisfaction or Sympathy of the Devil.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.propelled, 2.regarded, 3.stylish, 4.fledgling', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b4777d6-6594-5faf-a778-a45ed65d5e6f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b4777d6-6594-5faf-a778-a45ed65d5e6f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4dcdfe95-35d9-5ebf-8984-83d671833cc3'::uuid, NULL, E'The team have already begun their preparations for the first match of the season.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b4c3391-d6e7-5c57-9d8f-66d1c59fbf58'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b4c3391-d6e7-5c57-9d8f-66d1c59fbf58'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Carbon Dioxide Emission', E'When countries assess their annual carbon dioxide emissions, they count up their cars and power stations, but bush fires are not included presumably because they are deemed to be events beyond human control. In Australia, Victoria alone sees several hundred thousand hectares burn each year; in both 2004 and the present summer, the figure has been over 1 million hectares.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b4cd9f6-a129-5168-8519-0b8101469482'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b4cd9f6-a129-5168-8519-0b8101469482'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do you call the seasonal flying from cold to warmer areas, mitigation or migration?', '407ec09b-e9b2-5620-865c-dc4b5a25b924'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Migration', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b56ff78-17d7-5ea7-978e-778cb63ed7a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b56ff78-17d7-5ea7-978e-778cb63ed7a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vaccines', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 4, 1, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b58d482-e2f6-58df-aedc-919093953609'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b58d482-e2f6-58df-aedc-919093953609'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for a fast, rough drawing made to capture the basic elements and structure of a scene?', 'b7d81a80-f303-526b-bb2b-7f89b944fe5d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sketch', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b5b7f1c-8d8c-541c-b159-2ae4eb320393'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b5b7f1c-8d8c-541c-b159-2ae4eb320393'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Scientists', E'Social scientists use particular methods to gather qualitative evidence, from observation to interview, but they also use autobiographical accounts, journalism, and other documentary material to flesh out and add meaning to statistics. As with reading numbers, reading textual evidence requires us to practice, to set time aside to learn how to do it, and to understand the conventions of writing which operate in the different forms of writing we encounter. One of the main problems with reading textual evidence, though, is that, unlike the relationship most of us have with numbers where we may use them at a pretty basic level, most of us are, if anything, over-familiar with words. When we want to understand their value as social science evidence we need to forget how familiar we are with first person accounts and everyday speech - for example, in newspapers, magazines, and books - and learn a different approach to them.\nSocial scientists use observation, interviews and even print journalism as evidence for the claims they make. They may collect evidence through questionnaires with pre-set questions and by open-ended interviews which allow respondents to speak for themselves. They may observe social relations explicitly as social scientists or may participate themselves in a particular community to gain ''inside'' information.\nSocial scientists also draw on print journalism on occasion and may use the same sources, for example official statistics, and the work of other social scientists to support their claims. We need to remember, though, that journalists do not need to present the same rigorous referencing and support for their claims as social scientists are required to do. Most importantly, newspaper and magazine articles are written under commercial pressures; for example they must help to sell the newspaper by being deliberately provocative, or by reflecting the dominant views of its readers.\n\nAccording to this passage, what do social scientists use written sources to do?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Adding information to other data they have collected.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b61873b-0792-528b-a847-fedd323ce175'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b61873b-0792-528b-a847-fedd323ce175'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Feedback', E'Giving feedback is hard. It can be uncomfortable. And on some level, you worry that you could hurt the other person''s feelings because that''s sometimes what happens when you give feedback. But I want to say that getting good feedback can feel like an act of generosity, and I''ve experienced it firsthand. I had a boss who put so much thought and care into the way that she talked to me about my work, I felt like she was really invested, and I always felt better after talking to her and getting feedback. So really, constructive, actionable feedback is a gift. And in this episode, we''re going to teach you how to give it. But don''t worry; we have another episode coming about how to receive feedback, too, because, you know, we''re completists like that. What can I say? And while we''re mostly focusing on giving feedback in a workplace setting, by all means, please take this wisdom from Massella into your whole life. You won''t regret it.\n\nWhy does the woman mention her boss?', '5ee804e2-a08f-57a9-b25b-89c9305143e5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To prove that good feedback from others can be beneficial.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b62c439-a573-56d6-b435-5c68d84fe8cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b62c439-a573-56d6-b435-5c68d84fe8cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marshmallow', E'They call it the "marshmallow test". A four- to six-year-old-child sits alone in a room at a table facing a marshmallow on a plate. The child is told: "if you don''t eat this treat for 15 minutes you can have both it and a second one." Kids on average wait for five or six minutes before eating the marshmallow. The longer a child can resist the treat has been correlated with higher general competency later in life.\nNow a study shows that the ability to resist temptation isn''t strictly innate: it''s also highly influenced by environment.\nResearchers gave five-year-olds used crayons and one sticker to decorate a sheet of paper. One group was promised a new set of art supplies for the project—but then never received it. But the other group did receive new crayons and better stickers.\nThen both groups were given the marshmallow test. The children who had been lied to waited for a mean time of three minutes before eating the marshmallow. The group that got their promised materials resisted an average of 12 minutes.\nThus, the researchers note that experience factors into a child''s ability to delay gratification. When previous promises have been hollow, why believe the next one.', NULL, NULL, E'In the marshmallow test, the longer a child can resist the treat has been correlated with higher general competency later in life, but the ability to resist temptation isn’t strictly innate: it''s also highly influenced by environment, when experience factors into a child’s ability to delay gratification.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('3b634f49-eec7-5d1a-a73e-6f2d57a85ae0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b634f49-eec7-5d1a-a73e-6f2d57a85ae0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Culturomics', E'They call it culturomics: the obvious play on the word "genomics" looks at trends in human thought and culture. But scientists say culturomics has been hampered by a lack of quantitative data. So researchers at Harvard, along with Google, Encyclopedia Britannica, and the {{3}} Heritage Dictionary, have come up with a new tool.\nIt''s a database of 5.2 million books, published since the year 1500. That''s four percent of all the books ever published, with a total of 500 billion words. The focus is on English language culture, so three quarters of the books are in English.\nAmong the first findings of the research, published in the journal Science : about, 8500 new words enter the English language annually. But many of them don''t end up in {{4}} . And about fame — actors become famous around age 30, writers around 40, and politicians around 50. But the fame of politicians can {{5}} exceed that of actors.\nA Google tool called the Books Ngram Viewer is {{6}} based on this data — users can track the usage and {{7}} of a word or phrase over the past few centuries. Thus, we can watch the fall and rise of Melville. And soon the rise and fall of Snooki.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.American, 2.dictionaries, 3.eventually, 4.available, 5.frequency', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b643f10-242c-5c7b-8261-3f05f3434697'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b643f10-242c-5c7b-8261-3f05f3434697'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Illness', E'He spent a {{1}} night, struggling with his health. It was {{2}} for him to continue with his duties as usual. Despite his determination and eagerness to teach, he was not permitted to {{3}} class due to his health condition. He was {{4}} to attend and fulfill his responsibilities, but his illness prevented him from doing so.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.painful, 2.difficult, 3.attend, 4.happy', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b6682fa-536c-50f6-af9d-376f3f88359d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b6682fa-536c-50f6-af9d-376f3f88359d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Two Types of Genes', E'Recently, research into embryonic development has given us an even better insight into how major structural changes might occur in a given population of organisms. We now understand that there are two major types of genes: developmental and ''housekeeping'' genes. Developmental genes are those that are expressed during embryonic development, and their proteins {{1}} the symmetry, skeletal development, organ placement, and overall form of the developing animal. {{2}} , ''housekeeping'' genes are expressed during the animal''s daily life to generate proteins which keep the cells, tissues, and organs in the body functioning properly. {{3}} you might suspect, mutations in developmental genes can have radical consequences for body form and function, whereas mutations in ''housekeeping'' genes tend to {{4}} the health and reproductive success of the post-embryonic animal.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.control, 2.In contrast, 3.As, 4.affect', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b67b265-0429-55de-a2e6-a9a543a1352a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b67b265-0429-55de-a2e6-a9a543a1352a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '990d25c5-6a54-56cb-b186-72def7a494c7'::uuid, NULL, E'A study skills seminar is available for students who need assistance.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b6b4f6d-b410-5e92-a28c-7fc7ac0ed563'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b6b4f6d-b410-5e92-a28c-7fc7ac0ed563'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Climate and Precipitation', E'Warmer temperatures affect the hydrological cycle. The hydrological cycle, also known as the water cycle, is a process that helps with the constant circulation of water between the earth and its atmosphere. In the cycle, evaporation, transpiration, precipitation, condensation and runoff take place. These increase and decrease water availability.\nEvaporation occurs when warm temperatures heat the water on Earth, turning them into vapors that rise into the atmosphere. The same process happens in plants, but it is known as transpiration. Warm temperatures cause plants to lose water as vapor.\nVapor from the Earth’s surface rises to the atmosphere, where temperatures are cooler. Cooler temperatures cause condensation, turning the water vapor into liquid water. This then falls back to Earth as precipitation in many forms, including rain, snow and hail. Depending on the intensity of the precipitation, runoff may occur. Severe runoff from rain can cause serious floods.\nThe water cycle is heavily dependent on temperature. Climate change, which causes warmer temperatures, intensifies the water cycle. Warmer temperatures cause dry areas to lose water faster, creating more extreme drought events, while wet regions experience excessive rainfall. We are now facing an increasing risk of frequent, extreme precipitation and floods.\nThe U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) reports that intense precipitation will cause an increase in the frequency of extreme precipitation events. Additionally, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) reports that rainfall will reduce in dry areas and frequency will increase in storm-affected areas.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('3b6fcc38-5a6d-51d8-b7fb-bf3eda5649de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b6fcc38-5a6d-51d8-b7fb-bf3eda5649de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the generic term for a person who once had the same title as you have now?', '37e416ef-1e70-5b5a-9839-0370faafc4c6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Predecessor', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b71ba76-ed4b-57c6-9296-d3dbc3375dd1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b71ba76-ed4b-57c6-9296-d3dbc3375dd1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Female Employment', E'The female employment rate has {{1}} mainly in online businesses. The {{2}} of research has also increased mainly in small occupational {{3}} . There is growing {{4}} in the roles women play in a range of research studies that focus on small firms specifically.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.increased, 2.volume, 3.sectors, 4.interest', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b729ce7-e654-5122-98ef-bf4cedf4cd98'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b729ce7-e654-5122-98ef-bf4cedf4cd98'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ICU', E'Having a loved one in the hospital, especially the Intensive Care Unit, or ICU, can be a {{1}} experience. And it''s even more traumatic for the families of those who pass away. Or so you''d think.\nBut according to a study published in the November issue of the journal Chest, families whose loved ones die in the ICU tend to be more satisfied with the {{2}} they received than those whose loved ones survive.\nAlthough the results seem paradoxical, when you look more closely at how people define "quality of care," they do make sense. All patients who {{3}} up in the ICU, whether or not they walk out, receive a similar standard of care from a {{4}} medical point of view. But doctors, nurses, and other hospital staff may devote extra time and attention to the needs of families whose loved ones are near the end.\nThat compassion is what families who lose a loved one are responding to when they report a more satisfactory ICU experience. Just having someone who''ll explain what''s going on, answer their questions and offer {{5}} support makes all the difference. An observation that, in the end, is maybe not so surprising.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.harrowing, 2.care, 3.wind, 4.strictly, 5.emotional', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b787353-5df8-5377-8f2b-31f836129fb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b787353-5df8-5377-8f2b-31f836129fb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In mathematics and arithmetic, there are addition, multiplication, division. What''s the other one?', 'e7010221-c476-5e36-b46c-ac96e8c85e1f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Subtraction', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b7bf04f-f28b-572c-90bf-567989093798'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b7bf04f-f28b-572c-90bf-567989093798'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Virtual Reality', E'To what extent do you think virtual reality will change entertainment in the future?', NULL, NULL, E'I firmly believe that virtual reality (VR) is poised to revolutionize the entertainment landscape in the future. This innovative technology holds the potential to fundamentally change the way we consume media, introducing exciting new dimensions that will enhance and redefine our entertainment experiences.\nVirtual reality is set to revolutionize the entertainment industry by offering users a more immersive and realistic experience. Through the use of VR technology, users can step into virtual worlds that engage their senses and emotions, creating a deeply immersive experience that traditional forms of entertainment cannot match. This heightened level of immersion allows users to feel like active participants in the content they are consuming, enhancing their overall enjoyment and creating lasting memories.\nFurthermore, virtual reality''s capacity for interactive storytelling and engagement will redefine how entertainment is experienced. By enabling users to interact with the content and make choices that impact the narrative, VR opens up new possibilities for personalized and engaging storytelling. This interactive element not only enhances user engagement but also encourages creativity and exploration in entertainment, leading to dynamic and captivating experiences that cater to individual preferences and interests.\nIn conclusion, the impact of virtual reality on the future of entertainment cannot be overstated. Its ability to provide immersive experiences, interactive storytelling, and a plethora of entertainment options will undoubtedly change how we view and engage with the media. As technology advances, we can expect VR to become an integral part of our daily entertainment, shaping our experiences in ways we have yet to imagine.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3b7e791e-577f-5887-be6a-d6c8bd38efd5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b7e791e-577f-5887-be6a-d6c8bd38efd5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4cd58cea-d5ef-5b32-89c9-7e008c796491'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Today''s history class has been relocated to another lecture hall.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b822d42-7d33-5de2-8a48-a8199c2d1228'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b822d42-7d33-5de2-8a48-a8199c2d1228'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b25a2bcc-9aa4-5731-a6b4-85ff32a37a53'::uuid, NULL, E'Tuesday is the final day for students to submit their assignments without any penalty.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b8ab21c-134e-542a-8940-bf65d75d87c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b8ab21c-134e-542a-8940-bf65d75d87c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'Our oceans are really very well traveled on the surface, but in terms of the deep sea, uh, IT''s probably the one area of our planet that hasn''t been explored. The first visit by a human to the ocean floor was in nineteen sixty when the u s navy sent a vehicle to the mariana trench, the deepest part of the ocean. Anyway, what exactly do we know about the deep sea? Well, we define it as two hundred meters below the surface of the ocean. And around that point sunlight begins to disappear and temperatures begin to drop a thousand meters and beyond. There''s complete darkness, very little oxygen, and pressures that are a thousand times greater than at the earth''s surface. However, somehow it''s full of life life that has a huge effect on our own lives, because half of the oxygen we breathe is generated by living things in the ocean. So in the future, scientists are going to try and find out more about oh,\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '47f2fbba-1a31-54ac-8251-9ad0c0e38101'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'the creatures that exist there', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b915a8d-8074-5a74-a7f9-c65ebb62640d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b915a8d-8074-5a74-a7f9-c65ebb62640d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '19433d70-e912-50ad-bf9a-004aab10044f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The output should be proportional to the input.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b924b5a-6823-5e08-9576-782adab554b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b924b5a-6823-5e08-9576-782adab554b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b178da11-71f9-5e2a-92d0-684fde52101e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We will assess qualifications using a method based on conference criteria.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b96e60f-5487-512e-aac3-0f489e1a8ffc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b96e60f-5487-512e-aac3-0f489e1a8ffc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Night Sky', NULL, '1f96abef-b295-5632-b90b-692683a884c7'::uuid, NULL, E'As we gaze into the night sky, the cosmos whispers tales of ancient light and distant worlds. Astronomy, the study of celestial phenomena, reveals the grandeur of the universe and our unique position within it. This exploration begins with our solar system, a tiny enclave in the vast galactic expanse, where planets orbit a lone star we call the Sun. Further afield, we find that galaxies, those colossal collections of stars, gas, and dust, are not merely scattered randomly but are bound in a cosmic ballet, driven by the forces of gravity. This grand dance of the galaxies reminds us of the dynamic nature of the universe, one that is ever-expanding and full of wonders beyond our wildest imagination. In this pursuit of cosmic knowledge, we are reminded that despite the vastness of space, human curiosity knows no bounds. As we stand on the brink of new astronomical discoveries, let us carry the torch of inquiry forward, ever eager to uncover the secrets of the stars.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3b9769b7-9e5a-5a87-b742-68c32605ca57'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b9769b7-9e5a-5a87-b742-68c32605ca57'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indian Onion', E'The most {{1}} ingredient in Indian cooking, the {{2}} element with which all dishes begin and, normally, the cheapest vegetable available, the pink onion is an essential item in the shopping basket of families of all classes. A popular saying holds that you will never starve because you can always afford a roti (a piece of simple, flat bread) and an onion.\nBut in recent weeks, the onion has started to seem an unaffordable {{3}} for India''s poor. Over the past few days, another sharp {{4}} in prices has begun to unsettle the influential urban middle classes. The sudden spike in prices has been caused by large exports to neighboring countries and a shortage of {{6}} .With its capacity for bringing down governments and scarring political careers, the onion plays an explosive role in Indian politics. This week reports of rising onion prices have made front-page news and absorbed the attention of the governing elite.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.vital, 2.basic, 3.luxury, 4.surge, 5.supply', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b97d372-46bb-5000-9df9-482c26ab6abe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b97d372-46bb-5000-9df9-482c26ab6abe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b6b1e357-0ec3-531f-b193-5bce959c7fa7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mental health professionals are talking about the topic of vulnerability.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b9a4ce8-f21c-5748-a443-7ab0706bd5bf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b9a4ce8-f21c-5748-a443-7ab0706bd5bf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Direct Quotes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 5, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('3b9c6941-9ea5-5306-bf28-ea51215a7408'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3b9c6941-9ea5-5306-bf28-ea51215a7408'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Istanbul', E'Straddling Asia and Europe across the strait, the old city of Istanbul, Turkey, has embraced diverse cultural influences. Known for its monumental architecture, Istanbul has become a cherished travel destination.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3ba23481-7732-55ed-8a2b-96cf602c1d72'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ba23481-7732-55ed-8a2b-96cf602c1d72'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Andalucia', E'Here is a part of Spain''s sun-baked Andalucia that is extraordinary not only because of its unspoiled terrain and authentic Spanish traditions but also because of its caves. These are not dark, damp holes, with dripping water and evil smells. They are residences, ancient Bronze Age dwellings now being refurbished for hundreds of 21st century Spaniards. In Galera, the region''s most important village, it''s estimated that there are at least 1,000 such habitations carved into its hillsides. We take old caves renovate them, then sell them on, says Rob Oakley, office manager of leading developer Galera enterprises. Our company was set up by someone who discovered the area of Galera when it was just a tourist attraction 15 years ago and saw its potential. The ancient abodes are transformed from rough caves into relatively luxurious homes, equipped out with amenities like electricity and sewage, phone lines, running hot water, even internet connections.\n\nWhich of the following words in the passages have the same meaning as ''residences'' has?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Abodes\nDwellings\nHabitations', NULL, NULL),
  ('3ba26c71-9ba2-5c04-81dd-34458cf41aff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ba26c71-9ba2-5c04-81dd-34458cf41aff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2fce2260-7160-54e7-9143-e3ddb58534d0'::uuid, NULL, E'Our professor will host a business development conference next week.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3baa5ff5-db0e-51c5-8f01-8449c5c2fae0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3baa5ff5-db0e-51c5-8f01-8449c5c2fae0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8b166184-a4c1-516e-8f83-23bdef47d15e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students were instructed to stand in a straight line outside of the classroom.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bab84e5-c7f2-5ceb-a86b-2bafe3be3568'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bab84e5-c7f2-5ceb-a86b-2bafe3be3568'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Flags', E'In the Middle Ages, the design and use of flags were considered a means of identifying social status. Flags were, therefore, the symbols not of nations, but of the nobility. The design of each flag resembled the "devices" on the noble''s Coat of Arms, and the size of the flags was an indication of how high the owner stood in the nobility.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3baf99b0-aaba-5f89-bb0e-9c1a479dc6d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3baf99b0-aaba-5f89-bb0e-9c1a479dc6d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fostered Child', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'5, 3, 1, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bb3e594-67f9-558a-8596-08f1c9a7e894'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bb3e594-67f9-558a-8596-08f1c9a7e894'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modern Technology', E'Modern technology has enhanced the study of language by making its sounds observable in greater detail and with greater accuracy than ever before, but the thoughts associated with those sounds remain problematic. Currently developing {{1}} of brain imaging are allowing us to observe for the first time which parts of the brain are active in different circumstances. They do not, however, show experiences themselves, which may always remain {{2}} from public observation. There is a sense in which each of us knows what we are thinking, {{3}} we may not always have a good way of verbalizing it. But the only way we can know what someone else is thinking is through what that person says, or through some other overt action, a {{4}} expression or gesture, perhaps from which that person''s thoughts may be inferred, or from imagining what we ourselves would be thinking {{5}} similar circumstances.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.technologies, 2.hidden, 3.although, 4.facial, 5.in', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bb44aa3-521d-50bc-b8f9-c443f22480be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bb44aa3-521d-50bc-b8f9-c443f22480be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ford Company', E'The Ford Company provides plenty of opportunities for its employees. It guarantees not only comfortable and appropriate working conditions, but also many other advantages. Therefore, becoming a part of the Ford Motor company is always profitable and beneficial. Moreover, it is important to mention that Ford Motors provides its employees with effective and useful services and takes care of their well-being.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3bb656d4-0b19-59c0-aa20-f7c698727c05'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bb656d4-0b19-59c0-aa20-f7c698727c05'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2dcbe2ad-080f-5011-9b1a-439b4b3b7d6a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They developed a unique approach to training their employees.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bc12732-9114-56bc-95c8-6eba25f0894d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bc12732-9114-56bc-95c8-6eba25f0894d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'COVID-19', E'Currently in South Australia, the majority of people who have a positive COVID-nineteen test result will stay in the community in their home or in supervised or supported care. A team of health professionals will carry out an assessment and ask you a series of questions, including identifying your symptoms, your medical history and if you can safely isolate away from others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3bc237ae-54d2-5679-b066-91f03be2d3f2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bc237ae-54d2-5679-b066-91f03be2d3f2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What’s the antonym of large?', '575db74e-8677-50c6-8d75-3da2b54c243c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Small', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bc5171a-7771-5e26-915f-5f287c36113a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bc5171a-7771-5e26-915f-5f287c36113a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '835dd6a9-85c3-5c1a-aa00-25d616dbb285'::uuid, NULL, E'Doctor Green''s new office location is on the building''s second floor.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3bc70a2c-c153-58d5-9519-b2ff85806044'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bc70a2c-c153-58d5-9519-b2ff85806044'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the part of each day after sunset called?', 'e41bf139-d496-56d5-ab59-cef46d865a8d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Evening', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bcef451-dff9-54a2-ac7c-255c87a4805c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bcef451-dff9-54a2-ac7c-255c87a4805c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Laptop', E'UMN''s ALCs features large {{1}} tables that seat nine students and can accommodate laptop computers for {{2}} work. Typically, students bring their own computers to class and use the building''s ubiquitous wireless capability. The classrooms are designed to {{3}} hands-on activities and problems that require students to interact with each other to reach a solution. Students can display their work on large LCD screens mounted around the room to promote small- and large-group discussions. Each table is allotted three gooseneck microphones so that students can make themselves heard without shouting during group discussions. Additionally, students can press a button on their table console to light a {{4}} lamp to indicate when they need help or wish to speak. To facilitate brainstorming and group reporting, the room is also lined with erasable marker-boards.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.circular, 2.collaborative, 3.facilitate, 4.signal', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bd04be5-893b-5d6f-bd49-4bb46384f8cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bd04be5-893b-5d6f-bd49-4bb46384f8cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Internet', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 2, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bd8112b-b14e-5ad1-a792-3e8f3d452dbd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bd8112b-b14e-5ad1-a792-3e8f3d452dbd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3d48ccc1-61d2-57c0-9688-baba845365e9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The jury consisted of judges selected from all men and women.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bdd6754-f4b8-51af-ae66-e091433c9286'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bdd6754-f4b8-51af-ae66-e091433c9286'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for a push or pull that can change the motion of an object?', '6d62a213-89be-55b5-b3fb-13637189749d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Force', NULL, NULL),
  ('3bdea44a-6dab-5901-ba10-40a5eefdbc11'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3bdea44a-6dab-5901-ba10-40a5eefdbc11'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'de359a5d-e484-5296-9c5e-5ed13b7b2bd0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We managed to reach out to several subjects for research.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3be3d303-c442-58bc-ae72-aa3d195333b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3be3d303-c442-58bc-ae72-aa3d195333b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fuller', E'At the Paris Exposition in 1900, Fuller had her own theater, where, in addition to her own dances, she presented pantomimes by the Japanese actress Sada Yocco. She assembled an all-female company at this time and established a school around 1908, but neither survived her. Although she is remembered today chiefly for her innovations in stage lighting, her activities also touched Isadora Duncan and Ruth St. Denis, two other United States dancers who were experimenting with new types of dance. She sponsored Duncan''s first appearance in Europe. Her theater at the Paris Exposition was visited by St. Denis, who found new ideas about stagecraft in Fuller''s work and fresh sources for her art in Sada Yocco''s plays. In 1924 St. Denis paid tribute to Fuller with the duet Valse àla Loie.\n\nAccording to the paragraph, what was true of Fuller''s theater at the Paris Exposition?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'It presented some works that were not by Fuller.\nThe passage does not tell whether It ceased to operate as a theater after Fuller died.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3be52941-0da0-5d83-9f34-e9e5b2f38aa3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3be52941-0da0-5d83-9f34-e9e5b2f38aa3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Elephant', E'The elephant is the largest living land mammal. During evolution, its skeleton has greatly altered from the usual mammal, designed for two main reasons. One is to cope with the great weight of huge grinding cheek teeth and elongated tusk, making the skull particularly massive. The other is to support the enormous bulk of such a huge body.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
