  ('3c0c9a32-ce6b-5d96-9d33-c0b3639b420b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c0c9a32-ce6b-5d96-9d33-c0b3639b420b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bone Conduction Headphones', E'Bone conduction headphones, which rely on sound being {{1}} through vibrations on the user''s skull, are gaining popularity. For starters, there''s been an evolution of headphone-related technologies like noise cancellation technology. And unlike with phones and smart-watches, many people have {{2}} pairs of headphones that they want tailored specifically for different settings and scenarios. Bone conduction headphones, in particular, are "having a moment." {{3}} sitting inside or on top of the ear canal, bone conduction headphones rest in front of the ear, leaving it uncovered. They transmit audio along the user''s bones and jaw to the ears instead of directly into the ear canal. The exposed ear allows users to {{4}} up on sounds and the environment around them, crucial for safety when doing activities such as riding a bike or jogging.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.transmitted, 2.multiple, 3.Rather than, 4.pick', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c0f34ab-c9b0-5603-9793-3e3739b2050c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c0f34ab-c9b0-5603-9793-3e3739b2050c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Archaic Names', E'An archaic name is an older name for a chemical that predates the modern naming conventions. It''s helpful to know archaic names of chemicals because older texts may refer to chemicals by these names. Some chemicals are sold under archaic names or may be found in storage labeled with the older names.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3c162bef-a92c-5859-9224-62f0cc05bf1e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c162bef-a92c-5859-9224-62f0cc05bf1e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b28d6a04-9f78-5473-b235-e8ff3f441a48'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Remember, the gifts purchased by children should feature a striped pattern.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c1a4c9c-ad0b-5847-8f38-6d34bb0d797f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c1a4c9c-ad0b-5847-8f38-6d34bb0d797f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '966795a2-ef52-53e2-8691-df5e69a98b4c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The government is working on the shortage of affordable housing.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c1f05e6-8109-56f1-9ec7-6366efe6eed5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c1f05e6-8109-56f1-9ec7-6366efe6eed5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Giant Pandas', E'The panda, with its {{1}} black and white coat, is adored by the world and {{2}} a national treasure in China. Pandas live mainly in temperate forests high in the mountains of southwest China, where they {{3}} almost entirely on bamboo. They must eat around 26 to 84 pounds of it every day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distinctive, 2.considered, 3.subsist', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c21d0bc-1666-5006-873c-dd9f9b0934fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c21d0bc-1666-5006-873c-dd9f9b0934fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the long, orange thing that grows underground?', 'fc651f09-2101-5bed-8ba6-02da186bca84'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Carrot', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c27461c-cefd-5249-9f3b-db57c872cc89'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c27461c-cefd-5249-9f3b-db57c872cc89'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cook', E'Cook carriages make good housing for the homeless. That''s the idea behind the pop up house project, a project to turn rows of disused garages in london into temporary accommodation for homeless people. It would allow a small home to be created with a bedroom and shower room. And then every fifth carriage in the line would be used to shared laundry, kitchen and eating facilities. The homes would be put together by the people who will live in them in the future with the idea of teaching them building skills as well as giving them a home. IT''s hoped that because they will have their own space, their own front door, they''ll be more likely to get back into society more quickly than by putting them into shared accommodation. We know people don''t do well in that environment and it will give them the education they need to get back into work.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'ba63f58c-667c-5f7a-b0a3-220c14f58811'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A new project intends to use garages to provide housing for the homeless in London. Although small, there will be areas outside the home to prepare food and clean clothes. The houses will provide both accommodation and training for the people living there.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c28cd59-4e32-5728-9057-a640a6022028'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c28cd59-4e32-5728-9057-a640a6022028'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Disaster Preparedness Program', E'A comprehensive disaster preparedness program is being launched to enhance community resilience and response capabilities. The program includes initiatives to educate communities about potential hazards, develop emergency response plans, and improve communication systems for timely warnings and alerts during emergencies. The initiative also focuses on developing disaster-resistant infrastructure and promoting sustainable land use practices to reduce the impact of disasters on communities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3c2b24ac-bf9a-58cb-bc4a-6aea9b2ba4ad'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c2b24ac-bf9a-58cb-bc4a-6aea9b2ba4ad'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the part that extends beyond the end of a dog''s body?', '8b7bd146-53a9-5899-94e6-e26042ebca40'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tail', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c3e0d9a-3f4e-59f3-8d30-e48ddb330896'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c3e0d9a-3f4e-59f3-8d30-e48ddb330896'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aromatic Substance', E'Researchers have found a way to convert the aromatic substance vanillin into a redox-active electrolyte material for liquid batteries. The technology is an important step towards ecologically sustainable energy storage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3c4411d3-70bb-5327-a668-6ab03734f656'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c4411d3-70bb-5327-a668-6ab03734f656'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Speech of Alchemy', E'To learn the speech of alchemy, an early form of chemistry in which people attempted to turn metals into gold, it helps to think back to a time when there was no science: no atomic number or weight, no periodic chart, no list of elements. To the alchemists the {{1}} was not made of leptons, bosons, gluons, and quarks. Instead it was made of substances, and one substance-say, walnut oil-could be just as {{2}} as another—say, silver—even though modern {{3}} would say one is heterogeneous and the other homogeneous. Without knowledge of atomic structures, how would it be {{4}} to tell elements from compounds?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.universe, 2.pure, 3.scientists, 4.possible', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c441ee5-e1ab-57ec-a598-524d7c25d39a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c441ee5-e1ab-57ec-a598-524d7c25d39a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Geologists Harris and Gass hypothesized that the Red Sea rift developed along the line of a suture (a splice in the Earth''s crust) formed during the late Proterozoic era, and that significant observable differences in the composition of the upper layers of rocks deposited on either side of the suture give clues to the different natures of the underlying igneous rocks. Other geologists argued that neither the upper rock layer nor the underlying igneous rocks on the one side of the rift differ fundamentally from the corresponding layers on the other side. These geologists believe, therefore, that there is inadequate evidence to conclude that a suture underlies the rift. In response, Harris and Gass asserted that the upper rock layers on the two sides of the rift had not been shown to be of similar age, structure, or geochemical content. Furthermore, they cited new evidence that the underlying igneous rocks on either side of the rift contain significantly different kinds of rare metals.\n\nPart of the Harris and Gass hypothesis about the Red Sea rift would be weakened if it could be demonstrated that the composition of upper rock layers', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'cannot provide information about the nature of underlying rocks', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c46c9ac-e101-5c80-b9e0-a21af0beffbc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c46c9ac-e101-5c80-b9e0-a21af0beffbc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e0882b72-1fd6-5b10-b1ea-729c28396da1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Potential customers can see what employees say online.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3c4ed7b0-8fce-5301-9f3f-885211f51fa0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c4ed7b0-8fce-5301-9f3f-885211f51fa0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Home Education', E'In some countries, more parents prefer to educate their children themselves at home instead of sending them to school. What are the advantages or disadvantages of it?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('3c55b34d-9040-5145-aaab-2e9d5bc5ab04'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c55b34d-9040-5145-aaab-2e9d5bc5ab04'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'School Environment', E'The school environment plays a critical role in shaping young minds and preparing them for the challenges of the future. It should provide a safe and supportive space for learning, with qualified teachers, relevant curriculum, and opportunities for extracurricular activities such as sports and clubs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3c57fde3-fb78-5efe-b57b-19acfa358997'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3c57fde3-fb78-5efe-b57b-19acfa358997'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parenting', E'Parents teach us fundamental life {{1}} like walking and speaking, making them our first and arguably best teachers. They spend a {{2}} amount of time with us, understanding our strengths and {{3}} and helping us improve. They pass on valuable experiences and habits, shaping our behavior and character. Parents, with their unconditional love, educate us in {{4}} life aspects beyond academic knowledge.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.skills, 2.significant, 3.weaknesses, 4.numerous', NULL, NULL),
