  ('3dc7aa9b-94a6-5274-bc31-361a4dc1502f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dc7aa9b-94a6-5274-bc31-361a4dc1502f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language', E'Language comes so naturally to us that it is easy to forget what a strange and miraculous gift it is. All over the world members of our {{1}} fashion their breath into hisses and hums and squeaks and pops and listen to others do the {{2}} . We do this, of course, not only because we like the sounds but because details of the sounds contain information about the {{3}} of the person making them. We, humans, are fitted with a means of {{4}} our ideas, in all their unfathomable vastness. When we listen to speech, we can be led to think thoughts that have never been thought before and that never would have {{5}} to us on our own.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.species, 2.same, 3.intentions, 4.sharing, 5.occurred', NULL, NULL),
  ('3dc97480-37e4-54c4-bc18-fd1114ca3408'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dc97480-37e4-54c4-bc18-fd1114ca3408'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Housing', E'Housing is a key component of individual and family. In addition to being a place where family and friends can gather, housing is important for a sense of security and {{1}} . One {{2}} aspect of security is the wealth in the homes of owner occupiers.\nThe wealth of households {{3}} as the wealth (or equity) in the homes of owner occupiers increases through paying off {{4}} housing loans, or as property values rise. In 2003-04, the primary residence was, on average, the most valuable asset of owner-occupier households, with the net value of owned homes {{5}} an average of 55% of the net worth of those households.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.privacy, 2.significant, 3.increases, 4.outstanding, 5.accounting for', NULL, NULL),
  ('3dcd113b-f43c-5c42-ad14-4ba99deb0489'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dcd113b-f43c-5c42-ad14-4ba99deb0489'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c5b0004d-5878-5999-a069-dfb42aaa0760'::uuid, NULL, E'The investigation aims to find the stand on the problem.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3dcf4928-b90d-5dac-a80a-e7e5eba513e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dcf4928-b90d-5dac-a80a-e7e5eba513e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Chemistry', E'Okay, today''s our first class. So I''d like to begin with some important definitions. We''re going to use these terms all semester. So pay close attention to begin with. Chemistry is basically this study of matter. Matter is everything that makes up the universe. In this class, we''re going to study the various elements and how they interact with one another. Sometimes they unite. When two or more elements unite, we call them compounds. Now, uh, the study of chemical compounds is divided into two main branches of chemistry, organic chemistry and inorganic chemistry. Organic chemistry is the study of compounds that contain the element carbon. This basically covers well, uh, it covers all living things. Carbon is an element all living organisms have in common. As for inorganic chemistry, it''s the study of non carbon based compounds. There are five differences between organic and inorganic compounds. Listen carefully to these. First, there are more than ten million carbon compounds. That''s ten times the number of inorganic compounds. Why are there so many carbon compounds? Hm. Mostly because carbon bonds easily with other elements. It can also form complex cruise. Got it? Ok. Second, ah, organic compounds melt and boil at lower temperatures than in organic compounds. Third, organic compounds don''t dissolve in water as easily as an organic compounds. Fourth, organic compounds catch fire more easily than in organic compounds. However, in organic compounds conduct heat and electricity more easily. Finally, organic compound reactions take place, and slower rates then do inorganic compound reactions.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'c7e91978-3e77-565a-85f3-89d1ea8ed523'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A compound is made when two or more elements unite and there are two main branches of chemical compounds: organic and inorganic compounds. There are five differences between organic and inorganic compounds.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3dd2d496-85c4-5503-bf35-db0864aba87d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dd2d496-85c4-5503-bf35-db0864aba87d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '674f03c2-a5f0-529e-8070-808587cbe89a'::uuid, NULL, E'More and more people begin to be concerned about our natural environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3dd55d1a-9e36-5a22-9710-6552309c2bb7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dd55d1a-9e36-5a22-9710-6552309c2bb7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we describe a person''s emotion changing frequently?', 'c05f0638-f46a-5442-aeec-02821d9b5f73'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Fickleness / moody', NULL, NULL),
  ('3dd7b911-419e-5fcb-9af9-578df13a4d25'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3dd7b911-419e-5fcb-9af9-578df13a4d25'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Answering Questions', E'You have about 30 minutes to answer each question. You must take account of how many marks are {{1}} for each part when you answer it. Even if you think you can write more, don''t spend 15 minutes {{2}} a part worth only 5 marks. Leave space at the end of your answer and come back to it if you have {{3}} to spare later. And if you can''t think of an answer to some part, leave a space and move on to the next part. Don''t write about something else if you don''t know the correct answer — this is just a waste of your {{4}} time (and the examiner''s).', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.available, 2.answering, 3.time, 4.valuable', NULL, NULL),
  ('3ddd4f4c-971c-56e4-a9fa-a719a060dc74'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3ddd4f4c-971c-56e4-a9fa-a719a060dc74'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a small horse?', 'f01321e1-cc2b-5691-bb01-79b5f6b29dd0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pony', NULL, NULL),
