  ('3f414248-197b-5a64-8396-a2a0df327aa3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f414248-197b-5a64-8396-a2a0df327aa3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Emotional Intelligence', NULL, '3d953cee-23f0-54de-8793-9dca44acd2d2'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, I wish to highlight the crucial role of emotional intelligence (EI) in achieving personal and professional success. In an era where technical skills are highly valued, the importance of EI often goes unrecognized, yet it''s equally vital. Emotional intelligence involves understanding and managing our own emotions and empathetically interacting with others. It''s not just about self-awareness but also about recognizing the emotional states of those around us. For example, effective team collaboration in a workplace setting is greatly enhanced by high EI, fostering better communication and conflict resolution. Additionally, EI is pivotal for mental well-being. It aids in navigating the stresses of student life, from academic pressures to personal relationships. By understanding and regulating our emotions, we can maintain a healthier mental state, leading to improved focus and productivity. While technical skills are important, the development of emotional intelligence is equally critical for holistic success. It''s a skill that enriches both our professional and personal lives.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
