  ('3f8918fb-72eb-575c-aff0-dd927f899ba6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f8918fb-72eb-575c-aff0-dd927f899ba6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ccc13600-9c81-5dad-8102-b6e02d20c6f2'::uuid, NULL, E'The renewable energy alternatives were the main aspect of debate during the meeting.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3f8a8616-29e0-585e-905a-6b9924927034'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f8a8616-29e0-585e-905a-6b9924927034'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bird Legs', E'One of the reasons why bird legs seem so thin is that their body is largely hidden by feathers, which can make them look much bigger than they really are. Birds have more muscular thighs that are {{1}} by their feathers, and most birds have scaly skin on their lower legs, which makes these parts look very small and bare. Birds that have feathers {{2}} to their toes — such as owls and some breeds of chickens — seem to have thicker calves than their featherless-legged relatives. But it’s not only a matter of perception: bird legs have some real differences from legs of other living animals. Birds are the descendants of theropod dinosaurs, a group of animals that walked on two legs and varied in size. {{3}} most mammals that can walk on two legs — such as bears, chimpanzees and humans—who stand on their heels, dinosaurs walked on their toes and the front part of the foot, with the rest of their foot bones stretched and lifted off the {{4}} . Living birds inherited some of these features. However, as birds became more adapted to flying, they also developed some distinct {{5}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.covered, 2.all the way, 3.Unlike, 4.ground, 5.traits', NULL, NULL),
  ('3f8dbc0f-e8bb-5e92-b6d6-6c6ca089097f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f8dbc0f-e8bb-5e92-b6d6-6c6ca089097f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ponzi Scheme', E'Ponzi is an illegal business {{1}} . His original scheme was based on the legitimate arbitrage of international reply coupons for {{2}} stamps, but he soon began diverting new investors'' money to make {{3}} to earlier investors as {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.practice, 2.postage, 3.payments, 4.interest', NULL, NULL),
  ('3f926aa7-663d-511e-894d-03e7ade350de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f926aa7-663d-511e-894d-03e7ade350de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fd189f8b-c427-5c8a-9d7d-83a861b68cda'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This guide book offers information on local customs policies.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3f933f22-4e4b-502b-a8b4-322d2cb1e7b8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f933f22-4e4b-502b-a8b4-322d2cb1e7b8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9912bf7f-94f2-50f3-a298-1e1c1eb8fc43'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The materials from today''s lecture will appear on the upcoming exam.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3f96bfd7-2a3c-5168-ab81-5aa1efb08bc0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f96bfd7-2a3c-5168-ab81-5aa1efb08bc0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Environmental Damage', E'Environmental damage does not affect all people equally. For this reason, some people may feel anxiety around ecological issues more intensely. Some parts of the world are more vulnerable to the effects of extreme weather, including coastal communities and low-lying areas. Particularly, people whose livelihoods depend on the environment — such as those with jobs in fishing, tourism, and agriculture — are more likely to be affected.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3f98b8dd-f78d-50d8-96fd-82835af2cd41'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f98b8dd-f78d-50d8-96fd-82835af2cd41'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Welfare', E'Welfare has a special political meaning to the United States because it refers to how the poor receives financial aid. In comparison, Welfare services are regarded as a universal right in other regions like Europe, where it is believed that all citizens should be able to obtain a minimal level of social support and well-being.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3f9ef9e2-1a8c-5a1c-a108-b3efdb0910be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f9ef9e2-1a8c-5a1c-a108-b3efdb0910be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'When to Revise?', E'Timing is important for revision. Have you noticed that during the school day you get times when you just don''t care any longer? I don''t mean the lessons you don''t like, but the ones you usually find OK, but on some occasions, you just can''t be bothered with it. You {{1}} have other things on your mind, be tired, restless or looking forward to what comes next. Whatever the reason, that particular lesson doesn''t get 100 percent {{2}} from you. The same is true of revision. Your mental and physical {{3}} is important. If you try to revise when you are tired or totally occupied with something else, your revision will be inefficient and just about worthless. If you approach it feeling fresh, alert and happy, it will be so much easier, and you will learn more, faster.\nHowever, if you make no plans and just slip in a little bit of revision when you feel like it, you probably won''t do much revision!\nYou need a revision timetable, so you don''t keep {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.may, 2.effort, 3.attitude, 4.putting it off', NULL, NULL),
  ('3f9f7324-a680-55d7-b2f2-206853014882'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3f9f7324-a680-55d7-b2f2-206853014882'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the money an employer pay an employee because of the damage caused at work?', '472b3c3e-1872-58dd-946e-ed53b6f427a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Compensation', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fa62de4-eb88-519a-b647-531b0856a6bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fa62de4-eb88-519a-b647-531b0856a6bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Local Market', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 3, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fa745f7-f290-514a-9e12-46934451c5ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fa745f7-f290-514a-9e12-46934451c5ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Promise and Peril', E'Urbanization brings both promise and peril as populations concentrate. Cities foster innovation, cultural exchange, economic opportunity and improved {{1}} to resources. However, over time overcrowding strains infrastructure and the environment. If not {{2}} managed, cities struggle with pollution, waste disposal, public health issues, high costs of living and traffic congestion that diminish residents’ {{3}} of life. An urbanising world must plan habitable, eco-friendly cities and more equitable distribution of resources. Strong social bonds and governance help ensure cities remain livable, creative hubs as they continue to draw rural populations. With conscious development, cities can uplift and support growing populations. But without proper management, urban problems will {{4}} and cities may become unlivable, as the challenges associated with higher population densities rise exponentially.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.access, 2.sustainably, 3.quality, 4.intensify', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fa98ce5-d842-51f9-a065-7ccf258c5fc5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fa98ce5-d842-51f9-a065-7ccf258c5fc5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If a couple have a pair of children, how many children do they have?', '2229d90c-58b4-5e0b-9574-6d5e8997aeb9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Two', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fabf9d2-29cd-5bf2-9ae9-1b2e324e33fd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fabf9d2-29cd-5bf2-9ae9-1b2e324e33fd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What does the prefix retro- mean in words like retrospect?', 'f587d2ac-2631-5311-8aa1-a8b0d436878c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Back / backwards', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fac2080-24d4-52b3-bb83-4492a7037fb5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fac2080-24d4-52b3-bb83-4492a7037fb5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Examination of Domicile', E'At an early stage in the examination of the domicile of dependency rule in so far as it related to married women it seemed to the Commission that it would be better to examine the whole concept of domicile, particularly as dependent domicile arises in the case of minors (children under the age of majority) and mentally disordered persons as well as in the case of married women.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3faceca3-bb33-5b94-bfc7-c591709f087f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3faceca3-bb33-5b94-bfc7-c591709f087f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '03064218-1fcb-5c68-83e2-60063feac705'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The government is funding a new research on the consequences of unemployment.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fb031c0-92ec-5427-ac1c-23aa8621eaf3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fb031c0-92ec-5427-ac1c-23aa8621eaf3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Divorce', E'Researchers have found that divorce has different kinds of negative impacts on the planet, including higher demand for resources and a lower rate of efficiency in the use of household resources. People have been talking about how to protect the environment and combat climate change, but divorce is an overlooked factor that needs to be considered.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3fb4e9a6-d931-5522-94be-b51d3c86c339'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fb4e9a6-d931-5522-94be-b51d3c86c339'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd53a2553-1444-505b-8f4a-8e1d782af481'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You must register online or by post before attending the lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fb63056-9484-504f-88ae-078e2e066ff0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fb63056-9484-504f-88ae-078e2e066ff0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Building Meaningful Relationships', E'Building meaningful relationships is fundamental to human happiness and well-being. Whether it''s with family, friends, or romantic partners, healthy relationships provide support, love, and a sense of belonging. Nurturing relationships requires open communication, trust, and empathy. Investing time and effort into building strong connections enriches our lives and provides a support system during challenging times.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3fb9bbd9-b135-5698-94fa-ecc34507ac3d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fb9bbd9-b135-5698-94fa-ecc34507ac3d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '17201bfc-f1fd-56a7-9889-67438e5f8456'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Scientists recognize different ice types according to the water molecule content.', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fc3826b-2dc8-5551-b712-f0e5b189e3d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fc3826b-2dc8-5551-b712-f0e5b189e3d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ebfb6d0c-1d4c-5813-94b1-e71955d6e3f5'::uuid, NULL, E'The doctor has been accused of violating professional ethics.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('3fc53fd6-79d2-52c5-a219-4151c1574b5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fc53fd6-79d2-52c5-a219-4151c1574b5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call stop, comma or ellipsis?', 'cb2bc204-4309-5984-8194-d5cb800ebb1d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Punctuation', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fc7809a-08f8-5174-9078-fd6a33303b1a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fc7809a-08f8-5174-9078-fd6a33303b1a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bank', E'One very important institution in our economy is the bank. Banks manage money for individual people, corporations and the government banks provide a number of important services for you and your family. Most importantly, there a safe place to store your money. They also provide an easy way for you to transfer money from one place to another. When you write a personal check, the check authorizes the bank to give your money to the person or business whose name is on the check. Of course, banks also lend money. Ordinary people take out bank loans for a number of reasons, to pay for college, to buy or remodel a home, to start or expand a business, and so forth. Banks provide these services to individuals. However, their main function is to lend large sums of money, for example, to corporations. When people or corporations borrow money from a bank, they must, of course, pay interest a percentage of the money they borrowed. Banks pay interest on the money they hold and charge interest on the money they lend. For a bank to make a profit, it has to collect more interest than it pays out. Sometimes banks invest money as well as lend it. To invest money means to put it into a corporation or some other project, for example, building a housing complex or doing medical research in exchange for a share of the profits. Most businesses need loans and investments at some time, and banks are an important source of both. You might wonder what would happen if all the people with money in a bank wanted to take their money out at the same time. I mean, how would the bank be able to give everyone their money if it had lent out or invested most of it? In fact, this can be a serious problem for banks. They count on the fact that most people won''t want their money for a long time. Once it''s deposited, that leaves the bank free to lend or invest the money. If every person, or even lots of people tried to withdraw their money at the same time, the bank might not be able to honor all of its deposits. This causes some banks to fail or go bankrupt. Bank failures used to be common during times of recession or depression. They were especially common during the great depression of the nineteen thirties. When franklin roosevelt became president in nineteen thirty three, one of the first things he did was closed all the banks, so depositors wouldn''t panic and try to take all their money out. Number.\n\nFor what reasons do individuals take out bank loans?', '3f89d87c-fbef-5921-b6dc-bdb2d47dad6f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To pay for education\nTo purchase a home', NULL, NULL),
  ('3fcbd51c-2c51-51ab-8f0c-f3fc3e1d82e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '3fcbd51c-2c51-51ab-8f0c-f3fc3e1d82e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3987fcf5-a1b6-555b-8559-bb26a69a31a9'::uuid, NULL, E'During the next few centuries, London became one of the most powerful and prosperous cities in Europe.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
