  ('41048cc6-423b-5080-a7f8-09b8f0db18fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '41048cc6-423b-5080-a7f8-09b8f0db18fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pop Art', E'Emerging in the mid 1950s in Britain and late 1950s in America, pop art reached its peak in the 1960s. It began as a revolt {{1}} the dominant approaches to art and culture and traditional views on what art {{2}} . Young artists felt that what they were taught at art school and what they saw in museums did not have anything {{3}} their lives or the things they saw around them every day. Instead they {{4}} sources such as Hollywood movies, advertising, product packaging, pop music and comic books for their imagery.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.against, 2.should be, 3.to do with, 4.turned to', NULL, NULL),
