  ('49875d27-0f3f-5172-b1c1-190061dadf21'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '49875d27-0f3f-5172-b1c1-190061dadf21'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Donors', E'Americans approached a record level of generosity last year. Of the $260.28bn given to charity in 2005, 76.5% of it came from individual {{1}} . These people gave across the range of non-profit bodies, from museums to religious {{2}} , with a heavy {{3}} on disaster relief after the Asian tsunami and US hurricanes. In total, Americans gave away 2.2% of their household income in 2005, slightly above 40-year {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.donors, 2.organizations, 3.emphasis, 4.average', NULL, NULL),
