  ('4a707b26-d057-5e60-a59a-fc33a12faad6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a707b26-d057-5e60-a59a-fc33a12faad6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electric Vehicle', E'Do you agree that electric vehicles will completely replace fuel-powered cars?', NULL, NULL, E'Embracing the inevitable evolution of transportation, I firmly believe that electric vehicles will ultimately replace fuel-powered cars as governments worldwide implement policies to drive their adoption. This shift towards electric vehicles is not just a trend but a strategic move towards a sustainable and environmentally friendly future.\nElectric vehicles stand as champions of environmental progress, offering a tangible solution to reduce emissions and enhance sustainability. By eliminating harmful tailpipe emissions and reducing dependence on finite fossil fuels, electric vehicles play a pivotal role in combating climate change and improving air quality. The environmental benefits they bring align seamlessly with the sustainability goals championed by governments globally.\nThe accessibility and affordability of electric vehicles have seen a remarkable upsurge due to technological advancements and robust government support. Governments are actively implementing policies such as tax incentives, rebates, and infrastructure development to bolster the adoption of electric vehicles. These strategic interventions not only make electric vehicles more appealing to consumers but also underscore a commitment to fostering sustainable transportation solutions.\nIn conclusion, the convergence of environmental consciousness, technological advancements, and government support is propelling electric vehicles to the forefront of the automotive industry. With policies in place to encourage adoption and drive popularity, electric vehicles are well-positioned to replace fuel-powered cars and lead the transition toward a cleaner, greener future of transportation.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('4a72293d-7404-5ed4-90a7-ce7c9760e954'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a72293d-7404-5ed4-90a7-ce7c9760e954'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '178b8e50-e4d3-51ff-add8-8bb801dbeb16'::uuid, NULL, E'Starting a business or selling things abroad begins by talking to a bank.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4a725e06-b8e8-52ee-b224-51829af362df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a725e06-b8e8-52ee-b224-51829af362df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '913c26e7-4566-5063-9a37-7529620f5a88'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Candidates should remain seated until finishing their exams.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4a73253d-aa59-526d-b31b-780634ff9cf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a73253d-aa59-526d-b31b-780634ff9cf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wolf', E'Over time a split would have appeared in wolf populations, he says: those wolves that feared humans, and those that didn’t. "So this would have facilitated, I think, the domestication process." At which point humans deliberately took wolves as pets. But that domestication process, Frantz says, may have happened more than once: first in the west, in Europe. And again in the far east, in Asia.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4a754c43-a06d-573c-8db9-c718bcc72219'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a754c43-a06d-573c-8db9-c718bcc72219'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ikebana', E'More than simply putting flowers in a {{1}} , Ikebana is a {{2}} art form in which nature and humanity are brought together. Contrary to the idea of a particolored or multicolored {{3}} of blossoms, Ikebana often emphasizes other areas of the {{4}} , such as its stems and leaves, and puts emphasis on shape, line, and form. Though Ikebana is an expression of creativity, certain rules govern its form. The artist''s intention is shown through a piece''s color combinations, natural shapes, graceful lines, and the implied meaning of the arrangement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.container, 2.disciplined, 3.arrangement, 4.plant', NULL, NULL),
  ('4a7b82a8-d168-57e3-8e53-a20d1762f2fb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a7b82a8-d168-57e3-8e53-a20d1762f2fb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '69d672ef-dd10-51ae-818d-0504cdd9598f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Take the first step by applying for your university scholarship now.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4a810deb-aa5b-598b-bb28-b75564fcedbe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a810deb-aa5b-598b-bb28-b75564fcedbe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '466727ce-ca7f-5ef3-b29a-20abc6489fac'::uuid, NULL, E'The causality theory states that for every effect, there is a cause.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4a8231cc-1645-5686-9a30-67eb8f9a741c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a8231cc-1645-5686-9a30-67eb8f9a741c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Campus Life', E'Campus life is a unique experience that offers students the opportunity to learn, grow, and connect with others in a supportive and intellectually stimulating environment. From attending classes and participating in extracurricular activities to socializing with friends and exploring new interests, college provides a wealth of opportunities for personal and academic development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4a84b358-9a6c-50da-8c19-493691d8cb3f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a84b358-9a6c-50da-8c19-493691d8cb3f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Psychology', E'Psychology changed dramatically during the early 20th-century as another school of thought known as behaviorism rose to {{1}} . Behaviorism was a major change from previous theoretical perspectives, rejecting the emphasis on both the conscious and unconscious mind. Instead, behaviorism {{2}} to make psychology a more scientific discipline by focusing purely on observable behavior. Behaviorism had its earliest start with the work of a Russian physiologist named Ivan Pavlov. Pavlov demonstrated that this learning process could be used to make an {{3}} between an environmental stimulus and a naturally occurring stimulus. An American psychologist named John B. Watson soon became one of the strongest advocates of behaviorism. Initially {{4}} the basic principles of this new school of thought in his 1913 paper Psychology as the Behaviorist Views It, Watson later went on to offer a definition in his classic book "Behaviorism" (1924), writing: "Behaviorism that holds the subject matter of human psychology is the behavior of the human being".', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dominance, 2.strove, 3.association, 4.outlining', NULL, NULL),
  ('4a86c3df-e37d-5e7e-ab8e-31c13ee6ce7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a86c3df-e37d-5e7e-ab8e-31c13ee6ce7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '974a0280-e965-5345-82dc-afcee9a07f00'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Group assignments should be submitted promptly by a team member.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4a8ec710-6c68-5d4d-a88d-aaa40530b554'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a8ec710-6c68-5d4d-a88d-aaa40530b554'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dreams', NULL, 'bdeacd89-4007-50f3-a597-4ec409162962'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, let''s delve into the enigmatic world of dreams, a fascinating subject that bridges psychology, neuroscience, and even philosophy. Dreams have always been a source of mystery, inspiring countless theories and interpretations. Dreams are not just random images; they are a complex interplay of our subconscious mind. Modern research suggests that dreaming can be a way our brain processes emotions and experiences, integrating them into our memory and learning. For instance, some theories propose that dreams help us solve problems or cope with stress. Additionally, the study of dreams offers insights into various sleep disorders and mental health conditions. By understanding what happens in our brain during different stages of sleep and dreaming, we can better address issues like insomnia, sleepwalking, and nightmares. In conclusion, dreams are more than just nightly escapades of our imagination. They offer a window into our subconscious, providing valuable insights into our mental and emotional well-being.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4a924d75-64e2-5d24-a457-17e7047a5edd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4a924d75-64e2-5d24-a457-17e7047a5edd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the long, orange vegetable known for being eaten by rabbits?', 'e9ea71d8-6de6-552a-8c97-43d002c44dbb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Carrot', NULL, NULL),
