  ('4dbc6243-920b-5ab2-acce-af5e8368ea1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4dbc6243-920b-5ab2-acce-af5e8368ea1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-R', E'The differences in feeding preferences lead, in turn, to differences in migratory habits. The wildebeests follow, in their migration, the pattern of local rainfall. The other species do likewise. But when a new area is fueled by rain, the mammals migrate toward it in a set order to exploit it. The larger, less fastidious feeders, the zebras, move in first; the choosier, smaller wildebeests come later; and the smallest species of all, Thomson''s gazelle, arrives last. The later species all depend on the preparations of the earlier one, for the actions of the zebra alter the vegetation to suit the stomachs of the wildebeest, topi, and gazelle.\n\nAccording to the passage, which of the following is true of wildebeests?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'They tend to choose feeding areas in which the vegetation has been worn down.\nThey are relatively choosier than larger herbivores.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4dc1197e-9c5a-55e5-bdd2-aad283100f78'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4dc1197e-9c5a-55e5-bdd2-aad283100f78'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Peter Garrett', E'No one in Parliament would know better than Peter Garrett what largesse copyright can confer so it may seem right that he should announce a {{1}} for artists, amounting to 5 percent of all sales after the original one, which can go on giving to their families for as much as 150 years. But that ignores the truth that copyright law is a {{2}} , recently {{3}} by the Free Trade Agreement with the US which required extension of copyright to 70 years after death. Is it scandalous that really valuable copyrights end up in the ownership of corporations (although Agatha Christie''s no-doubt worthy great-grandchildren are still {{4}} the benefits of West End success for her whodunnits and members of the Garrick Club enjoy the continuing fruits of A.A. Milne''s Christopher Robin books)? No. The {{5}} is that bien pensants politicians have attempted to appear cultured by creating private assets which depend on an act of Parliament for their existence and by giving away much more in value than any public benefit could {{6}} . In doing so they have betrayed our trust.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.royalty, 2.scandal, 3.exacerbated, 4.reaping, 5.scandal, 6.justify', NULL, NULL),
  ('4dc1c18f-8725-5450-b951-0cc8d5c696be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4dc1c18f-8725-5450-b951-0cc8d5c696be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which organ does the word “cardiac” relate to?', '51911741-3831-546c-bba3-1a8bfab941b0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Heart', NULL, NULL),
  ('4dc2e995-7b7f-56d3-9c58-309dc4b15c83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4dc2e995-7b7f-56d3-9c58-309dc4b15c83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Australia', E'Australia is a dynamic multi-cultural society, viewed by many as the world''s most desirable place to live. Here Frank Welsh traces Australia''s intriguing and varied history to {{3}} how this society {{1}} , from its ancient Aborigine tribes and earliest British convict {{5}} to today''s modern nation - one that {{4}} strong links with its colonial past but is {{2}} independent and diverse.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.examine, 2.emerged, 3.settlements, 4.retains, 5.increasingly', NULL, NULL),
  ('4dc97c62-85aa-5bbb-911e-d6267d5089b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4dc97c62-85aa-5bbb-911e-d6267d5089b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bilingual Education', E'What is your opinion on the necessity of bilingual education in a globalized world?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s globalized world, the necessity of bilingual education cannot be overstated. Bilingualism is not merely a skill but a tool that enhances communication, opens up global career opportunities, and fosters cultural understanding and empathy. As the world becomes increasingly interconnected, the ability to speak multiple languages is a valuable asset that transcends borders and bridges diverse cultures.\nBilingual education plays a crucial role in facilitating effective communication and collaboration across diverse cultures. Proficiency in multiple languages enables individuals to engage in meaningful dialogues, break down language barriers, and build connections with people from different backgrounds. By mastering more than one language, individuals can navigate cross-cultural interactions with ease, fostering mutual understanding and cooperation in a global context.\nBeing bilingual opens up a wider range of career opportunities in a globalized job market. In an increasingly interconnected world where businesses operate on a global scale, multilingual individuals have a competitive edge. Bilingual professionals can access international job markets, work with diverse teams, and navigate multicultural environments with confidence. The ability to communicate effectively in multiple languages enhances employability and enables individuals to thrive in a globalized workforce.\nIn conclusion, the necessity of bilingual education in a globalized world is evident in its role in enhancing communication, creating global career opportunities, and promoting cultural understanding. Bilingualism is a valuable asset that empowers individuals to connect across borders, seize international prospects, and embrace diversity with empathy and respect. As we navigate an increasingly interconnected world, bilingual education stands as a cornerstone for building bridges between cultures, fostering collaboration, and shaping a more inclusive and harmonious global society.', NULL, 200, 300),
