  ('4e65e0aa-f166-5118-a895-2cf7957febf6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e65e0aa-f166-5118-a895-2cf7957febf6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0256d2d9-40ac-52a4-9629-4a3d15aef1e7'::uuid, NULL, E'What I have now is confidence and optimism.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e68bb8f-7b6d-5d3b-8e79-ee32fecf60f5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e68bb8f-7b6d-5d3b-8e79-ee32fecf60f5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which one is a psychologist good at, surgery or therapy?', 'c6642187-5045-5172-857e-e9fbda50f2b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Therapy', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e6caa16-949c-57c8-a2d9-9d32a291054f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e6caa16-949c-57c8-a2d9-9d32a291054f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Speed of Sight', E'The human capacity to perceive rapid alterations in visual scenes, colloquially referred to as “speed of sight”, exhibits a remarkable degree of variation among individuals, as revealed by the inaugural systematic {{1}} into this phenomenon. This variability in visual acuity may elucidate the differential aptitude observed in individuals when engaging in sports that require {{2}} of fast-moving objects, such as baseball and cricket. The study posits that certain individuals {{3}} an innate superior vision that enables them to follow fast-moving objects with greater precision than others. This {{4}} visual prowess could potentially account for the disparities observed in individuals’ performance in ball sports. The research, led by Clinton Haarlem at Trinity College Dublin, underscores the critical role of visual perception in our interaction with {{5}} changing environments and its potential implications in the realm of sports.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.investigation, 2.tracking, 3.possess, 4.inherent, 5.rapidly', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e7063ae-cfd4-5945-9629-caaf88b23118'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e7063ae-cfd4-5945-9629-caaf88b23118'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '304c498f-22f6-587e-8eca-8969b4923538'::uuid, NULL, E'Please make sure you have filled in all your details before submitting.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e71cfec-7d12-5d3b-a810-dc269781d911'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e71cfec-7d12-5d3b-a810-dc269781d911'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '612eb658-c804-5a94-922b-6b3ac66e6ff4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The committee is meeting to find out a solution to this problem.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e735670-ad65-50ce-8b3e-1b7913d12731'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e735670-ad65-50ce-8b3e-1b7913d12731'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '825ae961-541c-5e39-a908-4301dfce25ac'::uuid, NULL, E'Animal behavior appears to contain both similar and distinct aspects to that of humans.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e775127-e012-56de-a451-59a37fefff23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e775127-e012-56de-a451-59a37fefff23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wealthy Nations', E'Wealthy nations are required to share their wealth among poorer countries. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s world, there is a growing debate about whether wealthy nations should share their wealth among poorer countries. In my opinion, wealthy nations have a moral obligation to share their wealth among poorer countries.\nOne of the most compelling reasons for wealthy nations to share their wealth among poorer countries is to reduce global poverty and inequality. The gap between the rich and poor has widened in recent years, and many people in poorer countries are struggling to meet their basic needs. By sharing their wealth, wealthy nations can help alleviate poverty and improve the standard of living for people in poorer countries. This can also help reduce the economic and social disparities that exist between nations.\nAnother reason why wealthy nations should share their wealth among poorer countries is to promote international cooperation and diplomatic relations. Sharing wealth can help build trust and goodwill between nations, which can lead to increased cooperation on a range of issues, including trade, security, and environmental protection. It can also help create a more stable and peaceful world by reducing the economic and social pressures that can lead to conflict.\nIn conclusion, I believe that wealthy nations have a moral obligation to share their wealth among poorer countries. Sharing wealth can help reduce global poverty and inequality, promote international cooperation and diplomatic relations, and create a more stable and peaceful world. By working together to address these issues, we can build a more just and equitable world for all people.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('4e7b8257-598e-5cc6-8d38-1fa11db7a64e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e7b8257-598e-5cc6-8d38-1fa11db7a64e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Medical Innovation', E'A new study has shed light on how weight-loss and diabetes injections such as Wegovy and Ozempic may have wider medical benefits than we first thought. The researchers found that these drugs {{1}} on the brain to lessen body-wide inflammation, which could explain why they seem to reduce heart attacks more than {{2}} expected from their weight-loss effects alone. The drugs belong to a class of medications that mimic a gut hormone called GLP-1, which normally lowers appetite, makes people feel full and {{3}} the release of insulin, a hormone involved in blood sugar regulation. Several studies have suggested that, as well as causing people to lose weight, GLP-1 mimics also lower inflammation. To investigate the {{4}} behind this anti-inflammatory effect, the researchers conducted experiments in mice. They found that GLP-1 mimics reduced the animals’ inflammatory response to a bacterial infection, but only when the mice had the receptor for GLP-1 on their brain cells. This means that the drugs reduce inflammation by influencing the brain, and not just by {{5}} weight loss.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.act, 2.would be, 3.triggers, 4.mechanism, 5.inducing', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e7bb4e2-7a64-52af-b6c9-195a0a322d04'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e7bb4e2-7a64-52af-b6c9-195a0a322d04'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e99d47e2-9c52-5839-a252-e851b561ff79'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Her work in chemistry has greatly advanced the scientific community.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e7db24c-c5b2-5c44-bbfc-503d66d2790d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e7db24c-c5b2-5c44-bbfc-503d66d2790d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electricity', E'It would be very hard to imagine life without electricity. Most of the appliances and machines that are used in homes, offices and factories are powered by electricity and this equipment {{1}} people''s overall quality of life. For that reason, the wider provision of electricity supplies is a critical factor in reducing global poverty {{2}} . To meet the needs of users around the world, the global consumption of coal has risen more quickly {{3}} 2000 than any other fuel. For countries that do not have their own supply of natural energy resources, coal has become an essential {{4}} of producing power. On a global scale, coal is currently used to fire power stations and produces 40% of global electricity. This {{5}} is very likely to increase, and predictions are that by 2030 coal will fuel 44% of world''s electricity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.helps to improve, 2.levels, 3.since, 4.means, 5.figure', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e8252eb-6d35-57a9-aad0-8115738e007a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e8252eb-6d35-57a9-aad0-8115738e007a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Diabetes', E'Increasing levels of obesity, poor diet, and increased sedentary behavior are driving a rapid rise in the number of cases of type 2 diabetes worldwide. In 2021, 537 million adults were estimated to have diabetes worldwide, with an increasing number diagnosed at younger ages.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e8d09ce-c800-54be-8247-8dacc58d0caf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e8d09ce-c800-54be-8247-8dacc58d0caf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1f776842-3d7f-5942-bfa9-e6500d56d603'::uuid, NULL, E'I''d like to start a family when I''m about thirty years old.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e95aaa8-e235-544a-9279-fd4bd15e2484'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e95aaa8-e235-544a-9279-fd4bd15e2484'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Immune Machinery', E'''When a virus invades your cells, it kicks your immune machinery into motion. The first responders are signaling proteins, called interferon. And they trigger downstream immune responses. So you can kind of think of them as the hormones of the immune system. They''re triggered and then they stimulate a bunch of other immune responses that are more specific to that pathogen.'' Michelle Baker, a comparative immunologist at the Australian Animal Health Laboratory.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4e95bca4-37fb-577b-82ab-ac5ed8c9d7c4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e95bca4-37fb-577b-82ab-ac5ed8c9d7c4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wetland Plant', E'Experts have waited a considerable amount of time for this much-needed book. Now we have a new and very thorough survey of wetland plant species. The content is extensive and totally up-to-date and as reference {{1}} , it represents extremely good value. In addition to the editors, there are 3S well-chosen contributors who have put in a tremendous amount of work to {{2}} the reader with maps and indexes, and colorful photographs. The plant descriptions are straightforward, yet scholarly, and flicking through the pages, {{3}} the writers’ passion for the subject. Each of the eight sections has an overview, {{4}} current concerns and future conservation plans. Despite a few gaps and the occasional unsatisfactory illustration, this handbook will remind botanists and specialists of the importance of protecting the country''s plant life. {{5}} person interested in the topic, whether a student or a hardened expert, will find it indispensable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.material, 2.assist, 3.you can sense, 4.highlighting, 5.Every', NULL, NULL),
  ('4e9e5f18-c4aa-5e85-a35e-3c8b183f7ce1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4e9e5f18-c4aa-5e85-a35e-3c8b183f7ce1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Walking Stamina', E'If you''ve decided you want to improve your fitness, walking is a good choice. It''s free, simple, and adaptable to your schedule. If you''ve been relatively sedentary, you might find that you can''t walk very far at first without getting sore or out-of-breath. You just have to keep at it! If you try to walk a little further every day, you''ll find that your walking stamina gradually improves. If you don''t have the patience for that, there are a few other tricks you can try to help you reach your goals faster.\n\nAccording to the passage, what might the “tricks” mentioned in the last sentence refer to?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'methods to improve your stamina quickly.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ea201d4-3223-55fe-89dd-6bcc662eccc6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ea201d4-3223-55fe-89dd-6bcc662eccc6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '21e37206-a989-5907-8b1a-0c35405efe2d'::uuid, NULL, E'Science''s solutions often surpass the challenges it may introduce into society.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4ea39f82-d5fa-5223-a4cb-89c4b2fa9b3e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ea39f82-d5fa-5223-a4cb-89c4b2fa9b3e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1045fe54-ed19-525a-aabf-fce45ae8f4b9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The school canteen sells a large variety of water and food.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ea84ac9-f0f9-59cb-8c0a-a5f69a11ab73'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ea84ac9-f0f9-59cb-8c0a-a5f69a11ab73'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'North Sentinel Island', E'For centuries, the isolated, Indigenous people of North Sentinel Island (known as the Sentinelese) have rejected all attempts by the outside world to infiltrate their tiny tropical home in the Bay of Bengal. In fact, anthropologists have no idea how many Sentinelese live on the island: estimates vary between 50 and 500. North Sentinel Island is part of a much larger island chain called the Andaman and Nicobar Islands, currently governed by India. There are 184 islands in this tropical archipelago located in the Bay of Bengal about 300 miles off the coast of Myanmar and 700 miles from India. Only about 30 of the islands in the chain are inhabited and are home to Indigenous people like the Onge and the Jarawa, who speak different languages than the Sentinelese. In the 18th century, the Andaman and Nicobar Islands were first explored by Dutch, Austrian and British merchant ships looking for the best trade routes to the spice-rich Asian subcontinent. In 1771, a ship with the British East India Company was the first to spot signs of life on North Sentinel Island, cooking fires flickering in the night. The first permanent European settlers arrived in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands in the 1850s when the British built a penal colony on Grand Andaman Island, about 30 miles (50 kilometers) from North Sentinel Island, to house colonial prisoners from British-ruled India. In 1896, a prisoner tried to escape on a raft and washed up on the beach of North Sentinel Island. A search party found him a few days later, dead from multiple arrows.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('4eb33331-bcfb-597c-8da3-b8367305eaa9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4eb33331-bcfb-597c-8da3-b8367305eaa9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Late to School', E'You are late to school today and need to explain the situation to your teacher. How would you apologize for being late and provide a reasonable explanation for your delay?', '519182eb-82bc-5aa4-910a-901d36c719a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4ebc730f-c144-59c2-9ab4-af97437371bc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ebc730f-c144-59c2-9ab4-af97437371bc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9643e237-6dc1-5869-ba1b-55be6dde945c'::uuid, NULL, E'She had a sandwich for her meal and also drank some juice.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4ec1ff4e-ad72-5627-817a-2e378225a934'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ec1ff4e-ad72-5627-817a-2e378225a934'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Discrimination', E'When we discriminate, a negative outcome usually results. However, let''s say you are an employer of a business. And the government has told you that you must hire a certain number of women, or a certain percentage of black and white people. This would restrain you from hiring, promoting, and firing your employees. Ok, let''s take a step back and discuss why in some cases, individual freedom to choose or discriminate who will work for you can be a good thing. During the past forty years, the american government has put rules in place to increase the protection of the environment and groups such as minorities, women workers, and consumers. These new rules have resulted in numerous regulations and new bodies of law, which in some cases have resulted in extreme policies, like the one I described before about an employer not being able to select an employee of his or her choice based on sex or color. As a result, opponents argue that individualism has been lost with these new laws. On the other side of the coin, some anti-discrimination proponents argued against the traditional division of occupational roles between men and women. These arguments led to major legal cases, which in turn led to strong requirements to recruit women for jobs usually held by men.\n\nAccording to the lecture: what are the main changes since the 1970s?', 'b1aac2ad-86d6-5dfb-bb8a-4cd2c1a1c855'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Most jobs became open to ethnic groups.\nFiremen began to have women collegues.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ec3e5d9-de52-5bb3-9d90-ad6cbfa1944e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ec3e5d9-de52-5bb3-9d90-ad6cbfa1944e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nobel Peace Prize', E'This year’s Nobel Peace Prize justly rewards the thousands of scientists of the United Nations Climate Change Panel (the IPCC). These scientists are engaged in excellent, painstaking work that establishes exactly what the world should expect from climate change.\nThe other award winner, former US Vice President Al Gore, has spent much more time telling us what to fear. While the IPCC''s estimates and conclusions are grounded in careful study, Gore doesn''t seem to be similarly restrained.\nGore told the world in his Academy Award winning movie (recently labelled "one sided" and containing "scientific errors" by a British judge) to expect 20-foot sea level rises over this century. He ignores the findings of his Nobel co-winners, the IPCC, who conclude that sea levels will rise between only a half foot and two feet over this century, with their best expectation being about one foot. That''s similar to what the world experienced over the past 150 years.\nLikewise, Gore agonizes over the accelerated melting of ice in Greenland and what it means for the planet, but overlooks the IPCC''s conclusion that, if sustained, the current rate of melting would add just three inches to the sea level rise by the end of the century. Gore also takes no notice of research showing that Greenland’s temperatures were higher in 1941 than they are today.\nThe politician turned movie maker loses sleep over a predicted rise in heat related deaths. There''s another side of the story that''s inconvenient to mention: rising temperatures will reduce the number of cold spells, which are a much bigger killer than heat. The best study shows that by 2050, heat will claim 400,000 more lives, but 1.8 million fewer will die because of cold. Indeed, according to the first complete survey of the economic effects of climate change for the world, global warming will actually save lives.', NULL, NULL, E'Gore told the world to expect 20-foot sea level rises over this century, who agonizes over the accelerated melting of ice in Greenland and what it means for the planet, and overlooks the conclusion that the current rate of melting would add three inches to the sea level rise, but rising temperatures will reduce the number of cold spells, which are a much bigger killer than heat, so global warming will actually save lives.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('4ec8f981-7b05-54b4-bce1-b86a4763f52c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ec8f981-7b05-54b4-bce1-b86a4763f52c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Smart Cities', E'Smart cities are emerging as major engines for deploying intelligent systems to enhance urban development. In developing economies facing rapid urbanization and technological change, new cities are being built with smart technologies and ideals, complete with business districts and residential facilities to entice businesses and talents to relocate. Governments tout the potential of such ‘greenfield’ smart cities for innovation and sustainability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4ed53bef-5726-5e01-bf4c-2dd9f0093ecb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ed53bef-5726-5e01-bf4c-2dd9f0093ecb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gender in Books', E'Girls are more likely to have books read to them that include female {{1}} than boys. Because of these preferences, children are more likely to learn about the gender biases of their own gender than of other genders. The researchers {{2}} 247 books written for children 5 years old and younger from the Wisconsin Children''s Book Corpus. The books with female protagonists had more gendered language than the books with male protagonists. The researchers {{3}} this finding to "male" being historically seen as the default gender. Female-coded words and phrases are more outside of the norm and more notable. The researchers also compared their findings to adult fiction books and found children''s books displayed more gender {{4}} than fictional books read by adults. In particular, the researchers examined how often women were associated with good, family, language and arts, while men were associated with bad, careers and math.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.protagonists, 2.analyzed, 3.attribute, 4.stereotypes', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ed99c5f-c944-5c92-aa61-b1d0a181866d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ed99c5f-c944-5c92-aa61-b1d0a181866d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Over-competitive', E'What are the advantages and the disadvantages of being over-competitive to individuals and society?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s society, competition is often viewed as a driving force for success. However, when competition becomes excessive, it can lead to negative consequences for individuals and society. In this essay, I will discuss the advantages and disadvantages of being over-competitive.\nOn the one hand, being over-competitive can have certain advantages. It can motivate individuals to push their limits and achieve their goals. When individuals are competing against others, they are more likely to put in extra effort and strive for excellence. This can lead to personal growth and development, as well as progress in various fields.\nOn the other hand, being over-competitive can have significant disadvantages. Firstly, it can lead to stress, burnout, and mental health issues. When individuals are constantly competing against others, they may feel pressure to perform at their best all the time. This can lead to exhaustion and even mental health problems such as anxiety and depression. Secondly, being over-competitive can create a toxic work environment and damage relationships. When individuals are solely focused on winning at all costs, they may engage in unethical behavior or sabotage their colleagues. This can lead to a negative work environment and damaged relationships.\nIn conclusion, while being over-competitive can have certain advantages such as motivation and progress, the disadvantages far outweigh the benefits. Being over-competitive can lead to stress, burnout, a toxic work environment, damaged relationships, and unethical behavior. Therefore, it is important for individuals and society to recognize the negative consequences of excessive competition and strive for balance in all aspects of life.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('4edd66dd-c85d-5238-942d-25e2bc477a9c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4edd66dd-c85d-5238-942d-25e2bc477a9c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sunshine Revolution', E'The suburbs of Las Vegas do not look like the cradle of a revolution. Golden stucco-clad houses stretch for street after identical street, interspersed with gated communities with names such as Spanish Oaks and Rancho Bel Air. The sky is the deepest blue, the desert air is clear and the distant mountains are beautiful. The only sounds are the buzz of a gardener’s hedge trimmer and a squeaking baby buggy pushed by a power-walking mother. The bright lights of Sin City seem a very long way away. Yet these quiet streets are being changed by a movement that is gathering momentum across America and around the world, challenging one of the most fundamental of economic relationships: the way we use and pay for energy. There are now more than 7,000 homes in Nevada fitted with solar panels to generate their own electricity, and the number is rising fast. Just five years ago, residential solar power was still a niche product for the homeowner with a fat wallet and a bleeding heart. Not anymore. Technology, politics and finance have aligned to move it into the mainstream. Solar power has become the fastest-growing energy source in the US.\nFor decades the electricity industry has been a cautious and conservative business, but the plunging prices of solar panels, down by about two-thirds in the past six years, have woken it up with a bang. Dynamic rooftop solar power companies have entered the market, in the most radical change to electricity supplies since the industry was born in the 19th century. It has been described as the equivalent of the mobile revolution in telephony, or the PC in computing.', NULL, NULL, E'There is an important revolution in Las Vegas, which challenges the economic relationships including usage and payment for energy, and many households have been equipped with solar panels, while solar power has become the fast-growing energy source in the US; dynamic rooftop solar power companies have entered the market due to the plunging prices of solar panels, which is the most radical change to electricity supplies.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('4ee47ebf-3b7a-5767-9c15-340aaaa44ddf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ee47ebf-3b7a-5767-9c15-340aaaa44ddf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'UW Course Description', E'The UW course descriptions are {{1}} regularly during the academic year. All announcements in the General Catalog and Course Catalog are subject to change without {{4}} and do not constitute an {{3}} between the University of Washington and the student. Students should assume the responsibility of {{2}} the appropriate academic unit or adviser for more current or specific information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.updated, 2.notice, 3.agreement, 4.consulting', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ee4f186-8281-5071-a4d5-c3c2830c195e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ee4f186-8281-5071-a4d5-c3c2830c195e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Mayans', E'The Mayans were a group of people who lived in central America. They developed an advanced civilization. It lasted for, um, excuse me, it lasted for many centuries. Its high point was between the years two hundred and nine hundred. The Mayans are famous for a number of things. They built many city states. These were like small countries. Naturally, the center of each was a city farm, surrounded these cities and supported them with food. Mayan cities also contained exceptional works of architecture. The ruins of some buildings can be seen today. There are both large palaces and stepped pyramids. The Mayans had a writing system and literature, but they didn''t use paper. Odd know. Instead they wrote on stone, wood and tree bark. Lots of writing was done on the insides and outsides of their temples and palaces. They also formed books from tree bark. But sadly, few of these books have survived to the present day. What happened to them? Well, first, the heat and wet weather of the jungle destroyed many, but Spanish conquerors got most of them. They actively sought to destroy the Mayans, written records. Fortunately, other objects, including my and works of art, have survived. We can see some of this art on the stones of their temples and palaces. The Mayans were excellent pottery makers as well. They created figures of stone, clay, and wood, and they even made some objects out of metal. But there are few extant examples of any metal devices.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '909fd9b7-8e9a-5fb4-aedd-dc2b4f562324'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The lecture is mainly about various aspects of Mayan civilization. They developed exceptional works of architecture as well as writing system. However, all of these have not survived to present day due to Spanish conquerors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4ee985e8-c9f8-500a-ad02-cd50d1cf9201'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4ee985e8-c9f8-500a-ad02-cd50d1cf9201'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Willful Blindness', E'Willful blindness had started life as a legal concept in the nineteenth century. A judge in Regina v. Sleep ruled that an accused could not be convicted for {{1}} of government property unless the jury found that he either knew the goods came from government stores or had "willfully shut his eyes to the fact". {{2}} , English judicial authorities referred to the state of mind that accompanied one who "willfully shut his eyes" as "connivance" or "constructive knowledge." Over time, lots of other phrases came into play-"deliberate or willful ignorance", "conscious avoidance", and "deliberate indifference". What they all have in {{3}} is the idea that there is an opportunity for knowledge and a responsibility to be informed, but it is shirked. Nowadays, the law is {{4}} often applied in cases of money laundering and drug trafficking: if you''ve been paid a large amount of money to carry a suitcase, then you are being willfully blind if you don''t check what is inside.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.possession, 2.Thereafter, 3.common, 4.most', NULL, NULL),
  ('4eed08cf-b3d2-5023-b330-caddf9ab61af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4eed08cf-b3d2-5023-b330-caddf9ab61af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the average weather conditions in an area over a long period?', '5a5271e1-f692-5faa-a2b0-983916be2d7d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Climate', NULL, NULL),
  ('4efced25-2bc0-59f5-9050-99ae75015a12'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4efced25-2bc0-59f5-9050-99ae75015a12'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'First Vaccines', E'In December 2020, the first vaccines {{1}} on a type of genetic material known as mRNA rolled out to fight COVID-19. That was less than 12 months after the lethal disease came to the world’s {{2}} . Within a year, those new shots appeared to have saved nearly 20 million lives. Now, two biochemists who laid the {{3}} for mRNA vaccines have been {{4}} the 2023 Nobel Prize in medicine or physiology.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.based, 2.notice, 3.groundwork, 4.awarded', NULL, NULL),
  ('4f04e4c4-9a58-5086-b5d0-63c958801137'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4f04e4c4-9a58-5086-b5d0-63c958801137'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '22763b8a-844a-567d-8513-e63a33e2e23d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She once held the position of editor for the student newspaper.', NULL, NULL),
  ('4f067a77-7d68-5955-9768-23107239b8ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4f067a77-7d68-5955-9768-23107239b8ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'City Life', E'More and more people are choosing to live in cities. They offer better opportunities, better services, and sanctuary from conflict and the effects of climate change influences. Yet large numbers of people are unable for various reasons to move to cities — skills mismatches, reluctance to sell land at a loss, and sometimes because of explicit policy restrictions that limit people’s movement within countries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4f0daedd-3666-57d9-bad3-3023b1f5d8e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4f0daedd-3666-57d9-bad3-3023b1f5d8e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Twins', E'UCLA neurology professor Paul Thompson and his colleagues scanned the brains of 23 sets of identical twins and 23 sets of fraternal twins. Since identical twins share the same genes while fraternal twins share about half their genes, the researchers were able to compare each group to show that myelin integrity was determined genetically in many parts of the brain that are key for intelligence. These include the parietal lobes, which are responsible for spatial reasoning, visual processing and logic, and the corpus callosum, which pulls together information from both sides of the body. The researchers used a faster version of a type of scanner called a HARDI (high-angular resolution diffusion imaging) — think of an MRI machine on steroids — that takes scans of the brain at a much higher resolution than a standard MRI. While an MRI scan shows the volume of different tissues in the brain by measuring the amount of water present, HARDI tracks how water diffuses through the brain''s white matter — a way to measure the quality of its myelin. "HARDI measures water diffusion," said Thompson, who is also a member of the UCLA Laboratory of Neuro-Imaging. "If the water diffuses rapidly in a specific direction, it tells us that the brain has very fast connections. If it diffuses more broadly, that''s an indication of slower signaling, and lower intelligence."', NULL, NULL, E'The researchers scanned the brains of 23 sets of identical twins and 23 sets of fraternal twins, with a conclusion that myelin integrity was determined genetically in many parts of the brain that are key for intelligence, and the researchers used a faster version of a type of scanner called a HARDI, which tracks how water diffuses through the brain''s white matter.', NULL, 5, 75),
