  ('4fb92eee-3350-5c66-bfef-3b74b9b7344c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fb92eee-3350-5c66-bfef-3b74b9b7344c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tree and City', E'A new report by environmental {{1}} The Nature Conservancy lays out how trees could pave the way to cleaner air and cooler cities. Using {{2}} information on forest cover paired with air pollution data and population {{3}} for 245 cities, researchers found that trees have the biggest health {{4}} in densely populated, polluted cities like Delhi, Karachi and Dhaka. The Conservancy and the C40 Cities Climate Leadership Group presented the findings of their global survey this week at the American Public Health Association meeting in Denver, Colorado.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.nonprofit, 2.geospatial, 3.forecasts, 4.payoffs', NULL, NULL),
  ('4fb9c746-1218-51e0-bf55-e9b2b860db09'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fb9c746-1218-51e0-bf55-e9b2b860db09'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gut Microbiome', E'Research has shown that the gut microbiome is important for human physiology and health. Disturbances to the composition of the gut microbiome can be associated with chronic diseases such as gastrointestinal inflammatory disorders, neurological, cardiovascular and respiratory illnesses. The human body has evolved strategies to ensure that a symbiotic relationship exists between the microbes in our gut and our cells.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('4fbb553f-0d75-553a-b831-8f22ddd244f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fbb553f-0d75-553a-b831-8f22ddd244f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the room that is below the level of the ground?', 'fd87e74b-31fb-542a-8b76-a804881d9b64'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Basement / cellar', NULL, NULL),
  ('4fbde439-a9b0-5053-a95a-f2844a10af49'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fbde439-a9b0-5053-a95a-f2844a10af49'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Family Dinner', E'As a family therapist, I often have the impulse to tell families to go home and have dinner together rather than spending an hour with me. And 20 years of research in North America, Europe and Australia back up my enthusiasm for family dinners. It turns out that sitting down for a nightly meal is great for the brain, the body and the spirit. And that nightly dinner doesn''t have to be a gourmet meal that took three hours to cook, nor does it need to be made with organic arugula and heirloom parsnips.\nFor starters, researchers found that for young children, dinnertime conversation boosts vocabulary even more than being read aloud to. The researchers counted the number of rare words – those not found on a list of 3,000 most common words – that the families used during dinner conversation. Young kids learned 1,000 rare words at the dinner table, compared to only 143 from parents reading storybooks aloud. Kids who have a large vocabulary read earlier and more easily.\nOlder children also reap intellectual benefits from family dinners. For school-age youngsters, regular mealtime is an even more powerful predictor of high achievement scores than time spent in school, doing homework, playing sports or doing art.\nOther researchers reported a consistent association between family dinner frequency and teen academic performance. Adolescents who ate family meals 5 to 7 times a week were twice as likely to get A''s in school as those who ate dinner with their families fewer than two times a week.', NULL, NULL, E'Sitting down for a nightly meal is great for the brain, the body and the spirit; for young children, dinnertime conversation boosts vocabulary even more than being read aloud to, and older children also reap intellectual benefits from family dinners, because regular mealtime is an even more powerful predictor of high achievement scores, while other researchers reported a consistent association between family dinner frequency and teen academic performance.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('4fc017d0-2da5-503f-8051-d7c2b262b134'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fc017d0-2da5-503f-8051-d7c2b262b134'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rainforest', E'In the {{1}} rainforest, there is a remarkable tree whose seeds are spread by animals. Birds and mammals eat the fruit and later {{2}} the seeds across wide areas, helping to {{3}} the diversity and growth of the rainforest ecosystem.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.humid, 2.disperse, 3.maintain', NULL, NULL),
  ('4fc065ed-9fd5-54d4-9cee-a828dece50ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '4fc065ed-9fd5-54d4-9cee-a828dece50ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9686d3da-0cb6-569a-8ec1-1e8f7af804f5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This camera technology can locate and focus on human eyes.', NULL, NULL),
