  ('50465ed4-981d-5954-a992-eeda81d5afdf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '50465ed4-981d-5954-a992-eeda81d5afdf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f3b88486-52f0-50cf-a331-3a0d1e2f13d4'::uuid, NULL, E'This play is divided into three acts, and each act has three scenes.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5046f03f-de53-5d6c-a211-335af40e989f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5046f03f-de53-5d6c-a211-335af40e989f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9537a714-428f-5048-a059-8130a97e68a8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The department has not made the issue a high priority.', NULL, NULL),
  ('504f80ee-7221-598d-836b-057064887b37'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '504f80ee-7221-598d-836b-057064887b37'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tree Rings', E'Here''s how tree ring dating, known to scientists as dendrochronology, works. If you cut a tree down today, it is straightforward to count the rings inwards, starting from the tree''s outside. Hence the sequence of the rings in a tree cross-section is like a message in Morse code formerly used for sending telegraph messages; dot-dot-dash-dot-dash in the Morse code, wide-wide-narrow-wide-narrow in the tree ring sequence. Actually, the tree-ring sequence is even more diagnostic and richer in information than the Morse code, because trees actually contain rings spanning much different width, rather than the Morse code choice between dot and dash.\nTree ring specialists (known as dendrochronologists) proceed by noting the sequence of wider and narrower rings in a tree cut down in a known recent year, and also noting the sequences in beams from trees cut down at various times in the past. In that way, dendrochronologists have constructed tree ring records extending back for thousands of years in some parts of the world. A bonus of dendrochronology is that the width and substructure of each ring reflect the amount of rain and the season at which the rain fell during that particular year. Thus, tree ring studies also allow one to reconstruct the past climate.', NULL, NULL, E'While tree ring dating is straightforward to count the rings inwards, a bonus of dendrochronology is that the width and the substructure of each ring reflect the amount of rain and the season at which the rain fell during that particular year to reconstruct the past climate, because the tree-ring sequence is more diagnostic and richer in information with rings spanning much different width.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('504fff3a-c176-5b99-8a0a-877b6cd193a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '504fff3a-c176-5b99-8a0a-877b6cd193a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Carbon Cycle', NULL, '7c60a546-330f-55f5-af86-a20a5995f5e9'::uuid, NULL, E'Carbon dioxide, or CO2, is the main greenhouse gas in climate change. So how does CO2 get into our atmosphere? Well, carbon is part of a cycle. It starts with the sun, which heats the Earth’s surface with more energy in one hour than the whole world uses in a year. Plants, which are kind of like biological chefs, take that sunlight, and then suck in some CO2 from the air, mix them together, and BAM! They create a stored form of energy, in the form of carbohydrates such as glucose and sucrose. The process is called photosynthesis. When animals like us eat those plants our stomachs convert that food back into energy for our own growth. Greenhouse gases are a byproduct of this process, and are released through waste. If those plants die, they decompose, and tiny microorganisms break down those carbohydrates and again, release greenhouse gases as a byproduct. As you see, energy originates from the sun. It is then transferred as it moves through the food chain. But sometimes, carbon based organisms like plants or animals get stuck in the earth. When this happens, they’re compressed under tons of pressure, and turned into carbon-based fossil fuels like oil, coal or natural gas.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5050bfdc-c36a-5016-a18a-04514cd83764'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5050bfdc-c36a-5016-a18a-04514cd83764'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the natural underground space large enough for a human to enter, typically formed by the dissolution of rock and which may contain a river?', '11908107-2d3b-506a-82ac-35a57cd58ee2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cave', NULL, NULL),
  ('50524356-d5e9-5c2e-bc2e-ac5345792dce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '50524356-d5e9-5c2e-bc2e-ac5345792dce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '49a2b235-106e-507e-9415-c369e5bbb44e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Our laboratory equipment is provided free of charge.', NULL, NULL),
  ('505d8a9f-467e-5332-9a56-676ebdb699b1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '505d8a9f-467e-5332-9a56-676ebdb699b1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RL', NULL, '848fea37-1686-5f5d-ba9c-6cb9c085c609'::uuid, NULL, E'Machiavelli lived from 1469 to 1527. The philosopher Bertrand Russell referred to Machiavelli''s most well-known book, The Prince, as a "gangsters'' handbook". And while there''s no doubt that certain people have read and used it as such, I think that if we put it into the context of when it was written, which was Italy, especially Florence, In the 15''11 and 16" centuries, it will be easier to judge Machiavelli''s reasons for writing it. Now, the Italy of that period was made up of a number of city states, often at war with each other. Add to that threats from foreign powers, especially France, and it was a very unstable and dangerous situation. Machiavelli loved his home city, Florence, and wanted to protect its culture, history and above all independence at all costs. One way to do this was to establish an army of Florentines loyal to the city state of Florence.\nMuch of Machiavelli''s career was taken up with this issue. It must be remembered, though, that he led an active civic life, was deeply into politics, and was an ambassador for Florence. In this way, he got to meet and observe some of the key players of the time and through this came to understand the nature of power and how to hold on to it. The Prince was an attempt to teach Florence the lessons he had learnt.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('505e507e-145c-5d6d-8fb7-b790947b15d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '505e507e-145c-5d6d-8fb7-b790947b15d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4c39c606-5217-5374-97af-363425b78353'::uuid, NULL, E'Trainees should be invited to relate new ideas to their past experiences.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
