  ('528f1a5b-cbec-5916-9ede-277348d0c9c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '528f1a5b-cbec-5916-9ede-277348d0c9c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Books', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('5294533e-94be-55d4-9ad2-7ff265575e76'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5294533e-94be-55d4-9ad2-7ff265575e76'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the process by which the body breaks down food into absorbable nutrients?', 'ed1fe331-32fc-5557-974a-2822b7c5f846'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Digestion', NULL, NULL),
  ('529586ce-a199-5120-9265-b00b1be44c1a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '529586ce-a199-5120-9265-b00b1be44c1a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Whether the languages of the ancient American peoples were used for expressing abstract universal concepts can be clearly answered in the case of Nahuatl. Nahuatl, like Greek and German, is a language that allows the formation of extensive compounds. By the combination of radicals or semantic elements, single compound words can express complex conceptual relations, often of an abstract universal character.The tlamatinime (''those who know'') were able to use this rich stock of abstract terms to express the nuances of their thought. They also availed themselves of other forms of expression with metaphorical meaning, some probably original, some derived from Toltec coinages. Of these forms the most characteristic in Nahuatl is the juxtaposition of two words that, because they are synonyms, associated terms, or even contraries, complement each other to evoke one single idea. Used as metaphor, the juxtaposed terms connote specific or essential traits of the being they refer to, introducing a mode of poetry as an almost habitual form of expression.\n\nAccording to the passage, some abstract universal ideas can be expressed in Nahuatl by __', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'putting various meaningful elements together in one word', NULL, NULL),
  ('52a0aea7-4e6b-531d-8883-0a135a3e75b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52a0aea7-4e6b-531d-8883-0a135a3e75b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pima Cotton', E'Pima cotton is the predominant variety of cotton grown in California. It’s ideal for making premium fabrics for clothing and bed sheets. But Fusarium wilt disease, caused by a soil-borne fungus, can devastate a cotton crop. And this can be a very damaging disease in terms of greatly reducing yields, and to some extent, even making cotton uneconomical as a crop in a region. As it becomes more difficult to produce something economically, the only way to keep producing it is to have the cost of everything go up. So it’s responsible for crop losses in several production regions in the U.S. and worldwide.\n\nWhich statement below is not true?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Cotton price will decrease with the spread of Fusarium wilt disease.', NULL, NULL),
  ('52a25f79-2852-554f-ba20-157197648d4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52a25f79-2852-554f-ba20-157197648d4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'GPS Tracking(GPS定位)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('52a81003-2276-55e6-97d4-905863d88a63'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52a81003-2276-55e6-97d4-905863d88a63'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7d8ab54d-79a1-52b1-9377-5c0860b03542'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Teamwork is highly required in order to achieve these aims.', NULL, NULL),
  ('52ae6033-0ae4-5bcc-879a-b68fde7a25b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52ae6033-0ae4-5bcc-879a-b68fde7a25b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Eye Color', E'Brown is the most common eye color in the world — between 70 and 80 percent of the world''s population have eyes that are some shade of brown, from the darkest dark brown to light brown. It''s thought that all ancient humans living 10,000 years ago or more had brown eyes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52aeb923-fef3-58e2-a320-18a0be368b19'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52aeb923-fef3-58e2-a320-18a0be368b19'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are the white masses in the sky?', '806e90ae-02a0-526f-b968-c8319b5d1f10'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Clouds', NULL, NULL),
  ('52af97bb-bdec-56dd-a488-98f3f1d48adf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52af97bb-bdec-56dd-a488-98f3f1d48adf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roosmalens'' Dwarf Porcupine', E'A new study has provided valuable insights into the Roosmalens'' dwarf porcupine, a neotropical species that has been poorly understood until now. This research, conducted after 22 years of limited knowledge, reveals important information about its distribution, evolutionary relationships, and potential risks to its conservation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52b28eaa-18c9-5052-bad5-648ddb6ab89c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52b28eaa-18c9-5052-bad5-648ddb6ab89c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '17e53d0a-a433-557e-b447-90e55a82b668'::uuid, NULL, E'The campaign is intended to educate the public to respect the environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52bbb8f6-8387-56c6-904b-91f90e1d5f9f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52bbb8f6-8387-56c6-904b-91f90e1d5f9f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sake Yeast', E'Researchers have found that a mutant strain of sake yeast produces high levels of the amino acid ornithine. Ornithine has been found to reduce fatigue and improve sleep quality, and the non-genetically modified mutant yeast strain discovered in this study could be easily applied to brewing sake, a traditional Japanese alcoholic beverage, as well as wine and beer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52c19c61-9762-5c6e-acef-f5067089dca0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52c19c61-9762-5c6e-acef-f5067089dca0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a413a466-e19d-5955-ac23-e7b82f458118'::uuid, NULL, E'Such behaviors are regarded as a deviation of the norm.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52c70b89-f807-5044-8961-63f2d3d2aee8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52c70b89-f807-5044-8961-63f2d3d2aee8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Career Clusters', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 4, 1, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('52ca122c-fc4e-5c90-bb2a-a7791b815dc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52ca122c-fc4e-5c90-bb2a-a7791b815dc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Citizen Science', E'Motor learning researchers study how people learn from their own movement errors and how they adapt to changing environments. However, most of these studies are {{1}} in labs with expensive equipment and small samples of participants. A new research study, published in Nature Human Behaviour, has explored this question using a novel approach: citizen science. Citizen science is the involvement of the public in scientific research, often through online {{2}} . The study developed a simple web-based motor test that anyone could take at home. The test involved moving the mouse cursor to a target on the screen, {{3}} the cursor was rotated by a random angle. The participants had to {{4}} their movements to correct for the rotation. The test generated a large dataset of more than 2,000 sessions from a diverse group of participants and revealed how people corrected for motor errors using different strategies: some relied more on subconscious, implicit learning, while others used more conscious, explicit learning. The authors said that this large-scale approach could {{5}} traditional lab studies and help democratize motor learning research.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.conducted, 2.platforms, 3.while, 4.adjust, 5.complement', NULL, NULL),
  ('52d2d9be-8c19-576c-8fa2-cb015a71cd60'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52d2d9be-8c19-576c-8fa2-cb015a71cd60'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hearing Loss', E'Damage from unsafe listening can {{1}} over the life course. A study discovered that young people regularly listen to music at unsafe noise levels and concluded that {{2}} safer listening practices was urgent. Sensory cells and structures in the ear can become {{3}} from being exposed to sound at excessive volumes. If left unchecked for too long, it can cause {{4}} damage, such as deafness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.worsen, 2.promoting, 3.fatigued, 4.permanent', NULL, NULL),
  ('52d59013-6e67-55d6-84ab-27accb9f3fdd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52d59013-6e67-55d6-84ab-27accb9f3fdd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Psychology', E'Psychology as a subject of study has largely developed in the West since the late nineteenth century. During this period there has been an {{1}} on scientific thinking. Because of this, there have been many scientific studies in psychology which {{2}} different aspects of human nature. These include studies into how biology (physical factors) influences human experience, how people use their {{3}} (touch, taste, smell, sight and hearing) to get to know the world, how people develop, why people behave in certain ways, how memory works, how people develop language, how people understand and think about the world, what motivates people, why people have emotions and how personality develops. These scientific {{4}} all contribute to an understanding of human nature. What do we mean by the practical applications of these studies? An {{5}} of psychology is useful in many different areas in life, such as education, the workplace, social services and medicine. This means that people who have knowledge of psychology can {{6}} or apply that knowledge in areas such as the ones listed above.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.emphasis, 2.explore, 3.senses, 4.investigations, 5.understanding, 6.use', NULL, NULL),
  ('52d7d2e3-442a-5793-a0ac-4774cfa3ac6b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52d7d2e3-442a-5793-a0ac-4774cfa3ac6b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Research-based Programs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 2, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('52dbaea4-4a97-54d8-b08e-36ce152dd293'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52dbaea4-4a97-54d8-b08e-36ce152dd293'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dream Recall', E'People who are more introverted and inward-focused tend to remember more dreams, {{1}} those who are more extroverted and action-oriented tend to remember fewer. Imaginativeness and {{2}} to hypnosis are also linked to dream recall, as are some measures of creativity, though creativity is tricky {{3}} not all measures of creativity even line up with one another, much less with dream {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.while, 2.susceptibility, 3.because, 4.tendencies', NULL, NULL),
  ('52e1be87-bafd-5c2b-9763-3c454a68b936'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52e1be87-bafd-5c2b-9763-3c454a68b936'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Telescope', E'James Webb Space Telescope was specifically designed to observe this light, which comes from some of the oldest galaxies to take form. How did early stars and galaxies take shape? What about the cosmic material that is undetectable, known as dark matter? Is there evidence for it in the early eons of the universe? These are some of the perplexing and fascinating questions that astronomers can begin unraveling with Webb.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52e3c257-d5d4-5eab-9894-56db13c8c9c4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52e3c257-d5d4-5eab-9894-56db13c8c9c4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '32dbba1a-d1bc-5472-a100-b8b6e5a55508'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We had not been able to gain admittance to the flat.', NULL, NULL),
  ('52e7d121-acdf-5af0-bb92-128ffb152ee4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52e7d121-acdf-5af0-bb92-128ffb152ee4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lecture', E'A lecture tends to be a one-sided class where you and your fellow students will sit and take notes while a lecturer talks about a specific topic or gives a presentation. This class is information- heavy so taking notes is essential and there may be little time to ask questions. Lectures are the main method for your university to teach you the necessary material.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52ef75dc-2dad-5c78-9f7a-7fcd2d280159'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52ef75dc-2dad-5c78-9f7a-7fcd2d280159'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solution of Issue', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'5, 1, 2, 4, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('52f5d1ce-5aef-5e25-b926-e9c8ec27b579'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52f5d1ce-5aef-5e25-b926-e9c8ec27b579'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '349f08d2-c098-5cef-9630-9aa8ec0a3ed4'::uuid, NULL, E'Animals grow larger and stronger, which helps them hunt better.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52fb1f41-bca7-5eba-8891-1b68ed27dc65'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '52fb1f41-bca7-5eba-8891-1b68ed27dc65'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Employers', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 3, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('5308b74b-2545-5962-bdf7-c6569ba6751b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5308b74b-2545-5962-bdf7-c6569ba6751b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Too Much Information', E'We all know, that too much information can be a bad thing - this is as true in daily life as it is in business. Filtering useful from useless information has become a growing problem, bringing confusion with it, but this is where data curation can help. Curating data involves finding and displaying patterns in large volumes of disconnected and messy data to create meaningful information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('53102695-a1dc-5a50-874d-f70aecd26ccb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '53102695-a1dc-5a50-874d-f70aecd26ccb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Complaints', E'Humans love to complain to each other. It helps us feel less alone. Think about what happens when a family member or friend is going through a tough time; they call up someone who will listen to their tale of woe. Unfortunately, negative bonding is the default for many groups.\nIn some families, complaining is the only way to get attention. When one person says, I had a bad day; the other person has to top it, "You think you had a tough day. I had to do three TPS reports!" The same thing happens at work and social settings. "Your child didn''t sleep through the night until 6 months? Mine was a full year old before she went over six hours." It''s a race to the bottom, and the worst situation wins.\nIn Bitching is Bonding, A Guide To Mutual Complaint, Irene S. Levine, Ph.D., a professor of psychiatry at the NYU Langone School of Medicine says, "The reason why these conversations feel good is because we feel understood."\nPeople raised in negative environments learn early on. Being positive gets you thrown out of the club. When family dinner is a complaint fest, you’re not going to risk alienation saying, "Wow, I had an awesome day. Don''t you just love life?"\nTranslate this into a work setting: people, often unconsciously, believe being positive keeps you out of the cool club. When negativity provides bonding, humans are reluctant to abandon the behavior that brings them comfort.', NULL, NULL, E'Humans love to complain to each other, because it helps us feel less alone, and in some families, complaining is the only way to get attention, since the reason why these conversations feel good is because we feel understood, so people raised in negative environments learn early on, but when negativity provides bonding, humans are reluctant to abandon the behavior that brings them comfort.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('531714a3-9680-5f23-b3d6-b36cce5eae15'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '531714a3-9680-5f23-b3d6-b36cce5eae15'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Exploration', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 2, 4, 3, 5', NULL, NULL),
  ('5318fc99-596f-5b3c-a64c-1c05835c3c19'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5318fc99-596f-5b3c-a64c-1c05835c3c19'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Remembrance of Things Past', E'In Marcel Proust''s iconic Remembrance of Things Past, a taste of cake elicits a flood of {{1}} .\nNow a study finds that the stronger your memory of a {{2}} food, the more likely you are to choose it again. And it doesn''t matter how objectively unattractive the food may be—which perhaps explains why you may crave those peanut butter and {{3}} sandwiches from your youth or can''t break that fried chicken habit when trying to diet.\nThe food-memory study is in the journal Neuron.\nResearchers asked 30 hungry young people to rate snacks such as potato chips and chocolate. No actual food was presented. The snacks were merely displayed on screens associated with locations. Then the study {{4}} were asked to choose between two locations, as proxies for the snacks. And the hungry subjects went with memory over taste {{5}} —that is, they picked what they were better able to {{6}} even if they had rated them lower in the first part of the test.\nThe participants'' brains were scanned during the process of choosing. And the researchers found that the exercise caused {{7}} communication between the hippocampus, associated with memory, and the part of the frontal lobe home to decision-making.\nWhich may show why when we''re making food decisions, familiarity often wins out over other factors—and why your shopping list looks virtually the same week after week.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.memories, 2.particular, 3.marshmallow, 4.participants, 5.preference, 6.remember, 7.increased', NULL, NULL),
  ('53215e41-faca-556c-bce9-49cb343aa307'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '53215e41-faca-556c-bce9-49cb343aa307'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '28770fa3-24fd-53f0-b46f-7ccce4ecbca3'::uuid, NULL, E'The announcement to cancel the final exam has thrilled the students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('53216841-315b-5ef4-8e4a-0ea12b438e6f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '53216841-315b-5ef4-8e4a-0ea12b438e6f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Female Hummingbirds', E'Female hummingbirds don flashy feathers to avoid being bothered by other hummingbirds. They tend to have bright blue heads and throats. But mate choice doesn’t seem to drive these females’ pretty plumage since males don’t appear to prefer the blue females. Therefore, bright colors may help lady birds blend in with the guys, and as a result, feed for longer without harassment from other hummingbirds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
