  ('55144093-229d-58dd-8eab-7e8a5bc0cb44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55144093-229d-58dd-8eab-7e8a5bc0cb44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b38fb6ae-0622-5b3c-ba92-0f920565aba7'::uuid, NULL, E'Email me if you can''t finish the task on time.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5516b614-b0e9-52f6-a6bf-d8a104784120'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5516b614-b0e9-52f6-a6bf-d8a104784120'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Image of Africa', E'Africa is not homogeneous. The negative impression of Africa held internationally is very unfair to those African countries that are actually doing well in their development, because this continent has more than 50 countries rich in natural resources which have not been completely exploited and cultural diversity, and hardworking Africans are struggling to address issues of poverty, disease and war, so Africa can be an attractive place for business development and cultural tourism if concerted international support and assistance are provided. This skewed perception overlooks the vibrant reality and immense potential of the continent.\nAfrica has a lot of potential, and years ago it brought benefits to some companies. Historical engagements have proven that forward-thinking businesses can find success. In fact, Africa is the region with the best investment returns. It is a paradise for investors and adventurers, but it still needs international aid. It is good to do business with Africans because of the mutual money and long-term growth prospects. Furthermore, beyond business, Africa is also beautiful, boasting landscapes and cultural heritage that make it a premier destination for cultural tourism, offering profound experiences for visitors.\nHowever, to discuss Africa honestly, one must also acknowledge its struggles. Africa suffers from frequent wars and the causes are complex, rooted in historical legacies and competition over resources, not in any inherent trait of its people. Africans know what is needed in their development but need assistance in areas like technology transfer, infrastructure financing, and capacity building.', NULL, NULL, E'Africa can be an attractive place for business development and cultural tourism if concerted international support and assistance are provided, but this skewed perception overlooks the vibrant reality and immense potential of the continent, and Africa is the region with the best investment returns, which suffers from frequent wars and the causes are complex, so Africans need assistance in areas like technology transfer, infrastructure financing, and capacity building.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('551970fe-3bb6-5309-a1fd-3457163e562b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '551970fe-3bb6-5309-a1fd-3457163e562b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Unions work for who, workers or managers?', '14b5b7eb-06a2-5c59-8b12-179fcba922e5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Workers', NULL, NULL),
  ('551c23ad-cc7a-56ed-9488-302b8b1a23e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '551c23ad-cc7a-56ed-9488-302b8b1a23e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parents'' Attitude', E'When parents are asked how they handle their very unruly children, most will admit that they are likely to use physical forms of punishment. This is not to say that a parent generally hits their child each and every time they are bad. Nevertheless, parents generally use physical punishment as a last resort, after having unsuccessfully tried other forms of discipline with children who have become very bad. Those who believe in physical punishment, however, are unaware of the fact that it does not lead to better children. In fact, the opposite is true.\nResearch findings show that children from homes where corporal punishment is the norm exhibit more anti-social behavior than children whose parents seldom or never hit them. For example, children whose parents systematically use corporal punishment are more often than not behind any classroom disruptions. Such children not only create discipline problems at school, but they are also overly aggressive. In addition, they have extremely low self-esteem and a negative attitude to those around them. On the other hand, children whose parents use less harsh methods of discipline have a healthier attitude towards their school environment and (BEEP)\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'db47d614-c7e7-5d03-b42e-09681d7498a1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'peers', NULL, NULL),
  ('551da9c1-bb31-592c-a3f3-9ec8406a7da9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '551da9c1-bb31-592c-a3f3-9ec8406a7da9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sunshine', E'According to recent research, sunshine and warm weather have a positive effect on our moods. The British Journal of Psychology has published a report in which it claims that anxiety levels fall when temperatures rise, while increased exposure to sunshine makes us think more positively about our lives.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
