  ('55d45c9b-93f1-5acb-a1ed-67665710f5ee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55d45c9b-93f1-5acb-a1ed-67665710f5ee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sound Speed', E'The speed of sound (otherwise known as Mach 1) varies with temperature. At sea level on a ''standard day'', the temperature is 59°F, and Mach 1 is approximately 761 mph. As the altitude increases, the temperature and speed of sound {{1}} decrease until about 36,000 feet, after which the temperature {{2}} steady until about 60,000 feet. Within that 36,000 – 60,000 foot range, Mach 1 is about 661 mph. Because of the {{3}} , it is possible for an airplane flying supersonic at high altitude to be slower than a subsonic flight at sea level. The transonic band (the ''sound barrier‘) extends {{4}} around Mach 0.8 — when the first supersonic shock waves form on the wing — to Mach 1.2, when the entire wing has gone supersonic.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.both, 2.remains, 3.variation, 4.from', NULL, NULL),
  ('55d46e9e-be99-59ad-9e25-0827ef91019d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55d46e9e-be99-59ad-9e25-0827ef91019d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8cde4cd5-c653-5f1f-b32d-759fb3b19dcb'::uuid, NULL, E'Many of the urban poor lived in extremely cramped conditions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('55dcf439-78d5-50ae-b631-0319bcea1693'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55dcf439-78d5-50ae-b631-0319bcea1693'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Journalist', E'Being a journalist is one of the most difficult jobs in the world. To what extent, you agree with it?', NULL, NULL, E'Being a journalist is undoubtedly one of the most challenging professions in the world. The job requires a great deal of dedication, hard work, and a passion for uncovering the truth. In this essay, I will argue that being a journalist is one of the most difficult jobs in the world due to the significant role they play in keeping people informed and the challenges they face in doing so.\nFirstly, journalists play a crucial role in keeping people informed about current events and issues. They are responsible for gathering information and presenting it to the public in an accurate and unbiased manner. This requires a great deal of research, investigation, and fact-checking, which can be time-consuming and challenging. Furthermore, journalists often have to work under tight deadlines, which means they have to produce high-quality content quickly and efficiently.\nSecondly, journalists face significant pressure to produce stories under tight deadlines and with limited resources. They often have to work long hours and cover a wide range of topics, which can be mentally and physically exhausting. Moreover, journalists are often exposed to dangerous situations, such as war zones or areas of civil unrest. They risk their lives to report on important events and issues, which is a testament to their dedication and bravery.\nIn conclusion, being a journalist is indeed one of the most difficult jobs in the world due to the significant role they play in keeping people informed and the challenges they face in doing so. Despite the challenges, journalism remains a vital profession that provides an essential service to society. It is important that we continue to support and value the work of journalists, who are often at the forefront of uncovering the truth and holding those in power accountable.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('55dd355e-a967-5f65-a13b-6badc3b42df5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55dd355e-a967-5f65-a13b-6badc3b42df5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'World of Microbiomes', E'In the vast realm of biology, the study of microbiomes has emerged as a revolutionary field, revealing a hidden universe of microscopic organisms that play a crucial role in human health. A microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa, that inhabit various environments like the human body, soil, and oceans.\nThe human microbiome, particularly the gut microbiome, has garnered significant attention for its profound impact on overall health. These microscopic inhabitants of our intestines are not just passive residents; they actively participate in vital processes such as digestion, immune system regulation, and even the production of essential vitamins. A balanced gut microbiome is linked to a plethora of health benefits, including improved digestion, a robust immune response, and even mental well-being.\nRecent studies have revealed the intricate relationship between the gut microbiome and conditions like obesity, diabetes, and heart disease. Alterations in gut microbiota composition can influence the body''s metabolism, affecting weight and energy balance. Furthermore, the gut-brain axis, a communication pathway between the gut and the brain, highlights how gut bacteria can impact mental health, contributing to an understanding of depression and anxiety.\nThe environmental microbiome is equally significant. Soil and ocean microbiomes play a pivotal role in nutrient cycling, supporting plant growth and marine life, and maintaining ecological balance. They are also a rich source of novel compounds, including antibiotics and enzymes, with potential applications in medicine and biotechnology.\nIn conclusion, the study of microbiomes opens a window into a microscopic world with macroscopic implications for human health and the environment. Understanding and harnessing the power of these unseen allies can lead to breakthroughs in health, agriculture, and environmental conservation.', NULL, NULL, E'The study of microbiomes, encompassing diverse microorganisms in human bodies and the environment, is pivotal in understanding health and disease, influencing digestion, immunity, mental well-being, and ecological balance, offering potential breakthroughs in medical, agricultural, and environmental sciences.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('55e16c85-ca34-5928-9d8f-2436e94054e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '55e16c85-ca34-5928-9d8f-2436e94054e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Global Collapse', E'The global collapse of frogs and other amphibians due to the amphibian chytrid fungus exacerbated malaria outbreaks in Costa Rica and Panama during the 1990s and 2000s, according to new research. The findings provide the first evidence that amphibian population declines have directly affected human health and show how preserving biodiversity can benefit humans as well as local ecosystems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
