  ('5676f8b6-b50c-5a58-9f41-191a750b8aeb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5676f8b6-b50c-5a58-9f41-191a750b8aeb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd0b1c5a7-a780-5c74-a469-f0a218bb22b3'::uuid, NULL, E'Under normal conditions, markets will allocate resources efficiently.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('567bfcee-bfeb-59d9-b2aa-391d91c062ae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '567bfcee-bfeb-59d9-b2aa-391d91c062ae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Decreased Sunlight', E'The amount of sunlight that Earth reflects back into space has decreased measurably in recent years. Whether the decline in earthshine is a short-term blip or yet another ominous sign for Earth’s climate is up in the air, scientists suggest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('567d1e3d-4b6f-5666-8fc0-8757d3ff6e8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '567d1e3d-4b6f-5666-8fc0-8757d3ff6e8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Traditional Art', E'Do you agree that digital art is as valuable as traditional art?', NULL, NULL, E'In the contemporary art landscape, the question of whether digital art holds equal value to traditional art is a topic of ongoing debate. I firmly believe that digital art is as valuable as traditional art, offering unique advantages that cater to the evolving needs of artists and audiences alike.\nDigital art''s unparalleled accessibility through online platforms has revolutionized the art world by breaking down geographical barriers and reaching a global audience. This democratization of art appreciation allows for a diverse range of voices and perspectives to be heard, fostering inclusivity and cultural exchange in the digital realm.\nThe innovative nature of digital tools empowers artists to explore endless creative possibilities and experiment with new techniques in their artistic expression. The versatility of digital art enables artists to easily edit and share their work, facilitating rapid exploration of diverse styles and approaches that push the boundaries of traditional art forms.\nIn conclusion, the value of digital art is indisputable in today''s rapidly evolving artistic landscape. Through its accessibility, innovation, and versatility, digital art not only expands the horizons of artistic expression but also democratizes art appreciation, making it a valuable and essential component of the modern art world. Embracing the unique strengths of digital art alongside traditional forms enriches the artistic experience and ensures a vibrant and inclusive artistic community for generations to come.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('56825834-9e30-5e92-9c2c-fa9b895db06f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56825834-9e30-5e92-9c2c-fa9b895db06f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biodiversity''s Crucial Role', NULL, 'a19fb73d-c758-5e15-9c1d-162e7fbf5a3f'::uuid, NULL, E'As we gather here today, let''s reflect on the intricate symphony of life that is biodiversity. This variety of life forms the foundation of the ecosystems upon which we all depend. Biodiversity is not merely an assortment of flora and fauna; it''s the cornerstone of the services nature provides, from clean air and water to fertile soil and pollination, all critical for our survival and well-being. Additionally, biodiversity is a rich tapestry that supports economic prosperity. The variety of species and their interactions drive ecotourism and sustain traditional industries such as fishing and agriculture. The genetic diversity within wild species is also a reservoir for improving crop resilience and medicinal discoveries. As we forge our paths, let''s recognize the role we play in this balance. Our actions can either contribute to the harmony or disrupt the melody. It is our collective responsibility to conserve and sustainably manage our natural resources, ensuring this symphony continues for generations to come.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5685397f-7372-52fa-a1d7-a0c16bd81295'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5685397f-7372-52fa-a1d7-a0c16bd81295'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1890b3d7-61a1-57f7-b2d2-b07134503c4b'::uuid, NULL, E'The United States is the largest chocolate manufacturing country.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5685a6f4-b2cd-5fb6-97bc-cb7cb3229d28'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5685a6f4-b2cd-5fb6-97bc-cb7cb3229d28'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7307d0f8-d9a2-5f6b-9011-725003aa653b'::uuid, NULL, E'His research fascinates due to his natural curiosity and inquisitiveness.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('56879e6d-f707-5f96-b333-cbea7bcb4cee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56879e6d-f707-5f96-b333-cbea7bcb4cee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Carski Award', E'In 2001 he received the SIUC Outstanding Scholar Award. In 2003 he received the Carski Award for Distinguished Undergraduate Teaching from the American Society for Microbiology. Mike''s research is {{1}} on bacteria that inhabit {{2}} environments, and for the past 12 years he has studied the microbiology of permanently ice-covered lakes in the McMurdo Dry Valleys, Antarctica. In addition to his research papers, he has edited a major {{3}} on phototrophic bacteria and served for over a decade as chief editor of the {{4}} Archives of Microbiology. He currently serves on the editorial board of Environmental Microbiology. Mike’s non-scientific {{5}} include forestry, reading, and caring for his dogs and horses. He lives beside a peaceful and quiet lake with his wife, Nancy, five shelter dogs (Gaino, Snuffy, Pepto, Peanut, and Merry), and four horses (Springer, Feivel, Gwen, and Festus).', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.focused, 2.extreme, 3.treatise, 4.journal, 5.interests', NULL, NULL),
  ('568fad50-0aab-5bba-9256-223aee4ffccc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '568fad50-0aab-5bba-9256-223aee4ffccc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Making Suggestions', E'You have a great idea — a product tweak that will save your company money, a process change to increase your team’s productivity, or a plan for heading off a looming crisis. There’s just one snag: you’re not sure how to approach your boss about it, or worse, you’ve tried and failed to get the attention of higher-ups.\nDespite abundant research on the value of bottom-up innovation and problem-solving, many workers still feel stifled in giving their bosses feedback or making suggestions. One survey of U.S. employees found that a full 70% weren’t comfortable raising an issue with their boss even when it was important, and a landmark 2003 study found that 85% of employees withheld their ideas because they were afraid to speak up.\nAdditional research shows that even when employees do speak up, their suggestions usually don’t lead to change. For example, an Accenture study showed that nearly three-fourths of ideas submitted through corporate online suggestion tools languished and were never implemented. Another study of a hospital found that of 200 ideas shared by employees, most were initially rejected and fewer than a quarter were ever implemented.\nFor the past two decades, I’ve studied how employees offer solicited and unsolicited recommendations and how managers respond. Obviously, there are many reasons why ideas — including those from senior leaders — fail to make it to implementation. But too often good ideas are ignored or rejected. I’ve found that two factors are key to a successful pitch: having the confidence to make your suggestion and knowing how to frame it to get the best reception from your boss. Some managers will be more unapproachable and unresponsive than others, but research shows that the majority are more open to ideas and suggestions than you might imagine — provided they are approached effectively.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('568ffdac-5402-5ac0-8162-f8df06654005'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '568ffdac-5402-5ac0-8162-f8df06654005'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'National Parks', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('5697d283-9221-532d-b6ae-41067853e9d4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5697d283-9221-532d-b6ae-41067853e9d4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sustainability', E'On a planet with a growing population and shrinking natural resources, business-as-usual is no longer sustainable. But sustainability is very often good for the bottom line, as it''s in the best interest of businesses to responsibly manage our natural resources so we can continue to use them for years to come.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('56a22abf-d653-5f67-9b41-00336d8f0447'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56a22abf-d653-5f67-9b41-00336d8f0447'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'aa4f7a75-fbd2-56ab-87c1-81e46bf94b48'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Crucial details in the article are omitted from the summary.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56a2cdc9-4df0-572e-990a-42cd90df2f65'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56a2cdc9-4df0-572e-990a-42cd90df2f65'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a038d910-25cb-5185-b072-7fc9a75fa54f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Think of everything you get from the school as helpful tools.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56a456ee-033c-5912-99bd-8d80500967b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56a456ee-033c-5912-99bd-8d80500967b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Market Fluctuations', E'For the first time, economists conducted a controlled simulation that {{1}} how stock market fluctuations can occur seemingly without external triggers. They {{2}} trading bots to buy and sell shares at a steady rate. Initially, the market was {{3}} , but soon, variances in trade volumes emerged, causing clustered spikes and dips in stock prices. These fluctuations then {{4}} across the market like a ripple, mirroring real-world market volatilities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.illustrated, 2.programmed, 3.stable, 4.propagated', NULL, NULL),
  ('56abd2e3-66a3-532c-8b5b-65970e12b50d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56abd2e3-66a3-532c-8b5b-65970e12b50d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Scarce Land', E'Land is scarce in many parts of our fast-urbanizing world. Few communities have the chance to create something brand-new on a significant piece of land — and even fewer can develop that land in a way that confronts climate change, generates jobs, and attracts investment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('56aeacbc-af6c-5cea-8f73-c27f004eb9c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56aeacbc-af6c-5cea-8f73-c27f004eb9c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the political ideology that seeks to create an egalitarian society free from class distinctions?', 'bc8ddcc7-fb79-5dd0-9eea-2dfa0dfd51d2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Communism', NULL, NULL),
  ('56b1182c-7e2c-5085-a8e1-58789d5e7962'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56b1182c-7e2c-5085-a8e1-58789d5e7962'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Graphic Design', E'The Graphic Design degree provides students with a nurturing environment for learning, developing aesthetic appreciation and design skills with an emphasis on media and marketing. Students have the chance to develop their personal style, while broadening their technical repertoire as designers.\nThe academic staff are former working artists,theorists and designers who have been successful in achieving major awards, commissions and research grants. The facilities for the graphic design program include spacious design studios,colour and monochrome darkrooms and photography studios. Students will develop skills at a professional working standard in all computer-based programs that the design industry requires.\n\nWhat does the Graphic Design degree offer students?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'teachers who have practical experience in a creative field', NULL, NULL),
  ('56ba2adb-ce38-53cf-bf01-d7b0f74d840e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56ba2adb-ce38-53cf-bf01-d7b0f74d840e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e508675f-14cf-54c7-be79-2f01cd615f6d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She won a scholarship to study at a famous university.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56c9514b-0abe-5942-b4df-b9217425a3a9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56c9514b-0abe-5942-b4df-b9217425a3a9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2446b345-a940-570c-b965-f310b14e662a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The teacher explained the homework to the class.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56d1c9fa-6834-521c-b1ca-dcab5490976b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56d1c9fa-6834-521c-b1ca-dcab5490976b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'dbb36f42-ccfb-58ea-95e7-590f18a0f56c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There is a separate reading list for each course.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56d5d3b7-8a2f-5cc8-9dba-bee2747ac8ac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56d5d3b7-8a2f-5cc8-9dba-bee2747ac8ac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Business School Admission', E'Business school admissions officers said the new drive to attract younger students was in part the result of a realization that they had inadvertently limited their applicant pool by requiring several years'' work experience. Talented students who might otherwise have gone to business school instead opted for a law or policy degree because they were intimidated by the expectation of work experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('56d7b8df-20c5-5604-a4f4-7e308b99b7d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56d7b8df-20c5-5604-a4f4-7e308b99b7d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c76a02dc-789b-504e-8b57-839c3aecc219'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The study of ecology integrates both traditional sciences and life sciences.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56ddf759-8f5a-5f84-a5b9-a3ba7652e20c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56ddf759-8f5a-5f84-a5b9-a3ba7652e20c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4bdcebc8-882e-59b4-b915-1c97970f3e63'::uuid, NULL, E'Your boss requires you to finish the report before Friday.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('56ed9948-d648-561b-8a84-9d56cbd6b9de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56ed9948-d648-561b-8a84-9d56cbd6b9de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Content Marketing', E'Content marketing is the process of creating valuable, relevant content to attract, acquire, and engage your audience. Buyers and customers today are inundated by more marketing messages than ever before — more than 2,900 per day, by current estimations. This creates an environment of attention scarcity, challenging marketers with the task of producing engaging content that won’t get lost in the static. A well-crafted content marketing strategy places your business in the position of a thought leader, building brand preference as you inform and educate buyers. Providing helpful and entertaining content can form a strong bond between your brand and customers that continues to grow and strengthen over time. Traditionally, marketers have had to ‘rent attention’ from other people’s media through display ads on websites, booths at trade shows, or emails sent to third-party lists. For example, when a brand pays out millions of dollars for a Super Bowl ad, they are renting the attention that the TV networks have built. Content marketing, on the other hand, allows marketers to become publishers by building their own audiences and attracting their own attention. By creating and distributing content that buyers find useful, marketers increase their brand awareness and preference by establishing a relationship of trust with consumers as they move through the sales funnel. Additionally, content marketing is considered a less costly strategy than some others. It can have a bit of a slower start while your content library grows and reaches a larger audience.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('56f60871-8c48-5b4a-98c9-b95580c2d79f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56f60871-8c48-5b4a-98c9-b95580c2d79f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the process of teaching and learning called?', '0d831668-56d6-574f-a097-bdb93fe7b836'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Education', NULL, NULL),
  ('56f7160e-49f2-5e96-90a9-8cde439609c9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56f7160e-49f2-5e96-90a9-8cde439609c9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7231868e-a730-556b-99bf-72e23d3ba424'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students are encouraged to monitor studies by themselves.', NULL, NULL),
  ('56f8581b-c0ac-5b7d-a473-cdf279cd34c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '56f8581b-c0ac-5b7d-a473-cdf279cd34c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Navigational Abilities', E'Are animals'' innate navigational abilities universal or are they restricted to their home environments? Taking the premise to the extreme, the researchers designed a set of wheels under a goldfish tank with a camera system to record and translate the fish''s movements into forward and back and side to side directions to the wheels.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5703767e-2f22-5096-a931-a166250098b0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5703767e-2f22-5096-a931-a166250098b0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Subway', E'Last week we looked at urban regeneration and some of the consequences of this, one of which was the relocation of people from urban to suburban areas, to, er, to largely allow them a better standard of living - because housing is cheaper in the suburbs, so they have more disposable income. But they have to commute, and commuters need rapid transport to get them from A to B. So subway construction is, well, it''s booming in some parts of the world - it''s clearly being seen as the ''answer'' to the type of migration that I''ve just mentioned. It often gets huge public support because - well - if a subway''s going to help you have a better lifestyle. Then what''s there to argue about. Well, quite a lot actually. For a start, in order to go ahead with a major project of this kind you need to be absolutely sure that the ground, and more to the point, what lies beneath the ground, can support underground transport. And to address questions like that, engineers have to be really experienced,really knowledgeable about the local area,water levels,land formation and so on. And those key issues are what I want to focus on today. Passengers don''t think about construction, they trust other, better qualified people to do it for them,and governments have to choose these people very carefully.\n\nWhich aspects of subway construction will the speaker talk about in this lecture?', '36b3244f-4b44-50cc-868f-3159df8c700e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'geological conditions\nemploying professionals', NULL, NULL),
  ('57041f97-2d5b-51c5-94de-fda881aab359'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '57041f97-2d5b-51c5-94de-fda881aab359'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a6cc8ab6-32bf-5b00-b394-d242844c6561'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some students prefer to learn by images and pictures.', NULL, NULL),
  ('571390e1-cd7b-5dff-af6b-d2f2a940003b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '571390e1-cd7b-5dff-af6b-d2f2a940003b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marie Curie', NULL, '6d40e012-9949-58d5-ad2e-c7ecb9717cb0'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, we celebrate the life of Marie Curie, a woman whose brilliance in the realm of science illuminates the path for researchers and dreamers alike. She was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize and the only person to win in two different scientific fields. Curie''s relentless pursuit of knowledge led to the discovery of two elements, polonium and radium. Her work not only expanded the boundaries of our understanding of radioactivity but also laid the groundwork for developing treatments for cancer. Despite facing societal barriers, her dedication to science never wavered. Marie Curie''s legacy teaches us the power of perseverance and the impact of unwavering dedication to one''s passion. Her story is a testament to the fact that relentless curiosity and resilience can break through the barriers of gender and social conventions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5716ea06-49f6-543b-b8b0-60fe93d1cbb3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5716ea06-49f6-543b-b8b0-60fe93d1cbb3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Giant Exoplanets', E'Giant exoplanets, like the so-called ''hot Jupiters'' that are similar in {{1}} to the solar system''s biggest {{2}} and orbit very close to their host stars, are excellent targets for {{3}} in their search for their extrasolar worlds. The size and proximity of these planets is easy to {{4}} as they create a large decrease in brightness when passing in front of their parent stars.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.characteristics, 2.planet, 3.astronomers, 4.detect', NULL, NULL),
  ('5717fe46-9e4f-5669-b10f-7b3bc34634e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5717fe46-9e4f-5669-b10f-7b3bc34634e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '108e1957-d35f-56e7-a3a1-a0a91f92900e'::uuid, NULL, E'If you need a part-time job, it should not interfere with your studies.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('57201483-662d-5633-a72c-e2bd979f4aac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '57201483-662d-5633-a72c-e2bd979f4aac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dog Emotion', E'Can dogs tell when we are happy, sad or angry? As a dog owner, I feel {{1}} not only that I can tell what kind of {{2}} state my pets are in, but also that they respond to my emotions. Yet as a hard-headed scientist, I try to take a more {{3}} and pragmatic view. These {{4}} observations seem more likely to result from my desire for a good relationship with my dogs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.confident, 2.emotional, 3.rational, 4.personal', NULL, NULL),
  ('57209b81-0bc4-5666-b201-9d443dfd4832'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '57209b81-0bc4-5666-b201-9d443dfd4832'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '96664c8b-91e5-57c0-963f-df833b30db7e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The Industrial Revolution in Europe was driven by steam technology.', NULL, NULL),
