  ('586d7757-8eae-5a99-82dd-d16bb48b584b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '586d7757-8eae-5a99-82dd-d16bb48b584b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bad Media', E'Internet or media is bad for young people because they make the young generation poor in communication and forming relationships. Do you agree with this opinion? Please use examples or your personal experience to support your idea.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('58721238-379e-59b6-850a-b09dc1ba229e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '58721238-379e-59b6-850a-b09dc1ba229e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aaron Sorkin', E'Aaron Sorkin is a renowned screenwriter and playwright known for his distinctive style of writing and his ability to craft compelling narratives that captivate audiences. With numerous successful projects to his name, Sorkin has made a significant impact on the world of film and television. One of Sorkin''s most celebrated works is "The West Wing," a political drama series that ran from 1999 to 2006. The show received critical acclaim for its sharp writing, witty dialogue, and realistic portrayal of the inner workings of the White House. Sorkin''s scripts for "The West Wing" earned him multiple Emmy Awards and cemented his reputation as a masterful storyteller. Another notable achievement in Sorkin''s career is his work on "The Social Network," a 2010 film that explores the founding of Facebook. The film''s screenplay, written by Sorkin, received widespread acclaim and won him an Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay. "The Social Network" is praised for its sharp dialogue and its portrayal of the complexities of modern entrepreneurship and technology. Sorkin''s recent film, "Molly''s Game," released in 2017, marked his directorial debut. The movie tells the true story of Molly Bloom, an Olympic-class skier who ran high-stakes poker games for the rich and famous. Sorkin''s script for "Molly''s Game" was lauded for its fast-paced storytelling and dynamic characters. What sets Sorkin apart as a screenwriter is his ability to tackle complex subjects and create characters with depth and nuance. His distinctive dialogue style, characterized by rapid-fire exchanges and intelligent banter, has become a hallmark of his work. In conclusion, Aaron Sorkin is a prolific and influential screenwriter whose works, such as "The West Wing," "The Social Network," and "Molly''s Game," have left an indelible mark on the world of film and television. His talent for crafting engaging narratives and memorable characters continues to captivate audiences and inspire fellow writers in the industry.', NULL, NULL, E'Acclaimed screenwriter Aaron Sorkin, celebrated for his masterful storytelling and distinctive dialogue style, has left an indelible mark on the film and television industry with works like "The West Wing," "The Social Network," and "Molly''s Game," showcasing his ability to tackle complex subjects and create compelling characters that continue to captivate audiences and inspire fellow writers in the field.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('58726d1b-76a5-551d-9880-81b7d9ab2362'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '58726d1b-76a5-551d-9880-81b7d9ab2362'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Jupiter', E'Europe is set to {{1}} the elite club of exascale computing next year, with the completion of JUPITER, a supercomputer that can perform a billion billion operations per second. JUPITER will be hosted at the Jülich Supercomputing Centre in Germany, and will enable simulations and experiments that are currently only possible on a few machines in the US and China. The exascale supercomputer will use a modular architecture, {{2}} of several interconnected modules with different hardware and software configurations. This will allow JUPITER to {{3}} to different scientific and industrial applications, such as climate modeling, materials science, quantum computing, and artificial intelligence. JUPITER will also be {{4}} with other European supercomputing and data infrastructures, such as the European Open Science Cloud and the European Data Infrastructure.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.join, 2.consisting, 3.adapt, 4.integrated', NULL, NULL),
  ('5873d61c-e0b8-56a5-9621-7c3f15ecbd36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5873d61c-e0b8-56a5-9621-7c3f15ecbd36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '01649660-5032-53ff-8efe-4fbbc92497e4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Unfortunately, the microscope in the biology lab got broken by accident.', NULL, NULL),
  ('5881182d-9f87-5769-bfa6-2047aed41977'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5881182d-9f87-5769-bfa6-2047aed41977'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Puzzles', E'You may have heard that puzzles and other brain games sharpen your mind—boosting memory, attention span, thinking speed, creativity and problem-solving skills—and that may or may not be true. (Scientists can’t agree.) But we do know that they’re loads of fun and a great way to stay engaged and entertained.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('58823213-05c1-563b-b881-2037b4b057dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '58823213-05c1-563b-b881-2037b4b057dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a domesticated bird raised for its eggs or meat?', 'fb3682b0-8faa-5fd8-bad1-94c7c399cdd1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Chicken', NULL, NULL),
  ('5885b778-7584-5392-9095-f46ecadf04e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5885b778-7584-5392-9095-f46ecadf04e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Human Traits', E'The age-old question of whether human traits are determined by nature or nurture has been answered, a team of researchers say. Their conclusion? It''s a draw. By collating almost every twin study across the world from the past 50 years, researchers determined that the average variation for human traits and disease is 49 percent due to genetic factors and 51 percent due to environmental factors.\nUniversity of Queensland researcher Beben Benyamin from the Queensland Brain Institute collaborated with researchers at VU University of Amsterdam to collate 2,748 studies involving more than 14.5 million pairs of twins. "Twin studies have been conducted for more than 50 years but there is still some debate in terms of how much the variation is due to genetic or environmental factors," Benyamin said.\nHe said the study showed the conversation should move away from nature versus nurture, instead looking at how the two work together. "Both are important sources of variation between individuals," he said. While the studies averaged an almost even split between nature and nurture, there was wide variation within the 17,800 separate traits and diseases examined by the studies. For example, the risk for bipolar disorder was found to be 68 percent due to genetics and only 32 percent due to environmental factors. Weight maintenance was 63 percent due to genetics and 37 percent due to environmental factors. In contrast, risk for eating disorders was found to be 40 percent genetic and 60 percent environmental, whereas the risk for mental and behavioral disorders due to use of alcohol was 41 percent genetic and 59 percent environmental.\nBenyamin said in psychiatric, ophthalmological and skeletal traits, genetic factors were a larger influence than environmental factors. But for social values and attitudes it was the other way around.', NULL, NULL, E'The average variation for human traits and disease is 49 percent due to genetic factors and 51 percent due to environmental factors, as both nature and nurture are important sources of variation between individuals, and in psychiatric, ophthalmological and skeletal traits, genetic factors were a larger influence than environmental factors, while for social values and attitudes it was the other way around.', NULL, 5, 75),
