  ('599c9908-797c-5fbb-8668-64b2f0c0226f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '599c9908-797c-5fbb-8668-64b2f0c0226f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Roman People', E'The Roman people had at first been inclined to regard the French Revolution with either indifference or {{1}} . But as the months went by and the {{2}} who remained in the city were less and less {{3}} of an early return home, the mood of the Romans became increasingly antagonistic towards the ''assassins of Paris''.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.derision, 2.emigres, 3.hopeful', NULL, NULL),
  ('59a0cc1f-cfff-58ee-8c44-5168b129c324'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '59a0cc1f-cfff-58ee-8c44-5168b129c324'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Personalized Medicine', E'The field of personalized medicine, an approach that tailors medical treatment to the individual characteristics of each patient, has made significant strides in recent years, revolutionizing the way we approach healthcare. This innovative medical model takes into account differences in people''s genes, environments, and lifestyles, moving away from the traditional "one-size-fits-all" approach to treatment. Central to this advancement is the integration of genomic medicine, which utilizes genetic information to guide the diagnosis and treatment of diseases. For instance, cancer therapy has been transformed by personalized medicine, allowing doctors to select treatments based on the genetic makeup of an individual''s tumor. This approach can increase the efficacy of treatment while reducing side effects, as medications can be tailored to how a patient''s body will likely respond. Another key aspect of personalized medicine is the use of biomarkers - biological molecules found in blood, other body fluids, or tissues - which provide a snapshot of a person''s health. Biomarkers can predict the risk of disease, confirm a diagnosis, or monitor the progress of treatment, thereby improving patient care. Personalized medicine also extends to preventive health. With genetic testing, individuals can understand their susceptibility to certain diseases and take proactive steps to prevent them. This approach not only enhances patient outcomes but also can lead to cost savings in the healthcare system by reducing unnecessary treatments and hospitalizations. In conclusion, personalized medicine represents a paradigm shift in healthcare. By focusing on the individual''s unique genetic and biological makeup, it offers a more effective, efficient, and patient-centered approach to diagnosis and treatment. As research and technology continue to advance, personalized medicine is set to play an increasingly vital role in the future of healthcare.', NULL, NULL, E'Personalized medicine, leveraging genomic data and biomarkers, revolutionizes healthcare by tailoring treatments to individual genetic profiles, significantly enhancing the efficacy of therapies like cancer treatment, improving preventive health strategies, and offering a more efficient, patient-centered approach to healthcare management.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('59aa193d-8d4d-5524-9e7b-e3e03de50afb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '59aa193d-8d4d-5524-9e7b-e3e03de50afb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ada Lovelace', E'Ada Lovelace was born in London in 1815. Her father was the famous poet Lord Byron, but it was her mother''s love for math that influenced Ada the most, leading her down a path of scientific {{1}} rare for women of her time. As a child, Ada was fascinated by machines and mathematics. This interest led her to work with Charles Babbage, a mathematician and inventor who created early designs for a computing machine called the Analytical Engine. Ada {{2}} the potential of Babbage''s machine beyond simple number crunching. She wrote detailed notes explaining how the machine could follow a {{3}} of steps to solve problems, which is the basis of computer programming. They included what {{4}} consider the first-ever computer program, making her the world''s first computer programmer. She imagined a future where computers could create music and art, showing incredible {{5}} into their possibilities. Ada Lovelace''s work laid the foundation for the computers we use today, proving that great ideas can shape the future.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.inquiry, 2.saw, 3.series, 4.many, 5.foresight', NULL, NULL),
  ('59b6d9c0-f271-5607-a651-3e1cccd31811'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '59b6d9c0-f271-5607-a651-3e1cccd31811'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a picture sent from the post office without an envelope?', '9e9c1720-c8ed-51c1-86a5-31be3320f3ad'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Postcard', NULL, NULL),
