  ('5cc5475b-d064-58a8-816f-0dbf76c45973'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cc5475b-d064-58a8-816f-0dbf76c45973'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which one is used to describe things connected with the mind, mental or physical?', 'c6b82651-9f5e-557f-a3a1-1adf1a98ad7d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mental', NULL, NULL),
  ('5cc5f65e-a05b-5fa5-8cf4-2e586894977a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cc5f65e-a05b-5fa5-8cf4-2e586894977a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Panda(熊猫)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 2, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('5cc6da20-9c34-521a-89bf-0e904f2edae0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cc6da20-9c34-521a-89bf-0e904f2edae0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bear', E'Because of their protected status, a lot of bears have lost their fear of people. This may make them appear tame, but they''re still potentially very dangerous. Bears are wild animals. One or two bear attacks occur each year in glacier park. The majority of attacks occur because people have surprised the bear. What should we do? If we surprise a bear? You should try to avoid encounters in the first place by being alert and make noise. Talk loud. Holler. Bears will usually move out of the way. If they hear people approaching, some people say to carry bells or put bells on your pack. Most bells, even the so called bear bells, are not loud enough. Calling out or clapping hands at regular intervals are better ways to make your presence known. But isn''t it kind of rude to make a lot of noise in the woods? I mean people go there for peace and quiet. In bear country, noise is good for you. Hiking quietly endangers you, the bear and other hikers. People sometimes assume they don''t have to make noise while hiking on a well used trail. Some of the most frequently used trails in glacier park are surrounded by excellent bear habitat. You can''t predict when and where theirs might appear along a trail.\n\nWhich situations should hikers avoid?', 'e3dbc94f-883b-54a5-8f18-d29c148f6f3c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Approaching a bear\nHiking when it is dark', NULL, NULL),
  ('5cca5763-0b23-5957-a83d-ae82a57e2d32'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cca5763-0b23-5957-a83d-ae82a57e2d32'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Quick Learning', E'With the help of technology, students nowadays can learn more information and learn it more quickly. Do you agree or disagree with the statement?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s digital age, technology has become an integral part of education, revolutionizing the way students learn. It is undeniable that with the help of technology, students nowadays can access and absorb a vast amount of information more efficiently than ever before. This essay will explore three key reasons why I agree with the statement that technology enables students to learn more information and learn it more quickly.\nFirstly, technology provides students with unprecedented access to information. With a few clicks, students can explore a vast array of online resources, such as e-books, research databases, and educational websites. Unlike traditional learning methods, technology eliminates geographical limitations and time constraints, allowing students to learn at their own pace and convenience. This accessibility to a wealth of information empowers students to delve deeper into subjects that interest them, broadening their knowledge and fostering a love for lifelong learning.\nSecondly, technology facilitates personalized and interactive learning experiences. Educational software and online platforms offer adaptive learning algorithms that tailor content to individual student needs. Through interactive videos, simulations, and quizzes, students can engage in hands-on learning experiences that cater to their unique learning styles. This personalized approach not only enhances comprehension but also promotes critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Moreover, collaborative tools enable students to connect with peers from around the world, fostering a global perspective and encouraging cultural exchange.\nIn conclusion, the integration of technology in education has undoubtedly revolutionized the learning process for students. By providing easy access to vast amounts of information, promoting personalized learning experiences, and fostering collaboration, technology enables students to learn more information and learn it more quickly.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('5ccae1a4-be58-5941-a78f-1c43f240c8a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5ccae1a4-be58-5941-a78f-1c43f240c8a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8eec70a3-eb55-50f7-aabc-c712b90abf00'::uuid, NULL, E'Professor Smith will be late for today''s lecture.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
