  ('5cf2950a-9902-5b84-9e53-e99ae1fc4748'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cf2950a-9902-5b84-9e53-e99ae1fc4748'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pig-nosed Turtle', E'Scientists have discovered a five-million-year-old pig-nosed turtle fossil in Melbourne, thousands of kilometers south of their typical home. Pig-nosed turtles tend to be found in tropical freshwater ecosystems in northern Australia and New Guinea, only arriving here a few thousand years ago. The creatures are now endangered and the sole survivors of an extinct group of tropical turtles from the northern hemisphere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5cfc2d4a-27e7-5544-b03f-6f2e62ed24a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cfc2d4a-27e7-5544-b03f-6f2e62ed24a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '00cfd7da-0f7b-535a-97c8-0f0fc216c9f5'::uuid, NULL, E'Too much irrelevant information made me feel overwhelmed and confused.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5cff377d-0a8d-56c9-8fcb-d85a0ee6c8ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5cff377d-0a8d-56c9-8fcb-d85a0ee6c8ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '03ed6fb6-7016-598e-9369-d923b0de3d0a'::uuid, NULL, E'At present, I brim with a newfound sense of confidence and optimism.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d015581-477f-5651-9d84-a0d8388af1d4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d015581-477f-5651-9d84-a0d8388af1d4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Trees', E'Trees have developed intricate {{1}} to maintain a balanced structure. As they grow, they naturally {{2}} rid of branches that become redundant, usually due to lack of light or resources. This process is vital for the tree''s overall health, ensuring that only productive branches {{3}} . In drier regions, trees may {{4}} branches to conserve water. Additionally, some species use this as a means of propagation, with fallen branches taking {{5}} in new locations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.methods, 2.get, 3.remain, 4.shed, 5.root', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d01eace-01da-59b6-8b28-76ef40b1bdcb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d01eace-01da-59b6-8b28-76ef40b1bdcb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Emergence', NULL, '03ba39e8-5488-5f27-b397-143abd5812fe'::uuid, NULL, E'An ant is pretty stupid. It doesn’t have much of a brain, no will, no plan, and yet, many ants together are smart. An ant colony can construct complex structures. Some colonies keep farms of fungi, others take care of cattle. They can wage war or defend themselves. How is this possible? How can a bunch of stupid things do smart things together? This phenomenon is called emergence, and it’s one of the most fascinating and mysterious features of our universe. In a nutshell, it describes small things forming bigger things that have different properties than the sum of their parts. Emergence is complexity arising from simplicity, and emergence is everywhere. Water has vastly different properties to the molecules that make it up, like the concept of wetness. Take wet fabric, If you zoom in far enough, there is no wetness. There are just molecules sitting in the spaces between the atoms of the cloth. Wetness is an emerging property of water. Something new only created by a lot of individual interactions between water molecules. And this is sort of it. Many things interact under a certain set of rules, creating something above and beyond themselves.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d05e823-35ba-53ff-8ac8-becc8816c071'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d05e823-35ba-53ff-8ac8-becc8816c071'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Demands of Work', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 2, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d083d2e-6f40-520f-86ce-fde0daa34dc1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d083d2e-6f40-520f-86ce-fde0daa34dc1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Iphone', E'All of this suggests that our relationship to our phones might not be sufficiently intellectualized, which is why Brian Merchant’s book comes as a {{1}} . Like the best historians, Merchant, an American journalist and editor of Vice Media’s technology blog, Motherboard, {{2}} the history of the iPhone in a way that makes it seem both inevitable in its outline and {{3}} in its details.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.relief, 2.unpacks, 3.surprising', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d0d08c3-eac4-5c14-8501-031de8eaeb06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d0d08c3-eac4-5c14-8501-031de8eaeb06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a0792903-d46b-5412-81b9-411c154c8a1f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'These graduate students have been advised to seek other mentors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d0eaf8c-23d1-5565-9e1b-b53001828475'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d0eaf8c-23d1-5565-9e1b-b53001828475'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bf9317a4-ec81-5190-9c6b-15f6b36edbd5'::uuid, NULL, E'Students are allowed to bring dictionaries to the exam.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d1ca105-6623-525f-ab22-c66233acb11b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d1ca105-6623-525f-ab22-c66233acb11b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Collective Behavior', E'Animal collective behavior {{1}} itself in often-mesmerizing visual displays of swarming insects, flocks of birds in flight, and schools of fish pulsating underwater as a single unit. Now, researchers report they''ve found a possible reason for a {{2}} display of collective behavior from fish shoals in sulfur springs in Mexico: deterring predators. Behavioral ecologist Juliane Lukas explains to The Scientist that sulfur mollies gather in large shoals at the surface of the low-oxygen springs to avoid hypoxia. There, they''re {{3}} for the picking by predators such as kingfishers, kiskadees, and other birds. When presented with a threatening stimulus, these ''carpets of fish'', as Lukas describes them, repeatedly {{4}} the water in a wave-like fashion by diving down for a few seconds, triggering their neighbors to mimic their diving behavior. Lukas and her colleagues decided to investigate why.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reveals, 2.peculiar, 3.ripe, 4.disturb', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d201b40-66c0-5425-9307-aaccf80796b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d201b40-66c0-5425-9307-aaccf80796b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7a06b956-00bf-5b36-a7de-8be5d31ff155'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Rise in temperature is changing the wildlife population.', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d240712-83e1-58b1-aab4-95551645b59c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d240712-83e1-58b1-aab4-95551645b59c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Age of Exploration', E'The Age of Exploration in the 15th and 16th centuries saw European explorers travel around the world in search of new trade routes and territories. While this era brought about many significant advances in science, navigation, and cartography, it also had negative consequences like colonization and exploitation of indigenous peoples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d2b64af-aaae-51cf-9d79-7e6e431eaeed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d2b64af-aaae-51cf-9d79-7e6e431eaeed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b59ce056-5397-5a53-b724-71bb73ce133b'::uuid, NULL, E'We must let clients know about upcoming price increases in advance.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d36e2d7-fe6b-5d7b-9d2e-e74ddb8c8f2f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d36e2d7-fe6b-5d7b-9d2e-e74ddb8c8f2f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Notre-Dame Cathedral', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 4, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('5d3e87e1-c931-5611-82e9-e81a6131941b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d3e87e1-c931-5611-82e9-e81a6131941b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aging', NULL, '2ba1c219-220e-506c-ab75-7b85f1f37b59'::uuid, NULL, E'In 1997, a French woman named Jeanne Calment passed away after 122 years and 164 days on this Earth, making her the oldest known person in history. Her age was so astounding that a millionaire pledged $1 million to anyone who could break her record. But in reality, living to this age or beyond is a feat that very few, maybe even no humans, are likely to accomplish. Human bodies just aren’t built for extreme aging. Our capacity is set at about 90 years. But what does aging really mean and how does it counteract the body’s efforts to stay alive? We know intuitively what it means to age. For some, it means growing up, while for others, it’s growing old. Yet finding a strict scientific definition of aging is a challenge. What we can say is that aging occurs when intrinsic processes and interactions with the environment, like sunlight, and toxins in the air, water, and our diets, cause changes in the structure and function of the body’s molecules and cells. Those changes in turn drive their decline, and subsequently, the failure of the whole organism. The exact mechanisms of aging are poorly understood. But recently, scientists have identified nine physiological traits, ranging from genetic changes to alterations in a cell’s regenerative ability that play a central role.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d4b0877-2ce7-5740-9618-4c7e80e57a69'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d4b0877-2ce7-5740-9618-4c7e80e57a69'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a1df6455-f8b2-5009-ae18-a70f8822e57e'::uuid, NULL, E'What is the best possible way to get the work permit for this job?', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d5be6f4-b59a-562c-86b2-f5aaf1a9d142'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d5be6f4-b59a-562c-86b2-f5aaf1a9d142'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Melanin', NULL, '9adc89aa-f0ce-5fa4-af0a-0559d996337a'::uuid, NULL, E'Sunscreen as we know it today didn’t exist 50,000 years ago. So how did our ancestors cope with this onslaught of UV? The key to survival lay in their own personal sunscreen manufactured beneath the skin: melanin. The type and amount of melanin in your skin determines whether you’ll be more or less protected from the sun. This comes down to the skin’s response as sunlight strikes it. When it’s exposed to UV light, that triggers special light-sensitive receptors called rhodopsin, which stimulate the production of melanin to shield cells from damage. For light-skin people, that extra melanin darkens their skin and produces a tan. Over the course of generations, humans living at the Sun-saturated latitudes in Africa adapted to have a higher melanin production threshold and more eumelanin, giving skin a darker tone. This built-in sun shield helped protect them from melanoma, likely making them evolutionarily fitter and capable of passing this useful trait on to new generations.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d68c51f-a4d0-539c-ae9f-fdc7137d691d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d68c51f-a4d0-539c-ae9f-fdc7137d691d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7c146144-b427-5d5b-9d07-c324575e3cf0'::uuid, NULL, E'The public has a right to know what is contained in the report.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5d696cf7-5d94-581d-b845-0204278c1f41'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '5d696cf7-5d94-581d-b845-0204278c1f41'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Health and Wellness', E'In the pursuit of holistic well-being, self-care becomes an act of self-love. It is a gentle reminder to nourish the body, mind, and soul. From mindful meditation that calms the racing thoughts to nourishing meals that fuel vitality, each choice becomes a step towards a healthier, happier life. Embracing self-care is an empowering journey of self-discovery, where one finds balance, inner peace, and a renewed sense of purpose.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
