  ('602584e8-eec5-5cab-b7fd-77b17721011d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '602584e8-eec5-5cab-b7fd-77b17721011d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd3b37921-6559-521e-91aa-c02d5729865f'::uuid, NULL, E'This program is running in partnership with a number of departments.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('602fcc14-4cec-528f-bc04-3b1365d6cf75'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '602fcc14-4cec-528f-bc04-3b1365d6cf75'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alcohol', E'Most people are aware that excessive and chronic drinking can {{1}} impact their physical and mental health, but the exact effects will depend on the amount of alcohol {{2}} and how frequently someone drinks it. This can lead to {{3}} coordination, slurred speech, slowed reflexes and blackouts. Heavy drinking can lead to other problems such as sleep {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.severely, 2.consumed, 3.impaired, 4.disturbances', NULL, NULL),
  ('603811b0-4aec-5aa4-a51a-9cca2c918b4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '603811b0-4aec-5aa4-a51a-9cca2c918b4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the professional who prepares and dispenses prescribed medications?', '9b743907-e0b5-5bb5-8b9c-7cada088b321'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pharmacist', NULL, NULL),
  ('6039ad21-6d96-53cc-a65f-0c013b3e88e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6039ad21-6d96-53cc-a65f-0c013b3e88e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0ce6047a-d77a-5b7b-b73c-bb280bdc879c'::uuid, NULL, E'Please explain what the author means by sustainability.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('603b4d85-feeb-52cb-a8d7-ff894bf467ed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '603b4d85-feeb-52cb-a8d7-ff894bf467ed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'British Columbia', NULL, 'af427da1-0f22-5dfe-bbb3-bb6f5f18ef01'::uuid, NULL, E'British Columbia is the third largest Canadian provinces, both in area and population. It is nearly 1.5 times as large as Texas, and extends 800 miles(1,280km) north from the United States border. It includes Canada''s entire west coast and the islands just off the coast.\nMost of British Columbia is mountainous, with long rugged ranges running north and south. Even the coastal islands are the remains of a mountain range that existed thousands of years ago. During the last Ice Age, this range was scoured by glaciers until most of it was beneath the sea. Its peaks now show as islands scattered along the coast.\nThe southwestern coastal region has a humid mild marine climate. Sea winds that blow inland from the west are warmed by a current of warm water that flows through the Pacific Ocean. As a result, winter temperatures average above freezing and summers are mild. These warm western winds also carry moisture from the ocean.\nInland from the coast, the winds from the Pacific meet the mountain barriers of the coastal ranges and the Rocky Mountains. As they rise to cross the mountains, the winds are cooled, and their moisture begins to fall as rain. On some of the western slopes almost 200 inches (500cm) of rain fall each year.\nMore than half of British Columbia is heavily forested. On mountain slopes that receive plentiful rainfall, huge Douglas firs rise in towering columns. These forest giants often grow to be as much as 300 feet(90m) tall, with diameters up to 10 feet(3m). More lumber is produced from these trees than from any other kind of tree in North America. Hemlock, red cedar, and balsam fir are among the other trees found in British Columbia.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('604dd904-ce28-583e-b400-afa011129c06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '604dd904-ce28-583e-b400-afa011129c06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yellowstone Bison', E'Yellowstone is the only place in the United States where bison have lived continuously since prehistoric times. Yellowstone bison are exceptional because they {{1}} the nation’s largest bison population on public land. This population has thousands of individuals that are allowed to roam relatively freely over the expansive landscape of Yellowstone National Park and some nearby areas of Montana. They also {{2}} wild behavior like their ancient ancestors, congregating during the breeding season to compete for mates, as well as migration and exploration that result in the use of new habitat areas. These behaviors have enabled the successful restoration of a population that was on the {{3}} of extinction just over a century ago. However, some Yellowstone bison are infected with brucellosis, a livestock disease that can be {{4}} to wild bison and elk as well as to cattle through contact with infected fetal tissue. To prevent conflicts with ranching and other activities outside the park, the National Park Service works with other federal, state, and tribal agencies to manage and develop policies for bison access to {{5}} in Montana.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.comprise, 2.exhibit, 3.brink, 4.transmitted, 5.habitat', NULL, NULL),
  ('605baf1a-4df1-5955-98ee-24a7fe285ab8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '605baf1a-4df1-5955-98ee-24a7fe285ab8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '933d8597-23c4-5d01-a18f-33df2ca6607f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'These workbooks are available at many bookstores near our school.', NULL, NULL),
  ('605c9a25-0f6c-54d3-80fc-95adb048f3d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '605c9a25-0f6c-54d3-80fc-95adb048f3d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parkinson', E'C. Northcote Parkinson, a British writer, formulated Parkinson''s rule: "Work expands to fill the time allotted to it; or, conversely, the amount of work completed is in inverse proportion to the number of people employed." Simply said: If you have an hour to do a 5-minute job, it will take an hour to do it. A large number of people accomplish less work than a smaller number of people.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6060faa6-121e-5bcb-a047-6b36ca79fb6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6060faa6-121e-5bcb-a047-6b36ca79fb6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Italian Food', E'You are going to eat outside with your friends and they want to eat Italian food. You don''t like Italian food, but you want to dine out with them. What would you say to your friends?', 'cb32708d-1e27-5888-8436-b630945d4073'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey guys, I want to talk to you about something.\nWe seem to have a little issue with our dinner choice.\nIt''s like you want to eat Italian food, but I don''t like it, though I still want to dine out with you.\nAnd I''d like to know what you think.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('60691571-a29d-58fe-9973-878b409c0136'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '60691571-a29d-58fe-9973-878b409c0136'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Media', E'Social media are playing an increasingly important role as information sources for travelers. The goal of this study is to investigate the extent to which social media appear in search engine results in the context of travel-related searches. It also provides evidence for challenges faced by traditional providers of travel-related information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6071eff6-c7ec-5673-ac3f-df5b1664e251'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6071eff6-c7ec-5673-ac3f-df5b1664e251'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite of ending in a film or movie?', 'fdf2bb61-41a6-5b2b-b641-f5a39aa184e8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Prologue', NULL, NULL),
  ('6077c6fc-6803-56be-99d1-3b1ba588d2e5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6077c6fc-6803-56be-99d1-3b1ba588d2e5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Music', E'Music is a universal language that transcends cultural boundaries. It evokes emotions and memories, bringing people together in harmony. Whether it''s classical, pop, or rock, music has the power to inspire and uplift. It''s a form of self-expression that touches the hearts of millions worldwide.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('607dec65-ee1a-5293-afaf-486ebd7577a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '607dec65-ee1a-5293-afaf-486ebd7577a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd6c36090-0695-5cba-953b-51cdca21f7a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Next term, there will be changes to the office''s operating hours.', NULL, NULL),
  ('607f7bf0-da17-5eef-a836-70072c29f4b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '607f7bf0-da17-5eef-a836-70072c29f4b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '034fdbba-49b3-589b-bd2d-243ffad84d09'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You should plan your meetings at least two weeks before.', NULL, NULL),
  ('60800150-1300-5087-b59b-6ae2401e43ef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '60800150-1300-5087-b59b-6ae2401e43ef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High IQ', E'A smart brain might help you do well in tests, but there are many other ways it can affect your life, both positively and negatively. Exams are not the only {{1}} to success, as billionaire businessmen Richard Branson and Alan Sugar – who left school aged 15 and 16 – will attest. Nevertheless, good grades can open doors, and intelligence certainly helps when it comes to educational {{2}} . IQ test performance accounts for roughly two-thirds of the variance in people’s school exam scores – other factors including motivation and mental and physical health also influence how well children do. But intelligence isn’t just useful in school. IQ predicts how people will respond to workplace training and how well they will do their job, even in non-academic {{3}} such as being a car mechanic or carpenter. This is, perhaps, because general intelligence reflects people’s ability to handle complexity in everyday affairs. Many tasks, from supermarket shopping to juggling our diaries, require us to deal with unexpected situations, to {{4}} and make judgements and to identify and solve problems. This is true of our social interactions too.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.route, 2.attainment, 3.professions, 4.reason', NULL, NULL),
  ('60833c2b-e444-59f7-a062-8789a0e74e74'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '60833c2b-e444-59f7-a062-8789a0e74e74'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urban Landscaping', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('608c6c8d-9de3-5350-bbf1-6389f1b1f0e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '608c6c8d-9de3-5350-bbf1-6389f1b1f0e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nerd and Geek', E'Once upon a time, "nerd" and "geek" might have been playground put-downs, but now? They''re badges of {{1}} in the kingdom of cool. The journey from the shadows to the spotlight for these terms is like a plot twist in a superhero movie. "Nerd" used to conjure up images of bookworms {{2}} with grades and science, while "geek" was reserved for folks with a passionate, almost encyclopedic love for niche topics like comics or tech. Nowadays, these labels represent a deep {{3}} to one''s passions, whether that''s quantum physics or the latest Marvel saga. It''s a celebration of having the courage to dive deep into what you love, {{4}} of what the peanut gallery says. So, if you''ve ever been called a nerd or a geek, wear it like a crown; you''re royalty in the age of information and imagination.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.honor, 2.obsessed, 3.dedication, 4.regardless', NULL, NULL),
  ('608f9a71-f8d8-58c8-b2f4-d735d35a549a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '608f9a71-f8d8-58c8-b2f4-d735d35a549a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Event Management', E'Event management is particularly challenging from an operational viewpoint. In many cases, events are staged on sites where everything has been set up over a 24-hour period, with all elements carefully {{1}} .In contrast, many events are years in the planning: large convention bids are often won five years before the event is held. For the very {{2}} bidding process, budgets need to be developed and prices quoted, requiring a good understanding of market, economic and political trends, as well as consumer choices. This long-term view is the basis of strategic management, which is covered in Part 1, and focuses on the event concept, feasibility of the event, legal compliance and financial management. Marketing is a critical {{3}} factor and other important topic of this first section, many events (sporting, cultural and arts) involving long-term sponsorship {{4}} with key industry players. Relationship building is particularly {{5}} since there are so many stakeholders involved in events, including government agencies at many levels. Part 1 will look at all these aspects, including strategic risk, before moving on to the second part where operational planning and implementation will be covered in detail.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.synchronised, 2.competitive, 3.success, 4.arrangements, 5.challenging', NULL, NULL),
  ('609226df-d5ba-5acf-b7c6-7db93e1978d2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '609226df-d5ba-5acf-b7c6-7db93e1978d2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dog-assisted Interventions', E'A recent study published in the open-access journal PLOS ONE suggests that dog-assisted interventions can effectively reduce stress levels in children, regardless of whether they have special needs or not. The study, conducted by Kerstin Meints and colleagues from the University of Lincoln, UK, measured salivary cortisol levels to determine the impact of these interventions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
