  ('617093f9-295f-55a7-a096-ec56251e8a5a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '617093f9-295f-55a7-a096-ec56251e8a5a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call dollars, cents, pounds and euros?', '280c6af7-29b0-5698-bbcd-f2e34e28f62d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Currency', NULL, NULL),
  ('6170a124-21f8-5f50-8fcb-30e486885e47'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6170a124-21f8-5f50-8fcb-30e486885e47'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biosphere', E'Many people rely on the biosphere for basic {{1}} including food, medicine, construction materials, and fuel. Except for salt, all food comes from the biosphere, but established societies {{2}} to farm rather than forage. The biosphere is a relatively thin layer of the Earth’s surface that supports life, reaching from a few kilometers into the atmosphere to deep-sea vents. The biosphere is a global ecosystem made up of living organisms (biota) and the nonliving (abiotic) factors that provide them with energy and nutrients. The biosphere is a narrow zone on the surface of the earth where soil, water, and air combine to {{3}} life. Life can only occur in this zone. From fungi and bacteria to large animals, there are several different types of life. The biosphere is {{4}} as an area that contains all living organisms and the products of their activities. As a result, it plays a critical role in the {{5}} of ecosystems, i.e., the existence of species and their reciprocal interactions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.necessities, 2.prefer, 3.sustain, 4.characterized, 5.maintenance', NULL, NULL),
  ('617328d1-6b19-5d70-a5f0-938f5d6147b1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '617328d1-6b19-5d70-a5f0-938f5d6147b1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '99385d82-9dad-5318-9af5-3fd60a9d1857'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Global warming is a threat to economic growth.', NULL, NULL),
  ('61850b93-aa3d-591b-ae43-cb261d8f946b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '61850b93-aa3d-591b-ae43-cb261d8f946b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Brains or Brawn', E'While workers worry about whether robots will take their jobs, teachers are wondering how to use education to insulate the next generation from such a fate. This {{1}} before. When the last wave of automation swept the developed world at the start of the 20th century, policymakers decided education was the answer. If machines were going to substitute for brawn, they {{2}} , more people would need to use their brains. The US invested {{3}} in education, with good results. Workers reaped the benefits through better jobs and higher wages. Economists Andrew McAfee and Erik Brynjolfsson summed it up like this: ''The industrial revolution {{4}} a race between technology and education — and, for most of the 20th century, humans won that race.''', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.has worked, 2.reasoned, 3.heavily, 4.started', NULL, NULL),
  ('618ca36e-8e17-54a0-b5c4-6447616c2d88'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '618ca36e-8e17-54a0-b5c4-6447616c2d88'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '59e75f4a-f306-5ac1-a513-39cc2b260f2b'::uuid, NULL, E'The lecture tomorrow will discuss the educational policy in the United States.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
