  ('621a6109-9585-5886-9de6-168cab91e7a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '621a6109-9585-5886-9de6-168cab91e7a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What kind of knowledge do scientists believe in, subjective or objective?', '1a9e33af-ffb0-57c4-89da-784bae54ef49'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Objective', NULL, NULL),
  ('621afc74-537f-5042-b96a-3217b6b5cf54'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '621afc74-537f-5042-b96a-3217b6b5cf54'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Company Size', E'Some people prefer to work for a large company. Others prefer to work for a small company. Which would you prefer? Explain it with your own experience.', NULL, NULL, E'When it comes to choosing between working for a large or small company, I would personally prefer to work for a small company. While large companies may offer more resources and stability, small companies have their own unique advantages that make them an attractive option for many job seekers.\nFirstly, working for a small company can provide a greater sense of community and camaraderie among employees. In a smaller team, employees are more likely to know each other well and work closely together on projects. This creates a more positive work environment, which can lead to increased job satisfaction and a stronger sense of belonging. Additionally, working closely with colleagues at a small company can provide opportunities for mentorship and learning from experienced professionals.\nSecondly, working for a small company can offer more opportunities for growth and development. In a smaller organization, employees may have the chance to take on diverse responsibilities and gain experience in different areas of the business. This can lead to personal and professional growth, making it an attractive option for those seeking career development. Smaller companies may also offer greater flexibility and autonomy in the workplace, allowing employees to maintain a better work-life balance.\nIn conclusion, while large companies may offer certain advantages, working for a small company can provide a more positive work environment, greater opportunities for growth and development, and increased flexibility in the workplace. These factors make small companies an attractive option for those seeking a fulfilling and rewarding career.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('621f24c5-12e2-5d86-a10d-daf9eae51efc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '621f24c5-12e2-5d86-a10d-daf9eae51efc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cancer', E'The US cancer death rate has fallen 33 percent since 1991, which {{1}} to an estimated 3.8 million deaths averted, according to a report. The report {{2}} this steady progress to improvements in cancer treatment, drops in smoking and increases in early detection. Researchers also pointed to HPV vaccinations as {{3}} to reductions in cancer deaths.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.corresponds, 2.attributes, 3.connected', NULL, NULL),
  ('621f5c2b-81b7-510a-bc31-c213c20c0469'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '621f5c2b-81b7-510a-bc31-c213c20c0469'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '556630ea-ede2-5649-a55c-958a6c5856be'::uuid, NULL, E'The course comprises twenty hours of lectures, seminars and tutorials each week.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6222b0ab-3fb8-5d43-b22f-78143dd9863c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6222b0ab-3fb8-5d43-b22f-78143dd9863c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Edible Insects', E'Fancy a locust for lunch? Probably not, if you live in the west, but elsewhere it''s a different story. Edible insects, termites, stick insects, dragonflies, grasshoppers and giant water bugs, are on the menu for an estimated 80 percent of the world''s population. More than 1000 species of insects are served up around the world. For example, ''Kungu cakes'', made from midges, are a {{1}} in parts of Africa. Mexico is an insect-eating, or entomophagous - hotspot, where more than 200 insect species are consumed. {{2}} is so high that 40 species are now under threat, including white agave worms. These caterpillars of the tequila giant-skipper butterfly {{3}} around $250 a kilogram. Eating insects makes nutritional sense. Some contain more protein than meat or fish. The female gypsy moth, for instance, is about 80 percent protein. Insects can be a good {{4}} of vitamins and minerals too: a type of caterpillar (Usta Terpsichore) eaten in Angola is rich in iron, zinc, and thiamine. What do they taste like? Ants have a lemon tang, apparently, whereas giant water bugs taste of mint and fire ant pupae of watermelon. You have probably, inadvertently, already tasted some of these things, as insects are often accidental tourists in other types of food. The US Food and Drug Administration even issues guidelines for the number of insect parts allowed in certain foods. For example, it is acceptable for 225 grams of macaroni to contain up to 225 insect fragments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.delicacy, 2.Demand, 3.fetch, 4.source', NULL, NULL),
  ('6230732b-b665-55ee-b8e1-2f67bede83b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6230732b-b665-55ee-b8e1-2f67bede83b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Harder Objects', E'It''s common sense that some objects are harder than others. We refer to this characteristic as hardness, but what exactly is hardness? Let me tell you it''s the ability of a material to resist being damaged, scratched, or marred in any way. There''s even a way to measure it. It''s the most scale of hardness. A german scientist, um, a mineralogist named fredrick, most came up with the scale in eighteen twelve. Here''s how we made it. Most took ten different minerals, then he rated them from one to ten based on their ability to withstand damage and to damage other materials. Tell received a rating of one. It''s soft, it''s easily scratched, can hardly damage anything. Diamond received a rating of ten. It''s the hardest natural substance known to man. The other objects on this scale, that number from two to nine are gypsum, calcite, fluoride, appetite, feldspar, quartz, topaz, and corundum. I see worried looks on your faces. Don''t worry about writing them down there. Listed on page two hundred and thirty four of your text. Take a look. Now, what about the hardness of other objects? Hm. It depends on which of the ten minerals can scratch them. For instance, your fingernails get a rating of two point five on the most scale. So tell can gypsum can''t scratch them, but calcite can. Well, what are some others? Let''s see, iron is rated between four and five glasses between six and seven, and steel is close to eight.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '267931bf-5765-58b9-84e6-8c22e09c101d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mohs Scale of Hardness is created to rate minerals. Hardness refers to a material’s ability to scratch other objects and different materials are received different rank on this scale.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62312f3a-a582-5911-b464-5b12d2b2282f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62312f3a-a582-5911-b464-5b12d2b2282f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b3f55fa8-2545-54c5-8592-7139d7c6f3f2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Graduates from this course typically pursue careers in the financial sector.', NULL, NULL),
