  ('6256292d-90a2-568f-812e-b25ed1e9835a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6256292d-90a2-568f-812e-b25ed1e9835a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a system in which people are organized into different levels of importance from highest to lowest, especially in a society?', '720af4e2-06b8-501f-a128-064dea4b55d9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hierarchy', NULL, NULL),
  ('6257bcee-d38f-5ba5-ac54-e71f6b33e31d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6257bcee-d38f-5ba5-ac54-e71f6b33e31d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '699a0e61-ed0b-554c-8efd-9203043fcd3e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Newspapers are supported primarily by the sale of advertising space.', NULL, NULL),
  ('625bc3ca-ecad-55e4-8c1d-28ead747af1e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '625bc3ca-ecad-55e4-8c1d-28ead747af1e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Essential Transportation', E'To what extent do you agree that public transportation is essential for urban development?', NULL, NULL, E'Public transportation serves as a vital component that not only enhances mobility but also contributes to mitigating urban challenges. The role of public transportation in reducing traffic congestion, promoting environmental sustainability, and fostering social equity underscores its essentiality in shaping sustainable and inclusive urban environments.\nPublic transportation plays a crucial role in alleviating traffic congestion by offering a viable alternative to private vehicles. By providing efficient and accessible transit options, public transportation reduces the reliance on individual cars, easing traffic flow and congestion on urban roads. The availability of well-connected public transit systems encourages commuters to opt for sustainable modes of transportation, thereby minimizing traffic gridlock and improving overall mobility within cities.\nIn addition to easing traffic congestion, public transportation contributes significantly to environmental sustainability by curbing greenhouse gas emissions and reducing air pollution. By encouraging the use of public transit over private vehicles, cities can lower carbon footprints and combat the adverse effects of pollution on urban environments. Furthermore, public transportation plays a pivotal role in enhancing social equity by providing affordable and inclusive transportation options for all residents, regardless of socioeconomic status. Accessible and reliable public transit services ensure that communities have equal opportunities for mobility, connecting individuals to essential services, employment opportunities, and recreational activities.\nIn conclusion, public transportation is undeniably essential for urban development due to its multifaceted benefits in reducing traffic congestion, promoting environmental sustainability, and enhancing social equity. Embracing robust public transit systems not only improves the efficiency of urban transportation but also fosters sustainable growth and inclusivity within cities.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('6267ddba-b5ae-5b8a-b716-ff5039413eb7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6267ddba-b5ae-5b8a-b716-ff5039413eb7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call an animal that hunts for food or preys on other animals?', '54789b5c-9465-5f45-96f5-80565718b3ce'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Predator', NULL, NULL),
  ('626a80b7-3bb0-5708-8e14-14173a1502c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '626a80b7-3bb0-5708-8e14-14173a1502c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Regret', NULL, 'a372ab69-e920-524c-b2e3-bbef6a27029b'::uuid, NULL, E'But for these things that we actually do really care about and do experience profound regret around, what does that experience feel like? We all know the short answer. It feels terrible. Regret feels awful. But it turns out that regret feels awful in four very specific and consistent ways. So the first consistent component of regret is basically denial. When I went home that night after getting my tattoo, I basically stayed up all night. And for the first several hours, there was exactly one thought in my head. And the thought was, “Make it go away!” This is an unbelievably primitive emotional response. I mean, it’s right up there with, “I want my mommy!” We’re not trying to solve the problem. We’re not trying to understand how the problem came about. We just want it to vanish. The second characteristic component of regret is a sense of bewilderment. So the other thing I thought about there in my bedroom that night was, “How could I have done that? What was I thinking?” This real sense of alienation from the part of us that made a decision we regret. We can’t identify with that part. We don’t understand that part. And we certainly don’t have any empathy for that part — which explains the third consistent component of regret, which is an intense desire to punish ourselves. That’s why, in the face of our regret, the thing we consistently say is, “I could have kicked myself.” The fourth component here is that regret is what psychologists call perseverative. To perseverate means to focus obsessively and repeatedly on the exact same thing. Now the effect of perseveration is to basically take these first three components of regret and put them on an infinite loop. So it’s not that I sat there in my bedroom that night, thinking, “Make it go away.” It’s that I sat there and I thought, “Make it go away. Make it go away. Make it go away. Make it go away.” So if you look at the psychological literature, these are the four consistent defining components of regret.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6272e767-b442-5d23-b063-eb9117f78c5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6272e767-b442-5d23-b063-eb9117f78c5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Black Diamonds', E'An {{1}} type of diamond may have come to Earth from outer space, scientists say. Called carbonado or "black" diamonds, the {{2}} stones are found in Brazil and the Central African Republic. They are unusual for being the color of charcoal and full of frothy bubbles. The diamonds, which can {{3}} at more than 3,600 carats, can also have a face that looks like melted glass. Because of their {{4}} appearance, the diamonds are {{5}} as gemstones. But they do have industrial applications and were used in the drill bits that helped dig the Panama Canal. Now a team led by Stephen Haggerty of Florida International University in Miami has presented a new study {{6}} that the odd stones were brought to Earth by an asteroid billions of years ago. The findings were published online in the journal Astrophysical Journal Letters on December 20. The scientists exposed polished pieces of carbonado to extremely intense infrared light. The test revealed the presence of many hydrogen-carbon bonds, indicating that the diamonds probably formed in a hydrogen-rich environment—such as that found in space.\nThe diamonds also showed strong similarities to tiny Nano diamonds, which are frequently found in meteorites. "They''re not {{7}} ,” Haggerty said, "but they''re very similar." Astrophysicists, he added, have developed theories predicting that Nano diamonds form easily in the titanic stellar explosions called supernovas, which scatter debris through interstellar space. The deposits in the Central African Republic and Brazil, he said, probably come from the impact of a diamond-rich asteroid billions of years ago, when South America and Africa were joined.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exotic, 2.mysterious, 3.weigh, 4.odd, 5.unsuitable, 6.suggesting, 7.identical', NULL, NULL),
  ('627954ed-7e5d-5b87-9c09-3137ff3df628'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '627954ed-7e5d-5b87-9c09-3137ff3df628'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Would a supermarket, a cafe, or a bookstore probably have the widest range of products available?', '260033b1-6ce4-58e6-8b0a-93c6294c4b01'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A supermarket', NULL, NULL),
  ('6281fab0-bd8c-52ba-8209-e560872ef6b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6281fab0-bd8c-52ba-8209-e560872ef6b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Contexts', E'Contexts is a quarterly magazine of the American Sociological Association about society and social behavior. Directed to {{1}} interested in the latest sociological ideas and research, Contexts seeks to apply new knowledge, stimulate fresh thinking, and disseminate important information {{2}} by the discipline. The publication''s articles synthesize key findings, weave {{3}} diverse strands of work, draw out implications for policy, and debate issues of controversy. The hallmarks of Contexts are accessibility, broad appeal, and timeliness. By design, it is not a technical journal, {{4}} a magazine for diverse readers, {{5}} who wish to be current about social science knowledge, emerging trends, and their relevance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.anyone, 2.produced, 3.together, 4.but, 5.those', NULL, NULL),
  ('6283ee1c-986c-5b48-922e-4da2f4b4e48c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6283ee1c-986c-5b48-922e-4da2f4b4e48c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e953477b-e5be-5705-907c-3ea2ccc40636'::uuid, NULL, E'There is disagreement among researchers about why we dream.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6291514b-03d8-5812-a069-5c061a80da39'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6291514b-03d8-5812-a069-5c061a80da39'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If you want to find the map of U.S., what type of book should you use?', '72585d81-d636-58a6-8fd1-648e31cb0aba'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Atlas', NULL, NULL),
  ('62948183-22cd-5939-ae82-3786b254fbee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62948183-22cd-5939-ae82-3786b254fbee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Physical Books', E'Do you agree that physical books will eventually become obsolete?', NULL, NULL, E'The debate over the obsolescence of physical books in the digital age has sparked discussions on the future of reading materials. Despite technological advancements, physical books continue to hold a special place in the hearts of readers worldwide. This essay will delve into the reasons why physical books are unlikely to become obsolete.\nPhysical books offer a unique reading experience that digital formats cannot replicate. The sensation of turning pages, the smell of ink on paper, and the weight of a book in hand create a tangible connection between the reader and the text, evoking a sense of nostalgia and comfort. This tactile engagement enhances the overall reading experience and fosters a deep appreciation for the art of bookmaking.\nUnlike electronic devices, physical books do not rely on batteries or technology for reading, making them reliable and accessible at all times. Furthermore, physical books hold sentimental value as cherished collectibles that can be passed down through generations. The act of sharing a well-loved book with loved ones creates lasting memories and strengthens familial bonds, adding to the enduring appeal of physical books.\nIn conclusion, the enduring allure of physical books lies in their ability to provide a tangible reading experience, evoke nostalgia, and hold sentimental value as treasured possessions. While digital advancements have transformed the way we consume content, physical books continue to serve as enduring symbols of literary tradition and personal connection. As such, it is unlikely that physical books will fade into obsolescence, remaining valued artifacts in the realm of literature and culture.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('629f8f16-8122-57b2-af63-0b163e9e1433'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '629f8f16-8122-57b2-af63-0b163e9e1433'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is 3 quarters of 100%?', 'ac58ac8b-9831-5a07-9579-779b21f680b8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'75%', NULL, NULL),
  ('629fc9e7-39ea-5a9b-9092-1032b4e33329'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '629fc9e7-39ea-5a9b-9092-1032b4e33329'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f5fc0a95-66da-5df9-a885-d22471c92ed2'::uuid, NULL, E'The fertile plains in the east of the region provide excellent land for farming.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62a437e3-fd95-53b7-95a5-8cfead7c0328'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62a437e3-fd95-53b7-95a5-8cfead7c0328'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Active Listening', E'Active listening is a communication technique that has been around for many years and that has been used successfully in all types of {{1}} — not just business. Parenting classes, marital relationships, public schools, counseling, and tutoring are just some of the areas where active listening is a valued skill. As the name {{2}} , the focus of active listening as a tool for improving communication is on listening rather than talking. It is a process where the listener sets aside his own thoughts to concentrate more clearly what the speaker is actually saying instead of what the listener thinks the speaker is saying. It takes practice to {{3}} the basic techniques of active listening, and you will probably feel awkward applying the technique in the beginning. But because the point is to increase {{4}} by decreasing the possibility of misunderstandings, it is worth a little discomfort.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.endeavor, 2.implies, 3.master, 4.effectiveness', NULL, NULL),
  ('62a4946b-ffa4-578e-a0dc-55b335027ce4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62a4946b-ffa4-578e-a0dc-55b335027ce4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Raw Honey', E'According to Dr. Ron Fessenden, M.D., M.P.H. the average American consumes more than 150 pounds of refined sugar, plus an additional 62 pounds of high fructose corn syrup every year. In comparison, we consume only around 1.3 pounds of honey per year on average in the U.S. According to new research, if you can switch out your intake of refined sugar and use pure raw honey instead, the health benefits can be enormous.\nWhat is raw honey? It''s a pure, unfiltered and unpasteurized sweetener made by bees from the nectar of flowers. Most of the honey consumed today is processed honey that''s been heated and filtered since it was gathered from the hive. Unlike processed honey, raw honey does not get robbed of its incredible nutritional value and health powers. It can help with everything from low energy to sleep problems to seasonal allergies. Switching to raw honey may even help weight-loss efforts when compared to diets containing sugar or high fructose corn syrup. I''m excited to tell you more about one of my all-time favorite natural sweeteners today.', NULL, NULL, E'According to new research, if you can switch out your intake of defined sugar and use pure raw honey instead, the health benefits can be enormous, and unlike processesd honey, raw honey is a pure, unfiltered, and unpasteurized sweetener made by bees and does not get robbed of its incredible nutritional value and health power, which can help with low energy, sleep problems, seasonal allergies, and even weight-loss.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('62ab7cd7-16ea-5043-9a8e-08bfd8ddb0f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62ab7cd7-16ea-5043-9a8e-08bfd8ddb0f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Malaria', E'Malaria’s ability to resist drugs is one of the reasons success in eradicating it has leveled off. New ways to tackle malaria are being developed, seeking to wipe out the mosquitoes that carry the disease. A gene editing technology called CRISPR is being used to engineer a gene drive. This creates selfish genes that always passed onto offspring. The aim is to interfere the fertility by driving a gene for sterility through an entire population. As it is passed from generation to generation, the population would be swamped with insects that are unable to reproduce. In theory, they could be driven to extinction. Last year, a team at Imperial College London successfully created a gene drive that wiped out enclosed cohorts of one species of malaria-carrying mosquito. But there is no guarantee that gene drives could work in the many environments where malaria is found in the world, especially in Africa. Humanity had shown that it can control malaria. It has been eradicated in around 35 countries. Currently the best hope lies in the combination of methods. But in the future, a gene drive may be the most effective solution.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'aea332e7-8ccd-5147-947c-6e97c102d576'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Though it cannot be guaranteed that gene drives can completely eradicate malaria, they have already been proven to be effective in some parts of the world. In the future, gene drives may be the most effective solution.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62b19a92-c911-5190-bea1-97ffa8189651'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62b19a92-c911-5190-bea1-97ffa8189651'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heart Disorders', E'In the past decades, dramatic changes in diet and lifestyle have fueled a rampant increase in heart disorders. What is even more alarming is that heart conditions are no longer restricted to higher age groups, but affect young people as well. Heart disorders like strokes are the most commonly known today and its symptoms include chest pain, weakness and heart attack.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62b52b7d-b18c-5b66-87c0-e22a77c4e9db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62b52b7d-b18c-5b66-87c0-e22a77c4e9db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '86eb2682-3a73-5ea0-ad58-64956dae62e2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Lots of people still love listening to the radio.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62c6bd41-66bc-594b-995b-7a4e05efd247'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62c6bd41-66bc-594b-995b-7a4e05efd247'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the sound when people clap their hands?', 'c65652a8-bbe9-5fec-b38a-a2d7e41e5c1a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Applause', NULL, NULL),
  ('62c8366b-101a-5307-8fa2-624b881b73cf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62c8366b-101a-5307-8fa2-624b881b73cf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '503a810a-1efb-578e-ab0c-2fc1e8b0dbaa'::uuid, NULL, E'Being tired often leads to car accidents on the road.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62cb94db-e749-571b-aaa8-bf08475b28c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62cb94db-e749-571b-aaa8-bf08475b28c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Diplomas', NULL, '95e597aa-0bae-5bf8-80cd-308a0f66e559'::uuid, NULL, E'1.2 trillion dollars of debts for diplomas make it abundantly obvious that higher education is a consumer product you can buy. All of us talk about education just as the economists do now, as an investment that you make to improve the human stock by training them for work. As an investment you make to sort and classify people so that employers can hire them more easily. The U.S. News & World Report ranks colleges just as the consumer report rates washing machines. The language is peppered with barbarisms. Teachers are called “service providers,” students are called “consumers.” Sociology and Shakespeare and soccer and science, all of these are “content.” Student debt is profitable. Only not on you. Your debt fattens the profit of the student loan industry. The two 800-pound gorillas of which — Sallie Mae and Navient — posted last year a combined profit of 1.2 billion dollars. And just like home mortgages, student loans can be bundled and packaged and sliced and diced, and sold on Wall Street. And colleges and universities that invest in these securitized loans profit twice. Once from your tuition, and then again from the interest on debt. With all that money to be made, are we surprised that some in the higher education business have begun to engage in false advertising, in bait and switch in exploiting the very ignorance that they pretend to educate.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62d1100d-7084-5bbe-8853-10e7d01df0ee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62d1100d-7084-5bbe-8853-10e7d01df0ee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4a710651-47ea-53ca-887b-4dbe8d34fc79'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The change of policy will have a great effect on society.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62d4ae4e-7d00-5a7a-b5bc-0e1ccb661f4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62d4ae4e-7d00-5a7a-b5bc-0e1ccb661f4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Sessions', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('62d791e0-c197-55df-b8bb-d52d3fb3bb6c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62d791e0-c197-55df-b8bb-d52d3fb3bb6c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Financial Institutions', E'The economic {{1}} of globalization involves international financial institutions i.e. the IMF & WB. Stabilization and adjustment are sponsored by the two respectively and are rooted in the ideology of the free market. At the other end of the spectrum, protesters see globalization in a very different light than the treasury secretary of the United States, or the finance or trade ministers of most of the advanced industrial countries. The difference in {{2}} is so great that one wonders, are the protesters and the policy makers talking about the same {{3}} ? Are they looking at the same data? Are the visions of those in {{4}} so clouded by special and particular {{5}} ?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dimension, 2.views, 3.phenomenon, 4.power, 5.interests', NULL, NULL),
  ('62d911f2-6c32-5381-8d7d-84fb19a2fdba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62d911f2-6c32-5381-8d7d-84fb19a2fdba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '13eb5475-5794-5656-ac33-f75e8e1f64bd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The class schedule gives you lots of time to study alone.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62da520e-22d1-5414-b48c-91d0a495f847'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62da520e-22d1-5414-b48c-91d0a495f847'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Rising', E'The great advantage of early rising is the head start it gives us in our day''s work. The early riser has done a large amount of hard work before other men even get out of bed. In the early morning, the mind is fresh, and there are few sounds or other distractions. In many cases, the early riser also finds time to take some exercise in the fresh morning air.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62de7fe9-9935-5b27-a37c-67b8d499c47d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62de7fe9-9935-5b27-a37c-67b8d499c47d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Agricultural Science', E'While advances in agricultural science have always been critical to ensuring we help feed the world, its impact and importance is even greater now, as population grows at a rapid rate and the availability of arable land steadily declines. Science and technology solutions are essential to meeting growing demand for food, maintaining market competitiveness and adapting to land mitigating risks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('62e20176-d75b-588b-b963-18cc5a81106f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62e20176-d75b-588b-b963-18cc5a81106f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f34183a5-a994-5f1f-bfb1-2c8e9fdc1bcf'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sugar is a solid carbohydrate which is used to sweeten food.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62e66651-e2a3-50a5-8083-fdcde587a8d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62e66651-e2a3-50a5-8083-fdcde587a8d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Light Pollution', E'The widespread use of artificial light in modern societies means that light pollution is an increasingly common feature of the environments humans inhabit. This type of pollution is {{1}} high in coastal regions of tropic and temperate zones, as these are areas of high rates of human population growth and settlement. Light pollution is a threat for many species that inhabit these locations, particularly those whose ecology or behaviour depends, {{2}} , on natural cycles of light and dark. Artificial light is known to have detrimental effects on the ecology of sea turtles, particularly at the hatchling stage when they emerge from nests on natal beaches and head towards the sea. Under natural conditions, turtles hatch predominantly\nat night (although some early morning and late afternoon emergences occur) and show an innate and well-directed orientation to the water, {{3}} mostly on light cues that attract them toward the brighter horizon above the sea surface. Artificial lighting on beaches is strongly attractive to hatchlings and can cause them {{4}} the sea and {{5}} with their ability to orient in a constant direction. Ultimately, this disorientation due to light pollution can lead to death of hatchlings from exhaustion, dehydration and predation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exceptionally, 2.in some way, 3.relying, 4.to move away from, 5.interfere', NULL, NULL),
  ('62e9ec16-0131-56fa-93ed-90d23a985189'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62e9ec16-0131-56fa-93ed-90d23a985189'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the leafy green vegetable high in iron, often used in smoothies and salads?', '01431926-82a3-5fc5-a74f-3aad4f587609'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Spinach', NULL, NULL),
  ('62ed63c4-13c0-5d99-9cc6-c9ed0277e426'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62ed63c4-13c0-5d99-9cc6-c9ed0277e426'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2c1155ce-f344-5c82-82eb-aa9a003eb527'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Remember to sign the attendance register before leaving the lecture hall.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62f57f86-870f-55d2-903c-71cfa4389e7c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62f57f86-870f-55d2-903c-71cfa4389e7c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What historical period came after the Middle Ages in Europe?', '6a39116c-fcb0-54c4-85a5-47c5ffddb7df'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Renaissance', NULL, NULL),
  ('62fca40f-3b7d-5408-9f3c-46b04d4a2ec9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62fca40f-3b7d-5408-9f3c-46b04d4a2ec9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cc577d9e-adc8-54ca-aa93-df16e1f62854'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Field trips are an essential part of most geography courses.', NULL, NULL),
  ('62feb939-a21a-5887-aa31-62aa053715eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '62feb939-a21a-5887-aa31-62aa053715eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e2491f1f-8b27-5fd9-a794-4cbaaa9a9efa'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pick a question that''s safe when you make a new password.', NULL, NULL),
  ('630e525e-98ef-5401-be9d-dc84b7678212'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '630e525e-98ef-5401-be9d-dc84b7678212'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '13c5fbc7-ca4f-597f-94ac-332e4dd91536'::uuid, NULL, E'The law will compel employers to provide health insurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('63190a70-48c6-525f-a7a9-19575895e3d9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63190a70-48c6-525f-a7a9-19575895e3d9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dog and Mice', E'You''ve probably seen dogs working {{1}} at airports, sniffing for drugs, bombs and contraband food. Now our best-friend biosensors might have a new task: ferreting out the scent of bird flu.\nAnd they may not be alone on the job. Researchers from the U.S. Department of Agriculture and Monell Chemical Senses Center trained mice to identify duck droppings from animals infected with bird flu. The work was presented at the National Meeting of the American Chemical Society in Boston.\nThe {{2}} trained six mice to run a maze in search of infected feces. Every time they found the right feces, they got a drink of water. The mice learned to choose infected over noninfected duck feces about 90 percent of the time.\nThe researchers believe the {{3}} could be twofold. First, bird flu apparently leaves an odor imprint on bird feces, and so dogs—and even mice—could be trained to {{4}} it. Second, scientists might be able to isolate the cocktail of compounds that gives off the odor to develop lab instruments or automated field detectors. Until then, we may find four-legged sensors, large and small, sniffing away to protect us from a {{5}} epidemic.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.security, 2.scientists, 3.implications, 4.recognize, 5.bird-borne', NULL, NULL),
  ('631ee88f-f619-5f6e-b8f8-cd60c8dd2a80'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '631ee88f-f619-5f6e-b8f8-cd60c8dd2a80'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b467279e-1766-5626-b53f-a5510abacfb6'::uuid, NULL, E'The mountain was sharply defined against the eastern sky.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('632563ab-95c3-5b38-9832-55b8c24c9e97'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '632563ab-95c3-5b38-9832-55b8c24c9e97'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call one thousand years?', '1e79a654-e661-58cf-a6d7-09c901e7a658'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Millennium', NULL, NULL),
  ('632569b5-abf5-56ce-b859-fda5c1da08a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '632569b5-abf5-56ce-b859-fda5c1da08a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cuypers Library', E'The Cuypers Library is a research library in Amsterdam''s famous Rijks museum. It is the oldest and largest of its kind in the country and aesthetically astounding. However, despite the streams of tourists that flow through the museum, far too {{1}} seem to trickle into its remarkable reading room. The 19th-century library, which has recently been {{2}} , has been collecting content since 1885. Its {{3}} are stocked with manuscripts bound to entice any art history lover. While browsing its extensive collection, you''ll come across books, journals, and periodicals, as well as catalogues about art auctions, exhibitions, trades, and collections. Following its renovations, the museum opened the library''s reading room to visitors. Tourists, students, and art historians alike are welcome to delve into its rich collection. Tables on the ground floor allow people to hunker down with their research materials, surrounded by the library’s aesthetically astounding walls of books.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.few, 2.restored, 3.shelves', NULL, NULL),
  ('63289486-ea23-5658-b502-88721500bdec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63289486-ea23-5658-b502-88721500bdec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '30750d87-f5d1-5be8-8e0d-82c17abd87d3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some wonder if spending money on space is good.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63294d86-bfdf-58b1-ad7e-4c1985414dc1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63294d86-bfdf-58b1-ad7e-4c1985414dc1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Renewable Energy', E'The world is increasingly turning to renewable energy sources to combat climate change and reduce reliance on fossil fuels. Solar, wind, and hydroelectric power are among the key alternatives being explored. Governments and industries are investing in research and infrastructure to harness these clean energy sources, paving the way for a more sustainable future.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
