  ('6374cbf0-111a-52d2-b2e1-fc75e35f8180'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6374cbf0-111a-52d2-b2e1-fc75e35f8180'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Research', E'Research is a process of investigation leading to new {{1}} effectively shared and is central to the {{2}} of any university. Students have the right to be taught by acknowledged {{3}} in their field, which requires that staff members operate at the most advanced level appropriate to their {{4}} and level. Research is, therefore, crucial to a {{5}} student experience from further education to doctoral development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.insights, 2.purpose, 3.experts, 4.discipline, 5.positive', NULL, NULL),
  ('6376d50f-8df1-58c5-b8d2-2a36a0caf1d2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6376d50f-8df1-58c5-b8d2-2a36a0caf1d2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cell', E'All cells share some common characteristics that make them living things. All organisms are composed of cells, the basic fundamental unit of life. They contain DNA as a heritable genetic material, and they can reproduce. They transcribe DNA into RNA and translate RNA into proteins on ribosomes. They can also regulate transport across a cell membrane and require chemical energy for some cellular processes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('637b6ed3-555e-5ed8-8a23-ef8361076e78'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '637b6ed3-555e-5ed8-8a23-ef8361076e78'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9b300dd0-9fca-5c72-94d4-52dc9ffcfc0c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Schools should ensure the independence of education and academic research.', NULL, NULL),
  ('638242ea-96b1-50de-95f5-67014fc11867'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '638242ea-96b1-50de-95f5-67014fc11867'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Decision Making', E'Most of us believe that when we are making decisions about money we are being clear-headed and sensible, and assume that any rational person would {{1}} in the same way and make the same decisions. But our {{2}} are always based on the private logic of our own {{3}} mind-set, our deep beliefs about money and what it''s for, and no two people are the same. Even when two people come to the same {{4}} , they have probably used quite different logical paths.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.behave, 2.choices, 3.financial, 4.conclusion', NULL, NULL),
  ('6386a3e9-4e5e-5a04-a9c3-89f9a0bd0967'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6386a3e9-4e5e-5a04-a9c3-89f9a0bd0967'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '584992d6-3660-509f-b1da-0cbe4f03fcf2'::uuid, NULL, E'Our future well-being hinges on the actions we take in the present.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6396b8dc-75b3-57ee-8c68-a4c5225866a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6396b8dc-75b3-57ee-8c68-a4c5225866a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Media Organizations', E'Fake news is widely used to discredit any opposing viewpoint. Some people use it to {{1}} doubt on their opponents, controversial issues or the {{2}} of some media organizations. In addition, technological advances such as the {{3}} of social media enable fake news stories to {{4}} quickly and easily as people share more and more information online.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.cast, 2.credibility, 3.advent, 4.proliferate', NULL, NULL),
  ('639c7aab-4279-5687-92c7-4dd5d40a3909'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '639c7aab-4279-5687-92c7-4dd5d40a3909'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who writes a book?', '3f5beabe-7538-5f31-982b-e6ba4931f4df'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Author / writer', NULL, NULL),
  ('63a13fe6-400a-5ac4-bb91-fd70fe249c2b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63a13fe6-400a-5ac4-bb91-fd70fe249c2b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Preservation Act', E'The Endangered Species Preservation Act was the predecessor to the modern Endangered Species Act. It was enacted in 1966. The act empowered the United States Secretary to pilot and run conservation programs for indigenous species on the brink of extinction.\nThe Endangered Species Preservation Act was the government’s response to the declining numbers of the whooping crane, a bird species indigenous to North America. Two years later, in 1968, the government increased conservation efforts for America’s indigenous species and bought 2,300 acres in Florida. This enhanced protection for the National Key Deer through the National Key Deer Refuge. The government first established the refuge in 1957.\nThe U.S. was on the right step in protecting its animals and plants, then saw the need to expand the law to cover international species. It all started in the 1960s with a recording of the sound made by humpback whales. Their numbers were also dwindling, so much so that the International Whaling Commission temporarily stopped whale hunting. This meant that the ban would be lifted once the whale population stabilized. Conservationists were also watching, and the United States also had to act.\nThe Endangered Species Preservation Act of 1966, therefore, evolved into the Endangered Species Conservation Act in 1969. The U.S. could now add international species to its endangered species list and ban imports of products made from those species.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('63a57820-57c4-5973-b346-3153e2583698'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63a57820-57c4-5973-b346-3153e2583698'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Right Foundation', E'We {{1}} anyone can excel with the right foundation. By {{2}} the basis of information setting for knowledge, such as coding and other skills, participants gain essential expertise. Through 9-12 projects, you will {{3}} your portfolio, and upon {{4}} the program, you will have a robust showcase of your abilities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.believe, 2.understanding, 3.build, 4.completing', NULL, NULL),
  ('63ac7af2-2c71-5067-9630-21d1c44da987'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63ac7af2-2c71-5067-9630-21d1c44da987'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Botswana', E'Although Botswana is rich in diamonds, it has high unemployment and stratified socioeconomic classes. In 1999, the nation {{1}} its first budget deficit in 16 years {{2}} of a slump in the international diamond market. Yet Botswana {{3}} one of the wealthiest and most stable countries on the African {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.suffered, 2.because, 3.remains, 4.continent', NULL, NULL),
  ('63b4b824-bbd3-578e-b68b-1d43faf738e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63b4b824-bbd3-578e-b68b-1d43faf738e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c0b048b4-a705-5dd0-b61c-c4fe9218fd9f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The library boasts a large, important collection on economic history.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63b54a20-5456-59f7-bb57-89413373ab07'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63b54a20-5456-59f7-bb57-89413373ab07'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '91ce98a8-3946-53d8-991b-4d0b321e8624'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Good design can make a big difference and shouldn''t be ignored.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63b61c21-bee1-5a85-9af4-777996ae3216'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63b61c21-bee1-5a85-9af4-777996ae3216'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cultural Diversity', NULL, '612105c7-50b4-59cf-bfad-da7442283b8e'::uuid, NULL, E'Embracing cultural diversity is integral to enriching our university experience. It cultivates an environment where learning extends beyond textbooks, into the realms of personal interactions and shared experiences. This diversity introduces a multitude of perspectives, challenging us to think critically and broaden our understanding of the world. Engaging with ideas that differ from our own fosters innovation and problem-solving. For instance, group projects benefiting from diverse viewpoints often yield more creative solutions. Additionally, cultural diversity on campus prepares us for the global workforce. As the business world becomes increasingly interconnected, cultural competence is not just an asset but a necessity. It enables us to navigate cross-cultural communications and collaborations effectively. In conclusion, cultural diversity is not just about coexistence but about the synergetic fusion of ideas that prepare us for life beyond university walls.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('63b7fa74-f38e-5fca-bf63-f68d6fd99a93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63b7fa74-f38e-5fca-bf63-f68d6fd99a93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '61ba6588-67af-53b9-acf8-03bfacf23523'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You should be careful when searching internet sources.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63be69f1-ef5e-5277-b6c3-c81002143c84'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63be69f1-ef5e-5277-b6c3-c81002143c84'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Burial', E'Was burial of the dead practiced by Neanderthals or is it an innovation specific to our species? Researchers have demonstrated, using a variety of criteria, that a Neanderthal child was buried, probably around 41,000 years ago, at the Ferrassie site (Dordogne, France).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('63c0b354-7f99-5ed1-b86e-7fdf4b37d638'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63c0b354-7f99-5ed1-b86e-7fdf4b37d638'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Birds(鸟类是好是坏)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4, 5', NULL, NULL),
  ('63cbb2c5-5a1c-523f-acbc-2c33e44f78d7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63cbb2c5-5a1c-523f-acbc-2c33e44f78d7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the facts, signs or objects that make you believe something is true?', 'c5ec1bec-d000-5fbf-b6eb-f41304a51a32'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Evidence / proof', NULL, NULL),
  ('63d21c9c-0e64-528a-9d47-8ea24cd66c39'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63d21c9c-0e64-528a-9d47-8ea24cd66c39'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the field of study that deals with the location of countries, rivers, mountains and so on?', '1014b50c-d7c2-55f1-b287-3036e3bfa66c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Geography', NULL, NULL),
  ('63d5efc1-8809-5e1c-9e9a-3a2ad205a26a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63d5efc1-8809-5e1c-9e9a-3a2ad205a26a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Modern American Universities', NULL, '240eae88-d954-52ac-9230-d2770b25757a'::uuid, NULL, E'Before the 1850''s, the United States had a number of small colleges, most of them dating from colonial days. They were small, church connected institutions whose primary concern was to shape the moral character of their students.\nThroughout Europe, institutions of higher learning had developed, bearing the ancient name of university. In German university was concerned primarily with creating and spreading knowledge, not morals. Between mid-century and the end of the 1800''s, more than nine thousand young Americans, dissatisfied with their training at home, went to Germany for advanced study. Some of them return to become presidents of venerable colleges-----Harvard, Yale, Columbia---and transform them into modern universities. The new presidents broke all ties with the churches and brought in a new kind of faculty. Professors were hired for their knowledge of a subject, not because they were of the proper faith and had a strong arm for disciplining students. The new principle was that a university was to create knowledge as well as pass it on, and this called for a faculty composed of teacher-scholars. Drilling and learning by rote were replaced by the German method of lecturing, in which the professor''s own research was presented in class. Graduate training leading to the Ph.D., an ancient German degree signifying the highest level of advanced scholarly attainment, was introduced. With the establishment of the seminar system, graduate student learned to question, analyze, and conduct their own research.\nAt the same time, the new university greatly expanded in size and course offerings, breaking completely out of the old, constricted curriculum of mathematics, classics, rhetoric, and music. The president of Harvard pioneered the elective system, by which students were able to choose their own course of study. The notion of major fields of study emerged. The new goal was to make the university relevant to the real pursuits of the world. Paying close heed to the practical needs of society, the new universities trained men and women to work at its tasks, with engineering students being the most characteristic of the new regime. Students were also trained as economists, architects, agriculturalists, social welfare workers, and teachers.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('63da70f6-3dcd-5c7a-94ca-abdbc13fb70b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63da70f6-3dcd-5c7a-94ca-abdbc13fb70b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'eee811b9-0806-51db-b189-dc319ae5544b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A series of lectures showcasing economic research have been recorded.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63df80f6-64ba-545b-ab6f-53a9a4629662'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '63df80f6-64ba-545b-ab6f-53a9a4629662'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Therapy', E'Online therapy can’t always replace traditional face-to-face counseling, but it has been shown to be an effective {{1}} ,especially for treating commonplace mental health issues like {{2}} and anxiety. If {{3}} is an issue, online therapy is usually more affordable and cost-effective than traditional therapy, starting with the fact that therapists working online can save on overhead {{4}} like rent and travel, passing those savings onto their patients.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.alternative, 2.depression, 3.cost, 4.expenses', NULL, NULL),
