  ('6730b969-e136-5050-abd1-0bf045a10ee8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6730b969-e136-5050-abd1-0bf045a10ee8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9a9f05b4-ff3e-57d4-b9be-3139c23a3007'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Social psychology is about how people act and why.', NULL, NULL),
  ('67322f79-4df1-5ed4-8084-c65005026c8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67322f79-4df1-5ed4-8084-c65005026c8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wright Brothers', E'In 1903, Wilbur and Orville Wright, two brothers from Dayton, OH, became the first people to fly a heavier than air, power controlled machine, known as the Wright Flyer. This did not simply happen overnight. The brothers had been tinkering with the idea of flight off and on since childhood. They were mechanically inclined young men who were inspired by the efforts of others.\nIn 1878, the brothers’ father, Milton Wright, brought home a rubber band powered toy helicopter. Designed by French aeronautical experimenter Alphonse Pénaud, this toy did not simply fall to the ground as expected. Rather it "flew across the room till it struck the ceiling, where it fluttered awhile, and finally sank to the floor." Though the fragile toy soon broke, Wilbur and Orville never forgot it. They even attempted to build their own toy helicopters. In later years, Orville accredited this childhood toy as sparking their interest in flight.\nThroughout their lives, the brothers were involved in a variety of ventures to make money. But it wasn’t until 1892, when they formed the Wright Cycle Company, finding a successful business that allowed spare time for other projects, to sell bicycles, that they found a successful business that also allowed them spare time for other projects. With the business doing rather well, the brothers also opened a repair shop and later began to manufacture bicycles.\nThough the business was going well, the brothers were restless. Their energies were focused by two 1896 events: the death of Otto Lilienthal and the successful unmanned launching of powered models by Samuel Langley; the death of Otto Lilienthal, the celebrated glider experimenter, in a flying accident, and the successful unmanned launching of powered models by Samuel Langley. The creativity and ingenuity of these two men were well and truly captured. Fortunately, the bicycle business provided funds and sharpened mechanical skills for their new interest, for unlike others in aviation, the Wrights were never financed by anyone. Furthermore, the repair and manufacture of bicycles sharpened the brothers'' mechanical skills. In their construction of flying machines, Wilbur and Orville often used the same equipment and tools used in repairing bicycles. They conducted many of their scientific experiments in the backroom of their shop and most of the parts used in the first successful airplane were built there.', NULL, NULL, E'Wilbur and Orville Wright became the first people to fly the Wright Flyer, who were mechanically inclined young men who were inspired by the efforts of others, so throughout their lives, the brothers were involved in a variety of ventures to make money, and their energies were focused by two 1896 events, while the bicycle business provided funds and sharpened mechanical skills for their new interest.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('67353d40-dfe2-51fa-bca7-406fdc7230cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67353d40-dfe2-51fa-bca7-406fdc7230cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call a string of beads used for counting prayers, rosary or garland?', 'd920c779-1c21-5bd5-bfc8-5114d4223b7d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Rosary', NULL, NULL),
