  ('67d68f97-f936-5294-9243-e6531379c5b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67d68f97-f936-5294-9243-e6531379c5b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '456f0be2-10b3-5aa6-ab11-dd86bdacc3ca'::uuid, NULL, E'I think it''s one of the best things I have done really.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('67d6ad69-5d30-5fd7-a281-29c2422781a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67d6ad69-5d30-5fd7-a281-29c2422781a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sun and Moon', E'From the time of the very earliest civilisations man has wondered about the world he lives in, about how it was created and about how it will end.\nIn these distant times the sun was seen to make its daily {{1}} across the sky. At night the moon appeared. Every new night the moon waxed or waned a little and on a few nights it did not appear at all. At night the great dome of the heavens was dotted with tiny specks of light. They {{2}} known as the stars. It was thought that every star in the heavens had its own purpose and that the {{3}} of the universe could be discovered by making a study of them. It was well known that there were wandering stars, they appeared in different nightly positions against their neighbours and they became known as planets. It took centuries, in fact it took millennia, for man to {{4}} the true nature of these wandering stars and to evolve a model of the world to accommodate them and to {{5}} their positions in the sky.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.journey, 2.became, 3.secrets, 4.determine, 5.predict', NULL, NULL),
  ('67ea14f5-dda2-5a55-8893-824b3fcd5dae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67ea14f5-dda2-5a55-8893-824b3fcd5dae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'bee3ea29-da6e-500e-bfce-1092e0de03e6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Fewer students are choosing science courses nowadays.', NULL, NULL),
  ('67eae58d-8401-5713-ae82-af1f8fd72c28'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67eae58d-8401-5713-ae82-af1f8fd72c28'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c91adf8f-bd1d-5a19-89f4-46c3f70951fa'::uuid, NULL, E'The university supplies a number of scholarships for qualified students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('67f00ea0-d126-59ac-bf7e-172c99570918'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67f00ea0-d126-59ac-bf7e-172c99570918'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Evolution', E'We usually think of evolution as something that happens over eons, in remote places where people rarely venture. Not something that happens around the backyard {{1}} in just a few decades. But a study in the journal Current Biology suggests that feeding birds in winter can influence their course of evolution.\nThe birds in this study were central European {{2}} , a common kind of warbler. In spring, they breed in southern Germany. And when winter comes, they all fly south to the Mediterranean. At least they used to. In the 1960s, folks in Britain started putting out seed in winter. And the blackcaps split into two {{3}} groups. One goes to Spain to nosh on fruits and olives, the other heads north to take advantage of the easy English pickin''s.\nThe two {{4}} may even be splitting into two species. The blackcaps that winter in England tend to mate with each other when they return to Germany. So they''re {{5}} to look different from the birds that go south. Their beaks are longer and {{6}} , less suited to supping on Spanish olives. As birds of a feather, they definitely flock together. And to some degree, they have a bunch of {{7}} Brits to thank.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.birdfeeder, 2.blackcaps, 3.distinct, 4.populations, 5.starting, 6.narrower, 7.bird-feeding', NULL, NULL),
  ('67f6435a-9fdb-576d-829e-bea3cbf8fd7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '67f6435a-9fdb-576d-829e-bea3cbf8fd7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4ca6bf36-74c1-585b-bb28-db65c2c050ec'::uuid, NULL, E'Please remain seated until the aircraft has come to a halt.', NULL, NULL, NULL);
