  ('6a48f4c3-eeb5-5a5d-9bb6-96117ff4ee8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6a48f4c3-eeb5-5a5d-9bb6-96117ff4ee8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Increasing Productivity', NULL, '5a148ef9-70ee-5a61-94b1-5edf603a808e'::uuid, NULL, E'About a fifth of South Korea''s total exports are semiconductors, which have been booming in recent years and have helped drive the country''s economic growth. But things are looking less certain for the industry in the new year. Analysts expect the prices of DRAM and NAND flash chips, which are used to store data in our phones, computers and TVs, will keep falling. Jesse Yung reports. Industry insiders on Thursday said home prices are likely to fall in the coming months. The global semiconductor industry began to suffer from sluggish growth from the end of last year, and according to a report by market research firm Dynamics Change. Oversupply, shrinking demand and a gloomy economic outlook are factors behind this price fall. The report said if the current lack of demand continues to erode, prices will see a downward trend throughout 2019. It also projected a fall in NAND flash prices due to shrinking demand. The average price of eight gigabyte drams, the most widely used units last month was seven U. S. dollars, down 10 from its peak in September. The average price of 128 gigabyte NAND flash chips the most widely used NAND Flash also fell last month. The report said global chip makers, Samsung Electronics, SK Hynix and Micron Technology, which make up the majority of the global volume, have started readjusting their chip production and reducing investment in semiconductor facilities. However, some industry insiders say prices could even rise towards the end of the year, citing a growing demand for chips driven by 5G or the fifth generation of mobile communications as well as self-driving cars.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6a4b4109-f66b-510e-aecb-db5e8ae9e9a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6a4b4109-f66b-510e-aecb-db5e8ae9e9a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '701114dc-1fac-5068-957f-51125657fb24'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The employment opportunities available in engineering are increasing rapidly.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6a52f302-747f-5076-ac54-36a26f36110f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6a52f302-747f-5076-ac54-36a26f36110f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drones', E'Antarctic plants can be important indicators of subtle changes in environmental conditions, including climate change. Traditional ground-based assessments of vegetation health are, however, not ideal in Antarctica, as they can destroy the vegetation and are physically {{1}} in the harsh weather conditions.\nCo-author Professor Sharon Robinson from UOW’s School of Biological Sciences said the study found drone-based monitoring of vegetation health produced similar results to traditional techniques, but with much greater efficiency and with no damage to the vegetation.\n“Drones are a powerful tool for monitoring fragile Antarctic vegetation,” Professor Robinson said.\n“They could be used to provide timely warnings about specific environmental stress events, {{2}} monitoring the longer-term impacts of climate change.\n“These methods could also be adapted to monitor the health of other small-stature, patchy plant communities, including in alpine or desert regions.”\nThe researchers found that drones {{3}} with sensors were able to detect vegetation health indicators more accurately than satellite imagery.\nMosses are one of the key Antarctic vegetation types that need to be monitored. However, they tend to occur in patches among rocks, ice and soil, {{4}} it important that the imagery used to assess their health is as accurate and spatially detailed as possible.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.demanding, 2.as well as, 3.equipped, 4.making', NULL, NULL),
  ('6a55147a-eec0-5d03-944b-44c37b8ca7a8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6a55147a-eec0-5d03-944b-44c37b8ca7a8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a young pig used for food?', 'ee09e297-acb0-5058-9db0-957b82f28aed'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Piglet', NULL, NULL),
  ('6a5a4236-3ff8-5442-85e2-562fe1b3e71a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6a5a4236-3ff8-5442-85e2-562fe1b3e71a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Number and Form', E'Number and form are the essence of our world: from the patterns of the stars to the pulses of the market, from the {{2}} of our hearts to catching a ball or tying our shoelaces. Drawing on science, literature, history and philosophy, and introducing {{1}} from Alcibiades to Gauss, this {{3}} book makes the mysteries of maths accessible and its rich {{4}} brilliantly clear.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.beats, 2.geniuses, 3.inspiring, 4.patterns', NULL, NULL),
