  ('6b5f4b81-7450-5fcd-b329-2050db8534d1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b5f4b81-7450-5fcd-b329-2050db8534d1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coastal Development', E'Increased human activities and coastal development are quickly affecting the coastal {{1}} .Along the coastline, {{2}} waste water and solid waste can cause {{3}} in adjacent waters, fertilizer run-off from agricultural activities, invasive {{4}} from ballast waters, and pollution from oil and gas exploration further worsen the situation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.biodiversity, 2.untreated, 3.contamination, 4.species', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b5ff2e6-83d4-568f-a2ee-a3dc3f2dc25e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b5ff2e6-83d4-568f-a2ee-a3dc3f2dc25e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '79634f2b-c3b3-5518-98fe-70c69d5581d9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students will study the language and literature in ancient Greece.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b669a3a-201b-5300-9385-0badf2cc5089'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b669a3a-201b-5300-9385-0badf2cc5089'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vaccination', E'According to the literature, the history of {{1}} can be traced back to as early as the 7th century when the monks in India tried to immunize themselves by drinking snake {{2}} .The first vaccination was inoculation with human smallpox, a practice widely {{3}} out in ancient India, Arabia, and China. This method of vaccination consisted of collecting pus from a patient suffering from a mild form of smallpox virus infection and {{4}} the sample to a healthy human, which later led to a minor infection. This method was first introduced in England by a Greek named Timoni. However, this method had a risk of spreading smallpox in the community and even worsening the health condition of the person who received the inoculation. While the use of human smallpox vaccine was {{5}} , Jenner came up with bovine smallpox vaccine in 1796; this new method also faced controversy but continued to be {{6}} .Smallpox became a preventable disease by injecting pus extracted from a human infected with cowpox virus. Jenner named the substance "vaccine" after the Latin word "vacca" which means "cow," and thus the process of giving vaccine became "vaccination".', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.vaccination, 2.venom, 3.carried, 4.inoculating, 5.controversial, 6.universalized', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b70d77a-ba90-548f-8e4d-a3feb19c7795'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b70d77a-ba90-548f-8e4d-a3feb19c7795'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '712bfcef-755a-5eb5-ba9e-7c36eaa72ad3'::uuid, NULL, E'This is just one instance; there are numerous more examples.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6b737b90-1082-5853-8356-d87b2f62a566'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b737b90-1082-5853-8356-d87b2f62a566'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Employee Mood', E'Research from the Terry College of Business reveals {{1}} a happy, helpful employee takes effort and, eventually, that effort {{2}} the energy needed to do one’s job. It could lead to quiet quitting – the new term for just doing your job but not going above and beyond – or even actual quitting. The more people adjust their moods to be happy, the fewer emotional resources they have {{3}} the end of the day. That means they are less able to handle challenging tasks and interactions and have a harder time staying on task. Their tank is empty despite being in a good mood, Frank explained. For managers, this means it may make more sense to meet employees {{4}} they are emotionally and not force upbeat attitudes in the office. For employees, it may mean letting bad days happen and leaving more mood-demanding work — such as sales calls or tough conversations — for better days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.becoming, 2.erodes, 3.at, 4.where', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b7997b2-6f51-5c0b-a970-56716b3c458f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b7997b2-6f51-5c0b-a970-56716b3c458f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Energy Saving', E'Using less energy saves money and lowers greenhouse gas {{1}} . And various studies have looked at ways to get {{2}} to use less energy. Now there''s evidence that people in such a study use less energy...because they''re in a study.\nThe general {{3}} is called the {{4}} effect: study subjects change their behavior because they''re being observed. So {{5}} collaborated with a utility to test for the Hawthorne effect in electricity use.\nThey {{6}} almost 5,600 randomly selected households. Half received a postcard saying that their energy use would be monitored for a month for research purposes. They also got four follow-up reminder postcards over the month. They received no other information, instructions or incentives.\nThe control group monitored for the study got no notifications. That group continued using the same amount of electricity. But the families being tracked reduced energy use 2.7 percent. And when the study period ended, their energy use shot back up. The report is in the {{7}} of the National Academy of Sciences.\nClearly, mindful consumers can find ways to easily lower their energy consumption. Perhaps policy makers can find a way to use the Hawthorne effect to everyone''s advantage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.emissions, 2.households, 3.phenomenon, 4.Hawthorne, 5.researchers, 6.monitored, 7.Proceedings', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b7e4ee8-5bb5-580a-ab3e-0fdbc683a1dd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b7e4ee8-5bb5-580a-ab3e-0fdbc683a1dd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'New Words and Phrases', NULL, '752e501d-0469-55e6-a66f-522d9bf87fae'::uuid, NULL, E'John, what''s your favourite new word at the moment?\nReally I don''t have favourite new words, but let''s say that one of my favourite new words is screenager, which is a young person or a teenager who spends a lot of time in front of the computer.\nAny other favourites, John?\nSome of those rather unpleasant words like splod, somebody who is socially inept, a splody person, but as I said I don''t really have favourite words because all words as far as I''m concerned are objects of scientific study.\nAnd where do these new words and phrases come from?\nWell, words come out of the culture that they represent and they describe so if you''ve got a new development in medicine, for example bird flu, then you''ll get a new word coming out of that. If there''s a military conflict that may well bring all sorts of new words to the fore. Going back in time the First and Second World Wars were times of great creativity of language because people from different countries met each other and exchanged their words and words developed from there. So really words come from, they come from the playground, they come from politics, they come from any area of life because every area of life is changing from day to day.\nHow do you keep up with the huge weight of new words you must have to evaluate?\nWell, it''s not just me, we''ve got something like 60 editors working on the Oxford dictionary and we also have readers and word spotters throughout the world who are sending us information in. In the old days they used to write them out on index cards when they came across some in books, but nowadays they tend to type them onto their computers and send them into the central computer here. It''s an enormous issue, but one which we just about manage to keep under control. We don''t include words just because we''ve seen one example of them we have to wait for evidence of general currency to build up in our computer files before we start putting the word in the dictionary. So a lot of the time it''s collecting data, letting it build up and then reviewing it and seeing what you''ve got and so that''s how we manage the work.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6b82d03d-84a3-5626-93ec-75bfdf2510db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b82d03d-84a3-5626-93ec-75bfdf2510db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite of ''simplify''?', '02e3f7c9-cac1-579a-a065-728a1e27e171'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Complicate', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b8a1ed1-f3c8-59cc-8742-90a31c20ef18'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b8a1ed1-f3c8-59cc-8742-90a31c20ef18'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7595d282-1823-57af-9663-badcb2f0518c'::uuid, NULL, E'In the course of my everyday life, I had very little contact with teenagers.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6b8b02b4-03ac-5f4f-8ac5-8011b06a2ad6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b8b02b4-03ac-5f4f-8ac5-8011b06a2ad6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who gives treatments in the hospital?', '469597bf-3219-51d5-8e60-f2cda6b0ef4b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Doctor', NULL, NULL),
  ('6b8e6ddc-b6fe-5a44-8d31-de206b2038e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6b8e6ddc-b6fe-5a44-8d31-de206b2038e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we describe something between continents?', '31a77b7e-d921-5116-ac2d-216643ade24d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Intercontinental', NULL, NULL),
  ('6ba0b8f8-23ef-5758-8659-3f4bf823e5c4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6ba0b8f8-23ef-5758-8659-3f4bf823e5c4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vinyl Records', E'In recent times, vinyl records have spun back into popularity, challenging the notion that digital formats had {{1}} taken over. It''s curious, considering the convenience of streaming services, why people are returning to this bulky, seemingly outdated medium. Perhaps it''s the ritual — the tactile sensation of sliding the record out of its sleeve, the delicate process of placing the needle, and the rich, warm sound that follows. Or maybe it''s the artwork, {{2}} in size and detail, something tangible to hold and appreciate. Vinyl enthusiasts often talk about the depth and authenticity of the sound, something they claim digital formats can''t {{3}} .And while it might seem like a step backward technologically, this resurgence speaks to a {{4}} for a more personal and immersive listening experience. So, next time you''re about to press play on your phone, consider dropping the needle on a record {{5}} . You might just find a different kind of joy in the grooves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.permanently, 2.commanding, 3.replicate, 4.desire, 5.instead', NULL, NULL),
  ('6ba659a0-76f2-52b8-bebb-3526f12c0e71'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6ba659a0-76f2-52b8-bebb-3526f12c0e71'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7beab5aa-d06b-5c17-b0c3-33558fa7791b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Literature can be classified in various ways.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6ba9a239-b9c6-5041-81dd-7a6be988e46e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6ba9a239-b9c6-5041-81dd-7a6be988e46e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9f0f7f2e-d3d7-593a-b082-68c6d7e7fbfe'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We will study the following pictures in the next lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6baba47f-7b1d-58b6-ae80-bb953704c767'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6baba47f-7b1d-58b6-ae80-bb953704c767'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tsunamis', E'As we know from tsunamis, when water is moving at 50 or 60 kilometers an hour it becomes deadly.\nEven if a wave only {{1}} up to the knees, the {{2}} can knock a person down. Water flows around some obstacles, while slamming into large {{3}} , such as walls, which stand in its way. It also gathers {{4}} , like rocks and trees, as it flows,causing even more destruction when it crashes into buildings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.comes, 2.force, 3.objects, 4.debris', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bad355a-cb12-504a-b9fd-0aeeb5ebfb8e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bad355a-cb12-504a-b9fd-0aeeb5ebfb8e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f241f83a-2840-543a-9ae3-2bb47aff43ca'::uuid, NULL, E'The vehicle he traveled in collided with a train unexpectedly.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6baf976a-00df-52e4-830d-88b27749baf0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6baf976a-00df-52e4-830d-88b27749baf0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rosling''s Discoveries', E'A medical doctor and professor for international health at Stockholm''s Karolinska Institute, Rosling became famous as the public educator who used statistics to show how the world is changing. He chose this public role after making two significant discoveries.\nRosling''s first discovery was that many people are not aware of even the most basic facts about global health and global development. Through surveys he conducted, Rosling found that at a time when poverty is falling faster than ever before, the majority of people think that the proportion of the world population living in extreme poverty is rising. Similarly, he found that many underestimate global life expectancy widely, and are not aware of the success of delivering healthcare services — for example, vaccines — globally. He found that people''s worldviews often do not have much grounding in facts, even long before the "post-fact" era. Rosling was convinced that this unawareness of global progress matters. He made it his mission to fight this "devastating ignorance" that turns us into cynics, as we falsely believe that global development must be a mirage.\nRosling''s second discovery was that this lack of factual knowledge was not because people are not interested in global development, but because it is too hard for those that want to know about global development to access this knowledge. Neither the experts nor the media were presenting how global development changes the world. Based on these two insights, Hans Rosling made it his mission to bridge this gap and present the evidence that global development is a reality. His approach to communicating research on global development was through public talks and the use of data visualisation.', NULL, NULL, E'Rosling''s first discovery was that many people are not aware of even the most basic facts about global health and development, and the second one was that this lack of factual knowledge was because it''s too hard for those that want to know about global development to access this knowledge, so based on these two insights, he made it his mission to bridge this gap and present the evidence that global development is a reality.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('6bb7c8e5-4363-511e-af11-c837813c7c82'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bb7c8e5-4363-511e-af11-c837813c7c82'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the act of accepting someone as a student at a school?', 'cd6ad3a5-bae5-5c0a-837b-062e31dd06c1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Admission', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bbba1a2-e11f-581e-a029-3b077c860f7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bbba1a2-e11f-581e-a029-3b077c860f7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ocean Exploration', E'Do you think that ocean exploration is as important as space exploration?', NULL, NULL, E'I firmly believe that ocean exploration is just as important as space exploration. While space exploration captures our imagination and pushes the boundaries of human knowledge, the exploration of our oceans holds equal significance in unraveling the mysteries of our planet and understanding the intricate ecosystems that sustain life on Earth.\nThe oceans harbor vast biodiversity and abundant resources, including marine life and minerals that are vital for sustaining life on Earth. Exploring the depths of the oceans allows us to uncover new species, understand complex ecosystems, and harness valuable resources that can benefit industries such as medicine, energy, and conservation. By studying ocean biodiversity and resources, we gain crucial insights into the interconnectedness of life on our planet and the importance of preserving these delicate ecosystems.\nOcean exploration is crucial for understanding the oceans'' role in regulating the Earth''s climate. Oceans play a vital role in absorbing carbon dioxide and regulating global temperatures, making them a key player in mitigating climate change. By studying ocean processes and dynamics, scientists can better predict climate patterns, assess the impacts of human activities on marine environments, and develop strategies to protect our oceans and combat climate change effectively.\nIn conclusion, ocean exploration stands on equal footing with space exploration in terms of its importance and impact on scientific discovery, environmental conservation, and human understanding. The exploration of the oceans offers unparalleled opportunities to study biodiversity, resources, climate regulation, and make groundbreaking scientific discoveries that can shape our understanding of the natural world.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('6bc04bfb-7b47-58f8-8bd3-c4e813079d52'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bc04bfb-7b47-58f8-8bd3-c4e813079d52'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we describe a person who is educated?', 'b46dbe01-b6c9-5796-a912-4ed50f2dcd98'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Literate', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bc1b605-fbea-5c1f-aa2e-57c5fcc3d4ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bc1b605-fbea-5c1f-aa2e-57c5fcc3d4ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Media', E'Social media has transformed the way we communicate and interact with others by enabling instant communication across distances and facilitating connections with people from diverse backgrounds. However, it has also raised concerns about privacy and security as personal information can be easily shared or stolen online.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6bc34757-88cb-5a95-8b53-f0bd8a555fd6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bc34757-88cb-5a95-8b53-f0bd8a555fd6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In which direction does the sun come up?', 'b1c94289-eb5b-5be1-b687-02e19c37c215'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'East', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bcda3b4-1547-5267-8b0e-c2217742f6eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bcda3b4-1547-5267-8b0e-c2217742f6eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Consequences Of Poverty', NULL, '5b8de980-bfec-54c9-88dd-e677ebf5d7b3'::uuid, NULL, E'Now let’s turn to the second question. Could it be that these psychological consequences of poverty have implications for economic decision-making that make it hard to escape poverty? And there’s two ways that you might imagine this could happen. The first is that the stress that’s brought on by poverty might affect economic choices in subtle ways. And there’s now evidence suggesting that when you’re under stress you’re much more impatient than you are when you’re not stressed. And that’s not a good thing if you’re supposed to make long-term decisions and investments in things like health care and education. And so unless you, poverty causes stress, stress makes you impatient. And then that impatience doesn’t help you to lift yourself out of poverty. But there’s a second sense in which the psychological consequences of poverty might exacerbate poverty. And that is that they may simply incapacitate you. So when chronic stress turns into full-fledged clinical depression, it’s very hard for people to keep earning a living. So you don’t think your efforts will amount to anything. You know no amount of information about returns to education can convince you otherwise. It’s hard for you to even get out of bed in the morning and your livelihood crumbles. So this is bad enough when you’re wealthy, but it’s worse when you’re poor. And you don’t have as much of a safety net to fall back on. So as a result of this, there’s a silent epidemic of depression among the poor. And that’s the problem not only for psychological well-being, but also for economic outcomes.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6bce0c5a-f4af-5647-b3e4-af3321ab8955'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bce0c5a-f4af-5647-b3e4-af3321ab8955'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a pleasant song used for causing children to sleep?', '11b22ede-ad6e-54d2-94ce-cde7a4f9f839'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Lullaby', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bce187f-c4b3-5c12-b32d-cec26ae9ebd0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bce187f-c4b3-5c12-b32d-cec26ae9ebd0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the device with two or more blades turning quickly to cause a ship or an airplane to move?', '644b06e2-29c3-58e4-85d2-3fc135d2d5db'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Propeller', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bd03cda-805f-55d9-9c13-241f640412d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bd03cda-805f-55d9-9c13-241f640412d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Consistency', E'Consistency is key in maintaining an exercise {{1}} . Have you ever noticed how some days you''re too exhausted to even think about a workout? I''m not talking about those days when you''re just not in the {{2}} , but the ones where you''re physically or mentally {{3}} . Perhaps you''re preoccupied, fatigued, or anticipating {{4}} events. In such moments, forcing a workout might be counterproductive. A well-timed, energized exercise session can be far more {{5}} than a half-hearted effort.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.routine, 2.mood, 3.drained, 4.upcoming, 5.effective', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bd0ad97-1a56-5f9b-80c8-b56b97728775'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bd0ad97-1a56-5f9b-80c8-b56b97728775'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which part does a bird use for flying?', 'da49d11f-49d6-5289-9862-3f9c994df04a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Wing', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bd48054-c906-52c2-8481-844a520f14dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bd48054-c906-52c2-8481-844a520f14dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Individual and Collective', E'The formation of individual and collective identities is a key subject in sociological study. Sociologists explore how identities are shaped by various {{1}} including culture, social structures, and personal experiences. Theories in this field examine how individuals develop a {{2}} of self and belonging, and how social categories like gender, race, and class influence this {{3}} . Identity formation is not static but dynamic, continuously {{4}} by interactions and societal changes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.factors, 2.sense, 3.process, 4.molded', NULL, NULL),
  ('6bdbddf2-a1b5-543a-8b2f-7b401242d1af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6bdbddf2-a1b5-543a-8b2f-7b401242d1af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Learning', E'If you are interested in studying but have other {{1}} , our online and distance learning courses offer an alternative flexible {{2}} of study. Teaching is conducted through a mixture of audio-visual, written and interactive materials. There are also {{3}} for online discussion and collaborative projects with tutors and other students. Some programmes include residential {{4}} taught on campus, giving you the {{5}} to meet and work alongside your tutors and fellow students face-to-face. Our Graduate School provides comprehensive support for distance and part-time researchers, many of whom study for up to six years or more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.commitments, 2.mode, 3.opportunities, 4.modules, 5.chance', NULL, NULL),
