  ('6c1740a7-51c1-5eaf-8c5e-3c4e0b8b09ec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c1740a7-51c1-5eaf-8c5e-3c4e0b8b09ec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3b63cc41-5b08-5fb6-8922-94e1a299ca85'::uuid, NULL, E'The plan is to phase out all cars with internal combustion engines by twenty fifty.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c1ba13c-e186-5fc9-8f39-b746b5d26c10'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c1ba13c-e186-5fc9-8f39-b746b5d26c10'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0a5058f9-e369-5357-95a7-b502d2cba72e'::uuid, NULL, E'We provide a number of services to ensure a good experience for our students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c1f2aa2-8a46-564f-8cb6-38c7ab40b10f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c1f2aa2-8a46-564f-8cb6-38c7ab40b10f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vocal Learning', E'The European starling is known for its impressive vocal abilities. These versatile songbirds have the ability to learn a wide range of warbles, whistles, calls, and songs throughout their lives, making them one of the most advanced avian vocal learners. A recent study published in Science has discovered that starlings also excel in problem-solving tasks.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c21bc5f-7c89-54ba-ae9e-9097c4fc8d62'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c21bc5f-7c89-54ba-ae9e-9097c4fc8d62'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Consumer Confidence', E'The Conference Board’s consumer-confidence index, which measures both American consumers’ assessment of current conditions and their expectations, rose to its highest level since 2001. Updated figures from the Commerce Department confirmed earlier estimates that the economy grew by 1.6% year-on-year in 2016, the slowest rate for five years—though growth picked up to 1.9% in the final quarter.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c2305a0-07cc-5fa7-a40a-56b33990f159'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c2305a0-07cc-5fa7-a40a-56b33990f159'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Archaeology', E'Archaeology is the study of our human past. The evidence that archaeologists use to answer these questions is often found during excavations or digs. The evidence can {{1}} objects like pottery, jewelry, building materials, coins, weapons and tools. Soil samples from archaeological sites can reveal information about past environments, like what kinds of plants were {{2}} . Features like ditches, pits, post holes and the remains of walls can help archaeologists piece {{3}} what buildings looked like and what they were made of. The ways that people were buried tells us about past beliefs, and the skeletons themselves reveal information about people'' s health in the past and the types of diseases and injuries that killed them. Scientific {{4}} on teeth can even show where people came from.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.include, 2.growing, 3.together, 4.experiments', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c23194a-88b4-55c5-a807-5b10f0d02bae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c23194a-88b4-55c5-a807-5b10f0d02bae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '65c8ff58-ff7b-53f6-9c86-f92912260418'::uuid, NULL, E'If you need any information about the university, you can check with the information office located next to the corridor.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c23e4e5-c4fa-590e-a912-a66f6cb04c82'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c23e4e5-c4fa-590e-a912-a66f6cb04c82'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who has killed somebody deliberately and illegally?', '80d0ccd6-dff8-52f4-9bc6-ffd32b606a26'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Murderer / killer', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c313c97-d8d9-5ea9-873a-9152de75f2d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c313c97-d8d9-5ea9-873a-9152de75f2d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Surface Water', E'Research indicates that over billions of years, surface water has been transported deep into the Earth by descending, or subducted, tectonic plates. Upon reaching the core-mantle boundary, about 1,800 miles below the surface, this water triggers a profound chemical interaction, altering the core''s structure.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('6c31519b-9d9a-548d-b321-9f47a317cb5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c31519b-9d9a-548d-b321-9f47a317cb5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Trinitite', E'The {{1}} heat and pressure of the first atomic bomb test, in 1945, left {{2}} a glassy substance known as trinitite — and something even stranger. Within the trinitite, scientists discovered, is a rare form of matter called a quasicrystal. Quasicrystals have an {{3}} structure like a normal crystal, but that structure doesn''t repeat. {{4}} , these crystals had been found only in meteorites or made in the lab.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.intense, 2.behind, 3.orderly, 4.Previously', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c31e248-c8de-52f6-afae-6e27dfa6ec5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c31e248-c8de-52f6-afae-6e27dfa6ec5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '57bdcd9e-92ae-5075-b7cd-70cd20700912'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Please provide the reports to support your idea of these arguments.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c323b0e-a45b-57f7-849f-1cd4d8438ffb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c323b0e-a45b-57f7-849f-1cd4d8438ffb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Labor Shortage', E'A labor shortage - that is what a lot of people have been calling this moment. Here in the U.S., when the pandemic hit, 22 million jobs just went poof, gone, raptured by a tanking economy. Since then, jobs have come back, but workers sort of haven''t. In fact, a lot of people are quitting. Right now, there are a lot more job openings than there are people looking for work. And that usually does not happen. Economists are waiting for more data trying to understand this. Meanwhile, people are floating lots of vaguely sociological explanations. And so we decided, let''s do our own informal survey. Let''s find out what is going on in your world of work. So we asked you to tell us, are you hiring? Are you quitting? Are you looking for work? And you called us back from all over the place.\n\nAccording to the passage, which of the following statements about the labor shortage is true?', 'c61461d2-5a86-59e8-b400-3f71068933ae'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Economists have not pinpointed the causes for the labor shortage because of insufficient data yet.', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c323cac-1307-5eb0-9a69-9af33dd6ba8e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6c323cac-1307-5eb0-9a69-9af33dd6ba8e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ce7f962c-fb39-5076-98ef-dc0190842798'::uuid, NULL, E'Guidance on presentation focus will be more specific this time.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
