  ('6dff285f-89d5-5e11-b388-bedf3e6f2e39'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6dff285f-89d5-5e11-b388-bedf3e6f2e39'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Encyclopédie', E'The "Encyclopédie" is a landmark publication in European history, edited by Denis Diderot and Jean le Rond d''Alembert. First issued in 1751, the Encyclopédie {{1}} over two decades to complete, involving the contributions of more than 140 authors, and {{2}} 28 volumes of text and illustrations. It was a triumph of collaborative scholarship, {{3}} any of its contemporaries in scope and depth and {{4}} a benchmark for future encyclopedias.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.took, 2.comprising, 3.surpassing, 4.setting', NULL, NULL),
  ('6e004af8-c657-5930-8e20-dd3343f39da4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6e004af8-c657-5930-8e20-dd3343f39da4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Celebrities'' Privacy', E'People who are famous entertainers or sportspeople should give up the right to privacy as this is the price of fame. To what extent do you agree/disagree with this point of view? Give your opinion with your experiences.', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether famous entertainers or sportspeople should give up the right to privacy has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that famous people should sacrifice some privacy because of their mind influence, whereas opponents contend that celebrities'' deliberate concealment doesn''t mean they give up their privacy. From my perspective, I am convinced that famous entertainers or sportspeople should give up the right to privacy as this is the price of fame.\nTo begin with, famous people should give up some privacy because their huge influence requires public supervision. For example, celebrities'' high-profile actions impact fans'' values, so society must watch their behavior. In addition to this, influential stars'' choices might misguide young people''s moral standards and blur their ethical boundaries. Other than that, famous people''s social roles demand transparency, as their decisions affect public trust. It is thus shown that notable entertainers or athletes should relinquish their privacy as this is the cost of fame.\nBesides, I also believe that it helps the public see their real personalities, because authenticity builds credibility. On top of that, the secretive lives of stars often obscure their true characters, so exposure helps fans know the genuine truth. Moreover, famous people''s unfiltered moments display their genuine nature, so media should show their real side. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that public figures'' artificial personas mislead audiences, so supervision can stop fake identity building. This clearly proves that celebrities in entertainment or sports should surrender their right to privacy for this comes with being famous.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that faith gap and celebrities'' masked images are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that famous entertainers or athletes must cede their privacy, as the price for fame.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('6e0d4da3-1a5b-5cb9-9721-cd300db00101'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '6e0d4da3-1a5b-5cb9-9721-cd300db00101'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'How to Review', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
