  ('73146a5c-acd5-53b4-b32f-39b8fca343b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73146a5c-acd5-53b4-b32f-39b8fca343b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1076d6c4-67f4-55e0-8696-73a3bf8f21fc'::uuid, NULL, E'I''ll start with a brief history of the district, and then focus on life in the first half of the twentieth century.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('73161f49-3853-54ae-8470-dc86a91cfd26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73161f49-3853-54ae-8470-dc86a91cfd26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '23da9d7e-85cc-537a-b85b-9bb19e3d31b0'::uuid, NULL, E'In this library, the reserve collection of books can be borrowed for up to three hours.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('73168d21-ba2b-5d66-b634-e002fd7e3a2f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73168d21-ba2b-5d66-b634-e002fd7e3a2f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Historic Library', NULL, 'a3e59ceb-b1a1-55b7-8292-47d9ee5cccbe'::uuid, NULL, E'Indeed, the library. We''ve all been to a historic library. We''ve all enjoyed the smell of a historic library. But what is it? And what does it mean? When we''ve recently, when at UCL Center for Sustainable Heritage, we''ve recently been asked to assess the environment at another historical library at Saint Paul''s Cathedral, the Wren library, an incredible place. And it has a such an intensive smell of old books, and we were also asked for the first time really I was actually taken aback by the brief, we were asked what you do please preserve the smell. It is so important to our audience. It is so important how people perceive the library. So, that is, that was quite an important message in our research. And indeed the smell is an important way of how we communicate with the environment. This piece of research was done by an advertising company because advertisers are so interested in how we, how we interact with each other and the environment. And we see that the majority of people use sight obviously to interact with the environment, but on the second place, we see the smell is also very, very important.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7319f6ac-d885-50a5-9511-cd8ae64905cb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7319f6ac-d885-50a5-9511-cd8ae64905cb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f9c7d2bf-dbe6-561e-a404-717cfd1ce91a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Now we need to use computers for almost everything we do.', NULL, NULL),
  ('731b30ec-1257-552d-8ba9-389a4754cfd5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '731b30ec-1257-552d-8ba9-389a4754cfd5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0b3626c3-87b9-5f03-9312-4b07a95c53d1'::uuid, NULL, E'The context includes both the land history and the human history.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('731d5e6c-56e8-55fc-b3bd-48fb1ae3a6c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '731d5e6c-56e8-55fc-b3bd-48fb1ae3a6c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'US Market', E'The United States is at present the world''s market for motor cars and trucks. An agent for the U.S. Bureau of Foreign and Domestic Commerce reports a prosperous condition of affairs prevailing in Japan, which is buying more automobiles, especially large cars, than ever before.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('731f6936-87e6-531e-8b34-11f7381ee569'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '731f6936-87e6-531e-8b34-11f7381ee569'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the main ingredient in chocolate?', 'e3832de1-e17b-55ee-bd37-ce692a02c960'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cocoa', NULL, NULL),
  ('73202752-b716-5949-8445-a0bc02c7a940'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73202752-b716-5949-8445-a0bc02c7a940'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lightning Strike Incident', E'A drop in the incidence of lightning strikes could impact {{1}} the frequency of wildfires, especially in tropical regions. It could also lower the incidence of lightning strikes to infrastructure and affect how greenhouse gases in the atmosphere contribute to climate change. Scientists from the Universities of Edinburgh and Leeds and Lancaster University used a newly devised method to calculate the likely incidence of lightning flashes from storm clouds. {{2}} traditional calculations of lightning flashes at the global scale, which are based on the height of clouds, their approach takes into account the movement of tiny ice particles that form and move within clouds. Electrical charges build {{3}} in these ice particles, and in cold water droplets and soft hail formed inside clouds. These {{4}} during storms, giving rise to lightning flashes and thunder.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.on, 2.Unlike, 3.up, 4.are discharged', NULL, NULL),
  ('732393f3-70d6-576e-a16a-3f36ba678399'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '732393f3-70d6-576e-a16a-3f36ba678399'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indie Rock Aesthetic', E'Plants & Animals are a Montreal-based indie rock {{1}} that began playing together as kids. Touring {{2}} for about five years after their proper full-length debut in 2008, they pretty much made their records on the go until 2013. So the band''s decision to be slow, deliberate, and thorough on their latest offering Waltzed In From The Rumbling, represents a major change of pace. Finally sleeping in there in own beds while recording, the band assembled the album over the course of nine seasons. It''s a return to their origins, but it also pushes audaciously forward. The {{3}} varies wildly and wonderfully from track to track, each song having its own hermetic seal but somehow still melding {{4}} as a body of work. Jangling guitars, drums leaning toward the off-kilter swing of J Dilla, found sounds, a hint of shoegaze, and {{5}} instrumentation come together to keep the ear constantly {{6}} with a feeling of constant evolution. They found an antique guiro next to broken VCR and recorded both. They made an empty fridge sound like a timpani drum. They recorded gossip on a city bus. They brought in classical string flourishes. They sometimes left mistakes if they felt they were perfectly imperfect. It''s truly DIY, but with a feel of big production value that makes the album soar. Contemplative lyrics anchor the album through all the exploratory {{7}} . The words are delivered melodically, belying their potency, but listening beyond the pretty aesthetic reveals piercing observations and an undeniable translation of feeling. The simplicity of the penetrating refrain on the three-part mini-opus "Je Voulais Te Dire" is a paragon of how the lyrics effortlessly cut through the instrumentation. Guitarist or vocalist Warren Spicer sings "It''s only loving, but you want it bad." encompassing how we try to avoid and downplay our desire for love and affection, but ultimately search and long for it anyway.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.trio, 2.arduously, 3.aesthetic, 4.cohesively, 5.unorthodox, 6.engaged, 7.wandering', NULL, NULL),
  ('7331584b-4ab3-56ba-81ca-f33384aca9cb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7331584b-4ab3-56ba-81ca-f33384aca9cb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Young Artist', E'When the young artist was asked about his drawing, he explained that he had started by taking a photograph of himself sitting by a window at home. He then drew his face from the photograph and replaced the buildings which were outside the window with trees. This gave the picture a softer, more artistic background.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
