  ('7377b974-3958-5bb2-a603-f31548578aa1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7377b974-3958-5bb2-a603-f31548578aa1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bird''s Positioning', E'Birds have a variety of methods by which they are able to find their way across the flyways, year in, and year out. It seems that birds employ different geo-positioning strategies according to the conditions encountered during migration. They seem able to use the position of the sun and stars, the Earth''s magnetic field, smells and even landmarks to find their way.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('737906e3-0c6d-560d-9a9f-5a29fb419f7a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '737906e3-0c6d-560d-9a9f-5a29fb419f7a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Voice and Text', E'The terms ''voice'' and ''text'' are multifaceted. Both have a wide range of possible meanings in everyday speech and academic usage. You may encounter the two words used in a variety of ways, in connection with different subjects, and they won''t always mean exactly the same thing.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('737b62ef-bdb2-5f92-862d-8179b1fcdf83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '737b62ef-bdb2-5f92-862d-8179b1fcdf83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '77e04ee8-421e-5b1b-9008-bf9fcc259004'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some bad stuff comes from plants and animals we know.', NULL, NULL),
  ('73802991-7167-53fc-93f1-5190b964a565'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73802991-7167-53fc-93f1-5190b964a565'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Good Looks', E'It is tempting to try to prove that good looks win votes, and many academics have tried. The {{1}} is that beauty is in the eye of the beholder, and you cannot behold a politician''s face without a veil of extraneous {{2}} getting in the way. Does George Bush possess a disarming grin or a facetious {{3}} ? It''s hard to find anyone who can look at the president without assessing him politically as well as {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.difficulty, 2.prejudice, 3.smirk, 4.physically', NULL, NULL),
  ('73828c52-7965-5a2d-8eb3-826aebe1cb4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73828c52-7965-5a2d-8eb3-826aebe1cb4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What can be added to a drink to cool it down on a hot day?', '2dc8c7dc-d8bc-5ea5-8744-2b46823b10a6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ice', NULL, NULL),
  ('73880dd5-cd28-5376-b53a-a54a03f37fc6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73880dd5-cd28-5376-b53a-a54a03f37fc6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Different Lifestyle', E'Some people work long hours to achieve success, but others feel that we should spend more free time for fun than for money. Which lifestyle do you prefer? Explain your opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('738beccc-ea05-58d7-9f3b-979cbbf0ee91'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '738beccc-ea05-58d7-9f3b-979cbbf0ee91'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Suffrage Movement', E'The Women''s Suffrage Movement was a decades-long fight to secure the right to vote for women. Emerging in the mid-19th century, this movement represented a radical challenge to the {{1}} social and political order. Leaders like Susan B. Anthony, Elizabeth Cady Stanton, and Emmeline Pankhurst became icons of the struggle for gender equality. The movement {{2}} a range of tactics, from peaceful protests and lobbying to civil disobedience. Despite {{3}} significant opposition and ridicule, suffragists persevered, driven by a deep conviction in the principles of equality and democratic participation. In the end, their hard work paid off, and women in many countries finally got the right to vote around the late 1800s and early 1900s. The movement did not just {{4}} voting rights for women; it also opened doors for future advancements in women''s rights. It {{5}} a powerful example of activism and solidarity in the pursuit of social justice.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.existing, 2.utilized, 3.facing, 4.secure, 5.remains', NULL, NULL),
  ('738de9ce-1cb6-5ccc-bffd-c4083de3fead'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '738de9ce-1cb6-5ccc-bffd-c4083de3fead'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you use to light a stove?', '639f53c5-63d0-543a-a1e6-747854fe85fb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Igniter / lighter / match', NULL, NULL),
  ('738f3ca2-a18d-5324-8445-aff520a76902'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '738f3ca2-a18d-5324-8445-aff520a76902'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0605f103-a2d2-553d-b5b8-07f898f529ce'::uuid, NULL, E'Learning how to persuade people is helpful for talking to others.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('73929ea3-cde2-5a97-a1f9-550a16e87093'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73929ea3-cde2-5a97-a1f9-550a16e87093'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Infinite Monkey Theorem', NULL, 'fc632fc0-b05b-5808-a549-6cc59e09ed6d'::uuid, NULL, E'This illustration often used is the one that the monkeys and the typewriters. Ok, we have a monkey sitting at a typewriter and the claim here is basically if you leave chance in time long enough you will get life. Don''t worry about it. Yes, its''s strange. Yes, it''s wonderful. But leave enough matter 600 million years on earth and you will have life. So, the monkey sitting at the typewriter, the chances are eventually he produces the complete works of Shakespeare. So what''s the problem. But he doesn''t manage to do it in 600 million years. So, what I decided to do is run the numbers. I, instead of saying typing the complete work of Shakespeare, I just run the numbers for how long would it take a monkey, typing one key striker a second, to type ''to be or not to be that is the question''. Right? On average how long is it gonna take my monkey friend one keystroke a second. I don''t know how you think it would be. Maybe you could have a guess. Would it be less or more than 600 million years, which is the period life on earth isn''t supposed to have emerged within. And when I run the numbers ''to be or not to be is the question'' takes 12.6 trillion trillion trillion years to type just that phrase. And a DNA string, that complexity, emerges by chance undirected within 600 million years. Again, it''s mathematically possible but it''s so incredibly unlikely that, it would have, that it tilts me in favor of the Christian story in which God creating life, simply a question of saying let that be and there was.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7395c68b-f939-5c47-90c8-97dcea5cdd2c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7395c68b-f939-5c47-90c8-97dcea5cdd2c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fish Farms', E'Coastal fish farms seem to do less harm to nearby plants and animals than previously believed, a new study {{1}} . And marine ecosystems can recover from this damage {{2}} fast. But the analysis of a single trout farm in a Faroe Islands fjord over nearly a year also shows that these facilities need to be {{3}} carefully, and that there''s a limit to how many can {{4}} in a particular area before its biodiversity suffers lasting harm. In coastal farms, fish live in large cages hanging from pontoons on the surface. Fish feces and uneaten food sink to the seabed, affecting its ecosystem. Badly-managed farms can also have serious {{5}} on the surrounding water column.\nThe team monitored the cages, {{6}} containing some 770,000 young trout. They measured the flow of the vital nutrients carbon and nitrogen through the system, also tracking the farmer’s activities, changing water conditions and the quantity of waste deposited on the seabed below.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reveals, 2.surprisingly, 3.placed, 4.operate, 5.effects, 6.initially', NULL, NULL),
  ('739b9749-93d3-5812-af8b-34e8909f26f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '739b9749-93d3-5812-af8b-34e8909f26f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Focus Groups', NULL, '0e891163-1d51-5cd1-ad82-731c308f534b'::uuid, NULL, E'OK - to help you with your research, I just wanted to give you some tips today on using Focus Groups. These are groups of people that you get together to find out about their opinions and attitudes, for example, to review a piece of work or just basically provide some collective input to help you with whatever you''re researching.\nFirst of all, how large should a focus group be? Well, I would say that an ideal number of participants is around six or seven. If it''s any bigger, what quite often happens is they break into side-conversations and the focus is lost. If it''s any smaller, you may not get the range of views that you need to get a really good discussion.\nSecondly, it''s important that you have a moderator for the group, who''s able to facilitate and guide the discussions. The moderator must ensure that everyone participates and stop anyone dominating. And also, the moderator needs to make sure that the discussions don''t go off in the wrong direction.\nAnd thirdly, in order to help the group focus on what''s required, some basic materials should be used particularly to kick-start the discussions. This may be in the form of pictures, photos, diagrams, graphs, etc. And will help the group to understand the context of what needs to be discussed.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('73a49a17-f72a-5712-a551-82bd79c32035'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73a49a17-f72a-5712-a551-82bd79c32035'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heartbeat', E'Drivers may be more likely to crash if an obstacle appears at the same time as a heartbeat. To investigate how the beat of our hearts influences our {{1}} times, Sarah Garfinkel at the University of Sussex, UK, and her colleagues designed a virtual reality driving game. While participants were driving, obstacles would appear in the road, either in time with a heartbeat or between beats. When objects coincided with heartbeats, drivers’ reaction times were slower and they were more likely to {{2}} . Garfinkel presented the results at New Scientist Live in London on Thursday, where she discussed the possible effect of systoles – the squeezing of the heart ventricles that occurs in the middle of a heartbeat – on driving. “If you’re driving and you’re in a highly {{3}} state and your heart is beating strong and fast, you will have more cardiac systoles, and that is going to impair your reaction time and ability to avoid objects,” she said.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.reaction, 2.crash, 3.aroused', NULL, NULL),
  ('73adebcd-6400-5f53-8a1f-46e89858248a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '73adebcd-6400-5f53-8a1f-46e89858248a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7968d8cc-aeb2-5be5-b9f6-18c242dbe83b'::uuid, NULL, E'The eyesight can be corrected in minutes by the use of a laser.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
