  ('77b2c096-c478-575b-92c6-c160703365b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77b2c096-c478-575b-92c6-c160703365b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a baby kangaroo?', '94f80332-19c9-5f5f-aa3e-e4867beefebd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Joey', NULL, NULL),
  ('77b91c31-aacf-5084-ad46-7ea39e067647'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77b91c31-aacf-5084-ad46-7ea39e067647'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High‐fat Diet', E'While endurance exercise can effectively burn fat during physical activity, new research has uncovered muscles’ remarkable ability to process and consume fat for energy. Indeed, the fat being burned can be sourced from muscles’ internal storage as well as fat circulating within the blood. However, this natural fat‐burning capacity has clear biological boundaries and cannot be infinitely improved.\nRecently, some researchers have been investigating whether a high‐fat diet can further increase the rate of fat burning in human bodies. Their studies have shown that it can indeed enhance fat oxidation. However, this positive effect has only been observed in elite or well‐conditioned athletes rather than ordinary people. The article also mentioned the names of the researchers involved and explained the complex physiological mechanism behind this phenomenon. In the final section, it discussed the potential health risks of such a diet. Therefore, if your diet contains excessive fat over a long period of time, you face serious health risks such as high blood pressure.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('77be6c0d-50f6-55d8-9161-6fd52c998af7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77be6c0d-50f6-55d8-9161-6fd52c998af7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b1985221-5a75-5c80-8f90-d3e7d715774f'::uuid, NULL, E'Please be careful when using online translation programs.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('77bf05f0-e0a8-58b6-827b-f21dcb6fbdc5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77bf05f0-e0a8-58b6-827b-f21dcb6fbdc5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the period between childhood and adulthood?', 'bb51e481-6d03-5613-a7e8-34364f54fd86'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Adolescence / puberty', NULL, NULL),
  ('77bfb3fb-983b-5dfb-a6bb-7bb6a7a3a05b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77bfb3fb-983b-5dfb-a6bb-7bb6a7a3a05b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '88125c7f-7e42-5645-b1b4-bda01e26ab4e'::uuid, NULL, E'Rising consumer sales in the first half of the year spurred the economy to faster growth.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('77c3f542-f90c-5934-a5c8-d8dd5e5a7a5a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77c3f542-f90c-5934-a5c8-d8dd5e5a7a5a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c46dcbfe-b225-5e22-8eb8-7ff8c8c19ea3'::uuid, NULL, E'Without action, the possibility of energy shortages looms in the future.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('77ce6444-01cf-552d-8397-9f337a91d5b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77ce6444-01cf-552d-8397-9f337a91d5b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Intelligent People', E'Very intelligent people often make the {{1}} of assuming that other people''s minds work in the same way as theirs do. Economists, for example, create mathematically-based models on the {{2}} that people act rationally as far as their own economic {{3}} are concerned. You don''t have to look much further than family and friends to see how off the {{4}} this idea is. The problem with a lot of such scientifically-based theories is that they are not friendly to facts that don''t {{5}} the case.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.mistake, 2.notion, 3.interests, 4.mark, 5.fit', NULL, NULL),
  ('77cfa094-686c-53d5-b038-c93c031b6b60'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77cfa094-686c-53d5-b038-c93c031b6b60'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b302c1ec-8019-5ecd-8394-560c32f2d71e'::uuid, NULL, E'At the end of the ice age there would have been enormous changes in animal and plant life.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('77d0d934-dca9-52f8-9329-e3712e20ad87'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77d0d934-dca9-52f8-9329-e3712e20ad87'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Creative Imagination', E'To reach some kind of understanding of a period in the past - the Middle Ages, say- requires a creative act of the imagination not unlike that of a novelist getting inside the skins of their characters or establishing the environment they live in. What must it have been like to be a peasant under a feudal baron? What might his beliefs and politics have been? Did he, for example, think his situation was simply part of the natural order of things, or that it was grossly unfair and needed to be overthrown?\nSo, you have to imagine the terms under which life was lived in those days, and learn to feel in a different way about things by putting yourself into a world very different from your own. Now, of course, every age views the past from its own present and an 18th century historian''s concept of the Middle Ages will be very different from that of one from the 21st century- which is why each age has to write its history over again. It''s not so much that more facts or evidence come to light- if they do- but that sensibilities change too.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'bbdbba43-a08c-5e4d-bfc6-97e918974f7a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To understand the past, one must think as people of the period did (e.g., medieval peasants). But due to changing sensibilities, each era has a slightly different view of the same past, regardless of facts.', NULL, NULL),
  ('77d2482e-6203-5c0e-8b7e-e093245930c8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '77d2482e-6203-5c0e-8b7e-e093245930c8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gambling Scenario', E'New research has shown robots can encourage humans to take greater risks in a simulated gambling scenario than they would if there was nothing to influence their behaviors. Increasing our understanding of whether robots can affect risk- taking could have clear ethical, practical and policy implications, which this study set out to explore.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
