  ('783259b8-133d-5638-9a9c-d16c14693105'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783259b8-133d-5638-9a9c-d16c14693105'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '62ad1649-7ac5-5c13-bfd7-3658cf0f9123'::uuid, NULL, E'New scientific discoveries about ancient people have been made every year by scientists.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7836fc5f-c43f-5bf0-8d55-c2c49b66396a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7836fc5f-c43f-5bf0-8d55-c2c49b66396a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cold-blooded Fish', E'Cold-blooded animals, such as fish, rely heavily on the surrounding water temperature to {{1}} their body heat. When the water temperature rises, the fish''s body temperature also rises, {{2}} to increased metabolic activity. This means they swim faster, breathe quicker, and require more oxygen and food. Conversely, when the water temperature falls, their metabolism slows down, making them more {{3}} and less active.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.regulate, 2.leading, 3.sluggish', NULL, NULL),
  ('783837b9-992a-515b-ad90-40538aac9059'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783837b9-992a-515b-ad90-40538aac9059'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '80718102-c9f8-50a2-8a55-b4da4acc883a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The celebrated theory is still the source of great controversy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('783ad1ca-978d-5720-9d5a-88e83310690f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783ad1ca-978d-5720-9d5a-88e83310690f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '35b6d25c-5950-5380-b7cd-a00cceabe6c6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Printers now automatically print stuff on both paper sides.', NULL, NULL),
  ('783b5207-9c9e-5ad3-9798-6224b07eed6c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783b5207-9c9e-5ad3-9798-6224b07eed6c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Muscle’s Benefits', E'Muscle is a star player in keeping your body happy and healthy in the long-term, for several reasons. For starters, lean muscle mass can help manage blood sugar, keeping type 2 diabetes at bay. In fact, one 2017 cohort study found a negative association between muscle mass and risk of developing of type 2 diabetes. “The number one consumer of blood sugar in the human body is skeletal muscle,” says Tim Church, a professor of preventive medicine. So, the more muscle you have, the greater your potential to metabolize blood sugar.\nAlso, as you age, you’ll want a healthy amount of muscle, rather than fat. “Muscle is a commonly overlooked marker of healthy aging,” Church says. You lose about 1-2% of muscle mass starting around age 40 or 45, he adds. This age-related decline in muscle is known as sarcopenia, and it’s one of the biggest reasons many older adults can no longer do simple tasks without help. “You can’t put your jacket on, you can’t push yourself off the toilet, and you can’t get yourself off the ground after you fall,” Church says. “It all comes down to strength and muscle mass.”\nWhat’s even better news is that muscle can further help you maintain a healthy weight by raising your basal metabolic rate, or the number of calories you burn at rest. “That number has been widely discussed and argued over the years,” saysJoel Seedman, a neuromuscular physiologist. “But we do know the more muscle you have, the faster your metabolism.”\nLastly and least importantly, at least pertaining to health, the density of muscle might cause it to weigh more, it also means it takes up less space in the body. “If someone gains 10 pounds of muscle, a lot of times they’ll barely notice that on their body,” Seedman says.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('783f5cc2-f22a-59a3-973d-e9f8d4798f4e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783f5cc2-f22a-59a3-973d-e9f8d4798f4e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dairy-tech', E'Now, one tech startup wants to take wearables to another market: cows. The company’s “mooON” device goes around the animal’s leg, and {{1}} their activity levels. When cows are sick, they move less, and when they are ovulating, they move more. Stellapps combines information from the step trackers with data that farmers and vets enter into a smartphone app, which {{2}} reminders for routine protocols such as vaccinations and artificial insemination. Healthier cows produce more milk, and by tracking and better managing their animals, so farmers can increase {{3}} . In India, Stellapps uses an ultrasonic analyzer to measure the nutritional content of the milk. At the unit, volume sensors monitor the milk to prevent it from being watered down or stolen, says Mukundan. From there, the milk is taken to a processing plant to be pasteurized and packaged, or {{4}} into products like cheese or yogurt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.tracks, 2.issues, 3.yields, 4.converted', NULL, NULL),
  ('783f6f2b-591e-56a6-810f-f83651a724fd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783f6f2b-591e-56a6-810f-f83651a724fd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gray Wolf', E'The gray wolf is an extremely adaptable species and is one of those animal species that survived the last ice age. The gray wolf''s physical characteristics enabled it to adapt quickly to the harsh conditions of the ice age, and its cunning and adaptation helped it survive in the changing environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('783fc7bb-2f2f-57dc-a26c-4c6a4e3eb262'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '783fc7bb-2f2f-57dc-a26c-4c6a4e3eb262'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Super Moon', E'Watchers of the night sky are in for a treat this week with the arrival of what has been {{1}} a Super Flower Blood Moon. The lengthy name is the result of a few astronomical {{2}} coming together at once. The supermoon will be {{3}} all over the world, and the full lunar eclipse can be seen in many parts of the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dubbed, 2.phenomena, 3.visible', NULL, NULL),
  ('7840712b-cfd1-565e-a1ab-cdd2a9cae976'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7840712b-cfd1-565e-a1ab-cdd2a9cae976'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ff1b8e87-7047-547a-b33e-77a68705affe'::uuid, NULL, E'Animal science can be applied to a wide variety of careers and industries.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7841ff3c-6875-5ce2-b2e3-b077d6e36ab3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7841ff3c-6875-5ce2-b2e3-b077d6e36ab3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4a13ec04-5c1e-5c8d-8fa4-8d466e9c0baa'::uuid, NULL, E'Please close the door behind you when you leave the room.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('784866dc-6d6b-547e-ab79-be1aa7c6ef23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '784866dc-6d6b-547e-ab79-be1aa7c6ef23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ddc485c0-ac63-5c38-9ea5-edc46e3dc1da'::uuid, NULL, E'Students with queries about this term''s timetables must speak to the tutor immediately.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('784e62da-6c1c-5455-af80-e015d051236e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '784e62da-6c1c-5455-af80-e015d051236e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Global Leadership', E'As we begin the twenty-first century, technological, economic, political, and social forces have created a new era. Technological advancements and lower trade barriers have paved the way for the globalization of markets, bringing intense competition to the U.S. economy. Political systems and movements around the world are having a profound impact on our national security, as well as on our human security. The increasing diversity of our workplaces, schools, and communities is changing the face of our society. To confront the twenty-first century challenges to our economy and national security, our education system must be strengthened to increase the foreign language skills and cultural awareness of our students. America''s continued global leadership will depend on our students'' abilities to interact with the world community both inside and outside our borders.\nMost schools have not responded adequately to these challenges of the twenty-first century, and thus many American students lack sufficient knowledge of other world regions, languages, and cultures. Only about onethird of seventh to twelfth grade students — and just five percent of elementary school students — study a foreign language. Few students study the less-commonly taught "critical languages" that are vital to national security. State high school graduation requirements often include only minimal course work in international studies. At the postsecondary level, fewer than ten percent of college students enroll in a foreign language and only one percent of undergraduates study abroad.', NULL, NULL, E'Technological advancements and lower trade barriers have paved the way for the globalization of markets, while the increasing diversity of our workplaces, schools, and communities is changing the face of our society, so our education system must be strengthened to increase the foreign language skills and cultural awareness of our students, but most schools have not responded adequately, and thus many American students lack sufficient knowledge of other world regions, languages, and cultures.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('785bbb09-829e-5bee-8d47-01a6bbb4c0c8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '785bbb09-829e-5bee-8d47-01a6bbb4c0c8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coronavirus Pandemic', E'The legislation, which Democrats hope to push through the Senate by the weekend, remains among the largest federal relief packages in modern American history. It would deliver hundreds of billions of dollars for vaccine distribution, hospitals, state and local governments and families struggling to recover from the economic toll of the coronavirus pandemic.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('786055e2-024c-5edf-83cb-6036db5c33ed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '786055e2-024c-5edf-83cb-6036db5c33ed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rationing', E'Rationing may be of several types. Informal rationing, which precedes the imposition of formal controls, may consist of admonitions to consumers to reduce their {{1}} or of independent action taken by suppliers in allocating scarce supplies. Rationing according to use prohibits the less important uses of a commodity. Rationing by quantity may limit the hours during {{2}} the commodity is available or may assign quotas of a commodity to all known and approved claimants. Rationing by value limits the amount consumers may spend on commodities that cannot be {{3}} , consumers being allowed to make their own selections within the value limits imposed. Point rationing assigns a point value to each commodity and allocates a certain number of points to each consumer; this system is employed during periods of critical and increasing shortages when individuals begin {{4}} unrationed for rationed items, thereby spreading shortages. Consumers in a rationed economy are usually {{5}} to save by purchasing government bonds or by increasing their deposits in savings banks so that unspent money will not be used for increased purchases of unrationed items or for purchases on the black market.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.consumption, 2.which, 3.standardized, 4.substituting, 5.exhorted', NULL, NULL),
  ('7869f49a-2ea8-589a-8aab-3661eefdf63b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7869f49a-2ea8-589a-8aab-3661eefdf63b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Adaptability', NULL, '02e7dec3-40f2-5546-afe5-bad859ff8e95'::uuid, NULL, E'Today we delve into the essence of Adaptability — a trait not just desirable but essential in our fast-paced world. The ability to adapt is what enables us to navigate the unpredictable tides of life, particularly in our university years, which are a microcosm of the larger journey ahead. Imagine adaptability as a muscle — the more we exercise it, the stronger it becomes. Engaging with diverse cultures and perspectives on campus strengthens this muscle, equipping us with the flexibility to appreciate and assimilate varying viewpoints. It turns the unfamiliar into the familiar, fostering an environment where innovation thrives. Furthermore, adaptability enhances our resilience. It’s not the strongest of species that survives, nor the most intelligent, but the one most responsive to change, as Darwin posited. As we learn to pivot rather than pause in the face of change, we build a foundation for not just surviving but thriving in our chosen fields post-graduation. Let''s embrace adaptability, not as a challenge, but as the key to unlocking a world of possibilities.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('786f44d0-e269-5ef0-9920-d0c1503b30d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '786f44d0-e269-5ef0-9920-d0c1503b30d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Business', E'One {{1}} feature of business is its economic character. In the world of business, we interact with each other not as family members, friends, or neighbors, but as buyers and sellers, employers and employees, and the like. Trading, for example, is often {{2}} by hard bargaining, in which both sides conceal their full hand and perhaps {{3}} in some bluffing. And a skilled salesperson is well - {{4}} in the art of arousing a customer''s attention (sometimes by a bit of puffery) to {{5}} the sale. Still, there is an "ethics of trading" that prohibits the use of false or deceptive claims and tricks such as "bait-and-switch" advertising .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distinguishing, 2.accompanied, 3.engage, 4.versed, 5.clinch', NULL, NULL),
