  ('78f2eb23-e22e-5e81-8c97-41a83abd552b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '78f2eb23-e22e-5e81-8c97-41a83abd552b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '46b137ce-a9de-5827-875f-d7b61ee2aed9'::uuid, NULL, E'A potential solution involves implementing on-demand electric car rental systems.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('78fe4bfc-f923-5ee7-b933-d0fa930769eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '78fe4bfc-f923-5ee7-b933-d0fa930769eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '386b98a4-e44f-5e6a-ac5d-dc85c3ed58cc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The event featured speeches by government leaders including some city councillors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7902352c-3bd4-592d-b87b-3671bcba2984'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7902352c-3bd4-592d-b87b-3671bcba2984'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rosetta Stone', E'When the Rosetta Stone was discovered in 1799, the carved characters that covered its surface were quickly copied. Printer''s ink was applied to the Stone and white paper laid over it. When the paper was removed, it revealed an exact copy of the text—but in reverse. Since then, many copies or "facsimiles" have been made using a variety of materials. Inevitably, the surface of the Stone accumulated many layers of material left over from these activities, despite attempts to remove any residue. Once on display, the grease from many thousands of human hands eager to touch the Stone added to the problem.\nAn opportunity for investigation and cleaning the Rosetta Stone arose when this famous object was made the centerpiece of the Cracking Codes exhibition at The British Museum in 1999. When work commenced to remove all but the original, ancient material, the stone was black with white lettering. As treatment progressed, the different substances uncovered were analyzed. Grease from human handling, a coating of carnauba wax from the early 1800s and printer''s ink from 1799 were cleaned away using cotton wool swabs and liniment of soap, white spirit, acetone and purified water. Finally, white paint in the text, applied in 1981, which had been left in place until now as a protective coating, was removed with cotton swabs and purified water. A small square at the bottom left corner of the face of the stone was left untouched to show the darkened wax and the white infill.', NULL, NULL, E'When the Rosetta Stone was discovered in 1799, the carved characters that covered its surface were quickly copied, so inevitably, the surface of the Stone accumulated many layers of material left over from these activities, while an opportunity for investigation and cleaning the Rosetta Stone arose, and the different substances uncovered were analyzed, where a small square at the bottom left corner was left untouched to show the darkened wax and the white infill.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('790ac6d2-6068-56e7-96d0-09332bd18ba5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '790ac6d2-6068-56e7-96d0-09332bd18ba5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Prior Knowledge', E'What is known as prior knowledge (or pre-existing knowledge) is the knowledge, skill or ability that a learner brings to a new learning encounter. This includes all knowledge that is available before the learning event, and which has been gathered or developed by any means, and in any situation, including both formal and, quite often, informal learning situations. Learners need enough previous knowledge and understanding to enable them to learn new things; they also need help making links with new and previous explicit knowledge.\nIt is considered to be valuable to go through a process of what has been called "activating prior knowledge". Teachers often go through this process at the beginning of a new topic. They also use introductory strategies at the beginning of lessons which are continuations from previous lessons. In terms of the practicalities of teaching, this is a process of making children think about the topic or remember what has been covered already. In terms of theory, it is to do with activating particular schemas.', NULL, NULL, E'What is known as prior knowledge (or pre-existing knowledge) is the knowledge, skill or ability that a learner brings to a new learning encounter, and learners need enough previous knowledge and understanding to enable them to learn new things, so it is considered to be valuable to go through a process of what has been called "activating prior knowledge", while in terms of theory, it is to do with activating particular schemas.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('790f1499-78fd-51e8-a74b-de3221d47ecd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '790f1499-78fd-51e8-a74b-de3221d47ecd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'International Journal', E'The international journal of design is a peer-reviewed, open access journal devoted to publishing research papers in all fields of design, including industrial design, visual communication design, interface design, animation and game design, architectural design, urban design, and other design related fields. It aims to provide an international forum for the {{1}} of ideas and findings from researchers across different cultures and encourages research on the impact of cultural factors {{2}} design theory and practice. It also seeks to promote the {{3}} of knowledge between professionals in academia and industry by emphasizing research in {{4}} results are of interest or applicable to design practices.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exchange, 2.on, 3.transfer, 4.which', NULL, NULL),
  ('79167d62-cb4c-5e64-bb7a-4514d5873ea1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79167d62-cb4c-5e64-bb7a-4514d5873ea1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'United Nations', E'The United Nations is an international organization founded in 1945. Due to its unique international character, and the powers vested in its founding Charter, the organization can take {{1}} on a wide range of issues and provide a forum for its 193 Member States to {{2}} their views, through the General Assembly, the Security Council, the Economic and Social Council and other bodies and committees. The work of the United Nations reaches every {{3}} of the globe. Although best known for peacekeeping, peacebuilding, conflict {{4}} and humanitarian assistance, there are many other ways the United Nations and its System (specialized agencies, funds and programs) affect our lives and make the world a better place.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.action, 2.express, 3.corner, 4.prevention', NULL, NULL),
  ('791f2489-2ab2-543d-94c4-003c543dc91f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '791f2489-2ab2-543d-94c4-003c543dc91f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Blood', E'I hate the sight of blood. Looking at it makes me go all weak at the knees. I can’t even look at my own blood. I don’t know why. The thing I hate most is giving blood for a medical check. I fainted once after I saw my blood in a small bottle. If I have a nose bleed, I have to sit down for 30 minutes before I feel better. It’s impossible for me to watch operations on TV. I wish I could donate blood to others. I can’t. I know giving blood is really important, but I’m not brave enough. One thing about blood I do find interesting is blood types. I think your blood type can affect your personality. I know that in some countries, people with blood type A would not be a good romantic match for someone with blood type O.\n\nWhat is my attitude to blood?', '333715aa-0d29-52c0-99d3-e7f44352f99d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'I faint when I see my own blood.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7920f248-dece-5655-abd8-c068d2e35b5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7920f248-dece-5655-abd8-c068d2e35b5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the device that converts sound into electrical signals and back to sound?', 'f33c945e-e5ac-55a4-a5cb-0725b2863a13'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Microphone', NULL, NULL),
  ('792d248f-389e-5900-980a-339741ba9492'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '792d248f-389e-5900-980a-339741ba9492'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drainage', E'Although a plethora of issues might result in drainage problems at present, certain situations have been witnessed which are more typical than the others. The primary reason behind crawl spaces and {{1}} basements is that it is not possible to drain the water away from the residence appropriately. Most of the time, the reason for this happens to be the gutters. Either the spigots have become {{2}} blocked or they are not pointed away from the house as needed, and the water is not following the appropriate route and is getting {{3}} in locations around the base, resulting in structural as well as landscape damage. It has also been observed that several types of individuals require drainage solutions after {{4}} a new landscaping venture. It is very important to grade your backyard, and even landscapers forget regarding this every now and then. Therefore, if you are thinking of beautifying your garden, always keep in mind to grade away from your residence!', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.inundated, 2.excessively, 3.accumulated, 4.completing', NULL, NULL),
  ('79320d4f-0621-5b72-86b5-30bee059fd99'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79320d4f-0621-5b72-86b5-30bee059fd99'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Great Barrier Reef', E'One of Australia''s most remarkable natural gifts, the Great Barrier Reef is blessed with the breathtaking beauty of the world''s largest coral reef. The reef contains an {{1}} of marine life and is comprised of over 3000 individual reef systems and coral cays and literally hundreds of {{2}} tropical islands with some of the world''s most beautiful sun-soaked, golden beaches. Because of its natural beauty, the Great Barrier Reef has become one of the world''s most {{3}} -after tourist destinations. A visitor to the Great Barrier Reef can enjoy many {{4}} including snorkeling, scuba diving, aircraft or helicopter tours, bare boats (self- sail) glass-bottomed boat viewing, semi-submersibles and educational trips, cruise ship tours, whale watching and swimming with dolphins.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.abundance, 2.picturesque, 3.sought, 4.experiences', NULL, NULL),
  ('793248a1-9711-51f6-99d1-a51aa1f2c2ec'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '793248a1-9711-51f6-99d1-a51aa1f2c2ec'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Music', E'For many, music is an essential part of life, enriching experiences and {{1}} people across boundaries. It has the power to evoke deep emotions and to influence mood, {{2}} language and cultural barriers. The study of music''s psychological impact reveals its {{3}} to affect cognitive processes, memory, and social interaction. Whether as a form of entertainment, a tool for therapy, or a {{4}} for academic study, music remains an enduring element of human culture.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.connecting, 2.transcending, 3.capacity, 4.subject', NULL, NULL),
