  ('79e2e3a4-833c-5c4b-a927-4fe15ec9b80d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79e2e3a4-833c-5c4b-a927-4fe15ec9b80d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f1dfdb48-2d06-50ca-80e0-08423d4b9de5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The new construction project includes gigantic gas terminals and pipelines.', NULL, NULL),
  ('79e4e8f7-e77b-56f7-b30d-4007c8f75822'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79e4e8f7-e77b-56f7-b30d-4007c8f75822'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '209cfa0b-4e6e-58f4-a074-1aba672b8e3a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We need to raise public awareness of the issue.', NULL, NULL),
  ('79e7e83f-ab88-5620-837f-eefacbe3979e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79e7e83f-ab88-5620-837f-eefacbe3979e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Maya Site', E'Geologists have discovered a massive Maya site that {{1}} approximately 650 square miles. The findings were the result of an aerial survey that researchers {{2}} via airplane using lidar, in which lasers are beamed out and the reflected light is used to create {{3}} imagery of a landscape. Using data from the scans, the team {{4}} more than 1,000 settlements dotting the region.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.stretches, 2.conducted, 3.aerial, 4.identified', NULL, NULL),
  ('79ed249a-b2b0-572c-b96c-424c3c2fb1dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79ed249a-b2b0-572c-b96c-424c3c2fb1dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-R', E'In 1861, Matthew Brady, a well-known portrait photographer, approached President Lincoln requesting permission to move freely about the country photographing the Civil War. Lincoln granted him permission to travel anywhere with the Union armies, and his record of this conflict brought home to millions the horrors of war.\nBrady wasn''t the first official war photographer. Six years earlier, Roger Fenton, a lawyer and amateur photographer, had returned from the Crimea, having been personally chosen by Queen Victoria and Prince Albert. However, his instructions were more likely to have been to send back work that boosted morale back home rather than the terrible realities of war.\nBrady''s coverage of the war made him a household name, but he had hundreds of assistants, and it''s even possible that he didn''t take any of the 7,000 pictures that were marketed under his name. But no one else could have organized the large army of photographers needed to cover the broad sweep of the war and provided access to many leading generals and politicians.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true of Matthew Brady?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'He was given permission to travel anywhere in the US.\nHe was able to give his photographers introductions to politicians.\nHe was responsible for organizing a large number of photographers.', NULL, NULL),
  ('79ee5406-8fcd-554f-85a7-b01cf1d72334'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79ee5406-8fcd-554f-85a7-b01cf1d72334'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fda35cb1-6f40-5292-8142-df67f6e09e98'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The year when the ship of artifacts was wrecked interested historians.', NULL, NULL),
  ('79f71207-b0d4-5c5b-b12d-0d37a574a75d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79f71207-b0d4-5c5b-b12d-0d37a574a75d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Television', NULL, '7dcd1c1b-3a5d-500d-8873-2e2ace1e96de'::uuid, NULL, E'Television—the most pervasive and persuasive of modern technologies, marked by rapid change and growth-is moving into a new era, an era of extraordinary sophistication and versatility, which promises to reshape our lives and our world. It is an electronic revolution of sorts, made possible by the marriage of television and computer technologies.\nThe word "television", derived4 from its Greek (tele: distant) and Latin (visio: sight) roots, can literally5 be interpreted as sight from a distance. Very simply put, it works in this way: through a sophisticated system of electronics, television provides the capability6 of converting an image (focused on a special photoconductive plate within a camera) into electronic impulses, which can be sent through a wire or cable. These impulses, when fed into a receiver (television set), can then be electronically reconstituted into that same image.\nTelevision is more than just an electronic system, however. It is a means of expression, as well as a vehicle for communication, and as such becomes a powerful tool for reaching other human beings.\nThe field of television can be divided into two categories determined by its means of transmission. First, there is broadcast television, which reaches the masses through broad-based airwave transmission of television signals. Second, there is nonbroadcast television, which provides for the needs of individuals or specific interest groups through controlled transmission techniques.\nTraditionally, television has been a medium of the masses. We are most familiar with broadcast television because it has been with us for about thirty-seven years in a form similar to what exists today. During those years, it has been controlled, for the most part, by the broadcast networks, ABC, NBC, and CBS, who have been the major purveyors of news, information, and entertainment. These giants of broadcasting have actually shaped not only television but our perception of it as well. We have come to look upon the picture tube as a source of entertainment, placing our role in this dynamic medium as the passive viewer.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('79f89397-5f94-59dc-aaee-b65715d53f01'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79f89397-5f94-59dc-aaee-b65715d53f01'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Remains of Planet', E'In the 1980s, geophysicists made a startling discovery: two continent-sized blobs of unusual material were found deep near the center of the Earth, one beneath the African continent and one beneath the Pacific Ocean. Each blob is twice the size of the Moon and likely composed of different proportions of elements than the mantle surrounding it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('79f954cb-c9f3-5dbc-99c4-6146cbf19872'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79f954cb-c9f3-5dbc-99c4-6146cbf19872'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1dfccf06-c3ba-5219-acdb-a40d30bf11ef'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Please notify us when you have received the course textbook.', NULL, NULL),
  ('79ffe936-8edc-5282-bf8f-1697e67948d6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '79ffe936-8edc-5282-bf8f-1697e67948d6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Balanced Diet', E'A balanced diet is crucial for maintaining good health. It provides the nutrients and energy needed for optimal bodily function and can prevent chronic diseases such as cancer, diabetes, and heart disease. By eating a variety of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats, we can ensure that our body receives the nutrients it needs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a01b6eb-0da0-5255-b05e-5fefd8b02f71'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a01b6eb-0da0-5255-b05e-5fefd8b02f71'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8f7922be-4af0-538f-99a2-3b033687811f'::uuid, NULL, E'A tutor is a teacher that usually specializes in one particular subject.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a01fb88-e741-565a-a634-e6de7c67a923'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a01fb88-e741-565a-a634-e6de7c67a923'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '286c88ae-19eb-54ce-b5fb-5329d7c09516'::uuid, NULL, E'The concepts in this thesis were not new.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a034613-9e89-5c10-b343-9dd2f8ed3df9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a034613-9e89-5c10-b343-9dd2f8ed3df9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If a newspaper published every day is daily, a magazine published every week is weekly, what do we call a magazine published four times a year?', 'd35898b0-5f2e-541e-8d07-6e83f2d0e7c1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Quarterly', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a14674b-c6fe-5556-bd3e-cbc0b58847c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a14674b-c6fe-5556-bd3e-cbc0b58847c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the medicine that is used against headache?', 'e398d1c8-a9d1-5a50-977e-05579d9557b5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pain killer / painkiller', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a180262-36fb-578f-8555-383eb509a927'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a180262-36fb-578f-8555-383eb509a927'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Life Expectancy', E'People are generally living longer than previous generations across most parts of the world. Rising life expectancy is a result of advances in medicine as well as improving living standards and healthier lifestyles. But while this should be {{1}} for social reasons, is it beneficial in economic terms? Does the increase in the older population create an economic burden on society or can older people be mobilized to {{2}} the productivity of communities in which they work and live? New analysis of international data from 35 countries, published by the International Longevity Centre, provides more evidence in favor of a ''longevity dividend''. The authors found that as life expectancy increases, so {{3}} ''output per hour worked, per worker and per capita''.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.celebrated, 2.enhance, 3.does', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a1e4b92-a29b-53de-8570-75ac0b9d0c24'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a1e4b92-a29b-53de-8570-75ac0b9d0c24'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f9e8778b-0f3e-5836-a894-baee7129e87f'::uuid, NULL, E'Market research surveys might be conducted by telephone, the internet, or in person.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a1e4e42-244b-5040-b450-c50761f3ede2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a1e4e42-244b-5040-b450-c50761f3ede2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What kind of thing can play the role of protection that oranges and bananas all have?', 'f1e45842-b166-5f37-8531-9b087c145a17'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Peel', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a2397f0-a185-564e-b178-5520419eb116'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a2397f0-a185-564e-b178-5520419eb116'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bb0a5a60-edf5-5da9-88ed-0a1d2c1b13c7'::uuid, NULL, E'There will be a significant rise in tuition fees starting next year.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a25557b-56d8-538d-ac00-8e7ff3c98a2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a25557b-56d8-538d-ac00-8e7ff3c98a2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite of a bride?', '3e3f96de-9f15-5fe2-97cd-fa06f5c4ac61'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bridegroom / groom', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a385fcb-eea6-5308-88b5-fc875216a2b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a385fcb-eea6-5308-88b5-fc875216a2b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rapid Change', E'An environment of rapid change, technological innovations and increasing business competitiveness has highlighted the growing importance of management development. In particular, the general movement towards great employee involvement and making things happen through people has emphasized an integrating rather than a controlling style of management.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a3e6470-2151-5781-b4e1-ac6c1d36360a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a3e6470-2151-5781-b4e1-ac6c1d36360a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'City or Countryside', E'Some people prefer to live in cities, while some people prefer to live in the countryside. Which is better for you? Give your reasons or experience.', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether living in cities is better than living in the countryside has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that the convenience of leisure and entertainment in cities is greater when compared with the inadequate educational resources in the countryside, whereas opponents contend that rural living is preferable. From my perspective, I am convinced that living in cities is better than living in the countryside.\nTo begin with, I think city life is more convenient because it offers better services, facilities, and transportation. For example, grocery stores, large supermarkets, and shopping malls provide daily necessities easily. In addition to this, restaurants and delivery apps offer more accessible food options. Other than that, public transport like subways, buses, and taxis makes commuting fast and affordable. It is thus shown that city living is better than life in the countryside.\nBesides, I also believe that rural life is less convenient because it lacks high-quality schools, fast internet, and nearby medical care. On top of that, schools in villages are equipped with old classrooms, fewer teachers, and limited hobby groups. Moreover, network connectivity is slow, mobile signals are weak, and online applications often don’t work well. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that rural clinics have fewer doctors and medication, and long wait times for checkups. This clearly proves that living in urban areas has more advantages than living in rural areas.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that ease of everyday living and difficulty in accessing utilities are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that dwelling in cities is superior to dwelling in the countryside.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('7a3fd2c7-96f4-5621-ab78-4edee0c7dfb4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a3fd2c7-96f4-5621-ab78-4edee0c7dfb4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '97f3a448-a685-5d34-9f28-ece0a03ccc39'::uuid, NULL, E'Marks will be deducted for assignments handed in after the due date.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7a421e77-9a52-5765-8ec6-731ef923dd15'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a421e77-9a52-5765-8ec6-731ef923dd15'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gold', E'During the 19th century, the enormous expansion of world production and trade was {{1}} mainly by gold. Even the {{2}} issued by the banks were fully convertible to gold on demand, and this was the basis of their acceptance. However, production and trade were expanding at a faster {{3}} than new {{4}} of gold were being discovered. If trade was to continue growing at this rate, some commodity other than gold also had to be used as a {{5}} of exchange.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.financed, 2.notes, 3.rate, 4.supplies, 5.means', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a43e1cd-2113-5e4a-9731-8158b1e5f9cf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a43e1cd-2113-5e4a-9731-8158b1e5f9cf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'HCS', E'All whales, dolphins, and porpoises are social animals, although the degree of sociability varies greatly from one species to another. Differences of behavior have not evolved by chance. Living in close proximity to other animals has certain costs and benefits, so we can expect the group size adopted by a species to be the most suitable for its environment and lifestyle. River dolphins, for example, have a fairly simple social system, forming small groups of just a few animals- rarely more than ten. On the other hand, many of the oceanic dolphins may roam the seas in groups of thousands. Also, there can be differences within species: for example, with sperm whales, females and juveniles form groups while adult males are solitary. Some of the reasons for living in groups include greater efficiency in searching for and catching food, benefits for mating, learning, defence, and sensory integration. Now, sensory integration is the means by which each animal contributes to the information gained by the group as a whole, and this plays an important part in defence and in the search for food. For example, if one animal discovers a shoal of fish or a hungry shark, it can immediately pass on this information to the others in the group so that all may benefit. A single animal or small group may remain unaware of the food or predator, and so miss a meal or suffer an attack.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'b017c24c-ef10-58b3-8e3a-1a34d5da73b8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Dolphins, whales and porpoises are all social animals, but some species are more sociable than others. This depends on the environment because a species adopts the lifestyle most suitable for this. Among dolphins, forming groups makes it easier for them to find food, reproduce and gain knowledge. They are safer, too, because dolphins can communicate danger when there are threats around.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7a5580e8-d3ac-5188-8930-1136c1a13ccd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a5580e8-d3ac-5188-8930-1136c1a13ccd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Throw-away Society', E'We have entered a throw-away society and have filled the environment with rubbish. What are the causes and what are your solutions?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('7a5abeb4-df34-5c36-bdcf-edb13d45f8c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7a5abeb4-df34-5c36-bdcf-edb13d45f8c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'International Trade', E'International trade allows countries to expand their markets and access goods and services that {{1}} may not have been available domestically. As a {{2}} of international trade, the market is more efficient. This ultimately leads to more competitive pricing and brings {{3}} products to consumers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.otherwise, 2.result, 3.cheaper', NULL, NULL),
