  ('7b129bfc-7943-5c3e-89ed-d5fe681354c2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7b129bfc-7943-5c3e-89ed-d5fe681354c2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cognitive Dissonance', E'Cognitive dissonance is the discomfort a person feels when their behavior does not {{1}} with their values or beliefs. It can also occur when a person holds two {{2}} beliefs at the same time. Cognitive dissonance is not a disease or illness. It is a {{3}} phenomenon that can happen to anyone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.align, 2.contradictory, 3.psychological', NULL, NULL),
  ('7b144069-9886-56fb-b6c8-184c2a2180b0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7b144069-9886-56fb-b6c8-184c2a2180b0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tidal Energy', E'The Australian Renewable Energy Agency (ARENA) has {{1}} $2.49 million to cover a portion of the cost of a collaborative project led by the Australian Maritime College at the University of Tasmania, in {{2}} with The University of Queensland and CSIRO. The $5.85 million ''Tidal Energy in Australia - Assessing Resource and Feasibility to Australia''s Future Energy Mix'' project will map the country''s tidal energy in unprecedented {{3}} before assessing its ability to contribute to Australia''s energy needs.\nLead chief investigator Associate Professor Irene Penesis from the University of Tasmania said the project would help overcome {{4}} to investment in commercial-scale tidal farms in Australia.\n''With some of the largest tides in the world, Australia is {{5}} for this extremely reliable and low-carbon form of energy,'' she said.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.awarded, 2.partnership, 3.detail, 4.barriers, 5.ideal', NULL, NULL),
  ('7b154b44-87e0-537d-bbe4-5d743aaff582'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7b154b44-87e0-537d-bbe4-5d743aaff582'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solar Panel', E'In an unprecedented study of solar panel performance across diverse climatic zones, panels were deployed and {{1}} for their energy output. Initially, all panels performed optimally, but over time, efficiency {{2}} based on regional climatic conditions. Surprisingly, some panels in colder climates {{3}} those in warmer regions. This revelation suggests that solar energy efficiency hinges not solely on sunlight intensity, but {{4}} on a multifaceted interaction of environmental factors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.monitored, 2.varied, 3.outperformed, 4.rather', NULL, NULL),
