  ('7b16eb3c-3da6-5a27-8133-96be5f0bb3e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7b16eb3c-3da6-5a27-8133-96be5f0bb3e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'VR', E'Virtual reality (VR), once a futuristic concept, has cascaded into our daily lives with a vibrant splash, revolutionizing the way we experience digital content. This technological marvel, now accessible through headsets like Oculus Rift and HTC Vive, {{1}} users in a completely artificial world. Its allure lies not just in its novelty but in its {{2}} potential. From gaming to education, VR transcends traditional boundaries, offering an unprecedented level of interaction and engagement. The technology, at its {{3}} , manipulates our sensory perception, creating a convincing illusion of reality. As described in a recent interview with a VR developer, this medium is not just about visual spectacle; it''s about ''crafting experiences that resonate on a human level''. This statement {{4}} the idea that VR''s power lies in its ability to connect with users beyond the visual, tapping into a deeper, emotional response.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.immerses, 2.vast, 3.core, 4.underscores', NULL, NULL),
