  ('7c3b6bb4-1147-527f-b935-08616e94735e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7c3b6bb4-1147-527f-b935-08616e94735e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Farewell to Arms', E'A Farewell to Arms was published in 1929, and one of the best literary works of Ernest Hemingway. The novel describes the Italian campaign during the First World War. Written in the first-person point of view, the story shows Frederic Henry, a lieutenant working as an ambulance driver in the Italian forces is involved in a love affair with a nurse, Catherine Barkley. Apart from the love story, the novel exclusively talks about the absurdity of war and his flight from duty to Switzerland where he loses his love during childbirth. The novel was also adapted to screen, television, and stage several times. The novel presents the personal experience of Hemingway as an ambulance driver.\n\nAccording to the text, which statement below is NOT true about A Farewell to Arms?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The famous work of Ernest Hemingway-A Farewell to Arms-describes the Italian campaign after the First World War.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7c3c600e-50c2-5b08-88a8-e8d8ff14fc0d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7c3c600e-50c2-5b08-88a8-e8d8ff14fc0d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Motivation to Fight', E'USA sexually ‘teased’ its troops in the First World War to make them fight harder. Believing that sexually satisfied men could not be easily motivated, the aim of this teasing was to generate unmet sexual desire, which the War Department could leverage as motivation to fight.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
