  ('7da87883-6c58-56da-aadd-b20b94c5e2a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7da87883-6c58-56da-aadd-b20b94c5e2a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cryptocurrencies', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 5, 1, 4, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('7dbbfcb8-cf35-546c-b02e-a7a43909f7f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7dbbfcb8-cf35-546c-b02e-a7a43909f7f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Autism', E'Because autism is a spectrum disorder, each child {{1}} with an autistic disorder differs from every other in the suite of symptoms they {{2}} and the characteristics and intensity of those symptoms; thus, general descriptions of autistic behavior and characteristics do not {{3}} equally to every child.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.diagnosed, 2.display, 3.apply', NULL, NULL),
  ('7dc75bcd-280d-59ff-8f71-4c8aa6209f79'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7dc75bcd-280d-59ff-8f71-4c8aa6209f79'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Utopias', E'Many Utopias have been dreamed up through the ages. From Plato''s Republic to Thomas More''s Utopia and beyond, serious thinkers have {{1}} societies where people live in peace and harmony. Most of these imaginary worlds have things in common: everybody is equal and plays a part in the running of the society; nobody goes without the essentials of life; people live mostly off the land; often there is no money, and so on. Another thing they have in {{2}} is that, to the average person, they appear distasteful or unworkable since they do not take into account ordinary human nature or feelings. Architects have got in on the act, too. After the Great Fire of London, Christopher Wren drew up plans for a reconstruction of the whole city, including {{3}} street widths. And in the 20th century there was Le Corbusier''s Radiant City in which, if you weren''t in a car or didn''t have one, life would have been a nightmare. Also in the 20th century; another famous architect, Frank Lloyd Wright, {{4}} up a perfect city that got no further than the drawing-board. Wright believed that what was wrong with modern cities was, in his words, rent. Ideas, land, even money itself, had to be paid for. He saw this as a form of slavery and believed that modern city dwellers had no sense of themselves as productive individuals. Thus, Wright''s city was to be made up of numerous individual homesteads, and the houses themselves were to be simple, functional and in {{5}} with the environment. Everyone would own enough land to grow food for himself and his family. No outsiders would be allowed to come between the citizen and what he produced, or to exploit both for money. Goods and services would all be {{6}} , not bought and sold for profit.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.envisioned, 2.common, 3.precise, 4.dreamed, 5.harmony, 6.exchanged', NULL, NULL),
  ('7dcb2cf7-ff12-5a77-b2bb-ff6cd8328f07'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7dcb2cf7-ff12-5a77-b2bb-ff6cd8328f07'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Go Shopping', E'So what principles should you {{1}} when you go out shopping? If you keep your home, your car or any valuable {{2}} in excellent condition, you''ll be saving money in the long run. Before you buy a new {{3}} , talk to someone who owns one .If you can, use it or borrow it to check it suits your particular purpose. Before you buy an expensive {{4}} , or a service, do check the price and what is on offer. If possible, choose {{5}} three items or three estimates.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.adopt, 2.possession, 3.appliance, 4.item, 5.from', NULL, NULL),
