  ('7de1509e-3e3d-5bbb-8d85-5a5ad38314cb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7de1509e-3e3d-5bbb-8d85-5a5ad38314cb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bonobos', E'Individuals that tended to engage in cooperative behavior within their group were more likely to interact with bonobos in the other group that had the same tendency. This cooperation doesn’t appear to be solely motivated by immediate reciprocation, the researchers say. For instance, during the study, only 14 percent of bonobos that shared food with a partner in the other group had the deed reciprocated.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7de5b53b-f025-5133-be2b-3236ce1f5107'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7de5b53b-f025-5133-be2b-3236ce1f5107'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '426868c7-b9db-5e97-ac71-64f4f19b946a'::uuid, NULL, E'The modern approach to the problem is to stress the symbolic side of human nature.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7df20af9-f0b3-5962-9d6b-4f2d91da65d1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df20af9-f0b3-5962-9d6b-4f2d91da65d1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What animal is the national treasure in China?', 'a790c422-9c1f-524b-82e0-9315498f8017'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Panda', NULL, NULL),
  ('7df2d4ef-376f-5116-890c-e77445ea789c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df2d4ef-376f-5116-890c-e77445ea789c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6c1838fd-5acf-5f26-aaa6-80dfcf339768'::uuid, NULL, E'This is a two-year course taught by means of lectures and seminars.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7df4a490-821a-5def-8859-7f87c35eacd4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df4a490-821a-5def-8859-7f87c35eacd4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the process by which different cultures are absorbed and integrated into a dominant culture?', 'c7375f08-c643-59c3-a166-01fe88f85bce'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Assimilation', NULL, NULL),
  ('7df59d5a-fbfa-50a0-a979-ab8617a76e2a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df59d5a-fbfa-50a0-a979-ab8617a76e2a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skin Pattern', E'Animals have different skin patterns, such as spots, stripes, and hexagons. Scientists can explain how these patterns help animals adapt to their environment, but they don''t know how they are formed in the first {{1}} .Turing was a scientist who suggested that two chemicals in the skin can interact to form patterns by balancing each other out. But his theory could not explain why some animals have clear lines between different colors, like zebras and boxfish. Alessio and Gupta are two scientists who improved Turing''s theory {{2}} a new factor. They said that larger things in the skin, like color cells, can move because of smaller things, like soap molecules. They showed that this can make more defined patterns by {{3}} color cells into different areas. They also showed that their theory can create the same hexagon pattern as the boxfish, which Turing''s theory could not do. Their work indicates that this new factor may be {{4}} for creating animal skin patterns and other natural patterns.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.place, 2.by adding, 3.separating, 4.crucial', NULL, NULL),
  ('7df62bed-8582-5d9e-9106-eea46eea692c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df62bed-8582-5d9e-9106-eea46eea692c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7978c948-8be1-57cf-88f2-c20131b1d29c'::uuid, NULL, E'The Library is open on campus and online during Summer Semester.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7df8da07-63ea-55eb-91a2-709e427a24e1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7df8da07-63ea-55eb-91a2-709e427a24e1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sensation of Fullness', NULL, '6c3f326c-df09-5d7d-b0f8-1f16fd4d44aa'::uuid, NULL, E'The sensation of fullness is set in motion as food moves from your mouth down your esophagus. Once it hits your stomach, it gradually fills the space. That causes the surrounding muscular wall to stretch, expanding slowly like a balloon. A multitude of nerves wrapped intricately around the stomach wall sense the stretching. They communicate with the vagus nerve up to the brainstem and hypothalamus, the main parts of the brain that control food intake. But that’s just one input your brain uses to sense fullness. After all, if you fill your stomach with water, you won’t feel full for long. Your brain also takes into account chemical messengers in the form of hormones produced by endocrine cells throughout your digestive system. These respond to the presence of specific nutrients in your gut and bloodstream, which gradually increase as you digest your food. As the hormones seep out, they’re swept up by the blood and eventually reach the hypothalamus in the brain. Over 20 gastrointestinal hormones are involved in moderating our appetites. One example is cholecystokinin, which is produced in response to food by cells in the upper small bowel. When it reached the hypothalamus, it causes a reduction in the feeling of reward you get when you eat food. When that occurs, the sense of being satiated starts to sink in and you stop eating.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7dffc57d-e25d-5d3b-aa9c-2254643ac2ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7dffc57d-e25d-5d3b-aa9c-2254643ac2ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '859afed8-04fd-5cc9-9a77-81e62fec0004'::uuid, NULL, E'There is a pharmacy on campus near the store.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e0180f8-6d6a-562a-8d8b-8418e8f7b745'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e0180f8-6d6a-562a-8d8b-8418e8f7b745'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If you are feeling ''fed up''; is it a positive or negative feeling?', 'e51bc16a-d4fb-5a62-a8e1-4ab3d93e8c59'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A negative feeling', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e064b36-33e4-5fca-9288-407df0f38aa2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e064b36-33e4-5fca-9288-407df0f38aa2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Poseidon', E'The chief festival in Poseidon’s honor was the Isthmia, the scene of famous {{1}} contests (including horse races), celebrated in alternate years near the Isthmus of Corinth. His character as a sea god eventually became his most {{2}} in art, and he was {{3}} with the attributes of the trident, the dolphin, and the tuna. The Romans, {{4}} his other aspects, identified him with Neptune as sea god.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.athletic, 2.prominent, 3.represented, 4.ignoring', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e0c4bd2-cf2a-57ae-aa01-cd9e21e29e62'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e0c4bd2-cf2a-57ae-aa01-cd9e21e29e62'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Human Shoulders', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 2, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e0c7516-ffcf-5f4a-98f2-645e3c44ce4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e0c7516-ffcf-5f4a-98f2-645e3c44ce4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Monitor Ocean Floor', NULL, '666a9862-aefa-5126-8c18-3239116ee3e8'::uuid, NULL, E'This is the first ocean deployment of two new high-precision instruments designed to monitor the Earth''s signals from the seafloor. This housing contains the tilt meter and nano bottom pressure recorder and the associated electronics and cabling used for power and communications. The instruments were deployed on the sea floor by a remotely operated vehicle as part of the Mars seafloor. Observatory test bed located at a depth of three thousand feet in Monterey Bay in this first test deployment in the ocean. it have already detected the ground motion from several large earthquakes as far from the Mars site as Chile and the Mariana Trench in the future. The instruments will be part of a global network of cabled seafloor observatories. Because of their precision these two new instruments are already detecting signals, which could never be measured before.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e106a48-cfe7-5636-8441-917611e374e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e106a48-cfe7-5636-8441-917611e374e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Plastic', E'Plastic is lightweight, malleable, durable. But it has also become so widespread that it''s ending up in a lot of unwanted places—including our own bodies. That''s according to a new study, which found that humans are consuming a shocking amount of so-called "microplastics". "Microplastics, the kind of current working definition, is plastic less than five millimeters. So people commonly equate that to something like a grain of rice or a sesame seed and down in terms of size class. I will say that most of the microplastics that people are interacting with are quite a bit smaller than the sesame seed size, which I think always kinds of shocks people when we start talking about the numbers because they kind of can''t see a lot of these things, at least with the naked eye."\nKieran Cox, a PhD candidate in marine biology at the University of Victoria in Canada and one of the authors of the study, which is in the journal Environmental Science and Technology.\n\nWhich of the following statements about microplastics are incorrect?', '56cd51e9-59ba-52c8-91b7-75ae7637114b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Microplastics is not as widespread as plastics.\nMicroplastics are beneficial to people''s health.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e1cc95e-404a-5309-bd5b-15edc36310b8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e1cc95e-404a-5309-bd5b-15edc36310b8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Addictive Games', E'Bolstered by the result of laboratory experiments, researchers dare to say that gaming might be mentally enriching. These scholars are the first to admit that games could be addictive, and indeed part of their research explores how games connect to the reward circuit of human beings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e239b21-abbd-5c94-99d5-5ba68a6c5f59'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e239b21-abbd-5c94-99d5-5ba68a6c5f59'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite of artificial?', 'dfb9e2e3-6b8d-52bd-8eef-87543c8e42b0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Natural', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e29b3ee-0b35-5222-804b-b588538ff726'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e29b3ee-0b35-5222-804b-b588538ff726'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f4221420-0f63-59c5-a414-a9a99f4496ce'::uuid, NULL, E'The importance of law is present in an array of industries.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e2d4f62-b960-5080-9204-640ef387cd30'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e2d4f62-b960-5080-9204-640ef387cd30'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Flowers and Bees', E'Most people assume, correctly, that flowers look the way they do to attract insects that pollinate them. But that''s not the whole story. Scientists have now discovered that plants have another ‘trick up their leaves'' to make themselves {{1}} to even the most choosy insect. Cambridge University''s Beverley Glover and her {{2}} recently set up some fake flowers filled with a sugar solution, which they kept at different temperatures. Unleashing a team of bumblebees on their floral {{3}} , they watched as the insects visited the flowers to drink the surrogate nectar. Very quickly, it became obvious that the bees were concentrating on the flowers with the warmest nectar. Just in case it was something to {{4}} with the color of the fake flowers, the scientists also tried a different color {{5}} and got the same result.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.irresistible, 2.colleagues, 3.offerings, 4.do, 5.combination', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e2efb12-056c-5ea6-b94c-d1295ba28769'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e2efb12-056c-5ea6-b94c-d1295ba28769'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the leader of a tribe?', '10208f26-03fa-5288-8b8f-683c45e7f912'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Chief', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e36b7b1-f5a9-5b1e-8e3b-213c99775a61'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e36b7b1-f5a9-5b1e-8e3b-213c99775a61'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4954407f-43cc-55c2-8869-1ef7346fe2a8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Effective communication is the key to becoming a successful manager.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e380524-8841-5eee-b1f1-9d571ff5c3f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e380524-8841-5eee-b1f1-9d571ff5c3f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lego', E'Children will lack the work skills they need in the future because they are not spending enough time playing, a Lego executive has warned. John Goodwin, head of Lego''s charitable arm the Lego Foundation, says less time in the classroom and more time playing is the solution. The foundation has a 25% stake in the Danish toy market, giving it a vested interest in encouraging play.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e3ae055-d36c-5f48-866b-bcb142c2470b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e3ae055-d36c-5f48-866b-bcb142c2470b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Anger', E'Anger is a powerful emotion that can motivate us to {{1}} action against injustice, but it can also lead us to make rash decisions or harm others. How can we use anger in a positive and productive way? According to experts, the key is to understand the root cause of our anger, plan how to address it, and wait until we cool off before {{2}} . Anger can give us a false sense of certainty and clarity, making us think that we know the best solution to a problem. However, this can {{3}} us to other perspectives or alternatives. By reflecting on why we are angry and what our goal is, we can avoid acting impulsively or aggressively. Anger can inspire us to make positive changes in our personal lives, our communities, or the world. Instead of feeling hopeless or helpless about issues that anger us, we can channel our energy into {{4}} actions, such as contacting elected officials, attending protests, or donating to charitable organizations. We can also use our anger to accomplish tasks that we have been {{5}} , such as volunteering, apologizing, or learning something new.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.take, 2.acting, 3.blind, 4.constructive, 5.putting off', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e3f6b5b-ed82-503d-9867-08f592fa1b96'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e3f6b5b-ed82-503d-9867-08f592fa1b96'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Worker Bee', E'The body of the worker bee is divided into three segments, head, thorax, and abdomen. On the head are the mandible zwitter jar, like organs, which enable the bees to perform the necessary high duties and to mold the wax and build their combs. The honey bee''s four wings and six legs, are fastened to the thorax. Located in the abdomen are the honey sac and the sting with its highly developed poison sac. The sting is used by the workers for self defense and for the protection of their colony. The worker uses her sting only once for in doing so she ...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '25c492de-0376-5860-9feb-9181ba895e32'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'loses her life', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e467bfe-a39f-5916-a580-be09aadeaa8c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e467bfe-a39f-5916-a580-be09aadeaa8c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1816c890-3531-5e64-bb4d-e7f4485b82be'::uuid, NULL, E'This paper is the best one to look at first.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e4d6f48-1a6b-51ac-b597-f332d15fee6c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e4d6f48-1a6b-51ac-b597-f332d15fee6c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A Balanced Budget', E'Most state governments are subject to a requirement to pass a balanced budget. However, a budget that may fit the statutory definition of a "balanced budget" may not be financially sustainable. For example, a budget that is balanced by such standards could include the use of non-recurring resources, such as asset sales or reserves, to fund ongoing expenditures, and thus not be in structural balance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e4e5402-e9a8-59d5-82c6-34f575285339'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e4e5402-e9a8-59d5-82c6-34f575285339'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ddac7c4a-b169-51dd-8521-aae59fe83e8b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'When you finish researching, it''s a lot simpler to start writing.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e52a3c9-2d87-51f7-9d13-a1a6c9aaa64c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e52a3c9-2d87-51f7-9d13-a1a6c9aaa64c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9bd402cb-0339-5cef-aadf-fd716cf0a374'::uuid, NULL, E'In consultation with your supervisor, your thesis is approved by the faculty committee.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e59524e-1db7-5ff5-89a0-237ea8b294b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e59524e-1db7-5ff5-89a0-237ea8b294b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ethical Shopping', NULL, 'bf0dc2de-a524-5956-8987-3050002dfddd'::uuid, NULL, E'Ruth, just tell us what the Ethical Consumer Research Association is. OK, well the Ethical Consumer Research Association exists to provide information for shoppers, letting them know what the companies are doing behind the brands that they see on the shelves. So what makes an ethical shopper? Very broadly speaking, people who are concerned about ethical issues want to know that the product they''re buying hasn''t been made at the expense of the people who are producing it, whether it''s in this country or abroad. They might also be concerned with other kinds of issues: whether the company is involved in armaments, or whether they''re donating money to certain political parties. And that as a shopper, you might not want to give your money to that party so therefore you might not want to buy a product from a company who is supporting a political party that you don''t agree with. And is there any kind of rule of thumb? Is something that''s more expensive, for example, likely to be more ethical? Unfortunately it isn''t always the case that the more expensive something is, the more ethical it is. We can buy very cheap products and it''s very likely that when products are cheap, something has suffered in order to get it to us. Whether it''s the person making it or the animals or the environment. Quality however, is often a good indicator whether something, especially with clothes, has been made well. And unfortunately a lot of ethical products will cost more because they reflect the real cost of bringing that thing into the shops. So something that has been made in a factory where the workers have been paid a proper wage will cost you more to buy, simply because the people making it are getting paid enough to live on. Do you have to be well off then to be an ethical shopper? It really depends. You don''t have to be rich to be an ethical shopper. One way of thinking about ethical shopping is thinking about buying less. Sometimes we buy an awful lot more than we need. We buy more items of clothing than we need. So being an ethical shopper really means thinking a bit before you go and spend your money in the shops. Some things may cost a little bit more in the short-run, but be worth it in the long-run. If you are paying for quality, something will last you longer and then save you money. And sometimes you can buy things second-hand. There''s a lot of charity shops on the high street to buy good clothes. Sometimes you can look a lot better than someone who''s just bought off the high street because you can have quite a unique look, and the quality that you find in most second-hand shops is really very good these days. So it''s about thinking before you shop. Thanks Ruth.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e5ab96d-6f4f-5d54-881d-b312db385073'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e5ab96d-6f4f-5d54-881d-b312db385073'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Medical Test', E'Three professors from Hamburg University''s medical faculty traveled last month to Ingeborg''s sitting room in East Berlin to test her on the work she carried out in pre-war Germany. They were impressed and a special ceremony took place at Hamburg University Medical Centre on Tuesday, in which she finally received the Ph.D. that the Nazis stole from her.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e604f47-ce5f-5587-a78b-e1fdd42191ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e604f47-ce5f-5587-a78b-e1fdd42191ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Geography', E'Geography is the study of the earth''s physical features and human populations, providing insights into how our world is shaped and how we interact with it. It encompasses topics such as climate, geology, demographics, and cultural practices, and informs decision-making in areas such as urban planning and disaster management.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e626d3a-0fa8-5629-a655-7195198f1af1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e626d3a-0fa8-5629-a655-7195198f1af1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6bcd8bd9-6351-5618-afa1-f057b999cfab'::uuid, NULL, E'Many modern cities now require their citizens to sort the garbage.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e646c61-7d95-5549-8524-ed1f5c14253c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e646c61-7d95-5549-8524-ed1f5c14253c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Zebra Stripes', E'How did the zebra get its stripes? One theory holds that stripes help confuse predators. But stripes might be {{1}} to protect zebras from ferocious...insects. That''s {{2}} to a study in the Journal of Experimental Biology.\nHorseflies are abundant in Africa. They deliver painful bites that spread disease and distract animals from grazing. The flies use polarized light hitting water as a guide to places to mate and lay eggs. And they read such light hitting dark mammal hides as a sign of a blood meal.\nZebra embryos start out dark and develop their white stripes before birth. Could the stripes confuse flies?\nThe researchers went to a farm infested with horseflies, where they set up models of black and white stripes of varying angles and widths, thus changing the {{3}} of the reflected polarized light. They tracked how the patterns affected the flies'' interest.\nThey then tested models of horses colored black, brown, white or {{4}} . And again tracked the effect on flies.\nTurns out that the black and white stripes on a zebra are optimal for {{5}} a horsefly''s {{6}} . Meaning that zebras may have evolved stripes to ward off disease-carrying insects, and to dine in peace.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.primarily, 2.according, 3.direction, 4.zebra-striped, 5.avoiding, 6.attention', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e677078-5107-5d5b-961a-0267093b8c5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e677078-5107-5d5b-961a-0267093b8c5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '548be3e7-774a-5c85-9647-d43cbc274a5c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They''ve been working since last year to introduce paid services.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e709a03-1f2e-51d9-be92-25cab9dff0a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e709a03-1f2e-51d9-be92-25cab9dff0a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Master’s in Business Administration', E'The curriculum for the Master’s in Business Administration has been specifically crafted to help you advance your career or even manage your own business. Students will learn how to position organizations for a competitive advantage, manage team collaboration and formulate effective business strategies. Our curriculum has been developed by top notch academic leadership to help students succeed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e7590e4-55b3-52fd-b46b-7d90fa4f9f26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e7590e4-55b3-52fd-b46b-7d90fa4f9f26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Goat Towers', E'Goat towers date back over a century, but many more recent ones {{1}} their inspiration back to one in particular: Torre das Cabras (Tower of the Goats), a winding turret built in Portugal during the late 1800s. This particular tower {{2}} a jagged stone facade wrapped in a wooden ramp and topped with a round peaked roof. While not quite as aesthetically lofty as a faux Roman temple, Egyptian pyramid, or Gothic abbey, it was in many ways a product of its era, at home in a period filled with architectural follies designed to {{3}} up landscapes. Situated on a broad winery estate, the goat tower is one of various “artistic daydreams with no {{4}} explanation,” according to 13th-generation member of the family that owns the land. It was built by his ancestors, who believed that “the goats did not belong to the plains and thus built the goat tower, so they could have a mountain.”', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.trace, 2.features, 3.liven, 4.functional', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e77a9e0-caad-5473-8b48-4a345f120b0d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e77a9e0-caad-5473-8b48-4a345f120b0d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8f99cbf5-06f1-5760-9fd8-761c40315acb'::uuid, NULL, E'Our students have participated in Exchange Programs to widen their horizons.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e79e996-118f-593d-b74b-85d7dbd4ab26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e79e996-118f-593d-b74b-85d7dbd4ab26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Domestic Violence', E'Domestic Violence Increased During Lockdown In The United States - "A new study, published in Psychology of Violence, looks at rates of intimate partner violence during the pandemic in the United States. Like data from the UK, it suggests that domestic violence increased during lockdown."', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e7d7674-aaad-565e-857e-808fc2daa9ff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e7d7674-aaad-565e-857e-808fc2daa9ff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '71f82507-8fdd-5414-aa63-0d89bcc5feba'::uuid, NULL, E'The genetic biology technology lab is located at the North Wing of the library.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e7e1498-7363-52c1-bacd-397af651a929'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e7e1498-7363-52c1-bacd-397af651a929'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aurora', E'Many ancient people associated the auroras with fire, which is understandable: the sky can glow with ripples of yellow and red, as if it is itself aflame or perhaps instead reflecting some distant over-the-horizon conflagration on the ground. But the lights come in many other colors, too: green is the most common, and purple and pink can make appearances, too. Sometimes auroras can even glow an electric blue.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7e80074b-3e63-5d85-aa3b-22a30a2f40fb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e80074b-3e63-5d85-aa3b-22a30a2f40fb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Money', E'In the earliest stages of man’s development, he had no need of money. He was content with very simple forms of shelter, making his own rough tools and weapons and he could provide food and clothing for himself and his family from natural materials around him. As he became more civilized, however, he began to want better shelter, more efficient tools and weapons, and more comfortable and more lasting clothing than those that could be provided by the work of his own unskilled hands. For these things, he had to turn to the skilled people such as smiths, leather workers or carpenters. It was then that the question of payment arose.\n\nWhat can we infer from this passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Money is related to civilization.', NULL, NULL),
  ('7e938fb4-8a94-5e5b-99bb-a6dae632077d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7e938fb4-8a94-5e5b-99bb-a6dae632077d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ministerial Staffing', E'The contemporary ministerial staffing system is large, active and partisan - far larger and further evolved than any West minster equivalent. Ministers'' demands for help to cope with the pressures of an increasingly competitive and professionalized political environment have been key drivers of the staffing system''s development. But there has not been commensurate growth in {{1}} to support and control it. The {{2}} framework for ministerial staff is {{3}} and ad hoc.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.arrangements, 2.operating, 3.fragmented', NULL, NULL),
