  ('7ff705b4-02b4-5b5a-a384-fabe836590c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7ff705b4-02b4-5b5a-a384-fabe836590c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '68ef0013-a183-55e7-9d9b-f70c0518dcf6'::uuid, NULL, E'The museum is exhibiting fossils of a very large dinosaur.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('7ff96022-e59b-5b40-82c0-c394d9d6922b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '7ff96022-e59b-5b40-82c0-c394d9d6922b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Canada', E'Canada is a country of enormous natural resources. It is the world''s largest exporter of forest products and a {{1}} exporter of fish, furs, and wheat. Minerals {{2}} a key role in Canada''s transformation into an urban-industrial economy. Alberta, British Columbia, Quebec, and Saskatchewan are the principal mining regions. Ontario and the Northwest (NWT) and Yukon Territories are also {{3}} producers. Canada is the world largest producer of uranium and potash, the third-largest of asbestos, gypsum, and nickel, and the fourth-largest of zinc. Oil and gas are exploited in Alberta, off the Atlantic coast, and in the northwest - huge additional reserves are thought to exist in the high Arctic; oil price {{4}} extraction profitable at a growing number of the country''s deposit. Canada is also one of the world''s top hydroelectricity producers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.top, 2.have played, 3.significant, 4.is making', NULL, NULL),
  ('8000814d-158f-5705-9eeb-c57b9ee5a38a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8000814d-158f-5705-9eeb-c57b9ee5a38a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Apart from coffee and hot chocolate, what beverages also contain caffeine?', '0b3ba330-5c69-586d-a5ae-148d8204e754'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tea / coke / cocoa', NULL, NULL),
  ('800954f9-b09c-599d-804f-4b53a434ed88'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '800954f9-b09c-599d-804f-4b53a434ed88'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Assessment Systems', E'There are different assessment systems, putting all exams at the end of the term, or assignments and exams being spread out throughout the semester. What are the advantages and disadvantages of each system? Which system do you prefer?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8010d9a8-0ff8-5340-bfe1-8a13944c0e9a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8010d9a8-0ff8-5340-bfe1-8a13944c0e9a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Brain Development', NULL, '0fee9d10-75e7-5625-ac3d-939c675b67b8'::uuid, NULL, E'3 stages of Brain development- brain development during childhood, there are three stages, starting from the primitive brain (the action brain), limbic brain(feeling brain), and finally to the neocortex (thought brain).Although interrelated, the three had its own function. Primitive brain functions to manage the physical to survive, manage reflex, motor motion control, monitoring body funtions, and process information coming from sensing. Limbic brain functioning as a liaison to process emotions and the brain thinks, and the primitive brain.While the thinking brain, which is the most objective part of the brain, receiving input from the primitive brain and the limbic brain. However, he needed more time to process information from the primitive brain and the limbic brain. The brain thinks the merger is also a place of experience, memory, feeling, and thinking ability to give birth to ideas and actions.Nerve myelination of the brain take place in sequence, starting from the primitive brain, the limbic brains, and brain thought. Neural pathways are more frequently used to make more myelin thicken. Increasingly thicker myelin,the faster the nerve impulses or signals travel alone nerves. Therefore, a growing child is encouraged to receive input from the environment in accordance with its development.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('80148fde-06f7-5782-9a97-ee4c6c8befd6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '80148fde-06f7-5782-9a97-ee4c6c8befd6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '956e6bad-6a1c-5751-aca8-f25cbf93031f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The factory will compensate its workers if they are hurt at work.', NULL, NULL),
  ('801ada35-ddd7-5236-bff0-b15d38bd0a53'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '801ada35-ddd7-5236-bff0-b15d38bd0a53'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Advanced Machine', NULL, '522d1a64-3084-59b9-b3da-e60651328a0f'::uuid, NULL, E'The biotech engineering has undergone three phases.\nIn the first phase, people designed and made some simple machines, which aimed to help people understand ourselves.\nAnd first group of people that realized we could learn from ourselves were engineers.\nAnd then, based on the studies, people began to make complicated devices, in order to cure wounds, like the practice of suture, and to study physiology. This is the second phase.\nLater, since we went into the third phase, more complicated machines have been developed, like ECG (electrocardiography), able to have an insight of your internal body without intruding it, which can show the human brain''s functions. X-ray is a good example. In an X-ray picture, you can see the bright area is the heart with some vessels around it, and the dark area is the lungs. These devices benefit humans greatly in solving health problems, such as diseases.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('801ff7c2-4695-5615-8663-88fcc76335d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '801ff7c2-4695-5615-8663-88fcc76335d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Donor Countries', E'In 2005, donor countries agreed on an accord to harmonize their practices. Since then, aid officials have complained that too little has changed on the ground. Conferences of donors in developing countries still tend to be dominated by a small group of north European governments, with the US often absent.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('802e85e1-2eae-5eac-809a-969071659900'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '802e85e1-2eae-5eac-809a-969071659900'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the process of removing waste and excess substances from the bloodstream?', 'b3744d2c-74f2-543e-8576-8633490902b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Excretion', NULL, NULL),
  ('802eebc4-cdc2-5759-8843-e5ea7c32dca8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '802eebc4-cdc2-5759-8843-e5ea7c32dca8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vitamin D', E'When our skin is directly {{1}} to the sun, our bodies make vitamin D, a vital tool that helps with calcium {{2}} and building strong bones. Some of it comes from diet, but a good portion also comes from the sun. And according to the Mayo Clinic, as little as 10 minutes of sun {{3}} can provide us with our daily dose. According to the vitamin D council, "your body can produce 10,000 to 25,000 IU of vitamin D in just a little under the time it takes for your skin to {{4}} pink.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exposed, 2.absorption, 3.exposure, 4.turn', NULL, NULL),
  ('80328b01-1feb-5972-8db1-a7b016f9bc96'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '80328b01-1feb-5972-8db1-a7b016f9bc96'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ff7bb70d-af35-5302-9423-6443f77bb84e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some teachers prefer to teach by using images and pictures.', NULL, NULL),
  ('80374fcb-e2b2-532b-87b2-548cecccdc8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '80374fcb-e2b2-532b-87b2-548cecccdc8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the process where rainwater becomes slightly acidic due to atmospheric carbon dioxide and can dissolve limestone?', '7e09f5ab-499b-5f28-84cb-96aa0dd4d431'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Carbonation', NULL, NULL),
  ('803eaa36-b53c-5f57-b528-374ec6f57bb0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '803eaa36-b53c-5f57-b528-374ec6f57bb0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '87c92860-3a8c-599f-8c8c-66e421625930'::uuid, NULL, E'The first draft of the presentation is almost ready.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('803f8049-4f27-5344-b36b-097b5eaffa06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '803f8049-4f27-5344-b36b-097b5eaffa06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'International Women''s Day', E'International Women''s Day is marked on March 8 every year. Countries around the world celebrate it to give credit to the economic, political and social achievements of women and to show respect to their contributions in the development of their countries. It''s only in the beginning of the 20th century that the day was officially and internationally acknowledged due to the rapid industrialization and the social protest that it accompanied.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('80419743-2cb0-5e4d-8de1-9b69b3008032'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '80419743-2cb0-5e4d-8de1-9b69b3008032'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parliamentary&presidential', E'A government is the organization, machinery, or agency, through which a political unit exercises its authority, controls and administers public policy, and directs and controls the actions of its members or subjects. The government makes laws, regulates economies, conducts relations with other countries, provides infrastructure and services, and maintains an army and a police force amongst others on behalf of the people of the country.\nDemocracy is any system of government in which the people have the rule. The ancient Greeks used the word democracy to mean government by the many in contrast to the government by the few. The key to democracy is that the people hold ultimate power. Abraham Lincoln best captured this spirit by describing democracy as a government of the people, by the people, for the people. Democratic government is opposed to an authoritative government, where the participation of its citizenry is limited or prohibited, and a state of anarchy where no form of government exists.', NULL, NULL, E'A government is the organization, which controls the public policy, makes laws, regulates economies, conducts relations with other countries, also maintains an army and a police force, while democracy is any system of government in which the people have the rule, as a government of people, as opposed to an authoritative government, where the participation of its citizenry is limited or prohibited, and a state of anarchy where no form of government exists.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('80472c01-1fd1-5b7c-aa3f-1fb6679249a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '80472c01-1fd1-5b7c-aa3f-1fb6679249a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Domestic Division', E'Traditional divisions of domestic work are understood to persist because of the strong association of the home with femininity and paid work with masculinity - to challenge who does what in the home is arguably tantamount to challenging what it is to be a woman or a man.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8048c0e8-ea37-5ded-bf84-83a2681c01a8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8048c0e8-ea37-5ded-bf84-83a2681c01a8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Steps', E'There are several variables for calculating the distance a person can cover in 10,000 steps per day, including their height, stride length and physical ability, as well as the terrain. You can use a step count goal of 10,000 average daily steps as a personal activity benchmark to promote accountability and healthy habits in daily life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
