  ('8116fb04-1606-5705-bafe-a10f447d7c3b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8116fb04-1606-5705-bafe-a10f447d7c3b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Anesthetics', E'Before effective anaesthetics, surgery was very crude and very painful. Before 1800, alcohol and opium had {{1}} success in easing pain during operations. Laughing gas was used in 1844 in dentistry in the USA, but failed to ease all pain and patients {{2}} conscious. Ether (used from 1846) made patients totally unconscious and lasted a long time. However, it could make patients cough during operations and sick afterwards. It was highly flammable and {{3}} in heavy glass bottles. Chloroform (used from 1847) was very effective with few side effects. However, it was difficult to get the dose right and could kill some people {{4}} the effect on their heart. An inhaler helped to regulate the dosage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.little, 2.remained, 3.was transported, 4.because of', NULL, NULL),
