  ('8498479c-d025-5112-a12e-f7ddb372dee1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8498479c-d025-5112-a12e-f7ddb372dee1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parent Teacher Conferences', E'Schools host parent teacher conferences four times a year and it is important for families to attend. This is your chance to meet with teachers and ask questions about your child''s progress. It can be helpful to write down questions ahead of time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('849ee4c0-2ff0-5913-ba49-4f4442dc4695'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '849ee4c0-2ff0-5913-ba49-4f4442dc4695'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Women and Climate Change', E'It is women, more than men, who are disproportionately more {{1}} to the effects of climate change. This is not only because women perform up to 90 % of the agricultural work on farms, but also because of other {{2}} they face: they often have less access to opportunities and decision-making power than men. This increases their vulnerability to climate change and {{3}} them of their ability to manage its impacts. In Honduras, 2.2 million women live in rural areas. With limited access to resources, knowledge, and technical assistance, many of them have not been able to live up to their {{4}} and fully achieve their dreams. “Even though there are several actors and institutions supporting rural women in the region, their interventions are not fully aligned”, states Ruiz.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.vulnerable, 2.challenges, 3.deprives, 4.capacities', NULL, NULL),
