  ('84b8b883-ad6e-5958-81a4-cc3ba0e22f3a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84b8b883-ad6e-5958-81a4-cc3ba0e22f3a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Reconstruction of Paris', NULL, '0a7cfd9a-0fc1-573c-97c5-0a44bfa41efb'::uuid, NULL, E'Haussmann''s renovation of Paris was a vast public works program commissioned by Emperor Napoleon III and directed by his prefect of the Seine, Georges-Eugene Haussmann, between 1853 and 1870. It included the demolition of crowded and unhealthy medieval neighborhoods, the building of wide avenues, parks and squares, the annexation of the suburbs surrounding Paris, and the construction of new sewers, fountains and aqueducts. Haussmann''s work met with fierce opposition, and he was finally dismissed by Napoleon III in 1870; but work on his projects continued until 1927. The street plan and distinctive appearance of the center of Paris today is largely the result of Haussmann''s renovation.In the middle of the nineteenth century, the center of Paris was overcrowded, dark, dangerous, and unhealthy. In 1845 the French social reformer Victor Considerant wrote "Paris is an immense workshop of putrefaction, where misery, pestilence and sickness work in concert, where sunlight and air rarely penetrate. Paris is a terrible place where plants shrivel and perish, and where, of seven small infants, four die during the course of the year." The street plan on the Tie de la Cite and in the neighborhood called the "quartier des Arcis", between the Louvre and the "Hotel de Ville" (City Hall), had changed little since the Middle Ages. The population density in these neighborhoods was extremely high, compared with the rest of Paris;in the neighborhood of the Champs—EIysees, there was one resident for every 186 square meters;in the neighborhoods of Arc is and Saint- Avoye, in the present Third Arrondissement, there was one inhabitant for every three square meters. In 1840, a doctor described one building in the tie de la Cite where a single room five meters squares on the fourth floor was occupied by twenty-three people, both adults and children. In these conditions, disease spread very quickly. Cholera epidemics ravaged the city in 1832 and 1848. In the epidemic of 1848, five percent of the inhabitants of these two neighborhoods died. Traffic circulation was another major problem. The widest streets in these two neighborhoods were only five meters wide; the narrowest were only one or two meters wide. Wagons, carriages and carts could barely move through the streets. The center of the city was also a cradle of discontent and revolution;between 1830 and 1848, seven armed uprisings and revolts had broken out in the centre of Paris, particularly along the Faubourg Saint-Antoine, around the Hotel de Vi Ile, and around Montagne Sainte Genevive on the left bank. The residents of these neighborhoods had taken up paving stones and blocked the narrow streets with barricades, and had to be dislodged by the army.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('84b972d1-5e3e-5db7-b402-64aa5d7b73cb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84b972d1-5e3e-5db7-b402-64aa5d7b73cb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What handicap equipment is used for broken legs?', '8be6555f-bfa3-5898-9d8b-e3aaae0e3d06'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Crutch / walking stick / cane', NULL, NULL),
  ('84bb1968-a5aa-566d-bdd1-c38c11c5635f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84bb1968-a5aa-566d-bdd1-c38c11c5635f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ba0cd346-3b2a-5bbd-9c75-764f4b8a90d9'::uuid, NULL, E'Control systems in manufacturing require a high level of accuracy.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('84c36eaf-49bb-58f4-9f03-57b4d113a0f2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84c36eaf-49bb-58f4-9f03-57b4d113a0f2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bcd18cfb-739b-5213-b395-3c18838926f4'::uuid, NULL, E'Next week the department secretary will email you with the details of your tutorial groups.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('84c4f855-c7da-528b-afd7-4d6689c25bf6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84c4f855-c7da-528b-afd7-4d6689c25bf6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name for a building or complex of buildings where goods are manufactured or assembled chiefly by machine?', '7b7584d1-a4ba-5582-9dd5-c93d75e1b56f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Factory', NULL, NULL),
  ('84c975b7-9617-579d-be1c-ff62a7415c56'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84c975b7-9617-579d-be1c-ff62a7415c56'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'School Bullying', E'Spurred by the sense that disorderly behaviour among students in South Euclid was increasing, the school resource officer (SRO) reviewed data regarding referrals to the principal''s office. He found that the high school reported thousands of referrals a year for bullying and that the junior high school had recently experienced a 30 percent increase in bullying referrals. Police data showed that juvenile complaints about disturbances, bullying, and assaults after school hours had increased 90 percent in the past 10 years.\nThe SRO worked in close collaboration with a social worker and the university researcher. They coordinated a Response Planning Team comprising many stakeholders that was intended to respond to each of the areas identified in the initial analysis. Environmental changes included modifying the school schedule and increasing teacher supervision of hotspots. Counsellors and social workers conducted teacher training courses in conflict resolution and bullying prevention. Parent education included mailings with information about bullying, an explanation of the new school policy, and a discussion about what could be done at home to address the problems. Finally, student education included classroom discussions between homeroom teachers and students, as well as assemblies conducted by the SRO. The SRO also opened a substation next to a primary hotspot. The Ohio Department of Education contributed by opening a new training centre to provide a non-traditional setting for specialized help.\nThe results from the various responses were dramatic. School suspensions decreased 40 percent. Bullying incidents dropped 60 percent in the hallways and 80 percent in the gym area. Follow-up surveys indicated that there were positive attitudinal changes among students about bullying and that more students felt confident that teachers would take action when a problem arose. Teachers indicated that training sessions were helpful and that they were more likely to talk about bullying as a serious issue. Parents responded positively, asking for more information about the problem in future mailings. The overall results suggest that the school environments were not only safer; but that early intervention was helping at-risk students succeed in school (South Euclid (Ohio) Police Department, 2001).', NULL, NULL, E'The anti-bullying program of South Euclid, spurred by the sense of increasing disorderly behavior among students, was very successful because of the SRO worked closely with social worker and university researcher in four primary areas of concern, including the environmental design of the school, teacher knowledge of and response to the problem, parental attitudes and responses, and student perspectives behaviors, which were pointed out by conducted bullying crime incidents.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('84cdb980-f442-5a02-aed3-20da1a5535ba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84cdb980-f442-5a02-aed3-20da1a5535ba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pilot', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('84d2f2f2-cdca-5ae2-a0c1-c10550b9dc4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84d2f2f2-cdca-5ae2-a0c1-c10550b9dc4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9643a996-e809-5feb-ade8-f7f04cad4995'::uuid, NULL, E'This essay examined the use of computers in the science classroom.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('84d5c329-319a-53b8-99c9-1810516f8e5c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84d5c329-319a-53b8-99c9-1810516f8e5c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nutrition', E'Since nutrition scientists are constantly making new discoveries, we need to revise our {{1}} for healthy eating from time to time. However,nutrition is an art as well as a {{2}} . It''s an art because it requires creativity to develop a healthy eating plan for people who differ in their food preferences, beliefs and culture, let alone in their nutritional needs according to their genes and life stage. As we discover more about how our genes and our environment {{3}} , it''s becoming increasingly difficult to provide a single set of dietary recommendations that will be {{4}} for everyone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.recommendations, 2.science, 3.interact, 4.suitable', NULL, NULL),
  ('84d70179-f2f9-54e5-a581-570150ba4188'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84d70179-f2f9-54e5-a581-570150ba4188'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Programs', E'State institutions to aid the elderly have existed in varying degrees since the time of the ancient Roman Empire. England in 1601 {{1}} the Poor Law, which recognized the state''s responsibility to the aged, although programs were carried out by local church parishes. An amendment to this law in 1834 instituted workhouses for the poor and aged, and in 1925 England introduced social insurance for the aged {{2}} by statistical evaluations. In 1940 programs for the aged came under England''s welfare state system. In the 1880s Otto von Bismarck in Germany introduced old-age pensions whose model was followed by most other western European countries. The United States was one of the last countries to {{3}} such programs. Not until the Social Security Act of 1935 was formulated to relieve hardships caused by the Great Depression were the elderly granted old-age pensions. For the most part, these state programs, while {{4}} some burdens of aging, still do not bring older people to a level of income comparable to that of younger people.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.enacted, 2.regulated, 3.institute, 4.alleviating', NULL, NULL),
  ('84d9b77c-3f0f-5650-9b8d-7d78e3225dac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84d9b77c-3f0f-5650-9b8d-7d78e3225dac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '47721541-40ce-53a0-84e8-ddca3629c8ec'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Two drops of the solution were heated in a test tube.', NULL, NULL),
  ('84db87a8-7f5a-549b-b054-cf7c0aac380e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84db87a8-7f5a-549b-b054-cf7c0aac380e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bone Protection', E'Drugs we take can weaken our bones and so can aging, and scientists working to prevent both have some of the first evidence that the best target may not be the logical one.\nThey are finding that in aging bone, the mineralocorticoid receptor, better known for its role in blood pressure regulation, is a key factor in bone health, says Dr. Meghan E. McGee-Lawrence, biomedical engineer in the Department of Cellular Biology and Anatomy at the Medical College of Georgia. And drugs that block the receptor, like the hypertension medications spironolactone and eplerenone, may help protect bone cells.\nDrugs like prednisone are glucocorticoids, which are better known for their roles in reducing inflammation and suppressing the immune response, which is why they work so well for problems like irritable bowel syndrome and arthritis. But, like aging, they can also disrupt the healthy, ongoing dynamic of bone being made and being destroyed.\nOur natural glucocorticoid levels increase with age, and bone, at least when we are young, has more glucocorticoid receptors than mineralocorticoid receptors. Glucocorticoids can actually coax stem cells to make bone-forming osteoblasts, but it also causes those osteoblasts to store more fat, and too much fat in the bone, like anywhere on our body, is probably not good and typically correlates with bone loss.\nSo reducing the impact of glucocorticoid receptors seemed like a logical way to protect bone.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Aging can weaken our bones.\nWhen we are young, there are fewer mineralocorticoid receptors in the bones than glucocorticoid receptors.\nBone cells may be protected by drugs that block receptors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('84dd3bb1-de38-59c6-8f60-a53d892e542e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84dd3bb1-de38-59c6-8f60-a53d892e542e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'American Indian', E'Although the original American Indian cultures were highly diverse, they were similar in many of their traditions. Religious beliefs and rituals permeated every aspect of Indian life. Southwest tribes, such as the hopi and the apaches, had a rich and elaborate year round sequence of ceremonies including songs, dances and poetry. The hopi performed dances to bring rain. The apaches engaged in special dances and ceremonies to gain the support of the spirits before undertaking raids or going into war. The plains tribes often sought contact with the spirits by going on a vision quest.\n\nWhat is the topic of the lecture?', '7daa4746-13cb-5ac7-8956-3e4ad9263891'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Traditions of American Indian cultures', NULL, NULL),
  ('84e3e840-ac57-5a95-840c-af200c2f6543'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84e3e840-ac57-5a95-840c-af200c2f6543'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ae191928-1c1f-509f-aee1-a1b5b02c4662'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Presidential elections are held once every four years.', NULL, NULL),
  ('84e4d181-ac62-59ff-96f1-71797cdd7368'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84e4d181-ac62-59ff-96f1-71797cdd7368'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the liquid which is in a car?', '561246b7-9105-5b98-aa25-a7a9c0a61d03'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Gasoline / petrol / gas / fuel / diesel', NULL, NULL),
  ('84e7b7a0-a0b5-58bd-853e-fb2141ed24a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84e7b7a0-a0b5-58bd-853e-fb2141ed24a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Robot Definition', E'Joseph Engelberger, a pioneer in industrial robotics, once remarked "I can''t {{1}} a robot, but I know one when I see one." If you consider all the different machines people {{2}} robots, you can see that it''s nearly impossible to come up with a {{3}} definition. Everybody has a different idea of what constitutes a robot.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.define, 2.call, 3.comprehensive', NULL, NULL),
  ('84e98ecf-abe9-5af3-8b0a-85108486d91b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84e98ecf-abe9-5af3-8b0a-85108486d91b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4e002d7a-3840-5e09-957e-6e63215b3d66'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The ability to act on your own is called autonomy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('84ecd852-460d-5618-9c70-563a8a917a00'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84ecd852-460d-5618-9c70-563a8a917a00'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Newspapers', E'Who won the World Cup 1994 football game? What happened at the United Nations? How did the critics like the new play? Just when an event takes place, newspapers are on the streets {{1}} the details. Wherever anything happens in the world, reporters are on the spot to {{2}} the news.\nNewspapers have one basic purpose, to get the news as quickly as possible from its source, from those who make it to those who want to know it. Radio, telegraph, television, and other inventions brought competition for newspapers. So did the development of magazines and other means of communication. However, this competition merely spurred the newspapers on. They quickly made use of the newer and faster means of communication to improve the {{3}} and thus the efficiency of their own operations. Today more newspapers are printed and read than ever before. Competition also led newspapers to branch out into so many other fields. Besides keeping readers {{4}} of the latest news, today''s newspapers educate and influence readers about politics and other important and serious matters.Newspapers influence readers'' economic choices through advertising. Most newspapers depend on advertising for their very existence. Newspapers are sold at a price that fails to cover even a small fraction of the cost of production.The main source of income for most newspapers is commercial advertising. The success in selling advertising depends on a newspaper''s value to advertisers. This is {{5}} in terms of circulation.How many people read the newspaper? Circulation depends much on the work of the circulation department and on the services or entertainment offered in a newspaper''s pages. But for the most part, circulation depends on a newspaper''s value to readers as a source of information about the community, city, country, state, nation, and world--and even outer space.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.to give, 2.gather, 3.speed, 4.informed, 5.measured', NULL, NULL),
  ('84ed1d42-b952-5f78-9aab-b3a0dfba5533'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84ed1d42-b952-5f78-9aab-b3a0dfba5533'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd88f4a50-42a9-5f75-8556-430170a22a0e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Career management is a very important subject.', NULL, NULL),
  ('84ed4256-49b3-5380-8bc4-8edb2016a442'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84ed4256-49b3-5380-8bc4-8edb2016a442'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Education', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 2, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('84f2e040-964e-5110-8e87-975ffc945293'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84f2e040-964e-5110-8e87-975ffc945293'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A Team-building Event', E'You''re coordinating a team-building event for your department, and your team suggests going to an amusement park. However, you realize that some team members may not enjoy rides or have health conditions that prevent them from participating fully. What would you say to your team?', 'd578d44c-e948-529f-9146-2eb4a7b21ba1'::uuid, NULL, E'That sounds like a fun idea, but let''s consider activities that cater to everyone''s preferences and abilities. How about a team picnic in the park with games like frisbee, soccer, or a scavenger hunt? It allows for socializing, physical activity, and relaxation, ensuring everyone feels included and comfortable participating. Plus, it''s a great opportunity to bond outside of the office setting.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('84f418e2-6d9a-50cb-b2ba-5d9d65c8d5f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84f418e2-6d9a-50cb-b2ba-5d9d65c8d5f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Stress Relief', E'Want to find your way to stress relief? This recipe is for you: combine a passion for baking with the mindful practice of meditation. Studies show that baking can be a powerful tool for {{1}} mental well-being, offering a sense of calm and accomplishment. The key is to be present in the {{2}} , savoring the tactile sensations of kneading dough, the rhythmic whisking of eggs, and the sweet aroma of rising bread. This mindful approach not only {{3}} the baking experience but also provides a welcome escape from daily anxieties. Research suggests that baking can trigger the {{4}} of endorphins, the body''s natural mood boosters. The repetitive motions of mixing and kneading can be calming and meditative, helping to quiet the mind and {{5}} stress. Additionally, the act of creation and the satisfaction of producing something delicious can boost confidence and self-esteem.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.improving, 2.moment, 3.enhances, 4.release, 5.reduce', NULL, NULL),
  ('84f61d2a-d890-512f-8734-c3ce592b2da3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '84f61d2a-d890-512f-8734-c3ce592b2da3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Exploration', E'Do you believe that space exploration is a good investment for governments?', NULL, NULL, E'Undoubtedly, I wholeheartedly affirm that space exploration represents a strategic and invaluable investment for governments. Beyond driving technological progress and expanding scientific frontiers, space exploration serves as a beacon of inspiration for future generations and a catalyst for fostering international collaboration and diplomacy on a global scale.\nSpace exploration serves as a dynamic force for driving technological advancements and innovations that benefit society at large. The challenges inherent in space missions propel the development of cutting-edge technologies, leading to breakthroughs in diverse fields such as communications, materials science, and healthcare. These advancements not only enhance our daily lives but also stimulate economic growth and open up new avenues for progress and discovery.\nThe discoveries stemming from space exploration contribute significantly to scientific knowledge and deepen our understanding of the universe. By unraveling the mysteries of celestial bodies and cosmic phenomena, scientists expand the frontiers of human knowledge and inspire awe and curiosity in future generations. Furthermore, space exploration serves as a unifying force, fostering international collaboration and diplomacy as nations come together to embark on ambitious space missions, transcending boundaries and fostering a sense of global unity.\nIn conclusion, the multifaceted impact of space exploration in inspiring future generations, fostering international collaboration, and driving technological progress underscores its pivotal role as a wise investment for governments. As we continue to explore the vast expanse of space, we not only push the boundaries of human knowledge but also nurture a spirit of curiosity, innovation, and cooperation that transcends borders and unites humanity in a shared quest for exploration and discovery.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8501118d-b9d0-5d1f-8dcf-60cf9ed10a6c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8501118d-b9d0-5d1f-8dcf-60cf9ed10a6c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the unit that is used to measure the size of an angle?', 'dfdb6304-6a7a-52f6-8722-85e37adde0f4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Degree / radian', NULL, NULL),
