  ('86620a11-4382-5dd0-b310-0f6ecffab2b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '86620a11-4382-5dd0-b310-0f6ecffab2b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Your Thesis', E'It is normally expected that the final version of your thesis which must be submitted to the university library in both hardcopy and electronic form will be freely available to the public. Once in the library, your thesis may be consulted, borrowed and copied in accordance with the regulations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('866814bb-ab28-5b18-89b2-8e0a392fb535'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '866814bb-ab28-5b18-89b2-8e0a392fb535'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1f568b3f-9c2d-551b-8baf-9d7fa4138a68'::uuid, NULL, E'Copying from the internet threatens to damage your chances of success.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('86690188-ed22-5bf8-af56-e2b318e50ace'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '86690188-ed22-5bf8-af56-e2b318e50ace'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sociology', E'Sociology is, in very basic terms, the study of human societies. In this respect, it is usually {{1}} as one of the social sciences (along with subjects like psychology) and was {{2}} as a subject in the late 18th century (through the work of people like the French writer Auguste Comte). However, the subject has only really gained {{3}} as an academic subject in the 20th century through the work of writers such as Emile Durkheim, Max Weber and Talcott Parsons (names that will be visited throughout this course). One name that you may have heard of-Karl Marx (the founder of modern Communism)-has probably done more to stimulate people'' s interest in the subject than anyone else, even though he lived and wrote (1818-1884) in a period before sociology became fully established as an academic discipline. Sociology, therefore, has a reasonably long history of development(150-200 years), {{4}} in Britain it has only been in the last 30- 40 years that sociology as an examined subject in the education system has achieved a level of importance equivalent to, or above, most of the other subjects it is possible to study.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.classed, 2.established, 3.acceptance, 4.although', NULL, NULL),
  ('8669e2ff-b1fc-5c38-bfec-a3a9ecd87bca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8669e2ff-b1fc-5c38-bfec-a3a9ecd87bca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which system in the human body is responsible for protecting against disease and infection?', '3da5593c-9538-5ecc-89cc-72bdd220b7e8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Immune system', NULL, NULL),
  ('866ad7bd-0f9f-56f7-b2dd-b31961bedaa5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '866ad7bd-0f9f-56f7-b2dd-b31961bedaa5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Take Risks', E'Some people like to do only what they already do well. Other people prefer to try new things and take risks. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, E'In life, we are often presented with the choice of sticking to what we know or trying new things and taking risks. While some people prefer to do only what they already do well, I strongly believe that it is important to try new things and take risks.\nFirstly, trying new things can lead to personal growth and development. When we step out of our comfort zones and try new things, we open ourselves up to new experiences and opportunities that can help us grow as individuals. For example, learning a new language or taking up a new hobby can expand our horizons and broaden our perspectives. It can also help us to discover new passions and interests that we may not have otherwise known about.\nSecondly, taking risks can build confidence and resilience. When we take risks, we learn to face our fears and overcome challenges. This can help us to become more confident in our abilities and develop a sense of resilience that can serve us well in all areas of life. It can also help us to develop important skills such as problem-solving, decision-making, and adaptability.\nIn conclusion, while it may be tempting to stick to what we already know and do well, it is important to try new things and take risks in order to grow and develop as individuals. By stepping out of our comfort zones and embracing new experiences, we can learn valuable lessons and achieve personal growth that we may not have otherwise. It is important to strike a balance between the two approaches in order to achieve success in a sustainable and fulfilling way. Ultimately, taking risks and trying new things can lead to a more fulfilling and rewarding life.', NULL, 200, 300),
