  ('86864250-9e21-5f1e-b026-809d4b75bf23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '86864250-9e21-5f1e-b026-809d4b75bf23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Traditional Classroom', E'Do you agree that the traditional classroom model is outdated?', NULL, NULL, E'The traditional classroom model is outdated, failing to meet the diverse learning needs and preferences of students in today''s dynamic educational landscape. With limited adaptability, interaction, and technology integration, traditional classrooms risk falling behind in providing effective and engaging learning environments for modern learners.\nTraditional classrooms often struggle to adapt to the diverse learning needs and preferences of students. The one-size-fits-all approach may not effectively cater to individual learning styles, paces, and interests, hindering student engagement and comprehension. As educational diversity continues to evolve, the rigid structure of traditional classrooms may impede personalized learning experiences and hinder academic progress.\nThe traditional classroom model tends to limit student interaction and engagement, hindering collaborative learning experiences and social development. In a traditional setting, students may have minimal opportunities for active participation, peer collaboration, and real-world application of knowledge. Moreover, the inadequate integration of modern technology in traditional classrooms restricts access to innovative learning tools, digital resources, and interactive teaching methods that can enhance student learning outcomes and prepare them for a technology-driven world.\nIn conclusion, the outdated nature of the traditional classroom model is evident in its lack of adaptability, limited interaction, and inadequate technology integration. To meet the evolving needs of 21st-century learners, educational institutions must embrace innovative approaches that prioritize personalized learning, student engagement, and technology-enhanced instruction. By reimagining the classroom environment to foster adaptability, interaction, and technology integration, educators can create dynamic learning spaces that empower students to thrive in an ever-changing educational landscape.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('86879aa7-5f40-5ad8-8ee2-81f1d1f7ec26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '86879aa7-5f40-5ad8-8ee2-81f1d1f7ec26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mitigation', E'As far as politics go, the responses are just as varied. Mitigation is common and calls for a reduction of emissions and less reliance on fossil fuels. Coal burning power plants are now replaced with hydraulic power plants and electrical cars are replacing some gasoline efficient cars. Many people, however, feel that this is not enough.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
