  ('884817a6-8a0e-5bbe-8fde-b65fdb04ebf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '884817a6-8a0e-5bbe-8fde-b65fdb04ebf7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1faab870-444e-5a0a-b944-db39e64a7e7f'::uuid, NULL, E'The media''s coverage of the election has been skewed from the very beginning.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('884a7629-3801-5512-b598-daa2f50a2118'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '884a7629-3801-5512-b598-daa2f50a2118'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'New Houses', E'It’s an {{1}} truth, but many of our houses are bad for the planet. They’re defined by a pattern of consumption, from the raw materials to build them, to the fuel required to sustain them, and the waste generated by them. Despite an improvement in building energy efficiency, 2021 saw carbon emissions from building and construction hit an all-time high. But what if a house could {{2}} the people living inside and the world outside too? What if a house could feed its occupants? Power itself? Boost biodiversity? Bond a community? And at the end of its life, leave no trace? Authored by Courtney Smith and Sean Topham, “Houses That Can Save the World” features over 150 projects from all over the globe. Some {{3}} existing spaces, such as the renovated Ensamble Studio''s off-grid cave dwelling in Menorca, Spain. Others revive and {{4}} ancient construction methods, like ZAV Architects’ adobe building community in Hormuz, Iran. Despite their positive outlook, the authors acknowledge that implementing the ideas in their book can be challenging.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.uncomfortable, 2.nurture, 3.repurpose, 4.update', NULL, NULL),
  ('884c4009-ec1b-53f1-85d0-85fcdf6e4df5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '884c4009-ec1b-53f1-85d0-85fcdf6e4df5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a993ebe1-9b6a-5a7d-9d99-e7bd26026f07'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This course provides valuable information for work experience.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8850e9cc-c8e8-529a-8c0f-3f085ec42e44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8850e9cc-c8e8-529a-8c0f-3f085ec42e44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Salamanders', E'Salamanders are a group of amphibians typically characterized by a lizard-like appearance, with slender bodies, blunt snouts, short limbs projecting at right angles to the body, and the presence of a tail in both larvae and adults.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('885872b6-5741-53cc-9f73-8966afba18de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '885872b6-5741-53cc-9f73-8966afba18de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Interdisciplinary Centre', E'A new interdisciplinary center for the study of the frontiers of the universe, from the tiniest subatomic particle to the largest chain of galaxies, has been formed at The University of Texas at Austin.\nThe Texas Cosmology Centre will be a way for the university''s departments of Astronomy and Physics to {{1}} on research that concerns them both.\n''This center will bring the two departments together in an area where they {{2}} — in the physics of the very early universe,'' said Dr. Neal Evans, Astronomy Department chair.\nAstronomical observations have {{3}} the presence of dark matter and dark energy, discoveries that challenge our knowledge of fundamental physics. And today''s leading theories in physics involve energies so high that no Earth-bound particle accelerator can test them. They need the universe as their {{6}} .\nSteven Weinberg, Nobel laureate and professor of physics at the university, called the Center''s {{7}} a very exciting development for that department.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.collaborate, 2.overlap, 3.revealed, 4.laboratory, 5.advent', NULL, NULL),
  ('885ab890-9979-5398-95d0-1b6e55b46657'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '885ab890-9979-5398-95d0-1b6e55b46657'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Potential Buyers', E'A market can be defined as a group of potential buyers with needs and wants and the purchasing power to {{1}} them. During the exchange process, the potential buyers “vote” (usually with their dollars) for the market offering they feel best {{2}} their needs. When marketers understand how buyers {{3}} at a decision, they can create offerings that will attract buyers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.satisfy, 2.meets, 3.arrive', NULL, NULL),
  ('885b421a-5e28-5a4c-811b-6d6344e0cc35'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '885b421a-5e28-5a4c-811b-6d6344e0cc35'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call money borrowed from banks?', '5b0528c3-cf10-54a7-a6c2-d0407628f607'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Loan', NULL, NULL),
  ('88631f2a-1a8d-532b-806b-9a9394e0de44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '88631f2a-1a8d-532b-806b-9a9394e0de44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the nominal form of the wide?', 'dfb15b0f-0db2-58e2-bb2a-54f1da979ed0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Width', NULL, NULL),
  ('886464bb-f2a8-5822-8cba-4aac10b28d46'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '886464bb-f2a8-5822-8cba-4aac10b28d46'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Christopher Columbus', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('8869cb8c-3a31-5629-8f6f-85e55bb723ca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8869cb8c-3a31-5629-8f6f-85e55bb723ca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Greenhouse Gases', E'When an individual drives a car, heats a house, or uses an aerosol hair spray, greenhouse gases are produced. In economic terms, this creates a classic negative externality. Most of the costs (in this case, those arising from global warming) are borne by individuals other than the one making the decision about how many miles to drive or how much hair spray to use. Because the driver (or sprayer) enjoys all the benefits of the activities but suffers only part of the cost, that individual engages in more than the economically efficient amount of the activity. In this sense, the problem of greenhouse gases parallels the problem that occurs when someone smokes a cigarette in an enclosed space or litters the countryside with fast-food wrappers. If we are to get individuals to reduce the production of greenhouse gases to the efficient rate, we must somehow induce them to act as though they bear all the costs of their actions. The two most widely accepted means of doing this are government regulation and taxation, both of which have been proposed to deal with greenhouse gases.', NULL, NULL, E'When an individual drives a car, greenhouse gases are produced, which creates a classic negative externality, and that individual engages in more than the economically efficient amount of the activity, so if we are to get individuals to reduce the production of greenhouse gases, we must somehow induce them to act as though they bear all the costs of their actions, while the two most widely accepted means are government regulation and taxation.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('886b3348-4253-55b0-a591-0fadb4c63bef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '886b3348-4253-55b0-a591-0fadb4c63bef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solar System', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 5, 2', NULL, NULL),
