  ('8ae0a6b0-97b6-542d-99a8-bba353887700'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ae0a6b0-97b6-542d-99a8-bba353887700'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Essay', E'Essays are used as an assessment tool to evaluate your ability to research a topic and construct an argument, as well as your understanding of subject content. This does not mean that essays are a ''regurgitation'' of everything your lecture has said throughout the course. Essays are your opportunity to explore in greater depth aspects of the course - theories, issues, texts, etc. and in some cases relate these aspects to a particular context. It is your opportunity to articulate your ideas, but in a certain way: using formal academic style.\n\nAccording to the text, which statement below is NOT true about essays?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Essays are basically what your lecture has said throughout the course.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8ae2962c-9fab-593e-a85d-f3b50d063de6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ae2962c-9fab-593e-a85d-f3b50d063de6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '008bece2-d46e-5361-9968-b8454b79c6b5'::uuid, NULL, E'You must call your doctor to make an appointment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8ae3d996-66ed-53fc-aa2b-252421df2e9d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ae3d996-66ed-53fc-aa2b-252421df2e9d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'QWERTY keyboard', E'In fact, the QWERTY keyboard layout is so {{1}} simply because it won a practicality battle almost 150 years ago. In the 19th century, we’re using typewriters to write and every error means you have to start {{2}} with the entire page, but the QWERTY keyboard found an elegant way of {{3}} this, by encouraging the typist to type one letter with one hand and one letter with another hand.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dominant, 2.over, 3.alleviating', NULL, NULL),
  ('8ae5a9cb-71f9-579f-b901-f72d08248068'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ae5a9cb-71f9-579f-b901-f72d08248068'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '13ffecf3-4b65-53cb-8e5a-718472c61262'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ensure restful sleep the night before a test for optimal performance.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8aeb8490-94b3-5cbd-95cf-709a7b39804c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8aeb8490-94b3-5cbd-95cf-709a7b39804c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Privacy', E'In today''s digital age, concerns about digital privacy have become increasingly prevalent and significant. As we embrace the convenience and connectivity of the online world, we must also grapple with the challenges it poses to our personal privacy and security. One of the primary concerns is data privacy. Tech giants and online platforms collect vast amounts of data on individuals, often without their explicit consent. This data includes personal information, browsing habits, and even location data. The misuse or mishandling of such data can have severe consequences, from identity theft to invasive targeted advertising. Another issue is the erosion of anonymity. Our online activities are often tracked, leaving a digital trail of our behavior and preferences. This loss of anonymity can lead to unwarranted surveillance, online harassment, and the chilling effect on free speech as individuals become hesitant to express their views openly. Furthermore, the rise of social media has exacerbated concerns about privacy. Sharing personal information and updates on social networks can expose individuals to risks such as cyberbullying, misinformation, and the unintended spread of private content. Legislation and regulations regarding digital privacy are still evolving and often struggle to keep pace with rapid technological advancements. It is essential for individuals to take proactive steps to protect their digital privacy, such as using secure passwords, enabling two-factor authentication, and being cautious about sharing personal information online. Moreover, raising awareness about digital privacy issues and advocating for stronger privacy protections are crucial steps in addressing this growing concern. As individuals, organizations, and governments work together, we can find a balance between enjoying the benefits of the digital age and safeguarding our fundamental right to privacy.', NULL, NULL, E'In the digital age, increasing concerns about digital privacy encompass data protection, erosion of anonymity, social media risks, and the challenge of evolving legislation, necessitating proactive individual measures and collective efforts for stronger privacy safeguards to balance the benefits of connectivity with the fundamental right to privacy.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('8af28029-ed36-52e6-bee4-bd15a8d6a90d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8af28029-ed36-52e6-bee4-bd15a8d6a90d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mental Illness', E'One of the great contributing factors to mental illness is the idea that we should at all costs and at all times be well. We suffer far more than we should because of how long it can take many of us until we allow ourselves to fall properly and usefully ill.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8af3cc2e-1e45-5b05-aa76-42cb97caba99'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8af3cc2e-1e45-5b05-aa76-42cb97caba99'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Chapters', E'Most chapters have a mixed exercise after the {{1}} work of the chapter has been completed. This will help you {{2}} what you have done, either when you have finished the chapter or at a later date. All chapters {{3}} with some mathematical puzzles and practical investigational work. For this work you are encouraged to {{4}} your ideas with others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.main, 2.revise, 3.end, 4.share', NULL, NULL),
  ('8af63389-3ce6-5170-9689-8981800eb3b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8af63389-3ce6-5170-9689-8981800eb3b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3f662a71-5881-599e-8dc6-6f00e45fdd7e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To comprehend human behavior profoundly, one must scrutinize and analyze their actions.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8afa5c5d-45d4-5448-a8a3-3d9dc942df3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8afa5c5d-45d4-5448-a8a3-3d9dc942df3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drinking Water', E'Water involves in almost all the {{1}} in our body such as digestion, elimination, assimilation, respiration, maintaining body temperature, etc.. It is required to {{2}} the thirst of our body. We can live for days without food, however, cannot imagine living without water more than a day. The level of useful drinking water on the earth is very less and other water is salty and not useful to the living beings. Water is {{3}} by everything like plants, animals, microorganisms, human being, etc., to fulfill the body requirements. Do we imagine what will {{4}} if the drinking water gets {{5}} a day or gets polluted? Yes, it is the main question which has opened the eyes of everyone and starts saving water at every place we belong like home, surrounding area, office, school, college, etc..', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.processes, 2.remove, 3.required, 4.happen, 5.finished', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b0b7d78-2f82-5b85-a6a2-434a9691c7a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b0b7d78-2f82-5b85-a6a2-434a9691c7a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mental Health Problems', E'Many mental health problems emerge during adolescence. Among these are disorders such as depression and anxiety, which manifest as internalizing symptoms, including low mood and worrying. Other conditions such as attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) manifest as externalizing symptoms, such as impulsive behavior.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b0cb1bf-a954-571f-a3fc-60f84b22c5e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b0cb1bf-a954-571f-a3fc-60f84b22c5e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '76bb5755-f44a-5d68-91bb-93bdee1fadf6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A very basic feature of computing would be counting and calculating.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b0d9711-f763-5513-96fe-acae3a2852d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b0d9711-f763-5513-96fe-acae3a2852d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Business Schools', E'It''s been reported recently that some business schools have decided to make changes to students'' grades by increasing them by ten percent. This means that a C grade automatically becomes a B, and a B grade automatically becomes an A - under the new grading system. And the change is retrospective, which means that it applies to all grades that have been achieved since the schools'' current grading system - er, which was introduced in 2007 - has been in place. Now, there are at least eight business schools who''ve changed their grading levels, and they decided to award their graduates higher grades so they would be more attractive in the highly competitive job market.\nHowever, changing grades like this has been criticized by the academic and business communities, because many people think the grades have been falsely exaggerated and don''t reflect the true ability of the student. In fact, many employers realize when a school has made adjustments to students'' grades and so there is no real benefit in doing this. Um, lifting the grades may even be damaging to the students because employers may believe that the graduates were given the high grades when they didn''t deserve them.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '897aabe3-ad5b-588c-9ad5-d3481122e4af'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'In order to improve the chances of their students obtaining jobs after they have finished their courses, some business schools are adjusting their grades. These adjustments are being made to all grades awarded since 2007 but instead of C benefiting the students it is, in some instances, having the opposite effect.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b0e5147-24b0-597c-a3dd-0b5909bfdbf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b0e5147-24b0-597c-a3dd-0b5909bfdbf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Large Marimo', E'Large marimo are now thought to be exclusively found in Lake Akan, and as seen from the data, even there they have become threatened. Therefore, it is necessary to propose measures to protect marimo from global warming, such as utilizing the cooler river water that flows into the marimo colony.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b0eb77f-4900-5806-b6d7-eb5dd7bf87dd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b0eb77f-4900-5806-b6d7-eb5dd7bf87dd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Assistive Products', E'The primary purpose of assistive products is to maintain or improve an individual’s functioning and independence, {{1}} promoting their well-being. They enable people to live healthy, productive and {{2}} lives, and to participate in education, the labor market and civic life. Moreover, access to appropriate assistive products can have a {{3}} impact on community development and economic growth. Despite the global need and recognized benefits of assistive products, access to assistive products {{4}} limited.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.thereby, 2.dignified, 3.tremendous, 4.remains', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b195c53-4935-52cd-b005-2268004dd00a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b195c53-4935-52cd-b005-2268004dd00a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Boring Job(无聊的工作)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 4, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b2aaab6-8f1d-566c-b4ad-f422a1541377'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b2aaab6-8f1d-566c-b4ad-f422a1541377'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electricity', E'Every online interaction relies on a scaffolding of information stored in remote servers—and those machines, stacked together in data centers worldwide, require a lot of energy. Around the globe, data centers currently account for about 1 to 1.5 percent of global electricity use, according to the International Energy Agency. And the world’s still-exploding boom in artificial intelligence could drive that number up a lot — and fast.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b3b272a-a76f-5717-8da2-6eeaf395b656'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b3b272a-a76f-5717-8da2-6eeaf395b656'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Extraterrestrial Life', E'The search for extraterrestrial life has fascinated scientists and the public alike for decades. With advances in technology and the discovery of exoplanets, the possibility of finding life beyond Earth is becoming increasingly likely. However, the search remains challenging, requiring innovative approaches and sophisticated instruments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b496eb2-203a-5726-80e9-56c385715a05'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b496eb2-203a-5726-80e9-56c385715a05'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd69ea9b8-b70b-5fc7-8740-30c1945d569b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A thorough bibliography is needed at the end of every assignment.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b4c2d87-3a3f-5ef9-bb02-1d4fc5fdd431'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b4c2d87-3a3f-5ef9-bb02-1d4fc5fdd431'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Psychology and Law', E'Listen to part of a lecture in a psychology class. The professor is talking about stating laws in the science of psychology. Psychology is a relatively new science. Like other sciences, psychology must be able to state laws. A law is a way of organizing knowledge about something so that we can make predictions. When enough knowledge is gained about a subject, a scientist can state precisely what will happen under certain conditions. We experimental psychologists are interested in developing laws about human behavior, so we''ll be able to understand and predict what people do and why they do it. Of course, to develop laws about human behavior, we must assume there''s some regularity to it. We can''t be psychologists without making assumption. The behaviour follows certain patterns. One of the major law psychology start escaping is called the law of effect. The law of effect states that whether or not a person will repeat a behavior depends on the effect that behavior has. If an action is rewarded, it''s likely to be repeated. If the action is not rewarded, or if it''s punished, IT''s not likely to be repeated. How do psychologists state laws? First, using available knowledge, a psychologist makes a hypothesis about behavior. Then the psychologist tests the hypothesis through an experiment. But even if the experiment proves the hypothesis was correct, it''s not yet a law. it''s just the beginning of the work to arrive at a law that will apply to all humans. Many repetitions of the experiment must be conducted under different conditions. Only repeated verification, especially proof that the behavior can be predicted, will result in a law.\n\nAccording to the professor, why are psychologists interested in developing laws?', '0c93c025-3eee-5950-a5d1-5682413aac21'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To be able to make predictions about human behavior', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b4d77df-0abd-5c7f-8bf3-fe38fb4d5f82'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b4d77df-0abd-5c7f-8bf3-fe38fb4d5f82'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vitamin D', NULL, 'c3830f9b-0cf5-5e06-9acc-03281fd9a81f'::uuid, NULL, E'Vitamin D refers to a group of fat--soluble secosteroids responsible for enhancing intestinal absorption of calcium, iron, magnesium, phosphate and zinc. In humans, the most important compounds in this group are vitamin D3 and vitamin D2 Cholecalciferol and ergocalciferol can be ingested from the diet and from supplements. Very few foods contain vitamin D; synthesis of vitamin D (specifically cholecalciferol) in the skin is the major natural source of the vitamin. Dermal synthesis of vitamin D from cholesterol is dependent on sun exposure Vitamin D from the diet or dermal synthesis from sunlight is biologically inactive; activation requires enzymatic conversion (hydroxylation) in the liver and kidney.Evidence indicates the synthesis of vitamin D from sun exposure is regulated by a negative feedback loop that prevents toxicity, but because of uncertainty about the cancer risk from sunlight, no recommendations are issued by the Institute of Medicine (US), for the amount of sun exposure required to meet vitamin D requirements. Accordingly, the Dietary Reference Intake for vitamin D assumes no synthesis occurs and all of a person''s vitamin D is from food intake, although that will rarely occur in practice. As vitamin D is synthesized in adequate amounts by most mammals exposed to sunlight[citation needed], it is not strictly a vitamin, and may be considered a hormone as its synthesis and activity occur in different locations. Vitamin D has a significant role in calcium homeostasis and metabolism. Its discovery was due to effort to find the dietary substance lacking in rickets.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b515962-65fe-5e43-97c9-53ffd82c4d9c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b515962-65fe-5e43-97c9-53ffd82c4d9c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'War of Ideas', E'''In a war of ideas, it is people who get killed''. Does a common man suffer from a group’s ideology? Express your opinion and support the same with reasons and examples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8b58fc0b-1087-5878-a57a-59b1e6a4ebbd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b58fc0b-1087-5878-a57a-59b1e6a4ebbd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who extracts minerals from the ground?', '7e5e96ae-0fc9-5149-a525-8d6a89caa54c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Miner', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b5bee9f-253c-580e-ac54-574b1ca6570d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b5bee9f-253c-580e-ac54-574b1ca6570d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Columbus', E'Columbus was the first European to attempt to sail to China by sailing West across the Atlantic but he never actually landed on the mainland of North America. Since the Americas were already populated when he arrived at least one group of people had beaten him there. Archaeological evidence shows that several Viking expeditions reached North America and there are fringe theories of other Pre-Columbus visits to America.\nColumbus’s trip to America is often claimed as a voyage of discovery. In many senses it was, but it was not the first trip to the Americas nor even the first European expedition.\nHumans first crossed to the Americas from Asia during the last Ice Age. About 30,000 years ago a land bridge existed between Siberia and Alaska. These people can certainly be said to have discovered America quite some time before Columbus. But if you wish to overlook them, and they so often are, there were other discoverers of America.\nThe Icelandic Sagas talk of expeditions to the West which reached two landing sites- one called Greenland and one called Vinland. Greenland can be easily identified as the country we now call Greenland. But it was thought that visits to Vinland were mythical.\nIn 1960 at a place called Laux Meadows in Newfoundland the remains of a Viking settlement were discovered. Settled around 1000AD the village included houses and a forge built along traditional Viking lines. The discovery shows that Columbus was at least 500 years too late to be called the discoverer of America.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('8b5d1206-188b-5d7b-8a0e-0503299eb242'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b5d1206-188b-5d7b-8a0e-0503299eb242'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Who discovered gravity?', '3cda7cfb-5f25-534f-8ad6-482d2beb69f6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Newton', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b5fa9a8-3e7b-58ea-856f-3d2c8de351ff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b5fa9a8-3e7b-58ea-856f-3d2c8de351ff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fe05d0b9-5df8-56e7-b1ce-a7ea20fb0156'::uuid, NULL, E'Social events and training days are arranged for all the staff.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b6246c8-dca4-5be6-bb04-268e3781264f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b6246c8-dca4-5be6-bb04-268e3781264f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c7c4b376-4d3f-5ca7-83bc-c7311011d4c6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Eating too much can lead to too many health problems.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b651547-f432-5ec8-818c-577660429dd4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b651547-f432-5ec8-818c-577660429dd4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '77d96a4d-f284-53b4-b901-58cae96a0c51'::uuid, NULL, E'Experts cannot agree on a single definition of intelligence.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b6904b8-47bb-584d-9866-a3efe8942d6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b6904b8-47bb-584d-9866-a3efe8942d6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Magna Carta', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b6cbbad-c7c9-5940-8e81-8fd5c952c66e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b6cbbad-c7c9-5940-8e81-8fd5c952c66e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'America’s Economic Size', NULL, '522a2b5b-40a4-5628-904c-4c2451ae74e7'::uuid, NULL, E'One way to understand a country''s economic strength is by looking at the size of economy. In terms of overall economic size, the United States produces more than the total amount of several major economies, including China, Japan, the UK, and Germany. This comparison highlights the significant role the United States plays in the global economy. Another important indicator is the industrial output. US output is approximately $2.8 trillion, making it one of the largest manufacturing sectors in the world. Interestingly, this figure equals to the sum of China and Japan, showing the remarkable scale of American industrial production. Although many countries continue to expand their economies, the United States remains one of the world''s leading economic powers.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b6e5134-49d8-5ed1-a261-f1d3c8835fb5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b6e5134-49d8-5ed1-a261-f1d3c8835fb5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'SMW', E'I''d like to know more about psychology. I think it''s a very interesting subject to study. I''d like to know why I do the things I do. Looking at how the brain works and how we behave might make me understand people more. I''d particularly like to study child psychology. I love looking at children, playing, thinking, drawing, doing anything, really. But what makes them tick? What goes on in their little minds? Or perhaps I should say their big minds. If we all knew more about child psychology, perhaps we could do more to be a positive influence on children. Being a psychologist must be a very interesting job, listening to people talk all day and then analyzing their behavior. I wonder if they ever get.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '6ead6593-998a-5ef0-a0c6-41ca56db97c7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'bored', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b748ecd-36f7-52e9-8c37-998eb2dd7c26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b748ecd-36f7-52e9-8c37-998eb2dd7c26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8f957ef6-78e7-53fc-8043-0201413d2d2b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Everyone here has to follow the rules of this place.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b795b71-c3e6-5dd5-9100-cc1cfcd0a4ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b795b71-c3e6-5dd5-9100-cc1cfcd0a4ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Australian Women Novelists', E'In the literary world, it was an accepted assumption that the 1970s was a time of unprecedented growth in homegrown Australian fiction. And everybody was reading and talking about books by young Australian women. But it was {{1}} recently that a researcher was able to measure just how many novels were published in that decade, and she found that {{2}} a decline in novels by Australian writers overall, but confirmed an increase in women''s novels. It is this sort of research - testing ideas about literary history - that {{3}} possible with the spread of ''Digital Humanities.'' The intersection of Humanities and digital technologies {{4}} opportunities in the fields of literature, linguistics, history and language that {{5}} without computational methods and digitized resources to {{6}} information together in an accessible way. Transcription software is being developed for turning scans of books and documents into text, as the field of digital humanities really takes {{7}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.not until, 2.there had been, 3.is becoming, 4.is opening up, 5.were not possible, 6.bring, 7.off', NULL, NULL),
  ('8b889c6c-1b0e-5b66-bd85-e84c31721710'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b889c6c-1b0e-5b66-bd85-e84c31721710'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tuition Fees', E'University tuition fees are increasing. Some argue that higher education should be made free. To what extent do you agree?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8b8f0a42-94e4-50f5-904d-d335fc8a2274'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b8f0a42-94e4-50f5-904d-d335fc8a2274'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Danny Danziger', E'Using more than fifty interviews, award-winning writer Danny Danziger creates a fascinating mosaic of the people behind New York''s magnificent Metropolitan Museum of Art from the aristocratic, acerbic director of the museum, Philippe de Montebello, to the curators who have a deep knowledge and passionate appreciation of their collections, from the security guards to the philanthropists who keep the museum''s financial life blood flowing.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b93389f-b79e-50c2-878a-2e1303db6587'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b93389f-b79e-50c2-878a-2e1303db6587'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Stationary Bike', E'A stationary bike workout is a low-impact workout that uses smooth movements to strengthen bones and joints without putting much pressure on them. Because your feet don’t lift off the pedals with a stationary bike, this option is kinder to your joints, but it still provides a challenging and effective workout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8b9d9b45-272d-5481-bf93-2397d1cdd55b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8b9d9b45-272d-5481-bf93-2397d1cdd55b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Speaker', E'It is difficult to tell whether the speaker approves of Hemingway''s lifestyle or not. He was famously macho and spent a lot of time hunting wild animals, going to wars and getting into fights. All these things got into his books, and the speaker thinks that this is not necessarily a good thing as it means that too many people prefer reading about his life to his books.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8ba197ca-c205-5c72-8243-22adbeae67bc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ba197ca-c205-5c72-8243-22adbeae67bc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a noun that is made of two or more words,such as ‘greenhouse’ , ’bookshop‘ and ’deadline‘?', '55809cbf-7a91-559f-8e36-32d0eafd7aa8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Compound', NULL, NULL),
  ('8ba85107-55ff-5fec-9d8b-6c43a777c1ac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ba85107-55ff-5fec-9d8b-6c43a777c1ac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Green Tea', E'Green tea, one of the oldest herbal teas known, has been {{1}} for centuries in many countries. Modern research suggests that green tea can help in reducing the {{2}} of certain chronic diseases. This is largely {{3}} to its high content of antioxidants known as catechins. Despite these {{4}} , it''s important for people to understand that green tea is not a cure-all and should be part of a balanced {{5}} and healthy lifestyle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.consumed, 2.risk, 3.attributed, 4.benefits, 5.diet', NULL, NULL),
  ('8ba8c29a-a2f4-5a10-a1b4-4d836efce9a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8ba8c29a-a2f4-5a10-a1b4-4d836efce9a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e747fb35-55e2-5961-a131-815166f6de8c'::uuid, NULL, E'They have many ways to learn about our minds and what we do.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8bab9e0d-afab-52b1-816e-b4d555033e70'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bab9e0d-afab-52b1-816e-b4d555033e70'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bioluminescence', E'Bioluminescence, the extraordinary ability of some organisms to produce light, is one of nature''s most fascinating phenomena. Found in a variety of creatures, from deep-sea squids to fireflies, bioluminescence serves a range of unique functions in the biological world. This natural glow is the result of a chemical reaction within the organism, involving a light-emitting molecule called luciferin and an enzyme known as luciferase. The color of the light produced can vary from green to blue, and even red, depending on the species and the environment in which they live. In the deep sea, bioluminescence is often used for survival strategies. Many marine creatures, such as the anglerfish, use their luminous ability to attract prey or mates in the darkness of the ocean depths. Some species emit light to confuse predators or as a defense mechanism to avoid being eaten. On land, fireflies are among the most well-known bioluminescent organisms. These insects use their light as a communication tool to attract mates. The pattern of flashes is unique to each species, helping them find suitable partners. Research into bioluminescence is not just limited to understanding these organisms but extends to its application in science and medicine. Bioluminescent proteins have been used in research to track the spread of cancer cells, monitor bacterial growth, and even detect environmental pollutants. In conclusion, bioluminescence is a remarkable example of nature''s ingenuity. It not only adds beauty to the natural world but also plays a critical role in the survival of various species. With ongoing research, the secrets of bioluminescence continue to illuminate our understanding of life and offer exciting possibilities in scientific discovery.', NULL, NULL, E'Bioluminescence, a fascinating natural phenomenon where organisms like squids and fireflies emit light, plays crucial survival roles and has wide-ranging applications in scientific research, from cancer tracking to environmental monitoring, demonstrating nature''s complexity and its contribution to scientific advancements.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('8bb3b5d1-e9ca-532f-93ae-6aee8cd67101'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bb3b5d1-e9ca-532f-93ae-6aee8cd67101'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Holistic Medicine', E'A critique often directed at holistic medicine is that it {{1}} more towards philosophy than empirical science. While there is some {{2}} to this argument, proponents of holistic approaches do not understand the need to be defensive. This situation could {{3}} from the high regard society places on empirical evidence over holistic experiences.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.leans, 2.merit, 3.stem', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bb43e50-681b-5413-8b69-f49f37b99170'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bb43e50-681b-5413-8b69-f49f37b99170'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Smartphones', E'Smartphones have come a long way {{1}} they were just for calling and texting. It''s amazing how they''ve turned into these powerful devices that do so much more. Now, they''re like having a mini-computer in your pocket. You can do almost everything with them – {{2}} navigating around town, shopping online, to even managing your work and social life. The cameras on these phones are getting so good; some people don''t even bother with a separate camera anymore. And the apps – there are apps for just about everything you can think of. What''s {{3}} all these changes? It''s all about the technology. They''ve got better screens, faster processors, and cameras that can take some pretty amazing photos. But it''s not all perfect. As smartphones get more advanced, they also get more expensive. And then there''s the issue of {{4}} with all these changes. Not everyone can afford to get the latest model every year. Plus, there are concerns about things like privacy and how much time we''re all spending {{5}} at screens. Despite these issues, it''s clear that smartphones have become a crucial part of modern life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.since, 2.from, 3.driving, 4.keeping up, 5.staring', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bbc05ff-71ae-58f4-b2c9-567fb0598f85'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bbc05ff-71ae-58f4-b2c9-567fb0598f85'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ionizers', E'The role of ionizers is to purify the air with the help of electricity. During this process, negative ions are created that discharge these ions into the air. In this case, they are attached to particles with a positive charge. Some of these harmful particles include smoke, bacteria and pollen. The reaction between these ions helps purify the air inside your room office.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8bbd00dc-7ea5-5d14-8874-0bd8a94c91c7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bbd00dc-7ea5-5d14-8874-0bd8a94c91c7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mona Lisa', E'Mona Lisa depicts a woman with a mysterious smile and has become one of the most famous and iconic works of art in history. The painting''s enigmatic expression and subtle details have captivated viewers for centuries and inspired countless interpretations and analyses by art historians and critics.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8bbd1b68-88d0-5536-b92d-c1534c3e5eb8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bbd1b68-88d0-5536-b92d-c1534c3e5eb8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7f7940c7-26d5-5fc3-90da-277b5b06d008'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Effective communication is crucial for success in the business world.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bbd963e-215d-513b-a895-e04b0df1a10a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bbd963e-215d-513b-a895-e04b0df1a10a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neck Pain', E'There’s another culprit you may not be considering for neck pain -- how you sleep. Generally, when you wake up with neck pain, either your pillow isn’t right for you or the position in which your sleep is {{1}} your neck, or both. Experts suggest choosing a pillow that supports the natural curve of your neck. In general, sleeping on your back or side is best for preventing neck or back pain as both positions help {{2}} your spine’s natural curves. The ideal position is to sleep on your back on a pillow that allows your neck to be positioned so you’re looking {{3}} at the ceiling. If you’re a side sleeper, you might think that a hard pillow can hurt your neck, but it’s usually a pillow that’s too soft that makes you wake up with neck pain. Use pillows between your knees, and sometimes in front of your chest or belly to rest your arm to prevent your shoulders from rolling forward which could {{4}} your neck while you are sleeping. The idea is to keep blood flowing through your joints and subsequently your nerves to prevent pain.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.aggravating, 2.maintain, 3.straight, 4.rotate', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bc0f296-bc30-5085-92d3-8aaa816e923e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bc0f296-bc30-5085-92d3-8aaa816e923e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Speed of Earth', E'Our planet usually takes 24 hours to rotate on its {{1}} but not anymore. On July 29, Earth’s full spin was 1.50 milliseconds shorter than 24 hours, which means Earth experienced its shortest day ever. However, this wasn’t just a one-time fluke. Earth has been in a hurry in recent years. As per International Earth Rotation and Reference Systems (IERS), in 2020, Earth recorded 28 shortest days. Earth’s faster rotation could affect our clocks. The time that you and your mobile phone live by is {{2}} by Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). It is responsible for setting your time zone. This time, also known as astronomical time, is {{3}} on how long it takes for Earth to complete one rotation. As the rotation speed picks up, people who watch the Earth’s rotation and world’s clock for a living, will have to introduce a leap second to keep up with Earth’s pace and synchronize clocks with it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.axis, 2.dictated, 3.dependent', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bc46474-6e25-54e6-9e11-30cd896563e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bc46474-6e25-54e6-9e11-30cd896563e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '48c4aaf4-a2c7-59db-8f8f-51cb97bb0eee'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The lecture scheduled for the third day will cover essential course materials.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bc652d2-2fc0-56f0-9cac-18602deb85a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bc652d2-2fc0-56f0-9cac-18602deb85a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6391fea5-3179-568a-813d-79a7365d5929'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Trees benefit the city by soaking up the rainwater that runs off its road.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bc9be65-d4fd-5d2d-b575-12e7c29483e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bc9be65-d4fd-5d2d-b575-12e7c29483e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Plastic Pollution', E'There are at least five hotspots of floating plastic in the global ocean. These are gyres, where circulating currents trap debris. This one — the so-called Great Pacific Garbage Patch — is the largest, with almost 80,000 tonnes distributed over 600,000 square miles. The scientists teamed up with a charity that collects old fishing gear and other litter from the ocean, and gathered hundreds of plastic items to study in the lab. They found plants and animals, including anemones, tiny marine bugs, molluscs, and crabs on 90% of the debris they examined. As well as creating a semi-permanent floating habitat for coastal species in the open ocean, the researchers say all this plastic could be providing invasive species with rafts that allow them to cross the Pacific. This, they say, is yet another unintended consequence of plastic pollution for the ocean.\n\nAccording to the speaker, which of the statements below are true?', '9ee80e15-26cd-5632-a336-4ee3eb96afc3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ocean circulation will gather plastic in the sea.\nPlastic can provide space for invasive species, which allows them to invade.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bdfed52-5332-5f5c-8fee-7f986a75ff20'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bdfed52-5332-5f5c-8fee-7f986a75ff20'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fresh Water', E'Everybody needs fresh water. {{1}} water, people, animals and plants cannot live. Although a few plants and animals can make do with saltwater, all humans need a constant supply of fresh water if they are to stay {{2}} and healthy. Of the total supply of water on the Earth, only about 3 percent of it is fresh, and most of that is stored as ice and snow at the poles, or is so {{3}} under the surface of the Earth that we cannot get to it. Despite so much of the water being out of reach, we still have a million cubic miles of it that we {{4}} use. That''s about 4,300,000 cubic kilometers of fresh water to share out between most of the plants, animals and people on the planet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Without, 2.fit, 3.deep, 4.can', NULL, NULL),
  ('8bdffec7-ba9a-5850-baa3-4b1a9a4ed8cf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8bdffec7-ba9a-5850-baa3-4b1a9a4ed8cf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Robotics', E'What is your opinion on the role of robotics in the future of work?', NULL, NULL, E'I firmly believe that robotics will play a crucial role in boosting efficiency in future work environments. The integration of robotics offers a range of benefits that can revolutionize the way tasks are performed and enhance overall productivity in various industries.\nOne key benefit of robotics is their ability to automate repetitive tasks, which can significantly enhance productivity and efficiency in the workplace. By shouldering the burden of routine and monotonous tasks, robots liberate human workers to channel their energies towards tackling more intricate and innovative aspects of their roles, fostering a work environment characterized by enhanced creativity and streamlined operations.\nAdditionally, robotics excel in performing hazardous tasks that pose risks to human workers, thereby reducing the likelihood of workplace injuries. From working in dangerous environments to handling materials that could be harmful to humans, robots provide a safer alternative by taking on tasks that would otherwise jeopardize the well-being of human employees. Moreover, robotics offer high precision in tasks that require accuracy, leading to improved quality and consistency in work outcomes. Robots'' precision and accuracy guarantee meticulous task execution, leading to superior work quality and enhanced performance consistency.\nIn conclusion, the role of robotics in the future of work is poised to revolutionize industries by enhancing efficiency, ensuring safety in hazardous tasks, and delivering precision in work outcomes.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8be10199-c979-52a6-8242-f9f5a1857645'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8be10199-c979-52a6-8242-f9f5a1857645'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '856d65fe-d83d-533c-898d-92bfd0d56e91'::uuid, NULL, E'Our business is built on the network of alumni, friends and partners.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8be92c3c-3dcf-54bf-86e7-72e5de4be2ac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8be92c3c-3dcf-54bf-86e7-72e5de4be2ac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the medical tool used to compress a limb to control bleeding?', 'f366c1ef-0e78-5bdc-8794-914b501e1f94'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tourniquet', NULL, NULL),
