  ('8c2582ba-94e0-5487-88e5-98af48c0135f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c2582ba-94e0-5487-88e5-98af48c0135f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Questionnaire', E'The How I Feel About My School questionnaire, designed by experts at the University of Exeter Medical School, is {{1}} to download for free. It {{2}} emoticon-style faces with options of happy, ok or sad. It asks children to rate how they feel in seven situations including on the way to school, in the classroom and in the playground. It is {{3}} to help teachers and others to {{4}} with very young children on complex emotions. The project was supported by the National Institute for Health Research Collaboration for Applied Health Research and Care South West Peninsula ( NIHR PenCLAHRC). Professor Tamsin Ford, Professor of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry at the University of Exeter Medical School, {{5}} the design, involving children to give feedback on which style of questionnaire they could relate to best. She said: "When we''re {{6}} out research in schools, it can be really hard to meaningfully assess how very young children are feeling. We couldn''t find anything that could provide what we needed, so we decided to create something."', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.available, 2.uses, 3.designed, 4.communicate, 5.led, 6.carrying', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c2c73eb-a418-5eba-8796-ea8e1e9cf78d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c2c73eb-a418-5eba-8796-ea8e1e9cf78d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Employee Diversity', E'Until the 1950s and 1960s, diversity was not {{1}} with the workplace in the United States. In general, people were {{2}} based on their gender, race, social status, and religion. But there were a few exceptions, particularly in fields in which qualified employees were {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.associated, 2.hired, 3.scarce', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c2e7c09-6780-542c-8248-9e322512c630'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c2e7c09-6780-542c-8248-9e322512c630'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Beavers', E'Beavers are capable of building dams that can {{1}} for decades or even more. A dam with an underwater entrance can’t easily be {{2}} by a terrestrial predator and in times of emergency, and it can also be used as a {{3}} for a swift escape.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.last, 2.compromised, 3.tunnel', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c30675e-3751-5b9c-a577-de4307adf1ba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c30675e-3751-5b9c-a577-de4307adf1ba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Darkness', E'The increasing darkness in the Northern Hemisphere this time of year indicates to the plant that {{1}} is coming on. So it starts recouping materials from the {{2}} before they drop off. Evergreens protect their needle-like foliage from freezing with {{3}} coatings and natural "antifreezes." But broadleaf plants, like sugar maples, birches, and sumacs, have no such protections. As a result, they {{4}} their leaves. But before they do, the plants first try to {{5}} important nutrients such as nitrogen and phosphorus.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.autumn, 2.leaves, 3.waxy, 4.shed, 5.salvage', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c38262a-e506-5308-9f78-97d71c73d42b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c38262a-e506-5308-9f78-97d71c73d42b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bridges in Digital Age', E'In an era dominated by technology and screens, the significance of genuine human connections cannot be overstated. As our lives become increasingly intertwined with digital platforms, it''s essential to recognize and nurture the human relationships that form the foundation of our society.\nDespite the convenience and connectivity provided by social media and digital communication tools, there''s a growing concern that these virtual interactions often lack depth and authenticity. A simple "like" or "comment" on a social media post cannot replace the warmth of a smile, the comfort of a hug, or the understanding in a friend''s eyes during a face-to-face conversation.\nHuman connections are not just about the exchange of information; they are about empathy, shared experiences, and emotional support. They are about listening, understanding, and offering a helping hand when needed. These connections create a sense of belonging and contribute to our overall well-being.\nBuilding and nurturing meaningful human relationships require time, effort, and intentionality. It involves being present with others, actively listening, and showing genuine interest in their lives. It involves reaching out to friends and family, strengthening bonds, and creating a support network that can weather life''s challenges.\nIn a world that often values virtual connections and digital distractions, let us not forget the profound impact of human relationships. As we navigate the digital age, let us make a conscious effort to prioritize genuine human connections, for they are the threads that weave the fabric of our lives, providing comfort, joy, and a sense of belonging in an increasingly complex world.', NULL, NULL, E'In our technology-dominated era, the importance of nurturing genuine human connections is paramount, as they offer empathy, shared experiences, and emotional support beyond the superficial interactions of digital platforms, requiring intentional effort to build and maintain, ultimately enriching our lives with a sense of belonging and well-being.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('8c38f9f5-dafc-51dc-afea-3e74b291a1f4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c38f9f5-dafc-51dc-afea-3e74b291a1f4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dark Matter', E'Dark matter is an elusive substance that provides the skeleton for what cosmologists call the cosmic web, the large-scale structure of the universe that, due to its gravitational influence, dictates the motion of galaxies and other cosmic material. However, the distribution of local dark matter is currently unknown because it cannot be measured directly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8c3dd417-e2de-5d2d-b38f-40e6ac79a4d2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c3dd417-e2de-5d2d-b38f-40e6ac79a4d2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yolk and Sex', E'When it comes to lizard sex, size does matter. But not in the way you might think. Because in the June 4th online issue of the journal Current Biology, {{1}} say that for at least one type of lizard, larger eggs are more likely to make girls while smaller eggs yield boys.\nFor many animals, the sex of an individual is dictated solely by its {{2}} . But for small alpine lizards, gender isn''t so cut-and-dried. The scientists had earlier found that nest temperature can {{3}} the sex of lizard hatchlings. Cooler nests turn out more boys—no matter what their chromosomes say. At the same time, the researchers noticed that larger eggs seemed to make more {{4}} . But they wanted to put their observation to the test. So they took big eggs and removed some yolk—and, voila, they made males. Adding yolk to a little egg was a recipe for a female.\nThis size {{5}} might allow moms to balance their babies'' sexes when a chilly nest would otherwise produce mostly sons. Because when it comes to alpine lizards, sex {{6}} all comes down to a {{7}} yolk.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.scientists, 2.chromosomes, 3.influence, 4.daughters, 5.manipulation, 6.determination, 7.practical', NULL, NULL),
