  ('8c59cad0-560b-567d-a721-e7de76357338'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c59cad0-560b-567d-a721-e7de76357338'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is fake money called?', '8e8fb56a-db95-576c-8844-3eab52ec4632'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Counterfeit money / fake note', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c65ae21-a265-51ef-8b91-17762f5b6333'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c65ae21-a265-51ef-8b91-17762f5b6333'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Body Energy', E'If you''ve ever had to pick up and carry a tired child through the mall, you know that walking sometimes tuckers out the {{1}} . Now scientists think they know why. The results appear in the Journal of Experimental Biology.\nLarger animals tend to use less energy per gram of body {{2}} than smaller ones do, even at rest. But what happens when they''re in motion? Researchers {{3}} walkers of different ages and sizes, from a three-foot-tall kindergartner to a six-foot adult. While the subjects logged miles on the treadmill, the scientists {{4}} their stride and metabolism.\nAnd they found that people pretty much walk the same way, regardless of their stature. If you scaled a five-year-old up to be six-and-a-half feet tall, the giant child would lope along just like a similarly sized adult.\nWhat''s more, walkers of all heights use the same amount of energy per step. That means that big people don''t {{5}} energy by strolling in a more economical style. They expend less energy because—just as you may have always suspected —they simply need fewer strides to cover the same ground. Which means that for some people a walk in the park ain''t necessarily a walk in the park.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.toddlers, 2.mass, 3.recruited, 4.measured, 5.conserve', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c6f0481-4c85-5ab9-92e9-a8bf6bcd7489'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c6f0481-4c85-5ab9-92e9-a8bf6bcd7489'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Noisy Library', E'You have an assignment due next week. Now you are in the library, but someone next to you is playing a video without headphones. You are too distracted to focus on your study. You should have a conversation with him to make sure you have a quiet place. What would you say?', '70a7db05-c283-51c1-b914-af6491d2a432'::uuid, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
