  ('8c729bae-a8f8-5866-b75a-48b360872c0d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c729bae-a8f8-5866-b75a-48b360872c0d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '781343ac-0924-52fb-987c-98ae9ca32765'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The new rules will become effective in the next few days.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c7683f7-6ce2-5edd-b938-aae19257e0dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c7683f7-6ce2-5edd-b938-aae19257e0dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Property Right', E'A common way of permitting others to use an intellectual property right is to give express permission for it. This can be done in return for financial remuneration. In such cases, the holder of an intellectual property right is often referred to as granting a license to use what the holder otherwise has exclusive rights to, subject to certain conditions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8c76c6f7-ae57-59a8-add2-0d33b9401344'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c76c6f7-ae57-59a8-add2-0d33b9401344'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Quantum Foam', NULL, '32577b9f-902e-50ec-9cfb-932f71c3a6c2'::uuid, NULL, E'Quantum foam is an idea that emerges from the application of quantum physics to the fabric of space and time itself. You see Einstein taught us in general activity that space and time are not in an inert backdrop. They participate in an unfolding of the cosmos space and time can warp and curve that creates the force of gravity. When you recognize that space and time are dynamic, they can change that they''re real physical entities. Well, they must be subject to the laws of quantum physics. And the key element of quantum physics it''s relevant is the uncertainty principle. When applying to the space and time, it''s a space and time are uncertain which means they can wildly fluctuate. They can in a sense look like the violently boiling surface of a pot of water. When you examine space and time and fantastically small scales. So the idea is that if you examine space in small and small scales, not everyday scales, but tiny scales the uncertainty gets bigger and bigger and space and time became foam-like. They look bubbly. They look phonetic undulating. That''s quantum foam down of the ultra microscopic scale that we''ve been struggling to deal with for decades because the math Einstein doesn''t work down there. The math quantum mechanics and the math Einstein lock horns, we''ve been trying to resolve that conflict in the essence to understand what truly is going on with the quantum foam.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('8c76cf3e-1393-5293-ad25-8a1abec72cbd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c76cf3e-1393-5293-ad25-8a1abec72cbd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Do unions work for workers or management?', 'ca21c1de-2260-5a0a-9afa-7c962dcb6544'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Workers', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c7908f9-6a04-595a-8167-010693128634'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c7908f9-6a04-595a-8167-010693128634'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'English in Change', E'English has been changing throughout its lifetime and it''s still changing today. For most of us, these changes are fine as long as they''re well and truly in the past. Paradoxically, we can be {{1}} about word origins and the stories behind the {{2}} we find in our language, but we {{3}} a queasy distaste for any change that might be happening right under our noses. There are even language critics who are {{4}} that English is dying, or if not dying at least being progressively {{5}} through long years of mistreatment.\nFor example, many people in Australia worry about their language and its relationship with its powerful relative, American English. In particular, they express concern for the ''Americanisation'' of the language — it''s a hot topic here in Australia.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.curious, 2.structures, 3.experience, 4.convinced, 5.crippled', NULL, NULL),
  ('8c7af716-e853-52f0-83b5-2229258d52bd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '8c7af716-e853-52f0-83b5-2229258d52bd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Antecedents of Theater', E'In addition to exploring the possible antecedents of theater, scholars have also theorized about the motives that led people to develop theater. Why did theater develop, and why was it valued after it ceased to fulfill the function of ritual? Most answers fall back on the theories about the human mind and basic human needs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
