  ('90cfd746-32f6-531d-8870-ac1f2261a2af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90cfd746-32f6-531d-8870-ac1f2261a2af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'York', E'York was once a rich and populous city. Many houses {{1}} the narrow streets in the district, creating crowded living conditions. Records also show details about daily life, including {{2}} meals served every day. Religious festivals are {{3}} in St. Mary’s Church, which remain an important part of York’s traditions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.blocked, 2.the number of, 3.held', NULL, NULL),
  ('90dcd8ca-3cf1-59ed-a70a-7d5ed7a9cbbc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90dcd8ca-3cf1-59ed-a70a-7d5ed7a9cbbc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ancient Superhighway', E'Even after thousands of years exploring Earth, we''re still uncovering new things like an ancient ''superhighway'' in the Guatemalan rain forest. Hidden beneath a thick layer of vegetation, the {{1}} of roads stretches over 150 miles and was most likely built by the Mayan empire some 2,000 years ago. The newly mapped roads are connected to the ruins of El Mirador (sometimes called the Kan Kingdom) in northern Guatemala. Archaeologists believe El Mirador {{2}} around the 6th century BCE, and was at its most powerful around the early first century CE. At that time, it had a population of as many as a quarter of a million, a quarter the size of Rome itself at the time. It also has some of the largest pyramids in the world. It was the {{3}} of the Mayan civilization, and naturally needed some major roadways. The roads of El Mirador have been known about since 1967, but scientists had no idea how extensive they were until now. The thick jungle obscured the remnants of the road, {{4}} it difficult to see from the air.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.network, 2.was founded, 3.heart, 4.making', NULL, NULL),
  ('90de5966-bdc5-5ec1-862b-be1b8f76a8e1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90de5966-bdc5-5ec1-862b-be1b8f76a8e1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '168ed536-0252-50b1-9510-046b20c578e0'::uuid, NULL, E'To find the library, walk straight ahead, then turn left.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('90e24ade-bea2-56b4-b99d-a1254cb61b03'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90e24ade-bea2-56b4-b99d-a1254cb61b03'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sirhan', E'Sirhan, the {{1}} of US Senator Robert F. Kennedy, was granted {{2}} on Friday, after two of Kennedy‘s sons spoke in favor of Sirhan’s release, and lawyers {{3}} to argue that he should stay in jail. The decision was a major victory for the 77-year-old man, who spent 53 years in prison; however, it doesn’t {{4}} he is free. Douglas Kennedy, who was a toddler when his father was gunned down in 1968, said he was moved to tears by Sirhan‘s {{5}} , and he should be released if he‘s not a threat to others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.assassin, 2.parole, 3.declined, 4.guarantee, 5.remorse', NULL, NULL),
  ('90e6bb8b-9f4a-5ae2-83dd-02497796ad59'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90e6bb8b-9f4a-5ae2-83dd-02497796ad59'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biodiversity', E'We understand the importance of supporting and restoring biodiversity, and we are teaming up with the world’s leading molecular biologists, technologists, conservation biologists, conservation organizations, ethicists and thought leaders to call for ''Intended Consequences'' to help us safely use all of the available tools that can provide the advantage we need to turn the tide on species loss.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('90eaf288-0541-5e26-8f90-3e4feec82c03'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90eaf288-0541-5e26-8f90-3e4feec82c03'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Law Effect', E'Some people think human behavior can be changed by laws, while others think laws have little effect. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether human behaviour can be changed by laws has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that law acts as an effective guide, whereas opponents contend that legislation has limited impact. From my perspective, I am convinced that law can change human behaviour to some extent.\nTo begin with, various regulations restrict people’s behaviour in different aspects. For example, criminal laws prevent potential offenders from committing crimes and make them obey rules. In addition to this, traffic laws make drivers follow speed limits and wear seatbelts. Other than that, cyber laws make online social platforms prevent leaks and fraud, and protect privacy. It is thus shown that law is able to change people’s behaviour.\nBesides, I also believe that due to legal gaps and enforcement costs, laws fail to stop all violations. On top of that, despite penal codes, there are still many murders, armed robberies, and car thefts. Moreover, despite road safety rules, people still run red lights, jaywalk, and park illegally. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that despite digital governance, there are many cases of misinformation, identity theft, and online violence. This clearly proves that law has limitations to influence human behaviour.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that behavioral norms and public order are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that law can only change human behaviour in certain circumstances.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('90eeee1b-2f5e-58ad-bd1f-aab40c0fa8c1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90eeee1b-2f5e-58ad-bd1f-aab40c0fa8c1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0fa66048-86b0-58be-a020-87c719333343'::uuid, NULL, E'Visiting Blue National Park, seeing the spectacular wildlife there is essential.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('90f0f431-2897-5ff5-b0c3-161d4e4f12c1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90f0f431-2897-5ff5-b0c3-161d4e4f12c1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '424b4f55-3949-5fa7-a7e8-7a3c36147d78'::uuid, NULL, E'There is considerably less supervision at university.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('90f3e1aa-515a-54cf-ab03-4b02c362cb80'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90f3e1aa-515a-54cf-ab03-4b02c362cb80'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wind Turbine', NULL, 'b0e4f05e-5dd4-5f77-8739-9ddbcc032708'::uuid, NULL, E'Wind turbine is a device that will convert wind into mechanical movement, which we can use to power water pump or electricity generator. Now the power that the turbine creates is obviously depended on the wind speed, it also depended obviously on the number of sails, the area of the sails and the angle of the sails makes to the wind. So you can imagine if the turbine blades flat onto the wind, the wind''s going to just bend it, if there is slight angle when the wind hits it, it''s going to turn the blades. We can use that for powering things. Now, we''re going to have a go, making some of the very, very simple paper windmills, a sort of things that you can make from the bits and pieces lying around home, and use that to drive very small generator to power electronic devices.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('90f43a40-052b-56ec-9f6e-910f4bb455f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90f43a40-052b-56ec-9f6e-910f4bb455f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Birth of Coffee', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 1, 4, 5', NULL, NULL),
  ('90f46e07-5292-5117-abe6-daf56a52569d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90f46e07-5292-5117-abe6-daf56a52569d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hippocampus', E'If the hippocampus is damaged by disease or injury, it can influence a person''s memories as well as their ability to form new memories. Hippocampus damage can particularly affect spatial memory, or the ability to remember directions, locations, and orientations. Because the hippocampus plays such an important role in the formation of new memories, damage to this part of the brain can have a serious long-term impact on certain types of memory. Damage to the hippocampus has been observed upon post-mortem analysis of the brains of individuals with amnesia. Such damage is linked to problems with forming explicit memories such as names, dates, and events.\nThe exact impact of damage can vary depending on which hippocampus has been affected. Research on mice suggests that damage to the left hippocampus has an effect on the recall of verbal information while damage to the right hippocampus results in problems with visual information. There are a few different factors that can affect the function of the hippocampus.\nAge can also have a major impact on the functioning of the hippocampus. MRI scans of human brains have found that the human hippocampus shrinks by around 13% between the ages of 30 and 80. Those who experience such a loss may show significant declines in memory performance. Cell degeneration in the hippocampus has also been linked to the onset of Alzheimer’s disease.\nThe hippocampus may also play a role in contributing to the development of addictions. Because drugs and alcohol affect the brain''s reward systems, the hippocampus creates memories of these satisfying experiences. It also may help form memories of environmental cues associated with substance use that can contribute to intense cravings when these cues are encountered again.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('90f69b6f-50e1-5c37-8ebd-a76a05ebf255'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '90f69b6f-50e1-5c37-8ebd-a76a05ebf255'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '68ce1e04-c803-5634-a687-a5ac913af3de'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Children need to be educated on the danger of taking drugs.', NULL, NULL),
