  ('9163e4ed-e37d-5932-a361-e1b47d128f5c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9163e4ed-e37d-5932-a361-e1b47d128f5c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electronic Gifts', E'According to the Consumer Electronics Association, over two billion dollars was spent last year on {{2}} gifts for America''s six million high school graduates. Well, here''s some advice for anybody thinking of getting a {{3}} or other big ticket electronic gift for a high schooler about to set off for college in a few months—check the college for info or even {{4}} . So says John Campbell, associate vice president for information technology at Purdue. He points out that some colleges or even individual {{6}} may have certain system requirements that gift givers might want to be aware of. For example, some departments may suggest that students don''t use a Mac, while others may insist they do. Schools buy in bulk and may offer discounts on {{7}} , as well as printers, software, external hard drives, or even mp3 players. And university computers may be preloaded with software used on campus or configured to connect with specific campus networks. Consumer Electronic Association surveys found that a quarter of all high schoolers want a computer for graduation. The other three quarters presumably want a car and a computer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.electronic, 2.computer, 3.products, 4.departments, 5.computers', NULL, NULL),
  ('9170e4ed-ddd8-51c1-88dc-98207131d2e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9170e4ed-ddd8-51c1-88dc-98207131d2e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'What We Want', E'We want a recreation in adulthood of what it felt like to be administered to and indulged. In a secret part of our minds, we picture someone who will understand our needs, bring us what we want, to be immensely patient and sympathetic to us, act selflessly, and make it all better.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('9172a68d-f522-56fb-80ee-93cbaf2d3257'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9172a68d-f522-56fb-80ee-93cbaf2d3257'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '84ce281e-8816-5e6b-9fa4-c94860c3f71f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The guest speaker was previously a faculty member in our department.', NULL, NULL),
  ('917485cf-61c9-5b7c-a1bf-3351be038a0a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '917485cf-61c9-5b7c-a1bf-3351be038a0a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Weather Predictions', E'All kinds of predictions may be about to get even more difficult {{2}} climate change. Though no one is sure {{3}} what its effects will be, it seems that extreme weather conditions, {{4}} storms and hurricanes, are {{5}} become more common. Such events have far-reaching effects on distant weather systems, making general forecasting much harder.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.thanks to, 2.exactly, 3.such as, 4.likely to', NULL, NULL),
  ('917d1d55-1fa3-5082-a9dc-702095451756'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '917d1d55-1fa3-5082-a9dc-702095451756'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electorate', E'It would be reassuring to think that the {{1}} choose who to vote for based on the candidates'' track records and future policy promises. {{2}} , many of us are swayed simply by the way that politicians look. Consider a 2009 study that asked Swiss students to look at multiple pairs of unfamiliar French political candidates and in each case to select the one who looked most competent. Most of the time, the candidate selected by students as {{3}} the most competent was also the one who''d had real life electoral success, the implication {{4}} that voters too had been swayed by the candidates'' appearance (there’s little evidence that appearance and competence actually {{5}} ). Unsurprisingly, being attractive also helps win votes, especially in war time (in peacetime, looking trustworthy is more of an advantage). Other research has shown that we''re more likely to vote for male and female candidates with deeper voices.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.electorate, 2.In truth, 3.looking, 4.being, 5.correlate', NULL, NULL),
  ('917e3343-9ef4-52a6-a071-5fdd46cf694b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '917e3343-9ef4-52a6-a071-5fdd46cf694b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Avalanche', E'An avalanche is rapidly descending large mass of snow, ice, soil, rock, or mixtures of these materials, sliding or falling in response to the force of gravity. Avalanches, which are natural forms of erosion and often seasonal, are usually classified by their content such as a debris or snow avalanche.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
