  ('928e16f6-1038-5e27-964b-17b3da5f6f1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '928e16f6-1038-5e27-964b-17b3da5f6f1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Falkland Islands', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 1, 3, 5', NULL, NULL),
  ('928fa52a-da2e-501d-9eec-05c95f9d0750'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '928fa52a-da2e-501d-9eec-05c95f9d0750'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '48e40051-8786-5a3a-ab03-2d6f4cd5662e'::uuid, NULL, E'You should pre-select three to four courses that you are interested in taking.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('9296202a-a999-5bb0-ac2a-efa0b8464779'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9296202a-a999-5bb0-ac2a-efa0b8464779'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Making Australian Food History', E'In the past two centuries there has been a dramatic change in the role of food and eating in Australian public consciousness. Public discussion of food was largely confined to matters of supply, distribution and price. Towards the end of the nineteenth century some newspapers were offering regular columns of advice on housekeeping topics, including menu planning and recipes. However, eating remained essentially a private activity, even when undertaken in company.\nBy the late twentieth century, food and eating had become prominent public preoccupations. Evidence of this dramatic cultural revaluation abounds. In bookstores, for example, cookery and all things related to it are often among the larger displays. There are specialty stores selling all manner of cookware, tableware and other paraphernalia associated with food, eating and drinking.\nPerhaps most telling is the extension of the phenomenon of mass media celebrity to include culinary personalities. Scholars, too, have jumped on the commodification bandwagon. Now degrees in gastronomy seem set to emulate the MBA phenomenon of the 1980s and food has become a respectable subject for investigation with philosophers, sociologists, historians, cultural theorists, ecologists and many others all having a go at it.\nHowever, surprisingly, the question seems to have held little fascination for most historians. For the best part of two centuries they have managed to write their accounts of colonisation and nationhood with only scant reference to how the settlers and their descendants fed themselves.', NULL, NULL, E'In the past two centuries there has been a dramatic change in the role of food and eating in Australian public consciousness, and eating remained essentially a private activity, as by the late twentieth century, food and eating had become prominent public preoccupations; most telling is the extension of the phenomenon of mass media celebrity to include culinary personalities, but the question seems to have held little fascination for most historians.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('929eeb07-f198-5dd5-b3ee-575e24eccaea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '929eeb07-f198-5dd5-b3ee-575e24eccaea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Molecules', E'Normally, heat is what gets evaporation going, causing water molecules in the liquid to jostle more vigorously. That extra energy can break some of the bonds between molecules in the liquid, allowing molecules to escape as water vapor. Based on how much heat goes in, scientists can calculate the amount of evaporation expected.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('92ad18f6-406f-5418-9133-74a07a60eb79'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '92ad18f6-406f-5418-9133-74a07a60eb79'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Landlords', E'In Roman times, ordinary residents lived in the countryside, while landlords lived in villages. These landlords were well-defended and supplied food to the towns. They owned many farms, made {{1}} , and despite being relatively isolated, they managed to transport goods to different places. Cultivated fields were {{2}} in remote areas, and without proper {{3}} to roads and adequate {{4}} , it was hard to keep the region safe and stable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.profits, 2.limited, 3.access, 4.defenses', NULL, NULL),
  ('92b0c73b-f68f-5cb6-8a1d-cd4744052e23'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '92b0c73b-f68f-5cb6-8a1d-cd4744052e23'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Family Size', E'The world''s poorest countries tend to have the largest family sizes and fertility rates. When people have no economic security and cannot rely on their government, they often have children to ensure they will be looked after when they are older. Where child mortality is high, there is an even greater impetus to have more children.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('92b31c04-c0ac-550d-851b-06bab5f6fffa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '92b31c04-c0ac-550d-851b-06bab5f6fffa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '70481cb9-2548-5eee-a58e-a39a9f6bfb6e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Few students have received financial support from the local government.', NULL, NULL),
  ('92b50634-61ea-5dbf-a6fb-5b8eb72549b6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '92b50634-61ea-5dbf-a6fb-5b8eb72549b6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ibn Khaldun', E'Ibn Khaldun was a scholar from North Africa born in the 14th century. He is most renowned for his work "Muqaddimah," where he {{1}} out the foundations of several social sciences. Khaldun challenged how history was recorded, arguing that it should be based on societal trends and common patterns, not just stories of leaders and battles. He {{2}} concepts like "Asabiyyah," which is the social cohesion that keeps a society together, and discussed how economies and societies evolve over time. Khaldun''s ideas were {{3}} of their time, influencing not just the Islamic world but also later European thinkers. {{4}} the breadth of his work, Ibn Khaldun isn''t as widely known in the {{5}} historical narrative as some of his contemporaries or successors, mainly because his work was not widely translated, circulated, or appreciated by the dominant political and intellectual forces of his time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.laid, 2.introduced, 3.ahead, 4.Despite, 5.mainstream', NULL, NULL),
  ('92bef774-4399-58c6-9d2f-fe6452ce7297'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '92bef774-4399-58c6-9d2f-fe6452ce7297'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What color do you get when you mix black and white?', '6fdcf834-39bd-52f0-ba3e-1cc0dd6d3e46'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Gray / grey', NULL, NULL),
