  ('93c54029-bc46-55da-9e53-a0f669e73689'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93c54029-bc46-55da-9e53-a0f669e73689'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sales Training', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 4, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('93cc1181-f025-5988-96cf-d827dd60adf3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93cc1181-f025-5988-96cf-d827dd60adf3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Studying Climate Change', E'Imagine you have been assigned on the study of climate change. Which area of climate change will you focus on and why? Use examples.', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, the study of climate change has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that global warming should be emphasized because it leads to ecological imbalance, whereas opponents contend that ocean changes need to be studied due to species extinction risk. From my perspective, I am convinced that global warming should be focused on in the area of climate change.\nTo begin with, global warming is a real crisis that worsens human health conditions and causes resource shortages. For example, global warming causes extreme heat, threatening human lives, especially harming the elderly and outdoor workers. In addition to this, melting glaciers raise sea levels, flooding coastal cities and destroying human settlements. Other than that, extreme temperatures disrupt crop growth, reducing yields and threatening food security. It is thus shown that global warming should be prioritized in the field of climate change.\nBesides, I also believe that animals are more sensitive to temperature changes, which threatens their habitats and disrupts the food chain. On top of that, high heat causes bird nesting failures, reducing chick survival rates in extreme weather. Moreover, frequent forest fires destroy sloths'' homes, as their slow movement makes escape harder. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that droughts shrink grasslands, forcing hungry sheep to migrate to new habitats. This clearly proves that global warming requires focused attention in the domain of climate change.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that climate pattern disorder and biological survival crisis are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that the study of climate change should emphasize global warming as a critical area.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('93d2ee89-dde5-59ee-95cd-696aaa4c34d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93d2ee89-dde5-59ee-95cd-696aaa4c34d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Underground Houses', E'Underground houses have many advantages over conventional housing. Unlike conventional homes, they can be built on {{1}} surfaces and can maximize space in small areas by going below the surface.\nIn addition, the materials excavated in construction can be used in the building process. Underground houses have less surface area so fewer building materials are used, and {{2}} costs are lower. They are also wind, fire, and earthquake resistant, providing a secure and safe environment in extreme weather.\nOne of the greatest benefits of underground living is energy {{3}} . The earth''s subsurface temperature remains stable, so underground dwellings benefit from geothermal mass and heat exchange, staying cool in the summer and warm in the winter. This saves around 80% in energy costs. By {{4}} solar design this energy bill {{5}} to zero, providing hot water and heat to the home all year round.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.steep, 2.maintenance, 3.efficiency, 4.incorporating, 5.can be reduced', NULL, NULL),
