  ('93f1a2b3-52cc-58eb-8579-fe3c0710975d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93f1a2b3-52cc-58eb-8579-fe3c0710975d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bank Erosion', E'Riverbank erosion is an inevitable natural {{1}} of any floodplain region. Bank erosion involves the mechanism of {{2}} of bank materials from river banks by the fluvial actions like channel head pressure, velocity, discharge etc. The erosion takes place when the shear stress exceeds and the {{3}} support is collapsed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.phenomenon, 2.removal, 3.basal', NULL, NULL),
  ('93f44e45-e53e-5ab0-b783-a4d2f4863961'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93f44e45-e53e-5ab0-b783-a4d2f4863961'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dog and Human', E'Dogs, the first {{1}} animals, evolved from East Asian wolves approximately 20,000-40,000 years ago. Dogs understand human body languages, many spoken words, and even abstract symbols. Dogs pay attention to human faces and eyes, and they often {{2}} to humans to help solve problems. Dogs and humans form a {{3}} emotional bond that reduces stress in both species. Being {{4}} dogs improve human physical and mental well-being. Most dogs are very social and play with other dogs if they can. Stray and feral dogs are common on the edges of human society. They form social groups, and sometimes cooperate in territorial defense, much as wolves do.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.domestic, 2.turn, 3.mutual, 4.around', NULL, NULL),
  ('93fa7750-588f-552e-bfb5-d886c128c15e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '93fa7750-588f-552e-bfb5-d886c128c15e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Expectation', E'So I spent an hour trying on all these damn jeans, and I walked out of the store. Truth! With the best-fitting jeans I had ever had. I did better. All this choice made it possible for me to do better. But I felt worse. The reason I felt worse is that with all of these options available, my expectations about how good a pair of jeans should be went up. I had very low, I had no particular expectations when they only came in one flavor. When they came in 100 flavors, damn it, one of them should’ve been perfect. And what I got was good, but it wasn’t perfect. And so I compared what I got to what I expected, and what I got was disappointing in comparison to what I expected. Adding options to people’s lives can’t help but increase the expectations people have about how good those options will be. And what that’s going to produce is less satisfaction with results, even when they’re good results.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '40df6167-d37d-54b9-bb3a-cade75566e1b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'When people have more options, they will have a higher expectation, and tend to feel less satisfied with results, even when they’re good results.', NULL, NULL),
  ('9402564f-c007-578b-b041-39d15174405d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9402564f-c007-578b-b041-39d15174405d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1eee5901-9f7b-5a5c-ae46-d86693f1b0c7'::uuid, NULL, E'I''d like to find my own place as soon as possible.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
