  ('98b9337b-c7f3-526a-849d-f4e9cb46b975'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98b9337b-c7f3-526a-849d-f4e9cb46b975'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'bf5a7e01-3d7a-563d-be45-8b7f610de98a'::uuid, NULL, E'The course will be tested at the end of the semester.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('98b9a632-32a3-5c84-a491-057da812101b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98b9a632-32a3-5c84-a491-057da812101b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-R', E'Most investigators concur that certain facial expressions suggest the same emotions in all people. Moreover, people in diverse cultures recognize the emotions manifested by the facial expressions. In classic research Paul Ekman took photographs of people exhibiting the emotions of anger, disgust, fear, happiness, and sadness. He then asked people around the world to indicate what emotions were being depicted in them. Those queried ranged from European college students to members of the Fore, a tribe that dwells in the New Guinea highlands. All groups, including the Fore, who had almost no contact with Western culture, agreed on the portrayed emotions. The Fore also displayed familiar facial expressions when asked how they would respond if they were the characters in stories that called for basic emotional responses. Ekman and his colleagues more recently obtained similar results in a study of ten cultures in which participants were permitted to report that multiple emotions were shown by facial expressions. The participants generally agreed on which two emotions were being shown and which emotion was more intense.\n\nAccording to the paragraph, which of the following was true of the Fore people of New Guinea?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'They knew very little about Western culture.\nThey show similarities in their expression of emotions with Europeans.', NULL, NULL),
  ('98c0da00-ff8e-597d-8466-22319c8d6293'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98c0da00-ff8e-597d-8466-22319c8d6293'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Materials', E'Online materials like music, movies and other forms of content are accessible at no cost. Do you think online materials should be accessed at no cost?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('98c1e448-ea4d-5094-9cd4-6111d5d9c4fe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98c1e448-ea4d-5094-9cd4-6111d5d9c4fe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '53344d85-48d2-5881-a550-1fbe93319873'::uuid, NULL, E'If little action is taken, we could experience energy shortages.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('98cca898-c2f1-5406-9877-149dd5e5d92a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98cca898-c2f1-5406-9877-149dd5e5d92a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Financial Crisis', E'New research shows that during the global financial crisis, workers who stayed in jobs did not reduce their working hours, despite the claims that cuts in hours have led to job losses. A study found that the life of people who stayed with the same employer remained relatively unchanged.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('98cf7b9d-e285-56a3-97a9-c2581448ff9b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '98cf7b9d-e285-56a3-97a9-c2581448ff9b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bats Estimate', E'Historically what has been used to estimate bats has been photographic estimates, visual estimates, mark-recapture estimates, and those have been highly prone to bias. "Newer technology, like thermal imaging cameras is accurate, but expensive. So at a time of epic bat mortality - due to, for example, the fungal white-nose syndrome that''s wiping out bats in Canada and the U.S"', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
