  ('9c07b62c-06f0-5393-ad8b-80d476c6d5af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c07b62c-06f0-5393-ad8b-80d476c6d5af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e249e8ae-c55e-5963-911c-89dab0aef0a2'::uuid, NULL, E'Government policies, though tough, have been a blessing in disguise.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('9c0dab2c-16d9-5191-8e65-9b95e1461093'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c0dab2c-16d9-5191-8e65-9b95e1461093'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '00dbc5dd-214b-5514-84fe-063a1167ed36'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The university offers a wide range of courses according to your commitments.', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c0fa0ab-8ced-5071-b040-9d591c90d531'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c0fa0ab-8ced-5071-b040-9d591c90d531'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Noises', E'Noises are defined as disagreeable sounds, but this suggests that they are no more than an annoyance, something to be put up with. There is increasing evidence that noise, on the scale that people who live in big cities have to deal with, is dangerous and can give rise to serious health and social problems. Some of which, such as its effects on people''s behavior and anger levels, you might not have thought were caused by noise, and are health concerns. There is, of course, the almost constant noise of traffic, though this isn''t a particularly modern problem. In ancient Rome, there were rules to minimize the noise made by the iron wheels of wagons, which battered the stones on the pavement, causing disruption of sleep. Traffic noise is one of the health hazards, as it can lead to other problems, like noise-induced hearing impairment. It is also highly distracting, interfering with speech communication and leisure time relaxation, and while this doesn''t drive you mad in the medical sense, it is intensely annoying and can lead to mental health problems. Also, noise, whether you work in a place where loud machinery is operating or not, can have an effect on performance at work; though in itself not a health matter, this can lead to other problems.\n\nWhich of the following are mentioned as health problems caused by noise?', 'cda38e85-438c-5646-8147-076180449be0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A certain degree of hearing loss\nMental problems\nBehavioral and anger problems', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c0fbf8a-360a-54d5-9af1-9036405aff67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c0fbf8a-360a-54d5-9af1-9036405aff67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Elizabeth Holmes', E'Elizabeth Holmes is the CEO of Theranos, a blood-testing startup {{1}} in Palo Alto. Elizabeth''s entrepreneurial journey began when she {{2}} out of college in her sophomore year to start her own company, focusing on simplifying blood tests for consumers. Her vision is to revolutionize diagnostic health testing {{3}} innovative technology.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.based, 2.dropped, 3.through', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c1214a0-8d3a-5513-b167-5058b31aa170'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c1214a0-8d3a-5513-b167-5058b31aa170'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bird Food', E'If you''ve ever been to an all-you-can-eat buffet, you know how {{1}} it is to {{2}} weigh your options. You don''t want to fill up on salad when so many {{3}} delights await. It seems some birds also weigh their mealtime choices—literally. A study finds that Mexican Jays pick up and shake peanuts to assess their relative heft before choosing one. That report is served up in the Journal of Ornithology.\nFoods that hide their edible bits on the inside present a challenge to hungry diners. How can you tell which fruits are ripe or which shells harbor the biggest nuts? We humans knock on melons or squeeze avocados. But how do other species select the highest quality snacks?\nTo find out how the jays do it, researchers fiddled with their feed. First they doctored peanuts so that some contained three nuts while others had none. When they offered these pods to some jays, the birds turned their beaks up at the empty shells and instead chose those that were full. And when the jays were allowed to choose between normal peanuts and those that weighed just one gram more, because the researchers had stuffed them with clay, the birds again went for the heavier meal.\nVideos {{4}} that the jays shake the nuts before {{5}} one, which apparently lets them gauge the nut''s mass and perhaps also listen for the rattle of a well-packed shell. Pretty clever for a bird brain.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.important, 2.carefully, 3.calorie-laden, 4.revealed, 5.selecting', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c13d4f5-dc1c-58e9-904f-aba3945fc7ad'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c13d4f5-dc1c-58e9-904f-aba3945fc7ad'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the source of solar energy?', 'b17e09a3-b2a2-5585-a225-5916ccdec766'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sun', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c1eee44-08d2-544b-8da0-b8a7d8bad7f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c1eee44-08d2-544b-8da0-b8a7d8bad7f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the drops of liquid that forms on your skin when you are hot?', '27fa54ad-ce71-5d74-9b7d-24dccd5355d9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sweat / perspiration', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c214289-72e4-53ce-83bd-ac46b8f0a74e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c214289-72e4-53ce-83bd-ac46b8f0a74e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Self-rescue', E'Paper mills had the worst of it for years as newspapers reduced pagination, went wholly digital or shut for good. The papers were able to hammer down the cost of newsprint from firms fighting for business as demand declined. Price-taking paper mills suffered in silence. Many hesitated to shut massive machines costing hundreds of millions of dollars. That hesitance has disappeared; mills are taking out newsprint capacity and diversifying. Norske Skog, a Norwegian pulp and paper firm, said in June it would close its 66-year-old Tasman Mill in New Zealand, for example. Many mills are converting machines to make packaging for e-commerce. UPM, a Finnish firm, announced this year the sale of its Shotton newsprint mill in Wales to a Turkish maker of containerboard and packaging. For JCS Volga, a Russian mill, newsprint used to account for 70% of production; now half of what it makes is packaging.\n\nAccording to the speaker, which of the options below are right?', '84e69e9f-4841-5c8c-a44d-d5f4229c3256'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Paper mills are now reducing the newsprint production.\nMany paper mills have started to use machines to make packaging.', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c228e26-cdd4-5534-ae13-d09afbc7141f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c228e26-cdd4-5534-ae13-d09afbc7141f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Free Health Services', E'Some countries have free health services. However, some people claim that those who live unhealthy lives should not receive free health services. Do you agree or disagree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('9c25c0bd-198b-577a-aa67-d513cc3c0071'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c25c0bd-198b-577a-aa67-d513cc3c0071'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coins(跨越千年的硬币)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 2, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c2dd632-79cc-5fd5-b4cd-4846b6a7b0e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c2dd632-79cc-5fd5-b4cd-4846b6a7b0e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electric Vehicles', E'Electric vehicles have arrived. With technology led by Tesla, and all of the world''s major car manufacturers following along behind, electric vehicles are now a common sight on the roads of most developed countries. Yet the situation in less developed countries is rather different; the only African country to have started the change to electric vehicles is South Africa.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('9c2f1436-9823-5a5c-9387-557073fcb144'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c2f1436-9823-5a5c-9387-557073fcb144'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What global conflict was fought from 1914 to 1918?', '182e0c69-b221-5db3-82b4-0de72e236e0e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'World War One', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c2fc231-07ee-506c-b08f-4bf0d900172c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c2fc231-07ee-506c-b08f-4bf0d900172c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the hair that grows above your eyes?', 'b346de88-f9c0-55b0-a7e9-613fa5627848'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Eyebrow', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c2fcd9f-69d9-555d-a94d-7115bf9cbf15'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c2fcd9f-69d9-555d-a94d-7115bf9cbf15'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sharkbite', E'Sharks killed four people and bit 58 others around the world in 2006, a comparatively dull year for dangerous encounters between the two species, scientists said in their annual shark attack census on Tuesday. Sharkbite numbers {{1}} steadily over the last century as humans reproduced exponentially and {{2}} more time at the seashore. But the numbers have been {{3}} over the past five years as overfishing {{4}} the shark population near shore and swimmers got smarter about the risks of wading into certain areas, Burgess said.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.grew, 2.spent, 3.stabilized, 4.thinned', NULL, NULL),
  ('9c307902-95a2-5279-a64b-061aa0be14b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9c307902-95a2-5279-a64b-061aa0be14b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pay Scheme', E'If bonus or “incentive pay” schemes work so well for senior executives and bankers, why does everyone not get them? After all, many jobs involve making important decisions or taking risks. Is there anything about corporate decisions and financial risks that makes these categories of work special in terms of how they need to be incentivised and rewarded?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
