  ('9ea2bcd2-e86a-54b8-a09d-46e3455120c2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9ea2bcd2-e86a-54b8-a09d-46e3455120c2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Smartphones', E'Thanks to their ability to {{1}} our most primal desires for connection, distraction and validation, smartphones have become some of the bestselling devices of all time. Apple have sold more than a billion iPhones since its launch in 2007. By one estimate, we spend an average of almost five hours a day {{2}} at their little screens. The real figure is probably higher: a team of British psychologists found that people tend to underestimate the time spent on their phones by about half, whole hours just {{3}} in the fog.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.hijack, 2.staring, 3.evaporating', NULL, NULL),
