  ('9fabaca5-0b11-5976-9e10-0960ac829c1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9fabaca5-0b11-5976-9e10-0960ac829c1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Who prepares and sells medicine in shops or hospitals?', '4a1e33df-e02e-5884-8e20-9b7ba12aa9c1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Chemist / pharmacist', NULL, NULL),
  ('9facd43f-8378-5942-bea6-adc64caa44ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9facd43f-8378-5942-bea6-adc64caa44ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Eat Out', E'Some people prefer to eat at food stands or restaurants. Other people prefer to prepare and eat food at home. Which do you prefer? Explain it with your own experience.', NULL, NULL, E'Eating is an essential part of our daily lives, and how we choose to eat can impact our health, social life, and finances. In this essay, I will argue that preparing and eating food at home is the best option for me, based on my experience.\nCooking at home allows me to have more control over what I eat. When I prepare meals at home, I can choose the ingredients and cooking methods that best suit my dietary needs and preferences. This control over my food choices has helped me maintain a healthy and balanced diet.\nPreparing meals at home is also a fun and rewarding experience. I enjoy experimenting with new recipes and techniques, and the sense of accomplishment I feel after cooking a delicious meal is unmatched. Cooking at home has also allowed me to connect with my family and friends over food, creating cherished memories and bonding experiences.\nIn conclusion, cooking and eating at home is the best option for me. It allows me to have more control over what I eat, maintain a healthy diet, and enjoy the fun and rewarding experience of cooking. While some may argue that eating out provides a social experience and access to a wide variety of cuisines, the benefits of cooking at home far outweigh these potential advantages. Let us all strive to cook more at home and enjoy the many benefits it has to offer.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('9fb081dd-abb3-5b53-b164-42318d71cdc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', '9fb081dd-abb3-5b53-b164-42318d71cdc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bubbles', E'Let''s raise a toast to {{1}} . And its {{2}} bubbles. Because new {{3}} says the bubbles aren''t just tickling your tongue. They''re erupting with aromas vital to the taste of the beverage.\nA team of (who else) French researchers used mass spectrometry to nose around a glass of champagne. They found that concentrations of certain {{4}} compounds were higher at the surface of the glass than in the liquid itself. They report the finding in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.\nThe {{5}} say the sea shares champagne''s secret. If you''ve ever enjoyed ocean air, it''s because compounds called {{6}} are dragged along with bubbles in the waves. When those bubbles burst, the surfactants break into smaller molecules called aerosols that are suspended in the breeze, giving coastal areas their distinctive oceany odor. In essence, a glass of champagne hosts a small version of this process, but the bubbles bring more appetizing aerosols to the surface.\nLegend has it that Dom Perignon shouted "I''m tasting the stars" when he uncorked his first bottle of champagne. But it was physics and chemistry, not astronomy, that he was really {{7}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.champagne, 2.ubiquitous, 3.research, 4.molecular, 5.scientists, 6.surfactants, 7.savoring', NULL, NULL),
