  ('a05233cd-21d2-594f-b174-631ac655618b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a05233cd-21d2-594f-b174-631ac655618b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Families', E'Families provide emotional, physical and financial care and support to their members and are often the basis on which government assistance is determined and administered. Australians have {{1}} experienced three main living arrangements over a lifecycle: living with parents, living with a partner (for some of this period with children) and living alone in old age if that partner died. Now and into the future, living arrangements {{2}} a lifecycle may also include living alone or in a group household before perhaps forming a long-term partnership, or living as a {{3}} parent or alone after divorce or separation. These changes in living arrangements and family {{4}} are the outcome of various demographic and social trends, such as declining fertility, increased rates of divorce and longer life {{5}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.traditionally, 2.throughout, 3.lone, 4.characteristics, 5.expectancy', NULL, NULL),
  ('a057d2d7-3704-58d8-afc4-b5cedac08c5d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a057d2d7-3704-58d8-afc4-b5cedac08c5d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0d7904f9-2b07-56e7-8a7a-0c181768b460'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Active listening is vital for success in this particular course.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0614c06-c4d6-51ae-8323-f797ebc97291'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0614c06-c4d6-51ae-8323-f797ebc97291'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gombe National Park', E'The audio, which includes more than 1,000 separate data files, was captured in the early 1970s by the late Hetty van de Rijt. She recorded the various screams, barks, and how calls made by a group of chimps, including 17 youngsters, living in the Gombe National Park in Tanzania.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a061ade7-3966-549f-853a-7963c760c718'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a061ade7-3966-549f-853a-7963c760c718'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b50d9846-0ffe-5ccb-b6bd-6a6ac2fb7378'::uuid, NULL, E'Your tutor is there to help, so do ask if you don''t understand anything.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a0621b55-2b6c-57f9-9d34-b45561c1ae3b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0621b55-2b6c-57f9-9d34-b45561c1ae3b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '03d0e5a4-126e-553c-ab56-67cdf14b875c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Many undergraduate students choose to study sociology in France.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a06e220b-31a2-5ad6-81fe-438ff2c2c570'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a06e220b-31a2-5ad6-81fe-438ff2c2c570'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vanishing Teller Jobs', E'Technological advances are eliminating the need for bank tellers, threatening an entry point for women into the male-dominated industry which has sought to promote more females to leadership roles. While the climb remains steep, some financial companies have managed to improve the gender balance in their executive ranks. As teller jobs dwindle, there’s a risk that banks will raise the educational requirements for those jobs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a0732b2c-8585-5427-9355-15ce9d373be0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0732b2c-8585-5427-9355-15ce9d373be0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Perseverance Rover', E'NASA''s Perseverance rover touched down on the red planet, {{1}} a new era of Mars exploration. After sticking its landing, Perseverance {{2}} a small helicopter that completed the first {{3}} flight on another world. After an {{4}} failed attempt, the rover drilled and stored its first of many planned samples of Martian rock, which future space missions will {{5}} so scientists can analyze them for signs of past life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.kicking off, 2.deployed, 3.powered, 4.initial, 5.retrieve', NULL, NULL),
  ('a07be300-30ae-5f33-b88f-a8811731d3d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a07be300-30ae-5f33-b88f-a8811731d3d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Brand Loyalty', E'Brand loyalty exists when consumers repeat-purchase your brand rather than swapping and switching between brands. It is widely agreed that it is far more expensive to have to find a new customer than to keep existing ones happy, so brand loyalty is crucial for achieving high-profit margins. For charities, it is important to set a marketing objective of improving brand loyalty. If existing donors can be persuaded to set up a direct debit to the charity, its cash flow will improve significantly. Although some brands stay fresh for generations (Marmite is over 100 years old) others become jaded due to changes in consumer tastes and lifestyles. At this point, the firms need to refresh the brand image to keep the products relevant to the target market. A clear objective must be set. For instance: what brand attributes do we want to create? What do we want the brand to stand for? This occurs when a firm aims to change a brand’s image, so that the brand appeals to a new target market. Twelve years into its life cycle, McVitie''s decided to reposition its Hobnobs biscuit brand. Hobnobs had been positioned as a homely, quite healthy biscuit for middle-aged consumers. Research pointed McVitie''s in a new direction: younger, more male, and less dull. So new packaging was designed and then launched in conjunction with a new, brighter advertising campaign. In 2013 Hobnobs sales were worth 36 million pounds, 9 percent up on the previous year.', NULL, NULL, E'Brand loyalty exists when consumers repeat-purchase your brand rather than swapping and switching between brands, which is crucial for achieving high-profit margins; although some brands stay fresh for generations, others become jaded due to changes in consumer tastes and lifestyles, so the firms need to refresh the brand image to keep the products relevant to the target market, and a clear objective must be set.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a0865cf9-3680-54aa-980a-2df85b69cfb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0865cf9-3680-54aa-980a-2df85b69cfb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the line between a sunset and the sea?', 'b4e66274-767c-52e8-819d-91292d5ecf4b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sea-sky-line / horizon', NULL, NULL),
  ('a087f410-03a2-57ab-bc5b-47d353dd9634'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a087f410-03a2-57ab-bc5b-47d353dd9634'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cactus', E'You may have heard that you can get water from a cactus if you are ever lost and {{1}} in a desert. Does it sound like a nice survival tip to store away, but is it really that easy? It turns out that a cactus is not actually a spine-covered basin of fresh water. Such a plant would not last long in an {{2}} habitat filled with thirsty animals. Water is truly a precious resource in a desert, so, in addition to their {{3}} spines, most cactus species further protect their spongy flesh with acids and potent alkaloids. These chemicals are usually too acrid for most humans to tolerate and are {{4}} on the kidneys if ingested. The flesh of some cactus species can also cause vomiting, diarrhea, or temporary paralysis — none of which is {{5}} to your survival in an emergency situation. Cactus fruits are a better bet, though many are also unpalatable if eaten raw.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dehydrated, 2.arid, 3.intimidating, 4.taxing, 5.conducive', NULL, NULL),
  ('a08d35bf-11db-54c4-8031-ac766c0996cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a08d35bf-11db-54c4-8031-ac766c0996cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term used for raised tall geographical structures that usually have cooler climate?', 'c562af1a-23d3-5979-a026-af333fd33960'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mountains / hills', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0935793-bee9-5adf-9383-059357ad480b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0935793-bee9-5adf-9383-059357ad480b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'AI Use', E'Similar to how chatbots may sometimes generate false information or fabricate responses, machine learning models developed for scientific purposes can also produce misleading or inaccurate results. However, researchers have recently introduced a novel statistical method that enables the safe utilization of AI predictions to evaluate scientific hypotheses.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a0950f7b-b331-5120-a61d-783a827b8821'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0950f7b-b331-5120-a61d-783a827b8821'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are wine glasses and spectacles made of?', '5d6a4d6d-81b8-524f-bc07-e6d53def5021'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Glass', NULL, NULL),
  ('a095d080-2122-5602-9b18-5c83ae419c6c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a095d080-2122-5602-9b18-5c83ae419c6c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Leading Business Schools', E'In an attempt to {{1}} new students, leading business schools - including Harvard, Stanford, the University of Chicago and Wharton - have moved away from the unofficial admissions {{2}} of four years'' work experience and {{3}} have set their sights on recent college graduates and so-called early career {{4}} with only a couple years of work under their belt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.lure, 2.prerequisite, 3.instead, 4.professionals', NULL, NULL),
  ('a09e0baf-db99-504e-87b8-3e2fb88fa53d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a09e0baf-db99-504e-87b8-3e2fb88fa53d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Kava', E'If you''ve come across kava in the dietary supplement section of your favorite health food store, or stumbled across a kava bar in your hometown, you''re probably curious what the hype''s all about. Or perhaps you are familiar with this legal, all-natural high. Either way, you may benefit from a little background on the substance and some risks you should know about.\nKava — also referred to as Tonga and countless other names. This scientific name actually translates to "intoxicating pepper." Kava is a tall-growing perennial shrub native to the Pacific islands, including Hawaii. The term "kava" also refers to the psychoactive beverage made from the roots.\nKava, the beverage, is a folk medicine that''s been used for centuries by South Pacific islanders for social and ceremonial uses. Indigenous people of the Pacific islands offer kava as a sign of respect and a means of strengthening social and familial ties, particularly among men. It''s also used to assist in the communication with spirits and for medical purposes. Pacific islanders have placed certain restrictions on the use of kava that limit who can drink it and when it can be consumed, which helps promote the safe and controlled use.\nThe traditional preparation involves chewing or grinding the root until it produces a cloudy, milky pulp, and then soaking it in water to steep. The water is then strained out and served in a half coconut shell, then swallowed down in one gulp. The flavor is described as "earthy" or "like muddy water" — hardly appetizing terms. But people don''t drink it for the taste.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a0a93dd9-bd5d-55b1-8276-6db0dd0f60fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0a93dd9-bd5d-55b1-8276-6db0dd0f60fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How many legs do quadruped animals have?', 'd374b08f-0c99-5e8e-9901-b34d089d1777'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Four', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0add698-c79e-5722-bc27-314495dad54b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0add698-c79e-5722-bc27-314495dad54b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b5444d93-8d7e-5aea-84f3-3bd64cc7b021'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tutors will arrange to meet all new students next week.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0b1e391-9fa5-5e71-bd3c-f4c91ed2313e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0b1e391-9fa5-5e71-bd3c-f4c91ed2313e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'AI', E'There are alien minds among us. Not the little green men of science fiction, but the alien minds that power the facial recognition in your smartphone, determine your creditworthiness and write poetry and computer code. These alien minds are artificial intelligence systems, the ghost in the machine that you encounter daily.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a0b4bc11-242c-55aa-88bc-26531417c5da'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0b4bc11-242c-55aa-88bc-26531417c5da'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3e4bc580-d009-5b5f-ae72-624c3bd5d2f9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The way we see different countries is changing because of the internet.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0b5feab-7762-54ad-b036-ec3ee5f5990d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0b5feab-7762-54ad-b036-ec3ee5f5990d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the study of rock layers and layering?', '3da3edc3-683c-53a8-af2c-0665e7ab3f95'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Stratigraphy', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0bdcdaf-3b39-5b15-8af1-bdf88eadd60a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0bdcdaf-3b39-5b15-8af1-bdf88eadd60a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hibernation', E'Hibernation is a way for many creatures - from butterflies to bats - to survive cold, dark winters without having to forage for food or migrate to somewhere warmer. {{1}} , they turn down their metabolisms to save energy. Animals in hot climates also {{2}} a form of hibernation called aestivation. This works in a similar way and enables them to survive extreme heat, drought or lack of food.\nHibernating is much more {{3}} than simply sleeping, though. Depending on the species, it can vary from long, deep unconsciousness to light spells of inactivity. But hibernation carries risks as the dormant animal is {{4}} to predators and the unpredictable climate.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Instead, 2.undergo, 3.profound, 4.vulnerable', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0c06c74-59d5-5b30-830c-62d61b63af83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0c06c74-59d5-5b30-830c-62d61b63af83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-R', E'The impact of a meteorite released an enormous amount of energy, excavating a crater about twice as large as the lunar crater Tycho. The explosion lifted about 100 trillion tons of dust into the atmosphere, as can be determined by measuring the thickness of the sediment layer formed when this dust settled to the surface. Such a quantity of material would have blocked the sunlight completely from reaching the surface, plunging Earth into a period of cold and darkness that lasted at least several months. The explosion is also calculated to have produced vast quantities of nitric acid and melted rock that sprayed out over much of Earth, starting widespread fires that must have consumed most terrestrial forests and grassland. Presumably, those environmental disasters could have been responsible for the mass extinction, including the death of the dinosaurs.\n\nAccording to the paragraph, which of the following statements are true of the impact at the end of the Cretaceous period:', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'A large amount of dust blocked sunlight from Earth.\nEarth became cold and dark for several months.\nLarge quantities of nitric acid were produced.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0c06dd2-4476-5d02-9d0a-e43621907d77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0c06dd2-4476-5d02-9d0a-e43621907d77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ice Tongue', E'Ice tongue is a glacial formation created by an ice stream flowing faster than the surrounding {{1}} . As the glacier moves toward the sea or a body of water, it extends outward, forming a large, finger-like projection of ice. This happens when the glacier''s flow rate {{2}} the surrounding ice, causing the ice to break off and form an "ice tongue". Over time, sections of the ice tongue may {{3}} , creating icebergs and further shaping its structure. One well-known example is the Erebus Ice Tongue, located on the {{4}} of Antarctica near Mount Erebus. This ice tongue extends from the Ross Ice Shelf and is influenced by both the flow of the glacier and the nearby volcanic activity of Mount Erebus. The Erebus Ice Tongue is a significant feature in glaciology because it highlights the interaction between glacial dynamics and geothermal heat from the volcano. The formation and stability of ice tongues like Erebus are important for understanding sea-level {{5}} , as changes in the ice tongue''s size or structure can affect the flow of ice into the ocean. Studying these features helps scientists predict how Antarctica''s glaciers will respond to climate change and their potential contribution to rising sea levels.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.ice, 2.exceeds, 3.calve, 4.coast, 5.rise', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0c462d8-2087-5f6e-9d38-d56097cc2527'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0c462d8-2087-5f6e-9d38-d56097cc2527'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9dc8de2a-3004-53f7-98de-504c757da9bd'::uuid, NULL, E'I have a sandwich and milk for my breakfast.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a0c671c1-57ec-5a9c-8d96-b2f636f34323'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0c671c1-57ec-5a9c-8d96-b2f636f34323'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a student who works for a period of time at a job to get experience?', '45a13699-ac72-577b-9609-677c38dd84ce'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Intern / apprentice', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0cae800-4b57-5583-ad12-aced245a99b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0cae800-4b57-5583-ad12-aced245a99b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Extinct Animals', E'To understand what extinct animals such as dinosaurs eight, we can compare their tooth types to the range of tooth types that we see with modern animals, such as carnivorous and herbivorous animals. So when we look at a tiger skull, we can look at aspects of its dentition or its teeth to understand what it ate. So when we see pointed and sharp teeth, we can see that they are very well adapted for slicing, shearing, and cutting flesh. Unlike the tiger, when we look at a herbivorous animal, a horse, we can see that it''s teeth are arranged in a nice, flat, grinding surface. And so when the top and lower teeth fit together, they actually grind up plant material. When we look at fossils like this one, which belongs to an alice, or we can see teeth that are conical and re curve backwards with sharp points answer eighty dead jizz. But these kinds of clues tell us that this animal was a meat eating animal. Now we''ll look at the jaw of a hadrosaur on one side. You can see many of its teeth. When we turn it around, you can see a long, flat, grinding surface. By comparison, we can infer that this animal was also a plant eater, just like the horse that showed us a very similar kind of dentition. This animal also ate plants and other tough fibrous material.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '062abbfc-4d6d-557b-9905-ed19dc2c7003'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We can tell what kind of food an extinct animal such as a dinosaur ate by examining its teeth and jaw and comparing them with present-day animals. Sharp, serrated teeth imply that it was a carnivore, whereas flat surfaces for grinding tough fibres suggest a herbivorous diet.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a0ce2335-2397-50aa-8c38-d264a0ea525f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a0ce2335-2397-50aa-8c38-d264a0ea525f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'cbc638cd-7231-531b-99ae-84f1a9aaf1f1'::uuid, NULL, E'All students and staff have access to printers and scanners.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
