  ('a1a8f2e2-cf43-5e1b-b2a9-8d88a2205285'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1a8f2e2-cf43-5e1b-b2a9-8d88a2205285'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e011a7fb-6335-5da6-8c96-d7ae87830061'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A regional assembly was moved to the devolution of power.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1b96afa-12af-5992-a2e4-7fbcdb32a0e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1b96afa-12af-5992-a2e4-7fbcdb32a0e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Edison and Tesla', E'Tesla came over from Graz and went to work for Thomas Edison. Nonetheless Edison offered him a job, promising Tesla fifty thousand dollars if Tesla could redesign Edisons breakdown-prone DC generator designs. The new generator designs were a vast improvement over Edisons originals. Upon completing the job Tesla went to Edison to collect the $50,000 promised for the task. "Tesla", Edison replied, "you don''t understand our American humour." And Tesla was never paid. These two men became arch-rivals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1bf27fc-ea7d-5fc5-8781-f605a37f1c72'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1bf27fc-ea7d-5fc5-8781-f605a37f1c72'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Railway', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'5, 2, 4, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1c1914e-7545-5f68-8163-cc0f5bef08db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1c1914e-7545-5f68-8163-cc0f5bef08db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Unhealthy Food', NULL, '393c8aba-8db7-599b-a378-288a76328278'::uuid, NULL, E'Small changes can add up to big shifts in the environment. We know this from decades of research on addictive substances. I understand we really would all like to believe that we’re in charge, that we have complete freedom over what we eat. But how free can we be? Living in a saturated environment, one that continuously surrounds us with food products carefully engineered to get us hooked and keep us coming back for more. Those kids in the Tenderloin, they apparently live in what’s called a food desert. They don’t even have access to a grocery store, really. What’s a grocery store when it’s stuffed with junk food 74% of it loaded with added sugar? All the health experts will tell you, shop around the perimeter of this grocery store that way you can steer your way around all the junk that’s in the middle. But how different is that from a strategy that steers children around drug dealers in the Tenderloin. We can do so much better than this. We don’t have to live in an environment that is ready to get us fat, and then blames us for the health consequences in the medical bills. We don’t have to sit by and watch our children suffer from diseases of adulthood. We can rerigged this environment to make it safe. It’s not about personal choice anymore. It’s about our public choice.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1cc773d-abd4-508a-bbac-7e2cf2b1f7ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1cc773d-abd4-508a-bbac-7e2cf2b1f7ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fence', E'A typical fence with a few wires allows most animals – such as lions or wild dogs — to go over, under or through it. For larger mammals, such as elephants and giraffes, we will create large fence-gaps that consist of a sloping, loose rock wall. Because of rhinos’ short, stubby legs, they are unable to scale these rock piles.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1cdece1-a41c-59fc-a215-020654432326'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1cdece1-a41c-59fc-a215-020654432326'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for materials that allow some light to pass through them but not all?', 'be0b4fb1-1f49-5a03-b916-dae95dd9b034'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Translucent', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1d012da-30f7-5fd5-9fe7-13c710f6528a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1d012da-30f7-5fd5-9fe7-13c710f6528a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Facing Issues', E'The world''s governments and international organizations confront a multitude of global problems. Which do you think is the most pressing problem for the inhabitants of our planet and give the solution?', NULL, NULL, E'The world''s governments and organizations confront a multitude of global problems. Climate change has emerged as one of the most pressing problems facing our planet today. Its far-reaching consequences have the potential to disrupt ecosystems, endanger species, and impact the lives of billions of people. However, there are solutions that can help mitigate and address this global issue.\nOne of the key solutions to combat climate change is the transition to renewable energy sources. Fossil fuels, such as coal and oil, are major contributors to greenhouse gas emissions. By investing in renewable energy technologies like solar, wind, and hydroelectric power, we can significantly reduce our reliance on fossil fuels and decrease carbon emissions. This transition not only helps combat climate change but also creates new job opportunities in the clean energy sector.\nAnother crucial solution is adopting sustainable practices in various sectors. Industries, agriculture, and transportation are major contributors to greenhouse gas emissions. By implementing sustainable practices like energy-efficient technologies, responsible land management, and promoting public transportation, we can reduce our carbon footprint. Additionally, promoting sustainable agriculture practices and reducing food waste can also play a significant role in mitigating climate change.\nIn conclusion, climate change poses a significant threat to our planet, but there are viable solutions available. Transitioning to renewable energy sources and adopting sustainable practices across various sectors are key steps in addressing this global issue. It is crucial for governments, industries, and individuals to work together to implement these solutions and prioritize the well-being of our planet. By taking action now, we can pave the way for a more sustainable and resilient future for generations to come.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a1d0c1b9-4dbb-505b-9cce-bd03b44bcc33'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1d0c1b9-4dbb-505b-9cce-bd03b44bcc33'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '37669ed7-8833-530f-9a78-e18d79d88bac'::uuid, NULL, E'There is too much information on this topic.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1d76e70-7f75-531b-bd58-6d5c33ce1fdf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1d76e70-7f75-531b-bd58-6d5c33ce1fdf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '72c63ccd-b871-57f0-a3c0-6348ef578171'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There will be a prize for the most innovative design.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1db5fe4-b3e8-5390-b673-ca63a439b26e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1db5fe4-b3e8-5390-b673-ca63a439b26e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '93e5086f-73ea-5191-9331-ac4abc0e4b78'::uuid, NULL, E'The woman said she could help me get a replacement travel pass.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1dcee26-f2b9-5013-9c90-73301b54940f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1dcee26-f2b9-5013-9c90-73301b54940f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6138b27b-503b-5073-b0ab-ef869cd81513'::uuid, NULL, E'The full list of undergraduate and postgraduate programs can be found on the website.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1dd411c-37bb-5144-9b73-9b26d93af60e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1dd411c-37bb-5144-9b73-9b26d93af60e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Seminars', E'Seminars are not designed to be mini-lectures. Their educational {{1}} is to provide an opportunity for you to discuss interesting and difficult aspects of the course. This is founded on the {{2}} that it is only by actively trying to use the knowledge that you have acquired from lectures and texts that you can achieve an adequate understanding of the subject. If you do not understand a point, it is highly {{3}} that you will be the only person in the group in that position; you will invariably be undertaking a {{4}} for the entire group, if you come to the seminar equipped with questions on matters which you feel you did not fully understand. The seminar is to introduce and {{5}} discussion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.role, 2.assumption, 3.unlikely, 4.service, 5.provoke', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1e0b2a0-6f6b-5c4b-95a9-17cb85ff7583'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1e0b2a0-6f6b-5c4b-95a9-17cb85ff7583'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is at the top of an eyebrow?', '9b8cfabf-559b-5bdd-94ba-0e5a5bb4d3d9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Forehead', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1e26d66-87f2-542d-998c-e8fcaa1e2113'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1e26d66-87f2-542d-998c-e8fcaa1e2113'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'New Library', E'Hey, Jeff, have you been to the new library yet? Oh, hi, Jane. Yes, I went last week to check it out. I really like it. Yes, I like it too. I like the study areas. There seemed to be a lot of room to just spread out and focus on the books. It''s way better than the old library where it seemed like we were all jammed into one area. Sometimes it was even hard to find a spot to study because it was so crowded, especially during exams. I even like the chairs at the new place. They''re super comfy. You''re right. The only bad thing about it is that it''s pretty far away. It takes me about twenty minutes to get there by bus. So I can see myself not going all the way downtown. If I''m in a pinch for time. I''d probably just stay in residence and study there. I was thinking that too. It''s too bad. It takes so long to get there. I don''t like being dependent on the buses. Have you tried riding your bike there? It might take a little longer, but at least you''re getting a bit of exercise. That''s a good idea. Jen. Maybe I''ll try writing this week. I just have to make sure i''m good and rested. Sometimes when I''m over tired. I''m not to coordinated knowing me i''d have a load of books on my backpack and get distracted by something and crashed my bike. Well, you''ve just got to keep an eye out for those potholes. Oh, wow, look at the time i''ve got to get to my next class. I''ll see you around. Jeff, good talking to you. Jen, I''ll be seeing you.\n\nWhich of the following are mentioned about the new library?', 'b239d0cb-0298-51ee-94d3-a433af8b5141'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'It isn''t very near the university.\nIt has comfortable chairs.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1e452e4-f9c1-5780-a0b0-7ae45b2d1642'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1e452e4-f9c1-5780-a0b0-7ae45b2d1642'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you use to call or text a friend?', '23b308f4-7cd0-5a7c-a7c1-92757e4b737a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cell phone / mobile phone', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1e58dc2-4b03-5c52-96e7-f4135a43644b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1e58dc2-4b03-5c52-96e7-f4135a43644b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'dcb75279-1b2f-5a3b-bee5-d57edb19f931'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This year has witnessed the retirement of several senior professors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1eac58e-0df7-5281-9d41-61d169a18d83'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1eac58e-0df7-5281-9d41-61d169a18d83'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the opposite of destiny?', '45978a63-d44a-5493-a325-e869bd3d6fc0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Free will', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1ec5b03-b526-520c-911e-b9133a190564'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1ec5b03-b526-520c-911e-b9133a190564'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dennett', E'Dennett recognizes that all human minds are shaped not only by natural selection but by enormous cultural influences which effectively redesign our minds. He invites us to think of the conscious mind as consisting of those mental contents that win in competition against other mental contents in the battle for control of behavior. What we are is the “organization of all the competitive activity between a host of competences” that our bodies have developed. Consciousness is defined by what a mind can do – whether it can concentrate, be distracted, recall earlier events, keep track of a number of things at once etc.. Dennett urges us to resist the temptation to imagine animals as accompanying their clever activities with streams of reflective consciousness as we would. We may not know that they do not, but we certainly cannot assume that they do. He notes that the more we learn about clever activities in animals and how they are accomplished, the less the processes in their brains seem to resemble the thoughts we imagined were doing the work.\n\nAccording to Dennett, the mind displays which of the following characteristics?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Our minds are shaped by natural selection.\nOur conscious mind tries to control our behaviors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1ecd826-65d7-5aaa-91cd-a1b6e201972b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1ecd826-65d7-5aaa-91cd-a1b6e201972b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the opposite to “predecessor”?', '107cf72a-fe48-520d-ab63-1e0342b414ff'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Successor', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1efe49d-e8ae-5bd9-908e-490f63e70755'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1efe49d-e8ae-5bd9-908e-490f63e70755'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Liquidity', E'When people worry about a glut of liquidity, they are thinking of the first of these concepts. If money is too abundant or too cheap, inflationary {{1}} may build up or bubbles may appear in financial markets -- until central banks tighten policy or market opinion suddenly changes. A slackening of {{2}} activity or a drop in asset prices can leave households, businesses and financial institutions in trouble if their balance sheets are not liquid enough (the second concept) or if they cannot find a buyer for {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.pressures, 2.economic, 3.assets', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1f7470f-6b75-59a5-9bbf-1eca8c508974'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1f7470f-6b75-59a5-9bbf-1eca8c508974'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the curve of a road or a river?', 'ee3de711-5770-58e6-862f-be84f93ab1b0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bend', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1f8b83f-96b5-5ab8-8b10-df9812aad5bf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1f8b83f-96b5-5ab8-8b10-df9812aad5bf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd188474b-a271-5eb0-a263-d5c8de4bca58'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The factory has achieved a steady growth in output.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1f923e7-6976-597d-ab61-540d3ed0b8fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1f923e7-6976-597d-ab61-540d3ed0b8fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bones', E'Bones also protect the organs in our bodies. The skull protects the brain and forms the shape of the face. The spinal cord, a pathway for messages between the brain and the body, is protected by the backbone, or spinal column. The ribs form a cage that shelters {{1}} heart and lungs, and the pelvis helps protect the bladder, part of the intestines, and in women, the reproductive organs. Bones are made up of a framework of a protein called collagen, with a mineral called calcium phosphate that makes the framework hard and strong. Bones store calcium and release some into the bloodstream when it''s needed by other parts of the body. The amounts of certain vitamins and minerals that you eat, especially vitamin D and calcium, directly affect how much calcium is stored in the bones. Joints are where {{2}} bones meet. They make the skeleton flexible — without them, movement would be impossible. Joints allow our bodies to move in many ways. Some joints open and close like a hinge (such as knees and elbows), whereas others allow for more complicated movement — a shoulder or hip joint, for example, allows for backward, forward, sideways, and rotating movement. Joints are classified by their range of movement: Immovable, or fibrous, joints don''t move. The dome of the skull, for example, is made of bony plates, which move slightly during birth and then fuse together as the skull finishes growing. Between the edges of these plates are links, or joints, of fibrous tissue. Fibrous joints also hold the teeth in the jawbone. Partially movable, or cartilaginous, joints move a little. They are linked by cartilage, as in the spine. Each of the vertebrae in the spine moves in relation to the one above and below it, and together these movements give the spine its flexibility. Freely movable, or synovial (pronounced: sih-NO-vee-ul), joints move in many directions. The {{3}} joints of the body — such as those found at the hip, shoulders, elbows, knees, wrists, and ankles — are freely movable. They are filled with synovial fluid, which acts as a lubricant to help the joints move easily. {{4}} kinds of freely movable joints play a big part in voluntary movement: Hinge joints allow movement in one direction, as seen in the knees and elbows. Pivot joints allow a rotating or twisting motion, like that of the head moving from side to side. Ball-and-socket joints allow the greatest freedom {{5}} movement. The hips and shoulders have this type of joint, in which the round end of a long bone fits into the hollow of another bone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.the, 2.two, 3.main, 4.Three, 5.of', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1fed813-f545-5982-8f2f-40cd681443bf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1fed813-f545-5982-8f2f-40cd681443bf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the organs in our chest that we use to breathe?', '9f56e0a9-2419-52ae-983a-ed122429bb64'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Lungs / lung', NULL, NULL),
  ('a1fee04b-7b6d-58b3-b2e6-f712d1d35c31'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a1fee04b-7b6d-58b3-b2e6-f712d1d35c31'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '95b7103d-9ecb-59bd-ac93-c9fb9420ba22'::uuid, NULL, E'All sorts of knives will be banned from boarding a plane.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a201bc6a-ebf2-5b68-bd76-73ef44ecd3bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a201bc6a-ebf2-5b68-bd76-73ef44ecd3bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f946b5d4-1e2b-5538-bb56-3389b68a2eee'::uuid, NULL, E'It is generally accepted that people are motivated by success.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2032324-d14d-5e5c-a76f-924986478ef9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2032324-d14d-5e5c-a76f-924986478ef9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd12f2779-594f-5899-8f69-e1897d593473'::uuid, NULL, E'Taking a pre-bedtime shower can enhance the quality of sleep.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2074593-d24a-57d9-bf40-a774d08ccd45'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2074593-d24a-57d9-bf40-a774d08ccd45'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7c2aafe2-c3ee-508c-9f79-e1d055a6cb11'::uuid, NULL, E'The Prime Minister is understood to have been extremely angry about the report.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a20a054a-c80f-5683-a4b8-eebc24978ba1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a20a054a-c80f-5683-a4b8-eebc24978ba1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Congo Basin', E'Protecting the tropical forests of the Congo Basin conserves these forests and their resources on which the local and {{1}} people of the region {{2}} . The Congo Basin is home to the second largest tropical rainforest on Earth, which {{3}} as the green heart of Africa.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.indigenous, 2.depend, 3.serves', NULL, NULL),
  ('a20b1ba1-8288-5208-9c35-11e49bfa2c49'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a20b1ba1-8288-5208-9c35-11e49bfa2c49'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we describe something that can be processed and used again?', 'edac9540-9881-5cdb-b668-f6966c164b61'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Recyclable', NULL, NULL),
  ('a21763ea-0011-54ac-a95e-ba9b0de9bbf2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a21763ea-0011-54ac-a95e-ba9b0de9bbf2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Natural Selection', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2182718-be6f-5d44-bbc4-6aa9525fffb5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2182718-be6f-5d44-bbc4-6aa9525fffb5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marshmallow Test', NULL, '38af283c-da3e-5925-bd1b-f22e9448a9d1'::uuid, NULL, E'Let''s take a look at this video of these little kids. They were offered the option of having one marshmallow immediately or two marshmallows 15 minutes later and you''ve got some very cute video tape of this experiment. So let''s take a look. What we found is a very simple and direct way of measuring a competence that seems to make an important life difference. A researcher tells these preschoolers that she''s going to leave the room. If they wait for her to come back without eating the marshmallows, they''ll get two marshmallows. Or, they can ring the bell and she''ll come back right away but then they only get one marshmallow. I would ring the bell. You won''t ring the bell? Okay. Looking at children over time, Dr.Michelle has found that being able to wait longer at four has some pretty powerful implications. And what are those powerful implications? Is that later in life they''re more disciplined and have more self-control? Is that pretty much it. Well, they are more likely to achieve their life goals. They have better relationships. They do better on their SAT. Is that crazy all because they waited 15 minutes for two marshmallows? Well, I mean I think it is crazy. I probably would have eaten all three. Yeah, me too. But, um, you know, actually, yes, the ability to be able to pursue your goals, in this case, was that two marshmallows versus one, and not going automatic and just grab the marshmallow, is a very important skill. But I think a main point in mind in the making is that these skills can be caught, taught. If you''re 14 or 40 or four it''s not ever too late, and any child can learn, any adult can teach them. And it''s never too late.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2183a60-bf38-5b6b-a2cb-91313245c5fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2183a60-bf38-5b6b-a2cb-91313245c5fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Space Debris', E'Space debris or space junk is basically discarded material from launch vehicles like rockets or parts of spacecraft that are left to {{1}} around in space. Since this junk material floats around space, it can often come in contact with satellites or space stations {{2}} collision. Space debris can also come from explosions in space or through missile tests to destroy satellites. Since space debris floats in low Earth orbit and at speeds of around 15,700 miles per hour, this makes it highly possible for satellites or a spacecraft to {{3}} with the materials. According to the US Department of Defense’s global Space Surveillance Network, more than 15,000 pieces of space debris larger than 4 inches have been tracked. It is also estimated that there are around 200,000 pieces {{4}} between 0.4 and 4 inches, and millions of pieces smaller than 1cm.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.roam, 2.risking, 3.collide, 4.sized', NULL, NULL),
  ('a21a1955-6af3-50d2-b091-538b3f73725e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a21a1955-6af3-50d2-b091-538b3f73725e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '738aec78-cefd-551d-9e1f-6c8f610a4a4f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Organic food is considered to be free of chemicals.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a21aeda1-d8b6-5710-b7c1-53b566836f1a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a21aeda1-d8b6-5710-b7c1-53b566836f1a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the metric unit of length that equals to 1000 meters?', 'ad614328-f89d-5452-9fac-99df1577b207'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Kilometer', NULL, NULL),
  ('a21e2acb-c779-52f1-af05-edb60e1c8dd6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a21e2acb-c779-52f1-af05-edb60e1c8dd6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Health Worker', NULL, '8eb2740a-2d78-56b4-bf2f-2d7500bdcdba'::uuid, NULL, E'According to the World Health Organization, 400 million people worldwide have no access to essential health care. That’s a staggering number of people. Some of those services include things like basic sanitation and clean water, prenatal care, and vaccinations or immunizations for children. Many things contribute to this crisis. Sometimes people live to remotely to get timely care if emergency occurs. Even when living in a city, the patient to doctor ratio can be as high as 50,000 people to just one doctor, making it impossible for that doctor to meet the demands of health care in that area. These are valuable people made in the image of God who are physically suffering. Many of them go without a personal relationship with Christ. So we do this with a week of hands-on training, consisting of a variety of topics like basic sanitation and hygiene, taking vital signs, wound care and infection prevention, basic birth assisting and emergency skills. Those who participate in the training then have practical skills in supplies to care for others in their community in a way that glorifies God and opens the door for sharing the gospel in a new way.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a222abb4-d218-5c70-84a3-08cce4c44978'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a222abb4-d218-5c70-84a3-08cce4c44978'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7b72297d-0bda-599d-83ee-e118db365491'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The weather used to be lovely for this time of year.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a224904d-e633-5a2c-857b-ada6e30076f0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a224904d-e633-5a2c-857b-ada6e30076f0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sandra Lousada', E'London''s National Portrait Gallery is currently celebrating the fifty-year career of photographer Sandra Lousada. The twenty one portraits on display depict key figures in literature, film and fashion from the early 1960s. Subsequent to the acquisition of forty portraits by Lousada, the display at The National Portrait Gallery highlights shots taken between 1960 and 1964, many of which feature in Lousada''s book Public Faces Private Places.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a22892d7-1fcc-570b-a619-667048442579'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a22892d7-1fcc-570b-a619-667048442579'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mammals', E'Mammals can be one of the hardest-hit groups by habitat loss, and a lot of research has been carried out to find the best ways to conserve mammal diversity.\nMuch of this research has focused on very large-scale changes in land use and the impacts this will have on overall mammal diversity. However, many important decisions about land use are made at much more local scales, for example at the level of individual landowners.\nNow, in a detailed study led by Imperial College London that looked at mammal diversity across different small-scale landscapes in Borneo, researchers have identified previously logged forests as an overlooked source of refuge for mammals.\nThese ''selectively logged'' forests, where only certain tree species are removed, are often considered to be degraded and are frequently cleared to make way for plantations. The new results, published in the journal Ecological Applications, suggest they should be better protected.\nThe team recorded mammals using trap-and-release techniques and motion-sensing cameras over three years, creating an unprecedented 20,000 records of species in three land-use types: old-growth forest, logged forest and oil palm plantation.\nThis is one of the most intensive studies of rainforest mammal diversity ever undertaken.\nTo their surprise, they found that mammal diversity for large mammals, like the clouded leopard and civets, was similar for both old-growth forests and logged forests. For small mammals, such as squirrels and rodents, the diversity was actually higher in logged forests.', NULL, NULL, E'Mammals can be one of the hardest-hit groups by habitat loss, with a lot of research carried out to find the best ways to conserve mammal diversity, much of which has focused on large-scale changes in land use and the impacts on mammal diversity, and researchers have identified previously logged forests as an overlooked source of refuge for mammals, which should be better protected.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a22b0e1d-7358-5db5-b303-8db1f30b42fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a22b0e1d-7358-5db5-b303-8db1f30b42fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Law and Order', E'The narrative of law and order is located fundamentally at the level of individual {{1}} and responsibility. Criminal acts are seen as individual issues of personal responsibility and culpability, to which the state responds by way of policing, prosecution, {{2}} and punishment.\nThis is but one level at which crime and criminal {{3}} can be analyzed. The problem is that so often analysis ends there, at the level of individual action, characterized in terms of responsibility, guilt, evil.\nIn few other areas of social life does individualism have this hold? To take but one instance, it would be {{4}} to restrict analysis of obesity, to individual greed. It should similarly be widely seen as absurd to restrict analysis of criminal justice issues to the culpability of individuals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.guilt, 2.adjudication, 3.justice, 4.absurd', NULL, NULL),
  ('a22bac39-41da-506c-a997-497ce432c424'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a22bac39-41da-506c-a997-497ce432c424'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the meat from the leg of a pig that is cured and often eaten sliced thin?', 'ace796bc-1d5b-5c56-9287-5025627ccdd8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ham', NULL, NULL),
  ('a22c828c-e119-572a-826a-f4e50a5f9b42'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a22c828c-e119-572a-826a-f4e50a5f9b42'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '39572d5d-d2ca-5850-b84c-c8bde07f4ec7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Heavy drinking can cause permanent damage to the brain.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2314b69-c7d5-5427-9038-6ed26fc0780a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2314b69-c7d5-5427-9038-6ed26fc0780a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Foreign Cultures', E'With the development of globalization, the cultural communication between countries is becoming more and more frequent. Are you for or against foreign cultures? Support your ideas with your own experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a231578f-e047-567d-9c66-1ef8e2428eef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a231578f-e047-567d-9c66-1ef8e2428eef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'AVG', E'Currently, there is concern about the increasing amount of time children spend in sedentary activities, the number of children who fail to achieve {{1}} daily physical activity guidelines (i.e. 60 min of moderate-to-vigorous intensity activities every day), and the apparent increase in obesity prevalence as a result of such sedentary {{2}} . Screen-based activities, including television viewing and playing computer games are among the most frequently observed sedentary activities that children partake with children spending 2.5–4 h per day participating in such activities. The introduction of “active video games” (AVGs) into the gaming market presents an opportunity to convert traditional, sedentary screen-time into active screen-time and thus increase total daily energy expenditure (EE). Modern AVGs utilize cameras and motion sensors to allow the gamer to physically perform a variety of actions, {{3}} on the console, such as swinging a tennis racquet or running. The most demanding AVGs provided similar responses to walking and, based on international standards, should be classified as low-intensity activities. Whilst AVGs may provide children with a better alternative to sedentary gaming, they are not a sufficient {{4}} for normal physical activity, e.g. sports and outdoor play.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.minimum, 2.behaviors, 3.dependent, 4.replacement', NULL, NULL),
  ('a238a8bc-1018-58b1-830d-d8a029f0c83c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a238a8bc-1018-58b1-830d-d8a029f0c83c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Monkeypox', E'Countries that are members of the United Nations are obligated to report cases of unusual diseases that have the potential to become global health threats. In May 2022, more than a dozen countries in Europe, the Americas and other regions of the world that had never before had cases of monkeypox started to report cases occurring within their borders.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a23a011b-c67a-5f9f-9da3-1be2a21996d4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a23a011b-c67a-5f9f-9da3-1be2a21996d4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '497aff8c-0e6e-5361-8ddb-7417269198bc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The government has presented these changes as a major reform.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a23bee30-f044-5172-b380-4fb1c818d515'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a23bee30-f044-5172-b380-4fb1c818d515'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marks', E'Marks encourage students to learn. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'The role of marks in encouraging students to learn is a topic of much debate. While some argue that marks can create unnecessary stress and competition, I believe that marks are an important motivator for students to learn and improve their academic performance. This essay will argue that marks provide a measure of progress and achievement, allow for targeted support, and promote a culture of excellence.\nMarks provide a measure of progress and achievement, allowing students to track their growth over time. When students receive feedback in the form of marks, they can see how well they are doing in a particular subject or assignment. This can motivate them to work harder and strive for higher marks in the future. Additionally, marks can provide a sense of accomplishment and pride when students achieve high scores.\nMarks allow for targeted support and intervention. When teachers and parents see that a student is struggling in a particular subject or assignment, they can provide targeted support to help the student improve. This may involve extra tutoring, additional resources, or modifications to the learning environment. Marks can also help identify areas of strength and weakness, allowing for more individualized instruction.\nIn conclusion, I believe that marks encourage students to learn and improve their academic performance. Marks provide a measure of progress and achievement, allowing students to track their growth over time. They also allow for targeted support and intervention when students are struggling. Finally, marks promote a culture of excellence by encouraging students to work hard and strive for higher scores. While there may be some downsides to the use of marks, I believe that the benefits outweigh the drawbacks.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a23de754-1e47-55e2-8113-c0deb4c9b95c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a23de754-1e47-55e2-8113-c0deb4c9b95c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '76914094-fb52-50b0-bf33-63bf08eedd4e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The elephant is the largest animal living on land.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a24878ce-892c-5ee2-868b-67a3a193df4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a24878ce-892c-5ee2-868b-67a3a193df4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9687e3d6-10ca-5377-b91a-e6d239b06d0a'::uuid, NULL, E'The health center is situated at the corner of the university behind the library.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a248aafa-7f0f-510c-a7e8-d57b6639e934'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a248aafa-7f0f-510c-a7e8-d57b6639e934'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Diplomacy', E'For diplomacy the starting point must be that globalization requires bridges and removes barriers. A policy of containment is a difficult strategy in the age of the fibre-optic cable, the jumbo jet and the satellite dish. There will always be the exception, such as the murderous regime in Iraq where the only safe strategy is to keep it in the isolation ward until it accepts the norms of international behavior, or the military dictatorship in Burma which has persistently failed to respond to dialogue. It takes two to critically engage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a248e102-3b3a-51ea-8e0f-947f39cc6d55'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a248e102-3b3a-51ea-8e0f-947f39cc6d55'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '30105e39-8689-5cd6-bd88-87fc6766ebd9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Only some people are allowed to join this group.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a24b6c58-5246-5f26-bc4a-0a91523339df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a24b6c58-5246-5f26-bc4a-0a91523339df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language Learning', NULL, 'f5ace292-e7f7-55b4-87c4-9dcfb3db1f41'::uuid, NULL, E'It is wrong, however, to exaggerate the similarity between language and other cognitive skills, because language stands apart in several ways. For one thing, the use of language is universal-all normally developing children learn to speak at least one language, and many learn more than one. By contrast, not everyone becomes proficient at complex mathematical reasoning, few people learn to paint well, and many people cannot carry a tune. Because everyone is capable of learning to speak and understand language, it may seem to be simple. But just the opposite is true-language is one of the most complex of all human cognitive abilities.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a24e3741-abbb-59dc-a824-6a54d34dafb8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a24e3741-abbb-59dc-a824-6a54d34dafb8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5baca785-0f0d-5005-aa08-848fd7765797'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'An innovative scheme has been proposed by the students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a250edf0-3acf-5492-9702-db0b76e6e7c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a250edf0-3acf-5492-9702-db0b76e6e7c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e0575840-a4f8-5faa-8505-512c828e9c74'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Registration for the conference is now open for interested students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a25216f3-a32b-53bb-8113-30bb48738ced'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a25216f3-a32b-53bb-8113-30bb48738ced'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skoog', NULL, '4ce88df5-9a72-5cc3-b7ec-e130baa00017'::uuid, NULL, E'The Skoog is a new university accessible musical instrument. It is designed to use by children or adults with special needs or in fact be used by anyone. It’s soft, it’s easy to play, it’s robust and it can be customized to suit anyone’s abilities. The Skoog helps students with special needs by allowing them to get involved in making music themselves. It’s an instrument that they can play it and they can take ownership of and start creating their own sounds and music. Traditional instruments are the shape and size and made of the materials they are because of the sound that they need to make. If you want to make a sound like a plucked string, you need a string and it needs to be under tension, whereas with a Skoog, because it’s a mixture of software and a sensor, then thus the computer can handle making the sound. And so we can design an object that’s designed to be touched and designed to be played with. In developing the screen and working with kids in the schools and in the classrooms, it’s really helped us make the Skoog something that’s usable by the children themselves. They’ve informed us massively on how it needs to work and they’ve given their opinions on colors and designs. And just the feedback they’ve given to us has been just marvelous. It’s just so enriching and it’s really inspiring to actually work with these kids, particularly when you can provide them with an ability to start to playing their own music as opposed to just taking part through listening and listening to other musicians and really learning from.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a25531b1-bf5f-5e52-9fca-62a1ee38ffd9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a25531b1-bf5f-5e52-9fca-62a1ee38ffd9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7e1c06f9-7e88-5411-99e2-6aa44f9f4304'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Generally, young children worldwide derive enjoyment from listening to stories.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2581344-5fb8-5e1c-b0e1-278cf6599211'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2581344-5fb8-5e1c-b0e1-278cf6599211'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e0ea12f7-13a7-5d8b-a89a-c32a0b9a18d1'::uuid, NULL, E'The older equipment has been put at the back of the building.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a258fac1-c35e-5aff-a981-7209ee30f454'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a258fac1-c35e-5aff-a981-7209ee30f454'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bhutan', E'Bhutan is the last standing Buddhist Kingdom in the World and, until recently, has {{1}} much of their culture since the 17th century by avoiding globalization and staying isolated from the world. Internet, television, and western dress were {{2}} from the country up until ten years ago. But over the past ten years globalization has begun to change in Bhutan, but things remain {{3}} balanced.\nBhutan is the only country in the world that has a ''GNH.'' You may think GNH is just another {{4}} based term with no real-life application, but it refers to "Gross National Happiness." The process of measuring GNH began when Bhutan opened to globalization. It measures people''s quality of life, and makes sure that "material and spiritual development happen together." Bhutan has done an amazing Job of finding this balance. Bhutan has continually been (ranked) as the happiest country in all of Asia, and the eighth Happiest Country in the world according to Business Week. In 2007 Bhutan had the second fastest growing GDP in the world, at the same time as {{5}} their environment and cultural identity.\nBhutan is the only Buddhist Kingdom in the world; Mahayana Buddhism is the official religion of Bhutan. Over two thirds of the people are Buddhist, and Buddhism is supported by the government both politically and economically. The government gives {{6}} to Buddhist monasteries, shrines, monks and other Buddhist programs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.preserved, 2.banned, 3.perfectly, 4.statistically, 5.maintaining, 6.subsidies', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2599b75-6e19-5550-92cd-adc2379a5385'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2599b75-6e19-5550-92cd-adc2379a5385'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '76a6551f-3274-5153-99eb-405a4207e2bd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You must answer security questions when you reset your password.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a25c53bf-75b6-5418-a10c-e5692afa0ef8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a25c53bf-75b6-5418-a10c-e5692afa0ef8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '439dc33d-717a-5f86-a836-64a2c5da9b3a'::uuid, NULL, E'Extra seminars are scheduled to assist in your study preparation efforts.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a25dde98-d677-5daa-ae2c-c873ecc209f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a25dde98-d677-5daa-ae2c-c873ecc209f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Brain Research', E'Scientists have worked for many years to unravel the complex workings of the brain. Their research efforts have greatly improved our understanding of brain function. During the past decade alone, scientific and technical progress in all fields of brain research has been astonishing. Using new imaging techniques, scientists can visualize the human brain in action. Images produced by these techniques have defined brain regions responsible for attention, memory, and emotion. A series of discoveries (in multiple fields of study) has displaced the long-standing assumption that brain cells are stable and unchanging. Amazingly, new findings show that some adult brain cells can divide and grow! In addition, advances in research are allowing scientists to analyze and make progress toward understanding the causes of inherited brain disorders such as Alzheimer''s disease and Parkinson''s disease. Taken together, these discoveries provide hope for the recovery of nervous system function lost through injury or disease.Despite these and other significant advances in the field of brain research, most of the processes responsible for the integrated functioning of billions of brain cells remain a mystery. Research on the brain in the new millennium is crucial to our effort to come to a complete understanding of this fascinating organ. In turn, improved understanding makes the development of new treatment options possible. Research continues to bring new insights into how the brain is put together, how it works, and whether damage to the brain can be reversed.', NULL, NULL, E'Scientists have significantly improved our understanding of brain function with astonishing scientific and technical progress in all fields of brain research, which provides opportunities for the recovery of lost nervous system function, but most processes responsible for the integrated functioning of billions of brain cells remain a mystery, and research continues to bring new insights.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a25e37f8-1813-519e-bdac-506d69b66cb1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a25e37f8-1813-519e-bdac-506d69b66cb1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Foreign Plant', E'Although it hails from a remote region of the western Himalayas, this plant now looks entirely at home on the banks of English rivers. Brought to the UK in 1839, it quickly escaped from Victorian gardens and colonized river banks and damp woodlands. Now it is spreading across Europe, New Zealand, Canada and the US.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2688fa3-4021-5d59-bfff-897116d599e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2688fa3-4021-5d59-bfff-897116d599e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4534f08d-ac23-5558-9250-81f9169f0459'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Before choosing your university courses, you should consider your future career.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a268bfb7-32ab-57c5-a1e8-f95aa33ed9df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a268bfb7-32ab-57c5-a1e8-f95aa33ed9df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Eutrophication', E'Eutrophication is a process when bodies of water {{1}} to a high nutrient level due to extensive fertilizer in the soil. The water becomes overly enriched with minerals and nutrients which induce excessive {{2}} of algae and other aquatic species which may {{3}} minerals in the water, and thus endanger other species.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.accumulate, 2.blooms, 3.deplete', NULL, NULL),
  ('a26c91ec-cc21-5b4d-a20d-a3d0778ecd3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a26c91ec-cc21-5b4d-a20d-a3d0778ecd3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Crab', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 4, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('a270c65d-9d02-50c3-8da9-91e7e383713f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a270c65d-9d02-50c3-8da9-91e7e383713f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a word or a group of words with a particular meaning such as ''the other day''?', '8b177907-2d16-5795-8dd2-cdc4024948d8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Expression / phrase', NULL, NULL),
  ('a27128a9-01d5-5500-9385-0ae9bbd4a519'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a27128a9-01d5-5500-9385-0ae9bbd4a519'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b36bda13-39ba-54a0-bff0-9ec91e9514cd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The economic books are at the back on the left.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2827218-8290-597b-9cb5-3546eaeaed9d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2827218-8290-597b-9cb5-3546eaeaed9d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Childhood Disadvantage', E'Disadvantage in early childhood poses multiple risks to children''s development. Factors such as low socioeconomic status, long-term unemployment of parents, and social isolation may have lasting {{1}} on a child''s chance of reaching their full potential. Whilst not eliminating disadvantage, preschool education can help to {{2}} the effects of these risk factors and can provide children with a better start to school. However, some of these factors may also be {{3}} to preschool attendance for groups that would benefit most from preschool education. In Australia, the early years of children''s education is the responsibility of many government and non-government agencies and it occurs in a range of settings. Preschool is aimed at children around four years of age to {{4}} them for compulsory schooling from the age of six years. In most states and territories, children can start full-time schooling at five years of age, when they enrol in a kindergarten or preparatory year. In 2001, just over half of five-year olds (57%) were at school with about a third (34%) attending preschool. While in some states and territories children can {{5}} preschool before they turn four, participation rates for three-year olds are much lower than four-year olds (24% compared with 56% for four-year olds in 2001). The preschool participation rate of four-year olds in 2001 (56%) was similar to the rate in 1991 (58%).', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.impacts, 2.lessen, 3.barriers, 4.prepare, 5.commence', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2880773-80cb-5586-bdeb-a02ccde53ddf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2880773-80cb-5586-bdeb-a02ccde53ddf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Computer Science', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 3, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2886c6a-758e-5d85-b500-5ae2f7b41437'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2886c6a-758e-5d85-b500-5ae2f7b41437'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Diapers', E'In Germany, over 100,000 tons of diapers are discarded each year, resulting in the wastage of valuable resources. Diaper liners, which contain special polymers known as superabsorbers, are among the materials that end up in landfills. However, researchers have made significant progress in enhancing the recycling process for these liners, leading to substantial improvements.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a28a4b03-d9fd-5515-a2d7-ea9b35bb8ddc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a28a4b03-d9fd-5515-a2d7-ea9b35bb8ddc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '35dab300-e4f7-5f88-bda7-047066ac13b4'::uuid, NULL, E'If you are worried about your work, you should see a study counselor.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a28ad79d-98ae-50b2-acc0-3bb44a3dd6e4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a28ad79d-98ae-50b2-acc0-3bb44a3dd6e4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Airborne Diseases', E'Airborne diseases are very easily transmitted, and can result in respiratory illness that can be life threatening. It’s therefore no wonder that {{1}} of airborne infectious diseases are a major public health {{2}} , and that researchers are working hard to come up with technologies to provide clean air. So far, however, such technologies have had limited {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.outbreaks, 2.concern, 3.success', NULL, NULL),
  ('a29e8f8e-20a5-5f59-a8e3-cef84543122a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a29e8f8e-20a5-5f59-a8e3-cef84543122a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Barley Grains', E'University of Adelaide researchers have uncovered fundamental new information about the malting characteristics of barley grains. They say their finding could pave the way to more stable brewing processes or new malts for craft brewers. Published in the Nature publication Scientific Reports, the researchers discovered a new link between one of the key enzymes involved in malt production for brewing and a specific tissue layer within the barley grain.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a29f5c76-77a8-5892-b611-af24207c6e90'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a29f5c76-77a8-5892-b611-af24207c6e90'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Ties', E'Many types of scientific evidence show that involvement in social relationships benefits health. The most striking evidence comes from prospective studies of mortality {{1}} industrialized nations. These studies {{2}} show that individuals with the lowest level of involvement in social relationships are more likely to die than those with greater involvement. The risk of death among men and women with the fewest social ties was more than twice as high as the risk for adults with the most social ties. Social ties also reduce {{3}} risk among adults with documented medical conditions. Among adults with coronary artery disease, the socially isolated had a risk of subsequent cardiac death 2.4 times greater than their more socially connected {{4}} . In addition to mortality, involvement in social relationships has been associated with specific health conditions as well as biological markers indicating risk of preclinical conditions. Several recent review articles provide consistent and {{5}} evidence linking a low quantity or quality of social ties with a host of conditions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.across, 2.consistently, 3.mortality, 4.peers, 5.compelling', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2a20464-8e32-57cd-b568-6cb0f0a09f59'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2a20464-8e32-57cd-b568-6cb0f0a09f59'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call counting people who are living in a state or country?', '96aa8733-21a7-5e01-82d2-d51755a8da97'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Census', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2a4e06e-662c-52bf-a72e-d0a3bb0e7f3a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2a4e06e-662c-52bf-a72e-d0a3bb0e7f3a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are the fossil fuels that power cars?', 'bed72eb3-9823-5802-92b6-118209448ee6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Petrol /gasoline / diesel', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2aa71eb-b0dd-5172-a0f4-b808708482ff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2aa71eb-b0dd-5172-a0f4-b808708482ff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gauss', E'Gauss was a child prodigy. There are many {{1}} concerning his precocity as a child, and he made his first ground-breaking mathematical {{2}} while still a teenager. At just three years old, he {{3}} an error in his father payroll calculations, and he was looking after his father''s accounts on a regular {{4}} by the age of 5. At the age of 7, he is reported to have amazed his teachers by summing the integers from 1 to 100 almost instantly (having quickly spotted that the sum was actually 50 pairs of numbers, with each pair summing to 101 , total 5,050). By the age of 12, he was already attending gymnasium and criticizing Euclid''s geometry.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.anecdotes, 2.discoveries, 3.corrected, 4.basis', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2ae3b5b-bde3-5833-a427-c6ced178fa6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2ae3b5b-bde3-5833-a427-c6ced178fa6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the literature that withstands centuries?', 'd30bdfb3-de53-5a3a-8d64-d982441e4fa4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Classic literature', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2aed447-d055-522f-bdca-d9cb6fcdd30e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2aed447-d055-522f-bdca-d9cb6fcdd30e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Natural Environments', E'The environment consists of various components that interact and influence each other. For instance, the atmosphere provides the air we breathe, while bodies of water like rivers, lakes, and oceans support diverse aquatic ecosystems. Landscapes encompass forests, grasslands, mountains, and deserts, each with its unique characteristics and biodiversity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2b63180-48dc-5de6-af50-4cd85af3fcfd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2b63180-48dc-5de6-af50-4cd85af3fcfd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tunnel Excavation', E'Due to the lack of living space and the increase in population, there has been a construction {{1}} in the underground space to improve the quality of human life. In recent decades, {{2}} tunnelling techniques, particularly tunnel boring machines, have been extensively {{3}} to tunnel construction due to their high excavation {{4}} and low total cost for the excavation of long tunnels.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.boom, 2.mechanized, 3.applied, 4.rate', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2b95af2-245b-52cd-8f4d-2b10f095549f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2b95af2-245b-52cd-8f4d-2b10f095549f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4a406e7b-0e1e-5e66-8189-ee6eb55509c8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Her assets include shares in the company and a house in France.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2bb01ea-beb1-5ea5-827a-db54fefaa9de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2bb01ea-beb1-5ea5-827a-db54fefaa9de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Learning Multiple Languages', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 2, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2c0017f-06cc-51f2-95a3-c4bf6cd19830'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2c0017f-06cc-51f2-95a3-c4bf6cd19830'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9b44f6a9-0ca7-5b0d-b888-20691303a6ab'::uuid, NULL, E'Right now we have the ability to tackle these global issues.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2c15046-b152-57ff-a19c-3b29f1a14a3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2c15046-b152-57ff-a19c-3b29f1a14a3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sense of Number', E'As children, we arrive at what he called ‘the conception of number’ without {{1}} to counting words. Our non-linguistic sense of number implies that nonhuman animals can also, in principle, mentally represent the number of objects in a collection – and researchers have been building a growing {{2}} of evidence of the ways in which this actually happens. All these numbers can have an evolutionary significance, and if a creature can recognize them, this could afford an adaptive advantage. Bees can count dots one at a time while crawling over them; they might use this process to {{3}} flowers by the number of petals. A sense of number could also be valuable for surviving encounters with other creatures. Small fish join the largest shoal because it reduces the risk of predation. Numerical abilities are also important for navigation: honeybees count landmarks sequentially, one at a time, as a way of estimating the distance between the hive and a food source. This enables them to {{4}} their route back home.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.recourse, 2.body, 3.identify, 4.plot', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2ca740f-c98e-527c-954f-7b609d6c5cf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2ca740f-c98e-527c-954f-7b609d6c5cf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Economic Depression', E'An economic depression is a period of sustained, long-term {{1}} in economic activity in one or more economies. It is more severe than a recession, which is a slowdown in economic activity over {{2}} of a normal business cycle. Economic depressions are characterized by their length, and by abnormally large increases in unemployment {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.downturn, 2.the course, 3.rate', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2d4c4eb-8588-571c-99ab-fb3096b3c85b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2d4c4eb-8588-571c-99ab-fb3096b3c85b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '942e2cef-6386-5afc-b695-4eb4e7de3deb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'I would like all the engineering students to raise their hands.', NULL, NULL),
