  ('a2f850a7-72e4-5f0b-b2bd-f345c0c84ee1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2f850a7-72e4-5f0b-b2bd-f345c0c84ee1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'King Louis', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 5, 4, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2fa9ccd-2492-57a8-8309-1c6633ebab4a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2fa9ccd-2492-57a8-8309-1c6633ebab4a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Campus Research', E'Campus research is a vital component of higher education, offering numerous benefits to both students and institutions. It encompasses a wide range of academic activities that contribute to intellectual growth and innovation.\nFirst and foremost, campus research provides students with hands-on learning experiences. It allows them to apply classroom knowledge to real-world problems, enhancing their critical thinking, problem-solving, and analytical skills. Research projects also foster creativity and encourage students to explore their passions and interests in-depth.\nMoreover, campus research contributes to the advancement of knowledge. Faculty members and students engage in research to explore new frontiers in their respective fields, leading to groundbreaking discoveries and innovations. This not only elevates the reputation of the institution but also has a positive impact on society as a whole.\nFurthermore, campus research often results in valuable collaborations. It encourages interdisciplinary approaches and brings together experts from various fields to tackle complex issues. These collaborations can lead to cross-disciplinary breakthroughs that address pressing global challenges, such as climate change, healthcare, and technology.\nIn addition to academic benefits, campus research can also have economic advantages. It can attract funding, investment, and partnerships with industry, driving local and regional economic development. Research institutions often become hubs of innovation, creating jobs and fostering entrepreneurship.\nIn conclusion, campus research is a cornerstone of higher education, offering students valuable learning experiences, advancing knowledge, fostering collaborations, and contributing to economic growth. It plays a crucial role in shaping the future and addressing the complex challenges of our world.', NULL, NULL, E'Campus research is an essential component of higher education, providing students with hands-on learning experiences, advancing knowledge through groundbreaking discoveries and collaborations, and driving economic growth while addressing pressing global challenges, thus playing a pivotal role in shaping a brighter future.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a2ff4584-a01d-59cf-971f-ae8729cd5d93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2ff4584-a01d-59cf-971f-ae8729cd5d93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Valley Fever', E'Valley fever''s mortality rate is about one death per 1,000 infections, according to infectious disease physician John Galgiani, director of the University of Arizona''s Valley Fever Center for Excellence. It doesn''t need to be so high. There are medications to treat it, but patients often receive incorrect diagnoses.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a2ff5957-407c-5e6a-8b38-8c0103088e4a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a2ff5957-407c-5e6a-8b38-8c0103088e4a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'cf084f49-1ec4-5eb1-90e8-872bc119b9c5'::uuid, NULL, E'Before signing up, check our website for the list of courses.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3001f75-d73b-51d3-8877-8a2ebeb2c1ed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3001f75-d73b-51d3-8877-8a2ebeb2c1ed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Living Longer', E'In general, people are living longer now. What are the causes and problems it may bring?', NULL, NULL, E'In recent years, people are living longer than ever before. While this is a positive development in many ways, it also brings with it a number of causes and problems that need to be addressed. In this essay, I will discuss the main causes of increased life expectancy and the problems that it may bring.\nOne of the main causes of increased life expectancy is advances in medical technology and healthcare. With new treatments and medications being developed every day, people are able to live longer and healthier lives than ever before. Additionally, improved living conditions, such as access to clean water and better nutrition, have also contributed to longer lifespans. People are now able to live in environments that are more conducive to good health and longevity.\nHowever, increased life expectancy also brings with it a number of problems. One of the most pressing issues is an aging population. As people live longer, the number of elderly individuals in society increases. This can put a strain on healthcare systems and social security programs, as well as increase the burden on younger generations to care for elderly family members. Additionally, longer lifespans can also lead to a greater risk of age-related health problems, such as dementia and Alzheimer''s disease.\nIn conclusion, while increased life expectancy is a positive development in many ways, it also brings with it a number of challenges that need to be addressed. Advances in medical technology and healthcare have contributed to longer lifespans, but an aging population and increased risk of age-related health problems are just some of the problems that need to be addressed. It is important for society to come together to find solutions to these challenges so that people can continue to live longer, healthier lives.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a30c0c96-300e-52e5-ac3d-986258993697'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a30c0c96-300e-52e5-ac3d-986258993697'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the largest country in the world?', '6d2d4b76-6aa3-5d4b-ab2a-f3f7c3bc075a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Russia', NULL, NULL),
  ('a30d90dd-47ef-5350-ae5c-bd8968c40f73'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a30d90dd-47ef-5350-ae5c-bd8968c40f73'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gender Gap', E'Research suggests ADHD is three to four times more likely to be detected in childhood in boys as they tend to exhibit more disruptive behaviors. The symptoms in girls tend to be more subtle: less hyperactive, more inattentive. The diagnoses gap between males and females appears to shrink in adulthood, but psychologists say the bias can remain. The ADHD Foundation says increased awareness is needed in health and educational settings about how the condition can present differently. A late diagnosis can negatively impact on relationships, careers, and mental health. In England, NICE guidance has been updated to make it easier for doctors to detect women and girls with ADHD. Work to improve neuro developmental services is underway in Scotland and Wales. But there are currently no dedicated services for adults with ADHD in Northern Ireland.\n\nWhat will happen in people whose ADHD is diagnosed later on in life?', '2ad64eff-c816-557f-a8bb-2d19cb17584c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They can’t deal with their work well.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a30f15cd-2bfa-536b-b723-fb58160eecf9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a30f15cd-2bfa-536b-b723-fb58160eecf9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the ceremony called for marriage?', '5b52ad69-f8c3-50a0-82d4-566b2146c734'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Wedding', NULL, NULL),
  ('a316f2e9-be15-531a-94ec-da138bd3ad75'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a316f2e9-be15-531a-94ec-da138bd3ad75'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'aa785106-1c4b-5bfb-b956-feeac577b56e'::uuid, NULL, E'The visiting professor is going to give a lecture for geology.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3199748-0971-5d2d-8c7b-6ab3fb9401e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3199748-0971-5d2d-8c7b-6ab3fb9401e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Immanuel Kant', NULL, '1d5ba744-fcd8-50f4-a007-f88e53c8fbec'::uuid, NULL, E'So in the process, I learn all of these incredibly wonderful theories that the smartest people who have ever lived have developed over the last 2,500 years that help us make better decisions and become better people. For example, I learned about Immanuel Kant and the categorical imperative. So Kant says, when we''re about to do something we have to design a rule or a maxim that we could will to be universal. Meaning, we have to imagine, what if everyone did what we''re about to do, what would happen to the world? Would it be OK or would it get all screwed up? So the maxim I''m designing here is something like, anytime two people are in any kind of negotiation, one of them can drag into the negotiation an entirely unrelated global calamity and tell the other person that they shouldn''t care about whatever they care about, because they should care about that instead. That world would suck, right? Like, your sister borrows five dollars from you, you ask for it back, she says, "How dare you care about five dollars when the polar ice caps are melting?" No one wants to live in this world, right? Kant also says, by the way, that you should treat people as ends in themselves, and not a means to an end, meaning, you shouldn''t use people to get what you want. Well, that''s what I was doing.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a32a791f-0d5e-5ac2-ac79-cb386427cf3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a32a791f-0d5e-5ac2-ac79-cb386427cf3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Failure to Success', E'What is your view on the idea that it takes failure to achieve success?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a32fac4f-4587-5ef4-9852-554561484ba8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a32fac4f-4587-5ef4-9852-554561484ba8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Superhighway Network', E'Researchers have discovered a new superhighway network to travel through the Solar System much faster than was previously possible. Such routes can drive comets and asteroids near Jupiter to Neptune''s distance in under a decade and to 100 astronomical units in less than a century. They could be used to send spacecraft to the far reaches of our planetary system relatively fast, and to monitor near-Earth objects that might collide with us.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3317f94-bcf5-5b8f-b0e6-4354b003d223'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3317f94-bcf5-5b8f-b0e6-4354b003d223'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person whose responsibility is to correct others'' mistakes?', 'c5ff07ad-3e47-5b21-828e-9dd216490e85'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Corrector / proofreader / editor', NULL, NULL),
  ('a336e852-5efa-51c3-99df-14caf8d587f4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a336e852-5efa-51c3-99df-14caf8d587f4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the barrier that can prevent floods from damaging our home?', '06d1dbdb-4225-5a7e-8846-ec9d1bf84db9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Dam', NULL, NULL),
  ('a33a9c0b-aea3-5f95-880a-b71ed01e2d1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a33a9c0b-aea3-5f95-880a-b71ed01e2d1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Apple Cider Vinegar', NULL, '2544bd5f-42ae-5e02-a9f5-19538129bd8b'::uuid, NULL, E'But lowering your blood sugar after a meal is just about the only benefit of drinking apple cider vinegar. Research does suggest that acetic acid can slow down the accumulation of body fat and prevent metabolic disorders in mice and rats. But there’s little evidence that it has the same effect on humans. In one weight-loss experiment, 30 volunteers drank two tablespoons of either apple cider vinegar, malt vinegar, or a placebo drink, twice a day, for two months straight, and none of them lost weight. In an older study with a similar design, participants did lose weight, but only about a third of a pound each week, which McDonald says isn’t much. But if not for weight loss, what about using cider vinegar to whiten your teeth? I caution people against that. That’s because cider vinegar is an acid. In fact, most brands have a pH between 2 and 3, which is similar to stomach acid, so swishing it around in your mouth can over time wear down the enamel around your teeth, leaving them feeling rough to the touch and more susceptible to cavities and decay.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a343bdcc-89c7-5415-992b-0dfb01837809'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a343bdcc-89c7-5415-992b-0dfb01837809'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '68c414f3-0757-5d3d-9f24-0c5b6cbdddaa'::uuid, NULL, E'Trainees are taught to pay attention to details and to strive for perfection.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a34688b4-f620-5da4-8234-65e839918c2b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a34688b4-f620-5da4-8234-65e839918c2b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What kind of jewelry do we wear on the ear?', '0904a7f2-18b6-5ed6-bd97-4e79eaa5000d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Earring', NULL, NULL),
  ('a3482cf8-d488-5deb-b0b2-4568471d0e25'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3482cf8-d488-5deb-b0b2-4568471d0e25'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '07d7b4fe-5755-5205-b059-dca2a9e09adc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The field of journalism has been seen in decline in the decades.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a34be477-2869-50d2-8c52-82fa5cb9e20e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a34be477-2869-50d2-8c52-82fa5cb9e20e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the tallest mountain in the world?', '8cbb0292-dd9a-5c64-93d9-384801090c7b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mount Everest', NULL, NULL),
  ('a34d73c4-494e-5837-8893-8fe6c26631e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a34d73c4-494e-5837-8893-8fe6c26631e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Constellation', E'A constellation is an area on the celestial sphere in which a group of stars forms an imaginary outline or pattern, typically representing an animal, mythological person or creature, or an inanimate object. The origins of the earliest constellations likely go back to prehistory.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a356f138-8049-5dfb-9207-f562c6253c74'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a356f138-8049-5dfb-9207-f562c6253c74'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9dafd561-6e4b-5673-a11f-0399cb3979cf'::uuid, NULL, E'This school has provided its teachers with ten more days of sick leave.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a35e2afa-8750-5638-8d7f-ff793fb07512'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a35e2afa-8750-5638-8d7f-ff793fb07512'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fallacy', E'Things happen together, or one event happens after another, but this does not necessarily mean that one event causes the other. There may be other hidden factors that influence both events, or the connection between them may simply be a coincidence. Therefore, people need to consider all the relevant factors to determine the real relationship between two events instead of assuming that correlation is the same as causation.\nFallacies are common in daily life. For example, if person A lends a mobile phone to person B and the phone stops working after person B uses it, person A may believe that the phone broke because of person B’s use. However, this conclusion may be wrong because the phone might have already had a problem, or it might have stopped working for another reason. Similarly, a fallacy can lead to cognitive bias. For instance, if a student wears a particular shirt before an exam and gets a high score, the student may believe that the shirt brought good luck and continue wearing it before future exams, even though the result was probably caused by good preparation rather than the shirt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a370cab2-5a6a-594e-bc6d-ff9df3020a9b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a370cab2-5a6a-594e-bc6d-ff9df3020a9b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What city is known as the birthplace of democracy?', 'a9f46ca3-3508-56b3-bb22-8fbd3a704607'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Athens', NULL, NULL),
  ('a371df04-bd86-5fbd-a6e6-e192713aa170'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a371df04-bd86-5fbd-a6e6-e192713aa170'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Beach Vacation', E'The sun beats down on the golden sands of the beach, as waves crash rhythmically against the shore. The salty air fills your lungs as you kick off your shoes and feel the cool sand between your toes. You spread out your towel and relax, as the gentle hum of beach-goers and seagulls drowns out the stresses of everyday life.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3721dad-0d47-5076-9f76-eec56f4d5d45'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3721dad-0d47-5076-9f76-eec56f4d5d45'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'dba60c1d-3108-5d1a-a937-08f3e44d83c3'::uuid, NULL, E'Some benefits relate directly to the mental health of the teenagers.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
