  ('a3b78d70-745d-5d97-84b2-00d798321a40'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3b78d70-745d-5d97-84b2-00d798321a40'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the machine used for washing clothes?', '16e7a14e-911b-50ef-900f-4c2ce083acd7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Washing Machine', NULL, NULL),
  ('a3c27deb-a002-505e-8016-946358c8d380'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3c27deb-a002-505e-8016-946358c8d380'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a young dog?', '98b353d4-33f2-540f-b179-674db5d36a99'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Puppy', NULL, NULL),
  ('a3c337aa-20c7-5533-8ff2-3618aa4fd643'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3c337aa-20c7-5533-8ff2-3618aa4fd643'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Communication', E'Communication should be open, honest, and {{1}} . People feel {{2}} to express their thoughts, opinions, and potential solutions to problems. People feel as if they are heard out and listened to by team members who are {{3}} to understand. Team members ask questions for clarity and spend their thought time listening deeply {{4}} than forming rebuttals while their co-worker is speaking.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.respectful, 2.free, 3.attempting, 4.rather', NULL, NULL),
  ('a3cf97f0-beb6-5b9b-ba68-f3e05b2cea29'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3cf97f0-beb6-5b9b-ba68-f3e05b2cea29'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solar Cell Technology', E'Recent research has led to a significant breakthrough in solar cell technology, offering the potential to revolutionize the way we harness and utilize solar energy. This innovation promises to make solar power more efficient and accessible than ever before.\nTraditional solar cells, known as photovoltaic cells, have limitations when it comes to capturing sunlight and converting it into electricity. A major challenge has been maximizing the absorption of sunlight across a broad spectrum of wavelengths. However, researchers have now developed a new type of solar cell that addresses this issue.\nThe breakthrough involves the use of perovskite solar cells, a type of solar technology that has gained attention for its high efficiency and low production costs. Perovskite solar cells have the unique ability to absorb a wider range of light wavelengths, making them more effective in converting sunlight into electricity.\nFurthermore, perovskite solar cells can be manufactured using simpler and more cost-effective methods than traditional silicon solar cells. This means that solar panels incorporating this technology can potentially be produced at a lower cost, making solar energy more affordable and accessible to a broader range of people.\nAdditionally, the flexibility and versatility of perovskite solar cells open up new possibilities for integration into various applications, such as wearable technology, building-integrated photovoltaics, and portable electronic devices.\nThis breakthrough in solar cell technology not only holds promise for a more sustainable and eco-friendly future but also highlights the ongoing advancements in renewable energy. As researchers continue to refine and scale up perovskite solar cell production, we may soon see a significant increase in the adoption of solar energy as a clean and efficient power source.', NULL, NULL, E'Recent advancements in solar energy, marked by the development of perovskite solar cells, offer a major breakthrough in harnessing solar power, with these cells'' ability to absorb a wider range of light wavelengths and their cost-effective, versatile manufacturing, paving the way for a more sustainable, accessible, and integrated solar future.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a3d18f6d-5ff7-57c2-ae60-3c29d6ea46bc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3d18f6d-5ff7-57c2-ae60-3c29d6ea46bc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Independent Work', E'Working nine to five for a single employer bears little resemblance to the way a substantial share of the workforce makes a living today. Millions of people assemble various income streams and work independently, rather than in structured payroll jobs. This is hardly a new phenomenon, yet it has never been well measured in official statistics and the resulting data gaps prevent a clear view of a large share of labor-market activity. To better understand the independent workforce and what motivates the people who participate in it, the McKinsey Global Institute surveyed some 8,000 respondents across Europe and the United States. We asked about their income in the past 12 months-encompassing primary work, as well as any other income-generating activities, and about their professional satisfaction and aspirations for work in the future. The resulting report, Independent work: Choice, necessity, and the gig economy, finds that up to 162 million people in Europe and the United States - or 20 to 30 percent of the working-age population - engage in some form of independent work. While demographically diverse, independent workers largely fit into four segments (exhibit): free agents, who actively choose independent work and derive their primary income from it; casual earners, who use independent work for supplemental income and do so by choice; reluctants, who make their primary living from independent work but would prefer traditional jobs; and the financially strapped, who do supplemental independent work out of necessity.', NULL, NULL, E'Working nine to five for a single employer bears little resemblance to the way a substantial share of the workforce makes a living today, while millions of people assemble various income streams and work independently, since 20 to 30 percent of the working-age population engage in some form of independent work, who largely fit into four segments, including free agents, casual earners, reluctants and the financially strapped.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a3d4005d-f23d-5e78-b701-1fcce82f2d02'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3d4005d-f23d-5e78-b701-1fcce82f2d02'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tasmania', E'Tasmania is a large and relatively sparsely populated island off the south coast of Australia. The island is of particular interest to natural scientists, who go there to research the unique wildlife. Tasmania has, for example, twelve species of bird that are not found anywhere else in the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3d4c39c-70a1-5dc8-b6b1-09e02c0754ca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3d4c39c-70a1-5dc8-b6b1-09e02c0754ca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '53537999-49ca-5e51-a2da-da514cce4194'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Computers can be used to facilitate language learning.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a3dd6d61-13b7-5fa0-a775-eecf3dea554c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3dd6d61-13b7-5fa0-a775-eecf3dea554c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Body-confidence Education', NULL, 'a829c39d-00f3-51ed-8005-b19f5fede037'::uuid, NULL, E'If you actually want to make a difference, you have to do something. And we’ve learned there are three key ways: The first is we have to educate for body confidence. We have to help our teenagers develop strategies to overcome image-related pressures and build their self-esteem. Now the good news is that there are many programs out there available to do this. The bad news is that most of them don’t work. I was shocked to learn that many well-meaning programs are inadvertently actually making the situation worse. So we need to make damn sure that the programs that our kids are receiving are not only having a positive impact, but having a lasting impact as well. And the research shows that the best programs address six key areas: The first is the influence of family, friends and relationships. The second is media and celebrity culture, then how to handle teasing and bullying, the way we compete and compare with one another based on looks, talking about appearance — some people call this “body talk” or “fat talk” — and finally, the foundations of respecting and looking after yourself. These six things are crucial starting points for anyone serious about delivering body-confidence education that works. An education is critical, but tackling this problem is going to require each and everyone of us to step up and be better role models for the women and girls in our own lives. Challenging the status quo of how women are seen and talked about in our own circles.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a3df6fc7-53b3-57f5-930d-596b72442263'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a3df6fc7-53b3-57f5-930d-596b72442263'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8c787853-7b1c-5735-afa7-353dfee8fe87'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'In Britain, public transport is in fact becoming increasingly expensive.', NULL, NULL),
