  ('a528867c-28df-533e-b6c6-58835489f231'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a528867c-28df-533e-b6c6-58835489f231'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0f6a1436-44ea-57ea-8f9e-3871e7cd0ad0'::uuid, NULL, E'He tried to shift the blame for his mistakes onto his colleagues.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a5306efc-965f-5040-95be-bf5dc84ce14c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a5306efc-965f-5040-95be-bf5dc84ce14c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f34e4a22-5f59-571e-bf38-726254e2bbdb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Scientists used an analytical method to solve this issue.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a5394119-60ae-5c2f-b4b8-68254e176387'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a5394119-60ae-5c2f-b4b8-68254e176387'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What does the sun do during dawn?', 'd2ba5b04-8adb-51ea-a20e-b1da69eec405'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Sunrise', NULL, NULL),
  ('a53bb081-3dbc-52c6-80fe-c1c6ea0bd91e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a53bb081-3dbc-52c6-80fe-c1c6ea0bd91e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Reversible Diseases', E'Heart and blood vessel diseases still kill more people, not only in this country, but also worldwide, than everything else combined, and yet it’s completely preventable for almost everybody. It’s not only preventable: it’s actually reversible. And for the last almost 29 years, we’ve been able to show that by simply changing diet and lifestyle, using these very high-tech, expensive, state-of-the-art measures to prove how powerful these very simple and low-tech and low-cost interventions can be like quantitative arteriography, before and after a year, and cardiac PET scans. We showed a few months ago that we published the first study showing you can actually stop or reverse the progression of prostate cancer by making changes in diet and lifestyle. Now there is an epidemic of obesity: two-thirds of adults and 15 percent of kids. What’s really concerning to me is that diabetes has increased 70 percent in the past 10 years, and this may be the first generation in which our kids live a shorter life span than we do. That’s pitiful, and it’s preventable.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '672daaaa-73c3-53ae-a03c-cbfc6dd485f2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Heart and blood vessel diseases are not only preventable but also reversible. For individuals, simply changing their lifestyle and diet can make a difference. Such low-cost interventions can indeed help stop the cancer.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a53be33e-2da7-5478-b8c5-afd8eeece60e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a53be33e-2da7-5478-b8c5-afd8eeece60e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cb203d3a-3dcc-56ea-82c4-d04656fda132'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Many companies care about their public image whatever their size.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a53bf72f-6253-5e4b-86c7-3370676fa2cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a53bf72f-6253-5e4b-86c7-3370676fa2cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the study of the behavior of living organisms?', '9417d978-6700-59b6-ae34-21e592763894'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Biology', NULL, NULL),
  ('a53c05c3-9f88-5682-af5b-0c770dd2b8c9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a53c05c3-9f88-5682-af5b-0c770dd2b8c9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'de8247c8-7e34-528f-9dcd-295bba13c224'::uuid, NULL, E'The alarm should go off automatically as soon as smoke is detected.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a545f7e5-d931-5533-b6c6-da131c05c6fe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a545f7e5-d931-5533-b6c6-da131c05c6fe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the extra working time?', 'ffdf2821-a32a-5fb6-8dbb-702a7e215c1c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Overtime', NULL, NULL),
  ('a55b7bbf-f30c-58d1-b96e-9e6dba6d4bf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a55b7bbf-f30c-58d1-b96e-9e6dba6d4bf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pidgins', E'Pidgins are languages that are born after contact between at least two languages. As many pidgins developed during the period of empire and international trade, one of the language parents was frequently a European language such as French or English, and the other language parent was the language of the people with whom the Europeans were {{1}} or whom they were colonizing. Usually one of the languages provided the majority of {{2}} items and the other provided the grammatical structure. When pidgins become learned as a mother tongue, they become {{3}} as creoles. I am not going to discuss pidgins and creoles and contact languages as such in this book in any {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.trading, 2.vocabulary, 3.known, 4.depth', NULL, NULL),
  ('a560ce39-255a-5caa-bec8-245362317d3b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a560ce39-255a-5caa-bec8-245362317d3b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heat Pumps', E'Heat pumps are devices that use electricity to transfer heat from outside to inside a building, providing a clean and efficient way to heat homes. Heat pumps work by using a refrigerant, a material that changes state from liquid to gas and back {{1}} , to absorb heat from the air, ground or water outside and transfer it to the water or air inside the building. This process can {{2}} more energy than the electricity that is put into it, resulting in an energy efficiency of over 100%. They are considered a crucial technology for achieving the UK’s {{3}} of reaching net zero emissions by 2040, as they can replace fossil fuel-based heating systems such as gas boilers. However, heat pumps are still {{4}} uncommon in the UK, with only 1% of British homes having one installed, compared to 60% of Norwegian homes. The government aims to increase this number to 80% by 2048, and has recently {{5}} a 50% increase in its boiler upgrade grants, which offer households up to £7,500 to switch to a heat pump.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.again, 2.produce, 3.target, 4.relatively, 5.announced', NULL, NULL),
  ('a560e8be-7fd6-5534-aacd-6b02d7abd3f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a560e8be-7fd6-5534-aacd-6b02d7abd3f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'English Language', E'With about one and a half billion non-native speakers, English has become the world''s own language. Such {{1}} has its downside, of course. There are now about 6,800 languages left in the world, compared with perhaps {{2}} that number back at the dawn of agriculture. Thanks in {{3}} to the rise of über-languages, most importantly English, the remaining languages are now dying at the {{4}} of about one a fortnight. Want to learn Busuu, anyone? Then you''d better head to Cameroon fast, before one of the language''s last eight speakers kicks the bucket (as the Busuu-nese presumably doesn''t say).', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dominance, 2.twice, 3.part, 4.rate', NULL, NULL),
  ('a561f425-3664-5290-bd7e-aa5775b74944'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a561f425-3664-5290-bd7e-aa5775b74944'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd759d3f2-0e84-5c5c-82e1-d4bcadad9717'::uuid, NULL, E'We have strong relationships with counselors and teachers across the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a56dc7c5-bb63-593b-b612-c012c9f2cf4c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a56dc7c5-bb63-593b-b612-c012c9f2cf4c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Famous People', E'Have you ever known anyone famous? If so, you may have found that they are remarkably similar to the rest of us. You may have even heard them {{1}} to people saying there is anything different about them. "I''m really just a normal guy," {{2}} an actor who has recently rocketed into the spotlight. There is, of course, usually a brief period when they actually start to believe they are as great as their {{3}} fans suggest. They start to wear {{4}} clothes and talk as if everyone should hear what they have to say. This period, however, does not often last long. They fall back to reality as fast as they had {{5}} risen above it all.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.object, 2.protests, 3.worshipping, 4.fancy, 5.originally', NULL, NULL),
  ('a57692e7-f3d1-56d0-9442-7b5ac350fe06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a57692e7-f3d1-56d0-9442-7b5ac350fe06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Overcrowding', E'As the urban population grows, traffic is heavy and public areas such as parking lots are packed. What solutions do you think can address such problems?', NULL, NULL, E'As the urban population continues to grow, traffic congestion and parking shortages have become increasingly common problems. These issues can have a significant impact on the quality of life in urban areas, making it difficult for people to get around and access the resources they need. However, there are several solutions that can help address these problems.\nFirstly, encouraging the use of public transportation can help reduce the number of cars on the road. This can be accomplished through a variety of methods, such as providing incentives for people who use public transportation, improving public transportation infrastructure, and implementing congestion pricing policies. By reducing the number of cars on the road, traffic congestion can be relieved.\nSecondly, building more parking garages and implementing smart parking systems can help alleviate parking shortages. This can be accomplished by identifying areas where parking is in high demand and building new parking structures in those areas. Smart parking systems can also be implemented to help people find available parking spaces more easily, reducing the amount of time spent searching for a parking spot.\nIn conclusion, while traffic congestion and parking shortages can be significant problems in urban areas, there are several solutions that can help address these issues. Encouraging the use of public transportation, building more parking garages, and implementing smart parking systems are all effective strategies that can help make urban areas more livable and accessible. By working together to implement these solutions, we can create a more sustainable and efficient urban environment for everyone.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('a579d466-030e-5cf1-aaef-c0dcc269bc48'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a579d466-030e-5cf1-aaef-c0dcc269bc48'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Brain Wave', E'We can''t see it, but brains hum with electrical activity. Brain waves created by the coordinated firing of huge collections of nerve cells pinball around the brain. The waves can ricochet from the front of the brain to the back, or from deep structures all the way to the scalp and then back again.\nCalled neuronal oscillations, these signals are known to accompany certain mental states. Quiet alpha waves ripple soothingly across the brains of meditating monks. Beta waves rise and fall during intense conversational turns. Fast gamma waves accompany sharp insights. Sluggish delta rhythms lull deep sleepers, while dreamers shift into slightly quicker theta rhythms.\nResearchers have long argued over whether these waves have purposes, and what those purposes might be. Some scientists see waves as inevitable but useless by-products of the signals that really matter — messages sent by individual nerve cells. Waves are simply a consequence of collective neural behavior, and nothing more, that view holds. But a growing body of evidence suggests just the opposite: instead of by-products of important signals, brain waves are key to how the brain operates, routing information among far-flung brain regions that need to work together.\nMIT''s Earl Miller is among the neuro­scientists amassing evidence that waves are an essential part of how the brain operates. Brain oscillations deftly route information in a way that allows the brain to choose which signals in the world to pay attention to and which to ignore, his recent studies suggest.', NULL, NULL, E'Brains hum with electrical activity, where brain waves created by the coordinated firing of huge collections of nerve cells pinball around the brain, and these signals are known to accompany certain mental states, so brain waves are key to how the brain operates, but brain oscillations deftly route information in a way that allows the brain to choose which signals in the world to pay attention to and which to ignore.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('a57f0427-dc06-5c9c-a478-e568b1c486d1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'a57f0427-dc06-5c9c-a478-e568b1c486d1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the personal vehicle with four wheels, used for commuting and transport?', 'd7899305-0ab1-55c7-be8d-afed2a00e5b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Car', NULL, NULL),
