  ('aab81df7-5174-542e-a3d1-84d39c25aebf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aab81df7-5174-542e-a3d1-84d39c25aebf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Boeing Leadership', E'Across our global enterprise, Boeing employees are united by a shared {{1}} to our values — safety, quality, integrity, and transparency — above all else. We believe that compliance and {{2}} behavior are everyone’s responsibility. This means we must hold ourselves {{3}} to our values and to creating an open and inclusive workplace. Boeing leadership encourages employees to proactively seek out issues, speak up and report concerns, and engage with {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.commitment, 2.ethical, 3.accountable, 4.transparency', NULL, NULL),
  ('aabae644-f963-5485-bae0-a1f38bc90c4c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aabae644-f963-5485-bae0-a1f38bc90c4c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Pictures', E'The majority of early pictures in the Gallery''s care are by unknown artists, and fundamental questions, such as when, where and why they were painted still remain to be answered. Through the application of scientific methods, this project has potential to unlock key evidence that will allow us to determine answers to these questions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('aabccc11-f22d-50ef-81ad-1b043ec0f8a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aabccc11-f22d-50ef-81ad-1b043ec0f8a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Leadership and Management', E'Leadership is about establishing a direction and influencing others to follow. Management is about successfully {{1}} the many complex details involved in a business’s operations. Leadership pursues change and challenges the status quo, whereas management seeks to control and provide stability within the {{2}} circumstances. Both management and leadership are necessary skills, and they often {{3}} with one another. In most settings, the role of a manager includes both leadership and management functions. Leadership skills are needed to set the vision, and management skills are needed to {{4}} a plan to achieve that vision. Recognizing the difference between leadership and management, however, can help individuals focus on developing their skills in both arenas. The greatest success comes when strong leadership is {{5}} with effective management.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.administering, 2.existing, 3.overlap, 4.implement, 5.paired', NULL, NULL),
  ('aabda519-86b5-56c2-b2a2-bc69819cfab3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aabda519-86b5-56c2-b2a2-bc69819cfab3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '121b7bab-e333-5172-ad43-d71df96f211f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Before completing the exercise, you need to read the remaining chapters.', NULL, NULL),
  ('aac40138-8ddd-5bd7-be6a-c20c8a7c4046'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aac40138-8ddd-5bd7-be6a-c20c8a7c4046'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the condition characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest?', 'eaa18f61-b1f8-5713-a43c-ceae136f93d4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Depression', NULL, NULL),
  ('aac76f2b-3f64-52a4-a2d7-a81f95ef10aa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aac76f2b-3f64-52a4-a2d7-a81f95ef10aa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4ee5a24e-9eb6-5d3a-bcd7-d7eb800c3fd5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'After class, we can all meet in the main school office.', NULL, NULL),
  ('aac8e1e6-0050-5926-99f2-96e9fd6e8259'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aac8e1e6-0050-5926-99f2-96e9fd6e8259'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'A dozen is a grouping of which number?', '286ba4cc-25c8-53da-b938-756214a85d45'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Twelve', NULL, NULL),
  ('aacc30cd-ce4c-5394-982e-10439c0351be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aacc30cd-ce4c-5394-982e-10439c0351be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Purpose of Museums', NULL, '72bef1bd-dbc6-5f7b-a17e-34cdc71e1078'::uuid, NULL, E'I''ve been asked to speak today about the purpose of museums and I think that''s something we often take for granted, that we have museums and we need museums. But with so much information available now online, people have access to whatever it is they want to know so I think we need to consider carefully just what it is that we expect of our museums today. What makes them relevant in the information age.\nClearly, we''ve got to move beyond the early twentieth century concept of a warehouse full of old, remarkable, untouchable objects. This warehouse idea does very little to inspire people. What museum professionals need to do - what they should be doing, is make their collections and programs work towards the purpose of education. So whether that means having more hands-on exhibits, becoming involved with other community organisations, they should be doing whatever it takes to think about their visitors, to engage people, to educate them. And in that way, they can be instruments of social change. If they have knowledge and understanding of the people who visit, and the people they want to come and visit, they can take this as a starting point for providing exhibitions and services that are relevant to people''s lives.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('aacfad85-70b6-51d9-9471-5d6dc8d39f34'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aacfad85-70b6-51d9-9471-5d6dc8d39f34'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Birds that Talk', NULL, '8dbd290e-1544-5c83-a797-681564b6267b'::uuid, NULL, E'Birds can be very impressive at imitation, which is another word for copying. When chicks are born, they hear sounds made by the other birds in their flock, or their family. And they practice imitating those sounds, until they sound just like the rest of their flock! There are lots of reasons that birds might need to know the sounds that other animals make. For one thing, birds in the wild are very social. They help out other members of their flock. The calls of different flocks of birds, even two different flocks of the same kind of bird, are all different from each other! It helps to know who your family is by the familiar sounds they make! Plus, it’s helpful to learn animal calls that might scare away predators, so that the birds don’t get eaten! And being good at imitating shows that a bird is smart, and has a good memory and strong muscles, which makes it more appealing to other birds in its flock. The birds that can copy human speech are especially talented imitators. Birds that learn to imitate humans come from two groups: parrots, like African greys, cockatoos, and parakeets...and songbirds, like mynahs, starlings, and even crows! They’re such good imitators that sometimes they can even fool people! Some pet birds have escaped into the wild, and taught the calls they learned from humans, to the other birds in their new flock. So sometimes people have gone for a nature walk, and heard someone calling out. They looked around for a person ... only to realize that the birds were the ones talking.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('aad08edf-2145-5df4-85c5-5328efe20afd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aad08edf-2145-5df4-85c5-5328efe20afd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for a person who cuts, styles, and cares for hair?', '33c7e380-c776-5501-9409-59e9f3f11d7c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hairdresser / barber', NULL, NULL),
  ('aad6bb41-7be2-5366-82f2-745e71154ef7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aad6bb41-7be2-5366-82f2-745e71154ef7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '01d10a46-ac6d-53e8-96b2-9c63b3636c4d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The relative humidity is the amount of moisture that the air can hold.', NULL, NULL),
  ('aad74157-1fda-5217-a9bb-e7758da8bc27'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aad74157-1fda-5217-a9bb-e7758da8bc27'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ocean', E'Earth''s surface is dominated by oceans. But where did all that water come from?\n{{1}} and comets smashing into the early Earth have long been thought to be a promising source. But measurements of Halley''s Comet and five others threw cold water on the idea that comets {{2}} a large share of the oceans. Because the chemical {{3}} of the comets did not match the oceans. Specifically, the ratio of heavy {{4}} , or deuterium, to regular hydrogen was too high in the comets.\nBut now astronomers have gotten a glimpse of a comet with a different origin, and it matches the oceans much better. They used the Herschel space telescope to examine Comet Hartley 2, which originated in the Kuiper Belt. Halley and its ilk came from a distant swarm of comets called the Oort Cloud.\nAt a {{5}} science meeting last week in France, and in a study in Nature, the {{6}} {{7}} that Comet Hartley 2 has the same deuterium-to-hydrogen ratio as ocean water.\nSo maybe comets did play a major role in delivering Earth''s oceans. Something to ponder next time you have a day at the beach.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Asteroids, 2.provided, 3.signatures, 4.hydrogen, 5.planetary, 6.researchers, 7.announced', NULL, NULL),
  ('aae45e15-d0c4-581f-98a1-c10330d46404'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aae45e15-d0c4-581f-98a1-c10330d46404'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call an animal or plant that has parents of different species or varieties?', '307c2cdf-d888-50f4-af96-2a18529ecdd3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hybrid / crossbreed', NULL, NULL),
  ('aaec9889-f695-5f1f-b5ec-b1005dbcef87'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aaec9889-f695-5f1f-b5ec-b1005dbcef87'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd53cb83c-94e8-56e2-9b1a-a986e230bc55'::uuid, NULL, E'If I miss the call, please record the message in the office.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('aaece8c7-96a8-5ffb-8525-2b03e525e01a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aaece8c7-96a8-5ffb-8525-2b03e525e01a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mine', E'If you''ve ever spent time with toddlers, sooner or later you''ll hear the word "Mine!" It''s usually {{1}} by an adult saying, "Now, now, you have to learn to share." But a study in the August 28th issue of Nature suggests we may be wasting our breath. Because kids in the {{2}} set have no interest in making sure everyone gets their fair share.\nScientists from {{3}} wondered if, and when, young children begin to {{4}} the welfare of others. So they gathered up over 200 Swiss {{5}} and a small mountain of candy. And one-by-one they gave each child a choice that goes something like this: I can give one example to you and one to one of the other kids. Or I can give one to you—and none to anyone else.\nChildren who were three or four years old didn''t much care whether or not their friends also got an M&M, or a jellybean or any other sweet. But that attitude changed by the time the kids were seven or eight, when almost 80 percent of them opted to be fair. Okay, that doesn''t exactly make them {{6}} for a Nobel Peace Prize. But maybe {{7}} begins with an M&M.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.followed, 2.preschool, 3.Switzerland, 4.consider, 5.schoolchildren, 6.candidates, 7.magnanimousness', NULL, NULL),
  ('aaef9f5a-e314-5b6d-b333-d56dadcd4c33'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aaef9f5a-e314-5b6d-b333-d56dadcd4c33'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Writing', E'Writing is an important skill for academic success and professional development. Some tips for improving writing skills include practicing regularly, seeking out feedback from peers or instructors, and reading widely to develop a strong foundation in grammar, syntax, and style. Additionally, developing strong writing skills can help students in a wide range of careers, from journalism to marketing to law.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('aaf99872-23ca-52d7-b573-183b5db10210'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aaf99872-23ca-52d7-b573-183b5db10210'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urban Living', E'To what extent do you agree that urban living is better than rural living?', NULL, NULL, E'The debate between urban living and rural living has long been a topic of discussion, with proponents of each lifestyle advocating for its unique benefits. In considering the extent to which urban living is preferable to rural living, it is essential to examine the advantages that cities offer in terms of amenities, job opportunities, and infrastructure.\nUrban living stands out for its accessibility to a wide range of amenities, including healthcare facilities, educational institutions, and entertainment options. The concentration of services in cities ensures that residents have convenient access to quality healthcare, educational opportunities, and cultural experiences that contribute to a higher quality of life.\nMoreover, cities provide a plethora of job opportunities across various industries, offering residents a diverse range of career paths and higher earning potential compared to rural areas. The dynamic urban environment fosters innovation and entrepreneurship, attracting professionals seeking career advancement and financial stability. Additionally, the superior infrastructure, transportation networks, and connectivity in urban areas contribute to the efficiency and convenience of daily life, allowing residents to navigate the city with ease and access essential services with minimal hassle.\nIn conclusion, the advantages of urban living in terms of access to amenities, job opportunities, and infrastructure highlight the appeal of city life for many individuals. While rural living offers its own charm and tranquility, the conveniences and opportunities provided by urban areas make them an attractive choice for those seeking a vibrant and fast-paced lifestyle. Ultimately, the extent to which urban living is considered better than rural living depends on individual preferences and priorities.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('aafe43af-3d66-5119-923e-f314240952dc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aafe43af-3d66-5119-923e-f314240952dc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8b2b813c-9b33-504f-8bed-0b78255ca19c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There''s going to be a show in the main hall at school.', NULL, NULL),
