  ('aba689cb-66e1-5ab7-94c0-5eb238a76561'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aba689cb-66e1-5ab7-94c0-5eb238a76561'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Business Emission', E'An American retail giant is set to ask its suppliers to measure and report their greenhouse gas emissions. There is a need to {{1}} business emission. The {{2}} of emission can be used to test which company causes climate change, and {{3}} the government campaigners and environmental {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.disclose, 2.data, 3.conflate, 4.invigilators', NULL, NULL),
  ('aba6ab12-17fb-50ee-a568-bfe541b117a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'aba6ab12-17fb-50ee-a568-bfe541b117a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'National Services', E'As national services, which one deserves to receive more financial support, education or health?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, the controversy over whether education or healthcare should be allocated greater public financial resources has sparked intense debate and garnered widespread public attention. Advocates of educational investment assert that it lays the foundation for long-term prosperity, while proponents of healthcare contend that well-being constitutes the prerequisite of social progress. From my perspective, education merits higher fiscal priority due to its far-reaching social functions and decisive role in advancing medical innovation.\nPrimarily, education serves as an indispensable cornerstone for sustaining social stability and fostering sustainable development. By equipping individuals with knowledge, critical thinking and moral values, education cultivates responsible citizens and reduces social disparities. As Einstein profoundly remarked, “Well-educated citizens form the bedrock of a stable society”, a maxim that has guided the policy-making of countless nations. Therefore, investing in education is inherently an investment in the long-term stability and vitality of society.\nFurthermore, education acts as the primary driving force behind medical progress. Without robust educational systems, scientific research, technological breakthroughs and professional medical training would be severely restricted. Empirical studies published in Scientific American have validated that high-quality education directly propels the advancement of the healthcare industry, enabling more effective disease prevention, diagnosis and treatment. Evidently, the improvement of public health is ultimately rooted in educational development.\nIn conclusion, I firmly maintain that education deserves greater financial support than healthcare. Only by prioritising education can societies achieve enduring stability, continuous innovation and comprehensive advancement in public health.', NULL, 200, 300),
