  ('abe60e9b-394f-5686-8dd1-60696110a605'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abe60e9b-394f-5686-8dd1-60696110a605'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Science and Scientist', NULL, '6dc0209f-10f6-52f8-8094-1c488f565339'::uuid, NULL, E'Female: Which one are you going to write more in your book, science or scientists?\nMale: I do want very much to write something about science, actually. So I prefer to scientists.\nFemale: All right. What''s interesting in scientists then?\nMale: Science is just like complex furniture, which is all about evidence. But scientists can tell stories, do researches and propose questions to find what is true. They are like a focal point. They are always in interesting situations.\nFemale: Whether science or scientists your book mainly about, it seems to be rather hard for general readers to understand, doesn''t it?\nMale: I don''t think so, really. In fact the book I write is a science fiction, which is related with science but is not strictly scientific. So you don''t have to have a PhD degree in physics or other disciplines to understand a science fiction. And loving science is very different from being a scientist, which means fiction writing is not the same as writing scientific journals. When scientists fail, they will question the situation about why they have failed. But as a fiction writer, I don''t have to. In my book, you can always see stories about ''happy family''.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('abe6fc5f-cd7b-55ec-8472-ab3b09c3d0f4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abe6fc5f-cd7b-55ec-8472-ab3b09c3d0f4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skin Lesions', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('abea8653-5f03-507a-9517-63d788267ccf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abea8653-5f03-507a-9517-63d788267ccf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How would you describe an economy that is largely based on farming?', 'a641e34f-c133-5a36-8600-a8bd7d0e1d61'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Agricultural / Rural', NULL, NULL),
  ('abed8a28-4da1-5be7-ba8e-86b27610427c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abed8a28-4da1-5be7-ba8e-86b27610427c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '41a555c3-47d7-5b2e-9e6f-501e38e8b43c'::uuid, NULL, E'To be precise, your assignments need an abstract at the beginning.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('abee2915-6377-5d58-a331-8e2e4b52f59f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abee2915-6377-5d58-a331-8e2e4b52f59f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Desert Ants', E'There comes a time in a desert ant''s life when a piece of food is too large to ignore, but too heavy to lift, and the only way to get it home is to adopt a new style of walking.\nThe long-legged and speedy Cataglyphis fortis normally covers ground with a three-legged stride that moves two legs forwards on one side, and one on the other. For the next step, the insect mirrors the move with {{1}} other three legs.\nBut recordings of ants in the Tunisian desert reveal that when faced with oversized lumps of food 10 times their own weight, the forward ''tripod'' walking style is {{2}} . Unable to lift the morsels in their mandibles, the ants drag the food backwards instead, moving all six legs independently. ''This is the first time we {{3}} this in any ants,'' said lead author Sarah Pfeffer at the University of Ulm in Germany.\nThe ants'' long legs already help keep their bodies away from the {{4}} desert floor and enable them to speed around at up to 60 cm per second.\nThe researchers, who publish the findings on ant locomotion and navigation in the Journal of Experimental Biology, believe that robotics will be one of the first technologies {{5}} from the discovery.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.its, 2.abandoned, 3.have seen, 4.scorching, 5.to benefit', NULL, NULL),
  ('abee6628-f8b1-50d7-837e-52b852eb4cfa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abee6628-f8b1-50d7-837e-52b852eb4cfa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the combat sport of Japanese origin where competitors use throwing and grappling techniques?', '6a2b0206-5455-5d68-830d-03eaad803514'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Judo', NULL, NULL),
  ('abf36a56-67b4-5d65-992c-2a1167733dfd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abf36a56-67b4-5d65-992c-2a1167733dfd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Inquisitive and Eager', E'Children are naturally inquisitive and eager to learn about the world around them. It is essential to create educational environments that {{1}} their innate curiosity and encourage a love for learning. Educators and schools should strive to {{2}} a curriculum that not only imparts knowledge but also fosters critical thinking, problem-solving, and creativity. These skills empower children to navigate an ever-changing world. In addition to traditional classroom learning, hands-on experiences and interactive activities can {{3}} children''s understanding of complex concepts. Field trips, experiments, and collaborative projects can make learning engaging and memorable. Furthermore, it is crucial to acknowledge that every child is unique, with their own learning pace and style. Educators must {{4}} the diversity of learners and provide personalized support to help each child reach their full potential.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.stimulate, 2.implement, 3.enhance, 4.recognize', NULL, NULL),
  ('abf63832-b5cd-5c77-b3d5-65886a5019fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abf63832-b5cd-5c77-b3d5-65886a5019fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Economics', E'Economics is the study of choices. Though some believe that economics is driven purely by money or capital, the choice is much more {{1}} . If the study of economics is the study of how people choose to use their resources, analysts must also consider all of their possible resources, of which money is but one. In practice, resources can {{2}} everything from time to knowledge and property to tools. As such, economics helps illustrate how people interact within the market to {{3}} their diverse goals. Beyond defining what these resources are, the concept of scarcity is also an important consideration. These resources — no matter how broad the category — are limited, which is the source of tension in the choices people and society make: Their decisions are a result of the {{4}} tug of war between unlimited wants and desires and limited resources.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.expansive, 2.encompass, 3.realize, 4.constant', NULL, NULL),
  ('abf90bd2-a23e-5fa1-838b-4aa6e4967aae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abf90bd2-a23e-5fa1-838b-4aa6e4967aae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sales Jobs', E'Sales jobs allow for a {{1}} deal of discretionary time and effort on the part of the sales representatives - especially when compared with managerial, manufacturing, and service jobs. Most sales representatives work independently and outside the immediate presence of their sales managers. Therefore, some form of goals needs to be in place {{2}} their performance. Sales personnel are not the only professionals with performance goals or quotas. Health care professionals operating in clinics have daily, weekly, and monthly goals in terms of patient visits. Service personnel are assigned a number of service calls they {{3}} during a set time period. Production workers in manufacturing have output goals. So, why is achieving sales goals or quotas such a big deal? The answer to this question can be found by examining how a firm''s other departments are affected by how well the company''s salespeople achieve their performance goals. The success of the business {{4}} the successful sales of its products and services. Consider all the planning, the financial, production and marketing efforts that go into {{5}} the sales force sells. Everyone depends on the sales force to sell the company''s products and services and they eagerly anticipate knowing things are going.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.great, 2.to help motivate and guide, 3.must perform, 4.hinges on, 5.producing what', NULL, NULL),
  ('abf91866-e24c-5397-a837-1a449e33dc3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'abf91866-e24c-5397-a837-1a449e33dc3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Epigenetic_Research', NULL, '87bd8a2d-ac2c-5638-9dbc-e35823362bc1'::uuid, NULL, E'Now I like the history and one thing I want to go over briefly is a history of epigenetic research and this is from my perspective now. I got into this field in the early 90s. and what I have here is plotted publications total publications and function of time here. and on a linear graph. so what I did for this is I wanted to show that basically up untill around the year 2000. There''s an inflection point right around two thousand five right in here where it looks like basically nothing really is happening much in the field of epigenetics. To the point where it''s actually going vertical and a lot is happening in field of epigenetics. Now if you plot this rather than on linear paper semi-log paper. what you will find is that what I''m showing is an exponential growth curve for publications in the field of epigenetics. and that in the scientific community. There''s a doubling of the epigenetics papers every one and a half to two years. Last year alone we put into publication summers between fifteen and twenty thousand papers which took us 15 years from 1992 to 2005.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
