  ('afb2c20c-2479-50d0-b523-521693cc6112'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afb2c20c-2479-50d0-b523-521693cc6112'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Accent', E'"Your accent really reveals a lot about who you are and your identity. It will tell people what your native language is, be able to tell you probably where you come from." Marc Pell, a communications professor at McGill University in Montreal. And according to Pell, one reaction to a different accent can be a bias against that person.\n"Previous research that has been done elsewhere showed that people who have an accent tend to be trusted less, simply because they have an accent. But the idea that we would have a bias against anyone who sort of doesn''t sound like us I think probably relates to some sort of evolutionary or long-standing suspicion we have of outsiders or strangers. So this might be sort of an ingrained response that we have to the accent."\nBut accents aren''t the only thing we listen for when we have to decide if we trust another person. Tone of voice also plays a role. Pell and his team wanted to know if people would trust a confident tone, even if it came from someone with an accent.\n\nAccording to the passage, what can we know about accents?', '222004f4-5969-5891-ada6-c625a0ecf2de'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We may have a prejudice against people who don’t sound like us.\nAccents are not the only thing that can decide whether one is trustworthy.', NULL, NULL),
  ('afb487f7-9bc5-50d2-b698-1a0eeab6d1d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afb487f7-9bc5-50d2-b698-1a0eeab6d1d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Personal Savings', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('afb508c5-d021-5024-a7b6-47a2acd45226'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afb508c5-d021-5024-a7b6-47a2acd45226'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '84c22afc-5051-50d3-9bc3-316bfa36b974'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A few journalism students need to read the school newspaper.', NULL, NULL),
  ('afbbd159-35c1-5fea-8d30-f0d43219823a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afbbd159-35c1-5fea-8d30-f0d43219823a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cloud of Gas', E'Astronomers have recently discovered a large cloud of gas, in which many new stars are being formed, not far from our own solar system. While it would seem surprising that this phenomenon hadn’t been previously noticed, the researchers explained that recent innovations in measuring the distance of gas clouds more accurately led to this discovery after older observations were reinterpreted.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('afbd8e5c-954d-51c9-9dbc-523bfad5e268'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afbd8e5c-954d-51c9-9dbc-523bfad5e268'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we call that animals and plants preserved in the rocks?', 'd12f618c-1fec-5162-9a87-096ac72b1933'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Fossil', NULL, NULL),
  ('afc2024b-527f-512b-a47d-44f84e282446'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afc2024b-527f-512b-a47d-44f84e282446'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Baby Smell', E'That new baby smell could also serve an evolutionary purpose – for example, to help a mother identify her baby more easily, similar to how babies can identify their mothers by smell almost immediately. Several studies have shown that most mothers can identify their babies by smell alone. It may also help a woman bond to her baby.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('afc295cc-bf0a-5887-8125-83a641755a75'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afc295cc-bf0a-5887-8125-83a641755a75'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the sport where two teams try to ground a ball on the other team''s side of the net?', '6e963856-3a13-5e17-a588-9241c1dfba11'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Volleyball', NULL, NULL),
  ('afc896f1-ca84-5446-9052-56ecfc3ae078'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afc896f1-ca84-5446-9052-56ecfc3ae078'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e4b036ff-6152-50d3-a040-8f81f0bbfae9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The tests are designed by scientists to detect the disease early.', NULL, NULL),
  ('afce1a37-0a6a-59e2-b2a7-fab9eff9a76e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afce1a37-0a6a-59e2-b2a7-fab9eff9a76e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '09dc0ed1-12ab-55c8-aebe-c02d9d9af1b5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The university offers a variety of amenities for all campus users.', NULL, NULL),
  ('afd4c72d-37d4-5ad9-a89a-5d0c0b5a8b26'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afd4c72d-37d4-5ad9-a89a-5d0c0b5a8b26'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Trade-off Triangle', NULL, '485de71d-1f4b-546a-bb6b-b6d8e6e60404'::uuid, NULL, E'Well, it''s about whether you can achieve a win-win solution, whether you can achieve economic growth which brings wealth in order to cut poverty without damaging the biodiversity. And the argument is that if you want to protect biodiversity, you have to focus on that as a goal; but if you do that, you have ... you run the risk of hurting the poor and you also run the risk of inconveniencing and reducing the economic growth. We use the developed and industrialized countries to see this argument, this axis argued about with, let us say, a government wishing to start drilling for oil in place X which is full of wildlife, and wildlife conservation society is urging them not to on the grounds that it''s a wilderness refuge. We use to that debate. What I''m saying is that in the developing world there’s a third axis and it''s a complex one.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('afd72f51-0acb-50ff-8af4-3f1ef750e986'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'afd72f51-0acb-50ff-8af4-3f1ef750e986'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mittal', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 5, 2, 3, 1', NULL, NULL),
