  ('b16d5afd-fe13-51ff-aa62-852cc9c2895b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b16d5afd-fe13-51ff-aa62-852cc9c2895b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3b1a1525-c414-5310-8172-6a1b4525693f'::uuid, NULL, E'Costs can be calculated once the critical path has been established.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b16e290f-f473-5885-97ed-7e9f6243ecb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b16e290f-f473-5885-97ed-7e9f6243ecb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indian Onion', E'With its capacity for bringing down governments and scarring political careers, the onion plays an {{1}} role in Indian politics. This week, reports of rising onion prices have made front-page news and absorbed the attention of the governing elite.\nThe most {{2}} ingredient in Indian cooking, the {{3}} element with which all dishes begin and, normally, the cheapest vegetable available, the pink onion is an essential item in the shopping basket of families of all classes. But in recent weeks, the onion has started to seem an unaffordable {{4}} for India''s poor. Over the past few days, another sharp {{5}} in prices has begun to unsettle the influential urban middle classes. The sudden spike in prices has been caused by large exports to neighboring countries and a shortage of {{6}} . But the increase follows a trend of rising consumer prices across the board — from diesel fuel to cement, from milk to lentils.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.explosive, 2.vital, 3.basic, 4.luxury, 5.surge, 6.supply', NULL, NULL),
  ('b172cc5c-f81e-55ea-bccf-44bfb46c499f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b172cc5c-f81e-55ea-bccf-44bfb46c499f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '09ef0c34-c7f3-5c08-b4b2-79bb3b7ff374'::uuid, NULL, E'You must take three core and two elective courses in this semester.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b172dd45-861a-55ec-9bc0-d57ef3576126'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b172dd45-861a-55ec-9bc0-d57ef3576126'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the large vehicle used for carrying passengers long distances, usually between cities?', '5555563c-1264-5ccb-b620-a6e43abca6e8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bus', NULL, NULL),
  ('b17320a3-00a6-580e-be65-c22c1033af24'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b17320a3-00a6-580e-be65-c22c1033af24'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Food Supply Chain', E'In normal times, the different parts of the supply chain each maintain several months'' worth of safety stock, so that they can cope with fluctuations in supply and demand. When the corona-virus crisis hit, though, those backup supplies throughout the system were used up in just 10 days, according to Baker.\nReplenishing those supplies of food has been tougher, because of the corona-virus. So far, only a few facilities actually have had to suspend operations due to COVID-19 cases among the workforce, according to Martin Bucknavage, a senior food safety extension associate in the food science department at Penn State University. But staying open has necessitated changes in practices that can slow down and limit output.\n"These precautions are necessary to help protect workers who may work in close proximity to each other on production/processing lines," Gregory P. Martin, a poultry extension educator for Penn State Extension, explains via email. "Hand sanitizing and donning outerwear are normal practices in food processing plants, so additional personal protection equipment would be another layer of protection for the worker."\n"It has been an adjustment for facilities to adjust, for example, to enact spacing, where possible and other precautions," Bucknavage says. "We may be able to tell more after a few more weeks regarding supply chain issues."\n"In order to keep production rolling with those added measures, many operations have simplified their product offerings, and this is one thing that is noticeable at the grocery store — less selection, for example and sizes," Bucknavage explains.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('b178b29b-9878-5870-92b5-e8aa3416a3bb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b178b29b-9878-5870-92b5-e8aa3416a3bb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we describe a person who does something at the right time?', '55729fa4-26ef-5007-be09-dc960125be3e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Punctual', NULL, NULL),
  ('b17af5d0-2708-514c-9363-573ccd4bd6f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b17af5d0-2708-514c-9363-573ccd4bd6f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sharks', E'Sharks and rays are important marine species that play a significant role in maintaining the balance of the ocean ecosystem. However, their populations have been declining due to overfishing, habitat loss, and climate change. A new study by scientists has revealed that these threatened species are being caught off the coast of northern Cyprus, posing a threat to their survival.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b17bc434-9b75-5cea-b0d5-19226f6bd6b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b17bc434-9b75-5cea-b0d5-19226f6bd6b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'bd7bd87c-94a3-579e-8e4d-54fcc5ca0240'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Competition for places in this course is fierce.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b18871cd-09b4-5869-9fc2-02821d2ff243'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b18871cd-09b4-5869-9fc2-02821d2ff243'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What stellar system do the planets, such as Saturn, Jupiter, belong to?', '99dd0f0c-b66c-5367-af01-5fef176420fd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Solar system', NULL, NULL),
  ('b189d3a9-9eb9-5517-a7d1-09dd3175c569'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b189d3a9-9eb9-5517-a7d1-09dd3175c569'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9791bacd-0499-5cc6-882e-147c58915e70'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'It might take longer to process your paperwork than normal.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1919878-3f22-5a93-895b-358a5e128190'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1919878-3f22-5a93-895b-358a5e128190'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sofia', E'Over the past eight years, a modified Boeing 747 jetliner has flown hundreds of flights on a unique mission: carrying a 19-ton telescope known as Sofia, or the Stratospheric Observatory for Infrared Astronomy. Flying a telescope on a jumbo jet offered a way to peer into the heavens at wavelengths that could not be glimpsed from the ground.\nSofia was an innovative way to gaze at the infrared universe. Infrared light is essentially heat radiation — but astronomers can’t probe cosmic objects like dust-enshrouded stars and galaxies without the water vapor in Earth’s atmosphere absorbing that light. That confounds attempts to observe those objects with telescopes built on mountaintops, like the observatories in Hawaii and Chile. But by soaring through the stratosphere, at an elevation of 40,000 feet or higher, Sofia could fly above that water vapor and get a much better view.\nThe Sofia team have made a number of significant astronomical discoveries, including measuring cosmic magnetic fields permeating nearby galaxies, charting the growth of massive stars, and even discovering water on the sunlit surface of the moon’s southern hemisphere. The data from Sofia’s final flight will map stellar nebulas and help scientists study the magnetic fields of the Sculptor starburst galaxy.\nBut while flying a telescope in a jet is much less expensive than launching one aboard a spacecraft, it’s still not cheap. There are costs for the pilots, staff, engineers, and mechanics — plus a round of repairs to the aircraft that had to be made in 2018. Sofia costs NASA about $85 million per year, and that’s actually only 80 percent of the funding it needs: NASA’s German counterparts provided the rest. It was ultimately the mission’s high operating costs, relative to its scientific output, that took Sofia down.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('b191b518-bb1f-5864-b700-60a0cba1c7e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b191b518-bb1f-5864-b700-60a0cba1c7e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Burger King', E'Drive down any highway,and you''ll see a proliferation of chain restaurants—most likely, if you travel long and far enough you''ll see McDonald''s golden arches as well as signs for Burger King, Hardee''s, and Wendy''s the ''big four'' of burgers. Despite its name, though Burger King has fallen short of {{1}} the burger crown, unable to surpass market leader McDonald''s No. 1 sales status. Always the bridesmaid and never the bride, Burger King remains No 2.\nWorse yet, Burger King has experienced a six-year 22 percent decline in customer traffic, with its overall quality rating dropping while ratings for the other three {{2}} have increased. The decline has been {{3}} to inconsistent product quality and poor customer service. Although the chain tends to throw advertising dollars at the problem, an understanding of Integrated Marketing Communication theory would suggest that internal management problems (nineteen CEOs in fifty years) need to be {{4}} before a unified, long-term strategy can be put in place.\nThe {{5}} of consistency in brand image and messages, at all levels of communication, has become a basic tenet of IMC theory and practice. The person who takes the customer''s order must communicate the same message as Burger King''s famous tagline, ''Have it your way,'' or the customer will just buzz up the highway to a chain restaurant that seems more consistent and, therefore, more {{6}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.claiming, 2.contenders, 3.attributed, 4.rectified, 5.importance, 6.reliable', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1975dd8-419c-5628-8e48-af2bd8122efa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1975dd8-419c-5628-8e48-af2bd8122efa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'In order to keep food fresh, which equipment will you use?', 'd4356c50-d9fd-5eb1-acdb-d759d9e163df'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Refrigerator / icebox / fridge', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1a713a2-fdb5-52a4-9e18-a2c5c3d19761'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1a713a2-fdb5-52a4-9e18-a2c5c3d19761'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wolf''s Perspective', E'From the wolf''s perspective, this is clearly good news. But it also had beneficial effects on the ecology of the park, according to a study published in 2004 by William Ripple and Robert Beschta from Oregon State University. In their paper in Bio Science, the two researchers showed that reintroducing the wolves was {{1}} with increased growth of willow and cottonwood in the park. Why? Because grazing animals such as elk were {{2}} sites from which they couldn''t easily escape, the scientists {{3}} . And as the woody plants and trees grew taller and thicker, beaver {{4}} expanded.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.correlated, 2.avoiding, 3.claimed, 4.colonies', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1a74182-9a9f-5c05-91a3-6f0c7ed3c20d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1a74182-9a9f-5c05-91a3-6f0c7ed3c20d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2be6fbcf-aa92-5c9a-8199-21c1d3490796'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You should provide examples to support your ideas and arguments.', NULL, NULL),
