  ('b1bdf4b2-5eba-5ad5-ab3b-62844c4e4b68'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1bdf4b2-5eba-5ad5-ab3b-62844c4e4b68'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Growth of the Internet', E'The exponential growth of the internet was {{4}} , in the 1990s, as revolutionizing the production and {{5}} of information. Some people saw the internet as a means of {{3}} access to knowledge. For people {{2}} with African development, it seemed to offer the possibility of {{1}} over the technology gap that {{6}} Africa from advanced industrialized countries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.heralded, 2.dissemination, 3.democratizing, 4.concerned, 5.leapfrogging, 6.separates', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1c2c557-cf98-5c95-a660-f570ea5349c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1c2c557-cf98-5c95-a660-f570ea5349c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Advantages of Online Education', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('b1c9613a-ce6b-59a6-982f-dd1e5ca5c0d6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b1c9613a-ce6b-59a6-982f-dd1e5ca5c0d6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Digital Age', E'Some people claim that the digital age has made us lazier, while others claim it has made us more knowledgeable. Discuss both opinions, and use examples to support them.', NULL, NULL, E'In the digital age, there are contrasting opinions regarding its impact on society. While some argue that the digital age has made us lazier, others contend that it has made us more knowledgeable. This essay will explore both perspectives, providing examples to support each viewpoint.\nThe digital age has significantly increased access to information, leading to a more knowledgeable society. With the advent of the internet, vast amounts of information are readily available at our fingertips. For instance, online platforms such as Wikipedia, scholarly databases, and educational websites provide a wealth of knowledge on various subjects. People can now easily research and learn about diverse topics, expanding their intellectual horizons.\nHowever, critics argue that the digital age has made us lazier. The convenience of digital devices and technologies has led to a sedentary lifestyle. People spend more time engaging with screens rather than participating in physical activities. For instance, instead of going out for a walk or playing sports, individuals may prefer to stay indoors and browse social media or stream movies. This lack of physical activity can lead to health issues such as obesity and cardiovascular problems.\nIn conclusion, the digital age has both positive and negative impacts on society. While it has made us more knowledgeable by increasing access to information, it has also contributed to a sedentary lifestyle. It is crucial to strike a balance between utilizing digital resources for knowledge enhancement while also maintaining an active and critical mindset. By doing so, we can harness the benefits of the digital age while mitigating its potential drawbacks.', NULL, 200, 300),
