  ('b3c70076-c2cb-5790-b964-4d5bdb4aa4cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3c70076-c2cb-5790-b964-4d5bdb4aa4cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Giant Exoplanets', E'Giant exoplanets, like the so-called ''hot Jupiters'' that are similar in {{1}} to the solar system''s biggest {{2}} and orbit very close to their host stars, are excellent targets for {{3}} in their search for their extrasolar worlds. The size and proximity of these planets is easy to {{4}} as they create a large decrease in brightness when passing in front of their parent stars.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.characteristics, 2.planet, 3.astronomers, 4.detect', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3cdd2fd-8c3e-5510-b7e7-cd5db3087cef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3cdd2fd-8c3e-5510-b7e7-cd5db3087cef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c2ec3b11-db17-5e5d-a98a-180ee4219b53'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students should register to gain access to the library printers.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3d13e41-77ff-5a75-af87-4c6eb71a7751'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3d13e41-77ff-5a75-af87-4c6eb71a7751'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '3926407d-063f-51da-bc73-ecd6b15d6ac8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'One function of body fat is to keep all internal organs warm.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3d2450b-5421-5f0f-9546-bb430615b0e5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3d2450b-5421-5f0f-9546-bb430615b0e5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a59bfe19-76d7-5058-899d-0a96b5adb01a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To achieve full marks, an appropriate bibliography is required.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3dcacb3-2b1a-52ca-a8fc-99b58f36189f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3dcacb3-2b1a-52ca-a8fc-99b58f36189f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Grouping', E'Individual humans are relatively powerless creatures: it''s what we can do as groups that has {{1}} us to take over the planet. These groupings — corporations, religions, states — are now part of a vast {{2}} network of information flows. Finding points of resistance, where smaller units can {{3}} up to the waves of information washing round the globe, is becoming harder all the time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.enabled, 2.interconnected, 3.come', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3e8f345-b2a2-5976-81f7-dad3111c4d57'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3e8f345-b2a2-5976-81f7-dad3111c4d57'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the ceremony where college students receive their degrees or diplomas?', 'a2e06fd7-2213-5934-bec7-af1ee9f81d86'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Commencement / graduation', NULL, NULL),
  ('b3ed59c6-9992-5855-9a18-e08a5eab33da'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3ed59c6-9992-5855-9a18-e08a5eab33da'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urban Planners', NULL, '4e1beaaf-ebb0-5d5a-af73-fc08b592478b'::uuid, NULL, E'Now as urban planners, what we really need to start considering is the amount of space allocated for residential areas within a city or town. And when I say ''space'' I''m talking about space within a dwelling or home rather than the actual size of residential areas. There''s growing concern that the internal space of new homes is becoming far smaller. Too small, in fact.\nMaybe you''re thinking: Is it important for residents to have sufficient space? Is it merely a preference to have more space or are there more serious implications? Is there, in fact, any evidence to suggest cramped living conditions affect residents'' physical or mental well-being or their day to day life?\nWell, research from a number of sources indicates that this is an important issue which needs addressing. Cramped conditions can lead to aggressive behaviour, to family tensions, psychological anguish and, in the more extreme cases, physical illness as well. Not only this but there is a proven link between overcrowding and the social and emotional development of children as well as their educational attainment. So, the main issue here is that residents require enough individual space to be able to live and function together but with sufficient private space for personal time within the home.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b3ef4769-f1e1-5aaa-99eb-a2261bc313d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b3ef4769-f1e1-5aaa-99eb-a2261bc313d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Central Banks', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('b406deab-3a3c-55c2-a5de-a56782c0e6a2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b406deab-3a3c-55c2-a5de-a56782c0e6a2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fb569394-830c-57c5-a875-22d452ceddbe'::uuid, NULL, E'Volunteer work can be a rewarding way to give back to the community.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b407cec9-cd0c-5f19-a15e-5d35e3ac612a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b407cec9-cd0c-5f19-a15e-5d35e3ac612a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1c525ad3-4b2b-52bd-9c59-68d566abc2c2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We will discuss these two pictures in the next lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b40a689b-3f4c-5648-9f56-d975a344c1af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b40a689b-3f4c-5648-9f56-d975a344c1af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Transplantation', NULL, '51905dab-b778-5215-b8fe-f889e0c8983a'::uuid, NULL, E'Why can’t we transplant brains? First of all, we should look at what the brain actually does. This thing inside our skulls that weighs on average about 3.3 pounds is larger in humans than any other vertebrae when compared to body weight. That’s why we are so brainy. The busy brain is our command center for our nervous system, which takes in data from our body and gives directions to our muscles. In fact, it does so much work, it requires about 20 percent of our energy to run it. When we are brain dead, we no longer have any neurological activity. With the help of machines, we can be kept alive for a short time, but within a week, the body will not be able to function. While we may still be alive in some sense for that week, we are technically dead when the brain is dead. Some good news is that during the time we are kept alive, some of our other organs can be donated. But why can’t we accept someone else’s brain? When we transplant something such as a heart, surgeons use a mechanical pump to keep blood flooding through the body while the new heart is being put in. The new heart is then connected to the major blood vessels, and this might take several hours. You’ll stay in the hospital for one to two weeks, and if your body doesn’t reject its new heart, it’s said 87 out of 100 people make it through the year, and 60 out of 100 get through another decade. So, wouldn’t it just be possible to open the skull and connect a new brain where the removed brain was connected? This question was asked to a Professor of Neurosurgery at Yale in 2013. He actually did say that one day this operation might be successful, but right now we are not even close. The reason is because it’s just too darn difficult to connect nerve fibers from the new brain to the native spinal cord. This, he said, is why spinal cord injuries can be so devastating. If we could transplant brains, we would likely not have so many people that are disabled due to spinal injuries.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b40fae2b-9386-5eb3-bd1f-d72616eb2c89'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b40fae2b-9386-5eb3-bd1f-d72616eb2c89'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b960a9aa-7f8b-5367-8133-e93b42cf1534'::uuid, NULL, E'The manager is not available so the receptionist has to handle the matter.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
