  ('b8108852-73dc-5864-a091-4b34a13db0e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8108852-73dc-5864-a091-4b34a13db0e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Spoiled Food', E'You recently bought some food from a store, but after opening it at home, you realized it was spoiled. You decide to go back to the store and speak to the manager about the issue. How would you explain the situation and request a solution?', 'e1234806-254f-5332-a612-84dec260f1dd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b812aadb-642e-58a5-a331-eef06abd6a81'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b812aadb-642e-58a5-a331-eef06abd6a81'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-L', E'So today I''m going to talk about the key things you need to remember when you go out into the world as translators. The first thing is to be choosy about what commissions you accept. It''s not advisable to agree to do every job you·re offered even if you''re in need of work. You should refuse to do something if you don''t know anything about the topic as it would be impossible for you to produce a good piece of writing. And it could be serious - a mistranslation that''s going to be used for medical or legal purposes could have disastrous consequences. Having decided you can reasonably take on a commission, if you have the slightest doubt about what something means, then consult a dictionary or someone whose mother tongue is the language you''re translating from. It''s much better to devote a bit of time and effort to checking something than to risk making a potentially serious error.\n\nWhich of these tips about doing a good translation does the speaker mention?', '417135db-8a00-5e90-8ce1-fa10aa66c13e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ask a native speaker if you are not sure of the meaning of something.\nDon''t translate technical texts unless you are familiar with the subject.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8149de5-6f0b-51ec-b607-ba565e962a6a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8149de5-6f0b-51ec-b607-ba565e962a6a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '226ce166-b419-5cb9-bb8e-117933d6a39a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Our department shares responsibilities for developing human potential and expanding knowledge.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b819991c-f3f4-5201-94db-b29019a2deea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b819991c-f3f4-5201-94db-b29019a2deea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a piece of artificial hair worn by a judge in some courts of law?', 'bc9e80cb-2d27-5d9b-a965-84b9e06f487b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hairpiece / wig', NULL, NULL),
  ('b81e1cc0-a519-54c7-b962-ef6cc72eff55'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b81e1cc0-a519-54c7-b962-ef6cc72eff55'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which one is relating to our mind, mental or physical?', '8cbb31c7-75f7-5a7d-99ad-c47f05f75945'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mental', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8202e52-fb57-5797-b18e-41827f0fd8d2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8202e52-fb57-5797-b18e-41827f0fd8d2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Doctors'' Messages', E'The messages doctors give can {{1}} some treatments'' effectiveness. For example, it seems that information from a doctor affects outcomes for migraine {{2}} — whether they got a real drug or a placebo.\nResearchers studied 66 people with recurring migraines over the course of seven attacks.\nDuring the first {{3}} , the {{4}} received no treatment. For the next six, they were given either a placebo or a drug. Each time, regardless of which they got, some were told it was the drug, some were told it was the placebo, and the rest were informed that it could be either the drug or the placebo.\nOverall, the drug did work better than the placebo. But the placebo worked, too—both when the patients were told it was a placebo, and even better when the doctors told them that they were getting the drug. That is, when the docs set their expectations high.\nMeanwhile, the actual drug was least effective when the patients thought it was a placebo. The study is in the journal Science Translational Medicine.\nThe physician''s input thus plays a role in how migraine patients fare. Tell them they''re getting a good treatment, and they''re {{5}} more likely to respond.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.influence, 2.sufferers, 3.headache, 4.patients, 5.apparently', NULL, NULL),
  ('b820e56b-f16f-54b3-877d-e83201fd958e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b820e56b-f16f-54b3-877d-e83201fd958e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Low-Earth Orbit', E'"Low-Earth orbit is now more accessible for more people to experience the wonders of space", tweeted NASA administrator Bill Nelson, who was a congressman when he hitched a ride on a space shuttle decades ago.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b820fe4d-769c-54aa-86fe-5709aff6214a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b820fe4d-769c-54aa-86fe-5709aff6214a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '881f245f-0300-5af5-90d5-7bc065341738'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A world-renowned expert on financial management will give a guest lecture.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b82e6e6f-1b97-52b2-8bea-994fb40836f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b82e6e6f-1b97-52b2-8bea-994fb40836f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2677f406-4e66-5899-9502-2f55f77034ae'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Right now, we don''t have enough evidence to support these claims.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b82eab79-82e3-543e-8701-aa1dc4baa0f4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b82eab79-82e3-543e-8701-aa1dc4baa0f4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Leisure Activity', E'To what extent do you think that hobbies and leisure activities contribute to personal growth?', NULL, NULL, E'Hobbies and leisure activities are not just idle pastimes; they are powerful tools that contribute significantly to personal growth. This article delves into the impact of engaging in such pursuits on individual development.\nParticipating in hobbies offers a unique avenue for self-discovery and exploration. Whether it''s painting, hiking, or learning a new language, these activities provide opportunities to uncover hidden talents and passions. Through this process, individuals gain a deeper understanding of themselves, fostering personal growth and self-awareness. Exploring diverse interests not only enriches one''s life experiences but also nurtures personal development by encouraging continuous learning and self-improvement.\nMoreover, hobbies serve as effective stress relievers and promoters of mental well-being. Activities like gardening, yoga, or playing a musical instrument offer moments of relaxation and escape from daily pressures. By engaging in enjoyable pastimes, individuals can alleviate stress, enhance their mood, and boost their overall mental health. This aspect of hobbies contributes significantly to personal growth by fostering emotional resilience and maintaining a healthy work-life balance.\nIn conclusion, the impact of hobbies and leisure activities on personal growth is profound. From facilitating self-discovery and stress reduction to promoting skill development and emotional well-being, these pursuits play a crucial role in shaping individuals into well-rounded and fulfilled beings. Embracing hobbies not only enhances one''s quality of life but also propels them towards continuous growth and self-improvement.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('b82f7ec6-6ffc-59ec-927b-470049e3dab2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b82f7ec6-6ffc-59ec-927b-470049e3dab2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Diamonds, an occasional component of rare igneous rocks called lamproites and kimberlites, have never been dated satisfactorily. However, some diamonds contain minute inclusions of silicate minerals, commonly olivine, pyroxene, and garnet. These minerals can be dated by radioactive decay techniques because of the very small quantities of radioactive trace elements they, in turn, contain. Usually, it is possible to conclude that the inclusions are older than their diamond hosts, but with little indication of the time interval involved. Sometimes, however, the crystal form of the silicate inclusions is observed to resemble more closely the internal structure of diamond than that of other silicate minerals. It is not known how rare this resemblance is, or whether it is most often seen in inclusions of silicates such as garnet, whose crystallography is generally somewhat similar to that of diamond; but when present, the resemblance is regarded as compelling evidence that the diamonds and inclusions are truly cogenetic.\n\nAccording to the passage, the age of silicate minerals included in diamonds can be determined due to a feature of the', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'trace elements in the silicate minerals', NULL, NULL),
  ('b83133d9-7cc4-51df-b584-b7a16a987324'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b83133d9-7cc4-51df-b584-b7a16a987324'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ddd8756e-67ae-5e46-81dc-50d236fd563d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The winter sun is still sufficient for warmth despite its position.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b832dc7b-9989-512f-90d7-ad53f9c7dce6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b832dc7b-9989-512f-90d7-ad53f9c7dce6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e6fad5c0-e51f-57d3-b6b9-6dc8a80e9648'::uuid, NULL, E'There are hundreds of clubs and societies to choose from.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b837547b-8293-5550-9ae5-21f26a7b50f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b837547b-8293-5550-9ae5-21f26a7b50f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DNA and Crime', E'The presence or {{1}} of DNA evidence at a crime scene could mean the difference between a guilty {{2}} and an acquittal. DNA is so important that the United States government has spent {{3}} amounts of money to unravel the sequence of DNA in the human genome in hopes of understanding and finding cures for many {{4}} diseases.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.absence, 2.verdict, 3.enormous, 4.genetic', NULL, NULL),
  ('b83a3ecf-00c8-5b64-990c-3b5ec6a0e331'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b83a3ecf-00c8-5b64-990c-3b5ec6a0e331'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Christmas Cards', E'A few years ago, a university professor tried a little experiment. He sent Christmas cards to a sample of perfect strangers. Although he expected some reaction, the {{1}} he received was amazing — holiday cards {{2}} to him came pouring back from the people who had never met nor heard of him. The great majority of those who returned a card never inquired {{3}} the identity of the unknown professor. They received his holiday greeting card, and they automatically sent one in return. This study shows the action of one of the most powerful of the weapons of influence around us — the rule for {{4}} . The rule says that we should try to repay, in kind, what another person has provided us. If a woman does us a favor, we should do her one in return; if a man sends us a birthday present, we should remember his birthday with a gift of our own; if a couple invites us to a party, we should be sure to invite them to one of ours.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.response, 2.addressed, 3.into, 4.reciprocation', NULL, NULL),
  ('b83f3ec0-2b8c-5ceb-908f-309d7d69e898'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b83f3ec0-2b8c-5ceb-908f-309d7d69e898'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Daniel Harris', E'Daniel Harris, a scholar of consumption and style, has observed that until photography did finally {{1}} illustration as the "primary means of {{2}} clothing" in the 1950s, glamour inhered {{3}} in the face of the drawing, which was by necessity schematic and generalized, than in the sketch''s {{4}} , posture, and gestures, especially in the strangely dainty positions of the hands. Glamour once resided so emphatically in the stance of the model that the faces in the illustrations cannot really be said to have {{5}} at all, but angles or tilts. The chin raised upwards in a haughty look; the eyes lowered in an attitude of introspection; the head cocked at an inquisitive or coquettish angle: or the profile presented in sharp outline, emanating power of the severity like an emperor''s bust {{6}} on a Roman coin.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.supplant, 2.advertising, 3.less, 4.attitude, 5.expressions, 6.embossed', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8473b78-31fa-59da-92c8-05a0d49ebe35'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8473b78-31fa-59da-92c8-05a0d49ebe35'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Interior Design', E'Interior design is a professionally conducted, practice-based process of planning and realization of interior spaces and the elements within. Interior design is {{2}} to the function and operation of the aesthetics and its {{3}} . The work of an interior designer draws upon many other {{1}} , such as environmental psychology, architecture, product design and, aesthetics, in relation to a wide range of building spaces including hotels, corporate and public spaces, schools, hospitals, private residences, shopping malls, restaurants, theaters and airport terminals. As modern spaces grow more interconnected, interior design is an {{4}} part of creating environments that serve both practical and emotional needs. With shifts in lifestyle and technology, the core focus of interior design has {{5}} dramatically in recent years.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.related, 2.sustainability, 3.disciplines, 4.integral, 5.altered', NULL, NULL),
  ('b84b50bc-11a6-5038-9d55-81bea617a52d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b84b50bc-11a6-5038-9d55-81bea617a52d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f7e7434a-fd74-583b-a116-d759e71ef0a6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You can then reach a conclusion based on common knowledge.', NULL, NULL),
