  ('b8ed97b9-d368-508d-be17-a97c9187464f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8ed97b9-d368-508d-be17-a97c9187464f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c3d4da43-ab96-523b-ac97-79d3550e573e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students live in the hall of residence during term time.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8fbd340-dbcc-5a87-9ba2-82bbef2db86c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8fbd340-dbcc-5a87-9ba2-82bbef2db86c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Winter', E'This winter has been rather cold. It almost feels like we''re entering a new ice age. Now don''t laugh. This statement isn''t as crazy as it seems. Yes. Global warming is a uh, hot topic these days, but more and more scientists are considering the possibility of global cooling occurring soon. This would result in the average temperatures on earth dropping. It has happened in the past, and it will happen again in the future. Earth is warm now, but that''s not always the case. In the past, large parts of the planet were covered in ice. We call these periods ice ages. Note the plural. There wasn''t just one ice age. There have been several. During the recent past. We experienced the little ice age. It lasted almost five hundred years from around, um, say thirteen hundred to eighteen hundred. The ice pack in the arctic ocean grew larger and moved south. Glaciers in the european alps and on greenland grew bigger and advance southward temperatures dropped all over the northern hemisphere. Winters were longer, summers were shorter, and summer rains were heavier. There were numerous famines since the cold and rain frequently destroyed crops. Why did this ice age and others like it happen? One theory claims that earth''s orbit caused them. Earth orbit changes slightly over time, so the northern hemisphere receives less sunlight on those occasions. This reduces temperatures. IT''s possible that an orbITal change caused the major ice ages. In case you''re curious. The last such ice age happened around twenty thousand years ago. How often does earth''s orbit change? No one knows for sure. Scientists estimated changes between every twenty thousand to fifty thousand years. There''s also a second possible reason for global cooling. This relates to decreased solar activity. The appearance or lack of sunspots can affect temperatures here on earth. During the little ice age, there were significantly fewer sunspots. For instance, in one thirty year period, astronomers spotted a few dozens on spots. Normally, they would have seen tens of thousands of them with less solar activity. Some believe temperatures on earth decreased, thereby resulting in colder weather.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '8bbf8806-3a5a-50ca-9232-e5fb03bf6334'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Global cooling has taken place on Earth in the past and the Little Ice Age lasted from around 1300 to 1800. Some scientists think changes in Earth’s orbit make the temperature drop, and a lack of sunspots might affect temperatures on Earth.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8fc0d97-492b-5ea4-ae0e-1562a76ad12f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8fc0d97-492b-5ea4-ae0e-1562a76ad12f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which ancient civilization is known for creating the Olympic Games?', '478b6c16-d2ed-584c-a685-6799bf1938ae'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Greek', NULL, NULL),
  ('b8fe6c04-7a7d-5b9c-9059-4c10dc6440aa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b8fe6c04-7a7d-5b9c-9059-4c10dc6440aa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '080176f2-5e0b-52cb-98fa-ffb6909db75c'::uuid, NULL, E'The office opens on Mondays and Thursdays directly following the freshman seminar.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b9034e86-06c9-575b-98a1-acb7b2596183'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9034e86-06c9-575b-98a1-acb7b2596183'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Paraphrasing (B)', E'We define paraphrasing as putting a passage from an author into your own words. However, what are your own words? How different must your paraphrase be from the {{1}} ? The answer is it should be considerably different. The {{2}} point of paraphrasing is to show you have read and understood another person''s ideas, and can summarize them in your own writing style rather than {{3}} their phrases. If you just change a few words, or add some bits of your own to an {{4}} reproduced passage, you will probably be penalized for {{5}} . You should aim to condense and {{6}} a writer''s ideas and describe them {{7}} different sentence structures and expressions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.original, 2.whole, 3.borrowing, 4.otherwise, 5.plagiarism, 6.simplify, 7.using', NULL, NULL),
  ('b9058bbe-16c8-56b8-a379-6ab210526166'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9058bbe-16c8-56b8-a379-6ab210526166'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0e193b15-7b49-5232-829a-1bbd5e9819a5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The professor is taking a sabbatical to focus on her publication.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b914ea5d-f088-521d-8bd9-b30151533724'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b914ea5d-f088-521d-8bd9-b30151533724'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solar Energy', E'Solar energy is an excellent source of supplying power to homes and companies and by utilizing solar power you’re not merely protecting the environment from becoming polluted but also you are saving the rest of the earth’s natural resources. Capturing solar energy does not contribute to any pollution and does not harm the atmosphere. One of the factors why many individuals are still hesitant to make use of solar power is because it is expensive. The need of big location of space is another reason why people aren’t taking into consideration solar power.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b916a931-3820-5625-aef3-1b7db8fea446'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b916a931-3820-5625-aef3-1b7db8fea446'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd681a0d1-63e6-50f7-94d4-84a0a2602284'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The lecture will cover the reason of climate change.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b9181936-c830-5263-9cd1-7198c3538794'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9181936-c830-5263-9cd1-7198c3538794'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '25572cdc-0709-5ce3-95f4-c8e9ed95bb61'::uuid, NULL, E'It is interesting to observe the development of language skills of toddlers.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b9200028-d899-5fec-9894-f6519bf0896f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9200028-d899-5fec-9894-f6519bf0896f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the number obtained by dividing one number by another?', '272599f1-9905-50cf-bd69-04c954609978'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Quotient', NULL, NULL),
  ('b9248632-49b5-5a9a-9adf-e26973f66fce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9248632-49b5-5a9a-9adf-e26973f66fce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Women’s Equality Day', E'The fight for women’s rights has taken many forms throughout history and takes many forms today. In the US today, the fight for abortion access is a key piece of the fight for women’s rights. At the same time, women of color are still fighting against forced and coerced sterilization. While many fight against the sexualization of women in the workplace, a simultaneous fight for sex women’s rights is being fought. Concepts like solidarity and intersectionality can help us to connect these different struggles together under the umbrellas of feminism and women’s liberation. Through these frameworks we can understand that different women are involved in different struggles, that all contribute to our collective freedom.\nThere are many national and global acknowledgements of women and the struggles they face. Women’s Equality Day is an effort unique to the United States, one that recognizes the progress that has been made towards a more equitable state and the work that is left to do.\nWomen’s Equality Day is an annual recognition of the political and social fight women from all walks of life launched to secure voting rights for women in the United States. In addition to recognizing the so-called suffragette movement, this day of celebration and reflection has evolved to recognize the ongoing fight for women’s rights in the United States.\nWomen’s Equality Day happens on August 26th each year. Back in 1920, on this same date, the U.S. Secretary of State signed a proclamation that made the 19th Amendment to the Constitution law. The 19th Amendment gives women the legal right to vote.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('b9253883-4f9a-53fc-b0e2-bfba67a42826'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9253883-4f9a-53fc-b0e2-bfba67a42826'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '01cc70e0-6971-5354-b261-a49127025985'::uuid, NULL, E'You should study this document with the utmost care.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b92888e7-3a4c-595c-9bac-8bab7793ca53'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b92888e7-3a4c-595c-9bac-8bab7793ca53'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is vaccine used for?', '111293bc-250c-589d-b43b-4a79c56cf49a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Prevent disease', NULL, NULL),
  ('b92c9d01-9d7d-5fc4-bed1-fc7face04317'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b92c9d01-9d7d-5fc4-bed1-fc7face04317'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fa29ec60-31af-581f-8b55-ebaf5f6c196a'::uuid, NULL, E'Please remain seated after finishing your exam.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b92e6f22-0978-5192-88ac-23eb9a831e1a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b92e6f22-0978-5192-88ac-23eb9a831e1a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Consumer Behavior', E'A common way for marketers to think about consumer behavior today is as a set of activities a person goes through in order to solve problems. This problem-solving process is {{1}} when a consumer identifies some unmet need. For instance, a family {{2}} all of the milk in the house, or a birthday party is coming up and a gift is needed, or a soccer team is planning an end-of-season picnic. Each buying {{3}} presents a problem the buyer must solve. These problems can involve two types of needs: physical (such as a need for milk, a birthday gift, or picnic food) or {{4}} (for example, the need to feel secure, the need to be loved, or the need to have fun).', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.triggered, 2.consumes, 3.scenario, 4.psychological', NULL, NULL),
  ('b9343931-b243-5ead-a139-dba0714bc42e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9343931-b243-5ead-a139-dba0714bc42e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c2a48780-3c25-550e-9af2-1b74724b85c4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Studying philosophy can help learners think in new ways.', NULL, NULL),
