  ('b93bb1fb-71d4-555d-87bd-6bd56d7f2adc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b93bb1fb-71d4-555d-87bd-6bd56d7f2adc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5f5a2ebb-b446-5fae-a656-e06141a17f46'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The final election results will be announced on next Friday.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b93c42bb-de5b-5894-862e-d108c4f48fac'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b93c42bb-de5b-5894-862e-d108c4f48fac'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'HCS', E'I actually think we oftentimes confused skills and skills development with education. An education is actually designed to actually encourage the individual to consider questions they hadn’t considered before, to actually be able to assemble a vast array of information and then to synthesize that information and to come up with perhaps what one would think of as new answers. It’s not about learning the most recent technique. And the challenge is that if you only talk about skills development the way knowledge is produced these days a generation is 18 months. And so that means by the time you’ve actually finished school oftentimes you’re already behind the curve and some of that information is obsolete. If you’re really truly educated you then learn and you know how to go about pursuing the new acquisition of information and that information that you can then synthesize and apply to what you already know means then that you’re not behind the curve, you’re keeping pace with the change that’s always occurring in both technology and other aspects of American life.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '6f7768e4-335c-53ae-9ad1-db8a2046216f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Education is not about learning the most recent technique, but is to encourage people to synthesize the information they’ve learned and come up with their own answers. Otherwise you may be behind the curve of new information.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b93f7967-84a8-5212-bd23-9f2dd377621e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b93f7967-84a8-5212-bd23-9f2dd377621e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Christmas Tree', E'Decorating those lush evergreen trees during the jolly holiday season has been a tradition with serious history when it {{1}} to Christmas celebrations. Around the 16th century, people in Germany started this practice of the Christmas tree, and now it has become a {{2}} symbol of the holiday season. You can’t miss it – it’s in homes, public spaces, and city centers all over the place. Families get together and pick out that perfect Christmas tree, turning it into a whole bonding experience. Then, they decorate it with glittering lights, colorful ornaments, and an elegant tree topper, making it the focal point of all their activities and {{3}} all those warm, cheerful holiday emotions. {{4}} looking all kinds of fabulous, the Christmas tree carries a ton of cultural weight, reflecting traditions and rituals linked to the holiday season.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.comes, 2.universal, 3.evoking, 4.Apart from', NULL, NULL),
  ('b94001a3-6e5e-5ce3-b1ad-05e993b38155'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b94001a3-6e5e-5ce3-b1ad-05e993b38155'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the bone structure that protects the brain?', 'a0eac889-6a5a-59ad-89ef-f976c013787c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Skull / cranium', NULL, NULL),
  ('b9459639-5de2-544e-b9d6-e19cc54250e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b9459639-5de2-544e-b9d6-e19cc54250e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Warm Weather', E'It is in the southern coast lands that the climate has the greatest impact on human geography. There are several factors which affect human activity, humid subtropical climate, a long growing season, mild winter temperatures, and warm, humid summers. There are nine months or more of potential growth for agricultural crops for almost the whole region of the southern coast lands. The average annual rainfall is more than 125 centimeters, mostly between April and October. When warm temperatures support plant growth and sunlight is plentiful, it is enough rain for most agricultural activities for almost the entire region. These climatic conditions have brought forth two important results. Farmers can grow their crops until late in the fall without fear of frost, as long as agricultural conditions are met. I mean as long as there are fertile soil control of insect pests and appropriate ground drainage, it has even been possible to harvest two crops, and sometimes more for vegetable farmers. Of greater importance is the fact that there is the chance to produce specialty crops that cannot be produced in other parts of the united states.\n\nAccording to the lecture, what are the main consequences of the warm weather and a lot of rainfall in the Southern Coastlands?', '916a0003-8d2d-52b8-9d26-a8094210c732'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'People in the region can grow crops more than once in a year.\nPeople in the region can grow specialty crops.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b94f18da-2bb9-5da5-a746-eeb44397f78d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b94f18da-2bb9-5da5-a746-eeb44397f78d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '395dc0e4-2d76-58ee-b1e2-29564258a76d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The glittering of the lake surface camouflages the fish.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b94f2b3a-0dbf-511d-b09e-f3385d555d30'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b94f2b3a-0dbf-511d-b09e-f3385d555d30'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Deepest Lake', E'Lake Baikal is located in southern Russia, near the border of Mongolia. Its depth of 5,300 feet makes it the world''s deepest lake. The second-deepest lake, Lake Tanganyika in east Africa, is 4,710 feet deep by comparison. Crater Lake, the deepest lake in the U.S., is 1,900 feet deep.\nLake Baikal''s 12,200-square-mile size also makes it Earth''s largest. That size, by the way, makes it comparable in volume to the entire Amazon basin. For scale, it reportedly takes about 330 years for one water molecule to flow from inlet to inlet.\nSo how did Lake Baikal get so massive? About 25 million years ago, Lake Baikal formed through fractures and shifting within Earth''s crust. It wasn''t Lake Baikal as we now know it, though. Experts believe it was a series of lakes, similar to the Great Lakes in the U.S. While scientists aren''t positive how Lake Baikal went from many lakes to the behemoth it is today, they do have theories. It could''ve been sinking earth, erosion, earthquakes, increased water from melting glaciers, although it''s likely a mix of these factors and more.\nNow, that unifying change took place in the Pliocene Epoch (about 5.3 to 2.5 million years ago), but this lake is hardly finished growing. It''s expanding at a rate of 0.7 inches every year, the same speed at which Africa and South America are drifting apart. At this speed, some scientists believe Lake Baikal is actually an ocean in the making.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('b951fc6e-88d9-5c79-9733-c967355ecc1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b951fc6e-88d9-5c79-9733-c967355ecc1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f546283c-c437-5929-ba71-f86ef2a97c3b'::uuid, NULL, E'The team carried out a thorough inspection of the project.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b95885a9-d232-5132-8108-9bffc30e8876'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b95885a9-d232-5132-8108-9bffc30e8876'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd0498052-da5d-5e8d-a519-e83102b9c138'::uuid, NULL, E'London evolved into a powerful, prosperous city over several centuries.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b95c2cbd-d668-5e86-b79d-ce583bfb1655'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b95c2cbd-d668-5e86-b79d-ce583bfb1655'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Agrarian Parties', E'Agrarian parties are political parties chiefly representing the interests of peasants or, more broadly, the rural sector of society. The extent to which they are important, or {{4}} they even exist, depends mainly {{6}} two factors.\nOne, obviously, is the size of an identifiable peasantry, or the size of the rural relative {{2}} the urban population. The other is a matter of social integration: {{3}} agrarian parties to be important, the representation of countryside or peasantry must not be integrated {{1}} the other major sections of society. Thus a country might possess a sizeable rural population, but have an economic system in which the interests of the voters were predominantly related to their incomes, {{7}} their occupations or location; and in such a country the political system would be unlikely to include an important agrarian party.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.whether, 2.on, 3.to, 4.for, 5.with, 6.rather than', NULL, NULL),
  ('b962ae14-c228-5b6a-96ed-ae46144bbd20'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'b962ae14-c228-5b6a-96ed-ae46144bbd20'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5b383a50-2c52-5f47-9d01-7eae1bb6af74'::uuid, NULL, E'The scholarship is now encouraging applications from students who take undergraduate programs.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
