  ('badd9bbc-c1bf-52ba-8ebb-981ba39d7754'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'badd9bbc-c1bf-52ba-8ebb-981ba39d7754'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Part-time Jobs', E'Students are increasingly finding it necessary to obtain employment in order to subsidize their income during their time in higher education. The {{1}} income helps to pay for necessities, to maintain a social life and to buy clothes, and holding a part-time job helps students to {{2}} skills for life after university or college. Using a part-time job to cut down on borrowing is a sound investment, as it reduces the {{3}} that will be waiting to be paid off after graduation. How many hours students are currently working each week during term-time is not really certain. Some institutions advise that students should not work more than ten hours a week, and there are others that set a higher recommend {{4}} of fifteen hours a week. There is no doubt that some students {{5}} even fifteen hours a week.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.extra, 2.gain, 3.debt, 4.limit, 5.exceed', NULL, NULL),
  ('badf8708-817f-5e2f-a0eb-0ff18ebc5e65'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'badf8708-817f-5e2f-a0eb-0ff18ebc5e65'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9cd1ba3b-6c3f-5249-81a4-108dfd492d09'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The essay will be published once the research is finished.', NULL, NULL),
  ('bae361e6-5bed-5114-9ff4-38ff5f5ae849'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bae361e6-5bed-5114-9ff4-38ff5f5ae849'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the hardest natural substance on Earth?', 'f09ea409-eedf-5745-bc73-64b691eaf79c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Diamond', NULL, NULL),
  ('bae3bb14-560e-5b0f-968a-8fb2b7c16ad9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bae3bb14-560e-5b0f-968a-8fb2b7c16ad9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b5966225-f823-5cba-aa71-91870c8a6335'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The gap between the rich and the poor does not decrease.', NULL, NULL),
  ('baea174a-7786-51b8-8f2c-9ba9592e9bf1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'baea174a-7786-51b8-8f2c-9ba9592e9bf1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Armor', NULL, 'd5db0730-c01d-5833-81de-f1afdf7e81f7'::uuid, NULL, E'Hello, I''m David Brown, curator of Italian and Spanish paintings at the National Gallery of Art. The treasures in our exhibition, The Art of Power, Royal Armor and Portraits from Imperial Spain, come from the royal armory in Madrid. They range from the 15th to the 17th century and include some of the finest examples of Renaissance armor in the world. Fabricated by master craftsmen and artists, the shields, helmets and armor were made for Holy Roman emperors, kings, and the flower of Spanish royalty. This is parade armor, made for show, not combat. In form, it looks back to a world tournaments, jousts and noble gesture. And among the images worked into the steel is something quite different, a subtle advertising campaign for the imperial ambitions of the Spanish monarchy and the Hapsburg dynasty. Those who wore it took the words Holy, Roman and Empire very seriously.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('baecd8c6-6b3a-578e-a8fb-49506f49f90e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'baecd8c6-6b3a-578e-a8fb-49506f49f90e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wine''s Price and Quality', E'One experiment in Australia showed that people rated the same wine higher when they thought it was $53 rather than $16 or $6. But get this, the experimenters had actually made that wine objectively worse by adding tartaric acid. It didn’t matter — the price tag overwhelmed their taste buds. In another study, scientists scanned the brains of people tasting wines that they thought were either $10 or $90. In reality, it was the same wine, but when they thought it was expensive, their brains showed more activity in a region associated with pleasant tastes and smells. So expensive wines may actually taste...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'd8d6ba99-d5b2-531e-addd-a14d86af4af2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'better', NULL, NULL),
  ('bb00b848-084b-56c0-9d73-cc775b96983f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb00b848-084b-56c0-9d73-cc775b96983f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Extending Life Expectancy', E'Medical technology is responsible for increasing the average life expectancy. Do you think it is a curse or a blessing?', NULL, NULL, E'The advancement of medical technology has led to remarkable improvements in healthcare and has significantly contributed to the increase in average life expectancy. I am of the view that the benefits of this trend far outweigh any potential drawbacks.\nOne key reason for embracing the positive impact of increased life expectancy through medical technology is the considerable improvement in the quality of life for individuals. Medical advancements have enabled the prevention and treatment of numerous diseases that were once fatal or severely limiting. People can now lead healthier and more active lives well into their later years, free from the constraints of chronic illnesses that previously curtailed their daily activities. This not only benefits the individuals themselves but also contributes to a more vibrant and engaged aging population.\nAnother compelling reason to view the rise in life expectancy as positive is the potential for increased societal progress and the accumulation of wisdom. Longer lifespans provide individuals with more time to contribute to various fields, share their experiences, and participate in social, economic, and scientific advancements. This prolonged engagement in society fosters innovation and allows for the transfer of knowledge from one generation to the next. The collective wisdom accumulated over extended lifetimes can drive positive change and inspire future generations.\nIn conclusion, the increase in average life expectancy brought about by medical technology is undeniably beneficial. The improvements in the quality of life. As we continue to embrace and advance medical technology, we pave the way for a brighter and healthier future for generations to come.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('bb01e8b4-d10b-5dd8-94b4-27b58a6260c3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb01e8b4-d10b-5dd8-94b4-27b58a6260c3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rodents', E'Rodents are the workhorses of biomedical labs. So it''s important to know if they''re {{1}} out, which could affect results. Now we know that lab rodents may be regularly exposed to a big stressor: men.\nResearchers noticed that mice showed a lower pain {{2}} —a sign of stress—when a human was present. So they put mice and rats into clear cubicles, where their faces were visible, and {{3}} them with an irritant. The rodents expressed pain through grimacing when no humans were nearby. But when confronted with a male researcher, or even just his {{4}} T-shirt, the animals grimaced less.\nFemale observers did not get the same rodent {{5}} .\nTurns out that smelling a human male made rodents produce higher levels of a stress hormone and increase their body {{6}} . That stress response also blunted their sensitivity to pain. The study is in the journal Nature Methods.\nResearchers may have to come up with ways to ward off the stress effects of male researchers. Because to a rodent, men smell like hell.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.stressed, 2.response, 3.injected, 4.odoriferous, 5.reaction, 6.temperature', NULL, NULL),
  ('bb1251ee-d3ab-53a2-85dd-bfd55d75d58b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb1251ee-d3ab-53a2-85dd-bfd55d75d58b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9fadf748-5dde-5510-896c-710ce3a32e05'::uuid, NULL, E'Somehow they had managed to escape the forest fire.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('bb195283-47e7-5d94-9dd6-bf31e101133d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb195283-47e7-5d94-9dd6-bf31e101133d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Weathering of Rocks', E'The weathering of rocks {{1}} through both physical and chemical processes. Physical weathering is the breakdown of rock into smaller pieces without altering the chemical {{2}} of the rock. Chemical weathering occurs when the breakdown of rock {{3}} from chemical change in the rock, or when the rock is dissolved away. Plant growth, aside from physically breaking up rocks, can also change the environmental chemistry {{4}} to chemical weathering.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.occurs, 2.composition, 3.results, 4.contributing', NULL, NULL),
  ('bb1d0cdb-2db9-5457-9204-bac2d15e2558'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb1d0cdb-2db9-5457-9204-bac2d15e2558'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which sweet food is produced by bees?', '38811fe0-30db-55e0-bcf4-f20d38ba4647'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Honey', NULL, NULL),
  ('bb1fa4e6-12c3-53b2-95f1-7f440a41e75f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bb1fa4e6-12c3-53b2-95f1-7f440a41e75f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Durham University Sailing Boat Club', E'Durham University Sailing club {{1}} by Malcolm Dodds in1966. We {{2}} a lot since then and now our members take part in team racing, fleet racing, match racing and yachting events around the country. We have a jet {{3}} of eleven Fireflies and sail at Derwent Reservoir, which is about a 30-minute drive from Durham.\nAny Durham University students can join the sailing club, and while most of the sailing that we currently do is racing, there are other opportunities too, for example, {{4}} the sunshine in one of our summer sailing sessions.\nIt is always possible to come along to one of our sailing socials whether you are part of the team or not and if you would like to do some sailing while at Durham then it couldn''t be easier.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.was founded, 2.have grown, 3.flight, 4.enjoying', NULL, NULL),
