  ('bc990cbf-ee1d-5d27-a5e7-11dae13faffc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bc990cbf-ee1d-5d27-a5e7-11dae13faffc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alcohol Consumption', E'Alcohol consumption is a major risk factor for liver diseases, ranging from fatty liver to cirrhosis. The liver is responsible for detoxifying alcohol and other substances, as well as {{1}} hundreds of other vital functions. Alcohol {{2}} fat accumulation, inflammation, and scarring in the liver, which can impair its functions and lead to liver failure. If alcohol consumption continues, the liver becomes inflamed and tries to heal itself by forming scar tissue. This can {{3}} result in cirrhosis, which is the irreversible scarring and distortion of the liver structure. Nevertheless, the liver can recover from alcohol damage if alcohol consumption is stopped or reduced. The {{4}} and speed of recovery depend on the stage and extent of liver injury. Therefore, early detection and intervention are crucial for preventing or minimizing alcohol-related liver injury.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.performing, 2.induces, 3.eventually, 4.degree', NULL, NULL),
  ('bc996a33-a195-58c8-9659-d4277628f6a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bc996a33-a195-58c8-9659-d4277628f6a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd2be71d8-3023-5acc-9fca-0104424c1bf0'::uuid, NULL, E'Immigration policy is a complex issue that requires careful consideration.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('bc996a57-dd70-5806-b8d4-c0bcfb3777ba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bc996a57-dd70-5806-b8d4-c0bcfb3777ba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Natural Capital', E'Capital has often been thought of narrowly as physical capital — the machines, tools, and equipment used in the production of other goods, but our wealth and wellbeing also {{1}} natural capital. If we forget this, we risk degrading the services that natural ecosystems provide, which {{2}} our economies and sustain our lives. These services include purifying our water, {{3}} our climate, reducing flood risk, and pollinating our crops. The Natural Capital Project — a partnership {{4}} WWF, The Nature Conservancy, University of Minnesota and Stanford University — works to provide decision makers with {{5}} ways to assess the true value of the services that ecosystems provide. An essential element of the Natural Capital Project is developing tools that help decision makers protect biodiversity and ecosystem services.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.relies on, 2.support, 3.regulating, 4.among, 5.reliable', NULL, NULL),
  ('bc9a2f2a-adaf-54da-bba4-e43f392869f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bc9a2f2a-adaf-54da-bba4-e43f392869f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Volcanic Eruptions', E'Volcanic eruptions provide routes for material deep beneath Earth''s surface to escape to the surface. They also allow a world to {{1}} its heat. Active volcanoes on Earth and Venus are fed by subsurface molten rock. On Earth, the lava comes up from the mantle (which is the layer under the surface). Once there''s enough molten rock — called magma — and enough pressure on it, a volcanic eruption {{2}} . In many volcanoes, the magma rises up through a central tube or "throat," and {{3}} out the top of the mountain. Volcanic activity can be fairly quiet, or it can be quite {{4}} . In a very active flow, clouds of gas may come rolling out of the volcanic caldera. These are quite deadly because they''re hot and moving fast, and the heat and gas can kill someone very quickly.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.vent, 2.occurs, 3.emerges, 4.explosive', NULL, NULL),
  ('bc9f3905-8492-53c2-ad71-3ebc9c1b31a0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bc9f3905-8492-53c2-ad71-3ebc9c1b31a0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dam', E'Dams are huge man-made structures that act as {{1}} on a river. Today, the main reason people build dams is to produce electricity. They are also built to restrict and control the flow of water in a river. Throughout history, dams have been used to prevent flooding and to irrigate (water) farmland. Dams supply about a sixth of the world''s electricity and they significantly reduce the risk of floods and {{2}} . They also make water easier to access, especially in desertlike areas, where water is in low supply. There are however, some negative effects of damming rivers. Many people''s homes are knocked down to make space for the dam, and flooding can {{3}} in the reservoir, which is the area behind the dam where water {{4}} . This can cause valuable farmland to become submerged under the lakes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.barriers, 2.droughts, 3.occur, 4.collects', NULL, NULL),
  ('bca18b81-dfb4-55a2-aee8-54c0b435664b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bca18b81-dfb4-55a2-aee8-54c0b435664b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a baby who is just learning to walk?', 'f8e7bad9-92d0-5cfe-8fa3-e1b5169699c7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Toddler', NULL, NULL),
