  ('bcaed152-ab9a-525d-b2e0-ef9081b253f6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bcaed152-ab9a-525d-b2e0-ef9081b253f6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Full Moon', E'The Hunter''s full moon is the first full moon after the autumnal equinox, which marks the {{1}} of the colder months in the Northern Hemisphere. At higher latitudes in the Northern Hemisphere, the moon therefore {{2}} larger than the full moons of the summer months, as it {{3}} relatively low above the horizon. Its orange color was also more vivid than usual due to the light-scattering effect of Earth''s atmosphere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.arrival, 2.appeared, 3.lingered', NULL, NULL),
