  ('bcb43490-9664-5d09-bd84-fe436a8670ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bcb43490-9664-5d09-bd84-fe436a8670ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Reserving Land', E'Experts argue that human needs for farmland, housing and industry are more important than reserving land for endangered animals. Will you support this statement and why?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('bcc122bd-1fe7-5ace-9db3-52bcc9432bdc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bcc122bd-1fe7-5ace-9db3-52bcc9432bdc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where is the largest tropical rainforest in the world located?', '807e57b1-3eb8-5388-8e41-d49d7d70e7ee'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Amazon Rainforest', NULL, NULL),
  ('bcc7d185-cf0b-50f0-af94-78cb56c9527a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'bcc7d185-cf0b-50f0-af94-78cb56c9527a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Worker Decision-Making', E'In some companies, employers involve workers in the decision-making process about products and services. What are the advantages and disadvantages of such a policy?', NULL, NULL, E'Nowadays, whether employers involve workers in the decision-making process about products and services has fueled heated discussions. Proponents claim that by involving workers in the decision-making process, organizations can achieve higher employee engagement, whereas opponents contend that it leads to process challenges. From my perspective, I am convinced that employees’ participation in decision-making about products and services has both advantages and disadvantages.\nTo begin with, having employees participate in decision-making can boost work motivation and improve team dynamics. For example, in decision-making process, workers will develop a stronger sense of ownership, leading to higher job satisfaction and increased productivity. In addition to this, employees often provide practical insights and innovative solutions, ensuring more well-rounded policies. Other than that, involving workers fosters open communication and stronger teamwork, creating a more positive work environment. It is thus shown that the benefits of workers’ involvement in decision-making include increased productivity, innovative solutions and stronger teamwork.\nBesides, I also believe that involving employees in decision-making may result in reduced efficiency, poorer decision quality, and increased team conflicts. On top of that, prolonged discussions and conflicting opinions among workers can cause project delays. Moreover, workers may make wrong choices due to limited expertise or emotional biases. Recently, I have examined an article arguing that different goals and arguments about plans can strain relationships between coworkers, weakening team unity. This clearly proves that the drawbacks of including employees in product and service decision-making are reduced productivity, wrong decisions and straining relationships.\nTo conclude, there is no doubt that better team performance and team tension are essential in today''s world. While some might disagree, the evidence strongly supports that involving staff in product and service decision-making has both upsides and downsides.', NULL, 200, 300),
