  ('be0511c6-48b3-5fa3-a917-cfe1bd9049f5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be0511c6-48b3-5fa3-a917-cfe1bd9049f5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gas Drilling', E'Gas drilling on the Indonesian of java has {{1}} a “mud volcano” that has killed 13 people and may render four square miles (ten square kilometers) of countryside uninhabitable for years. In a report released on January 23, a team of British researchers says the deadly {{2}} began when an exploratory gas well punched through a layer of rock 9300 feet (2800 meters) below the surface, {{3}} hot, high-pressure water to {{4}} .The water {{5}} mud to the surface, where it has {{6}} across a region 2.5 miles (4 kilometers) in {{7}} in the eight months since the eruption began. The mud volcano is similar to a gusher or blowout, which occurs in oil drilling when oil or gas squirt to the surface, the team says. This upwelling, however, spews out a volume of mud equivalent to a dozen Olympic swimming pools each day. Although the eruption isn''t as violent as a {{8}} volcano, more than a dozen people died when a natural gas pipeline ruptured. The research team, who published their findings in the February issue of GSA Today, also estimate that the volcano, called Lusi, will leave more than 11,000 people permanently displaced.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.triggered, 2.upwelling, 3.allowing, 4.escape, 5.carried, 6.spread, 7.diameter, 8.conventional', NULL, NULL),
  ('be057579-1ea1-512f-9672-4584c0ae7a38'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be057579-1ea1-512f-9672-4584c0ae7a38'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'December Sales', E'Weakness in electronics, auto and gas station sales dragged down overall retail sales last month, but excluding those three categories, retailers enjoyed healthy increases across the board, according to government figures released Wednesday. Moreover, December sales numbers were also revised higher.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be0b232d-0b28-5b06-9752-e0352757548d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be0b232d-0b28-5b06-9752-e0352757548d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2fdd8319-857c-51c5-99ee-2297e488e7c9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The program must be conducted in abidance with general regulations.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be0d1ee3-8bf4-5d4d-a7c7-2126fcb4ea7d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be0d1ee3-8bf4-5d4d-a7c7-2126fcb4ea7d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Philosophy', E'The philosophy of mind is a certain area of {{1}} commonly recognized by English-speaking philosophers. But it is not an accident that this {{2}} is hard to translate into other languages. This is only partly due to the fact that the English word “mind” has no exact {{3}} in the other main European languages. It is also a reflection of the fact that the classification in which this label figures is itself based on certain profound philosophical assumptions, often unexpressed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.problems, 2.expression, 3.equivalent', NULL, NULL),
  ('be1de367-33c5-59f8-98f5-a290adffe494'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be1de367-33c5-59f8-98f5-a290adffe494'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aquatic Biomes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'5, 3, 1, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('be1fc077-6dc7-57e7-82df-66383f5546bd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be1fc077-6dc7-57e7-82df-66383f5546bd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Moscow Princes', E'Moscow has generally been considered fortunate in its princes. Sheer luck {{1}} an important part of the picture. For several generations, the princes of Moscow had the {{2}} of male succession without interruption or {{3}} . In {{4}} , for a long time the sons of the princes of Moscow were lucky not to have uncles competing for the Muscovite seat.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.constituted, 2.advantage, 3.conflict, 4.particular', NULL, NULL),
  ('be220808-22be-5a27-ad96-c8d9635e4203'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be220808-22be-5a27-ad96-c8d9635e4203'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fd30d012-7774-57e2-8844-a860aed4bf59'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Without doubt, this theory has a number of limitations.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be32ecb5-a623-5f45-8d1b-f6bdc8f99106'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be32ecb5-a623-5f45-8d1b-f6bdc8f99106'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person walking in the street or in a crosswalk?', '940f0a1f-8fd7-5012-b788-ac5768504d9c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pedestrian', NULL, NULL),
  ('be33632c-a03b-564d-9614-44f4df108d7f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be33632c-a03b-564d-9614-44f4df108d7f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ozone', E'Clones of an Eastern cottonwood (Populus deltoides) in the Bronx and other city spots grew to double the biomass of clones {{1}} outside small towns upstate or on Long Island, says Jillian Gregg, now of the Environmental Protection Agency''s western-ecology division in Corvallis, Ore. The growth gap comes from ozone damage, she and her New York colleagues report. Ozone chemists have known that concentrations may spike skyscraper high in city air, but during a full 24 hours, rural trees actually get a higher cumulative ozone exposure from urban pollution that {{2}} in and lingers. A series of new experiments now shows that this hang-around ozone is the {{3}} factor in tree growth, the researchers say in the July 10 Nature. "This study has profound importance in showing us most vividly that rural areas {{4}} the price for urban pollution," says Stephen P. Long of the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. "This work should be a wake-up call," he adds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.planted, 2.blows, 3.overwhelming, 4.pay', NULL, NULL),
  ('be34f11b-8a6d-58d9-bf65-f496780f89c1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be34f11b-8a6d-58d9-bf65-f496780f89c1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Historical Sites', NULL, '8924f945-f0c2-56ae-ab14-c1ed1bd93204'::uuid, NULL, E'As we weave through the fabric of our modern lives, let''s pause to acknowledge the ''Preservation of Historical Sites''. These landmarks are not mere relics; they are vital narratives that define our collective identity and heritage. The preservation of historical sites serves as an educational resource. Each structure is a tangible classroom, imparting lessons about our ancestors'' ingenuity, culture, and values. Studies show that students who engage with history in a tangible way develop a deeper understanding and appreciation for the past. Additionally, these sites contribute significantly to local economies through tourism. Preserving them not only honors our history but also promotes sustainable economic growth. According to UNESCO, cultural heritage sites attract millions of visitors each year, supporting local businesses and jobs. In safeguarding these treasures, we maintain a connection to our past, enrich our present, and invest in our future. Let''s champion the cause of conservation, ensuring that history''s echoes remain loud for generations to come.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be37b716-9450-5dd6-a8d5-fcd23b9dadb6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be37b716-9450-5dd6-a8d5-fcd23b9dadb6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3af60943-186d-58f5-9d65-7f357771ebbe'::uuid, NULL, E'We all know there are more important things in life than the rat race.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be3e2dab-df25-5580-b45a-f2ba546d9f6e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be3e2dab-df25-5580-b45a-f2ba546d9f6e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Innovation', E'People tend to think that any new technology or device is an act of genius; something that has required vision and insight to create and then develop into a marketable product. The fact is that innovations were often already ''out there'' in the public domain in some form or another. They tend to evolve from notions that have been around for years but that had not, until that point, been suitably adapted. One expert calls this the ''long nose'' approach to innovation, whereby new concepts come into the world slowly, gradually revealing all they have to offer.\n\nWhat is the writer''s main point about innovation?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'New products are not always based on new ideas.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be42ef23-3a8b-5c73-974b-296bb5e5e996'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be42ef23-3a8b-5c73-974b-296bb5e5e996'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'AQ', E'We’ve all heard of IQ, and terms like EQ, which relates to your emotional intelligence, are commonly used. But have you heard of AQ? AQ stands for adversity quotient and measures your ability to deal with the ups and downs of life. Being able to handle these rough patches we all go through is not only important in our personal lives but in our professional lives too. So how can we learn to be more resilient?\nLuckily, there are some steps you can take to help you be more resilient and adaptable in the face of adversity, according to Dr Shahram Heshmat, professor of health economics at the University of Illinois. First, try to find a meaningful goal. Resilient people often have an aim and are able to concentrate more on a desired outcome, seeing negative situations as a bump in the road on the way to achieving their goal. Learning to relax and regulate your emotions is another key step – one way to help you destress is by practising breathing exercises. Likewise, dwelling on things and letting them get to you can cause you to be stressed. See difficulties more as an opportunity to learn and grow emotionally. Finally, make sure you have a good social support network. Being able to talk with someone about the challenges we face can help.\nThings happen in life we can’t prevent – and sometimes they aren’t pleasant. But, taking a few steps to be more resilient can make them a little easier to get through.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('be46c9c6-4f3b-5254-9e94-32261b12e9de'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be46c9c6-4f3b-5254-9e94-32261b12e9de'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Zoom', E'The coronavirus pandemic has shifted many of our interactions online, with Zoom video calls replacing in-person classes, work meetings, conferences and other events. Will all that screen time damage our vision? Maybe not. It turns out that our visual perception is highly adaptable, according to new research.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be4981a6-8c8c-5319-ac7e-1425f0b8efb6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be4981a6-8c8c-5319-ac7e-1425f0b8efb6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0f9bc099-77d2-51f5-9a90-7c8e4ac63b5b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Class participation is an important part of your final grade.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be4bf6cd-c8a4-592c-ad11-49a12f6bfe4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be4bf6cd-c8a4-592c-ad11-49a12f6bfe4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a book listing acronyms?', '61bf8845-9f03-5e5b-bfc5-a624ed90d6c9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Abbreviation dictionary', NULL, NULL),
  ('be4de31a-0151-5c04-b10a-31f9f344e98f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be4de31a-0151-5c04-b10a-31f9f344e98f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fa3b007f-9862-5f6d-93a6-1c83a1b12428'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'He taught literature for several years before becoming a writer.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be5eadcb-183d-5518-a752-7d4914934c6f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be5eadcb-183d-5518-a752-7d4914934c6f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Emotional Memory', NULL, '166bd800-b908-53d5-ba9d-56b0f9fcb824'::uuid, NULL, E'Getting back to PTSD, another type of non-declarative memory is emotional memory. Now, this has a specific meaning in psychology and refers to our ability to learn about cues in our environment and their emotional and motivational significance. What do I mean by that? Well, think of a cue like the smell of baking bread, or a more abstract cue like a 20-pound note. Because these cues have been pegged with good things in the past, we like them and we approach them. Other cues, like the buzzing of a wasp, elicit very negative emotions and quite dramatic avoidance behavior in some people. Now, I hate wasps. I can tell you that fact. But what I can’t give you are the non-declarative emotional memories for how I react when there’s a wasp nearby. I can’t give you the racing heart, the sweaty palms, that sense of rising panic. I can describe them to you, but I can’t give them to you.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be6039af-7034-58b0-a2f6-c7536b1de2eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be6039af-7034-58b0-a2f6-c7536b1de2eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How many sides does a triangle have?', '206e23ef-c50d-5351-a8c1-fbc7f277f3f8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Three', NULL, NULL),
  ('be63693b-8a9d-5cf3-ad06-28c757ec1871'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be63693b-8a9d-5cf3-ad06-28c757ec1871'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6495acba-40b2-510f-be7a-159025cc8642'::uuid, NULL, E'Detailed analysis of population growth has revealed some alarming predictions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be63df7c-88f3-5ea5-a44e-c2c18f379cc4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be63df7c-88f3-5ea5-a44e-c2c18f379cc4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '475a423d-65f0-5499-97f0-f4d899afde28'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Please make sure you have collected all the necessary materials.', NULL, NULL),
  ('be64b47c-707d-5a8d-a7e2-393abcbcb229'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be64b47c-707d-5a8d-a7e2-393abcbcb229'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Windmills', E'This popularity was driven by the simplicity of windmills as mechanical energy generators. By simply putting a windmill with many vanes up, you could quickly garner access to a free mechanical energy source. Through the spinning of the blades, that rotational energy could be used to drive machines through gearing or used to push and pull water from the ground with simple water sucker-rod pumps.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be6d16f7-de78-5e27-8037-628adb77147b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be6d16f7-de78-5e27-8037-628adb77147b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ancient DNA', E'Pääbo, the director of the Max Planck Institute for Evolutionary Anthropology in Germany, developed methods to recover, sequence and analyze ancient DNA from fossils – a {{1}} that took decades. Researchers are using the techniques today to answer fundamental questions about human history and the planet’s deep past. Many of the discoveries upend assumptions about prehistoric times. When Pääbo’s lab in Leipzig {{2}} the first Neanderthal genome in 2010, many were startled to learn that our own species Homo sapiens encountered and had babies with Neanderthals. Paleogenetics has continued to {{3}} out astonishing secrets from DNA hidden in bones, teeth – even dirt. The Black Death, the world’s most devastating plague outbreak, killed half of medieval Europe’s population in the space of seven years in the 14th century, shifting the {{4}} of human history. Analysis of centuries-old DNA from both victims and survivors of the Black Death identified key {{5}} differences that helped people survive the plague, according to a study published in the journal Nature.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.feat, 2.sequenced, 3.tease, 4.course, 5.genetic', NULL, NULL),
  ('be72db85-439d-59b1-840e-70776024975e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be72db85-439d-59b1-840e-70776024975e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f3d71ce1-bf8a-54d6-8914-d31b97267e08'::uuid, NULL, E'I look forward to meeting you and to helping you realize your goals.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('be760819-7917-585f-a560-25aef572300d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'be760819-7917-585f-a560-25aef572300d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urbanization', E'Global urbanization is a significant trend, with more people moving to cities in search of better opportunities. This rapid urban growth presents challenges such as housing, transportation, and environmental sustainability. Urban planners and policymakers are working towards creating smart, livable cities that prioritize efficient infrastructure, green spaces, and social inclusivity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
