  ('c5ed1fcf-68a5-5181-a5f1-f60ea73d0ca0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c5ed1fcf-68a5-5181-a5f1-f60ea73d0ca0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The University of Maryland', E'The University of Maryland boasts 78 academic programs {{1}} in the top 25 nationally and 29 academic programs in the top 10 according to U.S. News and World report. By drawing top-notch faculty, attracting the brightest students and {{2}} in the quality of our academic programs, we are a force to {{3}} with on a national {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.ranked, 2.investing, 3.reckon, 4.basis', NULL, NULL),
  ('c5f48dcd-f490-5f19-afb5-fcc667746f8c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c5f48dcd-f490-5f19-afb5-fcc667746f8c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nutrition Scientists', E'Since nutrition scientists are constantly making new discoveries, we need to revise our {{1}} for healthy eating from time to time. However, nutrition is an art as well as a {{2}} . It''s an art because it requires creativity to develop a healthy eating plan for people who {{3}} in their food preferences, beliefs and culture, let alone in their nutritional needs according to their genes and life stage. As we discover more about how our genes and our environment {{4}} , it''s becoming increasingly difficult to provide a single set of dietary recommendations that will be {{5}} for everyone.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.recommendations, 2.science, 3.differ, 4.interact, 5.suitable', NULL, NULL),
  ('c5feae6b-4ea0-53e7-b452-3779d0883f85'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c5feae6b-4ea0-53e7-b452-3779d0883f85'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCM-R', E'Since 1980, the use of wind to produce electricity has been growing rapidly. In 1994 there were nearly 20,000 wind turbines worldwide, most grouped in clusters called wind farms that collectively produced 3,000 megawatts of electricity. Most were in Denmark (which got 3 percent of its electricity from wind turbines) and California (where 17,000 machines produced 1 percent of the state''s electricity, enough to meet the residential needs of a city as large as San Francisco). In principle, all the power needs of the United States could be provided by exploiting the wind potential of just three states—North Dakota, South Dakota, and Texas.\n\nBased on the information in the paragraph, which of the following best explains the term wind farms?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Types of power plant common in Denmark and California\nCollections of wind turbines producing electric power', NULL, NULL),
  ('c60966cc-3ac4-539f-9cf3-0ea0e3f4e7b3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c60966cc-3ac4-539f-9cf3-0ea0e3f4e7b3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fb6bea9c-56de-50bf-80df-4041f53b36d7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The needs of the nation determine a person''s achievements.', NULL, NULL),
