  ('c632b66d-1591-51ae-a149-2681eb7ef791'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c632b66d-1591-51ae-a149-2681eb7ef791'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Early Language', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 4, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('c6363286-bf25-5662-8257-cda63d0a2e7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c6363286-bf25-5662-8257-cda63d0a2e7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Educational Games', E'What are the advantages and disadvantages of incorporating video games into education and skill development?', NULL, NULL, E'The integration of video games into education and skill development has sparked debates regarding its benefits and drawbacks. While video games offer immersive learning experiences, they also pose risks such as addiction and limited real-world applicability.\nVideo games have the potential to revolutionize education by making learning fun and engaging. They enhance student motivation and participation through interactive gameplay, fostering a dynamic learning environment. Moreover, games often stimulate critical thinking and problem-solving skills, encouraging players to develop strategic thinking abilities essential for academic success. Additionally, the adaptability of video games to individual learning styles provides personalized learning opportunities, catering to diverse student needs and preferences.\nDespite the benefits, the integration of video games in education comes with its share of drawbacks. Excessive gaming can lead to addiction, diverting students'' focus from academic responsibilities and hindering their overall performance. Prolonged screen time from gaming may result in physical health issues such as eye strain, sedentary lifestyles, and poor posture, raising concerns about students'' well-being. Furthermore, while some video games promote cognitive skills, others lack direct applicability to real-world scenarios, limiting their educational value in practical contexts.\nIn conclusion, the incorporation of video games into education offers a blend of advantages and disadvantages. While they enhance engagement, critical thinking, and personalized learning experiences, they also pose risks of addiction, health concerns, and limited real-world relevance. Striking a balance between leveraging the benefits and mitigating the drawbacks is essential to harness the full potential of video games in education and skill development.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('c636b5f2-e004-50cb-a609-426aa25b1165'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c636b5f2-e004-50cb-a609-426aa25b1165'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'af9787e8-6fa7-55af-803f-46affbfe4b6e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You must develop a critical approach when engaging with academic literature.', NULL, NULL),
