  ('c742cb13-3447-5e71-b4ec-05fab4d49346'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c742cb13-3447-5e71-b4ec-05fab4d49346'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '553d65ad-4b86-5c5c-8ebe-bfb854b9b483'::uuid, NULL, E'Books in the reserve section are only loaned for a limited time.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c7468892-5348-5708-bb0d-2c40abb9b114'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c7468892-5348-5708-bb0d-2c40abb9b114'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pharaoh''s Mummy', E'You''ve probably heard the {{1}} "a heart attack on a plate." Maybe it''s fettuccini alfredo. Or maybe it''s a bacon cheeseburger, covered in batter and deep fried to artery-clogging perfection. Either way, it''s clear that our modern diet is not always the most cardio-friendly. But that doesn''t mean that heart disease is a recent invention. Because a report in the Journal of the American Medical Association reveals that some Egyptian mummies show signs of atherosclerosis, {{2}} of the arteries .\nPrevious examination of a pharaoh''s mummy in the Museum of Egyptian Antiquities in Cairo showed that he''d suffered from atherosclerosis. Intrigued by this observation, {{4}} from the University of California, Irvine, got to wondering whether damaged arteries were common among ancient Egyptians. So they collected 20 mummies from the museum basement and from various displays, and {{6}} them to whole-body CT scans to look at their insides. Sixteen mummies still had identifiable hearts or arteries. And nine of them showed hardening of those arteries.\nAlthough no one knows what those mummies were eating, it''s safe to say they never {{7}} a corn dog. Too many of those things will lead you to an early tomb.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.expression, 2.hardening, 3.scientists, 4.subjected, 5.encountered', NULL, NULL),
  ('c74f9e16-b845-53e4-80dd-1938faf84356'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c74f9e16-b845-53e4-80dd-1938faf84356'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b2d718f3-a312-5dc4-9091-a9b7f81b2b24'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There is a clear need for further research in this field.', NULL, NULL),
  ('c7572642-1320-5578-be2f-eab41aa1e1ba'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c7572642-1320-5578-be2f-eab41aa1e1ba'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6f2fbfc3-1a0b-5f37-aed3-f186d89cfe48'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'People will never learn that the life exists on the other planets.', NULL, NULL),
  ('c75ffba5-8783-5ae7-9a65-910a359e74ed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c75ffba5-8783-5ae7-9a65-910a359e74ed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hallucination and Personality', NULL, 'b42d929b-86d6-5225-a746-c42a3ea98e53'::uuid, NULL, E'A mild form of hallucination is known as a disturbance, and can occur in most of the senses above. These may be things like seeing movement in peripheral vision, or hearing faint noises and/or voices. Auditory hallucinations are very common in schizophrenia. They may be benevolent (telling the subject good things about themselves) or malicious, cursing the subject etc. Auditory hallucinations of the malicious type are frequently heard, for example people talking about the subject behind his/her back. Like auditory hallucinations, the source of the visual counterpart can also be behind the subject''s back. Their visual counterpart is the feeling of being looked or stared at, usually with malicious intent. Frequently, auditory hallucinations and their visual counterpart are experienced by the subject together.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c762e1d1-bee0-5cb5-a5bb-bf8af77e63d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c762e1d1-bee0-5cb5-a5bb-bf8af77e63d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the persons who study religions?', 'ec724c84-1c27-5d70-bfac-21da6b836d71'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Theologians / theologists', NULL, NULL),
  ('c76734f6-1eec-56fd-bd03-d77dcc31e991'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c76734f6-1eec-56fd-bd03-d77dcc31e991'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6b897b00-49cc-5d2d-9294-ad6c8b357d6c'::uuid, NULL, E'During times of change they should be thinking not only about the strain on their staff.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c76b1242-826c-5afd-92a9-83fe76965c22'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c76b1242-826c-5afd-92a9-83fe76965c22'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the shape formed by the set of all points in a plane that are a certain distance from a given point?', 'b9811df9-8b30-5234-a70e-336551ca9fa1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Circle', NULL, NULL),
  ('c76f61f9-31bb-58f0-9928-264d3db32edf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c76f61f9-31bb-58f0-9928-264d3db32edf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the phrase used to describe the way something repeatedly increases and decreases?', '996af786-aa1d-5a52-9f94-ab6cd6053276'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ebb and flow / wax and wane', NULL, NULL),
  ('c76fcffa-5b1c-5faf-b11a-fa5e2016241d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c76fcffa-5b1c-5faf-b11a-fa5e2016241d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5260b378-4a80-570c-bcf3-f7c5bb42afc1'::uuid, NULL, E'Opposition to the government tax policies is widespread across business sectors.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c771ddda-c938-5b43-9bcb-ea7fb02aa4f0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c771ddda-c938-5b43-9bcb-ea7fb02aa4f0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '07dd049b-eb9d-5bd3-b060-763d9b13f6fb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The course is designed to prepare graduates for business careers.', NULL, NULL),
  ('c7791df4-faa7-511c-b681-8fb290c67973'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c7791df4-faa7-511c-b681-8fb290c67973'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Attention to Celebrities', E'Television, newspapers, magazines, and other media pay too much attention to the personal lives of famous people such as public figures and celebrities. What is your opinion?', NULL, NULL, E'Media coverage of famous people has become a common occurrence in today''s society. While some argue that this coverage provides entertainment for the audience, I believe that it has a negative impact on the personal lives of those being covered. The constant attention and scrutiny from the media can invade their privacy, cause unnecessary stress, and lead to a distorted public image.\nOne negative impact of media coverage on famous people is the invasion of privacy. The media often goes to great lengths to obtain information about their personal lives, including stalking, hacking, and bribing sources. This can lead to a loss of privacy and a sense of vulnerability for those being covered. Additionally, constant attention can make it difficult for them to maintain personal relationships or engage in normal activities without being followed or photographed.\nAnother negative impact of media coverage is the distortion of public image. The media often focuses on sensationalized stories or rumors, rather than accurate reporting. This can lead to a distorted public image that is not reflective of the individual''s true character or accomplishments. Furthermore, constant scrutiny can create a stressful and hostile environment that can be damaging to mental health.\nIn conclusion, while some may argue that media coverage provides entertainment for the audience, it has a negative impact on the personal lives of famous people. The invasion of privacy, loss of personal relationships, distorted public image, and stress caused by constant attention can be damaging to mental health and well-being.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('c77b03c2-b295-5635-a886-58924a30a5dd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c77b03c2-b295-5635-a886-58924a30a5dd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Different Jobs', E'Young people should try different jobs before they decide which job or career they will do in the long term. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s rapidly changing world, young people face the challenge of choosing a career path that aligns with their interests and aspirations. It is my belief that young people should indeed try different jobs before making a long-term career decision. By exploring various employment opportunities, they can gain valuable experiences, discover their passions, and make informed choices for their future.\nFirstly, trying different jobs allows young people to gain a diverse range of experiences. Each job offers unique challenges and opportunities for growth. By exposing themselves to different work environments, young people can develop a versatile skill set and adaptability that will benefit them in the long term. These experiences also provide valuable insights into various industries, helping them make informed decisions about their career paths.\nSecondly, trying different jobs enables young people to discover their passions and interests. Often, it is through exposure to different roles that individuals uncover their true vocational calling. By exploring a variety of jobs, young people can identify what truly excites and motivates them. This self-discovery process allows them to pursue careers that align with their passions, leading to greater job satisfaction and personal fulfillment.\nIn conclusion, I strongly agree that young people should try different jobs before committing to a long-term career. By exploring diverse employment opportunities, they can gain valuable experiences, discover their passions, and make informed decisions about their future. This approach enables them to build a well-rounded skill set, find meaningful work, and ultimately lead fulfilling professional lives. Encouraging young people to explore various job options will empower them to make informed choices and embark on a career path that aligns with their unique talents and aspirations.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('c77c95c4-64b8-5255-b1e4-bd59a014e746'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c77c95c4-64b8-5255-b1e4-bd59a014e746'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Old Paris', NULL, '01f20e78-db86-5f7a-a26f-83f14a52cfcb'::uuid, NULL, E'Paris is very old-there has been a settlement there for at least 6000 years and its shape has been determined in part by the River Seine, and in part by the edicts of France’s rulers. But the great boulevards we admire today are relatively new, and were constructed to prevent any more barricades being created by the rebellious population; that work was carried out in the middle 19th century. The earlier Paris had been in part a maze of narrow streets and alleyways. But you can imagine that the work was not only highly expensive, but caused great distress among the half a million or so residents whose houses were simply razed, and whose neighborhoods disappeared. What is done cannot usually be undone, especially when buildings are torn down.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c77e4b0f-edc0-5ca8-8144-42b4f130860e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c77e4b0f-edc0-5ca8-8144-42b4f130860e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Chasing the Flame', E'It is precisely in observing the intertwinings of success and failure that Chasing the Flame makes its greatest mark. With piercing insight and relentless logic, it reveals the pitfalls of international politics and details an intricate struggle between individual and institution. It haunts us with the poignant truth that even a great man can do only so much to reinvent the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c77f4c50-4fd9-5a2e-bca8-ca0febb4d3c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c77f4c50-4fd9-5a2e-bca8-ca0febb4d3c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heart Functions', E'The heart functions as a pump at the centre of the circulatory system. In humans it is located in the chest cavity, between the lungs, {{1}} to the left. The heart consists of four chambers surrounded by a very strong muscular wall, the myocardium. The upper chambers, the right and left atria, {{2}} blood entering the heart, and the lower chambers, the right and left ventricles pump the blood out of the heart, via the pulmonary and the systemic circulatory systems.\nThe two systems work as {{3}} . Blood from the body enters the right atrium, {{4}} passed into the right ventricle and from there is propelled through the pulmonary artery to the lungs. In the lungs the blood releases carbon dioxide and absorbs oxygen and is then {{5}} back to the heart into the left atrium. From here it passes into the left ventricle, which pumps the oxygenated blood around the body.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.a bit, 2.receive, 3.follows, 4.is, 5.transported', NULL, NULL),
  ('c785ec29-0e22-5d42-afa6-3aa22a1e4875'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'c785ec29-0e22-5d42-afa6-3aa22a1e4875'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Locomotion', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 5, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
