  ('ca54a700-6ec7-5c8b-a65a-46cbae13c2b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ca54a700-6ec7-5c8b-a65a-46cbae13c2b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '36e3de2a-5269-5e1e-9218-eb010d567aae'::uuid, NULL, E'I spend my time really studying human beings.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ca56e713-4639-5c4c-b45f-4d9d48d7bc92'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ca56e713-4639-5c4c-b45f-4d9d48d7bc92'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Face to Face', E'Face-to-face communication is better than other types of communication, such as letters, email, or telephone calls. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'In today''s digital age, there are many forms of communication available to us, including letters, email, telephone calls, and video conferencing. While each of these methods has its own advantages, I believe that face-to-face communication is superior to other types of communication in certain situations.\nFirstly, nonverbal cues such as body language and facial expressions can enhance understanding and convey emotions. When we communicate face-to-face, we can read the other person''s body language and facial expressions, which can help us to better understand their message and emotions. This can be particularly important in situations where there is potential for miscommunication or where emotions are running high.\nSecondly, face-to-face communication allows for immediate feedback and clarification. When we communicate in person, we can ask questions and receive immediate feedback, which can help us to clarify any misunderstandings and ensure that our message is being understood as intended. This can be particularly important in situations where accuracy and precision are important.\nIn conclusion, while other forms of communication such as letters, email, and telephone calls have their own advantages, I believe that face-to-face communication is superior in certain situations. By allowing for nonverbal cues and immediate feedback and clarification, face-to-face communication can enhance understanding and improve accuracy and precision. It is important to consider the context and purpose of the communication when deciding which method to use, but in many cases, face-to-face communication is the best choice.', NULL, 200, 300),
