  ('cb5f53ac-ad35-5614-9ec7-349576c4a77b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cb5f53ac-ad35-5614-9ec7-349576c4a77b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2aa78413-937f-54db-939b-7e23dd1c2827'::uuid, NULL, E'The student council manages the use of the sports facility on campus.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cb620b61-9382-52d7-b0fe-97810ab1fd27'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cb620b61-9382-52d7-b0fe-97810ab1fd27'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Optimists', NULL, '7530bd43-3479-5bab-b9dc-5eed89b0f417'::uuid, NULL, E'So, my optimism is rooted in the fact that for almost over 200 years every year has gotten a little bit better when we look at the scientific evidence. And while it’s possible that... next year everything could change, that everything could collapse and fall to the ground, statistically, probabilistically it won’t it will continue because 200 years has gone and next year it probably will continue. But if you look at the kind of current political regime around the world and the factors of pressures, environmental pressures, the pressures of distraction that we have from the new media, then I think you have to resort to hope. In the long term, optimists decide the future. It’s the optimists who create all the things that are going to be most important in our lives, because it was optimists who built and invented all the things that are now important in our current lives. And I think people behave better when they’re optimistic. There’s absolutely a need to be critical and doubtful and skeptical and... even pessimistic. Just like if you have a car you have to have brakes. You can’t have a car, no matter where it is, without brakes. But it’s the engine, the optimistic engine that keeps going and going and refuses to stop and is only concerned about going forward that really drives a car.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cb719614-c9f8-58f4-8dc4-416778c3d6cb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cb719614-c9f8-58f4-8dc4-416778c3d6cb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alligators'' Lungs', E'If you''ve ever been to the {{1}} , or tuned into the Animal Planet, you know that ''gators can move through the water so {{2}} , barely {{3}} a ripple. It almost looks like they surface and sink, twist and turn, without so much as moving a muscle.\nWell, it turns out they are moving some muscles. Just ones you can''t see. According to a study from the University of Utah, American {{4}} navigate {{5}} through the murky water by shifting the location of their lungs. You see, the lungs act like internal flotation devices. And using a set of four muscles, including the alligator equivalent of our diaphragm, a gator can basically steer just by moving those floats around. When they want to surface, they shift their lungs forward. To dive, they push ''em back. And to roll off in another {{6}} , they just shift those babies to one side or the other. The {{7}} will appear in the April issue of the Journal of Experimental Biology.\nThis ability to slice silently through the water without actually having to swim no doubt helps alligators sneak up on unsuspecting prey. Who never knew what hit them. And so will never have a chance to say: "See you later, alligator...after a while, crocodile."', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Everglades, 2.silently, 3.creating, 4.alligators, 5.gracefully, 6.direction, 7.findings', NULL, NULL),
  ('cb73912f-4c26-52dd-8310-4fffa208559e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cb73912f-4c26-52dd-8310-4fffa208559e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The Illiterates', E'The illiterates of the 21st century will not be those who cannot read and write, but those who cannot learn, unlearn, and relearn. Agree or Disagree?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('cb7cb32b-52c5-5738-af58-9ab05530520a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cb7cb32b-52c5-5738-af58-9ab05530520a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Physical Characteristics', E'Usually, age is determined by physical characteristics, such as teeth or bones. Great if you have a body. Researchers have tried unsuccessfully to use blood. But in this study, the scientists used immune cells called T-cells. T-cells recognize invaders through receptors that match molecules on bacteria, viruses, even tumors. The cellular activity that produces these receptors also produces a type of circular DNA molecule as a by-product.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
