  ('ccc43e95-c5a9-5c74-9b42-f9726e7a85f3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc43e95-c5a9-5c74-9b42-f9726e7a85f3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a notice, picture or film telling people about a product or service?', '60ea57c3-190d-5eb2-8aa4-d1151341e054'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Advertisement', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccc65598-7b23-5cdd-8125-d867e4f49f0e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc65598-7b23-5cdd-8125-d867e4f49f0e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where do tourists ride a bus?', '9fb67769-7dee-5150-9806-a48f3338fbec'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tourist center / scenic spots / bus stops / bus stations', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccc6ac41-a487-50d8-8a85-aef151b5b366'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc6ac41-a487-50d8-8a85-aef151b5b366'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ageing World', E'We live in an ageing world. While this has been recognized for some time in developed countries, it is only recently that this phenomenon has been fully acknowledged. Global communication is "shrinking" the world, and global ageing is "maturing" it. The increasing presence of older persons in the world is making people of all ages more aware that we live in a diverse and multigenerational society. It is no longer possible to ignore ageing, regardless of whether one views it positively or negatively. Demographers note that if current trends in ageing continue as predicted, a demographic revolution, wherein the proportions of the young and the old will undergo a historic crossover, will be felt in just three generations. This portrait of change in the world''s population parallels the magnitude of the industrial revolution traditionally considered the most significant social and economic breakthrough in the history of humankind since the Neolithic period. It marked the beginning of a sustained movement towards modern economic growth in much the same way that globalization is today marking an unprecedented and sustained movement toward a "global culture". The demographic revolution, it is envisaged, will be at least as powerful. While the future effects are not known, a likely scenario is one where both the challenges as well as the opportunities will emerge from a vessel into which exploration and research, dialogue and debate are poured. Challenges arise as social and economic structures try to adjust to the simultaneous phenomenon of diminishing young cohorts with rising older ones, and opportunities present themselves in the sheer number of older individuals and the vast resources societies stand to gain from their contribution.', NULL, NULL, E'As it is fully acknowledged that we live in an ageing world, a powerful demographic revolution will be a possible result if current trends in ageing continue as predicted, which will not only bring challenges of adjusting social and economic structures but also opportunities to present themselves in older people and vast resources.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('ccc715fa-753b-5d96-aa08-43d49d46f3a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc715fa-753b-5d96-aa08-43d49d46f3a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Abstract', E'It is an original work, not an excerpted passage. An abstract must be fully self-contained and {{1}} sense by itself, without further reference to outside sources or to the actual paper. It highlights key {{2}} areas, your research purpose, the relevance or importance of your work, and the main outcomes.\nIt is a well-developed single paragraph of approximately 250 words {{3}} length, which is indented and single spaced. The function of the abstract is to outline briefly all parts of the paper.\nAlthough {{4}} at the beginning of your paper, immediately following the title page, the abstract should be the last thing that you write, {{5}} you are sure of the conclusions you will reach.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.make, 2.content, 3.in, 4.it is placed, 5.once', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccc9036b-59b2-51e6-b65d-628b59969532'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc9036b-59b2-51e6-b65d-628b59969532'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Visit to Canada', E'The best time to visit Canada is during fall months, when mild temperatures and vibrant fall foliage make scenic drives, hiking, and outdoor exploration especially enjoyable. Travel guides often highlight autumn — especially from late September through November — as a peak season for color changes in Ontario, Quebec, and other regions of the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ccc91e4a-bc8d-56a3-9ade-2194994ad221'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccc91e4a-bc8d-56a3-9ade-2194994ad221'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hairstyles', E'With their punk hairstyles and bright colors, marmosets and tamarins are among the most attractive primates on earth. These fast-moving, lightweight animals live in the rainforests of South America. Their small size {{1}} it easy for them to dart about the trees, catching insects and small animals such as lizards, frogs, and snails. Marmosets have another unusual food {{2}} - they use their chisel-like incisor teeth to dig into tree bark and lap up the gummy sap that seeps out, leaving telltale, oval-shaped holes in the {{3}} when they have finished. But as vast tracts of rainforest are cleared for plantations and cattle ranches, marmosets and tamarins are in serious {{4}} of extinction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.makes, 2.source, 3.branches, 4.danger', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccd09bac-63c9-576e-b34f-9ac439073149'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccd09bac-63c9-576e-b34f-9ac439073149'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '20de084f-cc56-5dca-9df7-030c16d8dcf6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A good academic paper should present a clear argument.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccd76fce-695a-50e6-90e2-7e724d4e4366'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccd76fce-695a-50e6-90e2-7e724d4e4366'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coffee', E'Coffee is a beloved beverage known for its ability to fine-tune your focus and boost your energy levels. In fact, many people depend on their daily cup of coffee when they wake up to get their day started on the right foot. In addition to its energizing effects, coffee has been linked to a long list of potential health benefits, giving you more reasons to get brewing.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ccd86204-b75c-56ee-a657-00b2f6358ac4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccd86204-b75c-56ee-a657-00b2f6358ac4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Acid Mine Drainage', E'Mineral resources are the {{1}} of human society and national economic development. At {{2}} , more than 200 kinds of mineral resources have been discovered in the world, mainly in Russia, China and other countries, among which coal, oil and natural gas are {{3}} to 120 trillion tons of standard coal. Acid mine drainage is produced in the process of mining and seriously {{4}} the health of plants, animals and humans.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.lifeblood, 2.present, 3.equivalent, 4.endangers', NULL, NULL),
  ('cce25040-b8ae-5ec1-9c15-3e00fe3cd838'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cce25040-b8ae-5ec1-9c15-3e00fe3cd838'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A Book of Learning', NULL, 'f7090ad7-741b-5e31-b06d-a5776b126aae'::uuid, NULL, E'This is the second edition of a book about learning and education. The book is about how to do research. Compared with the first edition, this version includes some updates and improvements to provide more useful information for readers. The second part of the book is specially designed for younger children. It uses simpler explanations and more suitable examples to help children understand important ideas about learning. The new part adds additional content that was not included in the previous edition. These changes make the book more complete and provide a better learning experience for different age groups.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cce2b1f8-58a0-5e70-9c5b-843c0987fa9a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cce2b1f8-58a0-5e70-9c5b-843c0987fa9a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the case you use to carry documents?', '5b64a88c-4460-5654-a5df-babae260e203'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Briefcase / portfolio', NULL, NULL),
  ('cce7b891-f6fe-5812-b61a-edfc02bf67d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cce7b891-f6fe-5812-b61a-edfc02bf67d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ceb7f761-1874-5145-aca1-c97ca41f2c3f'::uuid, NULL, E'Please go straight and turn left to reach the library.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cceae53a-c6e8-5feb-ab95-e6e563f5c252'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cceae53a-c6e8-5feb-ab95-e6e563f5c252'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Spokesman', E'A spokesman for the project said: " a car mechanic for {{1}} could find at a glance where a part on a certain car model is so that it can be identified and repaired. For the motorist the system could {{2}} accident black spots or dangers on the road." In other cases the glasses could be worn by people going on a guided tour, {{3}} points of interest or by people looking at panoramas where all the sites could be identified.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.instance, 2.highlight, 3.indicating', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccf031c1-7419-5c94-9ec7-ca7ac9c59153'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccf031c1-7419-5c94-9ec7-ca7ac9c59153'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hieroglyphics', E'You''ve all seen hieroglyphics. Hieroglyphics was used by the ancient Egyptians to write with. It''s based on pictograms. However, for centuries, no one knew how to read it. Then in seventeen ninety nine, some french soldiers and Napoleon, Zara, me discovered there was at a stone in Egypt. It was part of a wall in an old ford in the town of Rosetta. It was originally located in an ancient temple, but it was later moved to the ford. The Rosetta stone had some writing on it. The writing was in three languages. One was ancient greek, one was demotic. Uh, that''s an ancient Egyptian language, and the other was hieroglyphics. All three languages contain the same information. It was a decree issued by some priest in one ninety six B.C. It was about the new pharaoh of Egypt, but telling me the fifth, the priest declared that patella me had been chosen to rule, and they said that they would honor put on a me with a feast. Each year. The text on the Rosetta stone became the key to understanding ancient Egyptian hieroglyphics. Scholars started to compare the three writings. They understood the ancient greek very well. The second writing demotic was less well known, but some scholars came to understand it. Eventually, after much work, scholars started to decipher what the picture symbols and hieroglyphics meant. Two men were involved in most of the important translation work. The first was Thomas Young, an english man. In eighteen fourteen, he made the first major discovery. He realized that the three tax contained the same information. He found about eighty words in the demotic and hieroglyphic text that were similar to words in ancient Greek. For example, the neighbor ptolemy was greek. It appears several times. In all three texts, young was able to figure out which symbols and demonic and hieroglyphics represented the name for ptolemy. The other scholar was a French man. His name was john for a small shampoo young. In eighteen twenty two, he produced an alphabet for hieroglyphics based on the Rosetta stone inscriptions. Later, he made a grammar and a dictionary for hieroglyphics. What?\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '12f211e0-9ac8-52f8-8083-6bfc4cae1470'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Some French soldiers found the Rosetta Stone in 1799 and it contained information in three languages. Thomas Young discovered about eighty words in each text that were similar and then Jean-Francois Champollion wrote a grammar and a dictionary of hieroglyphics.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccf1096f-1e2e-55e4-bf0c-add8656fa62b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccf1096f-1e2e-55e4-bf0c-add8656fa62b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'bdc5ebd8-0142-59e1-806e-eeadf188334b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'When met with high potential risks, companies will raise their prices.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccf640a3-4a9e-55cd-8f33-d3d19cda7f75'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccf640a3-4a9e-55cd-8f33-d3d19cda7f75'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c26308ff-7e97-5c53-933b-56b16962cfcc'::uuid, NULL, E'History is not a simple collection of dates and events.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ccfdaed1-2bad-5b90-abf7-9a40fd2b18b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccfdaed1-2bad-5b90-abf7-9a40fd2b18b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Aging Infrastructure', E'Aging infrastructure presents unique challenges for societies around the world, requiring investment in maintenance and upgrades to ensure safe and reliable transportation, communication, and energy systems. Failure to address these challenges can lead to economic stagnation and reduced quality of life for communities.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ccfe9371-99b1-59de-928c-43f5b2951ce0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccfe9371-99b1-59de-928c-43f5b2951ce0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Good Information', E'One of the characteristics of ''good'' information identified earlier was that it should be ''balanced''. In an ideal world, '' {{1}} '' or ''balanced'' information would present all the {{2}} for and against, and leave you to weigh this up and draw conclusions. In the real world, however, we recognize that all information presents a position of {{3}} , although this may not necessarily be intentional. Objectivity may therefore be an unachievable ideal. This means that the onus is on you as the reader and user of the information to develop a {{4}} awareness of the positions represented in what you read, and to take account of this when you interpret the information. In some cases, authors may explicitly express a particular viewpoint — this is perfectly valid as long as they are open about the perspective they represent. Hidden bias, whether or not it is {{5}} , can be misleading. This could be particularly important in a subject area where there is controversy.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.objective, 2.evidence, 3.interest, 4.critical, 5.deliberate', NULL, NULL),
  ('ccff48cf-841d-56e0-986f-da1c7865ee8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ccff48cf-841d-56e0-986f-da1c7865ee8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '63d120e6-83be-54cc-9c6c-7c69d270b98f'::uuid, NULL, E'Online availability of lecture notes is common practice among our teaching staff.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd05b77e-f50d-5a76-aac2-7ad95c9bab60'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd05b77e-f50d-5a76-aac2-7ad95c9bab60'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which short TV program or a part of TV program tell whether it will be sunny or rainy tomorrow?', 'fe121d1a-bd49-52a2-89d3-f32ad282c42d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Weather forecast / weather report', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd0eaeb7-b50e-5021-a315-c5c952ed5743'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd0eaeb7-b50e-5021-a315-c5c952ed5743'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fleeing', E'Many families are fleeing their native countries due to sectarian repression and political uprisings. Consequently, thousands of people have been stranded in foreign lands for months; other families have gone missing in the sea, marooned in small boats, as the neighboring foreign countries refuse to take them in.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd10b9e5-324e-5774-b1a7-bc893ba6f6d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd10b9e5-324e-5774-b1a7-bc893ba6f6d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '72ad290b-a375-5fa9-a401-693d592b0731'::uuid, NULL, E'Starting your studies at a new university can be exciting but overwhelming experience.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd1271a1-3b2b-570e-9119-bd40b032d484'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd1271a1-3b2b-570e-9119-bd40b032d484'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Migration', E'When migrating to warmer areas for winter, there are more feeding {{1}} available. One major {{2}} of migration is the need to find food resources. In colder climates, food varies little and often becomes scarce, while in warmer regions, birds and animals are able to find enough to {{3}} themselves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.opportunities, 2.cause, 3.sustain', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd12a295-0b8d-560a-9771-70854623374e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd12a295-0b8d-560a-9771-70854623374e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '19bd72be-5da8-5404-b2db-d228859d7c2a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'If the roots get damaged, the plant''s leaves will start to die.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd2b6116-321e-531c-a0b8-2aca22b99674'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd2b6116-321e-531c-a0b8-2aca22b99674'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hearing Loss', E'Long term exposure to noise can lead to loss of hearing. The relative loudness of sounds is measured in decibels. Just to give you an idea of what this means. The sound of a whisper is thirty decibels, while a normal conversation is sixty decibels. The noise of vacuum cleaner makes is around eighty five decibels. The danger zone, the risk of injury begins at around ninety. Continual exposure to sound above ninety decibels can damage your hearing loud noises, especially when they come at you every day. All this noise can damage the delicate hair cells in your inner ear. Lots of everyday noises are bad for us in the long run. For example, a car horn sounds at around one hundred decibels. A rock band at close range is one hundred and twenty five decibels. A jet engine at close range is one of the worst culprits at an ear busting one hundred and forty decibels. The first thing to go is your high frequency hearing, where you detect the consonant sounds in words. That''s why a person with hearing loss can hear voices, but has trouble understanding what''s being said.\n\nWhich sounds could contribute to hearing loss?', '62ded3c5-afa2-56e9-9f2f-df25ffdd04e1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A rock band at close range\nA jet engine at close range', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd2eaa10-26eb-59a1-8eaf-d0b857c748e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd2eaa10-26eb-59a1-8eaf-d0b857c748e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What color is the opposite of white on the color spectrum?', 'd3cd430a-080b-53c8-a8d2-be45c57b805b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Black', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd323c62-acd3-536e-a829-f856500550b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd323c62-acd3-536e-a829-f856500550b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nature of Friendship', E'To what extent do you think the Internet has changed the nature of friendships?', NULL, NULL, E'In the digital era, the Internet has redefined the way we form and maintain friendships, reshaping the essence of human connections. I firmly believe that the Internet has indeed changed the nature of friendships, influencing emotional connections, communication dynamics, and social interactions in negative ways.\nExcessive online communication can lead to a lack of genuine emotional connection in friendships. The convenience of digital interactions often prioritizes quantity over quality, resulting in shallow exchanges that may lack depth and emotional resonance. Without the nuances of face-to-face interactions, friendships formed primarily online may struggle to cultivate the authentic emotional bonds that are essential for meaningful relationships.\nMoreover, misinterpretations in online communication can cause misunderstandings and conflicts among friends due to the absence of non-verbal cues and tone, leading to potential miscommunication and message misinterpretation. This can strain relationships as differences in perception and understanding in online interactions may escalate into conflicts that could have been avoided with clearer communication in face-to-face conversations. Additionally, dependency on online interactions may diminish face-to-face social skills and interactions, impacting the quality of real-world relationships. Excessive engagement with friends online can impede the development of crucial social skills needed for effective communication and relationship-building offline, potentially limiting opportunities for meaningful face-to-face connections.\nIn conclusion, the Internet has brought about significant changes in the nature of friendships, with both positive and negative implications. While online communication offers convenience and connectivity, it can also lead to a lack of genuine emotional connection, misunderstandings, and a reduction in face-to-face social skills.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('cd32925e-70e8-5f7b-bd6f-1963cfc335c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd32925e-70e8-5f7b-bd6f-1963cfc335c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '2415c27f-d951-59e8-aa54-38936a214332'::uuid, NULL, E'The energy that we absorb from food can help us prevent the cold and become warmer.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd333577-b719-51ff-87d1-3986ff50ed1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd333577-b719-51ff-87d1-3986ff50ed1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f1577b10-6324-50a5-8840-26b2f032247d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cells are the basic building blocks of all animals and plants.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd37db77-ef0c-572b-a4ac-de8bda2edc35'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd37db77-ef0c-572b-a4ac-de8bda2edc35'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Technology Prediction', E'As far as prediction is concerned, remember that the chairman of IBM predicted in the fifties that the world would need a maximum of around half a dozen computers, that the British Department for Education seemed to think in the eighties that we would all need to be able to code in BASIC and that in the nineties Microsoft failed to foresee the rapid growth of the Internet. Who could have predicted that one major effect of the automobile would be to bankrupt small shops across the nation? Could the early developers of the telephone have foreseen its development as a medium for person to person communication, rather than as a form of broadcasting medium? We all, including the ''experts'', seem to be peculiarly inept at predicting the likely development of our technologies, even as far as the next year. We can, of course, try to extrapolate from experience of previous technologies, as I do below by comparing the technology of the Internet with the development of other information and communication technologies and by examining the earlier development of radio and print. But how justified I might be in doing so remains an open question. You might conceivably find the history of the British and French videotext systems, Prestel and Minitel, instructive. However, I am not entirely convinced that they are very relevant, nor do I know where you can find information about them online, so, rather than take up space here, I''ve briefly described them in a separate article.', NULL, NULL, E'We all, seem to be peculiarly inept at predicting the likely development of our technologies, like the world needing a maximum of around half a dozen computers in the fifties, our inability to code in BASIC in the eighties, and Microsoft''s failure to foresee the rapid growth of the Internet, by trying to extrapolate from the experience of previous technologies, with how justified we might be in doing so remaining an open question.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('cd389ddb-2f76-51ee-8616-e1e97082e2af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd389ddb-2f76-51ee-8616-e1e97082e2af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Melting Pot Theory', E'The melting pot theory of multiculturalism assumes that various immigrant groups will tend to “melt together,” abandoning their individual cultures and eventually becoming fully assimilated into the predominant society. Typically used to describe the assimilation of immigrants, this theory is often illustrated by the metaphor of a foundry’s smelting pots in which the elements iron and carbon are melted together to create a single, stronger metal—steel.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd394bc4-6e89-5d4f-a368-28f0016b040e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd394bc4-6e89-5d4f-a368-28f0016b040e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the treatment in which people use needles to ease others'' pain?', 'a3fcbb49-a1f4-5ebc-a7d2-0dfea80d1560'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Acupuncture', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd3a9699-8705-5135-9987-323e26d9d1cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd3a9699-8705-5135-9987-323e26d9d1cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Circadian Clock', NULL, '77ebbd50-d5d2-50a7-bb37-8c5cd82f30df'::uuid, NULL, E'So the first thing to notice is that while the mechanical clocks that we make, even your quartz watch can tell time across a vast range of scales from tens of milliseconds to hours minutes and days and months and years. So the brain has many different clocks in order to tell the milliseconds and seconds and to tell the time of days. So one way to think about it is the circadian clock, the clock that tells you what time of day it is and when to arise and when to go to sleep. That doesn’t have a minute hand, much less a second hand. In contrast the clock that tells you — the timing device in your brain that tells you, “Hmm, this red light is taking a bit too long to turn.” “This traffic light is taking a bit long to turn” or “I think the waiter forgot my coffee.” That clock doesn’t have an hour hand much less number of days that have gone by. So the brain has different areas, different mechanisms in order to tell time. We don’t understand, fully understand, how the brain tells you what the tempo of a song is or when the red light is going to change. But it doesn’t seem to have to do with any oscillator-counter mechanisms. It seems to do with neural dynamics which is the fact that patterns of neurons neurons are coupled to each other, neurons are connected next to each other. And when you activate some neurons that group of neurons can activate another group of neurons which can active another group of neurons. So you can have these evolving patterns of neural activity.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd41edc4-b4ac-5fe2-96c3-09c554f62136'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd41edc4-b4ac-5fe2-96c3-09c554f62136'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lake Turkana', E'Lake Turkana is a large lake in Kenya, East Africa. This {{1}} of Africa was home to some of the first humans. Here, archaeologists have found piles of {{2}} ( both human and animal) and collections of stones that humans used as {{3}} . By carefully uncovering and {{4}} these remains, scientists have started to put together the story of our earliest ancestors. In 2001, a 4 million year-old skeleton was uncovered in the area. Although a link between it and modern-day humans has not been established, the skeleton shows the species was walking upright.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.part, 2.bones, 3.tools, 4.examining', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd48019a-4c14-523e-81ef-6031692ab58f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd48019a-4c14-523e-81ef-6031692ab58f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Layers of Body', E'Published March 27 in Scientific Reports, a new study co-led by an NYU School of Medicine pathologist reveals that layers of the body long thought to be dense, connective tissues -- below the skin''s surface, lining the digestive tract, lungs and urinary systems, and surrounding arteries, veins, and the fascia between muscles -- are instead interconnected, fluid-filled compartments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd48cbb9-1a10-5e15-ba2f-eb8b6c3bbc97'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd48cbb9-1a10-5e15-ba2f-eb8b6c3bbc97'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e294b0fe-5696-59a2-8dc3-2f0b981bfbb0'::uuid, NULL, E'Remember your essay should have less than two thousand words.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd51dbac-c9a2-51f3-af13-31c6fe4c7b02'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd51dbac-c9a2-51f3-af13-31c6fe4c7b02'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '815788cb-3925-5432-8220-5cfeff7ee187'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Financial literacy should be taught at secondary school.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd534d40-663c-550b-81f2-bc6d783c9d92'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd534d40-663c-550b-81f2-bc6d783c9d92'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Paper Submission', E'You can only submit a paper by entering into the ''classroom'' of a class in which you are enrolled. Enter the classroom by clicking on the class name in your class portfolio. Your classroom page is divided into two broad sections: to the left is your assignment list and to the right is your portfolio. In your assignment list, to the right of the assignment that you must submit, you will see an icon of a document beneath the submit column. Click this to submit an assignment. You will now be asked to attach your assignment. Before you submit your assignment, you will need to copy the following declaration and paste at the top of your title page: l declare that this assignment is original and has not been submitted for assessment elsewhere, and acknowledge that the assessor of this assignment may, for the purpose of assessing this assignment:\n1. reproduce this assignment and provide a copy to another member of faculty; and(or)\n2.communicate a copy of this assignment to a plagiarism checking service (which may then retain a copy of this assignment on its database for the purpose of future plagiarism checking).\n\nWhat problem does the way a paper should be submitted address?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'students copying others’ work', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd5379c6-4019-5a05-a6ee-6ae634e32956'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd5379c6-4019-5a05-a6ee-6ae634e32956'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'When something has increased by triple, how many times does it increase?', '351e1503-790b-5a9a-8b44-016df95bd5a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Three times / three', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd53c91b-2ea5-572f-8d48-765f16261f9e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd53c91b-2ea5-572f-8d48-765f16261f9e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mic-robot', E'Each tube-shaped mic-robot is a sandwich of three materials. A graphene outer layer, which binds to heavy metals. A middle layer of nickel, which gives the bots magnetic polarity, so they can be pulled through wastewater with magnets. And platinum inside for propulsion. Just add a bit of peroxide to the wastewater, and it''ll react with the platinum to form water and oxygen bubbles, which propel the tubes along.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd5c87c7-276f-5d27-bfb9-4af68a56a68f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd5c87c7-276f-5d27-bfb9-4af68a56a68f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Socrates'' Defense', E'The translation aims foremost at accuracy and {{1}} , including the liveliness of the dialogue form. We have striven to preserve the natural {{2}} of the speech. This both helps and, in a way, hurts the readability of the translation. After all, these texts portray people speaking, and speaking to one another, and humans are not always the most {{3}} of speakers. This is recreated by Plato. Socrates'' Defense is almost entirely comprised of Socrates speaking at length to his judges and so he sometimes finds himself, because he goes on for quite a while, and keeps {{4}} qualifications, and then loses his way, and so he moves to a new grammatical construction. Similarly, characters sometimes {{5}} one clause on top of another. Usually these run-on sentences are easy to follow and the effect is often an increasing intensity, but once or twice in Socrates'' Defense Socrates seems rather to be finding his way into an idea and is less than eloquent.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.completeness, 2.flow, 3.eloquent, 4.inserting, 5.pile', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd663910-f7c0-5c44-b9aa-db36ad3cd335'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd663910-f7c0-5c44-b9aa-db36ad3cd335'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we call the animals that are kept on farms or as pets?', 'e28ca5c8-b926-52df-a738-104804f50555'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Domestic', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd6eeec0-c188-5987-9b28-8713ab6cbea0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd6eeec0-c188-5987-9b28-8713ab6cbea0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Work', E'By beginning so early, he knows that he has plenty of time to do thoroughly all the work he can be expected to do. All his work having been finished in good time, he has a long interval of rest in the evening before the timely hour when he goes to bed. After a sound night''s rest, he rises early next morning in good health and spirits for the labors of a new day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd77d729-b6e9-5b13-a1ef-fb9f154411db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd77d729-b6e9-5b13-a1ef-fb9f154411db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Summer Research Scholarships', E'Summer Research scholarships offer a unique opportunity for external organizations, academics, and students to work together in research. Working with globally recognized researchers in a local setting, students gain valuable real-world experience as well as an insight into what research is all about.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd8a6eb5-36f8-5f61-9871-17146d2b0c80'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd8a6eb5-36f8-5f61-9871-17146d2b0c80'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '61d97fba-2919-577f-bd9a-e433da26b812'::uuid, NULL, E'We often ask our students to get access to all sorts of services.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cd8b9d13-5965-5e38-83cb-f376c36d1398'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd8b9d13-5965-5e38-83cb-f376c36d1398'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the liquid in the pen?', 'e0853550-a74f-525e-9252-b075b26a9015'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ink', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd8ef76b-49fd-5021-85e6-db1272eda790'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd8ef76b-49fd-5021-85e6-db1272eda790'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Self-Concept', E'Early childhood is a time of forming an {{1}} sense of self. A self-concept or idea of who we are and what we are {{2}} of doing is a social process that involves taking into consideration how others view us. It might be said, then, that in order to develop a sense of self, you must have {{3}} with others.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.initial, 2.capable, 3.interaction', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd94f579-2508-5983-abb7-1f2b9c1b75ee'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd94f579-2508-5983-abb7-1f2b9c1b75ee'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0a79f5ff-d7e1-584b-a56f-5fa891c87765'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The toughest part of postgraduate education is funding.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cd9cab6e-9977-556f-a068-f4e83637bfc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cd9cab6e-9977-556f-a068-f4e83637bfc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '992420f4-8a63-5c84-9f55-7828366ae141'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Please note, submission deadlines are only negotiable in exceptional circumstances.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cda2fd0d-b4d0-597a-b00f-6d1be4827664'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cda2fd0d-b4d0-597a-b00f-6d1be4827664'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Shyness', NULL, '5fd64d94-a656-5c59-ba23-02f67bdebb16'::uuid, NULL, E'Today we''re going to talk about shyness and discuss recent research on ways to help children learn to interact socially. Many people consider themselves shy. In fact, forty percent of people who took part in our survey said they were shy. That''s two out of every five people. And there are studies to indicate that the tendency toward shyness may be inherited. But just because certain children are timid, doesn''t mean they are doomed to be shy forever. There are things parents, teachers, and the children themselves can do to overcome this tendency and even to prevent it. One researcher found that if parents gently push their shy children to try new things, they can help these children become less afraid and less inhibited. Another way to help shy children is to train them in social skills. For example, there are special training groups where children are taught things like looking at other children while talking to them, talking about other people''s interests, and even smiling. These groups have been very successful at giving shy children a place to feel safe and accepted, and at building up their self-esteem.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cda6c9c9-4263-5c93-a91c-d83230dea466'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cda6c9c9-4263-5c93-a91c-d83230dea466'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '31f4537d-d314-5487-a4d1-4e10fb78b495'::uuid, NULL, E'You can return items in person or by post.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cda7fe37-0c5a-5f97-9ae1-b038efd819e0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cda7fe37-0c5a-5f97-9ae1-b038efd819e0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Clinical Psychology', E'The professor is talking about clinical psychology. In order to know how behavior patterns can be changed. The clinical psychologist has to know what causes the client to behave the way he or she does. Identifying the cause is called diagnosis. In diagnosis, a psychologist uses two basic tools, interviews and psychological tests. Through interviews and tests, the psychologist tries to classify the problem to see if it falls into any non categories. A psychologist may also attempt to describe the client''s personality in terms of how he or she deals with life, for example, some people like to lead, and some prefer to follow the lead of others. Some people are active and outgoing, while others are quiet and reflective. In a diagnostic interview, the psychologist takes the client''s case history. This means learning how the client got along with parents, teachers, and friends, as well as how the person handle difficult situations in the past. Psychological testing is the other way that a psychologist tries to diagnose the clients problems. Clinical psychologists have developed tests that can help them learn about a person''s intelligence and personality, as well as tests that show whether a person''s behavior or perception is influenced by emotions, disabilities, or other factors. Personality testing is useful in discovering how the client tries to adjust to life. Personality tests can reveal unconscious feelings. The person is unable to talk about. This information can be important and could help shorten the length of treatment required.\n\nHow do clinical psychologists diagnose client''s problems?', '799a0542-bd6e-5360-93f6-931339a6c1ad'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Psychological tests\nInterviews', NULL, NULL),
  ('cdaada81-f93a-5873-b47f-0253fc13de20'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cdaada81-f93a-5873-b47f-0253fc13de20'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sun Temperature', E'The Sun provides the primary source of energy driving Earth’s climate system, but its {{1}} have played very little role in the climate changes {{2}} in recent decades. Direct satellite {{3}} since the late 1970s show no net increase in the Sun’s {{4}} , while at the same time global surface temperatures have increased.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.variations, 2.observed, 3.measurements, 4.output', NULL, NULL),
  ('cdab6c2b-31c0-5653-b597-5122759461d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cdab6c2b-31c0-5653-b597-5122759461d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Financial Markets', E'Financial markets swung wildly yesterday in the frenzied trading market by further selling of {{1}} and fears about an unraveling of the global carry trade. At the same time, trading in the US and European credit markets were exceptionally {{2}} for a third consecutive day. London trading was marked by particularly wild {{3}} in the prices of credit derivatives, used to ensure investors against {{4}} defaults.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.equities, 2.heavy, 3.swings, 4.corporate', NULL, NULL),
  ('cdac1f9d-1603-5109-b2f5-e4ec5324086b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cdac1f9d-1603-5109-b2f5-e4ec5324086b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cultural Attendance', E'A person''s demographic and social background can influence their attendance at cultural venues and events. Household composition, in particular, plays a significant role in shaping cultural preferences. For instance, families with young children are more likely to visit theme parks and amusement centers, while single individuals may be more inclined to attend concerts and art galleries.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
