  ('ce04dac7-49ef-5bd2-b158-f66f7497e1fa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce04dac7-49ef-5bd2-b158-f66f7497e1fa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sea Turtles', E'Like the sea turtles, we are {{1}} to the bright lights of our phones, tablets, laptops, and TVs, our minds and bodies becoming {{2}} as we lose focus and direction. Each day, we are {{3}} between the value of tech and the cost to our health.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.drawn, 2.disoriented, 3.torn', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce0e1938-7fdd-5bdc-b85a-70bd064a6d34'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce0e1938-7fdd-5bdc-b85a-70bd064a6d34'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Health Professionals', E'If you are {{1}} with your mental health, you may benefit from seeing a psychiatrist or a psychologist. But what is the difference between them and how can you find one? A psychiatrist is a medical doctor who can diagnose, treat and prevent mental disorders. They can {{2}} medication, such as antidepressants, and admit people to hospital if needed. They usually deal with severe mental health conditions, such as schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or psychosis. A psychologist is a registered health professional who can help people understand and change their behavior. They use different types of {{3}} and psychotherapy to help people cope with problems such as anxiety, depression, stress, trauma or addiction. They cannot give you medication, but they can work with a psychiatrist or a GP if {{4}} . Both psychiatrists and psychologists can help you develop better ways of thinking and behaving. They work in various settings, such as hospitals, clinics, schools, prisons or private practices. You can find them {{5}} your doctor, who can refer you to one and help you access Medicare rebates.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.struggling, 2.prescribe, 3.counselling, 4.needed, 5.through', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce0fb51e-b28b-5376-9244-584b508d18a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce0fb51e-b28b-5376-9244-584b508d18a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9917fb5a-3799-5bff-b247-de97ebdba673'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Momentum is defined as the combination of mass and velocity.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce11c70d-4df9-553e-9e42-1e74e3234b95'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce11c70d-4df9-553e-9e42-1e74e3234b95'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3fdca7c1-bd33-5a37-9c33-883dfd43fe4d'::uuid, NULL, E'Higher numbers of patients were infected than in previous outbreaks of the illness.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce1415ed-728e-56b2-a760-e44df7a98c77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce1415ed-728e-56b2-a760-e44df7a98c77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Home to Work Place', E'Do you think it has a positive or negative impact on you if you buy a home close to the workplace?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('ce1a856d-a362-559d-820f-9b3d79d086e8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce1a856d-a362-559d-820f-9b3d79d086e8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'fc84cc67-04cc-5e70-9ff8-5c074503050b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Her statement was a clear expression of her views on this program.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce1abbc3-469e-5fee-b907-413eb2e9a1dd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce1abbc3-469e-5fee-b907-413eb2e9a1dd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Freedom of Speech', NULL, '1b0109b9-3cbf-574f-8397-8ce858fbef06'::uuid, NULL, E'To be a British, the first important thing is the freedom of speech that we have. It doesn''t matter how small you are, how big you are, you are able to shout. I think security is very important. It''s a society that has democracy as its basic value. There are people who come from a third world which wasn''t a British colony where they didn''t have democracy such way they grew up under what I called a law lord. A system where the king or the local headman was the ruler of that particular area and he laid down the laws. And there are still parts of Africa as well as Middle East where the system still exists. They have to follow that ritual and that''s it, they cannot argue against it. Well, in our British society, we can argue. As the American saying, we can fight the city hall and this is one thing which is very unique among the western civilization. Is that any voice is heard, however small is, however big is, we have the equal authority.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce23fae0-37e9-5803-ba57-d8065a0d2a01'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce23fae0-37e9-5803-ba57-d8065a0d2a01'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Microorganisms', E'Identification and characterisation of microorganisms is a key part of the management of food safety and quality, tracing contaminants and troubleshooting problems such as spoilage. Knowing how to identify bacteria or other unknown microorganisms that you have encountered can help to assess whether it poses a safety concern or is likely to be heat resistant, for example.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce263dcb-8dc1-5cde-b498-04d10b378ac9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce263dcb-8dc1-5cde-b498-04d10b378ac9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Parent’s Born Order', E'Parents'' own born order can become an issue when dynamics in the family they are raising replicate the family in which they were raised. Agati notes common examples, such as a firstborn parent getting into "raging battles" with a firstborn child. "Both are used to getting the last word. Each has to be right. But the parent has to be the grown up and step out of that battle," he advises. When youngest children become parents, Agati cautions that because they "may not have had high expectations placed on them, they in turn may not see their kids for their abilities." But he also notes that since youngest children tend to be more social, "youngest parents can be helpful to their firstborn, who may have a harder time with social situations. These parents can help their eldest kids loosen up and not be so hard on themselves. Mom Susan Ritz says her own birth order didn''t seem to affect her parenting until the youngest of her three children, Julie, was born. Julie was nine years younger than Ritz''s oldest, Joshua, mirroring the age difference between Susan and her own older brother. "I would see Joshua do to Julie what my brother did to me," she says of the taunting and teasing by a much older sibling." I had to try not to always take Julie''s side." Biases can surface no matter what your own birth position was, as Lori Silverstone points out. "As a middle myself, I can be harder on my older daughter. I recall my older sister hitting me," she says of her reactions to her daughters'' tussles.', NULL, NULL, E'As biases can surface no matter what your own birth position was, parents'' own born order can become an issue when dynamics in the family they are raising replicate the family in which they were raised; a firstborn parent getting into "raging battles" with a firstborn child, but the parent has to be the grown up and step out of that battle.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('ce277363-6430-5196-8107-0ca38d5c3e10'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce277363-6430-5196-8107-0ca38d5c3e10'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cities and Trees', NULL, 'e4df59c4-e017-52d1-93aa-4dcd3bc3bdde'::uuid, NULL, E'We may think of nature as being unconnected to our urban spaces, but trees have always been an essential part of successful cities. Trees act like a natural sponge, absorbing storm water runoff before releasing it back into the atmosphere. The webs of their roots protect against mudslides while allowing soil to retain water and filter out toxins. Roots help prevent floods, while reducing the need for storm drains and water treatment plants. Their porous leaves purify the air by trapping carbon and other pollutants, making them essential in the fight against climate change. Humanity has been uncovering these arboreal benefits for centuries. But trees aren’t just crucial to the health of a city’s infrastructure; they play a vital role in the health of its citizens as well. In the 1870’s, Manhattan had few trees outside the island’s parks. Without trees to provide shade, buildings absorbed up to nine times more solar radiation during deadly summer heat waves. Combined with the period’s poor sanitation standards, the oppressive heat made the city a breeding ground for bacteria like cholera.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce29fd44-ecc6-524a-9189-5904af693756'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce29fd44-ecc6-524a-9189-5904af693756'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Workplace Diversity', E'Workplace diversity means respecting and valuing the skills and differences that each staff member brings into the workspace. A diverse workplace is an inclusive environment that provides equal rights and opportunities for all workers. In Australia, it is law for workplaces to create a workplace free from discrimination and harassment. Employers are responsible for putting measures into place to overcome employment disadvantage and discrimination in the workplace.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce3044fb-49b8-5235-ac26-e9a9cfec48d3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce3044fb-49b8-5235-ac26-e9a9cfec48d3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neurotechnology', E'Neurotechnology is advancing rapidly, creating new possibilities for reading and manipulating our minds. But what are the ethical implications of these developments? And how can we ensure that our mental privacy and {{1}} are not violated by companies or governments that want to access our brain data? These are some of the questions that a group of experts have been trying to answer. They {{2}} five new human rights for the age of neurotechnology, or neurorights: mental privacy, personal identity, free will, fair access to mental augmentation, and protection from bias. Some countries and states have {{3}} taken steps to enshrine these rights in law. Chile became the first nation to amend its constitution to include the right to mental privacy and the right to free will. Colorado {{4}} legislation that would protect neural data as sensitive health data.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.autonomy, 2.propose, 3.already, 4.passed', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce304716-5fec-5dc2-82c2-a4fc69c7d432'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce304716-5fec-5dc2-82c2-a4fc69c7d432'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Climate Change', E'Climate change poses significant challenges to agriculture, affecting crop {{1}} and farming practices worldwide. The agricultural sector must {{2}} to shifting weather patterns and increased extreme events, which requires an understanding of both climatology and plant science. Researchers in this field are at the {{3}} of developing resilient agricultural systems that can {{4}} the impacts of a changing climate.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.yields, 2.adapt, 3.forefront, 4.withstand', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce31b542-5c4b-570e-abeb-6ce489e4a9b4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce31b542-5c4b-570e-abeb-6ce489e4a9b4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Joseph Engelberger', E'Joseph Engelberger, a pioneer in industrial robotics, once remarked ''I can''t {{1}} a robot but I know one when I see one''. If you consider all the different {{2}} people {{3}} robots, you can see that it''s nearly impossible to come up with a {{4}} definition. Everybody has a {{5}} idea of what constitutes a robot.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.define, 2.machines, 3.call, 4.comprehensive, 5.different', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce3af3c1-8814-576d-b9c5-74200e592efa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce3af3c1-8814-576d-b9c5-74200e592efa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5318e20f-1b6e-5586-8a6f-47b0aab66fb3'::uuid, NULL, E'The African elephant is the largest living land mammal in the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce425df0-0afa-5819-871f-de29f68c0f6a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce425df0-0afa-5819-871f-de29f68c0f6a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Silk Road', NULL, '7a4aef90-4a90-550c-8723-ba4fc1cd87d6'::uuid, NULL, E'In today''s lecture, I''m delighted to take you back in time to explore the historical impact of the Silk Road. This ancient network of trade routes not only facilitated the exchange of goods but also acted as a bridge between civilizations, cultures, and ideas. The Silk Road, spanning from China to the Mediterranean, was instrumental in the trade of precious goods like silk, spices, tea, and gold. However, its significance extends beyond commerce. It was a conduit for cultural exchange, allowing for the movement of philosophies, religions, and even artistic styles across continents. This cross-cultural interaction played a crucial role in the development of the societies it connected. For example, the Silk Road facilitated the spread of Buddhism from India to East Asia and brought Chinese inventions like paper and gunpowder to the West. The legacy of the Silk Road is a testament to the power of connectivity and exchange. It shows how the interaction of diverse cultures can lead to the enrichment and advancement of human societies. In conclusion, the Silk Road was more than just a trade route; it was a symbol of cultural synthesis and collaboration that shaped the course of history, reminding us of the value of open exchange and interconnectedness in our globalized world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce43b120-07a7-53c8-b30f-136d1288231e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce43b120-07a7-53c8-b30f-136d1288231e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'If something such as fabric or medicine is artificially made, not natural, what do we say it is?', '86cf5f80-9aeb-523b-8035-2509eed8272b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Synthetic / artificial', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce493fdd-1d1c-5667-9347-6cf45bb3b19f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce493fdd-1d1c-5667-9347-6cf45bb3b19f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '90fb9aa2-68fb-5934-9618-4a9f2acb05f9'::uuid, NULL, E'I would like to make an appointment to see the professor.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce4a182d-8152-5b08-9e3a-f115589af40e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce4a182d-8152-5b08-9e3a-f115589af40e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Emerald', E'Emerald is defined by its green color. To be an emerald, a specimen must have a {{1}} green color that falls in the range from bluish green to green to slightly yellowish green. To be an emerald, the specimen must also have a rich color. Stones with weak saturation or light tone should be called "green beryl". {{2}} the beryl''s color is greenish blue then it is an "aquamarine". If it is greenish yellow it is "heliodor." This color definition is a source of {{3}} . Which hue, tone, and saturation combinations are the dividing lines between "green beryl" and "emerald"? Professionals in the gem and jewelry trade can disagree on where the lines should be {{4}} . Some believe that the name "emerald" should be used when chromium is the cause of the green color, and that stones colored by vanadium should be called "green beryl". Calling a gem an "emerald" instead of a "green beryl" can have a significant {{5}} upon its price and marketability. This "color confusion" exists within the United States. In some other countries, any beryl with a green color - no matter how faint - is called an "emerald".', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distinctly, 2.If, 3.confusion, 4.drawn, 5.impact', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce4c8e54-0baf-5623-8399-5d54dcf24a4a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce4c8e54-0baf-5623-8399-5d54dcf24a4a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '44d1eed8-9b38-5c30-b956-c28854ed78de'::uuid, NULL, E'I think of those leaders who inspire us to go beyond the call of duty.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce517ca5-690d-5360-83aa-f4f9408b0523'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce517ca5-690d-5360-83aa-f4f9408b0523'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'cb43aabc-bb2f-52c7-bd74-c7ae4d590c81'::uuid, NULL, E'The university has a number of travel scholarships that students can apply for.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce5790af-2462-50e6-a621-dd747a468155'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce5790af-2462-50e6-a621-dd747a468155'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urbanization Trend', E'The second big driver that will transform our future is, of course, demographics. 1 billion children are alive today, all of whom will be adults within the next eighteen years. ALL of them will see your Lifestyle on CNN or NBC even, if they don''t own a TV, they will see it through the door of the bar. They will see it through the posters on the side of the highway, even if they don''t own a car. 1 billion children, all of whom will consume resources. Linked to that, an urbanization trend, at a pace which we have never seen before. 300 million people in China alone will move from rural areas into cities in the next 8 or 9 years. Another 450 million people will move in Africa off the Land and into cities. Most of them, most city dwellers already live in slums. They have no running water, or maybe the very first service they have is access to a tap, a hundred meters away. They have, at the moment, very little access to electricity, but they''re there. And they''re demanding infrastructure, and their homes will grow from the one-story shack, to 2 storeys, to 3 storeys, and then once the mains water supply arrives another crisis comes. And of course, as you''ve seen it, which is the puddles of water everywhere, the drains that are full of soap and human waste, the earth that used to be dry, because people only carried 10 Liters 100 meters every 10 hours, now we have Leaking taps, we have sewage problems, and we have a whole host of other issues requiring more infrastructure.\n\nWhich of the following are mentioned as problems caused by urbanization?', 'f91be451-cf27-515f-9542-099ec035c536'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Rising infrastructure needs\nWorsening sanitary conditions', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce5960b5-8465-5457-8192-fab42aec77b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce5960b5-8465-5457-8192-fab42aec77b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Olympic', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 5, 3, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce5bd96c-ee94-58ad-8d08-272fc5746eef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce5bd96c-ee94-58ad-8d08-272fc5746eef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Creative Writing', E'This exciting new M.A. in Creative Writing is designed for graduates who wish to examine and expand their work. Through workshops, seminars, and {{1}} tutorials, students will discover new writing strategies and refine their writing. The course {{2}} students the practical expertise needed for researching and structuring texts, and {{3}} traditions and genres, as well as the critical and creative proficiencies {{4}} to develop a career in creative writing or in a related {{5}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.individual, 2.offers, 3.understanding, 4.necessary, 5.field', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce5edc1c-28c5-5a6e-9230-75e6abec5357'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce5edc1c-28c5-5a6e-9230-75e6abec5357'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fd2ab9c7-26c1-5437-8d9d-3431f2504924'::uuid, NULL, E'Psychologists use a range of techniques to study the human mind and behavior.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce618bad-a634-51ec-8e48-dfdae0cedd63'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce618bad-a634-51ec-8e48-dfdae0cedd63'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Procrastination', E'To overcome procrastination you need to have an understanding of the reasons why you procrastinate and the function procrastination serves in your life. You can''t come up with an effective solution if you don''t really understand the root of the problem. As with most problems, awareness and self-knowledge are the keys to figuring out how to stop procrastinating.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce656d0b-caeb-56eb-bd6b-d33f35e7b13e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce656d0b-caeb-56eb-bd6b-d33f35e7b13e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'bdb62644-857d-5756-a62c-9921103fa82c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You can buy things for school at the shop for students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce6c5162-2d49-513f-8747-799649ef8793'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce6c5162-2d49-513f-8747-799649ef8793'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '420a2e0e-9067-51aa-b7ab-c490c1f8ed6c'::uuid, NULL, E'Hospitals now tend to discharge patients earlier than in the past.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce6ca5cc-2ad0-59db-b409-f9179e240b7e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce6ca5cc-2ad0-59db-b409-f9179e240b7e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'End of Days', E'The idea that Western power and influence is in gradual decline, perhaps as a prelude to a {{1}} fall, has been around for a while. But it has gained a new urgency with recent political events, not least the election of US president Donald Trump. For some, his turning away from international commitments is part of fulfilling his promise to “make America great again” by {{2}} on its own interests. For others, it’s a dangerous move that threatens to undermine the whole world order. Meanwhile, over in the old world, Europe is {{3}} in its own problems. Using science to predict the future isn’t easy, not least because both “collapse” and “Western civilization” are difficult to define. We talk about the collapse of the Roman Empire in the middle of the first millennium, for example, but there is plenty of evidence that the empire existed in some form for centuries afterwards and that its influence {{4}} today. So, when we talk about collapse, do we mean that people lose everything and go back to the dark ages? Or that it’s going to be socially and politically turbulent for a while?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.precipitous, 2.concentrating, 3.mired, 4.lingers', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce7150e3-d16a-591d-baf0-63fe4d020075'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce7150e3-d16a-591d-baf0-63fe4d020075'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'dde95bb7-b1d6-5877-a4e1-dc524a2042ae'::uuid, NULL, E'It is clear that there is little accurate documentation in support of this claim.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce7d6892-3e0a-51c8-812a-d7220fbbc709'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce7d6892-3e0a-51c8-812a-d7220fbbc709'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c9f57748-682f-5756-a3bc-185c1d2ae4c5'::uuid, NULL, E'None of the students found it difficult to get a job.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce7ecc93-72b3-5307-8968-5a4fdebaa260'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce7ecc93-72b3-5307-8968-5a4fdebaa260'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '32c90ef8-ec6d-5298-95dd-d1b5ac91df64'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The company needs to polish its image.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce8223ef-77ed-554d-aa32-b2b818866c86'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce8223ef-77ed-554d-aa32-b2b818866c86'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Arabic Students', E'HERIOT-WATT University in Edinburgh has become the first in Europe to offer an MBA in Arabic. Arab students will be able to sign up to study at a {{1}} for the business courses in their own language. The Edinburgh Business School {{2}} the project at a reception in Cairo on Saturday. It is hoped the course will improve links between the university and the Arab business world. A university spokeswoman said: "The Arabic MBA will {{3}} the profile of Heriot-Watt University and the Edinburgh Business School among businesses in the Arabic speaking world and will create a strong network of graduates in the {{4}} .” The first {{5}} of students is expected later this year. Professor Keith Lumsden, director of Edinburgh Business School, said: "Arabic is a major global language and the Arab world is a center for business and industrial development. We are proud to work with Arab International Education to {{6}} the demands of the region."', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.distance, 2.announced, 3.raise, 4.region, 5.intake, 6.meet', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce845e6f-8c1f-5b60-bfeb-ac2badb8d761'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce845e6f-8c1f-5b60-bfeb-ac2badb8d761'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the first paragraph of a report?', 'a2b9164e-b0f3-592f-903b-36b58b6f4cc4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Introduction', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce888d6a-edee-590f-b8df-d3e5fe6ea3b8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce888d6a-edee-590f-b8df-d3e5fe6ea3b8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Negotiation', E'We constantly negotiate at work. We negotiate for higher pay, promotions, vacations and even greater autonomy. In fact, every day we negotiate just to get our job done and to secure resources for ourselves and our teams. And yet when we go in with the wrong mindset, with a fist up ready to fight, we aren''t as successful. You know why? Because negotiation is not about dominating. It''s about crafting a relationship.\nAnd relationships thrive when we find ways to give and to take and move together in unison. And to do that, you have to be well prepared.\nFirst, do your research. Figure out whether what you''re asking for is realistic. What is your aspiration? What do you want, and what will make you walk away from the table? This might seem obvious, but too many people don’t think it through.\n\nWhat can we infer from the passage about negotiation?', '3adcc9bb-0dbb-5909-a843-c6c959aceb6e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'If your demands do not match reality, the negotiation may fail.\nNegotiation is not about holding your fist up for a fight. It''s about taking and giving.\nWe negotiate for what we want, such as salaries or promotions in work.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce895e86-effd-5534-9f86-7278515d7ca7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce895e86-effd-5534-9f86-7278515d7ca7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'aadf3f87-b1d1-552f-8446-ab93fa7c4fc2'::uuid, NULL, E'The students are supposed to assemble in the seminar hall before the announcement.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce8d26e2-1d44-57d2-a275-0c631618ecd0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce8d26e2-1d44-57d2-a275-0c631618ecd0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Turbine Blade', E'It’s not easy to make a wind turbine blade. Conventional blades require a lot of labor. They are a sandwich composed of fiberglass, sheets of balsa wood and a chemical called an epoxy thermoset resin. A heat oven is required to give blades the proper shape, strength, smoothness and flexibility to catch the wind and turn the turbine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce8e7b83-91b9-52dc-aff6-59472da37f94'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce8e7b83-91b9-52dc-aff6-59472da37f94'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Legal Writing', E'Legal writing is usually less discursive than writing in other humanities subjects, and precision is more important than variety. Sentence structure should not be too complex; it is usually unnecessary to make extensive use of adjectives or adverbs, and consistency of terms is often required.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ce90d019-3dd9-5e93-b96b-8f8078175bf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce90d019-3dd9-5e93-b96b-8f8078175bf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hearing Care', E'The profile and causes of hearing loss vary greatly across and within regions, as does the availability of {{1}} and resources to address it. It is important that each country develop its own {{2}} plan to deal with hearing loss and its causes. A national ear and hearing care strategy should seek to reduce the {{3}} , incidence and impact of hearing loss in the community.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.infrastructure, 2.strategic, 3.prevalence', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce9754f9-5bb1-5064-98b8-510fc902ed9e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce9754f9-5bb1-5064-98b8-510fc902ed9e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '57e336e9-bd12-5383-85f3-c3e1fbdbe169'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'We study how tropical storms work and how to predict them.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce9dc393-541a-5c05-b8ca-ebd01aa3c828'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ce9dc393-541a-5c05-b8ca-ebd01aa3c828'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Catholics', E'Catholics venerate the saints and look to them as examples of lives well lived in the faith. Many find comfort in the {{1}} that holy people shared in their same struggles, sins, doubts, or hardships and ask specific saints to pray for them. Some saints are the patrons of certain occupations or causes, and these saints are often invoked to aid people in those professions or situations. For example, St. Judas (Jude) is the patron saint of impossible or {{2}} causes, and many Catholics ask him to pray on their behalf for the {{3}} of seemingly impossible situations in their lives. Additionally, many Catholics take or are given a saint''s name for their confirmation. A confirmation saint is often seen as having an invested interest in {{4}} a new Catholic''s spiritual growth and is usually chosen because his or her life story {{5}} with the neophyte. Most saints have feast days observed by the Catholic Church in which their lives and contributions are formally celebrated, and some have large followings of devotees and even religious orders in their honor.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.knowledge, 2.desperate, 3.resolution, 4.fostering, 5.resonates', NULL, NULL),
  ('cea33d3d-dbda-57af-a570-5526169d2024'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cea33d3d-dbda-57af-a570-5526169d2024'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the joint that joins the leg to the rest of the body?', 'e08cc9ec-ecc3-5c37-9ebd-0069012c4082'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Hip joint', NULL, NULL),
  ('cea443f9-76f7-56de-b6ce-b4cee9b42479'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cea443f9-76f7-56de-b6ce-b4cee9b42479'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Window in Painting', E'We can see from the X-rays that at an early stage of painting, a window was painted at the left of the portrait. It seems that there may have been two windows in the initial design for the portrait or that the window was moved at an early stage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
