  ('cf01309f-35cd-5336-b849-14216a634190'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf01309f-35cd-5336-b849-14216a634190'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Teaching Machine', E'In 1953 Skinner visited his daughter’s maths class. The Harvard psychologist found every pupil learning the same topic in the same way at the same speed. A few days later he built his first "teaching machine", which let children tackle questions at their own pace. By the mid-1960s similar gizmos were being flogged by door-to-door salesmen. Within a few years, though, enthusiasm for them had fizzled out.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf0652f3-0227-5be2-9222-42caf3f89025'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf0652f3-0227-5be2-9222-42caf3f89025'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '08bb4d97-e318-557c-b049-238cf003836e'::uuid, NULL, E'Keeping organized class notes will make study time more efficient.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf07c3c3-20f9-5fb0-a2dc-56b1d306517a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf07c3c3-20f9-5fb0-a2dc-56b1d306517a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '434719e9-5bf3-5de0-9958-aad03ae9a2ff'::uuid, NULL, E'Please always keep the keys with you because the front door often locks automatically.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf10b325-62aa-5c55-881a-b64fb74c266f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf10b325-62aa-5c55-881a-b64fb74c266f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9eda6065-d1ba-5705-a7fb-4d47716c0adb'::uuid, NULL, E'The chemistry building is located near the entrance of the campus.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf1a2816-829a-50d3-8009-e977278e3588'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf1a2816-829a-50d3-8009-e977278e3588'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dangerous Activities', E'Many people engage in dangerous activities, such as sky-diving, skiing and extreme motorcycling. Are you in favor of such activities or not? Why?', NULL, NULL, E'In recent years, there has been a surge of interest in dangerous activities such as sky-diving, skiing, and extreme motorcycling. While some may view these activities as risky and unnecessary, I believe that they have several positive benefits. In this essay, I will discuss the advantages of engaging in such activities.\nOne of the most significant benefits of engaging in dangerous activities is the potential for personal growth. These activities require individuals to step outside of their comfort zones and face their fears, which can lead to increased confidence and self-esteem. Additionally, participating in these activities can help individuals develop important skills such as discipline, focus, and mental toughness, all of which can be applied to other areas of life.\nEngaging in dangerous activities can also provide a sense of freedom and adventure. These activities allow individuals to experience a level of excitement and adrenaline that is difficult to find elsewhere. For many people, these activities represent an escape from the monotony of everyday life and a chance to explore new horizons.\nIn conclusion, while some may view dangerous activities as unnecessary risks, I believe that they have several positive benefits. Engaging in such activities can promote personal growth, and provide a sense of freedom and adventure. However, it is important to approach these activities with caution and take necessary safety precautions. By doing so, we can continue to enjoy the benefits of these activities while minimizing the risks involved.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('cf256727-5aaa-5eb3-8e81-41856b00504c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf256727-5aaa-5eb3-8e81-41856b00504c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5ecdde4c-791c-5916-8cbb-648e2d83b0c6'::uuid, NULL, E'The technician left the new microscope in the biology lab.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf257f15-2d29-5d2e-b48c-bd4d40f282b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf257f15-2d29-5d2e-b48c-bd4d40f282b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the name of the ancient Greek city-state known for its artistic and intellectual achievements?', '9471d3bd-1298-52c6-a52e-c85aa934b8d1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Athens', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf2eb28f-c64f-5c06-9024-db3a7a7acb93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf2eb28f-c64f-5c06-9024-db3a7a7acb93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ed12eed8-d8a0-5fcf-a33a-c01e59cc6dd7'::uuid, NULL, E'May I record our lecture today with a video camera?', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf30d1ff-2995-559f-afbe-c5cad23f6dc9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf30d1ff-2995-559f-afbe-c5cad23f6dc9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'caf7235f-4282-52a6-b148-b97afdf4fdcf'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Your thesis should have a fairly limited scope.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf31f394-45d7-5677-9607-da1077f0dc52'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf31f394-45d7-5677-9607-da1077f0dc52'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dependance on Technology', E'Do you agree that people are too dependent on technology?', NULL, NULL, E'In the midst of the digital revolution, there is a prevailing notion that people have become excessively reliant on technology for various aspects of their lives. However, a closer examination reveals that while technology plays a significant role in modern society, individuals are not as dependent on it as commonly perceived. This essay explores the positive standpoint that people are not overwhelmingly reliant on technology and highlights the resilience and adaptability of individuals in navigating the digital landscape.\nContrary to the belief that technology dependency is ubiquitous, many individuals exhibit a balanced approach to technology use. While technology enhances convenience and efficiency, people demonstrate the ability to disconnect and engage in offline activities. Whether through mindfulness practices, hobbies, or outdoor pursuits, individuals actively seek moments of unplugged time to rejuvenate and connect with the world beyond screens. This intentional balance showcases a conscious effort to maintain autonomy and control over technology use.\nFurthermore, human ingenuity and creativity remain at the forefront of innovation, shaping technology to suit individual needs and preferences. Rather than being passive consumers of technology, individuals actively participate in its development and evolution. The diverse ways in which people customize technology to enhance productivity, creativity, and personal growth underscore the dynamic relationship between humans and technology. This proactive engagement demonstrates that while technology is a valuable tool, it does not dictate or dominate every aspect of human life.\nIn conclusion, the narrative of overwhelming dependency on technology overlooks the agency and adaptability of individuals in managing their relationship with digital tools. While technology has undoubtedly transformed society, people demonstrate a capacity to maintain autonomy and balance in their interactions with technology.', NULL, 200, 300);
