  ('cf32e44b-f9c4-503d-9e8e-a061c3b1b2ea'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf32e44b-f9c4-503d-9e8e-a061c3b1b2ea'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Climate', E'Climate is the word we {{1}} for weather over a long period of time. The desert has a dry climate because there is very little rain. The UK {{2}} a ‘temperate climate’, {{3}} means winters are, overall, mild and {{4}} , generally, don’t get too hot.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.use, 2.has, 3.which, 4.summers', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf38af45-f886-5fe6-8d7a-7c95efba751a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf38af45-f886-5fe6-8d7a-7c95efba751a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ad29b560-916d-5d4a-8336-b4041f78d13a'::uuid, NULL, E'To take this course students should have basic subject knowledge.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf43b1be-8a58-53ad-96e4-96962443b90f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf43b1be-8a58-53ad-96e4-96962443b90f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Crime', E'Why do we have crime? When will it all stop? IT''s sad that there is so much crime in our society. It hurts so many people. Most people in the world just want to live happily and be good neighbors. Why do some people turn to crime? Money is a big reason. Many criminals pickpocket, steal, kidnap or even kill people to get money. There are many terrible crimes in the world. Perhaps the worst is ethnic cleansing. This is a crime against humanity. Many people are killed because of their color or religion. People who commit this crime really go to prison. Have you ever been a victim of crime? What do you think we need to do to reduce crime rates? Perhaps you should run.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'e473d98b-0bfa-54a2-b014-1f08e818e53a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'to your government', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf468950-2be3-56c0-8bbd-44a0aa3537d6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf468950-2be3-56c0-8bbd-44a0aa3537d6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Skyrocketing Bills', E'Across Europe, electricity and gas prices are skyrocketing – this is a massive {{1}} for large sections of the population. In Greece, too, energy bills have risen {{2}} in recent months. Since the financial and economic crisis, many people are living on the {{3}} of poverty.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.burden, 2.sharply, 3.edge', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf47ee97-a06a-510c-b7b6-6d6c0ccd2bb0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf47ee97-a06a-510c-b7b6-6d6c0ccd2bb0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mosquitoes', E'Okay, so we''ve discussed the mosquitoes appearance and life cycle. Now let''s cover what mosquitoes are most famous for sucking blood. Mosquitoes suck blood from various animals. You see a a mosquito has a long feeder appendage in its mouth. The appendage penetrates an animal skin, then the mosquito sucks the animals''blood. Interestingly, only females suck blood. The blood they get enables them to reproduce. How so proteins in the blood they suck help them produce the eggs they lay, so they don''t use the bloodiest food for food. Both female and male mosquitoes usually nectar from plants. Tragically, mosquitoes kill more people than any other creature on earth. Their bites don''t kill though, but the diseases that mosquitoes carry do millions of people die every year from malaria, dengue fever, yellow fever, and other diseases that mosquitoes carry. When mosquitoes bite people, they transmit whatever diseases they happen to be carrying. Each year, more than two million people die from mosquito carry diseases. That''s a big number, huh? Unfortunately, controlling mosquitoes is difficult, since they breed and spread rapidly. They lay their eggs in stagnant water, like, um, in swamps. So draining these areas can control them. Insecticides, you know, insect killers can also eliminate them. D d t is one such insecticide. IT''s highly effective, but it''s banned in many countries. Some people claim that ddt harm certain animals. Still, in countries that use ddt, there are fewer deaths by disease is transmitted by mosquitoes.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'b15c2869-393f-54da-97db-e291c452d97e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mosquitoes cause some problems. Sucking animal’s blood enables female mosquitoes to reproduce. Mosquitoes kill more people than any other creature on Earth and the way to control them is difficult.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf48f016-ef63-50b6-8410-8e9f8f8fcef2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf48f016-ef63-50b6-8410-8e9f8f8fcef2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the 25th letter that we use to write English words?', 'daa08c5b-94a7-5aae-9710-3c7d1102d801'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Y', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf52f6a7-45d3-56f1-b02b-4355127d963d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf52f6a7-45d3-56f1-b02b-4355127d963d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '24dc8cf2-0846-5523-81b4-0b6a5d6742f3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'It showed that people are struggling in their lives.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf53930c-acb1-5737-b61e-53fe0560f337'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf53930c-acb1-5737-b61e-53fe0560f337'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Gene Sequencing', E'Scientists have completed the sequences for the coast redwood, which helps to better explain the genetic basis for these species’ ability to adapt to their changing environments. The research indicates that the coast redwood genome evolved from a single ancestral species. The coast redwood is the world’s tallest tree, and its genome is among the most complex sequenced. When comparing the coast redwood genome sequence to that of other conifers, researchers found hundreds of gene families unique to the coast redwood. Many are genes that help the trees respond to and fight stress, resist disease and repair after injury.\n\nAccording to the passage, which statement is true about coast red wood?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'It has genes that are beneficial to recovery.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf5c3203-e231-513e-8db2-dd1a3b4d2f50'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf5c3203-e231-513e-8db2-dd1a3b4d2f50'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fossil Fuels', E'But look beyond fossil fuels for the most intriguing trends. One is that the energy intensity of the world economy - the amount of energy it takes to produce one dollar''s {{1}} of income - keeps falling, at a rate of about 2 percent. What this means is that even without any change in the {{2}} shares of fossil-based and fossil-free sources in the world''s energy mix, we could have 2 percent annual economic growth without increasing carbon emissions from energy use. Of course that is not enough to {{3}} climate change and we need more economic growth than that. It is {{4}} a stunning number, which refutes the claim by some environmentalists that permanent economic growth is fundamentally incompatible {{5}} finite physical resources.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.worth, 2.relative, 3.address, 4.nonetheless, 5.with', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf5f7129-0732-5f1f-af51-58b46780c527'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf5f7129-0732-5f1f-af51-58b46780c527'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Solar Power', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 4, 2', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf611cc9-1536-5bc7-8705-85e3affd1e22'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf611cc9-1536-5bc7-8705-85e3affd1e22'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e308f22c-3d65-5efa-9286-b7589c76f0ef'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Social psychology is concerned with the understanding of human behavior.', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf616a29-81af-5b10-aa79-757d741d8bc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf616a29-81af-5b10-aa79-757d741d8bc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Introverts and Extroverts', E'For an introvert, lots of energetic social time can {{1}} to sensory overload. People like me just {{2}} to be happier with our own company and feel our best after some alone time. Introverts can {{3}} toward activities that are more thoughtful and solitary and are often considered to be {{4}} or reflective.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.lead, 2.tend, 3.gravitate, 4.reserved', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf65fae7-fab9-5ce2-bbe1-e9de39799027'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf65fae7-fab9-5ce2-bbe1-e9de39799027'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Artificial Intelligence', E'Artificial intelligence has been one of the most controversial domains of inquiry in computer science since it was first proposed in the 1950s. Defined as the part of computer science concerned with designing systems that exhibit the characteristics associated with human intelligence understanding language, learning, reasoning, solving problems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('cf66010b-5472-57ba-8eeb-097401fea980'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf66010b-5472-57ba-8eeb-097401fea980'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mothers'' Employment', E'Affordable early years education and childcare potentially enables parents, particularly mothers, to be in paid employment. International studies {{1}} that countries with greater enrolment rates in publicly funded or provided childcare also have higher maternal employment rates, although untangling causal relationships is complex. From the point of view of the household, additional income, especially for the less well-off, is itself associated with better outcomes for children, as child poverty {{2}} to be a key independent determinant of children''s outcomes. From the point of view of the public purse, as mothers {{3}} employment, they are likely to claim fewer benefits and to generate extra revenues {{4}} income tax and national insurance contributions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.have found, 2.has been shown, 3.enter, 4.through', NULL, NULL),
  ('cf6b548b-6539-53ea-a7a5-ad813bef9da4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'cf6b548b-6539-53ea-a7a5-ad813bef9da4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'World of Elephants', E'Elephants, the largest land animals on Earth, captivate us with their sheer size, intelligence, and gentle demeanor. These magnificent creatures have long held a special place in our hearts and the animal kingdom, representing a harmonious blend of power and grace. Elephants are renowned for their exceptional memory, social bonds, and complex communication skills. These qualities are prominently displayed within their tight-knit family groups, which are led by a matriarch — the oldest and wisest female. The family structure and intricate relationships within elephant herds are awe-inspiring and provide valuable insights into animal behavior and cognition. These gentle giants are also known for their emotional depth. Elephants can display a wide range of emotions, from joy and playfulness to grief and empathy. They mourn their dead, even returning to the remains of deceased herd members years after their passing, showcasing their profound emotional connections.\nDespite their remarkable intelligence and emotional capacity, elephants face significant challenges in the wild. Habitat loss, poaching for ivory, and human-wildlife conflicts threaten their survival. Conservation efforts are critical to ensuring the continued existence of these magnificent creatures. Efforts to protect and conserve elephants include anti-poaching initiatives, the establishment of protected areas, and public awareness campaigns to reduce demand for ivory products. Additionally, responsible tourism practices promote ethical interactions with elephants in captivity, ensuring their well-being. Elephants are not just charismatic megafauna; they are vital to the ecosystems they inhabit. They disperse seeds, create water holes, and shape their environment, making them keystone species with an essential role in maintaining biodiversity.', NULL, NULL, E'Elephants are renowned for their exceptional memory, social bonds, and complex communication skills, as well as their emotional depth, but elephants face significant challenges in the wild; conservation efforts are critical to ensuring their continued existence, because they are vital to the ecosystems they inhabit.', NULL, 5, 75),
