  ('d00ffac8-9d5b-5634-ab87-aa963246f5b7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd00ffac8-9d5b-5634-ab87-aa963246f5b7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Power of Music', NULL, '12fa2225-125e-51c6-83f3-3fd0ce5f73d7'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, I''m thrilled to explore the transformative power of music, a universal language that transcends cultural and linguistic barriers. Music, in its various forms, is not just a source of entertainment; it''s a profound medium for expressing emotions and connecting people across the globe. Music''s influence on human emotion is unparalleled. It has the ability to evoke deep feelings, from joy to sorrow, and can impact our mood and mental state. This emotional connection is why music is often used therapeutically, helping to relieve stress and promote well-being. Additionally, music serves as a cultural bridge, fostering understanding and unity among diverse groups. It reflects the history, struggles, and triumphs of different communities, offering insights into various cultural identities. Through music, we can experience the world from different perspectives, enhancing empathy and connection. Moreover, the evolution of music, from classical symphonies to modern pop, reflects the ongoing innovation and creativity of humankind. It adapts and evolves with societal changes, capturing the zeitgeist of different eras. In conclusion, music is a powerful tool that enriches our lives, offering both solace and celebration. Its ability to resonate with our deepest emotions and bridge cultural divides showcases its indispensable role in human society.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d0110691-28bd-5a22-b7a8-0e402049dd5c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd0110691-28bd-5a22-b7a8-0e402049dd5c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neutron Stars', E'Neutron stars — the compressed remains of massive stars gone supernova — are the densest "normal" objects in the known universe (black holes are technically denser, but far from normal). Just a single sugar-cube worth of neutron-star material would weigh 100 million tons here on Earth, or about the same as the entire human population.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d011397b-fc14-5cd6-973d-2eca1c5e2b82'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd011397b-fc14-5cd6-973d-2eca1c5e2b82'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a6b5ae62-c2e2-5cbb-8f5e-2c1d2d5704f0'::uuid, NULL, E'The university''s online courses provide flexible learning options for students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
