  ('d017fac6-0e26-5653-b5e8-439fbb520771'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd017fac6-0e26-5653-b5e8-439fbb520771'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4cede70d-fe0b-5ae0-b1c5-2b7461565523'::uuid, NULL, E'Submit your portfolio to the internal review office by Tuesday at the latest.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d0181057-87ed-5be3-85c9-c8fdb9e6e0cc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd0181057-87ed-5be3-85c9-c8fdb9e6e0cc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0753bf08-c056-505a-ba08-699b94c3f1bf'::uuid, NULL, E'In order to achieve the educational goals, tutors often have to encourage students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d01cd6f8-cca6-5e84-bf66-afdb82677f04'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd01cd6f8-cca6-5e84-bf66-afdb82677f04'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tutankhamun', E'The last tourists may have been leaving the Valley of the Kings on the West Bank in Luxor but the area in front of the tomb of Tutankhamun remained far from deserted. Instead of the {{1}} that usually descends on the area in the evening it was a hive of activity. TV crews trailed masses of equipment, journalists milled and photographers held their cameras at the ready. The reason? For the first time since Howard Carter {{2}} the tomb in 1922 the mummy of Tutankhamun was being prepared for public display.\nInside the subterranean burial chamber Egypt''s archaeology supremo Zahi Hawass, {{3}} by four Egyptologists, two restorers and three workmen, were slowly lifting the mummy from the golden sarcophagus where it has been rested -- mostly undisturbed -- for more than 3,000 years. The body was then placed on a wooden stretcher and {{4}} to its new home, a high- tech, climate-controlled plexi-glass showcase located in the outer chamber of the tomb where, covered in linen, with only the face and feet exposed, it now greets visitors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.tranquility, 2.discovered, 3.accompanied, 4.transported', NULL, NULL),
  ('d01d60e3-1bc6-5a1f-b22b-8a4ce3a3e954'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd01d60e3-1bc6-5a1f-b22b-8a4ce3a3e954'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mosquito''s Feet', E'Mosquitoes are a summertime menace...but they''re also a {{1}} of mechanical engineering. They can stick to your skin, {{2}} to a wall, and even walk on water. Now a team of physicists from China and Canada have {{3}} out how they do it.\nThe {{4}} is in the feet. First off, mosquitoes have tiny {{5}} on their tootsies , which they use to latch onto skin. And they hang onto walls the same way geckos do...using hairy little foot pads that let them stick to surfaces like they''re wearing Velcro socks.\nBut it''s their water walking that may be their most {{6}} , er, feat. To dance across a pond...or stand atop a puddle... mosquitoes use their superhydrophobic legs. These limbs are so phenomenally water repellant...that each one could effectively support 23 times the insect''s weight. At least that''s what the physicists discovered when they took a single mosquito leg and {{7}} the force needed to push it into a cup of water.\nThe reason the legs are so hydrophobic is because they''re coated with tiny, featherlike scales...that are in turn covered by even tinier ribbing. So next time you swat a skeeter, remember: you just whacked a wonder of nature.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.marvel, 2.cling, 3.figured, 4.trick, 5.hooks, 6.remarkable, 7.measured', NULL, NULL),
  ('d01e6889-c01f-522a-8e2a-c000c90eecc7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd01e6889-c01f-522a-8e2a-c000c90eecc7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4ecb0f4f-5d98-5ee0-ae86-e00c1a84eaf3'::uuid, NULL, E'I know most of you come to the National Park for Mt. Field.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
