  ('d2e3f0b0-c457-54ce-87fa-c6abb4738fd4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd2e3f0b0-c457-54ce-87fa-c6abb4738fd4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hotter Earth', E'There''s no question that the Earth is getting hotter. The real questions are: How much of the warming is our fault, and are we {{1}} to slow the devastation by controlling our insatiable {{2}} for fossil fuels?\nGlobal warming can seem too {{3}} to worry about, or too uncertain-something projected by the same computer {{4}} that often can''t get next week''s weather right. On a raw winter day you might think that a few degrees of warming wouldn''t be such a bad thing anyway. And no doubt about it: Warnings about {{5}} change can sound like an environmentalist scare tactic, meant to force us out of our cars and restrict our lifestyles.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.willing, 2.appetite, 3.remote, 4.techniques, 5.climate', NULL, NULL),
