  ('d3e9baac-db7a-5ebf-91f5-7cd90541e1c0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd3e9baac-db7a-5ebf-91f5-7cd90541e1c0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ac6a4eb8-830c-5c3d-8fd0-885f742c563a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The manager told us to finish the job within this week.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d3eafc5d-4a77-5b5e-a8c6-8e092e5b3c17'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd3eafc5d-4a77-5b5e-a8c6-8e092e5b3c17'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Theory of Resonance', E'The history of marketers seeking the advice of physicists is a short one, but an understanding of the Theory of Resonance may give communications experts the edge. Resonance Theory explains the curious phenomenon of how very small pebbles dropped into a pond can create bigger waves than a large brick. The brick makes a decent splash, but its ripples peter out quickly. A tiny pebble dropped into the same pond, followed by another, then another, then another, all timed carefully, will create ripples that build into small waves.\nAs Dr. Carlo Contaldi, a physicist at Imperial College London, explains, a small amount of energy committed at just the right intervals - the ''natural frequency'' - creates a cumulatively large effect.\nMedia consultant Paul Bay believes that just as with thepebbles in a pond, a carefully choreographed and meticulously timed stream of communication (a monthly ad in MT, for example) will have a more lasting effect than a sporadic big splash during primetime ad breaks.\nInnocent is the testament to the power of pebbles. Until last year, the maker of smoothies had never advertised on TV, instead drip-feeding the market with endless ingenious marketing ploys - from annotating its drinks labels with quirky messages to hosting its own music festival, Fruit stock. The company sent a constant stream of messages rather than communicating through the occasional big and expensive noise.', NULL, NULL, E'The Theory of Resonance, explaining how very small pebbles dropped into a pond can create bigger waves than a large brick, may give communications experts the edge, with a small amount of energy committing at just the right intervals creating a cumulatively large effect, which means a carefully choreographed and meticulously timed stream of communication will have a more lasting effect than a sporadic big splash during primetime ad breaks.', NULL, 5, 75),
