  ('d419bb88-40f2-5cee-823f-212f4da4a5da'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd419bb88-40f2-5cee-823f-212f4da4a5da'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Neutrality of American', E'The establishment of the Third Reich influenced events in American history by starting a chain of events which {{1}} in war between Germany and the United States. The complete destruction of democracy, the {{2}} of Jews, the war on religion, the cruelty and barbarism of the Nazis, and especially the plans of Germany and her allies, Italy and Japan, for world conquest caused great indignation in this country and brought on fear of another world war. While speaking out against Hitler''s atrocities, the American people generally favored isolationist policies and neutrality. The Neutrality Acts of 1935 and 1936 {{3}} trade with any belligerents or loans to them. In 1937 the President was empowered to declare an arms embargo in wars between nations at his {{4}} . American opinion began to change somewhat after President Roosevelt''s "quarantine the aggressor" speech at Chicago (1937) in which he {{5}} criticized Hitler''s policies. Germany''s seizure of Austria and the Munich Pact for the partition of Czechoslovakia (1938) also aroused the American people.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.culminated, 2.persecution, 3.prohibited, 4.discretion, 5.severely', NULL, NULL),
