  ('d471ab4e-b66a-5047-85dc-a2d6d2780f9e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd471ab4e-b66a-5047-85dc-a2d6d2780f9e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd2c6fb27-923b-556c-9483-33a2c2510c28'::uuid, NULL, E'She is an expert of the eighteenth - century French literature.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d47432ee-e9cd-5208-900a-0ea9080b9290'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd47432ee-e9cd-5208-900a-0ea9080b9290'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a2766040-3c2e-5219-a6b9-1be5b98a3c57'::uuid, NULL, E'Mitosis is the division of cells for growth and repair.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d475d317-f779-57dc-8880-d778c2c6fe56'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd475d317-f779-57dc-8880-d778c2c6fe56'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '79382bad-44e0-5248-9e95-76c1b55ba18f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Eating fish twice a week is recommended for a healthy diet.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d47676b7-68bb-5e97-9fc8-6f29eb14d9b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd47676b7-68bb-5e97-9fc8-6f29eb14d9b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Oil Price Decline', E'A plunging oil price has dragged UK inflation to zero over recent months. But analysts say the fall in retail prices cannot solely be attributed to oil. Discount retailers continue to steal market share from established industry giants, taking an increased chunk of both food and non-food markets. And, as retail analyst Nick Bubb notes, “the big supermarkets have had to respond to this by bringing down their own ‘rip off’ prices”. The result is a sector-wide fall in prices paid at the till. The growth of online retailers has also brought prices down, in part due to the ease with which customers can compare prices and purchase goods elsewhere if they find an item cheaper on a competitor’s site. Retailers are also reluctant to offer different prices in their physical and online stores, according to retail analyst Richard Hyman, which means shops are forced to cut prices on the high street. An ever-expanding range of shops is also to blame, according to Mr. Hyman. “Overcapacity is the biggest of the issues affecting prices,” he says. “In the last 10 years, online alone has added the equivalent of 110m square feet of trading space — that’s roughly equal to 65 additional Westfield London shopping malls. An increase in supply of retailers, with no increase in demand, has left the industry massively oversupplied.”', NULL, NULL, E'While analysts say the fall in retail prices cannot just be attributed to the plunging oil price, discount retailers continue to steal market share from established industry giants, and the growth of online retailers and the increase in supply of retailers are both to blame.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('d476fc74-2181-5b07-901a-8483a9578ff2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd476fc74-2181-5b07-901a-8483a9578ff2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ozone', E'A total of five ozone ascents were taken at Bharati station (Indian mission) Antarctica from April to June 2016. As a stratospheric temperature reduced to -82.24 °C on 20th June 2016 indicating the formation of stratospheric clouds, leading scientists at Bharati station feared that Montreal Accord has not succeeded to control the emission of ozone-depleting gases in the atmosphere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d480388b-08e0-5c72-b766-fdffdea2461d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd480388b-08e0-5c72-b766-fdffdea2461d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'European Culture', E'Many people today think of culture in the way that it was thought of in Europe during the 18th and early 19th centuries. This {{1}} of culture reflected inequalities within European societies and their colonies around the world. This understanding of culture equates culture with civilization and contrasts both with nature or non-civilization. According to this understanding of culture, some countries are more civilized than others, and some people are more cultured than others. Anything that doesn''t {{2}} into this category is labeled as chaos or anarchy. From this perspective, culture is closely tied to cultivation, which is the progressive refinement of human {{3}} .\nIn practice, culture referred to elite goods and activities such as haute cuisine, high fashion or haute couture, museum-caliber art and classical music. The word cultured referred to people who knew about and took part in these activities. {{4}} , someone who used culture in this sense might {{5}} that classical music is more refined than music by working-class people, such as jazz or the indigenous music traditions of aboriginal peoples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.concept, 2.fit, 3.behavior, 4.For example, 5.argue', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4844a9b-e694-5b03-bf00-88922999bbc1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4844a9b-e694-5b03-bf00-88922999bbc1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Water Temperature', E'Water temperature is an important physical property of every river and stream. Many plants, animals, and other organisms living in streams can {{1}} only in a specific range of water temperatures. Temperature can affect certain aspects of water quality. For example, higher temperatures reduce levels of dissolved oxygen in the water, which can negatively affect the growth and {{2}} of aquatic life. Persistently warmer temperatures in streams can accelerate natural chemical reactions and release excess nutrients into the water. Temperatures can {{3}} naturally along the length of a stream, from cold temperatures near a source of meltwater to higher temperatures near its outlet to the sea. The temperature at any given point is a product of many different factors, including sources of water, the amount of water in the stream, air temperature, plants along the {{4}} , and the amount of development within the watershed. Over time, however, an area’s climate has the strongest natural influence on a stream’s temperature.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.flourish, 2.productivity, 3.vary, 4.bank', NULL, NULL),
  ('d484a4ce-b56c-5d90-bc07-a92ce215fc2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd484a4ce-b56c-5d90-bc07-a92ce215fc2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Anti-brain', E'If you designed an almost perfect anti brain learning environment, it would look something like a typical classroom. And if you were to design an almost perfect anti brain working environment, it looks something like a typical office cubicle. Why? Because tiny proteins called a b d and f s are actually created when you exercise. And these help the brain to develop. So exercise boosts brain power. The problem lies in the fact that we measure distance today in terms of the space between the refrigerator, the bathroom and the couch, says robert hutchins. Whenever I feel like exercise, I lie down until the feeling passes. Our ancestors, on the other hand, walked an average of twelve miles a day, and hence the brain developed as a survival organ that was designed to solve problems in an unstable environment, in almost constant motion. If our ancestors had lain around, well, let''s just say that survival didn''t favor the sedentary types. So what are we to do? If I were an employer, i''d want the workplace environment to encourage exercise to boost my employees brain power.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '4d1b229c-ffa8-5023-b9f0-175acf5a18a1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Modern classrooms and offices don’t help people’s brains to work well. This is because they discourage exercise. Exercise boosts brainpower because during exercise the brain produces a protein that encourages brain development. Our ancestors did a lot more exercise than us and this helped them to survive.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4851db8-4cb9-5d70-95df-33a5d2dec585'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4851db8-4cb9-5d70-95df-33a5d2dec585'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9d66bd44-e80b-564f-8a09-417f3774ea22'::uuid, NULL, E'Please pass the handouts along to the rest of the people in your row.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d489770a-0e67-50e3-90b4-a1fd98dc1da5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd489770a-0e67-50e3-90b4-a1fd98dc1da5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b26d96b8-e34c-5012-bbbb-aa7545727994'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'All of your writing assignments will be reviewed by another peer.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4943279-a9ed-5ee2-8b23-cc2af8703c15'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4943279-a9ed-5ee2-8b23-cc2af8703c15'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Motorcyclist Accident', E'May 15, 2008 When motorcyclists have an accident they roll a dice, with escaping {{1}} on one side and very severe consequences on the other. And for those unlucky enough to {{2}} severe and permanent injuries like paraplegia, there''s often one huge regret - that they may never ride again on a real bike. A chance encounter with a paraplegic ex-motorcross champion in a hospital carpark inspired West Australian Darren Lomman to put together an audacious project: a motorcycle for paraplegic riders - and his working prototype, a heavily modified Honda CBR250RR, is now road licensed and {{3}} .With the right investment and profile, Lomman believes the Dreamfit bike isn''t too far away from production potential - and after around 150 enquiries from all around the world, he would love to be able to put the bikes in the hands of more people for whom riding has become an impossible dream. Started as a university project, the Dreamfit CBR250RR has been modified to {{4}} riders paralyzed from the chest down, with thumb-activated pneumatic rams for foot-free gear shifting, a combined braking system, custom-moulded ergonomic cups to hold the rider in place without any lower body strength, and a set of steel-braced "landing gear" wheels that drop to provide stability at very low speeds.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.unscathed, 2.sustain, 3.operational, 4.suit', NULL, NULL),
  ('d495fd6e-0b51-5ef9-b59d-11db23f566f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd495fd6e-0b51-5ef9-b59d-11db23f566f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we call animals or plants living or growing in natural conditions?', '5d14f5a0-03c6-5538-bc45-ee7746d753ed'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Wild', NULL, NULL),
  ('d49c1611-164f-583b-98ad-b1dbec360376'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd49c1611-164f-583b-98ad-b1dbec360376'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the process of water seeping into the ground called?', 'c1317bad-ecc7-51b0-9f8e-cf47c058e42c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Infiltration / percolation', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4a757f7-b763-5587-baa4-7e387e6fb862'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4a757f7-b763-5587-baa4-7e387e6fb862'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sleepless Cities', E'Living in cities that never sleep has its price: inhabitants are getting less, {{1}} quality, sleep. We cannot forget that sleep, though often undervalued, is a {{2}} part of staying in good health. It is well {{3}} that if we don’t get enough, we end up getting sick.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.worse, 2.fundamental, 3.established', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4ad3949-04d2-596e-8cbd-cc1c8160a6b5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4ad3949-04d2-596e-8cbd-cc1c8160a6b5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a8aeb2b0-385f-5e55-88be-30fd44b07ca8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The university canteen now offers many healthy meal options.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4aeb697-221b-55c4-a5c4-36b11649b26c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4aeb697-221b-55c4-a5c4-36b11649b26c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '70c06cd9-e4ac-561d-afab-8d8178ffb95d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The sports team members often practice on weekdays and play games on weekends.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4b2b5a6-87ac-56a2-a0c3-d04c34d0070b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4b2b5a6-87ac-56a2-a0c3-d04c34d0070b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Persian Empire', E'The Achaemenid Dynasty heralded the rise of the Persian Empire, {{1}} to prominence under Cyrus the Great around 550 BCE. This vast empire, renowned for its exceptional administrative systems and cultural diversity, sprawled across three continents, from the Indus Valley to the fringes of Greece, encompassing Egypt and touching the steppes of Central Asia. Its innovative imperial governance, characterized by the satrapy system, allowed for local autonomy and integration of a {{2}} of cultures, languages, and religions. The Royal Road, stretching over 2,000 miles, {{3}} unprecedented communication and commerce throughout the empire. Darius I’s creation of a standardized currency, the daric, {{4}} unified economic transactions across its extensive territories. Esteemed for their tolerance and diplomatic acumen, Persian kings established paradigms of rule that influenced {{5}} empires for generations. Persian society was illuminated by opulent architecture, vivid gardens, and advancement in sciences, which became the empire’s enduring legacy.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.ascending, 2.multitude, 3.facilitated, 4.further, 5.subsequent', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4b50ae3-9ade-5904-9d32-bacade4cfaff'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4b50ae3-9ade-5904-9d32-bacade4cfaff'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the phase in a trial in which both parties interrogate each other?', 'e229e3ac-eac1-5923-907d-3574f1cc44b5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cross examination', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4bcdb8f-8b22-5277-a5e4-322c3a59a39b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4bcdb8f-8b22-5277-a5e4-322c3a59a39b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which hospital department would you go for an X-ray, radiology or cardiology?', 'ad0767b4-738d-5fe1-aaa6-46e85c9c85d7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Radiology', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4c3c7e3-a61d-5563-a5c5-237eeed9a993'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4c3c7e3-a61d-5563-a5c5-237eeed9a993'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tree-planting Day', E'Tree-planting Day is popular worldwide. What are the advantages and disadvantages of it? Give your own experience and examples.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('d4c583f7-8546-58b0-9c04-c1f1d5007ef1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4c583f7-8546-58b0-9c04-c1f1d5007ef1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call the main entrance of a large building, often grand and imposing?', 'a68fbd98-3c73-58fa-875e-8455a4b9c14a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Portal', NULL, NULL),
  ('d4c73952-332d-56b7-b07f-35b561a8777c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'd4c73952-332d-56b7-b07f-35b561a8777c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Arctic and Antarctic', NULL, '8a4a8b8f-1e67-5958-a8e6-ddd86c1b36a0'::uuid, NULL, E'So, when we talk about the polar regions, just to clarify exactly what we mean. And we have first of all the Arctic at the top of the earth and the Antarctic at the bottom, and so the Arctic was named after the Greek word for bear. Now surprisingly it’s not after the polar bears that live in the Antarctic or live in the Arctic and based on it’s after the little and great bear constellations that can be seen in the sky. Now the Greek also hypothesize that there would be the Anti-arctic, which is how we get the name Antarctica and of course it wasn’t discovered until much later on. Now these regions are opposite in many ways other than just their names and their location on the globe, and so if we look at the arctic first of all, and the Arctic is actually ocean surrounded by land, and so you can see here this is the UK down here and this kind of Russia and then American Canada around here, and so there is a bit of land cover in our ice on the top in the Arctic, which is Greenland here and Macie all this area here. Surprisingly a lot of people don’t realize that this isn’t actually land. The north pole isn’t on land. It’s just one big ocean.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
