  ('da786e14-161b-51e6-96e0-f59d89c6f8ad'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da786e14-161b-51e6-96e0-f59d89c6f8ad'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dinosaurs', E'Dinosaurs largely died off when a Manhattan-size asteroid {{1}} into Earth 66 million years ago. Meanwhile, in the shadows, tiny mammals had steadily {{2}} up adaptations that helped them survive the disaster and {{3}} in its aftermath, a new study suggests. The study came to that conclusion by {{4}} the complex interactions between a huge range of ancient animals and their ecosystems before and after the asteroid hit.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.slammed, 2.picked, 3.thrive, 4.mapping', NULL, NULL),
  ('da7e6131-8b5c-57bd-b652-2502d0d6fe24'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da7e6131-8b5c-57bd-b652-2502d0d6fe24'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Distance Learning', E'If you are interested in studying but have other {{1}} , our online and distance learning courses offer an alternative flexible {{2}} of study. Teaching is conducted through a mixture of audio-visual, written and interactive materials. There are also {{3}} for online discussion and collaborative projects with tutors and other students. Some programs include residential {{4}} taught on campus, giving you the chance to meet and work alongside your tutors and fellow students face-to-face. Our Graduate School provides comprehensive support for distance and part-time researchers, many of whom study for up to six years or more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.commitments, 2.mode, 3.opportunities, 4.modules', NULL, NULL),
  ('da83cdde-2127-5204-9c83-59f6ed7937d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da83cdde-2127-5204-9c83-59f6ed7937d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Drought', E'Every year as summer approaches, areas around the world grow concerned about seasonal drought. Throughout the winter, many places {{1}} precipitation and the snowpack to prepare for what the warmer, drier months may bring. In addition, there are areas where drought is a regular year-to-year {{2}} that lasts longer than just the summer. From hot deserts to the freezing poles, drought is something that affects plants, animals, and people worldwide. Usually, drought is talked about in one of two perspectives — meteorological and hydrological. A drought in {{3}} of meteorology takes into account deficiencies in measured precipitation. Each year''s measurements are then compared to what is determined as a "normal" amount of precipitation and drought is determined from there. For hydrologists, droughts are monitored by checking stream flow and lake, reservoir, and {{4}} water levels. Precipitation is also considered here as it contributes to the water levels.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.monitor, 2.occurrence, 3.terms, 4.aquifer', NULL, NULL),
  ('da8788c8-9b4a-50a3-96f0-4ae1c23677c4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da8788c8-9b4a-50a3-96f0-4ae1c23677c4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Contagious Emotions', E'As research has shown, emotions are contagious. And empaths are especially {{1}} to others'' emotional energies. Because they''re so attuned to others. They can get easily exhausted in crowds, be drawn into codependent {{2}} , exhaust themselves trying to solve others'' problems, or burn out from too much caregiving. Yet empathy is also a gift that brings greater {{3}} and understanding. Some of the finest therapists, doctors, nurses, professors, writers, designers, musicians, artists and leaders in many have been empaths.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.sensitive, 2.relationships, 3.insight', NULL, NULL),
  ('da88d84d-5dae-55f3-a24e-0b4231981716'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da88d84d-5dae-55f3-a24e-0b4231981716'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Breast Milk', E'Breast milk changes by the third to fifth day after birth, becoming much thinner, but containing just the right amount of fat, sugar, water, and proteins to support overall physical and {{1}} development. It provides a source of iron more easily {{2}} in the body than the iron found in dietary supplements, and it also provides {{3}} against many diseases.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.neurological, 2.absorbed, 3.resistance', NULL, NULL),
  ('da8a924e-90db-5137-b3a8-31f33e1f9cce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da8a924e-90db-5137-b3a8-31f33e1f9cce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where are the eyes located?', 'd4ac2d32-a7ab-56fa-a04e-53d3608db5ec'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Face', NULL, NULL),
  ('da8ae96a-483e-527e-9fa9-243a30329f25'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da8ae96a-483e-527e-9fa9-243a30329f25'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Migrating Birds', E'For birdwatchers in southern New Mexico, September can be highly entertaining. Good numbers of many diverse {{1}} are on the move during this time, {{2}} southward from northern breeding grounds to places they will spend the winter, and there''s always a chance that some rare or unusual bird will turn up. Key to the flow of migrating birds through the area is our geography. Birds crossing over the southwest deserts tend to follow north-south watercourses like the Rio Grande and/or corridors of relatively green {{3}} , whether that be cottonwoods and willows lining the valleys or the coniferous forests of the higher mountains. Shorebirds, gulls, ducks and other birds that are closely associated with water typically follow the river southward, unless a desert playa along the way happens to catch their eye and {{4}} them. Migrating land birds, on the other hand, are looking for places to stop and rest on the southward journey, where they can feed on seeds, berries or insects to refuel for the next leg of their trip. Heading south out of Albuquerque, where the surrounding high mountains and lush, wide cottonwood bosques offer an abundance of habitat, they reach our area and are funneled into a relatively narrow sliver of {{5}} choices.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.species, 2.traveling, 3.vegetation, 4.divert, 5.foraging', NULL, NULL),
  ('da8bc2d8-50d3-582e-b15a-541b893a4774'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da8bc2d8-50d3-582e-b15a-541b893a4774'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Persuit of Happiness', E'Do you believe that the pursuit of happiness is the most important goal in life?', NULL, NULL, E'I firmly believe that the pursuit of happiness is the most important goal in life. Prioritizing happiness is crucial as it enhances overall well-being and mental health, leading to a more fulfilling and contented life. By focusing on happiness, individuals can cultivate a positive mindset and emotional resilience, fostering satisfaction and a sense of contentment. This emotional well-being serves as a foundation for a fulfilling existence, enabling individuals to navigate life''s challenges with optimism and experience greater joy in their daily lives.\nHappiness plays a pivotal role in enhancing overall well-being and mental health, ultimately leading to a fulfilling life. Embracing happiness enables individuals to cultivate a positive mindset and emotional resilience, fostering contentment and satisfaction. This emotional well-being serves as a foundation for a fulfilling existence, empowering individuals to navigate challenges with optimism and experience greater joy in their daily lives.\nFurthermore, the pursuit of happiness serves as a powerful motivator for individuals to set and achieve meaningful goals. When happiness becomes the driving force behind actions, individuals are inspired to pursue endeavors that align with their values and aspirations. This pursuit not only leads to personal growth and fulfillment but also fosters a sense of purpose and direction in life, propelling individuals toward success and self-actualization.\nIn conclusion, prioritizing the pursuit of happiness is essential for personal well-being, goal achievement, and societal contribution. By embracing happiness as a primary goal, individuals not only enhance their own lives but also radiate positivity and create a ripple effect of joy in their relationships and communities. The pursuit of happiness is pivotal in shaping a more fulfilling and harmonious existence for both individuals and society as a whole.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('da9934b8-3374-50db-9285-3166fea8308a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da9934b8-3374-50db-9285-3166fea8308a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '40219501-8e32-5e58-9263-d0997eb9139f'::uuid, NULL, E'Directly ahead is the car park, and to the left is our Gift Shop.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('da9a73ed-fe76-5226-ab8a-b97b0a9b890e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da9a73ed-fe76-5226-ab8a-b97b0a9b890e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Central Nervous System', E'The central nervous system controls most functions of the body and mind. It consists of two parts: the brain and the spinal cord. The brain is the center of our thoughts, the interpreter of our external environment, and the origin of control over body movement. The spinal cord is the highway for communication between the body and the brain. When the spinal cord is injured, the exchange of information between the brain and other parts of the body is disrupted.\nMost systems and organs of the body control just one function, but the central nervous system does many jobs at the same time. It controls all voluntary movement, such as speech and walking, and involuntary movements, such as blinking and breathing. It is also the core of our thoughts, perceptions, and emotions.\nThe central nervous system is better protected than any other system or organ in the body. Its main line of defense is the bones of the skull and spinal column, which create a hard physical barrier to injury. A fluid-filled space below the bones, called the syrnix, provides shock absorbance.\nUnfortunately, this protection can be a double-edged sword. When an injury to the central nervous system occurs, the soft tissue of the brain and spinal cord swells, causing pressure because of the confined space. The swelling makes the injury worse unless it is rapidly relieved. Fractured bones can lead to further damage and the possibility of infection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('da9cbdfc-b376-55b9-9b2f-869964359f92'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da9cbdfc-b376-55b9-9b2f-869964359f92'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ants', E'Ants are known for working together, operating as a unit for the good of the colony. But not so fast, say researchers from the Universities of Leeds and Copenhagen. It turns out that ants can scheme like a stage mom.\n{{1}} say that some ants hide out to ensure that their offspring become child-bearing queens instead of barren workers. The {{2}} hypothesis had been that random ants were fed certain foods that would allow them to develop into queens. But DNA tests on five {{3}} of leaf-cutting ants {{4}} that certain males have a better genetic chance of producing royal progeny.\nScientists believe these rare males stay anonymous, and thus avoid any problems with other ants that might otherwise lose their "one-for-all, all-for-one" attitude. In fact, the number of males {{5}} royal genes to those who aren''t may have settled at a low ratio through {{6}} — which cobbled together the best way for the ant gene pool to expand, while at the same time keeping the lucky males hidden from their possibly jealous rivals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.Scientists, 2.accepted, 3.colonies, 4.revealed, 5.carrying, 6.evolution', NULL, NULL),
  ('da9cd3ab-c4fe-523a-b790-729b5b9123b9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'da9cd3ab-c4fe-523a-b790-729b5b9123b9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Food Choices', E'Everybody eats. And consumers increasingly try to consider the {{1}} effects of their food choices. For example, if you want to eat meat, how do your choices compare? That''s what a group of researchers set out to {{2}} . And they found that raising one animal is dramatically more environmentally draining than all the others: cows. The research is in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences.\nThe scientists noted the challenge in accessing data and creating metrics that can be compared across livestock and to potato, wheat and rice {{3}} . They settled on national data from the U.S. Departments of Agriculture, the Interior and Energy. The team calculated the production costs by assessing land area, water needs and fertilizer. They also analyzed greenhouse gas {{5}} .\nProducing pork, poultry, eggs and dairy were between two and six times less efficient than growing potatoes, wheat and rice. And in the current {{7}} system, beef uses 28 times more land, 11 times more water and six times more fertilizer than the average of the other categories of livestock. Cattle ranching also creates five times more greenhouse gas emissions.\nThe researchers hope this data will help consumers make informed choices and policy makers create systems that can reduce the environmental costs of what we eat.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.environmental, 2.discover, 3.production, 4.emissions, 5.agricultural', NULL, NULL),
  ('daa73c20-3485-5c58-8905-6e42903ff6d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'daa73c20-3485-5c58-8905-6e42903ff6d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f7f6a310-92f2-5106-9f14-0fbacb7ea933'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'He has been developing a training course for academic staff.', NULL, NULL),
  ('daad7453-0205-52d5-adfb-724e67ccf38f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'daad7453-0205-52d5-adfb-724e67ccf38f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RL', NULL, '24814c15-421e-508f-9ca7-1fa7377e2f77'::uuid, NULL, E'What matters is how much does each person in the household get, how much income is supporting each person in a household. Look what happens we take that 18 percent figure. Again the figure I remind you is from 1976 until 2006 in inflation-adjusted terms. The income above the median household income of Americans rose only by 18 percent, but at the same time the size of the household has fallen. So what''s happened to the average income per person in the household. Per household person income per each individual in the household over that thirty-year period. We see that that rose not by 18 percent but by 32 percent because the number of people in a household haven fallen, the amount of income earned by the household goes further per person. Because there were fewer people to share per person. Each person gets a larger slice of the pie because of few people sharing the pie. Just making that one adjustment looking at what''s happened to the size of households causes that 18 percent figure to rise to 32 percent. 32 percent''s still not great over a 30-year period but it''s different than 18 percent, a little bit more optimistic and if nothing else, it should give you some sense that data have to be interpreted carefully.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('daae6b1c-1fe7-5dda-9c1d-fa9216ca986a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'daae6b1c-1fe7-5dda-9c1d-fa9216ca986a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Forest', E'The place had both mountains and a {{1}} . Every year, over 3.5 million {{2}} come to enjoy the scenery. There are also several miles of {{3}} that wind through the area.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.forest, 2.visitors, 3.trails', NULL, NULL),
  ('dab13ccc-e5ae-53e5-b26f-1898752b802d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dab13ccc-e5ae-53e5-b26f-1898752b802d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Paris Stage', E'In the preceding hundred years, Paris had been {{1}} stage for political and social {{2}} that had deeply affected all of Europe. The many ways in which tradition had already been challenged and {{3}} during those years helped make it easier for those to achieve a break with tradition art.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.center, 2.movements, 3.shaken', NULL, NULL),
  ('dab24560-1388-5464-b204-c77d64b17482'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dab24560-1388-5464-b204-c77d64b17482'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the connecting part between two bones?', '46941d03-0c37-5c24-bbb5-894377876bd4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Joint', NULL, NULL),
  ('dab6cbaf-dfbc-50ac-836f-da6ffc49245f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dab6cbaf-dfbc-50ac-836f-da6ffc49245f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cashless Transaction', E'To what extent do you think that cashless transactions will replace traditional money?', NULL, NULL, E'The evolution of payment methods has raised the question of the extent to which cashless transactions will replace traditional money. As digital technologies continue to advance, the convenience, security, and digitalization associated with cashless transactions are reshaping the way we conduct financial transactions. While traditional money still holds significance, the rise of cashless transactions is undeniable in today''s digital age.\nCashless transactions offer unparalleled convenience and efficiency in payment processes. With the tap of a card or a mobile payment, individuals can swiftly complete transactions without the need for physical currency. The ease of cashless payments streamlines financial interactions, making it a preferred choice for many consumers seeking quick and hassle-free transactions in various settings.\nOne of the key advantages of cashless transactions is the enhanced security measures they provide to protect financial transactions. Digital payment methods offer encryption and authentication protocols that safeguard sensitive information, reducing the risks associated with theft and fraud. The robust security features of cashless transactions instill confidence in users and contribute to a safer financial ecosystem.\nIn conclusion, the transition towards cashless transactions is driven by the convenience, security, and digitalization trends in society. While traditional money remains ingrained in daily transactions, the increasing reliance on digital payment methods signals a shift towards a cashless future. As technology continues to advance and consumer preferences evolve, the extent to which cashless transactions will replace traditional money will likely continue to grow.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('dab7bbe1-1863-5f59-93f1-a3c41009f25e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dab7bbe1-1863-5f59-93f1-a3c41009f25e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rising Temperature', E'You may have heard about global warming. It seems that in the last 100 years the earth''s temperature has increased about half a degree Celsius. This may not sound like much, but even half a degree can have an effect on our planet. According to the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) the sea level has risen 6 to 8 inches (15 to 20 cm) in the last 100 years.\nThis higher temperature may be causing some floating icebergs to melt, but this will not make the oceans rise. Icebergs are large floating chunks of ice. In order to float, the iceberg displaces a volume of water that has a weight equal to that of the iceberg. Submarines use this principle to rise and sink in the water, too.\nHowever, the rising temperature and icebergs could play a small role in the rising ocean level. Icebergs are chunks of frozen glaciers that break off from landmasses and fall into the ocean. The rising temperature may be causing more icebergs to form by weakening the glaciers, causing more cracks and making ice more likely to break off. As soon as the ice falls into the ocean, the ocean rises a little.\nIf the rising temperature affects glaciers and icebergs, could the polar ice caps be in danger of melting and causing the oceans to rise? This could happen, but no one knows when it might happen.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('dab982a1-d90a-5411-bc06-b45627e8df93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dab982a1-d90a-5411-bc06-b45627e8df93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bennett', E'In the last years of the wheat boom, Bennett had become increasingly frustrated at how the government seemed to be encouraging an {{1}} farming binge. He went directly after his old employer, the Department of Agriculture, for {{2}} people. Farmers on the Great Plains were working against nature; he {{3}} in speeches across the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.exploitative, 2.misleading, 3.thundered', NULL, NULL),
  ('dabef540-e0f6-529d-91b5-8bb77f67ff64'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dabef540-e0f6-529d-91b5-8bb77f67ff64'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9da033e2-74b7-59a6-aa78-593417fb08da'::uuid, NULL, E'To earn the best grade, you must achieve a high score.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dabff58a-d5fe-5bcd-afc5-d88ffc3e5434'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dabff58a-d5fe-5bcd-afc5-d88ffc3e5434'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Supply and Demand', E'The supply of a thing, in the phrase "supply and demand", is the amount that will be offered for sale at each of a series of prices; the demand is the amount that will be bought at each of a series of prices. The principle that value depends on supply and demand means that in the case of nearly every commodity, more will be bought if the price is lowered, less will be bought if the price is {{1}} . Therefore sellers, if they wish to induce buyers to {{2}} more of a commodity than they are already doing, must reduce its price; if they raise its price, they will sell less. If there is a general falling off, if in demand — due, say, to trade depression — sellers will either have to {{3}} prices or put less on the {{4}} ; they will not be able to sell the same {{5}} at the same price.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.raised, 2.take, 3.reduce, 4.market, 5.amount', NULL, NULL),
  ('dad0f12b-b494-59a3-8476-d0bcaf97ed59'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dad0f12b-b494-59a3-8476-d0bcaf97ed59'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Information Revolution', E'Some have begun to call it the Information Revolution. Technological changes brought dramatic new {{1}} to Americans living in the 1990s. From the beginning of the decade until the end, new forms of entertainment, commerce, research, work, and communication became commonplace in the United States. The {{2}} force behind much of this change was an innovation popularly known as the Internet. Personal computers had become widespread by the end of the 1980s. Through a device called a modem, individual users could link their computer to a {{3}} of information using conventional phone lines. What lay beyond the individual computer was a vast domain of information known as cyberspace. Upon its {{4}} in 1983 the Apple "Lisa" computer was supposed to revolutionize personal computing. But interest in "Lisa" was minimal due to its nearly $10,000 price tag and the introduction of the much more {{5}} "Macintosh" a year later.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.options, 2.driving, 3.wealth, 4.release, 5.affordable', NULL, NULL),
  ('dae6c006-9892-5ffa-8a47-0f9e1c5a0c58'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dae6c006-9892-5ffa-8a47-0f9e1c5a0c58'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '416512ef-48c4-5b8e-8719-c2e15bdc6da2'::uuid, NULL, E'You will be less stressed if you are well prepared for the exam.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
