  ('de15f978-f8b2-5d3a-9b25-6687325133e2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'de15f978-f8b2-5d3a-9b25-6687325133e2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '600cfde5-b7e1-549b-b3bd-afc67fff83ed'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Parents today are involved in the education of their children.', NULL, NULL),
  ('de212f00-d0b5-53d9-9b58-6a73ad606928'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'de212f00-d0b5-53d9-9b58-6a73ad606928'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Summer Vacation', E'There are few things U.S. students love more than summer vacation, that traditionally three-month break from school during June, July and August. But why does it even exist?\nA common theory holds that summer vacation was created for farm kids who needed to work. That''s only marginally true: students at rural schools did get time off for harvests, but those breaks fell in the spring and the fall. In fact, summer vacation was born in the city. Calls for a break began in the mid-19th century, when many urban schools met year-round. Warnings about "overstudy" led reformers like Horace Mann to argue that time off would be good for kids'' behavior and mental health, says Kenneth M. Gold, author of "The History of Summer Education" in American Public Schools.\nDoctors agreed: John C. Warren, a Harvard professor of anatomy and surgery, once remarked that ''too steady an application to literary pursuits'' led to a ''debilitated body''. And in an era before AC, experts worried that poorly ventilated school buildings compounded the risks. Debate raged for decades. But as railroads made nature more accessible for city dwellers, wealthier parents increasingly took matters into their own hands and took their kids out of school. Eventually, the vacationers won out, and the break became official.\nNowadays, reformers have changed their tune: they argue that eliminating long summer vacations could shrink achievement gaps between students. It''s an idea backed up by data—but one at which their forebears might shudder.', NULL, NULL, E'Summer vacation was born in the city, as too steady an application to literary pursuits led to a debilitated body, so eventually the vacationers won out, and the break became official; eliminating long summer vacations could shrink achievement gaps between students.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('de2585c4-a9f6-577e-816a-23988a3f9e89'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'de2585c4-a9f6-577e-816a-23988a3f9e89'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'c43dc862-a40d-5fc3-805e-c04100983796'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You are able to contact a number of research subjects.', NULL, NULL),
  ('de270e74-8273-5bf4-b03a-006d91bc7179'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'de270e74-8273-5bf4-b03a-006d91bc7179'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Natural Environment', E'The natural environment can be hazardous, and, with increased travel and leisure, people today are more likely than ever to be exposed to potentially life-threatening conditions. Although the human body can adjust to some extent, it cannot cope with poisons or prolonged exposure to extremes of environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
