  ('df42f9bb-d95a-5e87-899b-e2f64b1b28a4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df42f9bb-d95a-5e87-899b-e2f64b1b28a4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Walt Disney World', E'Walt Disney World has become a pilgrimage site partly because of the luminosity of its crosscultural and marketing and partly because its {{1}} aspects appeal powerfully to real needs in the capitalist {{2}} . Disney'' s marketing is unique because it captured the symbolic essence of {{3}} but the company has gained access to all public shows, comic books, dolls, apparels, and {{4}} film strips, which all point to the parks and each other.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.utopian, 2.society, 3.childhood, 4.educational', NULL, NULL),
  ('df444375-4d56-51b6-8287-d67da06aea0f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df444375-4d56-51b6-8287-d67da06aea0f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'cca78b9e-de90-5e8c-9292-1dabcb83818b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Science fiction stories often mention robots that can talk.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df487b36-5162-50d2-8091-1ec9bc83e8c2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df487b36-5162-50d2-8091-1ec9bc83e8c2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '503142c6-960b-5c20-ac16-3e8ade269b11'::uuid, NULL, E'Thousands of people paid good money to watch the band perform.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('df49c72b-84bf-59de-a022-c74f49f23c2d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df49c72b-84bf-59de-a022-c74f49f23c2d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Nonviolent Communication', E'Let’s imagine a college student being late for class. New Jay, who’s her current teacher, learned about nonviolent communication and knows that it begins with a clear observation. During observation he tries noticing concrete facts: things that happen at that very moment. New Jay jots down that Ann arrived 20 minutes late and that his pulse is up, possibly a sign of stress. When focusing on his feelings, New Jay connects with his heart and can learn to understand various underlying emotions. This is important because what seems to be anger, might in fact be sadness. During this step it is essential to distinguish feelings from thoughts. After class, New Jay shares his observation and explains to Ann that he feels disrespected when someone is late for his class. Knowing his needs is important because it allows him to enrich his life, and feel at peace. If we disregard our needs or don’t live up to our values, we experience stress and frustration.\nNew Jay tells Ann that they should find a way to respect each other’s values and desires. Lastly there is the request which clarifies what future New Jay wants for himself and this relationship. Clear requests are hence crucial to a transformative communication. When we ask for concrete actions, we often find creative ways to ensure that everyone’s needs are met. New Jay asks Ann not to come to class at all, if she happens to run later more than 1 minute.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '07d1af94-c4a9-586b-a4d3-8ddded8ad81a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ann’s teacher New Jay followed nonviolent communication, which started with observation. He then told Ann about his feelings and brought up his clear requests, so both of their needs were finally met in a peaceful way.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df4a0c22-acd7-5ff5-ba13-ab0d6327b776'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df4a0c22-acd7-5ff5-ba13-ab0d6327b776'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Soot Emission', NULL, '6490d6f4-cda4-597f-9314-d9b2aa4bc727'::uuid, NULL, E'Sometimes it''s the little things that can make big things happen. Fleas and the plague, atoms and nuclear bombs. Diminutive leaders in world history. Soot is one of these little things. Soot also known as black carbon is released when you burn dung, coal, diesel fuel and wood. From Los Angeles to Mumbai, soot causes respiratory illnesses like lung cancer and asthma and contributes to one point six million premature deaths every year. Mostly among the poor. And it gets worse. Atmospheric currents carry soot thousands of miles from where it is produced, to the Himalayas and the Arctic. Black carbon being black, absorbs sunlight, so even a little soot on snow makes it melt faster. And when snow melts global sea levels rise, threatening our freshwater indigenous communities and polar bears who hunt on the Arctic ice. Climate Change has been a big thing for a while and carbon dioxide has been its main cause. Scientists estimate that soot causes twenty five percent of human-caused global warming. It''s the second leading cause of Arctic warming after carbon dioxide. Let''s not underestimate the impact of this tiny particle. But there’s good news, reducing black carbon may be the fastest way to slow global warming. Buy time for the Arctic. Yes even more so than changing a light bulb. Since black carbon only stays in the atmosphere for a couple of weeks, reducing it will produce results immediately. Of course, reducing soot alone won''t solve global warming, but solving our soot problem now will help buy time for the Arctic and allow us to deal with the bigger problem of carbon dioxide. We have the cleaner industries, cook stoves, and diesel now we have to use them. In developed nations, we''ve significantly reduced our black carbon, but we still have much more to do. We need to tighten our standards at home and invest in cleaner technologies in developing nations. In a world going on seven billion people, you might feel rather little yourself. But if you urge the US government and the European Union to take the lead on black carbon reduction, you can make a big difference. Go to stopsoot.org and help stop these little things from causing big trouble.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('df4cae93-7aab-5d3d-99d5-ff4f56f44485'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df4cae93-7aab-5d3d-99d5-ff4f56f44485'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1876e16e-5f1c-5d67-a865-df8dd70047c2'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students do need opportunities to practice what they are learning.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df751a3d-f204-5db0-b121-792c73126f37'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df751a3d-f204-5db0-b121-792c73126f37'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Truancy', E'In reality, however, the causes of truancy and non-attendance are diverse and multifaceted. There are as many causes of non-attendance as there are non-attenders. Each child has her own {{1}} story, and whilst there may often be certain identifiable factors in common, each non-attending child demands and {{2}} an individual response, tailored to meet her individual needs. This applies {{3}} to the 14-year-old who fails to attend school because a parent is terminally ill, the overweight 11 -year-old who fails to attend because he is {{4}} about changing for PE in front of peers, the 15-year-old who is ''bored'' by lessons, and to the seven-year-old who is teased in the playground because she does not wear the latest designer-label clothes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.unique, 2.deserves, 3.equally, 4.embarrassed', NULL, NULL),
  ('df79216a-db27-594a-9a2b-48f74e9488f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df79216a-db27-594a-9a2b-48f74e9488f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f41c7dba-a830-59f1-94cb-31c74abddf58'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You can borrow eight books from the library at a time.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df7c07a3-e405-52aa-8b1a-26c359951be8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df7c07a3-e405-52aa-8b1a-26c359951be8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0ed5e11e-060e-5745-a25b-d6cf6845c251'::uuid, NULL, E'We know that sleep is essential for a normal life.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('df82c7ff-3da2-5c19-b6d4-fc791c02ce8c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df82c7ff-3da2-5c19-b6d4-fc791c02ce8c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ebd9d2f2-5d3d-5a22-ac3b-5fecbe80a207'::uuid, NULL, E'One widely accepted theory suggests that dreams contribute to long-term memory formation.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('df9024f5-b17e-5f02-9e8a-9c2cb19a6d36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df9024f5-b17e-5f02-9e8a-9c2cb19a6d36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'f5a67b10-332b-5522-8eab-95c3031b4ce7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Dark chocolate contains cocoa known to enhance immunity and mood.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df958c8d-816f-59c4-8d31-d92776bd0775'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df958c8d-816f-59c4-8d31-d92776bd0775'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Climate Pledges', E'Each year, the UN publishes a report evaluating the gap between the latest climate pledges and the Paris Agreement’s goals. It concludes that the world is falling short. This year’s report finds that the updated pledges would probably result in warming of around 2.7.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('df978cf6-2613-5b2d-8f79-327de78c574a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df978cf6-2613-5b2d-8f79-327de78c574a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mental Awareness', E'What is your opinion on the importance of mental health awareness in schools?', NULL, NULL, E'The significance of mental health awareness in schools is paramount for the well-being and academic success of students. As educational institutions play a crucial role in shaping young minds, fostering a supportive environment that prioritizes mental health is essential for nurturing students'' overall development and creating a conducive learning environment.\nEarly intervention plays a pivotal role in promoting mental health awareness in schools. Recognizing mental health issues early on allows for timely support and interventions, preventing long-term struggles and fostering well-being. Simultaneously, creating a supportive environment through open discussions, reducing stigma, and providing resources to help nurture a community where students feel safe, understood, and supported.\nFurthermore, addressing mental health concerns directly impacts academic performance. When students feel emotionally supported and mentally healthy, they are better equipped to focus on their studies, engage in learning, and excel academically. Investing in mental health resources and awareness not only enhances student well-being but also leads to improved academic outcomes, highlighting the interconnectedness of mental health and academic success.\nIn conclusion, the importance of mental health awareness in schools extends beyond academic performance to the overall well-being of students. By prioritizing mental health, schools can create a nurturing environment that supports students'' emotional growth and academic success. Investing in early intervention, fostering a supportive community, and addressing mental health concerns are essential steps toward building a school culture that values the holistic development of every student.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('df97a8a8-a602-5f9f-9f9b-abea78448348'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df97a8a8-a602-5f9f-9f9b-abea78448348'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'How do we describe a person who cannot read or write?', '86f77cb2-437f-571d-923d-bb292032322d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Illiterate / illiteracy', NULL, NULL),
  ('df994494-e360-55c7-aae7-236d69b171c9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df994494-e360-55c7-aae7-236d69b171c9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bilingual Individuals', E'Recent studies suggest that bilingual individuals may {{1}} trade-offs in language processing. While they benefit from the ability to {{2}} between languages, this comes with a potential {{3}} : a slight delay in word retrieval compared to monolingual speakers. This trade-off, a result of managing two linguistic systems, highlights the complex {{4}} of language cognition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.experience, 2.switch, 3.downside, 4.nature', NULL, NULL),
  ('df9a435e-d2ed-59fe-afb1-c5714f904809'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df9a435e-d2ed-59fe-afb1-c5714f904809'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e34ad018-5a6c-5520-a8cc-9e692cd3d0f8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The author''s early work initially emphasized experimental methods over philosophical.', NULL, NULL),
  ('df9b3a81-4027-55a0-9b2a-be2988c85050'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df9b3a81-4027-55a0-9b2a-be2988c85050'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Energy Flow', E'The fundamental source of energy in almost all ecosystems is radiant energy from the Sun. The energy of sunlight is used by the ecosystem’s autotrophic, or self-sustaining, organisms (that is, those that can make their own food). Consisting largely of green vegetation, these organisms are {{1}} of photosynthesis - i.e., they can use the energy of sunlight to {{2}} carbon dioxide and water into simple, energy-rich carbohydrates. The autotrophs use the energy stored within the simple carbohydrates to produce the more {{3}} organic compounds, such as proteins, lipids, and starches, that maintain the organisms’ life processes. The autotrophic segment of the ecosystem is commonly {{4}} to as the producer level. Organic matter generated by autotrophs directly or indirectly sustains heterotrophic organisms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.capable, 2.convert, 3.complex, 4.referred', NULL, NULL),
  ('df9b8a2d-c90a-5654-8ed5-1ddda1a7ecca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'df9b8a2d-c90a-5654-8ed5-1ddda1a7ecca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ae3d9e03-d62a-5e8a-adb6-408cb8fe0556'::uuid, NULL, E'They still haven''t had any news about when they''ll be able to go home.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfa189dc-f707-5fec-a8d8-6d6557b8a260'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfa189dc-f707-5fec-a8d8-6d6557b8a260'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Coriolis Effect', E'Prevailing winds are winds that blow from a single direction over a specific area of the Earth. Areas where prevailing winds meet are called convergence zones. Generally, prevailing winds blow east-west rather than north-south. This happens because Earth’s rotation generates what is known as the Coriolis effect. The Coriolis effect makes wind systems twist counter-clockwise in the Northern Hemisphere and clockwise in the Southern Hemisphere.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfa891d5-45d3-59e6-96ab-3912db599454'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfa891d5-45d3-59e6-96ab-3912db599454'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lingua Franca', E'English has emerged as the global lingua franca, spoken by a staggering one and a half billion individuals as a second language. It has become the language of {{1}} for individuals worldwide. However, with the ascendancy of English, the number of languages extant has dwindled significantly. Presently, we find ourselves with a mere 6,800 languages, a sharp decline from the multitude during the {{2}} of agriculture. The dominance of languages like English has expedited the {{3}} of others, witnessing the loss of approximately one language every fortnight. For {{4}} aspiring to master a unique language like Busuu, the urgency is palpable, considering that only eight individuals remain capable of {{5}} this linguistic knowledge to others. This accelerating erosion of linguistic diversity prompts reflection on the intricate tapestry of human expression, where the rise of one language signifies the fading whispers of countless others, each a repository of unique cultural narratives and perspectives.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.choice, 2.dawn, 3.demise, 4.those, 5.imparting', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfadba9d-0f62-50bd-8552-0056f2504c0f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfadba9d-0f62-50bd-8552-0056f2504c0f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the hair called that grows on the skin of a sheep?', '9480336c-42e5-552e-9635-45a1989443cb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Wool / fleece', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfb3910b-134b-53c4-b57e-12fed3ebf0a7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfb3910b-134b-53c4-b57e-12fed3ebf0a7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the room in which you keep things when you don''t need them?', 'ec62bb74-4b9e-5a17-bbbd-2dab984ccf43'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Storeroom', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfb54f34-458b-5627-beb8-d1a97b525cd0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfb54f34-458b-5627-beb8-d1a97b525cd0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Group Discussion', E'Group work is increasingly an important part of university study and students are likely to be asked to produce assignments with other group members. Some of the benefits of group work are that it prepares students for teamwork, something that they will probably encounter in the workplace. Also, work can be shared and it tends to produce more creative solutions to problems.\nHowever, we should be aware that conflicts may occur as individuals negotiate their place in the group and different personalities try to work together. To help overcome potential conflicts, the group can define the major task they need to complete, and then break the larger group objective into smaller tasks. It''s important to develop strategies to help the group achieve their short and longer term goals. And to do this, individual roles (including leader) need to be assigned.\n\nWhat does the speaker say can be done to avoid conflict within study?', 'fdd636a5-821f-5c9d-a717-1eaee91200f0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The main task should be divided into parts.', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfb62bd1-9461-54ab-a57d-cf73a35b9b77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfb62bd1-9461-54ab-a57d-cf73a35b9b77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Different Dimensions', E'The fact is that those different types of services affect many different dimensions of well-being of people. And defining the human well-being is also extremely challenging. However, we identified that there are certain items providing basic material for life, whether it is food, shelter or happiness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfb6e5fe-f027-5d02-b122-c3ba3d15cf02'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfb6e5fe-f027-5d02-b122-c3ba3d15cf02'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '976e81a1-f49d-5f89-ab50-4510fa506cf2'::uuid, NULL, E'Expertise in particular areas distinguishes you from other graduates.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfbbd1ea-30e9-5941-953e-7fbc1d48b4eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfbbd1ea-30e9-5941-953e-7fbc1d48b4eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Antarctic', E'At the height of summer in the Antarctic, tourist ships move gently around the coast. Even 30 years ago such sights would have been unthinkable, but today people are willing to pay large sums of money to see the last real wilderness in the world. In the Arctic, careless human exploitation {{1}} has damaged the fragile ecosystem. Today concerned governments are trying to find ways to develop the region {{2}} caring for the very special natural environment. {{3}} the Antarctic is less accessible than the Arctic, it is still largely undamaged by humans, although holes in the ozone layer above the Antarctic have {{4}} . Many people believe that one way to preserve the area is to make the whole region into a world park, with every form of exploitation internationally {{5}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.in the past, 2.while, 3.Because, 4.already been discovered, 5.banned', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfbc0a93-b571-5dfe-9a1d-83e14b6e1036'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfbc0a93-b571-5dfe-9a1d-83e14b6e1036'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Golden Goose', E'Successful economies and cultures are built on trust, but a number of high-profile data breaches and privacy intrusions have caused anxiety for consumers. New legislation may be needed to bolster confidence in the digital marketplace, but we’ve got to be thoughtful about it. So we don’t strangle the golden goose that we call the Internet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfc166fb-ac6a-5cc6-a89a-ceadecd4fc56'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfc166fb-ac6a-5cc6-a89a-ceadecd4fc56'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person whose job is to collect money from passengers on a bus?', 'b81bd1e5-a7eb-5ce3-8850-c60ec2289bf0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Conductor / Ticket seller', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfc3101e-71a8-574b-ac13-0e4aef884d1a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfc3101e-71a8-574b-ac13-0e4aef884d1a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a70a5eda-92de-5b62-a206-4a52271aecb6'::uuid, NULL, E'The workman expects to lose his job in the next few weeks.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfd00775-4b64-5f89-af8c-4b43794ed8d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfd00775-4b64-5f89-af8c-4b43794ed8d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dinosaurs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 5, 2, 1, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfd133d3-8436-5484-872e-104b6846a5bc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfd133d3-8436-5484-872e-104b6846a5bc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sleep Deprivation', NULL, 'eaa2b03e-905c-57f9-bf80-902e5f5ac2ec'::uuid, NULL, E'How can sleep deprivation cause such immense suffering? Scientists think the answer lies with the accumulation of waste products in the brain. During our waking hours, our cells are busy using up our day’s energy sources, which get broken down into various by products, including adenosine. As adenosine builds up, it increases the urge to sleep, also known as sleep pressure. In fact, caffeine works by blocking adenosine’s receptor pathways. Other waste products also build up in the brain, and if they are not cleared away, they collectively overload the brain and are thought to lead to the many negative symptoms of sleep deprivation. So, what’s happening in our brain when we sleep to prevent this? Scientists found something called the glymphatic system, a clean-up mechanism that removes this buildup and is much more active when we’re asleep. It works by using cerebrospinal fluid to flush away toxic byproducts that accumulate between cells. Lymphatic vessels, which serve as pathways for immune cells, have recently been discovered in the brain, and they may also play a role in clearing out the brain’s daily waste products. While scientists continue exploring the restorative mechanisms behind sleep, we can be sure that slipping into slumber is a necessity if we want to maintain our health and our sanity.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dfd75ad9-7c11-5791-9c9d-ff20de9da535'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfd75ad9-7c11-5791-9c9d-ff20de9da535'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4f6447f0-d232-5f8f-8d04-4e3fd09a07b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tests and exams will be the main part of your grade.', NULL, NULL),
  ('dfdead7d-04f6-5d65-aad7-db6074e66a79'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dfdead7d-04f6-5d65-aad7-db6074e66a79'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '70c2f1f2-3469-5783-9ea5-2faae5b9cd92'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Student reps will visit classes to distribute the voting paperwork.', NULL, NULL),
