  ('dff169f8-a42d-578c-b2b0-aebcb2dfc68a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dff169f8-a42d-578c-b2b0-aebcb2dfc68a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '20211059-6811-5a1c-95ca-26188674021b'::uuid, NULL, E'Late books at the library will have a daily fine added.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dff3254b-cb10-5626-bf62-1962e111f920'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dff3254b-cb10-5626-bf62-1962e111f920'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Biography', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 3, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('dff44407-973d-58bd-8dd1-9d4450cf4f05'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dff44407-973d-58bd-8dd1-9d4450cf4f05'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '939eaa3b-bdc4-5070-9b11-bbfeb1eab7ea'::uuid, NULL, E'The school''s audio apparatus includes a new set of multi-media devices.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dff9992d-862f-5b29-b4e3-0e4669c77872'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dff9992d-862f-5b29-b4e3-0e4669c77872'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Immediately relevant to game theory are the sex ratios in certain parasitic wasp species that have a large excess of females. In these species, fertilized eggs develop into females and unfertilized eggs into males. A female stores sperm and can determine the sex of each egg she lays by fertilizing it or leaving it unfertilized. By Fisher''s genetic argument that the sex ratio will be favored which maximizes the number of descendants an individual will have and hence the number of gene copies transmitted, it should pay a female to produce equal numbers of sons and daughters. Hamilton, noting that the eggs develop within their host—the larva of another insect—and that the newly emerged adult wasps mate immediately and disperse, offered a remarkably cogent analysis. Since only one female usually lays eggs in a given larva, it would pay her to produce one male only, because this one male could fertilize all his sisters on emergence. Like Fisher, Hamilton looked for an evolutionarily stable strategy, but he went a step further in recognizing that he was looking for a strategy.\n\nThe author suggests that the work of Fisher and Hamilton was similar in that both scientists', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Sought an explanation of why certain sex ratios exist and remain stable.', NULL, NULL),
  ('dffb4c34-c76c-5c73-b586-881fe651d6b1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dffb4c34-c76c-5c73-b586-881fe651d6b1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8cb90589-0125-54cb-b630-42214f9b78d1'::uuid, NULL, E'You can keep your bag in the back room.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('dffbca23-01e2-5faa-8777-09a44d47cf40'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dffbca23-01e2-5faa-8777-09a44d47cf40'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language Decaying', E'Let us begin by asking why the conviction that our language is decaying is so much more widespread than the belief that it is progressing, in an intellectual climate where the notion of the survival of the fittest is at least as strong as the belief in inevitable decay, it is strange that so many people are convinced of the decline in the quality of English, a language which is now spoken by an estimated half billion people – a possible hundredfold increase in the number of speakers during the past millennium. One''s first reaction is to wonder whether the members of the anti-slovenliness brigade, as we may call them, are subconsciously reacting to the fast-moving world we live in, and consequently resenting change in any area of life. To some extent this is likely to be true. A feeling that "fings ain''t wot they used to be" and an attempt to preserve life unchanged seem to be natural reactions to insecurity, symptoms of growing old. Every generation inevitably believes that the clothes, manners and speech of the following one have deteriorated. We would therefore expect to find a respect for conservative language in every century and every culture and, in literate societies, a reverence for the language of the ‘best authors’ of the past.', NULL, NULL, E'While English is widely spoken in the world, it is strange that so many people are convinced of the decline in the quality of English, and the reason may be that the members of the anti-slovenliness brigade are subconsciously reacting to the fast-moving world and consequently resenting change in any area of life because every generation inevitably believes that things in the following generation have deteriorated.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('dffbe8b0-468e-5101-9057-4c6674c6209d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'dffbe8b0-468e-5101-9057-4c6674c6209d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Rainbows', E'While rainbows appear magical, their formation is rooted in the {{1}} of science. Sunlight, composed of various wavelengths of light, enters a raindrop. These wavelengths bend differently, causing them to separate like a prism. As the light exits the raindrop, it bends again, creating the spectrum of colors we {{2}} as a rainbow. Interestingly, the order of colors is always the same, due to the specific ways light interacts with water. But rainbows are more than just captivating phenomena; they hold cultural {{3}} across diverse societies, often symbolizing hope, peace, or new beginnings. Next time you witness a rainbow, {{4}} a moment to appreciate not only its beauty but also the fascinating science behind it. Even the most ordinary phenomena can hold hidden wonders, waiting to be discovered.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.principles, 2.perceive, 3.significance, 4.take', NULL, NULL),
  ('e005740b-ee95-5426-825b-18d0dbafa3a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e005740b-ee95-5426-825b-18d0dbafa3a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Marine Biology', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'5, 1, 2, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('e00a42e6-9d86-53c6-939e-95e1cc210ba3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e00a42e6-9d86-53c6-939e-95e1cc210ba3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lute', E'The lute, a plucked string instrument, {{1}} a central role in European music from the late Middle Ages through the Baroque period. Its pear-shaped body and fretted neck {{2}} it a versatile instrument for both solo and ensemble performances. Unlike the modern guitar, the lute typically has paired strings, which {{3}} a richer, more resonant tone. During the Renaissance, the lute was highly valued by both professional musicians and amateur players. Its popularity gradually declined in the 18th century, as keyboard instruments became more fashionable. {{4}} , the lute remains an important subject of study for those interested in early music performance practices, and it {{5}} frequently used in historically informed concerts today.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.played, 2.made, 3.produce, 4.Nevertheless, 5.is', NULL, NULL),
  ('e01215a4-ce71-5cd3-8d1b-5a7f77b0fae7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e01215a4-ce71-5cd3-8d1b-5a7f77b0fae7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the people who work for a company?', '44bb4581-ced1-5d42-b290-34064881a403'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Employee', NULL, NULL),
  ('e01489f8-9732-53d9-80f2-2c1e0a60b5f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e01489f8-9732-53d9-80f2-2c1e0a60b5f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'AI for Teaching', E'Artificial intelligence is good in the teaching field. To what extent do you agree with this?', NULL, NULL, E'Artificial intelligence (AI) is revolutionizing the teaching field by introducing innovative ways to improve learning and teaching processes. Many argue that AI is a beneficial addition to education due to its ability to deliver personalized learning, ensure accessibility at all times, and reduce the workload of teachers. This essay will discuss these positive aspects in detail.\nFirstly, AI enables highly personalized learning experiences. Unlike traditional classroom methods, AI systems can tailor lessons to suit each student''s learning pace and style. For example, platforms powered by AI analyze students'' progress and provide targeted exercises to help them improve in weaker areas. This ensures that students receive focused attention, which boosts understanding and performance.\nSecondly, AI tools are accessible 24/7, making education more flexible and convenient. Students can use AI-based platforms to learn at their own pace and get instant feedback on their progress, even outside classroom hours. This round-the-clock availability is especially helpful for students who need additional support or prefer self-paced learning. Additionally, AI helps teachers by automating tasks like grading and lesson planning, allowing them to dedicate more time to direct student interaction.\nIn conclusion, artificial intelligence is significantly enhancing the teaching field by providing personalized learning, improving accessibility, and supporting teachers in managing their workloads. While it is not without challenges, the positive impact of AI in education is undeniable. By integrating AI into education, we can create a more efficient and student-centered learning environment.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e01875b2-fa7c-5edb-a2bd-1e59dab8cb70'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e01875b2-fa7c-5edb-a2bd-1e59dab8cb70'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the area of low land between hills or mountains?', '54b80412-e1ab-5783-b402-4f71f4b39f87'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Valley / canyon', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0190efa-373f-5a47-9419-e6c13b47c677'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0190efa-373f-5a47-9419-e6c13b47c677'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pewter', E'Pewter is an attractive metal which has been used for the {{1}} of household and other items in Britain since Roman times. It is an alloy {{2}} mostly of tin which has been {{3}} with small amounts of other metals such as copper, lead or antimony to {{4}} it and make it more durable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.production, 2.consisting, 3.mixed, 4.harden', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0203568-65cd-5783-9e77-f8c4b7967b0c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0203568-65cd-5783-9e77-f8c4b7967b0c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'X-ray', E'Using an X-ray laser, a research team has investigated how water heats up under extreme conditions. In the process, the scientists were able to observe water that remained liquid even at temperatures of more than 170 degrees Celsius. The investigation revealed an anomalous dynamic behavior of water, which is of fundamental importance for the analysis of sensitive samples using X-ray lasers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e0266a34-5414-5f9c-9627-a117cf4cdc51'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0266a34-5414-5f9c-9627-a117cf4cdc51'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Kindermann', E'Kindermann says he thinks the compound could be a win-win for the planet and the animals. "You know the methane is kind of a waste product. And this energy, instead of losing it for the animal, it can be reused for the animal in terms of performance, and at the same time we are doing something for greenhouse gas emission and climate change." The product''s not on the market yet - toxicology tests are ongoing.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e026d1e2-c8c3-58cb-9360-54daf60bf030'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e026d1e2-c8c3-58cb-9360-54daf60bf030'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Language Structure', NULL, 'a0dbee6d-53fb-5bbe-844b-cedf36cae1ff'::uuid, NULL, E'The structure of a language forces us to attend to certain aspects of language, at the moment of using that language. It''s known as the thinking for speaking hypothesis. There''s evidence that language involves some kind of image simulation and that that has a consequence for how we perceive of certain events. Color is quite a complex property of a visual world. Your brain is decoding color in quite a complicated way. So you have many languages that have a term to denote both green and blue and typically we call this a ''grue'' term. You find this in languages like the Himba, for example, in the Namibian plains. In this experiment, we asked participants to look at the color tile and then after 30 seconds we show them the full array of colors and we say, "Now, pick the one that you just saw." And it''s a very difficult task if you''re an English speaker but a Himba speaker can do it like child''s play because that color is central to them. You simply cannot recognize colors that are not easily encoded in your native language.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e02c333f-3bd1-5301-8492-c02e65e58d0b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e02c333f-3bd1-5301-8492-c02e65e58d0b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'dd32deb9-ba0a-5352-8af4-a585edba41db'::uuid, NULL, E'Lower speed limits are part of a new road safety campaign.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e02d2638-fd39-56d4-b8aa-07605cf08bf1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e02d2638-fd39-56d4-b8aa-07605cf08bf1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dinosaur Extinct', E'What killed off the dinosaurs?The end of the Cretaceous Period saw one of the most dramatic mass extinctions the Earth has ever seen.The fossil record shows that throughout their 160-million-year existence, dinosaurs took on a huge variety of forms as the environment changed and new species evolved that were suited to these new conditions. Others that failed to adapt went extinct.But then 66 million years ago, over a relatively short time, dinosaurs disappeared completely (except for birds). Many other animals also died out, including pterosaurs, large marine reptiles, and other sea creatures such as ammonites. Although the number of dinosaur species was already declining, this suggests a sudden catastrophic event sealed their fate, causing unfavourable changes to the environment more quickly than dinosaurs and other creatures could adapt.The exact nature of this catastrophic event is still open to scientific debate. The catastrophe could have been an asteroid impact, volcanic eruptions or the effect of both, together with more gradual changes in the Earth’s climate over millions of years.Whatever the causes, the huge extinction that ended the age of the dinosaur left gaps in the ecosystem that were subsequently filled by mammals and birds, allowing them to evolve rapidly.', NULL, NULL, E'Dinosaurs took on a huge variety of forms throughout their 160-million-year existence as the environment changed and new species evolved and disappeared completely 66 million years ago over a short time, suggesting a sudden catastrophic event, which is still open to scientific debate, sealed their fate and caused unfavorable changes to the environment, but the huge extinction left gaps in the ecosystem for mammals and birds to evolve rapidly.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e033d88c-b3bc-5807-95e2-87fab15c11bf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e033d88c-b3bc-5807-95e2-87fab15c11bf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ab31367b-0a1b-5887-9ec8-12a55811fcde'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'She could not bring herself to tell him the sad news.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0365a30-a731-5c8e-8fdf-8e69c3d3d841'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0365a30-a731-5c8e-8fdf-8e69c3d3d841'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '97597bff-0263-5f5f-99ea-4f34c77c7306'::uuid, NULL, E'The university hosts a wide range of events both on and off campus.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e03ff169-32bd-5f3b-9083-4fb7c959783a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e03ff169-32bd-5f3b-9083-4fb7c959783a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Microorganism', E'Although for centuries preparations derived from living {{1}} were applied to wounds to destroy {{2}} , the fact that a microorganism is {{3}} of destroying one of another species was not {{4}} until the latter half of the 19th century. When Pasteur noted the antagonistic effect of other bacteria on the anthrax organism and pointed out that this action might be put to {{5}} use.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.matter, 2.infection, 3.capable, 4.established, 5.therapeutic', NULL, NULL),
  ('e04108d9-7875-51b1-9065-ec918cdb4b2e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e04108d9-7875-51b1-9065-ec918cdb4b2e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Planet Formation', E'Theories have long proposed that icy pebbles forming in the cold, outer regions of protoplanetary disks -- the same area where comets originate in our solar system -- should be the fundamental seeds of planet formation. The main requirement of these theories is that pebbles should drift inward toward the star due to friction in the gaseous disk, delivering both solids and water to planets.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e041ebc7-cbf8-5a10-b4a8-207e59bdf64e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e041ebc7-cbf8-5a10-b4a8-207e59bdf64e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '21f7e5c1-7e12-5c78-9c30-f2309b358fc8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Honey can be used as food and a health product.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e049431c-4632-5c73-a74f-399814d29632'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e049431c-4632-5c73-a74f-399814d29632'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Octopus Communication', E'Octopus communication relies on a range of signals and gestures, {{1}} complex messages within their communities. When {{2}} a dominant octopus, a younger, less dominant one might display specific postures or colors as {{3}} of submissiveness. These can include arm gestures or color changes, often accompanied by jetting water or changing textures. The dominant octopus, in {{4}} , may respond with {{5}} signals, such as gentle arm touches or adopting a relaxed posture.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.conveying, 2.approaching, 3.signs, 4.turn, 5.reassuring', NULL, NULL),
