  ('e0944cbb-94dc-53e4-a33d-7cfb51dea626'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0944cbb-94dc-53e4-a33d-7cfb51dea626'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e540ffbd-22ab-56d9-8767-5600fbdce8ea'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Students working together often find their educational experiences enriched.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e09899ed-05cc-5a08-a84b-6a07afa0a475'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e09899ed-05cc-5a08-a84b-6a07afa0a475'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '02475a8b-d24d-5ff1-8eaa-2c2788169454'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The university awarded her a scholarship for her academic achievements.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e099493f-2e9d-5751-9a01-e4e166bf2947'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e099493f-2e9d-5751-9a01-e4e166bf2947'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Iceberg', E'B-15 broke off from the Ross Ice Shelf in Antarctica. It was the largest iceberg ever documented, with a surface area of more than 4,200 square miles — more than twice the size of the state of Delaware. After it started breaking up, the largest of its pieces, B-15a, drifted along the coast of Antarctica, lingered on a shallow seamount, and collided with an ice tongue, before running aground and breaking again. Late in 2007, the largest remaining chunk floated out into the South Pacific where, in the warmer water, it began to disintegrate.\nFor the whole of the next year, the ocean was noisier than usual. All the way up past the equator, 4,350 miles or so away from where B-15a broke apart, hydrophones that scientists from the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) had suspended underwater were picking up strange signals. Another set of hydrophones, this one in the Juan Fernández Islands, off the coast of Chile, picked up the noise, too, even louder. When the scientists used the two sets of data to determine the source of the noise, they found the most likely culprits: B-15a and C-19a, another giant iceberg.\nTwenty years ago, not so long before B-15 broke off from Antarctica, “we didn’t even know that icebergs made noise,” says Haru Matsumoto, an ocean engineer at NOAA who has studied these sounds. But in the past few years, scientists have started to learn to distinguish the eerie, haunting sounds of iceberg life — ice cracking, icebergs grinding against each other, an iceberg grounding on the seafloor — and measure the extent to which those sounds contribute to the noise of the ocean. While they’re just now learning to listen, the sounds of ice could help them understand the behavior and breakup of icebergs and ice shelves as the poles warm up.\n\nWhere did the largest piece off from B-15 eventually go?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Antarctica', NULL, NULL),
  ('e09bde68-53e5-5937-9e1b-df0ce670e420'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e09bde68-53e5-5937-9e1b-df0ce670e420'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '901b8be8-d5d8-50ec-911d-9ed051da386b'::uuid, NULL, E'Key business partners are often intertwined in expense accounts.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e0a655c8-0d72-5f67-848e-fde44d6c92d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0a655c8-0d72-5f67-848e-fde44d6c92d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Scientific Method', E'The logic of the scientific method was set out by John Stuart Mill in 1843 and was named the method of difference. A simple example of what he meant by this is to take two glasses of water which are {{1}} in every respect. Introduce a few drops of ink into one of these glasses. The water changes colour! According to Mill’s method of difference it is safe to assume that the change in the colour of the water is due to the {{2}} of a new factor - the {{3}} variable -in this case, the ink.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.identical, 2.introduction, 3.independent', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0a7a2c9-10d5-507f-8dd5-f2324b3f6401'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0a7a2c9-10d5-507f-8dd5-f2324b3f6401'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Leadership', E'A leader can define or clarify goals by issuing a memo or an executive order, an edict or a fatwa or a tweet, by passing a law, barking a command, or presenting an interesting idea in a meeting of colleagues. Leaders can mobilize people''s energies in ways that range from subtle, quiet persuasion to the coercive threat or the use of deadly force. Sometimes a charismatic leader such as Martin Luther King Jr. can define goals and mobilize energies through rhetoric and the power of example. We can think of leadership as a spectrum, in terms of both visibility and the power the leader wields. On one end of the spectrum, we have the most visible: authoritative leaders like the president of the United States or the prime minister of the United Kingdom, or a dictator such as Hitler or Qaddafi. At the opposite end of the spectrum is casual, low-key leadership found in countless situations every day around the world, leadership that can make a significant difference to the individuals whose lives are touched by it. Over the centuries, the first kind — the out-in-front, authoritative leadership — has generally been exhibited by men. Some men in positions of great authority, including Nelson Mandela, have chosen a strategy of "leading from behind"; more often, however, top leaders have been quite visible in their exercise of power. Women (as well as some men) have provided casual, low-key leadership behind the scenes. But this pattern has been changing, as more women have taken up opportunities for visible, authoritative leadership.', NULL, NULL, E'A leader can define goals by issuing a memo or an executive order, and can mobilize people’s energies in ways ranging from persuasion to the coercive threat or the use of deadly force, for leadership is like a spectrum, in terms of visibility and the power the leader wields, while top leaders have been quite visible in their exercise of power, but more women have taken up opportunities for visible, authoritative leadership.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e0aa68c5-8812-5802-b5a8-5507e3b73444'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0aa68c5-8812-5802-b5a8-5507e3b73444'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a group of islands?', '0b90bc70-23b6-5f1d-81b6-4a5edb96edeb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Archipelago', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0af199b-476b-5664-9315-7248609e1d45'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0af199b-476b-5664-9315-7248609e1d45'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Communication Tone', E'Communication is not just about what you say, but how you say it. Your tone of voice in communication can make or break your relationships, your career and your life. According to a study by researchers from the University of Southern California, the tone of voice in communication is a better {{1}} of relationship success than the actual words or behaviors of the partners. Your tone of voice in communication is {{2}} of four elements: pitch, pace, volume and modulation. These elements {{3}} your attitude, emotion and intention to your listener. By being mindful of these elements, you can watch your tone and use it to achieve your goals. {{4}} you want to build rapport, make connections, influence others or get what you want, your tone of voice in communication can help you do that.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.predictor, 2.composed, 3.convey, 4.Whether', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0b4717e-a73f-5c13-bb99-de693a5cb133'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0b4717e-a73f-5c13-bb99-de693a5cb133'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Infection', E'An analysis of ten different species finds that humans — followed by ferrets and to a lesser extent cats civets and dogs — are the most susceptible animals to SARS-CoV-2 infection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e0b7261f-c174-53ad-b978-6e399ae3a03e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0b7261f-c174-53ad-b978-6e399ae3a03e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the short sleep in the afternoon?', 'cc9e383d-e2a5-5b35-a44d-37e1ffdfa823'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Siesta / nap', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0bfe09c-50e5-5d93-be7e-6838ba123926'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0bfe09c-50e5-5d93-be7e-6838ba123926'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sleep Habbits', E'Sleep is essential for health and well-being, but many Americans do not get {{1}} of it. This problem may start as early as childhood, especially for racial and ethnic minorities, according to a study led by Julio Fernandez-Mendoza, a professor of psychiatry and behavioral health at Penn State Health. The study followed 700 children, ages 5 to 12, for seven years and found that Black children were seven times less likely than white children to develop good sleep habits, {{2}} socioeconomic status. The researchers {{3}} this disparity to racism, stress and discrimination, which may affect children’s ability to fall and stay asleep. They also found that poor sleep in childhood persisted into adolescence and adulthood, increasing the risk of chronic health conditions such as cardiovascular disease, diabetes and obesity. The findings suggest that sleep disparities are not only a consequence but also a {{4}} of social and health inequities. The researchers called for more awareness and intervention to promote sleep health among minority children and families, as well as policies to address the structural {{5}} of poor sleep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.enough, 2.regardless of, 3.attributed, 4.cause, 5.determinants', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0c19ce1-b233-5dde-9ec4-76a076513b1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0c19ce1-b233-5dde-9ec4-76a076513b1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e1a53c1b-17b7-5c7b-b63a-5159b289c3e5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You do not need to have specialist knowledge to be able to read the book.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e0c3a0be-daf2-5720-9a2e-b88182e14824'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e0c3a0be-daf2-5720-9a2e-b88182e14824'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Yellowstone', E'Yellowstone was initially made famous due to its unique geology caused by its location on the North American plate, which for millions of years has slowly moved across a mantle hotspot via plate tectonics. The Yellowstone Caldera is a volcanic system, the largest in North America, which has formed as a result of this hot spot and subsequent large volcanic eruptions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
