  ('e4bddbde-aac8-5976-a38a-6813ba944291'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4bddbde-aac8-5976-a38a-6813ba944291'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2e0d3c94-3128-51a6-9da3-789e183f790f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There are a number of people who like to go to the countryside areas.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4c29789-bfc5-54c9-b332-bef32d762c8f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c29789-bfc5-54c9-b332-bef32d762c8f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lifetime Employment', E'Businesses should hire employees for their entire life. What is the disadvantage? What is your solution?', NULL, NULL, E'The idea of lifetime employment has been a long-standing tradition in many industries. However, in today''s fast-paced and ever-changing business landscape, this practice may not be the most effective approach. While there are some benefits to hiring employees for their entire life, there are also significant disadvantages. This essay will explore the disadvantages of lifetime employment and provide solutions to address these issues.\nOne disadvantage of lifetime employment is that it can lead to a lack of fresh perspectives and new ideas. When employees remain with a company for their entire career, they may become too comfortable with the status quo and be resistant to change. This can stifle innovation and limit a company''s ability to adapt to new challenges and opportunities.\nTo address this issue, companies can implement regular job rotations and encourage employees to take on new challenges. By exposing employees to different roles and departments, they can gain new skills and insights. Additionally, companies can provide opportunities for employees to attend conferences, workshops, and training programs to stay up-to-date with the latest trends and technologies.\nIn conclusion, while lifetime employment may have some benefits, there are also significant disadvantages that must be considered. A lack of fresh perspectives and new ideas can lead to stagnation and limit a company''s ability to innovate. Additionally, financial burdens during economic downturns can be a significant challenge for companies. However, by implementing regular job rotations, encouraging professional development, offering flexible employment options, and providing retirement packages, companies can mitigate these risks and create a more dynamic and sustainable workforce.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e4c3121d-0938-52b6-9f43-48673c706cca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c3121d-0938-52b6-9f43-48673c706cca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'A University', E'A university is a lot more than just classes and exams. University is a concept that offers you a host of possibilities to develop both academically and personally. Find out about the different projects, clubs and societies that are in your university. You will definitely find something you are interested in.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4c35825-d00e-5e3a-bb26-91a40ae79c21'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c35825-d00e-5e3a-bb26-91a40ae79c21'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dog Training', E'Training your dog can provide a number of benefits, such as improving their temperament and obedience, and increasing their overall happiness and well-being. It is important to begin training early on, using positive reinforcement techniques such as treats and praise. Consistency is key in training, and it''s important to establish clear rules and boundaries for your dog to follow.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4c4567b-df3c-5678-85a1-cb05589afbf2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c4567b-df3c-5678-85a1-cb05589afbf2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ancient Rome', NULL, '8a317b79-4a58-5c7d-9ef5-96666938aa60'::uuid, NULL, E'Most of what the general public knows about daily life in ancient Rome comes from art, architecture and literature, which tell us more about the elites, especially ... urn ... the goings-on of the emperors... but how much do we know of the lives of ordinary Romans? Did they have a voice, apart, that is, from what we can gather from graffiti? The usual picture is one of time spent at festivals, baths and, typically, the games. However, for many Romans, terrible living conditions, poverty, debt and the chance of being sold into slavery at any moment - that is, if they weren''t slaves already - left no time or energy for such forms of entertainment, or for any interestin politics, for that matter.\nIndeed, after the death of Augustus, executive power was taken from the elected assemblies of the Roman people. Now it was the emperor''s job to look after the people, and his generosity often depended on the mood and behavior of the people - on how often and how violently they protested and rioted. One example would be clauctius ensuring a steady grain supply, even in winter, after rioters pelted him with stale crusts of bread. There is an anecdote about, urn, Hadrian. While touring the provinces, an old lady approached him with a complaint; he made excuses and tried to get away. She said that if he wouldn''t give her a hearing, he shouldn''t be emperor. She got her hearing.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4c7797b-fa03-5bce-ae5d-be575217ec25'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c7797b-fa03-5bce-ae5d-be575217ec25'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '41e65766-8433-5ada-aa51-c1e4baa63c9a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The words used in academic lectures tend to be more formal.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4c90c06-fec2-512c-b35d-ae70fb3609fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4c90c06-fec2-512c-b35d-ae70fb3609fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Eco-anxiety', E'Eco-anxiety refers to a fear of environmental damage or ecological disaster. This sense of anxiety is largely based on the current and predicted future state of the environment and human-induced climate change. Anxiety around environmental issues may stem from the awareness of a rising risk of extreme weather events, losses of livelihood or housing, fears for future generations, and feelings of helplessness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4cad1d2-8e64-55bd-a2d3-df97001e1140'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4cad1d2-8e64-55bd-a2d3-df97001e1140'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Dogs on Campus', E'Universities are the shared {{1}} for both staff and students. Thus, dogs and other animals are not {{2}} on campus. To ensure {{3}} , animals are banned unless the guidance dogs are here for the disabled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.wealth, 2.permitted, 3.safety', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4cfb91d-a610-5929-93fb-f72796e78b56'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4cfb91d-a610-5929-93fb-f72796e78b56'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ae8a5283-7417-5d8c-865d-cd4c57f42fc3'::uuid, NULL, E'Modern poetry often tests the conventions of language and rhythm.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4d8c766-07ed-5c51-aaa5-bdf04ef6f3be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4d8c766-07ed-5c51-aaa5-bdf04ef6f3be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Television and Communication', E'Television has destroyed communication among friends and family. Do you agree with that?', NULL, NULL, E'Television has been a popular form of entertainment for decades, but some people argue that it has destroyed communication among friends and family. However, I disagree with this statement and believe that television has not destroyed communication among friends and family, for several reasons.\nFirstly, television can provide a shared experience that brings friends and family together. Watching a favorite show or movie together can be a bonding experience that creates shared memories and inside jokes. This shared experience can provide a foundation for further communication and interaction among friends and family. For example, my family and I have a tradition of watching classic movies together during the holidays. These shared experiences have created lasting memories and strengthened our relationships.\nSecondly, television can provide a starting point for discussion and conversation among friends and family. Watching a thought-provoking documentary or news program can spark important conversations about current events or social issues. These conversations can deepen relationships and provide opportunities for meaningful communication. For instance, my friends and I often watch documentaries about environmental issues and discuss ways we can make a positive impact on the planet.\nIn conclusion, while some people may argue that television has destroyed communication among friends and family, I believe that it has not. Television can provide a shared experience, starting point for discussion, and even bridge generational gaps between family members. Therefore, it is important to approach television as a tool for entertainment and education, rather than as a hindrance to communication. With the right approach, television can actually enhance communication among friends and family.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e4e600cf-4cd3-5346-b638-4e9291c56639'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4e600cf-4cd3-5346-b638-4e9291c56639'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who repairs and maintains machinery, engines, and other mechanical equipment?', '11587d91-5509-5003-8fd4-49fb17aa0e86'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Mechanic', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4e93f4c-e7f5-55b3-8548-0faab556fcb9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4e93f4c-e7f5-55b3-8548-0faab556fcb9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '51d59469-9c37-53ef-af0d-b58c4ec4c635'::uuid, NULL, E'The bibliography needs to be removed prior to the publication.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e4f5fad3-8568-55a0-829e-003a9dd0691d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4f5fad3-8568-55a0-829e-003a9dd0691d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Physical Geography', E'Listen to part of a lecture and answer the questions. Hello, my name is jenny smith. I will be your physical geography teacher for this semester. Um. Since this is your first class, I want to talk about what physical geography is, what is physical geography. Does anyone have any ideas? Basically, it''s a science about the earth, but it differs from others in that it uses ideas from other sciences profoundly. For example, you will find information from chemistry, biology, climatology, astronomy, and many other sciences. And physical geography doesn''t sound scary. Actually, you don''t really need to worry about it. Fundamentally, this is a geography class. So we just we''ll use what we already know in those areas. We will not go into the details of those subjects. Ok, now let me show you some examples. Turn to page eleven, chapter one energy one.\n\nWhich statement is correct about physical geography?', '5fd0c2fe-dc03-501d-af8b-a15ed9834063'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Physical geography uses many other sciences.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4f8aba1-a4be-5435-957e-b3294bcea841'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4f8aba1-a4be-5435-957e-b3294bcea841'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Climate', E'Climate is the word we {{1}} for weather over a long period of time. The desert has a {{2}} climate, because there {{3}} very little rain. The UK {{4}} a temperate climate, which means winters are, overall, mild {{5}} summers, generally, don''t get too hot.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.use, 2.dry, 3.is, 4.has, 5.and', NULL, NULL),
  ('e4fb8090-bda6-53f1-b594-7511ebf181f6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e4fb8090-bda6-53f1-b594-7511ebf181f6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Photosynthesis', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 4, 2, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('e50b6275-3892-5738-9103-6d69b6ad9181'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e50b6275-3892-5738-9103-6d69b6ad9181'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High-protein Diet', E'In our studies, those people on a high-protein diet lost the same amount of weight as those on a higher-carbohydrate diet, since the two diets {{1}} an equal amount of kilojoules and the same amount of fat. However, body composition (that is, the ratio of fat to muscle) showed greater improvement among those people on the higher-protein diet. When the {{2}} in other studies were allowed to eat until they were no longer hungry, those on the higher protein diet lost more weight than those on the higher carbohydrate diet, even after more than a year. The reduction in hunger and the beneficial effect on muscle provided by the higher-protein diet is mostly related to its protein content, while the reduced triglyceride levels and enhanced fat-loss seem to be related to its lower amounts of carbohydrate. The diet is healthy because its protein comes from lean red meat, fish, chicken and low-fat dairy products, all of which {{3}} good nutrition. A high-protein diet in which the protein comes from protein powders and supplements is unlikely to be healthy, unless the supplements are {{4}} with vitamins and minerals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.offered, 2.participants, 3.provide, 4.fortified', NULL, NULL),
  ('e50eb50e-c17f-5281-ac45-6f42fee1220f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e50eb50e-c17f-5281-ac45-6f42fee1220f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '38f340ab-1dfa-520e-b11c-845326d54d5f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There are not many interconnections between philosophy and psychology.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e510a595-e67d-592d-bcb5-3d028aa0eb4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e510a595-e67d-592d-bcb5-3d028aa0eb4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Urbanization', E'Do you agree that urbanization has more advantages than disadvantages for society?', NULL, NULL, E'Urbanization, the process of population concentration in urban areas, has become a defining feature of modern society. While it poses challenges, I firmly believe that urbanization brings more advantages than disadvantages to society. The enhanced infrastructure, economic opportunities, and cultural vibrancy that urbanization fosters contribute significantly to societal progress.\nOne of the primary advantages of urbanization is the improved infrastructure and services available in cities, which directly benefit residents. Urban areas typically have better transportation systems, healthcare facilities, and educational institutions, enhancing the quality of life for individuals. Access to these services not only improves daily living but also promotes overall well-being and productivity among urban dwellers.\nFurthermore, urban areas serve as economic powerhouses, offering a multitude of job opportunities and fostering economic growth. The concentration of businesses, industries, and commercial activities in cities creates a vibrant environment that encourages innovation and entrepreneurship. This economic dynamism not only generates employment prospects but also drives overall economic progress, leading to greater prosperity for society as a whole.\nIn conclusion, urbanization offers a myriad of advantages that outweigh the drawbacks for society. From improved infrastructure and economic opportunities to cultural diversity and social interactions, urbanization contributes positively to societal development. Embracing the benefits of urbanization while addressing its challenges is essential for harnessing the full potential of urban living in shaping a vibrant and inclusive society.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e515b59f-68a3-50d3-9e72-fb0e4b85e4a1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e515b59f-68a3-50d3-9e72-fb0e4b85e4a1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the antonym of depression, and especially is used to describe financial success?', 'da1b312c-4993-505b-8bdb-cb73ec0738ff'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Prosperity', NULL, NULL),
  ('e51dc181-6b99-544d-b93a-84989d4107ca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e51dc181-6b99-544d-b93a-84989d4107ca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Lions and Lionesses', E'Lions and lionesses play different roles in the life of the pride. The lionesses work together to hunt and help rear the cubs. This allows them to get the most from their hard work, keeping them healthier and safer. Being smaller and lighter than males, lionesses are more agile and faster.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e51e4ea5-0134-5435-989c-135638d4b6e3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e51e4ea5-0134-5435-989c-135638d4b6e3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the scientific study of rocks?', '78bd0aa2-9079-59c7-8cb2-1a8240aff55d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Geology', NULL, NULL),
  ('e532ffb3-3257-5365-b444-837a9f59bc4b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e532ffb3-3257-5365-b444-837a9f59bc4b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'af9e87a8-2fa2-5c93-bc2e-8ba811398031'::uuid, NULL, E'Fishing is both a sport and a means of survival.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e5371b6a-40d0-5408-86c1-180d3947aeb6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e5371b6a-40d0-5408-86c1-180d3947aeb6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Which country is both a continent and a country?', '54de92ba-6b78-5bf4-bf71-1306ce2163ce'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Australia', NULL, NULL),
  ('e53bf7e1-b031-5762-af49-6c5deda55877'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e53bf7e1-b031-5762-af49-6c5deda55877'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'a47135ff-3c06-5108-860c-0fb43a8e52a3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Graduates have to fight for jobs in the highly competitive market.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e53e630e-2a48-5249-9323-2ee29516970a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e53e630e-2a48-5249-9323-2ee29516970a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Vitamins', E'While vitamins are essential for maintaining overall health and well-being, excessive or inadequate intake may have adverse effects. Research suggests that certain vitamins, such as vitamin D and vitamin E, may play a role in reducing the risk of mortality from specific causes, such as cardiovascular disease or cancer.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e53f1096-db20-5f94-96f1-08e26b3587cf'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e53f1096-db20-5f94-96f1-08e26b3587cf'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the collection of maps called?', '986c1ee0-565c-51a3-be68-50aa36e1090b'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Atlas', NULL, NULL),
  ('e540edcd-37f4-51ac-9943-24dc2f4e2f4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e540edcd-37f4-51ac-9943-24dc2f4e2f4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'c825d3e5-488e-5c7a-93ee-3aceae7a74a8'::uuid, NULL, E'Companies need to satisfy customers’ needs if they want to be successful.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e544615f-f984-55e3-af8c-e3d1cfe9c7e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e544615f-f984-55e3-af8c-e3d1cfe9c7e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Important Environment', E'Environment is important. It is better for children to grow up in the countryside than in a big city. To what extent do you agree with this statement?', NULL, NULL, E'The environment in which children grow up plays a crucial role in their development. While some argue that it is better for children to grow up in the countryside, I believe that a big city offers unique advantages and opportunities for a child''s overall growth and development. In this essay, I will present the negative standpoint of growing up in the countryside and highlight the benefits of a big city environment.\nOne of the drawbacks of growing up in the countryside is limited access to educational and cultural opportunities. In a big city, children have access to a wide range of educational institutions, museums, libraries, and cultural events that can broaden their horizons and enhance their learning experiences. The diverse population in a city also exposes children to different perspectives and cultures, fostering tolerance and understanding.\nAnother disadvantage of growing up in the countryside is the lack of diversity. In a big city, children are exposed to people from various backgrounds, ethnicities, and socioeconomic statuses. This exposure promotes inclusivity and helps children develop a global mindset. It also provides them with a greater understanding of the world and prepares them for the multicultural society they will encounter as adults.\nIn conclusion, while the countryside may offer a serene and natural environment, growing up in a big city provides children with numerous advantages. Access to educational and cultural opportunities, exposure to diversity, and the development of a global mindset are just a few of the benefits that a big city environment offers. It is essential to consider the unique opportunities that urban settings provide when discussing the importance of a child''s environment.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e54e95f3-8af5-5768-9a65-adfd160b864b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e54e95f3-8af5-5768-9a65-adfd160b864b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '0b4eb0ff-f3af-5275-84ce-fbda1b41d4ba'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There will be no sports matches during the exam period.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e54f12f1-00e2-538a-b08b-447c1b99e76f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e54f12f1-00e2-538a-b08b-447c1b99e76f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Online Shopping', E'To what extent do you think online shopping will replace traditional shopping?', NULL, NULL, E'The evolution of online shopping has revolutionized the retail landscape, raising questions about the extent to which it will replace traditional shopping methods. The convenience, accessibility, and global reach of online shopping have reshaped consumer behavior and preferences, signaling a potential shift toward a digital retail environment.\nOnline shopping offers unparalleled convenience and accessibility, with the flexibility of 24/7 availability and a vast array of products at consumers'' fingertips. The ability to shop anytime, anywhere, and browse through a diverse selection of items without leaving the comfort of one''s home has made online shopping a preferred choice for many modern consumers seeking convenience and efficiency in their shopping experience.\nMoreover, online shopping often provides competitive prices, discounts, and cost-saving opportunities that surpass those offered in traditional brick-and-mortar stores. The ease of comparing prices, accessing exclusive deals, and benefiting from a global marketplace allows consumers to make informed purchasing decisions and secure value for their money. Additionally, the global reach of online shopping enables consumers to access a wide range of products from around the world, expanding choices beyond what local stores can offer.\nIn conclusion, the rise of online shopping has significantly transformed the retail landscape, offering unparalleled convenience, competitive prices, and global accessibility to consumers. While traditional shopping methods continue to hold significance for certain consumers, the convenience and benefits of online shopping are undeniable. The increasing shift towards digital platforms suggests that online shopping is poised to play an increasingly dominant role in the retail sector, potentially replacing traditional shopping methods as consumers seek efficiency, value, and a diverse range of products in the digital age.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e55b9777-4140-550f-b827-0172913d7545'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e55b9777-4140-550f-b827-0172913d7545'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '4d2ec530-637f-585e-99be-ce66feea10e0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Libraries provide lots of useful services for students.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e55da5ea-c32b-5f9f-a143-753264ea08ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e55da5ea-c32b-5f9f-a143-753264ea08ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Kitchen Sponge', E'Ask bacteria where they''d like to live, and they''ll answer: a kitchen sponge, please. Sponges are microbe paradises, capable of housing 54 billion bacteria per cubic centimeter. In addition to being damp, airy and loaded with food scraps, sponges provide an optimal physical environment for bacteria, researchers report February 10 in Nature Chemical Biology.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
