  ('e6e4842a-a8ce-5e3c-b375-82bda6a13aae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6e4842a-a8ce-5e3c-b375-82bda6a13aae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Understanding Bias', E'A word on bias: some consider bias to be a problem. However, we might argue here that bias is a normal part of life and human interaction. We are all biased by our upbringing, our experiences, and our perspectives. While any attempt to be {{1}} in your analysis is a good thing, it can be just as useful to {{2}} your biases in your research and arm the reader or consumer of your material accordingly. In a way, this is a form of respect to your readership; you acknowledge their critical thinking role in {{3}} your material and also acknowledge that {{4}} out all bias—no matter how professional or scientific one’s research approach might be—is ultimately impossible.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.objective, 2.acknowledge, 3.consuming, 4.ruling', NULL, NULL),
  ('e6e79c63-faa2-5f2a-91c5-72a0a27ca597'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6e79c63-faa2-5f2a-91c5-72a0a27ca597'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '6ae4fe76-8e1a-5652-9cdd-876814af5207'::uuid, NULL, E'Media attention has recently shifted to environmental and educational issues.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e6e90cce-caba-54ab-b9e5-35a25930f959'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6e90cce-caba-54ab-b9e5-35a25930f959'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the cool area under a tree?', 'f8ec138b-a813-517c-9ea4-90329a778222'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Shade', NULL, NULL),
  ('e6ea8392-a377-5564-b31e-e26616abd079'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6ea8392-a377-5564-b31e-e26616abd079'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Push and Pull', E'People move to a new region for many different reasons. The {{1}} for moving can come from a combination of what researchers sometimes call ''push and pull {{2}} '' — those that encourage people to leave a region, and those that attract people to a region. Some of the factors that motivate people to move {{3}} seeking a better climate, finding more affordable housing, looking for work or retiring from work, leaving the {{4}} of city living, wanting a more pleasant environment, and wanting to be near to family and friends. In reality, many complex factors and personal reasons may {{5}} to motivate a person or family to move.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.motivation, 2.factors, 3.include, 4.congestion, 5.interact', NULL, NULL),
  ('e6f3ed05-c169-58a2-8919-1cfb42737e71'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6f3ed05-c169-58a2-8919-1cfb42737e71'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is a small handheld light that usually gets its power from batteries?', 'aa03e995-8dc0-547b-84b9-c227368e2510'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Flashlight / torch', NULL, NULL),
  ('e6f93669-0b0b-5b3a-a484-74069a650c06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6f93669-0b0b-5b3a-a484-74069a650c06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term used for see-through items such as clear glass?', 'ff930907-a281-574c-9273-0984fbaafc5a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Transparent / lucid / pellucid / crystal', NULL, NULL),
  ('e6fed0d9-0c24-54a4-bfe9-a28609d31fef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e6fed0d9-0c24-54a4-bfe9-a28609d31fef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Melatonin', E'Most people think of melatonin as a natural nod-off aid. Experts strongly urge people to consult their doctor or a sleep specialist before taking melatonin, in part because the supplement does not address many underlying health problems that may be disrupting sleep. Instead of a lights-out trigger, melatonin acts more like a dimmer switch, turning the day functions off and switching night functions on. So taking a melatonin supplement is sort of like taking a dose in sunset, tricking your body into feeling like it’s nighttime. It doesn’t put you to sleep as much as it tells the body that it’s time to sleep.\n\nWhat is purpose of this passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'To introduce melatonin.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e700f0ef-4e71-52c8-9c09-4d5bef5d47af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e700f0ef-4e71-52c8-9c09-4d5bef5d47af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Social Networking Websites', E'If you truly want to leverage social networking websites to build your multilevel marketing or other online business, you need to listen first and develop trust second. That’s when you can begin to use your community marketing abilities that used to work so well before everyone experienced to be so transparent.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e709593f-493f-5f0d-98ad-c5475816b6a2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e709593f-493f-5f0d-98ad-c5475816b6a2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ad0ce213-a584-5f7e-877a-93e2b0e989d3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'These writing tips on the website contribute to professional writing skills.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e70ec831-b435-5b4f-808a-b09bf2181994'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e70ec831-b435-5b4f-808a-b09bf2181994'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'ff7acf21-4d0c-554f-a4f4-ed23d23fa8f0'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The student union hosts a variety of social events.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e713f5d9-d4e5-5d16-a294-c13453a55e46'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e713f5d9-d4e5-5d16-a294-c13453a55e46'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Current Law', E'The current law, which enables employers to fire new staff within the first 90 days without giving a reason, and without facing legal action for unfair dismissal, was introduced in 2009. Under the new law, the 90-day trial will remain as it is for businesses with fewer than 20 employees. Larger businesses will still be able to use the 90-day trial as a probationary period, but with greater protections for employees.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e716e3b4-2852-59a3-9e88-65f372006732'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e716e3b4-2852-59a3-9e88-65f372006732'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The English', E'The English have the reputation of being a nation of tea drinkers, but this wasn''t always the case. By the end of the 17th century, the English were the biggest coffee drinkers in the Western world, and coffee houses became the places to be seen. As well as gossip, you could pick up talk of the latest intellectual developments in science, politics, and so on, in this age of scientific discovery and progress. At first coffee houses were very basic; a room with a bar at one end and a few plain tables and chairs. Customers paid a penny for a bowl -- not a cup -- of coffee. A polite young woman was usually in charge of the bar because it was thought her presence would ensure that the customers didn''t use bad language or cause any trouble. An added attraction was that coffee houses provided free newspapers and journals.\nBut people didn''t go to the coffee houses just to drink coffee. They went to talk. They soon developed from simple cafes, where anyone with a penny could go for a drink and a chat, into clubs. People started to go to coffee houses where they would find other people who had the same jobs or who shared their interests and ideas, to talk and conduct business.\nThe great popularity of coffee houses lasted about a hundred years. In the later 18th century, increased trade with other countries made such luxuries as coffee cheaper and more easily available to the ordinary person. As a result people started to drink it at home. Also at this time more tea was imported from abroad, and the century of the coffee house was replaced by the domestic tea-party as the typical English social occasion.', NULL, NULL, E'By the end of the 17th century, the English were the biggest coffee drinkers in the Western world, and coffee houses became the places to be seen, where people, who didn''t go there just to drink coffee but also to talk, could pick up talk of the latest intellectual developments as well as gossip, which lasted about a hundred years until people started to drink it at home and more tea was imported from abroad.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e71d2789-574e-59e6-af43-1139b11aa12a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e71d2789-574e-59e6-af43-1139b11aa12a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call a person who studies the weather?', '849b00db-be7d-5a99-8bc6-8810360021cb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Meteorologist / climatologist', NULL, NULL),
  ('e721e3af-3539-52da-822d-0a43064da414'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e721e3af-3539-52da-822d-0a43064da414'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Powerless Creatures', E'Individual human beings are relatively powerless creatures, no match for lions or bears. It’s what they can do as groups that has {{1}} them to take over the planet. These groupings – corporations, religions, states – are now part of a vast network of {{2}} information flows. Finding points of resistance, where smaller units can {{3}} up to the waves of information washing around the globe, is becoming harder all the time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.enabled, 2.interconnected, 3.stand', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7287014-befd-574c-9e9f-73a6b9de7ec4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7287014-befd-574c-9e9f-73a6b9de7ec4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Getting up Early', E'The old generation like to get up early and start the day''s work. But the younger generation like to get up late and work late into the night. Choose one lifestyle you like and discuss its advantages or disadvantages.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e72ea4e1-5b75-5758-bc10-d2b8c96ddd4f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e72ea4e1-5b75-5758-bc10-d2b8c96ddd4f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4aaa18a9-5ed7-599d-b78f-975d7a198f8e'::uuid, NULL, E'Experience would be an advantage for this managerial role.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7380702-9b24-5730-b8ae-2fe52fa60f0c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7380702-9b24-5730-b8ae-2fe52fa60f0c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '197d23ad-ca6e-5eca-adc9-78c67797528f'::uuid, NULL, E'I need somebody to fix the problem with the computer screen.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7396aac-3340-5df3-9680-6f607a2eef73'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7396aac-3340-5df3-9680-6f607a2eef73'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mexican Women', E'In The Women of Mexico City, 1796-1857, Sylvia Marina Arrom argues that the status of women in Mexico City improved during the nineteenth century. According to Arrom, households headed by females and instances of women working outside the home were much more common than scholars have estimated; efforts by the Mexican government to encourage female education resulted in increased female literacy; and influential male writers wrote pieces advocating education, employment, and increased family responsibilities for women, while deploring women''s political and marital inequality. Mention of the fact that the civil codes of 1870 and 1884 significantly advanced women''s rights would have further strengthened Arrom''s argument. Arrom does not discuss whether women''s improved status counteracted the effects on women of instability in the Mexican economy during the nineteenth century. However, this is not so much a weakness in her work as it is the inevitable result of scholars'' neglect of this period. Indeed, such gaps in Mexican history are precisely what make Arrom''s pioneering study an important addition to Latin American women''s history.\n\nThe passage is primarily concerned with doing which of the following?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Reviewing a historical study of the status of women in Mexico City during the nineteenth century', NULL, NULL),
  ('e742cbb6-40a8-5c2b-b736-a747cf69e8c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e742cbb6-40a8-5c2b-b736-a747cf69e8c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'HCS', E'Genealogy can be defined as the compilation of information necessary to construct what is usually known as a family tree, our pedigree or our ancestry. It is a chart which shows the relationships between individual people in an extended family over a period of time.\nThe first records of genealogy can be traced back to the earliest civilisations in Northern Africa who recorded successions of dynasties and wealthy families reaching back hundreds of years. This was usually done to establish rights to title, land and property. There is evidence that this happened in many places in the world. However, it was the domain of the wealthy and few people outside those circles were even aware that family ancestry could be recorded and traced. This situation changed in the early nineteenth century when genealogy became more generally well-known after the first practical guide to research was published. But it was not until the mid twentieth century that family history was no longer solely devoted to tracing the genealogies of the great. the wealthy, or the famous and it became a more common activity among the general population.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '451d04f8-23c4-5dd7-843f-1a44a0bc2dcf'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Originally. tracing family history was only used in order to establish the origins of prosperous and powerful families. However. by the middle of the twentieth century. ordinary people were also starting to show an interest in researching their family background too.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7442bff-3e20-5056-a1b9-4ab52eb4847a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7442bff-3e20-5056-a1b9-4ab52eb4847a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Certain Gestures', E'When learning a foreign language, most people fall back on traditional methods: reading, writing, listening and repeating. But if you also gesture with your arms while studying, you can remember the vocabulary better, even months later. Linking a word to brain areas responsible for movement strengthens the memory of its meaning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e74b9b3d-fa93-5b2e-a5c3-85a8f07b7581'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e74b9b3d-fa93-5b2e-a5c3-85a8f07b7581'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a841c152-999d-5dff-a961-81f859dfcd15'::uuid, NULL, E'He seemed to take it for granted that he should speak as a representative.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e750b240-06a8-5037-80c6-e1f7c768aac2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e750b240-06a8-5037-80c6-e1f7c768aac2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9219e6b4-51e0-5f5f-9b69-baccffc9814e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The key to clear writing is clarity of thought.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e75b5427-8fdc-596e-9cf3-09d33c50d5a8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e75b5427-8fdc-596e-9cf3-09d33c50d5a8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Psychology', E'What psychology has focused primarily on throughout the years, and that''s over the last one over a hundred year since William James, is mostly on the negative on getting people from the negative to the zero point, to be OK, not to be sick. But then as Henry Thoreau once said, most men live of quiet desperation. So quiet desperation is not necessarily depressed, it''s not necessarily anxious but it''s not happy. And we''re not fulfilling our potential if we don''t focus on things that go beyond zero. So positive psychology came to rectify that you take us from the zero to the positive. But there is another reason why positive psychology is important. And that is before psychologists have found is that not only does it get us from the zero to the positive, but it also strengthens our immune system, i.e. makes us more resilient when dealing with the negative.\n\nWhat''re the positive psychology contributions on treatment of depression?', '87e422bf-012d-5753-a2e6-d8667466248d'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'to make patients happier\nto strengthen the immune system', NULL, NULL),
  ('e75d9724-9564-5092-bebf-f989f62cb22e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e75d9724-9564-5092-bebf-f989f62cb22e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ancient Greek', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('e75e18e6-682e-5071-8c06-3a20d81dd554'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e75e18e6-682e-5071-8c06-3a20d81dd554'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '338da3fc-7bfd-548b-b44c-1fa164a03254'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The features provide the same explanation for the problem.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7618a46-5e21-5d73-bc69-5e43329f6daa'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7618a46-5e21-5d73-bc69-5e43329f6daa'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sponsorship Marketing', E'Over the past three decades, sponsorship marketing has been a major contributor to the popularity of sports, particularly football. From 1996 to 2010, the sponsorship market worldwide experienced exponential growth, with brands paying large sums of money to leverage sponsorship rights and properties. Sponsorship marketing grew increasingly popular in the late 1980s when a significant shift was introduced in marketing. The shift was an effort by firms to differentiate themselves in the sponsorship market by moving away from the common ratification of products’ aspects and functional benefits towards brands’ symbolic overtones. Associating with sports properties allowed firms to illuminate their purpose and position, and get closer to consumers. Over time, firms have become critical of sponsorship and the value they bring given their cost. The criticism comes as there are no deliberate nor quantifiable derived benefits. As a result, firms focus more on title sponsorship of short-term tournaments instead of long-term sponsorship commitments. Short-term tournaments have generally been used as tactical selling assets. Short-term tournaments enable firms to easily and continually assess their financial commitments to the sponsored properties. The continued growth of title sponsorship in short-term tournament sports is attributable to several factors, but importantly, it is to get the consumers excited and remain engaged for the duration of the tournament. Short-term tournaments are beneficial for fans as they give instant gratification wherein their team could be crowned champions without waiting for the season-long league to conclude. Short-term tournaments are an instrument to elicit excitement for fans but also to deliver impact for sponsor firms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e7647e9f-2589-51d4-9445-0d88a4291890'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7647e9f-2589-51d4-9445-0d88a4291890'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd00767cb-4ecd-5349-a8a0-794451cdacf9'::uuid, NULL, E'The department determines whether or not the candidates pass.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e765786c-8d9a-5913-bf9f-51186a285d9e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e765786c-8d9a-5913-bf9f-51186a285d9e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wildlife', E'But they did find something that had a much bigger impact on wildlife: habitat quality. The best predictor of wildlife abundance was not human activity, but factors like forest connectivity, nearby housing density, and the amount of adjacent agriculture. The results were published in the Journal of Applied Ecology.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e765dc45-48f3-5c58-b8b8-9dd13b35d222'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e765dc45-48f3-5c58-b8b8-9dd13b35d222'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the chair a king or a queen sits in?', 'a44e3766-0a36-5dc1-8205-148d8523eefe'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Throne', NULL, NULL),
  ('e766bde5-c38b-5fc2-839b-b9263af2c3d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e766bde5-c38b-5fc2-839b-b9263af2c3d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the red liquid that flows through a body?', '473d2f0c-7ceb-5096-942a-efbbefc8bae4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Blood', NULL, NULL),
  ('e76773b5-d159-5a14-b026-8d5769104d9f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e76773b5-d159-5a14-b026-8d5769104d9f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '6a6d9387-b76e-54a5-afc5-d8c639823f24'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The new theory takes all the latest research results into account.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e76dca87-bd2d-5abe-88c3-b556bf25df58'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e76dca87-bd2d-5abe-88c3-b556bf25df58'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'India_Debt', NULL, '4fa64baf-1411-5d72-948b-1735538b8afd'::uuid, NULL, E'Today a hundred and fifty thousand farmers in India have committed suicide in areas where seed has been destroyed where they have to buy the seeds from Monsanto, and buy every year at very, very high cost and that high-cost seed is getting him into debt and the debt is pushing them to suicide. What we''ve done is create community seed banks, places where we collect and save seeds, rescue them from disappearance, multiply them and then distribute them according to farmers needs. And about 40 community seed banks have been created across the length and breadth of India. Places where these have been created farmers are not in distress because the biggest cost today is seeds and chemicals. These seed banks are now being a new place where we can respond to the new crisis of globalization on the one hand and climate change on the other. Globalization has led to farmer suicides. We are able to take seeds to the suicide zones and distribute the seeds so that farmers can break out of that dependency, grow food crops, get out of debt. We''ve been able to create community seed banks to deal with climate change for the extreme flooding the new droughts, the cyclones, the hurricanes that lead to salinization. And today for us the work on seed has become the place from where we are responding to the worst tragedies and the worst crisis of our times.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e770145c-96c2-5d38-a6d5-cda68f60138c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e770145c-96c2-5d38-a6d5-cda68f60138c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '000c20b7-ae32-5f74-be0f-27f8bd79e9b3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Certain individuals thrive in competitive scenarios, while others favor cooperative endeavors.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7703e14-80e7-50ce-909c-f4709c1322a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7703e14-80e7-50ce-909c-f4709c1322a3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Library Introduction', NULL, '056a6e2a-dbfe-59b2-ab4c-f2305222d49c'::uuid, NULL, E'There are many functional areas and services in the library.\nYou’ll see the service desk after entering the library and you can have these services at the service desk.\nThere are computers with special software on each floor, by which you can gain access to the internet and check emails and library catalogues.\nFollow the orange signs and you will find printers. Then, follow the instructions to use them.\nRemember to bring student cards. You have to use printers with your card. You can charge your card at the front desk.\nIf necessary, you can ask the staff at the front desk to help you.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
