  ('e7af708a-a892-530f-91e5-565317ebe091'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7af708a-a892-530f-91e5-565317ebe091'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'f35287b0-a057-55e6-86cf-9c1b1686da4d'::uuid, NULL, E'The object is to gather as great a diversity of genetic material as possible.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7af9dc6-4d18-502b-a687-1e4b50cd7c0c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7af9dc6-4d18-502b-a687-1e4b50cd7c0c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Private Equity', E'It isn''t rare for private equity houses to hire grads fresh out of business school, he said, but 9 times out of 10, the students who nab these jobs are the ones who had private equity experience under their belt before even starting their MBA program.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7b33be4-6514-5002-b046-b1ec2c238246'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7b33be4-6514-5002-b046-b1ec2c238246'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Existential Humility', E'We live in a time of unprecedented polarization and misinformation, where social media feeds us with dubious evidence to support our beliefs. How can we {{1}} this tendency and challenge our views? One possible answer is to embrace a little "existential humility". Existential humility is the ability to recognize the limits of our knowledge and the possibility of being wrong. It is a form of intellectual humility, which has been shown to have many benefits, such as reducing prejudice, increasing curiosity, and improving learning. Existential humility goes beyond acknowledging our factual errors, and also involves {{2}} our moral and philosophical assumptions. One way to cultivate existential humility is to experience awe, the emotion we feel when we encounter something vast, beautiful, or mysterious. Awe can expand our {{3}} and make us more open to new ideas and experiences. By embracing existential humility and cultivating awe, we can become more aware of our {{4}} and more willing to revise our opinions. We can also become more respectful of others and more interested in learning from them. In a world of division and confusion, existential humility and awe can help us open our minds and find {{5}} ground.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.overcome, 2.questioning, 3.perspective, 4.biases, 5.common', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7b518b1-8c54-5cd7-a710-ff3a38d34ab9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7b518b1-8c54-5cd7-a710-ff3a38d34ab9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8bbaf9c2-c9c8-58e0-ad0b-2188555c2009'::uuid, NULL, E'In the Middle Ages, a disease caused the world population to fall.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7b91a57-d2b7-5abf-b524-861f81bd8a8f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7b91a57-d2b7-5abf-b524-861f81bd8a8f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8f907851-dfd6-5575-a3ba-466fba90f23a'::uuid, NULL, E'I used to have a cup of coffee with one sugar.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7bb4d13-47b5-556f-906c-92b22d3c3b22'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7bb4d13-47b5-556f-906c-92b22d3c3b22'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a3710442-f88d-5536-b951-318d17e64254'::uuid, NULL, E'They have no way to dispose of the hazardous waste they produce.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e7be520f-cdad-55d1-bf9b-40931f83bf79'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7be520f-cdad-55d1-bf9b-40931f83bf79'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Groundwater is the word used to describe water that saturates the ground, filling all the available spaces. By far the most abundant type of groundwater is meteoric water; this is the groundwater that circulates as part of the water cycle. Ordinary meteoric water is water that has soaked into the ground from the surface, from precipitation (rain and snow) and from lakes and streams. There it remains, sometimes for long periods, before emerging at the surface again. At first thought it seems incredible that there can be enough space in the ''solid''ground underfoot to hold all this water. The necessary space is there, however, in many forms. The commonest spaces are those among the particles—sand grains and tiny pebbles—of loose, unconsolidated sand and gravel. Beds of this material, out of sight beneath the soil, are common. They are found wherever fast rivers carrying loads of coarse sediment once flowed. For example, as the great ice sheets that covered North America during the last ice age steadily melted away, huge volumes of water flowed from them. The water was always laden with pebbles, gravel, and sand, known as glacial outwash, that was deposited as the flow slowed down. The same thing happens to this day, though on a smaller scale, wherever a sediment-laden river or stream emerges from a mountain valley onto relatively flat land, dropping its load as the current slows: the water usually spreads out fanwise, depositing the sediment in the form of a smooth, fan-shaped slope. Sediments are also dropped where a river slows on entering a lake or the sea, the deposited sediments are on a lake floor or the seafloor at first, but will be located inland at some future date, when the sea level falls or the land rises; such beds are sometimes thousands of meters thick.\n\nAccording to this passage , where is groundwater usually found?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'In spaces between pieces of sediment', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7bf8138-3c2a-57b8-960e-f5781273cf8d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7bf8138-3c2a-57b8-960e-f5781273cf8d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Below-ground Organisms', E'"If you want to find unique {{1}} and if you want to find a wide range of {{2}} below-ground organisms, you don''t have to travel around the world. You can walk across Central Park."\nThat statement comes from Noah Fierer, an ecology and evolutionary biology professor at the University of Colorado, Boulder. He''s also a {{3}} of a study that uncovered the surprisingly large diversity of subterranean microbial life at the 843-acre green rectangle in the heart of Manhattan. The research is in the Proceedings of the Royal Society B.\nInvestigators looked at 596 {{4}} soil samples from the park and found thousands of different types of {{5}} . They also compared those microbes with those living in 52 other soil samples taken from all around the planet. The park had organisms that also exist in deserts, frozen tundra, forests, {{6}} and prairies. Antarctica was the only area that had microbes that did not overlap with those found in Central Park. And only a small percentage of the park''s microbes were found to be already listed in databases.\nThe variety of microbes probably reflects a diversity of soil conditions within the park.\nSeems that New York is a melting pot for people above the surface. And for microbes beneath it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.diversity, 2.different, 3.coauthor, 4.separate, 5.microbes, 6.rainforests', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7c1f5af-bce6-5e22-9a71-864545c304fc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7c1f5af-bce6-5e22-9a71-864545c304fc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Ocean', E'The ocean, a vast and mysterious expanse, conceals hidden wonders in its depths. Dive {{1}} the surface, and you''ll find coral reefs teeming with life, like {{2}} underwater cities. In these intricate ecosystems, even the tiniest organisms play crucial roles in {{3}} life and balance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.beneath, 2.bustling, 3.sustaining', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7c3def8-6ef6-5205-9273-a3b09f6daed3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7c3def8-6ef6-5205-9273-a3b09f6daed3'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What instrument would scientists use to examine very small life forms?', 'ad63bd13-282d-5adc-9795-d91096571a4e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Microscope', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7c481d0-4a4c-56bc-a00a-d9edbcf68742'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7c481d0-4a4c-56bc-a00a-d9edbcf68742'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Video Games', E'Video gaming is highly {{1}} in modern culture, particularly among young people, and a healthy hobby for most users. However, in recent years there has been increasing global recognition among public health professionals and academics that particular patterns of video gaming may lead to marked {{2}} in personal, family, social, educational, occupational or other important areas of functioning and psychological distress for a significant minority of players. People who partake in gaming should be {{3}} to the amount of time they spend on gaming activities, particularly when it is to the exclusion of other daily activities, as well as to any changes in their physical or psychological health and social functioning that could be {{4}} to their pattern of gaming behavior.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.prevalent, 2.impairment, 3.alert, 4.attributed', NULL, NULL),
  ('e7c8cd0b-ca56-52f4-a438-59bf5ba8f6d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e7c8cd0b-ca56-52f4-a438-59bf5ba8f6d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'60,000 Charity(6万个慈善机构)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 1, 2, 4, 5', NULL, NULL),
