  ('e98f7bdc-33ad-590d-af4a-89dd93867551'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e98f7bdc-33ad-590d-af4a-89dd93867551'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '8955891c-3552-5c04-addb-18d6fb364be3'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The university provides legislation for students and staff.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e9932c1c-393a-5352-8d7d-26027084713a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9932c1c-393a-5352-8d7d-26027084713a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the term for the rate of doing work or the rate of using energy?', '1bc75bbe-4f5d-5231-85a3-b6277ba7c485'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Power', NULL, NULL),
  ('e9938d77-cdc5-5d04-ae13-a64b804ee5be'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9938d77-cdc5-5d04-ae13-a64b804ee5be'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Shy Fish', NULL, '4e46c374-f7d0-5612-a4f3-bef706e2eee1'::uuid, NULL, E'But a new study of fish called sticklebacks shows that shy individuals actually prefer to follow fish that are similarly timid. Researchers had trios of sticklebacks with known personalities play follow the leader. The fish were placed in a tank that had some plastic plants at one end and some food hidden at the other. In some of the groups, a bold fish and a shy fish acted as leaders, while another shy fish followed. And in other groups, it was a bold fish that did the following. The researchers recorded whether the follower sallied forth more frequently with the fish that was behaviorally similar or the one that was different. What they found is that shy fish were more likely to emerge from undercover when an equally wary fellow was already out there. Bold follower fish did not seem to care which leader they followed. Of course, no matter which fish a stickleback chose to stick with, the bold fish did lead more expeditions over the course of the experiment than their more retiring friends. That''s because the bold fish initiated more trips, regardless of who might be tailing them. The researchers write that "when offered a choice of leaders, sticklebacks prefer to follow individuals whose personality matches their own, but bolder individuals may, nevertheless, be able to impose their leadership, even among shy followers, simply through greater effort."', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e99f1ea2-5ad2-598c-ade1-21f1b545c7a9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e99f1ea2-5ad2-598c-ade1-21f1b545c7a9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '586cc1d0-c874-5a2d-9830-67a154a5aa91'::uuid, NULL, E'Students can avoid viruses by eating lots of fruits and vegetables.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e9a13d48-bb6c-5694-8f1c-159146e4139e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9a13d48-bb6c-5694-8f1c-159146e4139e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mars Geology', E'The primary driver of modern Martian geology is its atmosphere, which is mostly made of carbon dioxide, nitrogen, and argon. By Earth standards, the air is preposterously thin; air pressure atop Mount Everest is about 50 times higher than it is at the Martian surface. Despite the thin air, Martian breezes can gust up to 60 miles an hour, kicking up dust that fuels huge dust storms and massive fields of alien sand dunes.\nOnce upon a time, though, wind and water flowed across the red planet. Robotic rovers have found clear evidence that billions of years ago, lakes and rivers of liquid water coursed across the red planet’s surface. This means that at some point in the distant past, Mars’s atmosphere was sufficiently dense and retained enough heat for water to remain liquid on the red planet’s surface. Not so today: though water ice abounds under the Martian surface and in its polar ice caps, there are no large bodies of liquid water on the surface there today.\nMars also lacks an active plate tectonic system, the geologic engine that drives our active Earth, and is also missing a planetary magnetic field. The absence of this protective barrier makes it easier for the sun’s high-energy particles to strip away the red planet’s atmosphere, which may help explain why Mars’s atmosphere is now so thin. But in the ancient past, Mars seems to have had an inner dynamo powering a planet-wide magnetic field. What shut down the Martian dynamo? Scientists are still trying to figure out.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e9a39657-e90a-5723-a6ce-061eb41e66d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9a39657-e90a-5723-a6ce-061eb41e66d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'd275244a-da08-5b91-8b72-118aa620d9a2'::uuid, NULL, E'Today''s lecture on modern American literature has been cancelled.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e9a84e34-3285-5c2b-a5ce-cdd7cc5e2efe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9a84e34-3285-5c2b-a5ce-cdd7cc5e2efe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'MCS-R', E'Currently, the paramount problem in the field of biomaterials, the science of replacing diseased tissue with human-made implants, is control over the interface, or surface, between implanted biomaterials and living tissues. The physical properties of most tissues can be matched by careful selection of raw materials: metals, ceramics, or several varieties of polymer materials. Even the requirement that biomaterials processed from these materials be nontoxic to host tissue can be met by techniques derived from studying the reactions of tissue cultures to biomaterials or from short-term implants. But achieving necessary matches in physical properties across interfaces between living and non-living matter requires knowledge of which molecules control the bonding of cells to each other—an area that we have not yet explored thoroughly. Although recent research has allowed us to stabilize the tissue-biomaterial interface by controlling either the chemical reactions or the microstructure of the biomaterial, our fundamental understanding of how implant devices adhere to tissues remains woefully incomplete.\n\nThe author''s primary purpose is to __', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'discuss the current state of technology in the field of biomaterials', NULL, NULL),
  ('e9a98d41-a2be-5ca8-91e5-93b94ba4e3b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9a98d41-a2be-5ca8-91e5-93b94ba4e3b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'External appearances', E'One should never judge a person by external appearances. Do you agree or disagree? Support your ideas with details.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('e9ab1b2f-608f-5269-8a86-1327e09b7869'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9ab1b2f-608f-5269-8a86-1327e09b7869'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '0922930b-e78d-5213-a93e-93db4071346f'::uuid, NULL, E'This Thursday is the last day for students to withdraw subjects without any penalty.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e9ab3527-80c0-5f20-927f-8ea04dd65823'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9ab3527-80c0-5f20-927f-8ea04dd65823'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '5280b144-aaf1-53e2-8069-afcbb5e0c0bd'::uuid, NULL, E'The paper must be reviewed thoroughly and appropriately.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('e9af65e8-0b0e-526b-be63-ccd712f58d00'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9af65e8-0b0e-526b-be63-ccd712f58d00'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mass Transportation', E'Mass transportation revised the social and economic fabric of the American city in three fundamental ways. It catalyzed physical expansion, it sorted out people and land uses, and it accelerated the inherent instability of urban life. By opening vast areas of unoccupied land for residential expansion, the omnibuses, horse railways, commuter trains, and electric trolleys pulled settled regions outward two to four times more distant from city centers than they were in the premodern era. The new accessibility of land around the periphery of almost every major city sparked an explosion of real estate development and fueled what we now know as urban sprawl.\n\nWhich one is not related to mass transportation according to this passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'To create better networks of public transportation.', NULL, NULL),
  ('e9b06f95-9402-561d-8bab-3a0cf6b04f4a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'e9b06f95-9402-561d-8bab-3a0cf6b04f4a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '02e289af-9e04-5be0-98ba-588851c90878'::uuid, NULL, E'You should sign up for classes using the university''s website.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
