  ('eb4a1716-7fa3-5e4d-a868-ce92051986fd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb4a1716-7fa3-5e4d-a868-ce92051986fd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '00342e3b-c3ad-5098-bded-949c3d2aa7b6'::uuid, NULL, E'Ideally, free trade is mutually beneficial for both trading partners.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eb5550f7-6236-5380-9e1d-46d1a84215df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb5550f7-6236-5380-9e1d-46d1a84215df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Great Zimbabwe', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb593c65-5bcc-5349-99df-aa6896bd3b2c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb593c65-5bcc-5349-99df-aa6896bd3b2c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the people who are taking an exam?', '69b5f936-e4ce-5db5-9e06-5bbb95af0405'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Candidates / test takers / exam-sitters', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb5af1a9-c2bd-5e7e-b97e-069f604b4860'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb5af1a9-c2bd-5e7e-b97e-069f604b4860'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Contemporary Writers', E'The earliest writers on politics - and I''m thinking of Plato and Aristotle here - felt free to draw insights from all areas of human knowledge, unlike modern academic writers who tend to put things into smaller and smaller compartments, or focus more closely on one area of enquiry. For example, Plato would examine a whole political system and the philosophy that underlies it, whereas modern writers on politics might concentrate on one particular institution in that system - the House of Lords in England - or on voting patterns within a country. With this focus the bigger questions that the ancients dealt with - "What is the best form of government?" or "What is justice?" -tend to get left behind. Many writers on politics these days are university-based and so have to have specialized interests, and while they may make new and interesting discoveries in their special field, it is at the loss of a broader perspective - not to mention the loss of a general audience or readership. In the 19th century, there were still writers who used the same freedom of enquiry as the ancients, and are all the more readable - and relevant - because of it.\n\nWhich of the following are suggested as reasons why contemporary writers on politics are less readable and relevant than the ancient writers?', 'e06b5e2f-5a85-573c-a91c-0966f499de5c'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'They tend to focus on only one aspect of political systems.\nBeing university-based forces them to specialize.', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb607e04-e3f0-5f40-a798-00e3a630059b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb607e04-e3f0-5f40-a798-00e3a630059b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Salt', NULL, 'c7f2580f-21b2-5784-bf98-e206dc962716'::uuid, NULL, E'So today we''re continuing to talk about the social history of foodstuffs, and we''re going on to consider next the importance of salt and the significant role it has played. Salt was a highly valued commodity in ancient times. Not because it made food taste nicer, but because of the way it could be used to preserve food. This meant that people were not so dependent on seasonal variations in what was available for them to eat - they could preserve what they produced and consume it as required. It also meant that food could be transported long distances. Salt was not easy to obtain and so prices for it were high. It was often necessary to transport it long distances and it is believed that one of the reasons for building some of the roads that led to the ancient city of Rome was to make it easier to bring salt to the city from various parts of the Roman empire. Roman rulers took financial advantage of the population''s need for salt.\nWhen they wanted to raise money for some war or another, they raised the price of salt. Elsewhere salt was important too. In Africa, for example, caravans consisting of up to forty thousand camels are said to have travelled four hundred miles across the Sahara to transport salt to the inland markets of places like Timbuktu.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eb60bf5b-62a8-5cca-a645-116c745d644c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb60bf5b-62a8-5cca-a645-116c745d644c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'dd5ab6d7-33c1-562a-b048-7c1f3be350b8'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Now we can safely draw some conclusions from our discussion.', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb61d659-3ddb-5bc2-8e4a-4b55b3d40769'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb61d659-3ddb-5bc2-8e4a-4b55b3d40769'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What organ do cardiologists specialize in?', '9aead17a-180e-5889-b0da-e110b8e94183'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Heart / hearts', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb6303e9-b112-5eb7-a9ba-9386905e88c6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb6303e9-b112-5eb7-a9ba-9386905e88c6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Proust''s Novel', E'In his great novel Remembrance of Things Past or In Search of Lost Time, Marcel Proust explored what are called "involuntary memories" - those that come to us quite suddenly without conscious effort, usually triggered by one of the senses. The fact that his book has two titles in English might suggest there is some doubt as to how our minds go about remembering things. In perhaps the most well-known such episode in the novel, the character Marcel is reminded of his childhood by the aroma produced when dunking a cake in a cup of tea. This is not far away from the belief that as we get older we can remember quite clearly incidents from years ago, but find it hard to remember what we did last week. Proust''s insight into memory is certainly true of one way the mind works. But why and how do we remember what we do?\nExperts believe that we store memories in three ways. First, there is the sensory stage which is to do with perception and lasts only a fraction of a second, taking in sight, sound, touch, and so on. These first perceptions and sensations are then stored in the short-term memory, which is the second stage. Finally, important information or information that has been reinforced by, for example, repetition, is then filtered into the long-term memory. Naturally, we tend to more easily absorb material on things we already know something about, as this has more meaning for us and can create a web of connections with related material that is already stored in the long-term memory.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'bf480130-f688-52dd-bd06-f96fefaa1605'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'What we experience is processed by the brain into memories in three stages. First, there is the sensory input, which is momentary. This is then stored in the short-term memory. If this experience is important or meaningful to us, we will reinforce the memory, possibly by repetition, and it will then be stored in the long-term memory.', NULL, NULL),
  ('eb647239-7b1b-52f5-a142-c38a34a0fa24'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb647239-7b1b-52f5-a142-c38a34a0fa24'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '92fcdd2e-5e7f-55e1-a12b-1e997696a76e'::uuid, NULL, E'Getting involved in volunteering opportunities helps to develop your leadership skills.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eb6b9d77-7b26-5032-b88a-65e7992a0506'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb6b9d77-7b26-5032-b88a-65e7992a0506'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Alzheimer’s Disease', E'Researchers have published a study that addresses possible associations between chronic stress, mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer’s disease. The study shows how people aged between 18 and 65 with a previous diagnosis of chronic stress and depression were more likely than other people to be diagnosed with mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer’s disease.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eb6c8a33-416b-5369-b4c9-3049ec9a5310'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb6c8a33-416b-5369-b4c9-3049ec9a5310'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Omicron', E'With omicron spreading globally at a dizzying pace, scientists are scrambling to learn as much as they can about the latest worrisome variant of the coronavirus. First {{1}} in South Africa and Botswana at the end of November, omicron is already {{2}} to soon become the dominant variant — dethroning delta — in some regions, public health officials warn. In a few places, it already has. So answers, including how sick does omicron make people and how well do vaccines {{3}} it, can''t come fast enough. A rising tide of data on omicron is beginning to provide a glimpse at what''s ahead as we enter year three of the global pandemic, though many questions linger. And with many people preparing to gather with family and friends for holidays, experts are {{4}} for yet more case surges, compounded by already high infection rates in some countries linked to the still-prevalent delta variant. Omicron''s collision with the holidays and travel is "a perfect storm". At this point, even vaccinated people should be {{5}} precautions, such as wearing masks indoors and testing before family gatherings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.spotted, 2.poised, 3.hobble, 4.bracing, 5.taking', NULL, NULL),
