  ('eb9c20e1-b159-5e97-ae15-0844d099cd1e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eb9c20e1-b159-5e97-ae15-0844d099cd1e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Iceland', E'On average, Iceland {{1}} a major volcanic event once every 5 years. Since the Middle Ages, a third of all the lava that has {{2}} the earth''s surface has erupted in Iceland. However, according to a recent geological hypothesis, this estimate does not include {{3}} eruptions, which are much more extensive than those on the land surface.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.experiences, 2.covered, 3.submarine', NULL, NULL),
  ('eba3bab3-7629-5b4b-800f-92958f3e0e45'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eba3bab3-7629-5b4b-800f-92958f3e0e45'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Flies and Mosquitos', E'Scientists at Johns Hopkins Medicine meticulously counted brain cells in fruit flies and three species of mosquitos, revealing a number that would surprise many people outside the science world. The insects’ tiny brains, on average, have about 200,000 neurons and other cells, they say. By comparison, a human brain has 86 billion neurons, and a rodent brain contains about 12 billion. Even though these brains are simple (in contrast to mammalian brains), they can do a lot of processing, even more than a supercomputer. They enable the insects to navigate, find food and perform other complicated tasks at the same time.\n\nAccording to this passage, we can know that fruit flies __', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'can do more processing than a supercomputer.', NULL, NULL),
  ('eba59773-d23c-58cf-962c-eed125730f5e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eba59773-d23c-58cf-962c-eed125730f5e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'fa6b42ae-3b36-571b-a9ef-d74bdb7ef3c9'::uuid, NULL, E'The aesthetic implications of this study have not yet been fully explored.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eba71aaf-5ca7-5685-9b66-b7ed8762a8f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eba71aaf-5ca7-5685-9b66-b7ed8762a8f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Body Tolerance', E'Cells cannot remain alive outside certain limits of temperature. In much narrow limits mark the boundaries of effective functioning. Enzyme systems of mammals and birds are most efficient only within a narrow range around thirty seven degrees centigrade. A departure of a few degrees from this value seriously impairs their functioning. Even though cells can survive wider fluctuations, the integrated actions of bodily systems are impaired. Other animals have a wider tolerance for changes of bodily ...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'cbb8bab7-9cfa-5687-8ea6-c32312f3bc28'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'temperature', NULL, NULL),
  ('ebaff801-1932-5f64-802c-8bb354492e36'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ebaff801-1932-5f64-802c-8bb354492e36'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Tsunami', E'Talk in an earth science class. The professor is talking about tsunamis. The term tidal wave is often inaccurately used for a tsunami. Soon, armies have nothing to do with the action of tides. A more accurate term is seismic sea wave. There has to be a disturbance of the earth''s crust to produce a tsunami. Large earthquakes with epicenters under or near the ocean are the cause of most tsunamis. Volcanic eruptions and undersea landslides are also responsible. But unless accompanied by movements of the ocean floor, their effects are usually localized. Possibly this was true about the eruption of krakatau a in eighteen eighty three, as soon army was responsible for most of the deaths caused by crack at our yet this soon army did not sink any ships. It did wash away several coastal villages and kill more than thirty six thousand people. Tsunamis work in complex ways. Some pounce on coastal settlements, like large breakers. Others produce a gentle wave that floats buildings off their foundations. But then a violent backwash may sweep buildings and people out to sea. The tsunami that wrecked hilo, hawaii, in nineteen forty six was so forceful, it folded parking meters. It caused needless deaths. When people return to save their belongings and got caught between waves, the deeper the water, the lower the tsunami, and the faster it moves. In the open ocean. It travels at about seven hundred kilometers per hour, but being sometimes know more than a metre in height, as soon, army often passes a ship unnoticed. This is what happened in eighteen ninety six during a catastrophic tsunami in japan, which was the result of an undersea earthquake. Thousands of people were drowned on shore, while fisherman far out at sea didn''t notice the waves passing beneath their boats. But when they went home, they found their villages destroyed.\n\nWhy is the term "tidal wave" inaccurate for a tsunami?', 'c8235d98-8550-5857-a52c-c666f6ff5b1f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Tsunamis are not related to tides.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ebb67ef4-4809-57fd-9e8f-f9594b167634'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ebb67ef4-4809-57fd-9e8f-f9594b167634'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is the process you do when you are not satisfied with a verdict of your lawsuit?', 'd1d37be7-3cae-52cf-9fbe-cf1348522012'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Appeal', NULL, NULL),
  ('ebb77e97-ee65-5423-95f6-f1295799353c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ebb77e97-ee65-5423-95f6-f1295799353c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the objects put in the room , such as chairs, tables, beds, and so on?', 'a61e88d3-7b49-56bf-b89b-16556d4fac39'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Furniture', NULL, NULL),
