  ('ec96103c-6827-5404-b365-8e379f0632ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ec96103c-6827-5404-b365-8e379f0632ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4da32bdc-d075-5e25-ae15-65195381cda8'::uuid, NULL, E'There is little evidence available to contradict his viewpoints.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('eca3354b-df28-5f63-8904-761dd5d8382d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eca3354b-df28-5f63-8904-761dd5d8382d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the study of the Earth''s physical features and the atmosphere?', 'a9b6ceb5-80ec-5e35-8efd-28d2109f7d41'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Geography', NULL, NULL),
  ('eca5203e-df02-5466-aae6-a1ee7a0f3f3c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eca5203e-df02-5466-aae6-a1ee7a0f3f3c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Migration Patterns of Birds', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 4, 2, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('eca72f56-bafb-539d-851e-568c49a1d4d4'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eca72f56-bafb-539d-851e-568c49a1d4d4'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Deep-sea Mineral Resources', E'The National Oceanography Center (NOC) is engaged in research into the potential risks and benefits of exploiting deep-sea mineral resources, some of which are essential for low-carbon technology, as well as using ocean robots to estimate the environmental impact of these potential deep-sea mining activities.\nLate last year the NOC led an expedition on the RRS James Cook that found enough of the scarce element Tellurium present in the crust of a submerged volcano that, if it were all to be used in the production of solar PV panels, could provide two-thirds of the UK''s annual electricity supply. Recently, the NOC also led an international study demonstrating deep-sea nodule mining will cause long-lasting damage to deep-sea life, lasting at least for decades.\nThese nodules are potato-sized rocks containing high levels of metals, including copper, manganese and nickel. They grow very slowly on the sea-bed, over millions of years. Although no commercial operations exist to extract these resources, many are planned.\nProfessor Edward Hill, Executive Director at the NOC commented, "By 2050 there will be nine billion people on earth and attention is increasingly turning to the ocean, particularly the deep ocean, for food, clean supplies of energy and strategic minerals. The NOC is undertaking research related to many aspects and perspectives involved in exploiting ocean resources. This research is aimed at informing with sound scientific evidence the decisions that will need to be taken in the future, as people increasingly turn to the oceans to address some of society''s greatest challenges."', NULL, NULL, E'The NOC is engaged in research into the potential risks and benefits of exploiting deep-sea mineral resources, which also led an international study demonstrating that deep-sea nodule mining will cause long-lasting damage to deep-sea life, and the NOC is undertaking research related to many aspects and perspectives involved in exploiting ocean resources, which is aimed at informing with sound scientific evidence the decisions that will need to be taken in the future.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('eca8f2ba-63e2-55fb-ae79-b0e736a55536'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eca8f2ba-63e2-55fb-ae79-b0e736a55536'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Indigenous Genetics', E'A new study has revealed that Indigenous Australians are the most genetically diverse people in the world, with greater genetic {{1}} than between people of European or Asian ancestry. The study, which involved analyzing the genomes of 83 Indigenous Australians from {{2}} the continent, also pushed back the {{3}} of genetic separation between people in Papua New Guinea and those in Australia to about 37,000 years ago. The researchers, led by Professor David Reich from Harvard Medical School, said that the findings shed light on the ancient history and diversity of Indigenous Australian peoples, who were {{4}} up of at least 200 distinct nations before colonization. They also said that the study could help improve the health and well-being of Indigenous Australians, who suffer from higher rates of chronic diseases and lower life {{5}} than non-Indigenous Australians.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.variability, 2.across, 3.date, 4.made, 5.expectancy', NULL, NULL),
  ('eca9f771-2faa-5413-9ba5-341ffe1464f8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'eca9f771-2faa-5413-9ba5-341ffe1464f8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'International Environmental Law', NULL, 'db68a36f-0202-5a2f-a278-b032fd4a4113'::uuid, NULL, E'Before we consider international environmental law and climate change we need to consider domestic legislation, as it is within the sovereign states that international law is put into practice. This reflects the environmentalists'' maxim, ''think globally act locally''. United Kingdom legislative control over the impacts of mans'' activity on the environment is not new. As long ago as the reign of Charles II the main concern was the production of smoke from the burning of ''sea coal. Almost all areas of trade and industry were subject to very detailed legislative controls at that time, although some were governed by ''self-regulation'' in the form of guilds, who regulated both supply and methods of production. However, the measures implemented were mostly ineffective because then, as now, the specifying of legal duties and standards without providing any appropriate enforcement merely indicated good intentions but were of little practical effect.\nThe next stage was prompted by the Industrial Revolution with the urbanization of society and its profound effects on the environment. Local industrialists used the Adam Smith model to maximize their economic benefit, but this was to the detriment of the local environment with the operation of ''Gresham''s Law'' that is, the bad drives out the good.\nThose industrialists who were concerned for either the health of their employees or the local environment faced higher costs than their competitors. The result was the need for increasingly comprehensive statutory controls on the discharge of pollutants into various receiving media.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ecb77def-3b7d-5afb-91e1-cbee3dfba226'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecb77def-3b7d-5afb-91e1-cbee3dfba226'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '81bd74cc-c7df-57d1-b5f6-9cb1c2e7795a'::uuid, NULL, E'Building connections between individuals holds great importance for social well-being.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ecb7fdc6-bfed-5a7b-a938-649b966d565b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecb7fdc6-bfed-5a7b-a938-649b966d565b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a vehicle equipped for carrying the injured or sick?', 'd89f7c8d-8b5b-55eb-8cbc-74b25cdb8e30'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ambulance', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecb86e63-e44f-5b3c-bfdf-1bc927d9df88'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecb86e63-e44f-5b3c-bfdf-1bc927d9df88'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Back to Countryside', E'Half a lifetime ago I made a lifestyle choice to exchange a city terrace for a farm cottage. I knew it was a good idea because I had been there before. Born and reared on a farm I had been seduced for a few years by the idea of being a big shot that lived and worked in a city rather than only going for the day to wave at the buses. True, I was familiar with some of the minor disadvantages of country living such as an iffy private water supply sometimes infiltrated by a range of flora and fauna (including, on one memorable occasion, a dead lamb), the absence of central heating in farm houses and cottages, and a single track farm road easily blocked by snow, broken down machinery or escaped livestock. But there were many advantages as I told my wife back in the mid Seventies. Town born and bred, eight months pregnant and exchanging a warm, substantial Corstorphine terrace for a windswept farm cottage on a much lower income, persuading her that country had it over town might have been difficult.', NULL, NULL, E'Half a lifetime ago I made a lifestyle choice to exchange a city terrace for a farm cottage, and I knew it was a good idea because I had been there before, although I was familiar with some of the minor disadvantages of country living; there were many advantages as I told my wife back in the mid Seventies, but persuading her that country had it over town might have been difficult.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('ecbcb405-64ad-515d-bc26-285bb3deb8a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecbcb405-64ad-515d-bc26-285bb3deb8a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What are the units like grams and kilograms used to measure?', 'ae242926-0e75-5992-8d12-77097564c6b1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Weight / mass', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecccf47f-a8f8-5246-98ea-6384729dcd1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecccf47f-a8f8-5246-98ea-6384729dcd1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High Noise', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1, 2, 4, 3', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecd1704a-f766-55b0-90eb-df6679c706b2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecd1704a-f766-55b0-90eb-df6679c706b2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'dbd9e291-cb1c-5e4c-9af4-abb2ba8bcd44'::uuid, NULL, E'Tuesday sessions will last for approximately two hours.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ecd861d8-dc8f-5087-956b-bb060ab5742e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecd861d8-dc8f-5087-956b-bb060ab5742e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '67aeae11-ff4f-53f5-ae1a-9b00071804e1'::uuid, NULL, E'I spoke to him in English, but I couldn’t make myself understood.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ecda23db-0cb3-572b-beed-9bbbe10bdfbc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecda23db-0cb3-572b-beed-9bbbe10bdfbc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'e3bb3023-7032-5e39-8784-0210ab1315f5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This is the first example of a modern and professional army.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecdd0c0d-afa0-54ce-b0d7-898511f0592e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecdd0c0d-afa0-54ce-b0d7-898511f0592e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Electric Eels', E'Electric eels are born to shock. Thanks to cells called electrocytes which, stacked like batteries, make up 80% of their bodies, these cunning South American {{1}} can deliver debilitating blows of up to 600 volts to their prey. But they’ve harnessed their electricity to pack even bigger punches. Last year, Vanderbilt University biologist Kenneth Catania revealed electric eels bring their positively charged head and negatively charged {{2}} closer together to generate a more powerful {{3}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.hunters, 2.tail, 3.current', NULL, NULL),
  ('ece0136e-95db-53b1-a4f2-d0290c3ddca1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece0136e-95db-53b1-a4f2-d0290c3ddca1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8bc1083f-5359-54e4-9a27-2a3c7cceacdf'::uuid, NULL, E'There is a position available for a junior lecturer in media studies.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ece1d1b9-4811-55de-ba35-0b0b4484ec91'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece1d1b9-4811-55de-ba35-0b0b4484ec91'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Television', E'Television has transformed politics in the United States by changing the way in which information is disseminated, by altering political campaigns, and by changing citizen''s patterns of response to politics. Television has altered the forms of political communication as well. The messages are briefer than they once were. A political speech given by traveling politicians and lasting 1 to 2 hours has given way to the 30-second advertisement and the 10-second sound bite in broadcast news. The audience for speeches is not that standing in front of the politician but rather the viewing audience who will hear and see a snippet of the speech on the news.\n\nWhat is the main idea of this passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The change of politics given by televisions.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ece346a7-89fd-5bd0-a50f-c320315bff8e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece346a7-89fd-5bd0-a50f-c320315bff8e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Friendship', E'My best piece of advice would be to join like-minded groups. So, for example, if you''re into dance, join a dance group. And you can find a lot of these on, you know, something like Meetup or some sort of app. But you want to find groups that are similar to you. And then you can build a friendship from there because typically, if you''re interested in something, those might be those type of people that you want to build a friendship with. One of my favorite quotes from Maya Angelou I think can apply to friendships. “When someone shows you who they are, believe them the first time.” So when you''re building friendships with people, they''re going to show you initially who they are. So trust that. And I''m a big proponent of trusting your instincts and investing in friendships that make you feel comfortable from the outset.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '24dc8c35-b1e8-5413-a904-10e69e574ebc'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'To build a friendship, an effective way is to join like-minded groups, who share the same interest. Also, you should trust your instincts and make friends with people who make you feel comfortable from the beginning..', NULL, NULL),
  ('ece36a5f-f347-530d-9395-3da76f5b5017'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece36a5f-f347-530d-9395-3da76f5b5017'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cuteness', E'Cuteness in offspring is a {{1}} protective mechanism that {{2}} survival for otherwise completely {{3}} infants. Previous research has linked cuteness to early ethological ideas of a "kindchenschema" (infant schema) where infant facial features serve as "innate releasing mechanisms" for {{4}} caregiving behaviors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.potent, 2.ensures, 3.dependent, 4.instinctive', NULL, NULL),
  ('ece51d15-7e0d-5cab-a766-aeede1f98823'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece51d15-7e0d-5cab-a766-aeede1f98823'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wind', E'Your classmate is on vacation and your are at her home. The strong wind damaged the furniture on the balcony, so you want to inform your classmates so that she could be mentally prepared. What do you say to her?', 'cd5d048d-d1e6-520d-a364-fcc2d23efa75'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey Lily, I want to talk to you about something.\nWe seem to have a little issue with the balcony furniture at your house.\nIt''s like the strong wind damaged the furniture on your balcony. I''m calling to tell you so you can be mentally prepared.\nAnd I''d like to know what you think.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ece79086-8166-5fb6-8074-06fdbb1367b0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece79086-8166-5fb6-8074-06fdbb1367b0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do bees collect and use to create honey?', '7a4f7a5d-022a-593b-82c5-8064d6f5ccc9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Nectar', NULL, NULL),
  ('ece9d552-d70d-578c-8d08-6f7eaea4d38f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ece9d552-d70d-578c-8d08-6f7eaea4d38f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Prisoners', E'The primary goal for this year-long campaign, founded by the English lawyer Peter Benenson and a small group of writers, academics and lawyers including Quaker peace activist Eric Baker, was to identify individual prisoners of conscience around the world and then campaign for their release. In early 1962, the campaign had received enough public support to become a permanent organization and was {{1}} Amnesty International. Under British law, Amnesty International was classed as a political organization and therefore excluded from tax-free charity status. To work around this, the "Fund for the Persecuted" was established in 1962 to receive donations to support prisoners and their families. The name was later changed to the "Prisoners of Conscience Appeal Fund" and is now a separate and independent charity which provides relief and {{2}} grants to prisoners of conscience in the UK and around the world. Amnesty International has, since its founding, pressured governments to release those persons it considers to be prisoners of conscience. Governments, conversely, tend to deny that the specific prisoners identified by Amnesty International are, in fact, being held on the grounds Amnesty claims; they allege that these prisoners pose {{3}} threats to the security of their countries. The concept of "Prisoners of conscience" became a controversy around Nelson Mandela''s {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.renamed, 2.rehabilitation, 3.genuine, 4.imprisonment', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecebc25c-ba50-5eb4-aa2e-8a587e8dff5c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecebc25c-ba50-5eb4-aa2e-8a587e8dff5c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wheat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 1, 3, 4', NULL, NULL),
  ('ecf10fce-77f6-556e-b91b-2cfda1bb2252'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecf10fce-77f6-556e-b91b-2cfda1bb2252'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Quantum Behavior', E'Particles can act like clumps of matter or ripple through space like waves, and they can even exist in two places at once. A new device harnesses this strange quantum behavior to measure Earth’s gravity. Slight changes in gravity from place to place reveal changes in the density of material beneath the sensor. This allows the instrument to detect underground objects.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ecfa417a-7581-53f3-9941-beb2ad6415db'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ecfa417a-7581-53f3-9941-beb2ad6415db'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '3270434e-d7cc-5995-b816-551aac983e8a'::uuid, NULL, E'We have gathered together the answers to some of our most frequently asked questions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ed047688-5d0f-57e5-89fa-e1ab213cb75b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed047688-5d0f-57e5-89fa-e1ab213cb75b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do you call a part of a line that has a fixed starting point but no end point?', '5d4b7243-5cbf-5202-802a-505145b08d47'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Ray', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed0a7319-2c72-5438-addf-ee3364f6f4c5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed0a7319-2c72-5438-addf-ee3364f6f4c5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Niche Technologies', NULL, 'd3af2b38-c56b-56c5-98df-c898f371d2aa'::uuid, NULL, E'And so there’s two things there: One is, smaller projects that have bigger impact and societal impact kind of get ignored. Also, niche technologies that we can build on for future things will not thrive, will go away. A lot of the things that we''re reaping the benefit of today was because of the basic scientific research that we funded in the 60s and the 70s and the 80s. So if they stop doing that kind of funding by the government, after a while we just won’t have anything to build on top of. We’ll just be advertising to each other, and connecting with each other on social media. And that’s it. And that’s not where we want to end up. So there is a role for government, in terms of promoting scientific research, for both the sake of scientific research and also for commercializing the scientific research. The government is the only entity that can take a slightly longer point of view, in terms of these developments. But I think it’s good for that to happen. Because sometimes good ideas need a little bit of funding, before they can become bigger ideas.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ed0b8eb7-4a3c-5d8e-8f65-8467333c6eef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed0b8eb7-4a3c-5d8e-8f65-8467333c6eef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '12b80568-ab6f-5dd0-9f37-7a530ff6503f'::uuid, NULL, E'I found the author''s stance on immigration to be ambiguous and unclear.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ed0e98f8-793a-5aef-a007-ee33b09cf686'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed0e98f8-793a-5aef-a007-ee33b09cf686'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '56114a04-c61f-518d-bc9c-55ec557a4a9e'::uuid, NULL, E'American children did less well in math than their peers in Japan.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ed0fdc64-3763-5a0a-831c-a40d3743f499'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed0fdc64-3763-5a0a-831c-a40d3743f499'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the government run by a dictator, autocracy or democracy?', 'bf97ec0e-7685-5b6c-898b-32bd7bf5b426'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Autocracy', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed1aa0ed-1746-5cb5-ac00-7067bd79e2bd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed1aa0ed-1746-5cb5-ac00-7067bd79e2bd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Negative Punishment', E'Negative punishment involves removing something that is desired in order to decrease the likelihood that a behavior will {{1}} again in the future. Putting a child in time out can {{2}} as a negative punishment if the child enjoys social interaction. Taking away something that is desired encourages the child to {{3}} from engaging in that behavior again in order to not lose the desired object or activity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.occur, 2.serve, 3.refrain', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed1ae67e-f84e-5280-8b51-579fac90f521'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed1ae67e-f84e-5280-8b51-579fac90f521'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Crime Prevention', E'The landscape of crime prevention is constantly adapting, reflecting a nuanced understanding of the social factors contributing to criminal behavior. Modern approaches emphasize the importance of social and community interventions, acknowledging that factors such as low education levels and family discord can significantly increase the {{1}} of criminal activity. Programs like the Perry School Project in the USA and the Troubled Families Initiative in the UK have shown {{2}} in addressing these root causes. By focusing on early intervention and community engagement, these programs aim to not only curb immediate criminal activity but also to foster long-term societal change, transforming potential offenders into contributing members of society. {{3}} , critics argue that while these programs address certain social factors, they may {{4}} deeper systemic issues like inequality inherent in the capitalist system, pointing to a need for a more holistic approach to crime prevention.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.likelihood, 2.promise, 3.However, 4.overlook', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed1f3ad6-f214-5db6-a5fe-828711d787f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed1f3ad6-f214-5db6-a5fe-828711d787f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'd90a3ba4-d2de-5bc3-a0ae-70fbe99eb09e'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Our course topics range widely from social science to engineering.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed211913-0543-575e-a85f-1a56375c3898'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed211913-0543-575e-a85f-1a56375c3898'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '2960d369-ed4a-5452-a581-d0cdf926d5e1'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There has been a sharp slowdown in economic growth.', NULL, NULL),
  ('ed219ffe-52c0-5be6-89e0-16d07298326b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed219ffe-52c0-5be6-89e0-16d07298326b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Overqualified Worker', NULL, 'fbdb7d50-223e-5d26-9def-b99fd4729d24'::uuid, NULL, E'If your recruiting efforts attract job applicants with too much experience—a near certainty in this weak labor market—you should consider a response that runs counter to most hiring managers'' MO: Don''t reject those applicants out of hand. Instead, take a closer look. New research shows that overqualified workers tend to perform better than other employees, and they don''t quit any sooner. Furthermore, a simple managerial tactic—empowerment—can mitigate any dissatisfaction they may feel.The prejudice against too-good employees is pervasive. Companies tend to prefer an applicant who is a ''perfect fit'' over someone who brings more intelligence, education, or experience than needed. On the surface, this bias makes sense: Studies have consistently shown that employees who consider themselves overqualified exhibit higher levels of discontent. For example, overqualification correlated well with job dissatisfaction in a 2008 study of 156 call-center reps by Israeli researchers Saul Fine and Baruch Nevo. And unlike discrimination based on age or gender, declining to hire overqualified workers is perfectly legal.But even before the economic downturn, a surplus of overqualified candidates was a global problem, particularly in developing economies, where rising education levels are giving workers more skills than are needed to supply the growing service sectors. If managers can get beyond the conventional wisdom, the growing pool of too-good applicants is a great opportunity. Berrin Erdogan and Talya N. Bauer of Portland State University in Oregon found that overqualified workers'' feelings of dissatisfaction can be dissipated by giving them autonomy in decision making. At stores where employees didn''t feel empowered, ''overeducated'' workers expressed greater dissatisfaction than their colleagues did and were more likely to state an intention to quit. But that difference vanished where self-reported autonomy was high.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('ed23048e-2b0c-51cf-a63f-9ea2daefeceb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'ed23048e-2b0c-51cf-a63f-9ea2daefeceb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Costly Panda', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 1, 4', NULL, NULL),
