  ('f050102b-f196-5723-8619-a306d9a96efd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f050102b-f196-5723-8619-a306d9a96efd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Hearing in Babies', E'The development of hearing in babies is a complex and fascinating process. From the moment they are born, infants possess the ability to hear and distinguish various sounds in their environment. The auditory system undergoes rapid development during the first years of life, with critical periods for the acquisition of language and speech perception.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f0513980-8d4d-532b-a009-35e4be53ae44'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f0513980-8d4d-532b-a009-35e4be53ae44'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pet Diets', E'Numerous studies over the last 15 years have shown dogs and cats can {{1}} healthy lives on nutritionally sound plant-based diets provided they are made to {{2}} essential nutrients normally found in meat. Researchers have now begun to {{3}} the environmental impact of pet diets and how that could change if they went vegan.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.lead, 2.contain, 3.quantify', NULL, NULL),
  ('f054580e-01f8-551b-aee1-ad900fc91f1b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f054580e-01f8-551b-aee1-ad900fc91f1b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '5c84df33-e2a7-5939-a62f-f957d8a15453'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Those who are considering a career in marketing should attend the talk.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f05f0509-9b65-53f0-8b65-f5252829eb1c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f05f0509-9b65-53f0-8b65-f5252829eb1c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Blue', E'While blue is one of the most popular colors, it is one of the least appetizing. Food researchers say that when humans searched for food, they learned to avoid toxic or spoiled objects, which were often blue, black, or purple. When food dyed blue is served to study subjects, they lose appetite.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f0622b93-b2a1-5bea-acc2-bd921c4c0b94'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f0622b93-b2a1-5bea-acc2-bd921c4c0b94'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '1bba197c-a770-5b16-adcf-106a965453b5'::uuid, NULL, E'The university welcomes applications from overseas students.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f06c1729-c8de-5488-abdf-040e053d8073'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f06c1729-c8de-5488-abdf-040e053d8073'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'cdaa5589-9dea-5e0b-b345-66708ec83457'::uuid, NULL, E'He has found a job in a local newspaper agency.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f06eab75-f2d3-5cd1-8767-196e220800eb'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f06eab75-f2d3-5cd1-8767-196e220800eb'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7990a59f-6621-5712-8646-1d65f06c4b20'::uuid, NULL, E'Our university has organized a visit to the tallest building in the world.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f07398f0-2361-5e07-9d79-3919045c730f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f07398f0-2361-5e07-9d79-3919045c730f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Basic Diet', E'The basic English person''s diet in medieval times was made up of bread, cheese and beef, while ale was the drink for all ages\nand social classes except for the aristocracy, who drank wine. In winter there were no root crops to feed the animals, so they were killed in autumn and the meat salted to preserve it. People kept livestock even in the towns: cows were usually kept tied or tethered, but pigs were allowed to wander at will, feeding on the rubbish off the streets.\nBy the 16th century, however, choice in foodstuffs had grown, including exotic spices to add flavor to the usual diet. This had come about because European rulers wanting to increase their power and wealth and also, in fairness, in the spirit\nof enquiry and the quest for knowledge, had financed voyages of exploration overseas.\nThis opened up trade routes, bringing precious spices - and vast profits - from the East, and to the west Spanish and Portuguese explorers had brought back such novelties as potatoes, tomatoes, maize, peppers and chocolate. It must be said, though, that it took people some time to accept some of these new foods, as they feared they were poisonous.\n\nWhich of the following statements is true, according to the text?', 'e342eda1-4538-5119-9361-052f18a355dd'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'In the 16th century people had a wider choice of food.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f077a35f-e9fb-5e21-83bb-bb55e80b6fed'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f077a35f-e9fb-5e21-83bb-bb55e80b6fed'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What is a polygon of eight angles and eight sides called?', 'abc05396-7447-569d-b83d-be072fe6fa05'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Octagon', NULL, NULL),
  ('f0797736-3e73-59a7-b14f-3a8962556e77'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f0797736-3e73-59a7-b14f-3a8962556e77'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'The City of London', E'Who would have thought back in 1698, as they downed their espressos, that the little band of stockbrokers from Jonathan''s Coffee House in Change Alley EC3 would be the founder members of what would become the world''s mighty money capital?\nProgress was not entirely smooth. The South Sea Bubble burst in 1720 and the coffee house exchanges burned down in 1748. As late as Big Bang in 1986, when bowler hats were finally hung up, you wouldn''t have bet the farm on London surpassing New York, Frankfurt and Tokyo as Mammon''s international nexus.\nYet the 325,000 souls who operate in the UK capital''s financial hub have now overtaken their New York rivals in size of the funds managed (including offshore business); they hold 70% of the global secondary bond market and the City dominates foreign exchange trading. And its institutions paid out £9 billion in bonuses in December. The Square Mile has now spread both eastwards from EC3 to Canary Wharf and westwards into Mayfair, where many of the private equity ''locusts'' and their hedge fund pals now hang out.\nFor foreigners in finance, London is the place to be. It has no Sarbanes Oxley and no euro to hold it back, yet the fact that it still flies so high is against the odds. London is one of the most expensive cities in the world to live in and its transport systems groan and there''s an ever present threat of terrorist attack. But, for the time being, the deals just keep on getting bigger.', NULL, NULL, E'The little band of stockbrokers would be the founder members of what would become the world''s mighty money capital, but the progress was not entirely smooth, and they hold 70% of the global secondary bond market, so for foreigners in finance, London is now the place to be, which is one of the most expensive cities in the world to live in and its transport systems groan.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('f07a2e71-16be-5ddb-aba3-63f8e868fd67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f07a2e71-16be-5ddb-aba3-63f8e868fd67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the technology that allows data transfer over short distances between devices?', '0574e794-8c06-5ac3-ae05-1967c2df09fa'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Bluetooth', NULL, NULL),
  ('f08530c9-29ed-5a7b-a9a3-5caec9f51c99'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f08530c9-29ed-5a7b-a9a3-5caec9f51c99'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Bird Migration', E'For birdwatchers in southern New Mexico, September can be highly entertaining. Good numbers of many diverse {{1}} are on the move during this time, {{2}} southward from northern breeding grounds to places they will spend the winter, and there''s always a {{3}} that some rare or unusual birds will turn {{4}} .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.species, 2.traveling, 3.chance, 4.up', NULL, NULL),
  ('f08aafcd-5818-509a-be31-84fabdbaa568'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f08aafcd-5818-509a-be31-84fabdbaa568'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '99c87720-f75e-5745-b5bf-b5f23b24bda4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'These words recognize the excellence of the undergraduates'' research projects.', NULL, NULL),
