  ('f2daf716-e3d0-5c4e-ab4d-ee7fdd18d4b8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2daf716-e3d0-5c4e-ab4d-ee7fdd18d4b8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Not Enjoying', E'People should sometimes do things that they do not enjoy doing. Do you agree with that?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('f2dc37a2-d80b-54d2-8fa1-3290ef9c0009'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2dc37a2-d80b-54d2-8fa1-3290ef9c0009'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Playing an Instrument', E'Playing a rhythm-based game for eight weeks helps non-musicians become better at remembering recently seen faces. This suggests that learning to play an instrument could {{1}} short-term memory for non-musical tasks. There have been several studies showing that musicians tend to have better short-term memory than non-musicians when it comes to music-related tasks, such as remembering musical {{2}} . It is less clear whether these benefits carry over to non-musical tasks or to non-musicians who are learning to play an instrument, and how these changes might actually be seen in the brain. Theodore Zanto at the University of California, San Francisco, and his colleagues, randomly {{3}} a group of 47 non-musicians, aged between 60 and 79, to play either a tablet-based musical rhythm training game, which {{4}} learning to hit a drum in time with a teacher, or a word search game for eight weeks. At the start and end of the eight weeks, participants took a short-term memory test to measure their ability to remember a face they saw seconds before. Only the group who played the rhythm training game showed an improvement on their initial scores – of around 4 per cent.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.improve, 2.sequences, 3.assigned, 4.emulates', NULL, NULL),
  ('f2dcac1d-cf84-5a7d-b9b8-eeb68ddc6a0d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2dcac1d-cf84-5a7d-b9b8-eeb68ddc6a0d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'Where do you pay for your purchases at a supermarket?', 'e24f9a5e-448c-5d72-a13f-e15c32d0a574'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Cashier / till / checkout / counter / cash desk', NULL, NULL),
  ('f2e12085-e122-51c5-92fc-9455cab46201'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2e12085-e122-51c5-92fc-9455cab46201'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who studies the stars, planets, and other celestial objects?', 'b2f56218-568b-510f-af6b-50b838531b23'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Astronomer', NULL, NULL),
  ('f2e6179f-7aa5-5902-a050-d0519f498eb7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2e6179f-7aa5-5902-a050-d0519f498eb7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Wage Gap', E'Until the early 1960s, newspapers published separate job listing for men and women. It wasn''t until the passage of the Equal Pay Act on June 10, 1963 that it became illegal to pay women lower rates for the same job strictly on the basis of their sex.\nThe wage gap is a statistical indicator often used as an index of the status of women''s earnings relative to men''s. It is expressed as a percentage (e.g., in 2005, women earned 81% as much as men) and is calculated by dividing the median annual earnings for women by median annual earnings for men. Since 1963, when the Equal Pay Act was signed, the closing of the wage gap between men and women has been at a rate of about half a penny a year.', NULL, NULL, E'Until the early 1960s, newspapers published separate job listing for men and women, and the wage gap, whose closing has been at a rate of about half a penny a year since 1963, when the Equal Pay Act was signed, is a statistical indicator often used as an index of the status of women’s earnings relative to men''s.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('f2e70af2-0f7c-5437-9547-42d976adb6f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2e70af2-0f7c-5437-9547-42d976adb6f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'a36aa7d9-7d4e-5372-abd5-eab71f61a2bc'::uuid, NULL, E'The plan raised a lot of money and improved the economy of the country.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f2e8969e-7e91-5850-8d72-c35004b6cd86'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f2e8969e-7e91-5850-8d72-c35004b6cd86'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Workplace Stress', E'Work and personal lives underwent enormous disruption during the pandemic, with people working from home experiencing increased loneliness and a range of mental health issues. Under normal circumstances, the younger generations of workers need additional support from their managers and that was exacerbated during the pandemic, when we saw that relative newcomers to the workforce did not cope as well under the pressures of remote working.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
