  ('f3de6a95-8c8b-5322-9683-40405f759a4b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3de6a95-8c8b-5322-9683-40405f759a4b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Happiest Times', E'University is one of the happiest times of our life. If you go to university, that is I totally loved my university days. I also loved my university. I had three great years of being a student. It was the first time I lived alone without my parents. I had to cook, wash and clean for myself. I loved it. I had complete freedom. I also loved the studying. It was much more interesting than studying at school. It was nice to just wander along to a lecture, do the reading, and then do the assignments. I really felt like I was learning something. I also loved the social life at university. It''s almost twenty four seven. There always parties and things to do. You have to get the right balance between.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', 'c82c3c42-a549-5839-8263-011a1ee810e9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'studying and partying', NULL, NULL),
  ('f3df18c0-414b-5655-9d86-b12e1fbc439e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3df18c0-414b-5655-9d86-b12e1fbc439e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '7482ee47-d7d0-5ff3-98a1-84b6478e9ef9'::uuid, NULL, E'There''s an hourly bus service from the campus into town.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f3e265e8-6e27-5d8c-bcb4-28b01fe26251'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3e265e8-6e27-5d8c-bcb4-28b01fe26251'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Environmental Factors', E'Weather, climate change, air quality, and natural disasters are all environmental factors. Some industries are {{1}} at risk from changes in the natural environment, including manufacturing, agriculture, tourism and travel, and sports and entertainment. Many pollution regulations limiting water and air pollution have been passed that affect the {{2}} of businesses. Today, the impact of climate control is being debated in Congress, and organizations in many industries are {{3}} how this latest environmental threat will affect their operations. Recently, Shell Oil spent more than $7 billion exploring parts of the Arctic Circle for oil – a {{4}} that was not possible before global warming increased drilling access in the area. They have since cancelled this initiative due to a lack of results, as well as strong international {{5}} that it may cause further damage to an environmentally sensitive location.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.especially, 2.operation, 3.concerned, 4.venture, 5.protests', NULL, NULL),
  ('f3e319b6-0f27-5176-82f7-359363510589'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3e319b6-0f27-5176-82f7-359363510589'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Sleep Issue', E'Sleep {{1}} is a global issue in all the major cities around the world where the amount of sleep is {{2}} over decades. Now, the decrease is growing with the {{3}} of the COVID-19 pandemic. Stress plays a major role in how we sleep. People are {{4}} to have some kind of routines, and many people lost them during the pandemic and especially during lockdowns. People woke up and went to sleep at {{5}} times, they ate at odd times, and all of that definitely affected their biological rhythms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.deprivation, 2.decreasing, 3.onslaught, 4.meant, 5.odd', NULL, NULL),
  ('f3e66624-9350-5a91-9bf9-0d1b02ef063b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3e66624-9350-5a91-9bf9-0d1b02ef063b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'How Smell Works', NULL, '387a5f0b-6153-5129-aa65-63a385a0d050'::uuid, NULL, E'First, let’s talk about how smell works. From coffee to stinky trash, the substances around us give off volatiles, which you can think of as tiny smell molecules. We breathe in these smell molecules, which then stimulate the olfactory sensory neurons that sit high in the nose. Each of these neurons contains an odor receptor on its surface. Once the odor receptors are triggered by these smell molecules, the neurons send information about them to the brain. Here’s what I think is so cool. The brain not only categorizes that information as a particular odor, it may also begin to associate feelings like pleasure or disgust and other moods and emotions with that odor for future reference. For example, you sniff bacon. You eat it. Your taste buds get salt, and then your body gets a whack of fat, which is an energy source. So the brain loves it and attaches a positive label to it. The next time you smell bacon, a sensation associated with pleasure arises.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f3e93f8b-cf1e-5ec6-a2d5-24c2c226f7f7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f3e93f8b-cf1e-5ec6-a2d5-24c2c226f7f7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a female heir, especially one who has received or will receive a large amount of money?', 'b739e437-e0d9-53eb-80ec-ff385c2ec0f9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Heiress / inheritress / inheritrix', NULL, NULL),
