  ('f701b6f1-cf4f-5176-80be-bee8bab495d0'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f701b6f1-cf4f-5176-80be-bee8bab495d0'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Pollutants', E'Air pollution is contamination of the indoor or outdoor environment by any chemical, physical or biological agent that modifies the natural {{1}} of the atmosphere. Outdoor and indoor air pollution cause respiratory and other diseases and are important sources of {{2}} and mortality. Policies to reduce air pollution, therefore, lower the burden of disease {{3}} to air pollution, as well as contributing to the long-term mitigation of climate change.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.characteristics, 2.morbidity, 3.attributable', NULL, NULL),
  ('f7096bc7-323e-578c-9bb8-ea600db4c7b1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f7096bc7-323e-578c-9bb8-ea600db4c7b1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'High Quality of Life', E'In spite of the spectacularly high quality of life for the vast majority of the people who live in the European Union, its inhabitants seem obsessed by the region''s relative decline in the world. Slow economic growth rates and high unemployment have reinforced the impression that Europe is unhappy with today and unsure of tomorrow.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f70d34cb-986d-5418-af66-e66c6d8532f5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f70d34cb-986d-5418-af66-e66c6d8532f5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '659e32fb-b058-57d9-aa97-c219062be797'::uuid, NULL, E'Thank you for representing our department at this event; we appreciate it.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f70e1bfa-88fe-513c-9b9a-1c8bbd89cc33'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f70e1bfa-88fe-513c-9b9a-1c8bbd89cc33'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the things of 88 keys covered by colors white and black?', '0bea8997-950d-5ed9-87cd-b52e5c924e14'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Pianos / piano', NULL, NULL),
  ('f718a936-abf8-5fc7-9925-1c179c1337f9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f718a936-abf8-5fc7-9925-1c179c1337f9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Evolving Theater', E'A closely related theory sees theater as evolving out of dances that are primarily pantomimic, rhythmical or gymnastic, or from imitations of animal noises and sounds. Admiration for the performer''s skill, virtuosity, and grace are seen as motivation for elaborating the activities into fully realized theatrical performances. In addition to exploring the possible antecedents of theater, scholars have also theorized about the motives that led people to develop theater. Why did theater develop, and why was it valued after it ceased to fulfill the function of ritual? Most answers fall back on the theories about the human mind and basic human needs. One, set forth by Aristotle in the fourth century B.C., sees humans as naturally imitative—as taking pleasure in imitating persons, things, and actions and in seeing such imitations. Another, advanced in the twentieth century, suggests that humans have a gift for fantasy, through which they seek to reshape reality into more satisfying forms than those encountered in daily life. Thus, fantasy or fiction (of which drama is one form) permits people to objectify their anxieties and fears, confront them, and fulfill their hopes in fiction if not fact. The theater, then, is one tool whereby people define and understand their world or escape from unpleasant realities.But neither the human imitative instinct nor a penchant for fantasy by itself leads to an autonomous theater. Therefore, additional explanations are needed. One necessary condition seems to be a somewhat detached view of human problems. For example, one sign of this condition is the appearance of the comic vision, since comedy requires sufficient detachment to view some deviations from social norms as ridiculous rather than as serious threats to the welfare of the entire group. Another condition that contributes to the development of autonomous theater is the emergence of the aesthetic sense. For example, some early societies ceased to consider certain rites essential to their well-being and abandoned them, nevertheless, they retained as parts of their oral tradition the myths that had grown up around the rites and admired them for their artistic qualities rather than for their religious usefulness.\n\nWhich of the following best describes the organization of this passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The author presents two theories for a historical phenomenon.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f71ba4a3-86c1-502a-9d57-6c41eaddd597'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f71ba4a3-86c1-502a-9d57-6c41eaddd597'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Knitted Jerseys', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'3, 2, 5, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
