  ('f8b28af1-e4ca-50a2-9f72-af01dcf80950'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8b28af1-e4ca-50a2-9f72-af01dcf80950'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Barred Owls', E'Barred owls can be found in {{1}} forests right across North America. They feed on small mammals, fish, birds and small reptiles — pretty much anything that comes their way. The barred owl grows up to half a metre tall and has {{2}} as a very adaptable nocturnal predator. And, {{3}} they have been long-thought to live in old-growth forests, they are now building up quite an {{4}} population. In Charlotte, North Carolina, barred owls tend to nest in the cavities of the numerous willow oak trees that line the city''s streets. Far from being endangered, the owls have expanded their range; and now, in some places, conservationists are worried about the effects they might have on other {{5}} species .', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.dense, 2.emerged, 3.whereas, 4.urban, 5.native', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8b6104b-de59-5c7b-bec1-b8da14bf2b86'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8b6104b-de59-5c7b-bec1-b8da14bf2b86'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Greenery', E'On many summer days, photosynthesis by trees and gases in New York City absorbs all the greenhouse gas emissions {{1}} by cars, trucks, buses, and even more, according to a new study. The findings show the importance of greenery for cities as part of their efforts to {{2}} their emissions. This includes scattered trees and lawns along sidewalks and pavements, which {{3}} up to produce a strong carbon-absorbing effect.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.produced, 2.tackle, 3.add', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8b811ae-841e-54d3-a92a-558b7323963d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8b811ae-841e-54d3-a92a-558b7323963d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Minority Languages (Similar)', NULL, 'ebc46af0-f51e-58e4-9e35-2a2a5f5714ae'::uuid, NULL, E'Welsh is a Celtic language spoken in Wales by about 740,000 people, and in the Welsh colony in Patagonia, Argentina by several hundred people. There are also Welsh speakers in England, Scotland, Canada, the USA, Australia and New Zealand.At the beginning of the 20th century about half of the population of Wales spoke Welsh as an everyday language. Towards the end of the century, the proportion of Welsh speakers had fallen to about 20%. According to the 2001 census 582,368 people can speak Welsh, 659,301 people can either speak, read or write Welsh, and 797,717 people, 28% of the population, claimed to have some knowledge of the language.According to a survey carried out by S4C, the Welsh language TV channel, the number of Welsh speakers in Wales is around 750,000, and about 1.5 million people can ''understand'' Welsh. In addition there are an estimated 133,000 Welsh--speakers living in England, about 50,000 of them in the Greater London area.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f8baa8e8-24df-5ea6-b78e-d633affefa9b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8baa8e8-24df-5ea6-b78e-d633affefa9b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Compulsory Voting', E'Political parties in most democracies not only have to win more votes than their rivals to get into power, they also have to persuade the electorate that it is worth their going out to vote in the first place. In the UK, turnout is frequently low, and one reason cited is ... the weather! Some countries, therefore, have made voting compulsory; it is against the law not to vote and failing to vote is a punishable offense.\nIn Austria, for example, failure to vote results in an automatic fine, as it does in Australia. As a consequence, voter turnout is rarely less than 92% in both these countries. Other countries have penalties that affect the individual in more practical ways. In Greece, for example, although it is no longer acted on, passports were confiscated or not granted; and in Bolivia, non-voters may be banned from using banks or schools for up to three months. The punishment in countries, such as France, Germany, the UK, and so on, is seeing the government you didn''t elect raise your taxes.\n\nWhich of the countries listed below continue to enforce punishments for failure to vote?', '496393f6-6b80-5611-b72b-8a5a15b4662f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'France\nBolivia\nthe UK\nAustralia\nAustria', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8c74400-edc1-5f39-bb47-7f989913eeda'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8c74400-edc1-5f39-bb47-7f989913eeda'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '7ab3152f-7327-5378-a571-7e590c87dc4a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Momentum is about how quick something moves and its weight.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8cb8c25-264e-5d09-87d2-8598c5f374d5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8cb8c25-264e-5d09-87d2-8598c5f374d5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '1457e018-c25f-52c1-9fcc-a5a2e3c17a6f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Members can contribute to the association of operating firm.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8cbabe1-b1aa-59b3-9942-5d27d380c296'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8cbabe1-b1aa-59b3-9942-5d27d380c296'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Decision', E'By the laws of probability, most decisions made under pressure should be flawed ones, yet psychologists have found that people routinely make correct judgments most of the time, even with limited information. One of Gladwell''s surprising points is that we can actually learn how to make better snap judgments, in the same way that we can learn logical, deliberative thinking. But first we have to accept the idea that thinking long and hard about something does not always deliver us better results, and that the brain actually evolved to make us think on our feet.\n\nWhich of the following does the passage tell us about decision making?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The brain is designed to enable quick decision making.\nQuick decision making can be improved.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8cc837e-1cee-545c-ac13-0c675fedcfc2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8cc837e-1cee-545c-ac13-0c675fedcfc2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '9e03c4e7-bca9-5f76-abe4-0cb4db75de00'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'There is an agreed consensus that the leadership skills can be taught.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8d85ab4-66e6-51dd-9835-1ec6a6e13998'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8d85ab4-66e6-51dd-9835-1ec6a6e13998'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '8416610c-b422-5137-9fb2-dbbd222048d9'::uuid, NULL, E'We would like a first draft of the assignment by Monday.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f8d95162-9e5b-5f55-bb52-786459b01c4d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8d95162-9e5b-5f55-bb52-786459b01c4d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Internet', NULL, '24c412d5-b9f9-5b91-940f-86c966a8359e'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, I''m excited to discuss the transformative power of the Internet, a technological marvel that has reshaped every aspect of our lives. The Internet is not just a network of computers; it''s a platform for global connection, innovation, and expression. The Internet''s inception has marked a turning point in human history. It has revolutionized communication, making it instant and borderless. We can now connect with someone across the world in seconds, something unimaginable just a few decades ago. Moreover, the Internet has been a powerful tool for education and knowledge dissemination. It offers an unprecedented access to information, breaking down barriers to education and learning opportunities. Online resources, courses, and platforms have democratized education, making it accessible to a broader audience. The Internet has also fueled innovation and entrepreneurship. It has given birth to new industries, transformed traditional businesses, and provided a platform for startups and individual creators to showcase their ideas and products to a global audience. However, the Internet''s impact is not without challenges, including issues related to privacy, misinformation, and digital divide. It''s essential to navigate these challenges thoughtfully as we continue to harness the Internet''s potential. In conclusion, the Internet is a cornerstone of modern society, a tool that continues to evolve and shape our world in profound ways. It''s a testament to human ingenuity and our relentless pursuit of connection and progress.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f8da589f-de47-513a-bfaf-c5349e0f5d67'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8da589f-de47-513a-bfaf-c5349e0f5d67'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '4eb1b645-6599-54d3-aafa-b329e1ba350d'::uuid, NULL, E'They opened a new store in Europe to test out the market.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f8daa180-99e1-531f-90a4-0ea46bf30a82'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8daa180-99e1-531f-90a4-0ea46bf30a82'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call a person who doesn’t eat meat or fish?', '7dfdc34f-83c1-5d67-9e33-6ca322524c69'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Vegetarian / vegan', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8de2f37-5fcb-5c52-b5bb-fbbbb49adda8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8de2f37-5fcb-5c52-b5bb-fbbbb49adda8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fascination', E'A fascination with the fate of those who show great early talent remained with me. Then in 1981, I happened upon a radio documentary {{1}} Hephzibah, who died earlier that year. Produced and narrated for the Australian Broadcasting Commission’s The Coming Out Show by the influential feminist commentator and academic Eva Cox – who was, I learnt for the first time, Hephzibah’s stepdaughter – it {{2}} interviews with Hephzibah and with those who had {{3}} her. I heard her light, precise voice with its slightly Germanic vowels and hint of an American {{4}} as she spoke about things that were important to her, and I was drawn to her warmth, thoughtfulness and humor.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.commemorating, 2.featured, 3.known, 4.drawl', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8de3b94-8f79-5911-9a44-be11a4b7f107'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8de3b94-8f79-5911-9a44-be11a4b7f107'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Mayan Civilization', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 4, 3, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('f8e053dd-9043-5622-bd79-c35436367605'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8e053dd-9043-5622-bd79-c35436367605'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Cultural Diversity', E'Do you agree that cultural diversity strengthens society?', NULL, NULL, E'Cultural diversity plays a vital role in strengthening society by offering enriched perspectives, promoting creativity and innovation, and fostering tolerance and understanding. Embracing diverse cultures enriches societal discussions, inspires innovative thinking, and nurtures empathy and mutual respect among individuals and communities. In exploring the impact of cultural diversity on society, it becomes evident that the tapestry of varied traditions and experiences contributes to a more inclusive and harmonious world.\nCultural diversity brings a variety of viewpoints and experiences that enrich societal discussions and decision-making. By embracing diverse perspectives, individuals gain a broader understanding of complex issues, fostering inclusivity and comprehensive solutions. Different cultural backgrounds encourage critical thinking and a deeper appreciation for human experiences, leading to a more vibrant social landscape.\nEncountering diverse cultures fosters creativity and innovation by promoting unique perspectives in thinking and addressing challenges. The blend of cultural practices ignites fresh concepts, encourages innovative methods, and propels revolutionary advancements. Varied viewpoints cultivate an environment conducive to creative expression, leading to significant progress in multiple domains and enriching society collectively.\nCultural diversity is a powerful force that strengthens society by enriching perspectives, promoting creativity, and nurturing tolerance. By celebrating the value of cultural diversity, societies can build a more prosperous, harmonious, and interconnected world where differences are embraced and valued for the collective benefit of all.', NULL, 200, 300),
  ('f8e5fdc9-acf7-5085-98db-3192504f50da'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'f8e5fdc9-acf7-5085-98db-3192504f50da'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '99e30e0b-66d7-5100-8fbb-c44b3b1f8864'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You should submit your essay by midnight tomorrow.', NULL, NULL),
