  ('fa150a7d-1efd-5342-abc7-e8ceaa6a56c2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa150a7d-1efd-5342-abc7-e8ceaa6a56c2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '874b7fcc-4646-5e37-8d18-3575a629bc33'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'This course provides students with practical experience relevant to the industry.', NULL, NULL),
  ('fa1912c7-e4a2-5a9f-8924-4320aac50143'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa1912c7-e4a2-5a9f-8924-4320aac50143'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fundamental Forces', NULL, '58245f3b-6d76-5c61-844f-0f60aeeb8e62'::uuid, NULL, E'There are four fundamental forces at work in the universe. Some of them are very familiar from everyday life, some of them are not. So we all know about gravity. That''s one of the four forces. It''s what keeps us anchored to the surface of the earth, keeps the Earth in orbit around the Sun. There is another force that we''re very familiar with, which is the electromagnetic force, that is the force that is responsible for the electricity, electric currents for light, for the sun''s light, that''s electromagnetic radiation coming from the Sun to the Earth. There are two other forces though, that are somewhat less familiar, they are the nuclear forces. They are forces that are at work within the nuclear atoms. One of those forces is called the strong nuclear force, that really is the force that bides protons to proton, bides the corks inside of the protons and neutrons keeping them from flying out. The other nuclear force is called the weak nuclear force. And that''s a force that predominantly we know of because it''s responsible for radio activity, radioactive decay. So those four forces, strong nuclear force, weak nuclear force, electromagnetic force and gravitational force, those are the forces that work in the universe.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fa1af8e2-52da-5eb4-8709-6a84268a34af'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa1af8e2-52da-5eb4-8709-6a84268a34af'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Heart of Study', E'Turning now to the heart of the study, in two divisions an attempt {{1}} to change the supervision so that the decision levels were {{2}} and detailed supervision of the workers reduced. More general supervision of the clerks and their supervisors was introduced. In addition, the managers, assistant managers, supervisors and assistant supervisors of these two divisions were {{3}} in group methods of leadership, which they {{4}} to use as much as their skill would permit during the experimental year. For easy reference, the experimental changes in these two divisions {{5}} the ‘participative program’!', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.was made, 2.pushed down, 3.trained, 4.endeavored, 5.will be labelled', NULL, NULL),
  ('fa1feb08-c7ca-5299-a3dd-c4b806a106a6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa1feb08-c7ca-5299-a3dd-c4b806a106a6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Athens Games', E'While the preparations for the Athens games were {{1}} by construction delays and an epic race to complete {{2}} before the opening ceremonies, the game''s return to their historic home ended as a surprising success. Participation {{3}} were once again broken, with 201 nations and 10,625 athletes taking part in 301 different events. Nearly as {{4}} as the competitions were the historic sites used for the games.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.marred, 2.venues, 3.records, 4.compelling', NULL, NULL),
  ('fa2b3a4a-5ce7-56a8-8c0f-5ec09ff354ef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa2b3a4a-5ce7-56a8-8c0f-5ec09ff354ef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, 'b796672e-ae84-5cbe-b40c-1ae555395732'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The fund aims to support a variety of scholarship in the college.', NULL, NULL),
  ('fa3722e6-3f1c-5e1a-8d75-20427c3eb2c9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa3722e6-3f1c-5e1a-8d75-20427c3eb2c9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'American Economy', E'As we have already seen, the American economy is increasingly global and effects of a downturn in one area of the world can immediately affect the value of American stocks at home. Throughout the first half of the year, it was widely speculated that Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan would choose to raise interest rates in the US to cool down the economy a bit and prevent inflation from creeping in. By late September, though, he was coming under increasing pressure to lower interest rates to fend off deflationary pressure. What happened?', NULL, NULL, E'the American economy is increasingly global, with a downturn in one area of the world able to immediately affect the value of American stocks at home, and although it was widely speculated that Greenspan would choose to raise interest rates in the US to cool down the economy and prevent inflation, he was coming under increasing pressure to lower interest rates to fend off deflationary pressure.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('fa38646b-d65c-57c2-8a4c-eb7f38f5f90b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa38646b-d65c-57c2-8a4c-eb7f38f5f90b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Fish Dispersal', E'Small lakes with a surface area of less than 100 m2 represent the majority of global freshwater ecosystems. Many of these lakes are found in {{1}} , often mountainous areas with no inflow and outflow. Yet in most of these lakes, there are fish. So how do fish reach lakes and ponds that are not connected to other bodies of water?\nThis question was already addressed by some of the leading natural scientists of the 19th century such as Charles Darwin, Alfred Russel Wallace and Charles Lyell, who all came to the same conclusion – water birds must be responsible for fish {{2}} .\nAnd they had a plausible explanation for this: fish eggs of some species are sticky and can survive for some time out of water. The theory is thus that the fish eggs stick to water birds’ {{3}} or feet; the birds then fly from one body of water to the next, where the fish {{4}} from their eggs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.remote, 2.dispersal, 3.feathers, 4.hatch', NULL, NULL),
  ('fa420fe3-7476-5f95-95e7-c8e87eec1dae'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fa420fe3-7476-5f95-95e7-c8e87eec1dae'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'b23140ef-bc43-5be4-9c8c-2c3f29c941d1'::uuid, NULL, E'The firm decided to bring in a new management team.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
