  ('fd4ca89a-6d39-5746-a89c-54acec080779'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd4ca89a-6d39-5746-a89c-54acec080779'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, '9830987d-7435-51e7-be61-cc7374f16d2f'::uuid, NULL, E'A campaign has begun to try to save a species of birds from extinction.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd4e6868-12b1-5434-b2b2-98fee9d0a255'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd4e6868-12b1-5434-b2b2-98fee9d0a255'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '51bbe1e3-d37a-5cc6-a5cf-14700f16244a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Marine environments have been destroyed through pollution and unsustainable development.', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd538c23-f8e5-57a8-9176-a768d7d3e452'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd538c23-f8e5-57a8-9176-a768d7d3e452'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'King', NULL, 'd6480280-2625-5602-a44c-e34d912afc9d'::uuid, NULL, E'At the top, you would have a king. Now the king would rule over a kingdom. Now, this is not so easy to govern especially during the Middle Ages. And the king might owe many people, things especially people who help the king come to power, helped him dispose the previous king or to conquer this land. And so in exchange for that and to help govern, he might grant land or feasts to other people. And the key currency in the Middle Ages under the feudal system is land. And land in exchange for loyalty and service. So this whole thing is a kingdom. Now right over here, this is a Duchy. And a Duchy will be controlled by a Duke. I guess I didn''t call it duckie because that just doesn''t sound as serious. So the king might grant a Duchy, a Duchy to a Duke and in exchange, the Duke would provide loyalty pledged their fealty. If the kingdom is threatened, the Duke will fight alongside. The King would provide their own troops if the king wants to go conquer other territories, same thing, and also provide the king with taxes which might be in the form of coinage depending on what time and region we are in the Middle Ages or it might be in the form of a percentage of the agricultural production from this Duchy.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd5a1cee-7ee0-5114-8d7b-acea5e630d6f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd5a1cee-7ee0-5114-8d7b-acea5e630d6f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Archean Eon', E'During the Archean Eon, methane droplets in the air shrouded the young Earth in a global haze. There was no oxygen gas on Earth. Oxygen was only in compounds such as water. Complex chemical reactions in the young oceans transformed carbon-containing molecules into simple, living cells that did not need oxygen to live. Instead they made energy out of sulfur and other elements.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd5bbea3-09a6-5e8c-9072-7bf7eb53251b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd5bbea3-09a6-5e8c-9072-7bf7eb53251b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Artificial Intelligence', E'Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming many aspects of modern society, from healthcare and finance to transportation and entertainment. AI refers to the development of computer systems that can perform tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as speech recognition, decision-making, and problem-solving.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd5e324b-2eb2-58ff-ae8a-1809c86b0ed8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'WRITE_FROM_DICTATION', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd5e324b-2eb2-58ff-ae8a-1809c86b0ed8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'WFD', NULL, '62f97118-f7bd-5c98-a538-53f1f4b45bbb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'You can find the complaint form on the website.', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd61c49e-16bb-519d-86d8-b74edf87751c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd61c49e-16bb-519d-86d8-b74edf87751c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'ASQ', E'What do we call the subject that studies weather and temperature?', 'fbdc21e7-c8be-5e5a-b84b-542ec32231ef'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Meteorology / climatology', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd664456-cc64-5a4a-9d89-e67cddec2870'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd664456-cc64-5a4a-9d89-e67cddec2870'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Networking Primates', E'Good news for {{1}} networking primates: other primates that live in large social groups have more street smarts than their comrades with smaller social circles. So finds a study in the journal PLoS ONE.\nResearchers tested the {{2}} under which lemurs would pilfer food from people. The study included ring-tailed lemurs, which come from large social groups, as well as lemurs from small-groups, like the mongoose lemur. The lemurs all had the same brain size, so would be presumed to have similar raw {{3}} .\nHumans sat in a room with either a plate of food on the table in front of them or behind them. A third group of people was {{4}} ed, with the plate in front of them.\nLemurs from large social groups tended to steal the food if the person''s back was to it. Lemurs from smaller social groups went for the food as {{5}} regardless of its position. And no lemurs appeared to {{6}} the purpose of a blindfold.\nThe {{7}} interpret the results as showing that social factors can influence a species'' smarts. So you could be outwitted by a birdbrain, if he has a lot of friends.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.big-time, 2.circumstances, 3.intelligence, 4.blindfold, 5.frequently, 6.understand, 7.researchers', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd6fe6d8-f8b6-5a28-8a93-5a79c9a030e7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd6fe6d8-f8b6-5a28-8a93-5a79c9a030e7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'ea8e5129-a4a9-5f9f-832b-13f96c5c5e6c'::uuid, NULL, E'Sleep science is a field of research that is currently highly active.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd714e04-6daf-5129-8e9e-5ac52e2d213e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd714e04-6daf-5129-8e9e-5ac52e2d213e'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Printing Press', NULL, '910d47eb-2f8a-59c4-b860-a664241f361c'::uuid, NULL, E'Today, let''s delve into the revolutionary impact of the printing press, an invention that transformed society and laid the groundwork for the modern world. Invented by Johannes Gutenberg in the 15th century, the printing press ushered in an era of mass communication, altering the course of history. Before the printing press, books were hand-copied and scarce, limiting knowledge to a privileged few. Gutenberg''s invention made it possible to produce books quickly and in large numbers, democratizing information and making it accessible to a broader audience. This was a turning point that fueled the Renaissance, the Scientific Revolution, and the Reformation. The spread of printed material led to increased literacy rates and the dissemination of new ideas across Europe. It broke the monopoly of the elite over knowledge and education, empowering individuals with information and fostering critical thinking and debate. Furthermore, the printing press played a crucial role in preserving and sharing knowledge. It helped standardize languages and texts, shaping cultural and national identities. Its influence extended beyond literature to politics, religion, and science, paving the way for societal advancements. In conclusion, the printing press was not just an invention but a catalyst for change. It highlights the power of technology to drive societal progress and reminds us of the ongoing impact of our communication tools.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('fd78e41e-c61c-510a-84ce-43b993a83d09'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd78e41e-c61c-510a-84ce-43b993a83d09'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Plant-based Milk Products', E'If you go to the store in search of milk, there are a dizzying number of products to choose from. There’s dairy milk, but also plant-based products. To turn a plant into something resembling milk, it must be either soaked, drained, rinsed, and milled into a thick paste, or dried, and milled into flour. The plant paste or flour is then fortified with vitamins and minerals, flavored, and diluted with water. The result is a barrage of options that share many of the qualities of animal milk.\n\nWhat does the speaker say about plant-based milk products?', '73d60b24-a6a5-5a07-b759-ffa7285758fe'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Although made from plants, plant-based products still share many qualities with animal milk.', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd792b49-eda4-5f39-a2ed-ddb2fbf0bf10'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd792b49-eda4-5f39-a2ed-ddb2fbf0bf10'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'Learn and Sleep', E'But scientists have found that there might be a way to boost the part of the learning process that happens during sleep. Sleep plays a vital role in how you create and store memories. While you''re awake, you learn all sorts of new stuff, taking in facts and experiences just from going about your everyday life. That''s when your brain encodes memories, making new connections between neurons so you can remember it all later. Then, when you go to sleep, your brain goes through the consolidation phase of memory formation. Scientists aren''t totally sure how that works, but they think your brain turns all that stuff you just learned into solid, long term memories by reactivating them and strengthening those...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '52fa5538-d58a-5002-a9c6-cdbb233b3898'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'new connections', NULL, NULL),
  ('fd88a7ea-df27-57d3-a970-8fa447eac924'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', E'SHARED', NULL, E'APPROVED', 'fd88a7ea-df27-57d3-a970-8fa447eac924'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'RS', NULL, 'e799203b-740c-5a48-95c4-41a58135fef5'::uuid, NULL, E'Marks will be awarded for a bibliography in the correct format.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
