  ('2b168b6a-d426-5cd5-875d-f63da71df193'::uuid, 'bda372f4-83cc-52cb-acaa-53a70f0e955e'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'care', TRUE, 7, NULL, 2),
  ('7bb199e4-52de-59fb-84e0-ffb6b6ab095d'::uuid, 'bda95504-88dd-50e1-a431-feda85985085'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'Once plants and animals die, the carbon they contain can turn into fossil fuels, like coal and oil.', FALSE, 0, NULL, NULL),
  ('81ff540d-4592-5378-8132-76290a77cf61'::uuid, 'bda95504-88dd-50e1-a431-feda85985085'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'Humans have burned so much fossil fuel, and the earth is getting hotter and hotter, which is called global warming.', FALSE, 1, NULL, NULL),
  ('ad10d410-6adb-5e82-91f6-695fef3e187d'::uuid, 'bda95504-88dd-50e1-a431-feda85985085'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'All living things are made of carbon. In the atmosphere, carbon bonds with oxygen to form carbon dioxide, which plants use to grow.', FALSE, 2, NULL, NULL),
  ('9dbe16d8-df56-51ed-bb9a-cc2461eca7b6'::uuid, 'bda95504-88dd-50e1-a431-feda85985085'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'When humans burn fossil fuels, the carbon combines with oxygen to form C02 and is released into the atmosphere, where it traps in heat to keep the earth warm.', FALSE, 3, NULL, NULL),
  ('925d0bde-a25f-5739-ad66-03adb9a0d096'::uuid, 'bdaa71a7-4225-5e62-a456-ebe0d011faf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'For example, the sherbet you used for the chapter problem on page 25 is a mixture of baking soda and citric acid.', FALSE, 0, NULL, NULL),
  ('5c929d93-b833-560b-95c6-19c51e8e486e'::uuid, 'bdaa71a7-4225-5e62-a456-ebe0d011faf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'Another example of an endothermic reaction is seen with the cold packs used by athletes to treat injuries. These packs usually consist of a plastic bag containing ammonium nitrate dissolves in the water.', FALSE, 1, NULL, NULL),
  ('797c511e-8c05-5514-b770-792a5a2c2cb6'::uuid, 'bdaa71a7-4225-5e62-a456-ebe0d011faf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'When it is mixed with water in your mouth, an endothermic reaction occurs, taking heat energy from your mouth and making it feel cooler.', FALSE, 2, NULL, NULL),
  ('c9c64ba5-5487-59b8-bf0f-264c938f05aa'::uuid, 'bdaa71a7-4225-5e62-a456-ebe0d011faf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'A reaction that needs some type of energy to make it go is said to be endothermic. It takes in energy.', FALSE, 3, NULL, NULL),
  ('0f13a97f-ed49-57f9-b07d-839b696ab375'::uuid, 'bdaa71a7-4225-5e62-a456-ebe0d011faf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'This process is endothermic-taking heat energy from the surroundings and cooling the injured part of your body. In this way, the cold pack acts as an ice pack.', FALSE, 4, NULL, NULL),
  ('dca0ac4b-bd61-560a-a094-778cd89143f3'::uuid, 'bdb98e9e-58a2-568e-bb12-869a9db514a3'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-09-23 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'requires', TRUE, 0, 0, NULL),
